(comment TheInternationalNews-Online "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment TheDailyHerald-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment Haaretz-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment News24DotCom "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment TheAustralian-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TheJerusalemPost-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment ElMundo-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment SpeedOfSound "This is the (range of) #$Speed at which #$Sound travels in #$Air: 300-340 #$MetersPerSecond, or #$approximately 673-761 #$MilesPerHour.  The speed of sound varies depending on atmospheric conditions, such as #$Temperature and altitude.  At sea level, sound travels at approximately 340 #$MetersPerSecond.")
(comment JeuneAfriqueLIntelligent "An instance of #$MagazineSeries.")
(comment HeraldSun-Newpaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment NewsInteractive-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries based in #$Australia.")
(comment NewsdayDotCom-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment TheJerusalemReport-Magazine "An instance of #$MagazineSeries.")
(comment ArabNews-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TheDesertSun-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment SeattlePostIntelligencer-Newpaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment FarEasternEconomicReview-Journal "An instance of #$JournalIssue.")
(comment TheDailyGamecock-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment ColumbiaDailyTribune-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment ChannelNewsAsia-Online "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment PhilippinesDailyInquirer-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment RediffDotCom-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries based in #$India.")
(comment CNN-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment MiddleEastNewsline "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment WorldTribune-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment TheWorldNews-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries based in #$Australia.")
(comment TheJakartaPost-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment MilwaukeeJournalSentinel-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TheIndianExpress-Newpaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries published in #$India.")
(comment WorldNewsConnection-OnlineNews "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries based in #$NewZealand.")
(comment MiddleEastTimes "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment NewYorkPost-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment PakistanToday-Newpaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TheCourierMail-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TheNationalInterest-Periodical "An instance of #$JournalIssue.")
(comment TheWeeklyStandard-Magazine "An instance of #$MagazineSeries.")
(comment PakTribune-Online "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment TallahasseeDemocrat-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(disjointWith TradeAssociation Anti-AbortionGroup)
(disjointWith ChamberOfCommerce Anti-AbortionGroup)
(comment Anti-AbortionGroup "A specialization of #$AdvocacyOrganization and #$IdeologicalOrganization.  Each instance of #$Anti-AbortionGroup is an organization whose members are anti-abortion.  Groups in this collection often are active in the political arena hiring lobbyists to promote their cause among politicians.  There can be peaceful as well as violent anti-abortion groups (c.f. #$Anti-AbortionTerroristGroup).")
(comment CommunistOrganization "A subcollection of #$PoliticalOrganization.  This is the collection of all organizations whose main belief system is communism.  This includes all the various communist parties as well as organizations that support communism but are not political parties.")
(comment HumanRightsViolation "A specialization of #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal.  Each instance of this collection is an action that violates some provision of the #$BasicHumanRights-UNDeclaration as represented in #$HumanRights-COC.")
(comment orgMilitaryWing "A predicate for relating an organization to a military organization that promotes the aims of that organization. (#$orgMilitaryWing ORG MILORG) means that ORG has MILORG as one of its military wings.")
(comment NorthCountyTimes-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment BusinessWorld-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TheReview-Journal "An instance of #$JournalIssue.")
(comment TheHollandSentinel-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TheOlympian-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment PortlandTribune-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment StLouisPostDispatch-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment IndianapolisStar-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment BigNewsNetworkDotCom "An instance of #$OnlineNewsSeries.")
(comment someAndOnlyTypePlaysRoleInSituationType "<code>(#$someAndOnlyTypePlaysRoleInSituationType SIT-TYPE TYPE ROLE)</code> means that for any instance <code>SIT-TYPE-INST</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, there exists an instance of <code>TYPE</code> that plays the role <code>ROLE</code> in <code>SIT-TYPE-INST</code>, and that only an instance of <code>TYPE</code> plays that role.  Cf. the more general predicate #$onlyTypePlaysRoleInSubSituationType, which does not require an instance of <code>TYPE</code> to play <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, but rather requires that whatever plays <code>ROLE</code> in <code>SIT-TYPE</code> be of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment ZamanOnline-News "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment EveningStandard-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment TurkishDailyNews-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment KashmirHerald-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment ArmyTimes-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment EnglishPeoplesDailyOnline "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment Passport-Agreement "A specialization of #$AuthorizedAgreement and
#$LegalAgreement. Each instance of Passport-Agreement is an
authorization issued by the government of some country to a person
stating that he or she is allowed to leave the country and
re-enter. This agreement typicaly includes a formal recognition that
the person is a legal citizen of the government's country, and may
have other privileges and qualifications.")
(comment FivePillarsOfIslam "An instance of #$CodeOfConduct.  These are the five most
fundemental obligations of Islam.")
(comment Shahadah "An instance of #$CodeOfConduct and a #$subObligations of
#$FivePillarsOfIslam.  The faithful profess the belief there is only
one god and #$MuhammadTheProphet is His prophet.  One only needs to
recite the Arabic form aloud in front of two Muslims to be converted
to Islam.")
(comment Salah "An instance of #$CodeOfConduct and a #$subObligations of
#$FivePillarsOfIslam.  These are the five daily prayers the faithful
offer to God.  The prayers are named: Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and
Isha'a.  They are named for the time of day the prayer is performed.
They are complusory for every #$MuslimPerson.")
(comment Zakat "An instance of #$CodeOfConduct and a #$subObligations of
#$FivePillarsOfIslam. These are monetary donations that are
compulsaory for the faithful and subsequently are distributed among
designated categories of people, including those with insufficient
means and those who fight for Allah's cause.")
(comment Siyam "An instance of #$CodeOfConduct and a #$subObligations of
#$FivePillarsOfIslam. This obligation involves fasting during
#$RamadanHoliday.  Specifically, the faithful should refrain from
eating and drinking, sexual intercourse, games of chance, and smoking
during the daylight hours.  There are groups of people exempt from
observances: young children, soldiers on the battlefield, pregnant
women, the sick and elderly.  The faithful are encouraged to spend
time reading and/or listening to the Koran.")
(comment PilgrimageToMecca "An instance of #$CodeOfConduct and a #$subObligations of
#$FivePillarsOfIslam. This obligation requires every able-bodied
Muslim to make a pilgrimage to #$CityOfMeccaSaudiArabia, if he or she
can afford to do so.  See also #$Hajj-Pilgrimage, which the
over-arching performance of the pilgrimage.")
(comment AllegedPersonTypeFn "An instance of #$UnaryFunction. This function takes for its
value a specialization of #$Person, <b>TYPE</b>, and returns
the collection of #$Persons alleged instances of <b>TYPE</b>. See also #$AllegedTypeFn.")
(comment argSometimesIsa "(#$argSometimesIsa RELATION POSITIVE-INTERGER-N COLLECTION) means that semantic
well-formedness requires that anything given as the Nth argument to RELN must be
an instance of COL at sometime or other.  More precisely, if (#$argSometimesIsa RELATION POSITIVE-INTERGER-N COLLECTION) then in order to assert: (RELATION ARG-N ... OTHER-ARGS)<MT TIME PAR>, it must be the case that there exists some time interval, t, such that (#$isa ARG-N COLLECTION)<MT t PAR>.")
(comment ConcealingTypeWithinTypeFn "An expression of the form (#$ConcealingTypeWithinTypeFn SMALL-TYPE BIG-TYPE) is used to denote a sub-collection of #$HidingAnObject where an instance of SMALL-TYPE, some sub-collection of #$PartiallyTangible is hidden within an instance of BIG-TYPE, some other instance of #$PartiallyTangible.  In all instances of the denoted sub-collection, the instance of SMALL-TYPE plays the role of #$objectHidden and the instance of BIG-TYPE plays the role of #$instrumentForHiding, and during the course of the event, the relationship #$spatiallyContains holds between the instance of SMALL-TYPE and the instance of BIG-TYPE.")
(comment typeIsConcealingTypeWithinType "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$HidingTypeWithinTypeFn.")
(comment instrumentForHiding "A #$BinaryRolePredicate #$instrumentForHiding is used to represent the instance of #$PartiallyTangible within an instance of #$ConcealingFromSight that does the work of hiding the object in the role of #$objectHidden.  For instance, a suicide bomber might hide a bomb within his coat when traveling to the target.  The bomb plays the role of #$objectHidden, the coat plays the role of #$instrumentForHiding.")
(comment HavingPhysicalAccessToSomething "A sub-collection of #$Situation, instances of #$HavingPhysicalAccessToSomething means that some instance of #$IndividualAgent can physically interact with, including entering, some instance of #$PartiallyTangible.  This is a very broad sub-collection of #$Situation and is subsumes situations where someone can walk into a particular #$Cave with an open mouth, being able to enter a locked building when one has a key, as well as being able to open an unlocked filing cabinet. Key roles for instances of this collection are #$accessibleObject and #$accessor.")
(comment HavingEntryAccessToSomePlace "A sub-collection of #$HavingPhysicalAccessToSomething.  All instances of #$HavingEntryAccessToSomePlace are those situations in which some #$IndividualAgent can physically enter into a #$Place.  In such situations, the relevant #$IndividualAgent would play the role of #$accessor and the relevant instance of #$Place would play the role of #$accessibleObject.")
(comment accessibleObject "An assertion of the form (#$accessibleObject ACCESS THING) means that in the instance of #$HavingPhysicalAccessToSomething ACCESS, the instance of #$PartiallyTangible THING can be physically interacted with by some #$IndividualAgent, who would play the role of #$accessor in ACCESS.")
(comment accessor "An assertion of the form (#$accessor ACCESS AGENT) means that in the instance of #$HavingPhysicalAccessToSomething ACCESS, the instance of #$IndividualAgent AGENT is capable of physically interacting with some instance of #$PartiallyTangible, which would play the role of #$accessibleObject in ACCESS.")
(comment BombingWithHiddenDevice "A sub-collection of #$Bombing,  all instances of this collection involve the delivery of a #$Bomb to some location with the bomb being hidden within some other #$PartiallyTangible.")
(comment ProcessType "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  #$ProcessType is the collection intersection of #$TemporalStuffType and #$DurativeEventType; that is, a thing is an instance of #$ProcessType if and only if it is an instance of both #$TemporalStuffType and #$DurativeEventType.  Instances of #$ProcessType can be constructed from instances of #$AccomplishmentType using #$ProcessFn (q.v.).")
(disjointWith AccomplishmentType ProcessType)
(comment ProposeSentenceFromPartialParseInfo-ClarificationStrategy "An instance of #$ClarificationStrategy in which one reasons about the known semantic components of a query that hasn't been fully parsed, and proposes an interpretation of that query.")
(comment genlKBContentTests "A specialization of #$genlSpecifications (q.v.) that relates instances of #$KBContentTest (q.v.) that ask the same question, but where one of the tests might specify more fully how the query is to be carried out (see #$softwareParameterValueInSpecification).  
<p>
<code>(#$genlKBContentTests SPECTEST GENLTEST)</code> means that the #$InferenceParameter values specified for SPECTEST subsume those specified for GENLTEST, and that SPECTEST and GENLTEST have the same \"question-content\" (see #$kbContentTestQuestion-Content).  The latter condition can be broken down into two cases:  either (i) SPECTEST and GENLTEST both have the same CycL formula as their respective #$InferenceSentenceParameter values or (ii) SPECTEST has the CycL formula <code>SENT</code> as its #$InferenceSentenceParameter value and GENLTEST is a #$KBContentTest-QueryContentOnly (q.v.) whose question-content is the intensional meaning (see #$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn) expressed by <code>SENT</code>.
<p>
In cases (i) above, GENLTEST might be a #$KBContentTest-QuerySentenceOnly (q.v.) that serves as a common generalization of various #$KBContentTest-FullySpecifieds.  In cases (ii), GENLTEST will be a #$KBContentTest-QueryContentOnly (q.v.) that serves as a common generalization of various fully- and partially-specified KB content tests whose specified inference sentence is logically equivalent to or synonymous with SENT.
<p>
The intended use of #$genlKBContentTests is for tying together #$KBContentTest-FullySpecifieds that amount to variations on the same question, either because their respective query sentences are logically equivalent, or because they use the same query sentence but differ in some other inference parameter settings, such as the maximum time or the allowance of HL predicate transformations.")
(comment kbContentTestQuestion-Content "A binary predicate that relates a given #$KBContentTest (q.v.) to the propositional or otherwise intensional content (see #$Information-Content) of the question that the test is asking.  <code>(#$kbContentTestQuestion-Content TEST CONTENT)</code> means that TEST asks about CONTENT.  If the question being asked in TEST is a \"Yes/No\" question, then CONTENT will be a #$Proposition.   If the question being asked in TEST is a \"what things are such that\" question -- i.e. a question that asks for bindings for variables -- then CONTENT will be an intensional property or propositional function.
<p>
If TEST has a specific CycL sentence SENT as its #$InferenceSentenceParameter (q.v.) value, then CONTENT will be (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn SENT): the intensional meaning of SENT with respect to its potential use in a Cyc query.  If TEST is a #$KBContentTest-QueryContentOnly, then any specialization SPECTEST of TEST (see #$genlKBContentTests) must have CONTENT as its question-content as well; and if SPECTEST has SPECSENT as the value of its #$InferenceSentenceParameter, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn SPECSENT) will be equal to CONTENT.")
(comment kbContentTestImplies-QuerySentenceOnly "A binary predicate that holds between two instances of #$KBContentTest-QuerySentenceOnly (q.v.) such that the query sentence of the first logically entails the query sentence of the second.  <code>(#$kbContentTestImplies-QuerySentenceOnly TEST1 TEST2)</code> means that if both of these hold:
<pre>
  (#$softwareParameterValueInSpecification
    #$InferenceSentenceParameter SENT1 (#$TestQueryFn TEST1))

  (#$softwareParameterValueInSpecification
    #$InferenceSentenceParameter SENT2 (#$TestQueryFn TEST2))
</pre>
then so does this:
<pre>
  (#$sentenceImplies SENT1 SENT2) .")
(comment indMightPlayRoleInSitType-Evidential "An assertion of the form (#$indMightPlayRoleInSitType-Linkage OBJ ROLE SIT-TYPE) is used to assert that there exists evidence that the #$SomethingExisting OBJ may be filling ROLE, an instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate, in an instance of SIT-TYPE, some sub-collection of #$Situation")
(comment setOfIndMightPlayRoleInSitType "An assertion of the form (#$setOfIndMightPlayRoleInSitType SET ROLE SIT-TYPE) is used to assert that there exists evidence that the #$SetOrCollection SET is such that all of its elements may be filling ROLE, an instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate, in an instance of SIT-TYPE, some sub-collection of #$Situation.")
(comment indMightPlayRoleInSitType-Linkage "An assertion of the form (#$indMightPlayRoleInSitType-Linkage IND ROLE SIT-TYPE) means that there is speculative evidence that the #$SomethingExisting IND might play the #$BinaryRolePredicate ROLE in an instance of the sub-collection of #$Situation SIT-TYPE.  By speculative evidence, we mean evidence that is based on other hypotheses.  Contrast with #$indMightPlayRoleInSitType-Evidential.")
(comment banksAt "An instance of #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate.  (#$banksAt AGENT BANK) means that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent AGENT banks at -- has an active account with -- the instance of #$BankOrganization, BANK.")
(comment bank-Role "(#$bank-Role SITUATION BANK) says that the instance of #$Agent-Generic, BANK is playing the role of bank in the situation SITUATION. BANK might be a bank, a savings-and-loan, or a loan shark.")
(comment evaluateImmediately "(#$evaluateImmediately FUNCTION) means that the canonicalizer will translate each non-atomic term (see the collection #$CycLNonAtomicTerm) whose initial (or \"0th\" argument-place) term denotes FUNCTION into the value to which the non-atomic term evaluates.  For example, if (#$evaluateImmediately #$PlusFn) held, then the non-atomic term `(#$PlusFn 2 3 4)' would canonicalize as `9'.  Note that a non-atomic term containing a nested non-atomic term whose initial term denotes another instance of #$EvaluatableFunction (call that instance OTHER-FUNCTION) will not canonicalize in this way, unless (#$evaluateImmediately OTHER-FUNCTION) is also true.  For example, `(#$PlusFn 2 (#$DifferenceFn 3 4))' would not canonicalize as `1' unless    
(#$evaluateImmediately #$DifferenceFn) were also true.")
(comment quasiTemporalVersionOfTemporalRelation "<code>(#$quasiTemporalVersionOfTemporalRelation TEMP-PRED QUASI-TEMP-PRED)</code> means that <code>QUASI-TEMP-PRED</code> is the quasi-temporal version of <code>TEMP-PRED</code>.  
<p>
In other words, <code>QUASI-TEMP-PRED</code> is the predicate used to assert that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of some situation-type <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, sub-situatons of <code>SIT</code> bear the relation <code>TEMP-PRED</code> to one another.
<p>
For example, (#$quasiTemporalVersionOfTemporalRelation #$startsAfterEndingOf 
#$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType) is true because  #$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType is the quasi-temporal version of #$startsAfterEndingOf.")
(comment energySourceTypeForDeviceType "This predicate is used to identify the types of energy sources used to
make types of #$PoweredDevices run. (#$energySourceTypeForDeviceType DEVICETYPE
ENERGYSOURCETYPE) means that ENERGYSOURCETYPE provides (some of) the energy
used to power DEVICETYPES. ENERGYSOURCETYPE might be #$Electricity, #$NaturalGas, etc.. Note that any given device may be powered by more than one type of energy source.")
(comment profiledCycLTermFor "(#$profiledCycLTermFor CYCL-TERM THING) means that CYCL-TERM is an instance of #$CycLTerm that 1) refers to THING, and 2) has been introduced as part of Cyc's dialogue modelling as a way to track at a linguistic level which objects (e.g., THING) have been mentioned by the relevant speaker in past conversations.")
(comment Cancan-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the cancan style.")
(comment bugKeywordString "(#$bugKeywordString BUG KEYWORD) means that the
#$BugzillaBugReport BUG has the string KEYWORD as one of its 'keyword'
values.")
(comment SKSISupportedOperator "#$SKSISupportedOperator is the collection of CycL
#$Relations which are translatable into their SQL equivalents by SKSI
removal modules. Its two disjoint specializations are
#$SKSISupportedComparisonPredicate and #$SKSISupportedFunction.")
(disjointWith SKSISupportedFunction SKSISupportedComparisonPredicate)
(comment SKSISupportedFunction "This is the collection of evaluatable functions which are
supported by SKSI in the sense that they are translatable to their SQL
equivalents.")
(comment TransportedInTypeFn "(#$TransportedInTypeFn TRANSPORT-TYPE) denotes the collection of all #$PartiallyTangibles which are #$transportedInTypes TRANSPORT-TYPE. Example: (#$TransportedInTypeFn #$Balloon) denotes the collection of all things which are transported in a balloon.")
(comment DeviceUsingEnergyTypeFn "(#$DeviceUsingEnergyTypeFn ENERGY-TYPE) denotes the collection of all #$ArtifactTypes which have ENERGY-TYPE as their #$energySourceTypeForDeviceType. Example: (#$DeviceUsingEnergyTypeFn #$NaturalGas) denotes the collection of all #$NaturalGasPoweredDevices.")
(comment HomemadeArtifact "A specialization of #$Custom-Made. Easch instance of this
collection is an #$Artifact produced by means of domestic manufacture.
Positive examples of this collection would be the batch of strawberry
jam someone makes in his or her kitchen, and the clock someone makes
in his or her woodshop. Negative examples of this collection would
include those products mass produced by companies, #$CocaCola, for
example and even those mass produced items that claim to be
'homemade,' think cookies.")
(comment homemadeTypeOfType "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate that relates a
specialization of #$HomemadeArtifact to the specialization of
#$PartiallyTangible of which they are homemade versions. Thus, (#$homemadeTypeOfType HOMEMADE-TYPE TYPE) means that the collection HOMEMADE-TYPE is the homemade subcollection of TYPE. For instance, (#$homemadeTypeOfType HomemadeCookie #$Cookie) means the collection HomemadeCookie is the collection of #$HomemadeArtifact that are also instance of #$Cookie (q.v.).")
(comment commitsCrimesInLocation "(#$commitsCrimesInLocation AGENT CRIME-TYPE LOCATION) means
that AGENT is the #$perpetrator of crimes of CRIME-TYPE in LOCATION. For example, (#$commitsCrimesInLocation #$RevolutionaryArmedForcesOfColombia #$DrugTrafficking #$Colombia) means that the Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia engages in drug trafficking in Colombia.")
(comment MostlyCloudCoveredArea "Cloud coverage is 6/8 to 7/8 of the sky.")
(comment MostlyCloudlessArea "Cloud coverage is 1/8 to 2/8 of the sky.")
(comment ModerateWindArea "An instance of #$OutdoorLocationByWeatherType.  It is characterized by wind speeds of 25-35 mph.")
(comment HighWindArea "An instance of #$OutdoorLocationByWeatherType.  It is characterized by wind speeds of 35-45 mph.")
(comment DangerousWindArea "An instance of #$OutdoorLocationByWeatherType.  It is characterized by wind speeds in excess of 45 mph.")
(comment LightBreezeArea "#$LightBreezeArea is an instance of #$OutdoorLocationByWeatherType.  It is characterized by wind speeds of 5-15 mph.")
(comment CalmAirArea "#$CalmAirArea is an instance of #$OutdoorLocationByWeatherType.  It is characterized by an absence of wind.")
(comment ambientWindChill "This predicate relates an object to the ambient wind chill
temperature in the region 'around' the object. (#$ambientWindChill
PLACE TEMP) means that given the current atmospheric conditions
'around' PLACE, the temperature feels like TEMP. The wind chill
is the temperature the body feels when cold and wind speed are combined.")
(comment temporalMicrotheoriesIntersect "This predicate takes an arbitrary number of single fixed dimension temporal microtheories (e.g., #$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn expressions) and is true if and only if there is some #$TimeInterval subsumed by the intersection of the #$TimeIntervals of the arguments and which subsumes an instance of the largest #$TimeParameter of the arguments.  So, e.g., (#$temporalMicrotheoriesIntersect (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn (#$YearFn 2004) #$TimePoint) (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn (#$DecadeFn 200) #$CalendarMonth)) is true.")
(comment resultSetCardinalityWithConstraints "This predicate is similar to #$resultSetCardinality in that it is used by the SKSI code to estimate the cost of querying the fields of a physical schema.  More precisely, let SCHEMA denote a physical schema, let PF-1, PF-2, ..., PF-N, denote the physical fields of SCHEMA, and let SELECT_SET and WHERE_SET denote two disjoint subsets of (#$TheSet PF-1 PF-2 ... PF-N) and ..... Then (#$resultSetCardinality SCHEMA SELECT_SET WHERE_SET CONSTRAINTS NUM) means that NUM is the average cardinality of the result set returned from a query in which the fields in SELECT_SET left unbound and the fields of WHERE_SET are bound and the constraints expressed the CycL sentence in CONSTRAINTS are all satisfied.")
(comment Porpoise "Refers to mammalian dolphins and porpoises, as opposed to the fish often called a dolphin.")
(comment foreignFormalLanguageFunctionExpansion "Relates an evaluatable CycL function to a pattern (asserted in a similar style to #$expansions) that can be used to translate an expression using that CycL function into its foreign equivalent.")
(comment WordNetSynsetRelationPredicate "The collection of predicates which describe semantic relations between two WordNet synsets, or lexical relations between particular words in WordNet synsets.")
(comment quotedDefnSufficient "A #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicate. (#$quotedDefnSufficient COL TEST) means that TEST is the name of a piece of code in the SubL implementation of Cyc that specifies, and tests for, a sufficient condition for a CycL term's denoting a quoted instance of (see #$quotedIsa) the collection COL. If TEST returns `T' (for `True') when applied to a particular term, then that term's denotatum is considered to be a quoted instance of COL. Note that TEST isn't necessarily a necessary test for quoted membership in COL; that is, not all quoted instances of COL must pass the test, unless TEST is also a #$defnNecessary for COL, or the term is asserted to be a quoted instance of COL using #$quotedIsa. See the related predicates #$quotedDefnNecessary and #$quotedDefnIff.")
(comment quotedDefnIff "A #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicate. (#$quotedDefnIff COL TEST) means that TEST is the name of a piece of code in the SubL implementation of Cyc that specifies, and tests for, a necessary and sufficient condition for a CycL term's denoting a quoted instance of (see #$quotedIsa) the collection COL. If and only if TEST returns `T' (for `True') when applied to a particular term can that term's denotatum be considered a quoted instance of COL; all and only terms that denote quoted instances of COL must fulfill TEST's requirements.  However, terms asserted to be quoted instances of the collection COL using #$quotedIsa are exempt from fulfilling TEST's requirements. See also #$quotedDefnNecessary and #$quotedDefnSufficient.")
(comment quotedDefnNecessary "A #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicate. (#$quotedDefnNecessary COL TEST) means that TEST is the name of a piece of code in the SubL implementation of Cyc that specifies, and tests for, a necessary condition for a CycL term's denoting a quoted instance of (see #$quotedIsa) the collection COL. Only if TEST returns `T' (for `True') when applied to a particular term can that term's denotatum be considered a quoted instance of COL; all terms that denote quoted instances of COL must fulfill TEST's requirements, although there may be additional requirements for denoting an instance of COL as well. However, terms asserted to be quoted instances of the collection COL using #$quotedIsa are exempt from fulfilling TEST's requirements. See also #$quotedDefnSufficient and #$quotedDefnIff.")
(disjointWith InsuranceProvider YouthCenterOrganization)
(comment YouthCenterOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that provide certain services for youths in their own facilities.  These services are, in general, related to helping youths who have various problems.  Instances of #$YouthCenterOrganization may be either #$CommercialOrganizations or #$NonProfitOrganizations and may be either #$GovernmentalOrganizations, #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations, or #$PrivateSectorOrganizations.")
(comment YouthCenter "A building or section of a building that houses an instance of #$YouthCenterOrganization.")
(comment SubLStringFormConcatenationFn "SubLStringFormConcatenationFn takes a list of valid CycL terms, and returns the concatenation of their string forms.")
(comment LoggingInToAComputerProgram "A specialization of #$AuthenticationEvent.  Each instance of #$LoggingInToAComputerProgram is an event in which a computeruser authenticates himself or herself to a running computer program.  Typically the authentication involves checking a username/password combination entered by the computer user.")
(comment NooescapeProgramComponent "A specialization of #$ComputerProgramModule-CW.  Each instance of #$NooescapeProgramComponent is a sub-program of #$Nooescape-TheProgram.")
(comment sentenceLocalVariable "An assertion of the form (#$sentenceLocalVariable SENTENCE-REP VAR-REP) states that the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLVariable) VAR-REP is a syntactic element of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENTENCE-REP.")
(comment literalPredicate "An assertion of the form (#$literalPredicate LIT PRED) states that the #$Predicate and #$CycLConstant PRED is the value of the 'zero-th' argument of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment literalHasVariableInArg "An assertion of the form (#$literalHasVariableInArg LIT VAR N) states that the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT has the #$CycLVariable VAR as the value of its Nth argument.")
(comment LocalVariableFn "An expression of the form (#$LocalVariableFn SENTENCE VARIABLE) picks out an instance of (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLVariable).  Specifically, the expression (#$LocalVariableFn SENTENCE VARIABLE) picks out the #$CycLVariable VARIABLE based on its appearance in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENTENCE. Although, closely related to the syncategorematic 'function' #$Quote, #$LocalVariableFn is significantly different because of its relativization of VARIABLE to SENTENCE.   The primary utility of this function is for representing assertions about #$CycLSentences in a form that can be easily fed out to alternative representational systems that cannot support second-order representations.  The relativization of VARIABLE to SENTENCE allows us to unambiguously refer to the variables of one  #$CycLSentence, even if syntactically-identical variables appear in multiple #$CycLSentences. NOTE:  The first argument of this function is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to denote SENTENCE without VARIABLE being symbolically represented within that term.")
(comment literalVariable "An assertion of the form (#$literalVariable LIT VAR) states that the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLVariable) VAR is the value of an argument of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment ArgSentenceFn "An expression of the form (#$ArgSentenceFn ATOM SENT) is used to pick out an instance of #$CycLSentence based on its appearance as the value of an argument in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) ATOM. Specifically, it is used to denote the #$CycLSentence SENT with regard to its being the value of an argument of the #$CycLAtomicSentence represented by ATOM. Although closely related to the syncategorematic 'function' #$Quote, the expression (#$ArgSentenceFn ATOM SENT) does not denote SENT per se.  Instead, it refers to ATOM relativize to SENT.  The primary utility of this function is for representing assertions about #$CycLSentences in a form that can be easily fed out to alternative representational systems that cannot support second-order representations.  The contextualization of SENT relative to ATOM allows us to unambiguously refer to the elements of one #$CycLSentence, even if syntactically-identical elements appear in mulitple #$CycLSentences.  NOTE:  The first argument of this function is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to denote ATOM without it being the case that the term is an actual sentence that has SENT as the value of one of its argument.")
(comment literalArgSentence "An assertion of the form (#$literalArgSentence LIT SENTENCE) states that the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT has the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENTENCE as the value of one of its arguments.")
(comment SubSentenceFn "An expression of the form (#$SubSentenceFn SENTENCE SUB) is used to pick out an instance of  #$CycLAtomicSentence.  Specifically, it is used to denote the #$CycLAtomicSentence SUB with regard to its being a syntactic element of the canonical representation of the #$CycLSentence represented by the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENTENCE.  Although closely related to the syncategorematic 'function' #$Quote, the expression (#$SubSentenceFn SENTENCE SUB) does not denote SUB per se.  Instead, it serves to pick out SUB as a part of the canonical representation of the #$CycLSentence  SENTENCE.  The primary utility of this function is for representing assertions about #$CycL sentences in a form that can be easily fed out to alternative representational systems that cannot support second-order representations.  The contextualization of SUB relative to SENTENCE allows us to unambiguously refer to the elements of one #$CycLSentence, even if syntactically-identical elements appear in multiple #$CycLSentences. NOTE: The first argument of this function is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to refer to the relevant #$CycLSentence without the actual symbols of SUB appearing within SENT.")
(comment literalCDT "An assertion of the form (#$literalCDT LIT CDT) states that the #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerm CDT is the value of an argument of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT. The collection #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerm covers a number of significant collections for the #$CycL syntax, including #$CycLConstant, #$SubLAtomicTerm (for handling the representation of strings and numbers), and #$CycLNonAtomicReifiedTerm.")
(comment normalizedLiteral-Positive "An assertion of the form (#$normalizedLiteral-Positive SENTENCE LIT) states that when the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENTENCE is represented in either Conjunctive Normal Form or Disjunctive Normal Form, then one of its literals is (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT. Compare with #$normalizedLiteral-Negated.  If SENTENCE is itself a (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence), the assertion (#$normalizedLiteral-Positive SENTENCE SENTENCE) is true.")
(comment SentenceFn "#$SentenceFn is a function that is used to denote an instance of #$CycLSentence.  Semantically, this function is equivalent to an application of the syncategorematic 'function' #$Quote and then an applicaton of #$IdentityFn.  In short, an expression using the #$SentenceFn function denotes the same #$CycLSentence that is its first argument.  The primary utility of this function is for representing assertions about #$CycL sentences in a form that can be easily fed out to alternative representational systems that cannot support second-order representations.")
(comment representsVariableInSentence "An assertion of the form (#$representsVariableInSentence REP VARIABLE SENT) means that the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLVariable) REP 'represents' the #$CycLVariable VARIABLE that appears in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLSentence) SENT.  REP does not denote VARIABLE.  Instead, it is a relativized representation which considers VARIABLE as a syntactic element of SENT. This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$LocalVariableFn. NOTE:  The third argument of this predicate is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to denote SENT without it being the case that the symbols that compose VARIABLE appear within the symbols that compose SENT.")
(comment representsSentenceAsArgOfSentence "An assertion of the form (#$representsSentenceAsArgOfSentence REP SENT ATOM) means that the #$LocalVariableFn #$CycLSentence) REP represents the #$CycLSentence that is the value of one of the arguments of the #$CycLAtomicSentence ATOM.  REP does not denote exactly the same sentence as SENT, instead this is a relativized representation intended to refer to SENT as it appears within ATOM.  This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$ArgSentenceFn.  NOTE:  The third argument of this predicate is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to denote ATOM without it being the case the term is an actual sentence that has SENT as the value of one of its argument.")
(comment representsSentenceWithinSentence "An assertion of the form (#$representsSentenceWithinSentence REP  ATOM SENT-REP) states that that the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) REP represents the #$CycLAtomicSentence ATOM in relation to the #$CycLSentence represented by the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn SENT).  Specifically, ATOM is a syntactic element of SENT and REP does not represent ATOM per se, but represents ATOM as an element of SENT.  This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$SubSentenceFn. NOTE: The third argument of this predicate is not quoted so that it is possible to use a term to denote the relevant #$CycLSentence SENT without the actual symbols of ATOM appearing within SENT.")
(comment normalizedLiteral-Negated "An assertion of the form (#$normalizedLiteral-Negated SENTENCE LIT) states that when the #$CycLSentence SENTENCE is represented in either Conjunctive Normal Form or Disjunctive Normal Form, then one of its negated literals is the #$CycLAtomicSentence LIT.  Compare with #$normalizedLiteral-Positive")
(comment representsTheSentence "An assertion of the form (#$representsTheSentence REP SENTENCE) means that the #$CycLSentence REP is the #$CycLSentence  SENTENCE.  This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$SentenceFn.  NOTE:  The first argument of this predicate is not quoted, so that it is possible to use a term besides SENTENCE to represent SENTENCE.")
(comment literalHasRealNumberInArg "An assertion of the form (#$literalHasRealNumberInArg LIT NUMBER N) states that the #$RealNumber NUMBER is the value of the Nth argument in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment literalRealNumber "An assertion of the form (#$literalRealNumber LIT NUMBER) states that the #$RealNumber NUMBER is the value of an argument of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment literalNART "An assertion of the form (#$literalNART LIT NART) states that the #$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLNonAtomicReifiedTerm NART is the value of an argument of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment literalHasNARTInArg "An assertion of the form (#$literalHasNARTInArg LIT NART N) states that the  #$CycLNonAtomicReifiedTerm NART is the value of the Nth argument in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment literalHasConstantInArg "An assertion of the form (#$literalHasConstantInArg LIT CONST N) states that the #$CycLConstant CONST is the value of the Nth argument in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence )LIT.")
(comment literalConstant "An assertion of the form (#$literalConstant LIT CONST) states that the #$CycLConstant CONST is the value of an argument of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment representsRealNumber "An assertion of the form (#$representsRealNumber REP NUMBER) means that the #$RealNumber REP represents the #$RealNumber NUMBER.  The second argument is quoted, but the first argument is not.  Therefore, although (representsRealNumber (#$Quote NUMBER) NUMBER) is true, it is possible to have terms that differ from (#$Quote NUMBER) filling the first argument position.")
(comment literalString "An assertion of the form (#$literalString LIT STRING) states that the #$SubLString  STRING is the value of an argument of the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment representsNART "An assertion of the form (#$representsNART REP NART) means that the #$CycLNonAtomicReifiedTerm represents the #$
CycLNonAtomicReifiedTerm NART.  The second argument is quoted, but the first argument is not.  Therefore, although (representsNART (#$Quote NART) NART) is true, it is possible to have terms that differ from (#$Quote NART) filling the first argument position.")
(comment literalHasStringInArg "An assertion of the form (#$literalHasStringInArg LIT STRING N) states that the #$SubLString STRING is the value of the Nth argument in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment representsString "An assertion of the form (#$representsString REP STRING) means that the #$SubLString REP represents the #$SubLString
STRING.  The second argument is quoted, but the first argument is not.  Therefore, although (representsSTRING (#$Quote STRING) STRING) is true, it is possible to have terms that differ from (#$Quote STRING) filling the first argument position.")
(comment WordNetWorkflowStatus "The collection of WordNet workflow status collections.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ProposedCollection "The collection of ambiguous noun #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that are proposed #$Collections.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ProposedIndividual "The collection of ambiguous noun #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that are proposed #$Individuals.")
(disjointWith WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ProposedCollection WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ProposedIndividual)
(comment CycLObjectTypeFn "An expression of the form (#$CycLObjectTypeFn EXPRESSION-TYPE) denotes a sub-collection of #$CycLExpression.  #$CycLExpression and all of its sub-collections have the property #$quotedCollection.  However, there is some utility in having instances #$CycLExpression that refer to other #$CycLExpressions, even though they are syntactically different.  For example, let us assume that term (#$Quote #$Sentence212) was created to refer to the sentence (#$Quote (#$isa #$GeorgeWashington #$HomoSapiens)).  While the latter is an instance of the #$quotedCollection #$CycLClosedSentence, the former is not.  The #$CycLObjectTypeFn function allows us to create new, unquoted collections that allow for #$CycLExpressions to refer to other instances of #$CycLExpression.  For instance,  #$Sentence212 can be an instance of (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLClosedSentence).")
(comment cycLObjectTypeRepresentsType "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$CycLObjectTypeFn.")
(comment uninterestingArgInRelnForType "(#$uninterestingArgInRelnForType THING RELN NUM TYPE) means that for any instance of TYPE, any sentence about that instance that has an arg0 of RELN and has an arg NUM of THING, is uninteresting.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-DeterminedIndividual "The collection of ambiguous noun #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that are reviewed and are determined to be #$Individuals.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-DeterminedCollection "The collection of ambiguous noun #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that are reviewed and are determined to be #$Collections.")
(comment syntaxDataMtForProgram "#$syntaxDataMtForProgram relates a #$SKSISupportedDatabaseServerProgram to the #$DataMicrotheory used to describe aspects of its SQL syntax.")
(comment WNVerbFrame-2 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-1 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s\".")
(comment TransitiveGerundPPFrameType "Frames used for verbs appearing in the progressive aspect that have a single PP complement. Examples include 'Fred is looking at Steve', and 'The dog is sitting on the rug'.")
(comment literalHasCDTInArg "An assertion of the form (#$literalHasCDTInArg LIT TERM N) states that the  #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerm TERM is the value of the Nth argument in the (#$CycLObjectTypeFn #$CycLAtomicSentence) LIT.")
(comment VariableArityPredicate "A specialization of both #$Predicate
and #$VariableArityRelation (qq.v.).  Each instance 
of #$VariableArityPredicate is a predicate that can 
take a variable number of arguments. The degree 
of variability for a given such predicate can 
be constrained using the predicates #$arityMin 
and #$arityMax.  Examples of #$VariableArityPredicate 
include #$commutativeInArgs and #$different. Thus both '(#$different 1 2)' and '(#$different 1 2 3)' are syntactically well-formed.")
(comment HypothesizedAdjectiveSenseFn "(#$HypothesizedAdjectiveSenseFn WORD POS) denotes a hypothesized (and potentially underspecified) sense of WORD which is approriate for part of spech POS (where POS is restricted to be some spec of #$Adjective).  The results fo this Function can be used as semantic placeholders which may be refined as time,  interest, and project demands allow.")
(comment most-RelationFrom "<code>(#$most-RelationFrom BINPRED THING SOC)</code> means that most elements <code>ELEM</code> of <code>SOC</code> are such that <code>(BINPRED THING ELEM)</code>.  It is equivalent to the more complex form:
<pre>
(#$most SOC (#$TheSetOf ?OBJ (BINPRED THING ?OBJ))).
</pre>
When <code>SOC</code> is a #$Collection, use the more specialized predicate #$relationInstanceMost.")
(comment generateWithFormWhenArgInReln "(#$generateWithFormWhenArgInReln THING FORM ARGNUM RELN) means that any formula whose arg0 is RELN and whose ARGNUMth argument is THING should generate in natural language with a phrase whose head is of the word form FORM.  For example, (#$generateWithFormWhenArgInReln #$Deceased #$regularDegree 2 #$isa) means that a sentence of the form (#$isa FOO #$Deceased) should generate as \"FOO is deceased\" or \"FOO is dead,\" as opposed to something like \"FOO is a dead thing.\"")
(comment WNVerbFrame-4 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something is ----ing PP\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-3 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"It is ----ing\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-8 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-6 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s Adjective/Noun\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-7 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s Adjective\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-5 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s something Adjective/Noun\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-10 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s somebody\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-15 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s something to somebody\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-13 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s on something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-11 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-9 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-14 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-12 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s to somebody\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-19 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s something on somebody\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-17 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody with something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-20 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody PP\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-18 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody of something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-16 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s something from somebody\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-21 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s something PP\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-26 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s that CLAUSE\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-24 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody to INFINITIVE\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-22 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s PP\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-25 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody INFINITIVE\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-23 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody's (body part) ----s\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-28 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s to INFINITIVE\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-27 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s to somebody\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-29 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s whether INFINITIVE\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-30 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s somebody into V-ing something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-31 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s something with something\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-32 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s INFINITIVE\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-35 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Something ----s INFINITIVE\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-33 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"Somebody ----s VERB-ing\".")
(comment WNVerbFrame-34 "This is the WordNet verb frame exemplified by the sentence \"It ----s that CLAUSE\".")
(comment fosterChildren "(#$fosterChildren PARENT FOSTER-CHILD) holds just in case PARENT is a foster parent of FOSTER-CHILD.")
(comment RuralRegionFn "A unary function that denotes the (possibly) discontinuous region that is the sum of all the rural regions located in the argument.  For example, (#$RuralRegionFn #$Nebraska-State) denotes the discontinuous geographical region that consists of all the regions in Nebraska minus the urban areas.")
(comment polityHasRuralRegion "(#$polityHasRuralRegion POLITY RURAL-REGION) holds just in case RURAL-REGION is the (possibly) discontinuous geographical region that consists of the whole region of POLITY minus the urban areas.  The is the corresponding predicate to #$RuralRegionFn.")
(comment drugTherapySideEffects "(#$drugTherapySideEffects THERAPY-TYPE CONDITION) means that the instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType CONDITION is one of the possible side-effects of undergoing THERAPY-TYPE, a specialization of #$DrugTherapy.")
(comment shortTermDrugTherapySideEffects "(#$shortTermDrugTherapySideEffects THERAPY-TYPE CONDITION) means that the instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType CONDITION is one of the possible side-effects of undergoing THERAPY-TYPE, a specialization of #$DrugTherapy, for a short period of time.")
(comment longTermDrugTherapySideEffects "(#$longTermDrugTherapySideEffects THERAPY-TYPE CONDITION) means that the instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType CONDITION is one of the possible side-effects of undergoing THERAPY-TYPE, a specialization of #$DrugTherapy, for an extended period of time.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ReadyForPossibleMatching "The collection of #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that are ready for possible matching with Cyc concepts.")
(comment PersonTypeByNationality-Defunct "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$PersonTypeByNationality-Defunct is a #$PersonTypeByNationality whose corresponding #$Country (#$countryOfNationality) no longer exists (as a country).  Note that assertions of the form <code>(#$isa NATIONALITY #$PersonTypeByNationality-Defunct)</code> should be temporally qualified.  For example:
<pre>
Monadic Mt:     #$WorldPoliticalGeographyDataMt
Time Interval:  (#$IntervalStartedByFn (#$YearFn 1991))
Time Parameter: #$TimePoint
HL Formula:     (#$isa #$SovietUnionPerson #$PersonTypeByNationality-Defunct).")
(comment PlaqueStuff "The collection of all samples of plaque, a naturally occurring substance found in the mouth, composed of mucuous and food particles.  Plaque contains germs that can damage teeth and gums.")
(comment TartarStuff "The collection of all samples of hardened #$PlaqueStuff, typically removed from ones' teeth by a dentist.")
(comment IntentionallyPreventingOrganismsAdequateSleep "A specialization of (#$PreventionFn #$Sleeping),
#$HarmingAnAgent, and #$ControllingSomething. In each
instance of this collection, some agent intentionally prevents an
organism from receiving adequate sleep. Positive examples of this
collection include specializations in which scientists studying sleep
disorders intentionally keep test subjects from getting adequate sleep
or torture events where an agent is prevented from getting enough
sleep.  Negative examples of this collection would include new parents
prevented from sleep by an infant, as , presumably, the infant is not <i>intentionally</i> preventing the parents from sleeping.")
(comment Indoctrination-Script "A specialization of #$Education. Each instance of this
collection is the entire series of events in which one agent becomes
indoctrinated by another. Essentially, this event type requires that
the latter agent instructs the former in a particular point of view,
opinion, idea, belief, and so forth in order to convince him or her to
accept it as true, as well the acceptance of these views by the
instructed agent. See also #$IndoctrinationGoal.  This collection of
events requires the instruction of one agent by another.  Thus, for an
agent to search out information on his or her own and establish
beliefs in them would not be considered an instance of this collection.")
(comment SleepDeprivation "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of
this collection is a condition that results when an organism does not
sleep enough.  Positive examples of this collection include cases in
which someone is prevented from sleeping, for example, from loud
noises as well as the instances of #$SleepDeprivation that occur from
#$Insomnia.")
(comment SpiritualElitism "A specialization of #$PrideOfMembership.  Each instance of
this collection is feeling of pride associate with membership in a
particular religious group.")
(comment IncitingBeliefFervor "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction and #$Encouraging.
Each instance of this collection is an event in which one agent
incites belief fervor in one or more other agents.  Frequently the
type of belief is religious or political.")
(comment IndoctrinationGoal "A specialization of #$OrganizationalProsperityGoal. Each
instance of this collection is the goal one agent has in instructing
another agent on a particular point of view, opinion, idea, belief,
and so forth, in order to persuade them to accept it as true. Positive
examples of this collection include the indoctrination that occurs
with new members of a cult or terrorist group. Typically, this
collection has a negative connotation, like 'brainwashing,' but the
determination of something as 'indoctrination' can be considered
arbitary. Consider that some believe the D.A.R.E. program or
green ideology taught in American schools is indoctrination.")
(comment ControllingAnAgentsMediaExposure "A specialization of #$ControllingSomething.  Each instance
of this collection is an event that may span days up to years, in
which one agent intentionally limits the media to which another agent is
exposed.  Positive examples of this collection include the
subevents of sequestering a jury, in which the members of the jury are
prohibited from watching, reading, or listening to news about the
trial.  Another example of this collection includes the events in
which a parent limits a child's media exposure, like using the
V-chip to prevent the child from watching movies and shows at an R
rating.  In addition to preventing an agent from seeing undesired
media, specializations of this collection would include deliberate
exposure to desirous media.  For example, a conservative Christian
household may show children 'Veggie Tales' because it contains a
Christian message.")
(comment researches "This predicate relates an agent to a thing that it is currently researching, in the sense of thinking about the thing in a focused way in order to determine what some of its significant features are. <code>(#$researches AGENT THING)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is researching <code>THING</code>.")
(comment FosteringSpiritualElitism "A specialization of #$Encouraging and #$PurposefulAction.
Each instance of this collection is an event in which a religious
group encourages a sense of elitism among its members.")
(comment SigningOverOnesAssets "A specialization of #$HandingOverControlOfSomething and
#$LegalProceeding. Each instance of this collection is an transfer in
which one agent signs over his or her assets to another.")
(comment ExecutionStyleMurder "A specialization of #$Murder. Each instance of this
collection is an event in which an agent murders a person
'execution-style.' Execution-style may mean several things, but
essentially the idea is that an agent kills another in the manner that
someone might be put to death as in a #$Execution-Judicial.  A notable
specialization of this collection is #$ShootingSomeoneExecutionStyle,
and this collection may include murders by beheading, hanging,
burning, and so forth.")
(comment physicalFieldConversionFunction "#$physicalFieldConversionFunction is used by the SKSI web
integration code to specify the data-type level function which is used
to convert the raw 'web scraping' value for a physical field into a
more managable form for query evaluation. These functions are not
evaluated in Cyc, but are instead translated into their Java
equivalents and are implemented on the web server side. This permits
us to continue treating web sites as databases and moving as much of
the computational operation on to the server side query.")
(comment PFIAliasFn "#$PFIAliasFn is an unreifiable function which is used to
capture the SQL idiom 'AS', or the'table aliasing' capability, when
stating SKSI meaning sentences.")
(comment PsychologicalStressorType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection. Each instance of
this collection is also a collection of events in which the organism
in the #$performedBy or #$objectActedOn role, depending on the
collection, is under some amount of pyschological stress. The level of
stress experienced will depend on the event type as well as person
undergoing the experience. Notable instances of this collection would
include #$DischargeWithPrejudice and (#$ObservationOfFn #$Murder), and
notable specializations of this collection include types of torture
methods. Other positive examples would include the collections of
events in which a person engages in combat.")
(comment some "An instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-MonotoneIncreasing (q.v.).  <code>(#$some SETORCOL1 SETORCOL2)</code> means that at least one thing is an instance of both <code>SETORCOL1</code> and <code>SETORCOL2</code>.")
(disjointWith GeneralizedQuantifier-RightMonotone GeneralizedQuantifier-NonMonotone)
(comment IndoctrinationMethodType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection. Each instance of
this collection is a type of event that may be used as a method to
indoctrinate an instance of #$IntelligentAgent. Some of these methods
tend to lower an individual's resistance to the indoctrination and/or
to distract the individual from the process of indoctrination they are
undergoing, for example,
#$IntentionallyPreventingOrganismsAdequateSleep and #$Isolation. Or,
these methods may increase the individual's dependancy on the agent
preforming the indoctrination, like #$ControllingAnAgentsMediaExposure
and #$SigningOverOnesAssets.")
(comment groupUsesIndoctrinationMethod "<code>(#$groupUsesIndoctrinationMethod ORG
METHOD-TYPE)</code> means that <code>ORG</code> uses instances of
<code>METHOD-TYPE</code> to indoctrinate new members.<p> For example, (#$groupUsesIndoctrinationMethod #$AlQaida #$Isolation) means that Al-Qaida uses isolation as a method to indoctrinate its members.<p> Indoctrination methods would include those events that made the indoctrinated more susceptable to the group's message (for example, a restricted diet and sleep deprevation) as well as the direct indoctrination methods, like chanting group slogans or reading group propaganda.")
(comment BefriendingAnAgent "A specialization of #$ExpressingFriendship and
#$SocialOccurrence. Each instance of this collection is a event in
which one agent acts friendly toward another to establish a
friendship. Positive examples of this collection would include the
overtures made to a shy cat to befriend it as well as the approachs of
children on a playground to become friends.")
(comment ControllingAnOrganismsDiet "A specialization of #$ControllingSomething. Each instance of
this collection is an event in which the diet of one agent is
controlled by another agent. This collection is more restrictive than
one that which would include the suggested meal plans a nutritionist
gives a client, because the client could easily eat differently than
the suggested plan. Rather, this collection is the events in which an
organism's diet is controlled (almost) completely. Positive examples
would include the diet of a prisoner, who relies probably exclusively
on someone else for food and those animals maintained at zoos and
such. While organisms might rarely gain food some other way, for
example, if a patron of a zoo passed a chimp a banana, primarily the
chimp depends on the zookeepers for sustenance.")
(comment IndoctrinatedIntoIdeologyFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes for
its value an instance of #$BeliefSystem and returns the collection of
all #$IntelligentAgents that have been indoctrinated into that belief
system.  For example, (#$IndoctrinatedIntoIdeologyFn #$Communism)
denotes a specialization of #$IntelligentAgent, who have been
indoctrinated into #$Communism.  See also #$Indoctrination-Script.")
(comment agentTypeIndoctrinatedIntoIdeology "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation. (#$agentTypeIndoctrinatedIntoIdeology AGENT-TYPE DOCTRINE) means that the instances of AGENT-TYPE have been indoctrinated into believing DOCTRINE.  See also #$Indoctrination-Script.")
(comment agentBetterThanAtType "(#$agentBetterThanAtType GROUP1 GROUP2 EVENT-TYPE) means
that GROUP1 is considered better than GROUP2 at instances of
EVENT-TYPE.  For example, (#$agentBetterThanAtType #$DallasCowboys
#$WashingtonRedskins #$PenetratingADefense) means that the
#$DallasCowboys are considered better at instances of
#$PenetratingADefense than the #$WashingtonRedskins are.")
(comment relativelyFew "An instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  <code>(#$relativelyFew SOC1 SOC2)</code> means that the percentage of instances of <code>SOC1</code> that are instances of <code>SOC2</code> is relatively small, by some standard that is left implicit.  For example,
<p>
(a)  <code>(#$relativelyFew #$UnitedStatesPerson #$BuddhistPerson)</code>
<p>
means that relatively few Americans are Buddhists -- compared to, say, the percentage of people in the world who are Buddhists.  (In this case, the implicit comparison class is #$Person.)  This does not entail:
<p>
(b)  <code>(#$few #$UnitedStatesPerson #$BuddhistPerson)</code>,
<p>
for it might be true that relatively few Americans are Buddhists even if many Americans are Buddhists.
<p>
Moreover, (b) does not entail (a): consider the case in which few Americans are Buddhists, but <i>no one</i> of any other nationality is a Buddhist.  In that case, (b) would be true but (a) would be false.
<p>
See also #$relativelyFewComparedTo and #$relativelyFewComparedToType.")
(comment relativelyFewComparedTo "A ternary #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  <code>(#$relativelyFewComparedTo SOC1 SOC2 SOC3)</code> means that the percentage of instances of <code>SOC1</code> that are instances of <code>SOC2</code> is less than the percentage of instances of <code>SOC3</code> that are instances of <code>SOC2</code>.  For example,
<p>
<code>(#$relativelyFewComparedTo #$UnitedStatesPerson #$BuddhistPerson #$ChinesePerson)</code>
<p>
means that the percentage of Americans who are Buddhists is lower than the percentage of Chinese people who are Buddhists.  See also #$relativelyFew and #$relativelyFewComparedToType.")
(comment relativelyFewComparedToType "A ternary #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  <code>(#$relativelyFewComparedToType SOC1 SOC2 SOC3)</code> means that the percentage of instances of <code>SOC1</code> that are instances of <code>SOC2</code> is less than the percentage of instances of the average instance of <code>SOC3</code> that are instances of <code>SOC2</code>.  For example,
<p>
<code>(#$relativelyFewComparedToType #$UnitedStatesPerson #$BuddhistPerson #$PersonTypeByNationality)</code>
<p>
means that the percentage of Americans who are Buddhists is lower than the percentage of the average nationality who are Buddhists.  See also #$relativelyFew and #$relativelyFewComparedTo.")
(comment operatesInRegion-BroadestNaturalTerritory "<code>(#$operatesInRegion-BroadestNaturalTerritory AGENT REGION)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> performs (at least once) a task central to her/its job function or group mission in some region subsumed by the landmass of <code>REGION</code>.  For example, if a terrorist organization <code>ORG</code> operates only within the borders of a specific country <code>COUNTRY</code>, it would be correct to say <code>(#$operatesInRegion-BroadestNaturalTerritory ORG COUNTRY)</code>.  However, if <code>ORG</code> is not known to operate outside of <code>COUNTRY</code>, it would be wrong to say of the continent <code>CONTINENT</code> that subsumes <code>COUNTRY</code> that <code>(#$operatesInRegion-BroadestNaturalTerritory ORG CONTINENT)</code>.  Generally, it is not correct to say <code>(#$operatesInRegion-BroadestNaturalTerritory ORG #$PlanetEarth)</code>, since there is so much territory of the earth in which no agent operates.  Thus even for \"global\" organizations it is more proper to use this predicate to enumerate the specific contentents, islands, or seas in which the organization operates.")
(disjointWith GeographicalAgent Technology-Artifact)
(comment Technology-Artifact "The collection of all pieces of technology.  Instances are artifacts, typically devices and machines, but also computer programs and other constructed systems that are 1) the result of applying scientific knowledge to real-world problems, and 2) can be used as a tool in the construction of additional artifacts (e.g., technology, such as a bulldozer or a crane, used in the construction of a building) or in generating a desired state of affairs, such as the creation of an artificial environment (e.g., technology used in refrigeration). Note that there is a normative sense of the word \"technology\" that refers to new or relatively modern pieces of technology, which this this collection does not represent.")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrink Technology-Artifact)
(comment DecontaminationEquipment "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$DecontaminationEquipment is a deveice used for decontaminating people, areas, or opbjects that have been exposed to toxic substances.")
(comment ObservationOfTypeFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction and
#$TermMacroFunction which takes for its value a specialization of
#$TemporallyExistingThing, TYPE, and returns all instances of
#$Observing TYPE.  For example, (#$ObservationOfTypeFn #$Chimpanzee)
denotes all instances of observations such that the #$thingsObserved
are instances of #$Chimpanzee.")
(comment observationTypeOfType "(#$observationTypeOfType OBSERVING-TYPE THING-TYPE) means
that OBSERVING-TYPE, a specialization of #$Observing are the events in
which THING-TYPE.  ")
(comment HistoryDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$History-FieldOfStudy.")
(comment relationMostExists "A #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$relationMostExists BINPRED COL1 COL2)</code> means that #$most instances <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code> are such that for some instance <code>INST2</code> of <code>COL2</code>, <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to the more complex form
<pre>
(#$most COL1 (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn COL1 BINPRED COL2)).
</pre>
For example, <code>(#$relationMostExists #$owns #$Musician #$MusicalInstrument)</code> means that most musicians own a musical instrument.  See also #$relationMostInstance.")
(comment relationMostInstance "A #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$relationMostInstance BINPRED COL THING)</code> means that #$most instances <code>INST</code> of <code>COL</code> are such that <code>(BINPRED INST THING)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to the more complex form:
<pre>
(#$most COL (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn COL BINPRED THING)).
</pre>
For example, <code>(#$relationMostInstance #$knowsAbout #$Philosopher #$Aristotle)</code> means that most philosophers know about Aristotle.  See also #$relationMostExists.")
(comment relationExistsMost "A #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$relationExistsMost BINPRED COL1 COL2)</code> means that #$most instances <code>INST2</code> of <code>COL2</code> are such that for some instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to the more complex form
<pre>
(#$most COL2 (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn COL2 BINPRED COL1)).
</pre>
For example, (#$relationExistsMost #$owns #$Millionaire #$Mansion) means that most mansions are owned by millionaires.  See also #$relationInstanceMost.")
(comment Projection-CW "A specialization of #$Prediction-CW.  Instances of
#$Projection-CW are predictions which are based on extrapolation from
current conditions and/or trends.")
(comment requires-Underspecified "A binary #$UnderspecifiedPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$requires-Underspecified THING REQUIREMENT)</code> means that there is some sense in which <code>THING</code> requires, needs, depends on, or is conditional upon <code>REQUIREMENT</code>.  See the many specializations of #$requires-Underspecified for the range of senses that this is meant to cover.")
(comment relationInstanceMost "A #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$relationInstanceMost BINPRED THING SOC)</code> means that #$most instances <code>INST</code> of <code>SOC</code> are such that <code>(BINPRED THING INST)</code>.  It is equivalent to the more complex form
<pre>
(#$most SOC (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn SOC BINPRED THING)).
</pre>
For example, <code>(#$relationInstanceMost #$hasBeenIn #$TonyBlair #$EuropeanCountry)</code> means that Tony Blair has been in most European countries (i.e. most European countries are such that Tony Blair has been in them).  See also #$relationMostInstance.")
(comment SubLExpressionType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$SubLExpressionType is a type (i.e. a subcollection) of SubLSExpression.")
(comment creationTemplateMembers "(#$creationTemplateMembers TEMPLATE TERM) means that TERM is one of the terms that forms the instance of #$CycCreationTemplate, TEMPLATE.  If TERM is a FORT, this means that the code-level function associated with TEMPLATE (see #$creationTemplateForSUBLFunction) is responsible for the reification of an analogous FORT.  If TERM is an assertion, the code-level function is responsible for adding an analogous assertion to the KB.")
(comment creationTemplateFORTs "(#$creationTemplateFORTs TEMPLATE FORT) means that FORT is an exemplar such that the code-level function associated with TEMPLATE (see #$creationTemplateForSUBLFunction) is responsible for reifying an analogous term when it is called.  For information about how creation templates are used, see the #$comment on #$CycCreationTemplate.  See also #$creationTemplateAssertions.")
(comment CreationTemplateMicrotheory "The collection of all instances of #$ApplicationContext that contain assertions that describe the structure of instances of #$CycCreationTemplate.  Each instances of #$CycCreationTemplate should have its own instance of #$CreationTemplateMicrotheory, to which it bears the relation #$creationTemplateMt. ")
(comment CreationTemplatesMt "The common #$genlMt for all instances of #$CreationTemplateMicrotheory.  This microtheory contains general rules for describing or inferring properties of instances of #$CycCreationTemplate.")
(comment creationTemplateMt "(#$creationTemplateMt TEMPLATE MT) identifies MT as the instance of #$CreationTemplateMicrotheory that contains the assertions that define the instance of #$CycCreationTemplate TEMPLATE.")
(comment programActionTypeRules "(#$programActionTypeRules PROCESS RULE) means that the instance RULE of #$CycRelatedProgramAction is relevant for inferencing in performances of PROCESS, a type of #$CycRelatedProgramAction.  Specifically, (#$programActionTypeRules PROCESS RULE) tells the system to consider RULE when performing a PROCESS.  Where the complete extent of #$programActionTypeRules is known for PROCESS (see #$completeExtentDecidableForValueInArg), the set of possible values of RULE form a closed set of all and only rules that will be used in inference during a performance of an instance of PROCESS.")
(comment programActionTypeTemplate "(#$programActionTypeTemplate PROCESS TEMPLATE) identifies TEMPLATE as the instance of #$CycCreationTemplate that can be used to evaluate and optimize any instance of PROCESS, a type of #$CycRelatedProgramAction.  For more information on how creation templates are used, see the #$comment on #$CycCreationTemplate.")
(comment linkingSentence "#$linkingSentence relates a #$LinkViaBinaryPredicate with an
#$AspatialInformationStore which expresses the content, or meaning of
the link.")
(comment CycLVariableList "A subcollection of #$SubLList, each instance of of which is an expression consisting of a sequence of Variables enclosed in parentheses. ")
(comment creationTemplateAllowableRules "(#$creationTemplateAllowableRules TEMPLATE RULE) means that the instance RULE of #$CycLRuleAssertion may be considered when calling the code-level function associated with TEMPLATE, an instance of #$CycCreationTemplate.  When the complete extent of #$creationTemplateAllowableRules is known for TEMPLATE, only those rules in the extent will be considered.  For more information about how creation templates are used, see the #$comment on

#$CycCreationTemplate.")
(comment PostNominalAdjFrame "Frames for adjectives that can be used postpositively, following nouns, like 'akimbo' in 'Sally stood, arms akimbo, refusing to move.'.")
(comment PostPronominalAdjFrame "Frames for adjectives that can be used postpositively, following indefinite pronouns, like 'useful' in 'Please bring me something useful.'.")
(comment PostNominalOnlyAdjFrame "Frames for adjectives that can *only* be used postpositively, following nouns, like 'proper' as in 'Taxes are collected from residents of the city proper.'.")
(comment CivilServant "A specialization of #$GovernmentEmployee.  Each instance of #$CivilServant is a person who is employed by a government department or agency.  Instances of #$CivilServant include, but are not limited to, government interpretors, cartographers, and administrators.  Note that some public sector employees are not #$CivilServants, for example, elected officials, diplomats, and military personnel.")
(disjointWith CivilServant ElectedOfficial)
(disjointWith Diplomat CivilServant)
(comment FileOnSystemAtFn "An expression of the form (#$FileOnSystemAtFn COMP PATH) denotes the #$HostedComputerFile that can be found on the #$ComputationalSystem COMP at the location denoted by the #$SubLString PATH.")
(comment isFileOnSystemAt "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$FileOnSystemAtFn.")
(comment stringIsRepresentedByAssertion "An expression of the form (#$stringIsRepresentedByAssertion STRING ASSERT) relates an instance of #$CycLAssertion to an instance of #$SubLString.")
(comment fileFromURI "An assertion of the form (#$fileFromURI FILE URI) means that the #$ComputerFile-Abstract FILE is a copy of the file that is located at the #$UniformResourceIdentifier URI.  This is a #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation.")
(comment fileFromStringOnEngine "An assertion of the form (#$fileFromStringOnEngine FILE STRING ENGINE) means that the #$ComputerFile-Abstract FILE represents a result that was generated during an internet search that used the #$SubLString STRING as its search string with the #$SearchEngine ENGINE.")
(comment LinkingTogether "A specialization of #$Event. Each instance of #$LinkingTogether is an event in which two or more things are linked or associated, e.g., in a physical configuration (see #$ConfiguringEvent) or, e.g, in a mental event (see #$DeterminingInterrelationship).")
(comment linkedThing "<code>(#$linkedThing LINKING THING)</code> means that in the linking together event, <code>LINKING</code>, one of the things linked is <code>THING</code>.")
(comment frequentsLocation "<code>(#$frequentsLocation AGENT LOCATION)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is a regular or frequent visitor to the place, <code>LOCATION</code>.  For example, <code>(#$frequentsLocation #$WoodyAllen #$CentralParkNY)</code> means that Woody Allen is a regular visitor of Central Park.")
(disjointWith ExternalAnimalBodyRegionType InternalAnimalBodyRegionType)
(comment PhysicalAttackWithMeleeWeapons "The collection of actions which are attacks using melee weapons (e.g. clubs, knives, cat o' nine tails, etc.).  Instances of this collection can be performed either by individual persons or by groups or organizations of persons.")
(comment CharlesRiver "A #$River in in eastern #$Massachusetts-State that empties into #$BostonHarbor and that separates #$CityOfCambridgeMA from #$CityOfBostonMA.")
(comment EarthRadius-Mean "The average distance from the center of the #$PlanetEarth to
the surface, where the average is taken over all points on the globe.
Equivalently, the radius of the hypothetical perfect sphere with the
same surface area as the #$PlanetEarth. Approximately ((#$PerFn #$Mile #$Radian) 3959).")
(comment EarthRadius-QuadraticMean "The 'quadratic mean radius' of the earth, which is given by
the formula (3a^2 + b^2)^1/2 / 2, where 'a' is the equatorial radius
of the #$PlanetEarth (#$EarthRadius-Equatorial) and 'b' is the polar
radius of the #$PlanetEarth (#$EarthRadius-Polar). It is approximately equal to ((#$PerFn #$Mile #$Radian) 3960).")
(comment EarthRadius-Polar "The radius of the #$PlanetEarth at the #$NorthPoleOfEarth, approximately ((#$PerFn #$Mile #$Radian) 3950).")
(comment GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn "#$GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn is an #$IntermediateVocabTerm; it should be used only in NL applications and not for purposes of representation.  (#$GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn STRING GEOPOL) applied to a (quoted) #$ProperNameString STRING which is the name of a #$GeopoliticalEntity in region GEOPOL returns the #$GeopoliticalEntity in that region with that name.  Examples: (#$GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn \"Budapest\" #$Hungary); (#$GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn \"North Tripura\" #$India);  (#$GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn \"Austin\" #$Texas-State); (#$GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn \"Austin\" #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica).")
(comment SocialBeliefSystem "A specialization of #$BeliefSystem.  Each instance of this
collection is a system of beliefs that deals with human society,
how it should be organized, or how human interactions should take
place.  Notable instances include #$Sexism and #$Feminism.")
(comment PrisonGuard "The collection of individuals who work as prison guards.")
(comment mtCardinality "(#$mtCardinality MT N) means that there are N assertions in the currently represented extent of the #$Microtheory MT.")
(comment mtCardinalityForTerm "(#$mtCardinalityForTerm MT TERM N) means that there are N assertions in the currently represented extent of the #$Microtheory MT that reference the #$CycLTerm TERM.")
(comment CrewChief "The collection of all non-commissioned officers in military services who are in charge of the crew that is responsible for maintaining military aircraft.")
(comment supervisesInAction "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate and a specialization of #$temporallySubsumes.  <code>(#$supervisesInAction AGT ACTION)</code> means that <code>ACTION</code> is the #$PurposefulAction being supervised by the agent <code>AGT</code>.")
(comment aideDeCamp "A #$PersonalAssociationPredicate and specialization of #$hasAssistants.  <code>(#$aideDeCamp SUP SUB)</code> means that <code>SUB</code> is an \"aide-de-camp,\" or personal military assistant, to <code>SUP</code>.")
(comment objectContaminatedInAttack "An #$ActorSlot that relates a #$TerroristAttack to a #$PartiallyTangible that is contaminated in (some proper subevent of) that attack.")
(comment possibleIntendedAttackTargets "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an #$AttackOnObject to a #$PartiallyTangible.  <code>(#$possibleIntendedAttackTargets ATTACK OBJECT)</code> means that <code>OBJECT</code> may have been an intended target of <code>ATTACK</code> -- that is, some relevant agent or source has reason to believe that <code>(#$intendedAttackTargets ATTACK OBJECT)</code> is true.  (Note that the relevant notion of possibility here is an epistemic one.)")
(comment coConspirators "A symmetric #$PersonalAssociationPredicate and specialization of #$collaborators.  <code>(#$coConspirators AGT1 AGT2)</code> means that for some instance <code>CONSPIRE</code> of #$ConspiringToDoSomething, <code>AGT1</code> and <code>AGT2</code> are both #$deliberateSocialParticipants in <code>CONSPIRE</code>.")
(comment NationalConference-PoliticalParty "An instance of #$PoliticalParty.  This party is focused in
the region of #$JammuAndKashmir-StateIndia.")
(comment ChiefMinister-HeadOfGovernment "A specialization of #$ElectedOfficial, #$Minister-Governmental, and
#$HeadOfGovernment.  Each instance of this collection is a the elected
head of a British overseas territory, which is self-governed.
Additionally, the title is found in some former UK territories like
Australia and India.")
(comment Superintendent-Police "A specialization of both #$LawEnforcementOfficer and
#$Supervisor. Each instance of this collection is a person charged
with oversight of part of a law enforcement organization.")
(comment USAgencyForInternationalDevelopment "An instance of #$USFederalGovernmentAgency.  This agency
assists countries to recover from disasters, to relieve poverty, and
to aid democratic reforms.")
(disjointWith SelfEmployedWorker FreelanceWorker)
(disjointWith Employee FreelanceWorker)
(comment FreelanceWorker "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance
of this collection is a person that does particular pieces of work of
different organizations.")
(comment FlagOfFreedomOrganization "An instance of #$PoliticalOrganizaiton based in #$Iran that
promotes democratic change in that country.")
(comment CentralReservePoliceForce-India "An instance of #$MilitaryOrganization.  The
#$CentralReservePoliceForce-India has the role of the striking reserve
to assist local police forces in police operations to maintain law and
order and contain insurgencies.")
(comment SamataParty "An instance of #$PoliticalParty in #$India.  This party
split from the #$JanataDalParty in 1994.  It's leader is George
Fernandes.")
(comment JanataDalParty "An instance of #$PoliticalParty based in #$India.  The
#$JanataDalParty broke from the Janata Party.  This party has been a
part of a number of coalitions in India's recent political history.")
(comment TelanganaRashtraSamiti "An instance of #$PoliticalParty in #$India.")
(comment TribalYouthFederation "An instance of #$PoliticalOrganization formed in 1967 and is
affiliated with the Democratic Youth Federation of India.  This group organizes youth from the tribal populations of #$Tripura-StateIndia.")
(comment WordNetSynsetWorkflowStatus "The collection of WordNet synset workflow status collections.")
(disjointWith WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ProposedIndividual WordNetSynsetImportStatus-UndeterminedIndividual)
(disjointWith WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ProposedCollection WordNetSynsetImportStatus-UndeterminedIndividual)
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-UndeterminedIndividual "The collection of ambiguous proper noun #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that might be #$Individuals.")
(comment RequiredPredicateForFunctionalTemplate "A collection of predicates that govern the behavior of #$FormulaTemplates. A #$FormulaTemplate requires an assertion on each of these predicates in order to function in the Fact Entry Tool. Templates missing an assertion on onw or more of these predicates will not function, and may crash the tool.")
(comment MotleyFoolUK-Website "The Motley Fool UK site.")
(comment TheMotleyFoolUKCorpusMt "The microtheory in which assertions made as part of the MotleyFool domain ontologization effort go.")
(comment GeneralizedQuantifier-CoIntersective "A #$PredicateType ans a specialization of #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  A generalized quantifier <code>QUANT</code> is an instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-CoIntersective just in case knowing what things are elements of <code>SOC1</code> but not of <code>SOC2</code> -- that is, knowing the extent of <code>(#$SetOrCollectionDifferenceFn SOC1 SOC2)</code> -- is sufficient to determine the truth value of <code>(QUANT A B)</code>.  The most notable instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Intersective is #$subsetOf.  Other (non-reified) examples include \"all but three\" and \"every ___ but John\".  Non-instances include #$some, #$many, #$few, and #$most.")
(comment GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional "A #$PredicateType and a specialization of #$GeneralizedQuantifier. A generalized quantifier QUANT is an instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional just in case it expresses a proportional quantificational relationship between sets or collections.
<p>
A <i>binary</i> generalized quantifier BIN-QUANT is a #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional just in case the truth value of (BIN-QUANT SOC1 SOC2) is determined by the proportion of elements of SOC1 that are instances of SOC2. Notable instances of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional include #$most and #$half.  #$subsetOf, #$no, and #$some are included as limiting cases, since they are equivalent to \"exactly 100%\", \"exactly 0%\", and \"not 0%\", respectively. Other (non-reified) examples include \"fewer than half\" and \"four out of five\". Non-instances include #$aFew, #$many, and #$both.")
(comment setOrCollectionIntersection2 "<code>(#$setOrCollectionIntersection2 INT SOC1 SOC2)</code> means that <code>INT</code> is the intersection of <code>SOC1</code> and <code>SOC2</code>.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$SetOrCollectionIntersection2Fn (q.v.).")
(comment typeAssociatedPaymentPlan "An assertion of the form (#$typeAssociatedPaymentPlan TENDER-TYPE PAYMENT-TYPE) states that the use of an instances of the collection TENDER-TYPE, some sub-collection of #$FinancialAccountTenderObject requires that the owner of the card repay such expenditures according to PAYMENT-TYPE, some sub-collection of #$PaymentSchedule.")
(comment instrumentTypeForEventType "An assertion of the form (#$instrumentTypeForEventType ARTIFACT-TYPE EVENT-TYPE) means that the sub-collection of #$Artifact ARTIFACT-TYPE has been designed to play an instrumental role or otherwise be used in instances of EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment UnrunnableQuery "The collection of all queries that are currently unrunnable because they crash the system when run. Since no query should be permitted to crash the system, these all trigger some bug which should be fixed.  Consequently, membership in this collection should be temporary until these various bugs get fixed.")
(comment OverdrawingABankAccount-Authorized "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount-Authorized is an instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount that is authorized by the administrator (#$accountAdministrator) of the account.  See also #$OverdrawingABankAccount-Unauthorized.")
(comment OverdrawingABankAccount-Unauthorized "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount-Unauthorized is an instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount that is not authorized by the administrator (#$accountAdministrator) of the account.  See also #$OverdrawingABankAccount-Authorized.")
(disjointWith OverdrawingABankAccount-Authorized OverdrawingABankAccount-Unauthorized)
(comment CreditCardInsurance "#$CreditCardInsurance is a specialization of #$InsurancePlan.
Each instance of #$CreditCardInsurance is an agreement in
which the #$insuredAgent is covered for activities that involve the
use of a credit card, such as carrying a balance or making purchases.")
(comment CreditCardAgreement "A specialization of #$Loan-WrittenLegalAgreement.  Each instance of #$CreditCardAgreement is an agreement between a creditcard hoplder and a credit card issuer, whereby the holder is granted, under specified terms, a #$CreditCardAccount by the issuer.")
(comment DefaultingOnCreditCard "A specialization of #$DefaultingOnLoan in which the loan defaulted on
is an instance of #$CreditCardAgreement.")
(comment OverdrawingABankAccount-InterestFree "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$OverdrawingABankAccount-Authorized.  Each instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount-InterestFree is an instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount such that the amount of money overdrawn is not subject to interest.  See also #$OverdrawingABankAccount-InterestFree.")
(comment OverdrawingABankAccount-SubjectToInterest "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount-SubjectToInterest is an instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount such that the amount of money overdrawn is subject to interest.")
(disjointWith OverdrawingABankAccount-InterestFree OverdrawingABankAccount-SubjectToInterest)
(comment contractedFormOfWord "(#$contractedFormOfWord ?WORD ?SHORT-FORM means that the word unit ?SHORT-FORM holds syntactic forms which are shortened versions of forms of ?WORD.")
(comment TransferringACreditCardBalance "A specialization of #$MoneyTransfer.  Each instance of #$TransferringACreditCardBalance is an event in which an agent transfers his or her credit card balance on one card to another.")
(comment LowCreditCardInterestRateEnthusiast "#$LowCreditCardInterestRateEnthusiast is an instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$LowCreditCardInterestRateEnthusiast is a person, sometimes known as a \"rate tart\", who who moves their credit card balance between providers with introductory offers of 0% interest for a set period.")
(comment CreditCard-RevolvingAccount "A specialization of #$CreditCard and an instance of #$CreditCardTypeByBalanceCarryFeature.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card that allows one to carry a balance from month to month.  Most, if not all, charge some sort of interest on any balance carried over from the previous month.  Contrast this with 
#$CreditCard-NonRevolvingAccount which are credit cards in which the balance must be paid off each month.")
(disjointWith CreditCard-RevolvingAccount CreditCard-NonRevolvingAccount)
(comment CreditCard-NonRevolvingAccount "A specialization of #$CreditCard and an instance of #$CreditCardTypeByBalanceCarryFeature.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card which the user must pay off the balance each month.  The most famous example of this sort of credit card is the American Express card (#$AmExCard).  Contrast this with #$CreditCard-RevolvingAccount.")
(comment overdraftCharge "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot and specialization of #$bankCharge that relates an instance of #$OverdrawingABankAccount to a #$MonetaryValue.  <code>(#$overdraftCharge OVERDRAFT MV)</code> means that the the charge to the customer for <code>OVERDRAFT</code> is <code>MV</code>.")
(comment arrangementFee "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot and specialization of #$bankCharge that relates an instance of #$ArrangingForSomething to a #$MonetaryValue.  <code>(#$arrangementFee ARRANGE MV)</code> means that the the charge to the customer for <code>ARRANGE</code> is <code>MV</code>.")
(comment prefixSubstring "A spec pred of #$substring, (#$prefixSubstring PREFIX
STRING) is true iff i) PREFIX is a #$substring of STRING and PREFIX
occurs at the beginning of STRING. For example, (#$prefixSubstring
\"lazy\" \"lazy dog\") is true whereas (#$prefixSubstring \"zy do\"
\"lazy dog\") is false. See also #$suffixSubstring.")
(comment suffixSubstring "A spec pred of #$substring, (#$suffixSubstring SUFFIX
STRING) is true iff i) PREFIX is a #$substring of STRING and SUFFIX
occurs at the end of STRING. For example, (#$suffixSubstring
\"dog\" \"lazy dog\") is true whereas (#$suffixSubstring \"zy do\"
\"lazy dog\") is false. See also #$prefixSubstring.")
(comment PFAliasFn "#$PFAliasFn is an unreifiable function which is used to
capture the SQL idiom 'AS', or the'table aliasing' capability, when
stating #$resultSetCardinality and #$resultSetCardinalityWithConstraints GAFs.")
(comment CreditCardAgreementWithZeroPercentInitialInterestRate "#$CreditCardAgreementWithZeroPercentInitialInterestRate is a specialization of #$CreditCardAgreement.  It is, of course, the collection of credit card agreements that offer card holders a zero percent initial interest rate.")
(comment BankAccountStatement-Hardcopy "A #$FirstOrderCollection and specialization of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject.  Each instance of #$BankAccountStatement-Hardcopy is a #$BankAccountStatement that is issued in hardcopy format (usually on paper).  Instances of #$BankAccountStatement-Hardcopy are typically mailed to account holders on a monthly, quarterly, or annual basis.")
(comment BankAccountStatement-Online "A #$FirstOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$BankAccountStatement-Online is a #$BankAccountStatement that is online; typically, the account holder can access the statement at any time by logging on to the bank's website.")
(disjointWith BankAccountStatement-Hardcopy BankAccountStatement-Online)
(comment BankAccountStatement-Monthly "A #$FirstOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$BankAccountStatement-Monthly is a #$BankAccountStatement that details bank transactions occurring within a particular one-month period.")
(comment BankAccountStatement-Historical "A #$FirstOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$BankAccountStatement-Historical is a #$BankAccountStatement that details the history of transactions on a bank account -- perhaps up to some specified limit, e.g. one year.")
(disjointWith BankAccountStatement-Monthly BankAccountStatement-Historical)
(comment EuropeanStockExchange "A specialization of #$StockExchange.  Each instance of
#$EuropeanStockExchange is a stock exchange headquartered in a
European country.")
(comment LoanAgreementWithZeroPercentInitialInterestRate "#$LoanAgreementWithZeroPercentInitialInterestRate is a specialization of #$LoanAgreement.  It is, of course, the collection of loan agreements that offer a zero percent initial interest rate.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-UndeterminedCollection "The collection of ambiguous proper noun #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that might be #$Collections.")
(comment InternetActivity "The collection of all activities that involve the #$Internet as an #$instrument-Generic.")
(comment debtFromObject "An assertion of the form (#$debtFromObject DEBT OBJ) means that the #$PaymentObligation DEBT was created based on the acquisition or use of the #$SomethingExisting OBJ.")
(comment EPIC-FinancialIDString "A subcollection of #$UniqueID, an EPIC stands for Exchange Price Information Code, and is used to represent the companies listed on the #$LondonStockExchange.")
(comment KeepingMoneyInAnAccount "A sub-collection of #$Banking.  These are situations in which someone stores some amount of #$MonetaryValue via a #$BankAccount with some #$FinancialOrganization.  This is a more general type of situation than saving and can include such things as maintaining a checking account, etc.")
(comment AvoidingSomething "Intentionally avoiding something.  In general, avoidance of a thing may entail limiting proximity to and/or familiarity with the   object in question..")
(comment websiteSupportsActivityType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$WebSite to a specialization of #$HumanActivity.  (#$websiteSupportsActivityType SITE ACT-TYPE) means that people can engage in instances of ACT-TYPE on SITE.  For example, (#$websiteSupportsActivityType #$EBay-WebSite #$Auctioning) means that people can engage in auctioning on the eBay website.")
(comment MonitoringOfFinancialAssetTypeFn "A unary #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes a specialization of #$FinancialAsset and returns a specialization of #$Monitoring.  (#$MonitoringOfFinancialAssetTypeFn ASSET-TYPE) denotes the collection of all events in which an agent monitors the status of an instance of ASSET-TYPE.")
(comment Stock-UK "Each instance of #$Stock-UK is an instance of #$Stock that is (or can be) traded on one a British stock exchange, e.g. the #$LondonStockExchange.")
(comment CollectivelyManagedFundOrganization "A specialization of #$InvestmentOrganization.  Each instance of #$CollectivelyManagedFundOrganization is an organization which manages funds collectively for a large pool of investors.  Noteable specializations include #$MutualFund and #$UnitTrust.")
(comment SharesInFundTypeFn "A unary #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes a specialization of #$CollectivelyManagedFundOrganization and returns a specialization of #$CollectivelyManagedFundOrganizationShare.  (#$SharesInFundTypeFn FUND-TYPE) denotes the collection of all shares in instances of FUND-TYPE.  For example, (#$SharesInFundTypeFn #$MutualFund) is the collection of all shares in mutual funds.  See also #$SharesInFundFn.")
(comment situationTypeStages "(situationTypeStages SIT-TYPE LIST) means that LIST is an ordered list of specializations of #$Situation, such that each element of LIST is known to be a #$properSubSituationTypes of SIT-TYPE, such that the ordering of LIST corresponds to the temporal ordering of of sub-situation types scripted via #$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType, and such that, for any two successive elements of LIST, MEMBER1 and MEMBER2, it isn't the case that there exists a MEMBER-MID such that (properSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE MEMBER-MID) and such that (startsAfterEndOfInSituationType SIT-TYPE MEMBER-MID MEMBER1) and (#$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType SIT-TYPE MEMBER2 MEMBER-MID) (i.e., any two successive elements of the list are immediate successors with respect to SIT-TYPE.")
(comment situationTypeStages-Maximal "(#$situationTypeStages-Maximal SIT-TYPE LIST) means that LIST is the complete list of all situation types that are known to be #$properSubSituationTypes of SIT-TYPE, appearing in the order, from left to right, that corresponds to the temporal ordering specified by the 'script' of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment situationTypeStages-ForRole "Where LIST is a list such that each element is a list consisting of a situation type and a #$BinaryRolePredicate, (#$situationTypeStages-ForRole SIT-TYPE ROLE LIST) means that in normal circumstances, any agent that plays the role ROLE in an instance of SIT-TYPE will play each of the roles appearing the elements of list, in situations of the types that appear with them, and in the temporal order given by LIST.  Thus, for example, (#$situationTypeStages-ForRole #$ContractKill-Simple #$directingAgent (#$TheList (#$TheList #$EmployeeHiring #$hiringAgent) (#$TheList #$Murder #$beneficiary) (#$TheList #$PayingForServices #$fromPossessor)))) means that in a #$ContractKill-Simple, the #$directingAgent hires somebody (is the #$hiringAgent in an #$EmployeeHiring), benefits from the Murder (is the #$beneficiary in a #$Murder), and makes a payment (is the #$fromPossessor in a #$PayingForServices).")
(comment situationTypeStages-ForRole-Maximal "(#$situationTypeStages-ForRole-Maximal SIT-TYPE ROLE LIST) means that LIST gives a complete listing of all the roles that an agent playing the role ROLE in SIT-TYPE will play, together with the situation types in which s/he plays them, in the temporal order in which they are played.")
(comment CreatingAComputerPassword "The collection of all events in which a user creates a password as directed by the authentication protocols of some computer program, to be used in future #$AuthenticationEvents.  Note that this collection should not be confused with #$EnteringAComputerPassword, wherein a pre-existing password is entered in an #$AuthenticationEvent.")
(comment CorporateBond-Agreement "A specialization of #$Bond-Agreement.  Each instance of #$CorporateBond-Agreement is a debt obligation issued by a public or private institution.")
(disjointWith MunicipalBond-Agreement CorporateBond-Agreement)
(comment TransitivePPGenericFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly
one complement, a PP. In HPSG terms: [COMPS <PP>]. Example: 'Fred went
to the store'. Note that we have the vocabulary to specify which
preposition heads the phrase -- (#$PPCompFrameFn #$TransitivePPCompFrame
#$To-TheWord). Use this frame when the assertion needs to be made
generically.")
(comment TransitivePPGenericFrame "This frame is used for transitive 
words that take exactly
one complement, a PP. In HPSG terms: [COMPS 
<PP>]. Example: 'Fred went
to the store'. Note that we have the 
vocabulary to specify which
preposition heads the phrase -- 
(#$PPCompFrameFn #$TransitivePPCompFrame
#$To-TheWord). Use this frame when the 
assertion needs to be made
generically.")
(comment monitoringTypeOfFinancialAssetType "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a specialization of #$FinancialAsset to a specialization of #$Monitoring.  (#$monitoringTypeOfFinancialAssetType ASSET-TYPE MONITOR-TYPE) means that MONITOR-TYPE is the collection of all #$Monitoring events in which an instance of ASSET-TYPE is monitored.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$MonitoringOfFinancialAssetTypeFn (q.v.).")
(comment ArgQuotedIsaTernaryPredicate "A specialization of #$ArgQuotedIsaPredicate (q.v.). Each instance of #$ArgQuotedIsaTernaryPredicate. is a ternary predicate used to place an \"quoted isa\" constraint on (and thereby specify an argument-type for) one or more argument-places of a relation. To be more precise, each instance PRED of #$ArgQuotedIsaTernaryPredicate takes a #$Relation RELN as its first argument, a #$NonNegativeInteger N as its second argument, and a #$SubLExpressionType collection COL as its third argument. PRED places an \"quoted isa\" constraint on RELN's Nth argument-place that is based on COL, so that a ground atomic sentence (GAF) of the form (RELN ARG1..ARGN..) is semantically well-formed only if ARGN is a quoted instance of COL. (Note that if N = 0 then this same constraint is placed on _all_ of RELN's argument-places. An important instance of #$ArgQuotedIsaTernaryPredicate is #$argQuotedIsa.")
(comment averageAppreciationRate "<code>(#$averageAppreciationRate INVESTMENT RATE)</code> means that <code>INVESTMENT</code> (an instance of #$InvestmentVehicle) appreciates at the rate <code>RATE</code>.  Assertions using this predicate should be asserted in the appropriately temporally qualified context.")
(comment averageAppreciationRateOfType "(#$averageAppreciationRateOfType INVESTMENT-TYPE RATE) means that all
instances of INVESTMENT-TYPE (a specialization of #$InvestmentVehicle)
average an appreciation of RATE.")
(comment averageAppreciationRateOfType "(#$averageAppreciationRateOfType INVESTMENT-TYPE RATE) means that all instances of INVESTMENT-TYPE (a specialization of #$InvestmentVehicle) average an appreciation of RATE.  Assertions using this predicate should be made in the appropriately temporally qualified context.")
(comment lender "A specialization of #$obligationParticipants that relates a #$LoanAgreement to an #$IntelligentAgent.  (#$lender AGREEMENT AGENT) means that AGENT is a lender in AGREEMENT.")
(comment FOL-PredicateFn "(#$FOL-PredicateFn TERM ARITY) denotes a predicate that has
arity ARITY in the first-order projection of CycL based on the CycL
term TERM, which must be either a predicate or a collection.  For
example, (#$FOL-PredicateFn #$eventOccursAt 2) denotes the binary
first-order predicate associated with #$eventOccursAt,
(#$FOL-PredicateFn #$different 2) denotes the first-order binary
version of the predicate #$different, and (#$FOL-PredicateFn #$Date 1)
denotes the unary first-order predicate associated with #$Date")
(comment FOL-FunctionFn "(#$FOL-FunctionFn FUNC ARITY) denotes a function that has
arity ARITY in the first-order projection of CycL based on the CycL
function FUNC.  For example, (#$FOL-FunctionFn #$YearFn 1) denotes the
unary first-order function associated with #$YearFn, and
(#$FOL-FunctionFn #$PlusFn 2) denotes the first-order binary function
associated with #$PlusFn")
(comment FOL-TermFn "(#$FOL-TermFn TERM) denotes a first-order constant symbol
based on the CycL term TERM.  For example, (#$FOL-TermFn #$Dog)
denotes a first-order term based on the collection #$Dog,
(#$FOL-TermFn 212) denotes a first-order term based on the integer
212, and (#$FOL-TermFn #$isa) denotes a first-order term based on the
predicate #$isa.  See also (#$FOL-PredicateFn #$isa 2) for the
first-order binary predicate based on #$isa.")
(comment collectionExpansion "(#$collectionExpansion COL FORMULA) states that membership
of a term in the collection COL is equivalent to FORMULA involving
that term being true.  The meta-variable :ARG1 is used to stand for
the term in FORMULA, and the meta-variable :ARG2 is used to stand for
the collection in FORMULA.")
(comment DitransitiveFrameType "Frames used for words that take exactly two complements.  Example: 'Sally took Fred to the show.'")
(comment TransitiveCopulaFrameType "Frames used for copulas that take 
exactly one complement.  Example: 'Fred is 
hungry', 'Sally appears happy'")
(comment CopulaNPFrame "This frame is used for copulas 
that take exactly
one complement, an NP. Example: 'He seemed 
a fool.'")
(comment CopulaADVPFrame "This frame is used for copulas 
that take exactly
one complement, an ADVP. Example: 'He seems 
well.'")
(comment CopulaPPFrame "This frame is used for copulas 
that take exactly one
complement, a PP. Example: 'The matter 
seems in dispute.'")
(comment CopulaADJPFrame "This frame is used for copulas 
that take exactly
one complement, an ADJP. Example: 'He 
appears crazy.'")
(comment DitransitivePP-GenericFrame "This frame is used for 
ditransitive words that take exactly
two complements, an NP and a PP. Example: 
'Sally added the flowers to
the bouquet.' Note that we have the 
vocabulary to specify which
preposition heads the phrase -- 
(#$PPCompFrameFn
#$DitransitivePPFrameType #$To-TheWord). 
Use this frame when the
assertion needs to be made generically.")
(comment TripleComplementFrameType "Frames for words that take three 
complements. Example: 'Fred
took the plane from London to Paris.'")
(comment NP-ADVP-PPFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly three
complements, an NP, an ADVP, and a PP. Example: 'They carried the
documents southward to the airport.'")
(comment DitransitiveNP-ADVPFrame "This frame is used for ditransitive words that take exactly
two complements, an NP and an ADVP. Example: 'Fred put his coat
there.'")
(comment TransitiveADVP-DirectionFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly
one complement, a directional ADVP. Example: 'Sally headed home.'")
(comment DitransitivePP-PPFrame "This frame is used for ditransitive words that take exactly
two complements, a PP and a PP. Example: 'They flew from London to
Rome.'")
(comment DitransitiveGerundPhrase-NPFrame "This frame is used for ditransitive words that take exactly
two complements, a gerund phrase and an NP. Example: 'He discussed
writing novels.'")
(comment DitransitivePP-NPFrame "This frame is used for ditransitive words that take exactly
two complements, a PP and an NP. Example: 'Sally added to the bouquet
the flowers I picked yesterday.'")
(comment PP-PP-PPFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly three
complements, a PP, a PP, and a PP. Example: 'Fred went from London to
Paris to Rome.'")
(comment NP-PP-PPFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly three
complements, an NP, a PP, and a PP. Example: 'They carried the
documents from the embassy to the airport'.")
(comment TransitiveADVP-MannerFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly
one complement, an ADVP of manner. Example: 'They always acted that
way.'")
(comment DitransitiveADVP-PPFrame "This frame is used for ditransitive words that take exactly
two complements, an ADVP and a PP. Example: 'Corporations react
violently to short-range stimuli.'")
(comment DitransitiveGerundPhrase-PPFrame "This frame is used for ditransitive words that take exactly
two complements, a gerund phrase and a PP. Example: 'She began
drinking at 9:00 every night.'")
(comment PP-PP-NPFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly three
complements, a PP, a PP, and an NP. Example: 'They carried from the
embassy to the airport the documents ratified by the premier.")
(comment minimumBalance "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$BankAccount to a #$MonetaryValue.  (#$minimumBalance ACCOUNT MIN) means that the administrator of the account (#$accountAdministrator) requires the holder of the account (#$accountHolder) to maintain a balance (#$accountBalance) of at least MIN.  Failure to maintain a balance of MIN results in a penalty.")
(comment AchievingSomething "The act of achieving something.  In general, this collection can be used to describe (in a generic way) events in which result in the achievement of some situation (e.g. a goal state or #$StaticSituation).")
(comment priceToEarningsRatio "#$priceToEarningsRatio denotes the relation between a share of stock and its last 12 months' earnings per share. <code>(#$priceToEarningsRatio STOCK NUM)</code> means that <code>NUM</code> is the ratio of the price of a share of the stock <code>STOCK</code> to the past 12 months' per-share earnings of the company in which <code>STOCK</code> shares are shares.")
(comment TransitiveParticleNPFrameType "Frames used for verbs that join with particles to form
multi-word verbs that take exactly one complement, an NP. Example: 'Fred
broke apart the puzzle.'")
(comment ParticleCompFrameFn "(#$ParticleCompFrameFn FRAME PARTICLE) returns an instance of
ParticleCompFrame FRAME that represents a frame for the
multi-word verb, VERB + PARTICLE.")
(comment ParticleFrameType "Frames used for verbs that join with particles to form
multi-word verbs. Example: 'Fred broke apart the puzzle.', 'Take off
your coat, please.'")
(comment DitransitiveParticleNP-PPFrameType "Frames used for verbs that join with particles to form
multi-word verbs that take exactly two complements, an NP and a PP. Example: 'Fred
made up stories about Sally.'")
(comment IntransitiveParticleFrameType "Frames used for verbs that join with particles to form
multi-word verbs that take no complements. Example: 'Sally came back.'")
(comment ProjectManagement-Requests-TemplateTopic "An instance of FormulaTemplateTopicType. This is used for the creation of instances of #$Assignment-Specification as well as instances of #$ResourceRequest for those assignments.")
(comment CharityCard "A specialization of #$CreditCard-RevolvingAccount.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card that allows one to carry a balance from month to month.  In addition, a small percentage of the purchase price of every object purchased with the card is donated to some charity or other.")
(comment reportDetailsActivityOnAccount "A specialization of #$containsInformationAbout-Focally that relates an instance of #$FinancialDocument to an instance of #$Account.  (#$reportDetailsActivityOnAccount DOCUMENT ACCOUNT) says that DOCUMENT is a report on the activity (typically, in the case of a financial account (c.f., #$FinancialAccount), withdrawals and deposits) on the account ACCOUNT.")
(comment ReducingALiquid "A specialization of #$Boiling.  Instances of this collection are events in heat is applied to a liquid  with the intent of concentrating the liquid by reducing it's volume.")
(comment StoreChargeCard "A subcollection of #$CreditCard.  Each instance of #$StoreChargeCard is a card issued by a retail organization that allows users to purchase items in their stores and pay for them later.  Usually the card agreement is a revolving agreement that lets the users pay a monthly payment on their balance.  These cards often have high interest rates.")
(comment ProjectManagement-Allotments-TemplateTopic "An instance of #$FormulaTemplateTopicType. Instances are collections of instances of FormulaTemplate used to create new instances of #$Assignment-Specification and instances of  #$Allotment for project management.")
(comment slotForTypeHasValueWRTType "(#$slotForTypeHasValueWRTType TYPE1 TYPE2 SLOT VALUE-PRED) holds just in case a typical instance of 
TYPE1's value in the second argument of SLOT is VALUE-PRED with respect to typical instances of TYPE2 (that are not instances of TYPE2).  For example, to state that store credit cards have a high interest rate compared to other credit cards we assert:

<pre>
(#$slotForTypeHasValueWRTType #$StoreChargeCard #$CreditCard-RevolvingAccount  
                                                   #$interestRate #$highAmountOf)
</pre>

.")
(comment LocalAuthoritySearch "A specialization of #$ServiceEvent and #$Evaluating.  Instances are events in which a lawyer does research to determine whether there are any development plans that might impact those living in a given area.  This service enables a home-buyer to make an informed decision as to whether s/he should purchase a particular property.")
(comment ConstructionPlan "The collection of instances of Plan in which the eventTypePlanned is some type of construction (c.f., Constructing).")
(comment eventTypePlanned "(#$eventTypePlanned PLAN EVENT-TYPE) means that the instance of #$Plan PLAN is a plan to bring about an instance of an event of type EVENT-TYPE.")
(disjointWith IndividualVoluntaryArrangementForRepayment CorporateVoluntaryArrangementForRepayment)
(comment ApplyingAPCW "A specialization of #$Evaluating.  Instances of this collection are events in which an agent endeavors to evaluate the consequences (e.g. entailments or predictions) of a particular #$PropositionalConceptualWork bear on a particular #$Situation.")
(comment proposingAgents "(#$proposingAgents PROPOSAL AGENT) means that the intelligent agent (c.f., #$IntelligentAgent) AGENT is one of the agents proposing the instance of #$Proposal PROPOSAL.")
(comment proposalTargets "(#$proposalTargets PROPOSAL AGENT) means that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent is the target of the instance of #$Proposal PROPOSAL.  In other words, PROPOSAL was authored with the intent of proposing (see #$Propose) it to AGENT, with the intent of forming an agreement (c.f., #$Agreement).")
(comment IntroducingSomeone "A specialization of #$SocialOccurrence.  Instances of this collection are events in which someone is explicitly (but not necessarily formally) introduced to someone else.. In an event of this sort, it is presumed (prehaps incorrectly) that the introduced agents not familiar with (cf. #$acquaintedWith and #$mutualAcquaintances) each other.")
(comment effectiveActTypeForActType "An assertion of the form (#$effectiveActTypeForActType TYPE GOAL-TYPE) means that the performance of some instance of TYPE, a sub-collection of #$PurposefulAction are an effective way of making progress on achieving an instance of GOAL-TYPE, some sub-collection of #$PurposefulAction.")
(comment DirectDebit "#$DirectDebit is a sub-collection of (#$OnlineActivityTypeFn #$Paying) that is characterized by the creditors having access to a person's accounts so that they can make regular withdrawals.")
(comment OnlineActivityTypeFn "A collection denoting function.  An expression of the form (#$OnlineActivityTypeFn TYPE) denotes the sub-collection of TYPE, some sub-collection of #$PurposefulAction that uses the Internet.")
(comment debtAmount "An assertion of the form (#$debtAmount DEBT VALUE) means that the #$PaymentObligation DEBT has a #$MonetaryValue of VALUE.")
(comment debtPartiallyFulfilled "An assertion of the form (#$debtPartiallyFulfilled PAY DEBT) means that the instance of #$Paying, PAY involves the transfer of some #$MonetaryValue to meet part of the #$PaymentObligation DEBT.")
(comment onlineVersionOfActivityType "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$OnlineActivityTypeFn.  An assertion of the form (onlineVersionOfActivityType ON-TYPE REG-TYPE) means that ON-TYPE is the sub-collection of REG-TYPE that uses the Internet.")
(comment LongTermPaymentObligation "A sub-collection of #$PaymentObligation characterized by the size of the debt and the expectation that it will be paid off in increments in an interval measured in years.")
(comment ComparisonTable-CW "A type of #$Table-VisualCW.  Instances of #$ComparisonTable-CW are used for listing the relevant the features of two similar entities so as to readily reveal their similarities and differences.")
(comment companyEPIC "A specialization of #$stockTickerSymbol, (#$companyEPIC ORG STRING) states that the #$CommercialOrganization ORG is represted via the #$EPIC-FinancialIDString STRING on the #$LondonStockExchange.")
(comment companyEPIC "A specialization of #$stockTickerSymbol.  (#$companyEPIC CORP SYM) means that SYM is the EPIC (Exchange Price Information Code) for CORP.  Every company listed on the London Stock Exchange has a unique EPIC.")
(comment ExpendingSomething "A specialization of Evemt  Instances of this collection are events in which some resource is expended. This may be the result of a transfer (cf. #$TransferOut), as in #$SpendingMoney, or some destructive process (cf. #$PhysicalDestructionEvent), as with the inputsDestroyed to a #$CombustionProcess.")
(comment benefitsForRolePlayerInSitTypeWRTAgentType "<pre>(#$benefitsForRolePlayerInSitTypeWRTAgentType AGENT-TYPE ROLE SIT-TYPE BENEFIT-SENTENCE)</pre> holds just in case instances of AGENT-TYPE playing ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE will gain the benefit described by BENEFIT-SENTENCE.")
(comment typeMaximizesTypeWRTType "<code>(#$typeMaximizesTypeWRTType SIT-TYPE-1 SLOT SIT-TYPE-2)</code> holds just in case being the performer or doer of instances of <code>SIT-TYPE-1</code> will tend to maximize the second argument of <code>SLOT</code> with respect to <code>SIT-TYPE-2</code>.")
(comment typeMinimizesTypeWRTType "<pre>(#$typeMinimizesTypeWRTType SIT-TYPE-1 SLOT SIT-TYPE-2)</pre> holds just in case being the performer or doer of instances of SIT-TYPE-1 will tend to minimize the second argument of SLOT with respect to SIT-TYPE-2.")
(comment MinimumPaymentMaker "A subcollection of #$Person.  This is the collection of people who tend (on a regular basis) to make only the minimum payments on their credit card bills.  This is a temporally qualifiable collection -- a person may be an instance of this collection for only a few months if, for instance, there were down on their luck and had only enough money to make the minimum payments.")
(comment PaysInFullEachMonth "A subcollection of #$Person.  This is the collection of people who tend (on a regular basis) to fully pay off their credit card bills each month.  This is a temporally qualifiable collection.  A person who is normally in this collection may fail to be for several months if they are down on their luck and can only make the minimum payments.")
(comment CreditCardHolder "A subcollection of #$Person.  This is the collection of all people who have credit cards.")
(comment CreditCardDefaulter "A subcollection of #$Person.  This is the collection of credit card holders that default on their credit card agreements.")
(comment PaysMoreThanTheirMonthlyPayment "A subcollection of #$Person.  This is the collection of credit card holders that usually make more than their minimum monthly payments on their credit card bills.  Exceptions arise when their balance that month equals their minimum monthly payment.  In those cases they are still considered members of this collection.  While the generation is perhaps unintuitive, this collection is meant to represent persons who are responsible credit card users and making the name and generation of the collection disjunctive as in \"Pays more than monthly payment or pays the monthly payment when it is equal to their balance\" seemed a mouthful.")
(comment AcquiringACreditCard "A subcollection of #$MakingLegalAgreement and #$AcquiringAnObject-Legally.  This is the collection of
all events in which an agent has acquired a credit card.  The result of these actions is that an instance of #$CreditCardAgreement is reached with some instance of #$CreditCardCompany.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ReadyForLexification "The collection of #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that are ready for lexification.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-NPObjComplementFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly two NP complements, where one NP plays the role of direct object and the other the role of object complement.  Example: 'Fred called Sally a liar'.  One salient way in which this frame is distinguished from #$DitransitiveNP-NPFrame is that the latter undergoes #$DoubleObjectAlternations, while the former does not. Example: 'Fred gave Sally a book' alternates with 'Fred gave a book to Sally' but 'Fred called Sally a liar' does not -- *'Fred called a liar of Sally'.")
(comment SaleTypeByCreditCardType "A collection of specializations of #$SaleByCreditCard. Each instance of #$SaleTypeByTenderType is a type of buying, or selling, in which the same type of credit card is used. For example, #$SaleByVisa and #$SaleByMasterCard are instances of #$SaleTypeByCreditCardType.")
(comment costBenefitSentenceForSituationType "<code>(#$costBenefitSentenceForSituationType SITUATION-TYPE ROLE SENTENCE)</code> holds just in case SENTENCE is a sentence that describes some relevant cost/benefit for individuals who play ROLE in instances of SITUATION-TYPE.")
(comment CreditCardWithLowAPR "A specialization of #$CreditCard-RevolvingAccount.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card with a low APR (annual percentage rate).  By \"low\" we mean not more than 6 or 7 points above the prime rate.")
(comment SaleByCreditCardWithLowAPR "A specialization of #$SaleByCreditCard.  Each instance of #$SaleByCreditCardWithLowAPR is a purchase in which the buyer (see the predicate #$buyer) pays by using some instance of #$CreditCardWithLowAPR (q.v.).")
(comment Allowance "A specialization of #$Agreement. Each instance of #$Allowance is an agreement in which one party agrees to reimburse (usually monetarily) another party that meets certain criteria.  Important specializations include the various types of tax allowances.")
(comment transferValue "(#$transferValue NEW-PENSION OLD-PENSION VALUE) means that VALUE is the amount of money that must be transferred to NEW-PENSION for the person holding NEW-PENSION to get the same benefits built up under OLD-PENSION.")
(comment interestBill "(#$interestBill PAY AMOUNT) means that AMOUNT is the amount of money in the #$PaymentObligation PAY that goes toward paying interest on some debt owed.")
(comment WarrantyTypeByCoverage "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollection.  Each instance of #$WarrantyTypeByCoverage is a specialization of #$Warranty all of whose instances have roughly the same degree of coverage (both in terms of the duration of the warranty, and the parts and services covered by the warranty). Instances of #$WarrantyTypeByCoverage include #$ImpliedWarranty and #$ExtendedWarranty.")
(comment BondTypeByIssuingAgentType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollection.  Each instance of #$BondTypeByIssuingAgentType is a specialization of #$Bond-Agreement all of whose instances are issued by the same type of agent (usually some specialization of #$Organization). Instances of #$BondTypeByIssuingAgentType include #$CorporateBond-Agreement and #$MunicipalBond-Agreement.")
(comment serviceTypesCoveredByWarranty "An instance of both #$BinaryPredicate and #$IntangibleObjectPredicate. (#$serviceTypesCoveredByWarranty WARRANTY TYPE) means that WARRANTY, a #$Warranty for a certain product, covers services of the type TYPE for that product, so that if a service of type TYPE is needed for the maintenance of PRODUCT, such a service will be provided free of charge, or at a reduced price.")
(comment warrantyForProduct "A #$BinaryPredicate relating a #$Warranty to a #$PartiallyTangible. (#$warrantyForProduct WARRANTY ITEM) means that WARRANTY covers ITEM.")
(comment MarketTypeByProductSold "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$MarketTypeByProductSold is a subcollection of #$Market, each of whose instances is a market for the same type of product.  For example, #$HousingMarket is an instance of #$MarketTypeByProductSold.")
(comment itemTypesCoveredByWarranty "An instance of both #$BinaryPredicate and #$IntangibleObjectPredicate. (#$itemTypesCoveredByWarranty WARRANTY TYPE) means that WARRANTY, a #$Warranty for a certain product, covers items of the type TYPE for that product, so that if an original part of type TYPE in the product is defective, or becomes worn out, a replacement part of type TYPE will be provided free of charge, or at a reduced price.")
(comment HypothesizedPrepositionSenseFn "(#$HypothesizedPrepositionSenseFn WORD POS) denotes a hypothesized (and potentially underspecified) sense of WORD which is approriate for part of spech POS (where POS is restricted to be some spec of #$Preposition)  The result of this Function can be regarded as a semantic placeholder which may be refined as time,  interest, and project demands allow.")
(comment alternativeActionTypes "A binary #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate.  <code>(#$alternativeActionTypes ACTTYPE1 ACTTYPE2)</code> means that performing an  act of <code>ACTTYPE1</code> is commonly considered to be salient and often viable alternative to performing an act of <code>ACTTYPE2</code>, and vice versa.  In some (but not all) cases, <code>ACTTYPE1</code> and <code>ACTTYPE2</code> will be sibling nearest-specializations of some slightly more general type of #$Action.  
<p>
For example, baking-bread-from-scratch and baking-bread-from-a-mix are #$alternativeActionTypes, and both are specializations of #$BakingBread.")
(comment accountMediator "A binary predicate that relates an #$Account to an #$Organization that sets it up on behalf of one of its members, who is in turn the #$accountHolder (q.v.). <code>(#$accountMediator ACCT ORG)</code> means the <code>ORG</code> has set up <code>ACCT</code> for some member <code>INDIV</code> of <code>ORG</code>, and serves as mediator, with respect to <code>ACCT</code>, between <code>INDIV</code> and the #$accountAdministrator (q.v.) <code>ADMIN</code> of <code>ACCT</code>.  Typically, <code>ACCT</code> will be of a type available to many or all of <code>ORG</code>'s members, with <code>ORG</code> acting as mediator (and <code>ADMIN</code> as administrator) in each case.  For example, <code>ORG</code> might be a #$Business with <code>INDIV</code> as one of its #$employees and <code>ACCT</code> a #$CompanyPension (q.v.).")
(comment ExtractedByNounLearner "The collection of instances of #$CycLTerm that represent concepts that are the denotations of nouns and noun phrases that have been extracted by the Cyc Noun Learner (c.f., #$CycNounLearnerTool) against some corpus.")
(comment subcatFramesForAlternation "(#$subcatFramesForAlternation ALTERNATION FRAME1 FRAME2)
means that #$SubcategorizationFrame FRAME1 and FRAME2 alternate under
ALTERNATION.")
(comment DitransitivePP-NPFrameType "Frames used for verbs that take a PP complement followed by an NP complement. Example: 'Fred gave to Sally a big kiss.'")
(comment Cohabitating-Married "A specialization of #$CohabitationSituation. Each instance of #$Cohabitating-Married is a situation in which a couple is married and live together.")
(comment DomesticSituationByMaritalStatus "The collection of collections of instances of situations that pertain to marital and cohabitation status.  Instances include #$Cohabitating-Married, #$NonCohabitating-Married, #$Cohabitating-Unmarried.  These collections characterize the states of affairs of being in a certain sort of domestic situation.  For example, instances of #$Cohabitating-Married are all situations that endure (for some length) through time during which a couple are married and live together.")
(comment NonCohabitating-Married "A specialization of #$Situation. Each instance of #$NonCohabitating-Married is a situation in which a couple is married and doesn't live together.")
(comment Cohabitating-Unmarried "A specialization of #$CohabitationSituation. Each instance of #$Cohabitating-Unmarried is a situation in which a couple is not married and live together.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-DoNotImport "The collection of #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that have been reviewed and determined not for import into Cyc.")
(comment argsQuotedIsa "A binary #$ArgQuotedIsaPredicate (q.v.) that is used to put a specified quoted-isa based argument-type constraint on all of a given relation's argument-places at once. (#$argsQuotedIsa RELN COL) means that semantic well-formedness requires that each argument to which RELN is applied (regardless of argument-place) be a quoted instance of COL. For example, '(#$argsQuotedIsa #$and #$CycLSentence-Assertible)' means that the relation #$and must only be applied to assertible CycL sentences. #$argsQuotedIsa is particularly useful for constraining (any and all of) the arguments of a VariableArityRelation (the preceding example being a case in point); though #$argQuotedIsa may be applied to fixed-arity relations as well. For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see CycLExpression-Assertible and its immediate specializations.")
(disjointWith ComputerIBT CohabitatingPerson-Unmarried)
(comment HavingATaxObligation "A collection of static situations holding between an agent and some geopolitical entity.  Each instance of this collection is a situation in which someone has a current tax obligation (#$TaxObligation).  These situations hold from the time the obligation is incurred until it is discharged either by payment or by the obligation passing to the individual's heirs or estate.")
(comment taxesOwed "<code>(#$taxesOwed OWING-TAXES MONETARY-VALUE)</code> holds just in case the money owed in the situation OWING-TAXES is MONETARY-VALUE.")
(comment SubcollectionWithRelativeGenericValueFn "(#$SubcollectionWithRelativeGenericValueFn COL SLOT VALUE) denotes the subcollection of COL whose SLOT value is VALUE compared to other instances of COL.")
(comment adjectiveOfGenericValue "(#$adjectiveOfGenericValue SLOT VALUE WU) means that the #$regularDegree form of WU can be used to modify a noun NOUN to form a phrase meaning 'NOUN whose SLOT value is VALUE compared to other NOUNs'.")
(comment GarnisheeOrder "The collection of all judicial #$Writs (q.v.) whereby monies owed to a debtor by a third party, or being held by a third party on behalf of a debtor can be seized. This is commonly used to freeze monies held in a bank account.")
(comment PayingForLivingExpenses "A collection of events; a subset of #$Paying.  Every instance of #$PayingForLivingExpenses is a particular paying event in which some item is bought or bill is paid and the outlay is considered a \"living expense\".")
(comment HighCourtJudgment-PCW "A specialization of #$NormativeSpecification.  The collection of judgements made by the #$HighCourt-UK (q.v.).  A high court judgement is similar to a #$CountyCourtJudgment-PCW (q.v.), but usually involves debts owed in excess of 15,000 pounds.")
(comment HelpPage-AIS "A specialization of #$WebPage-AIS.  Each instance of #$HelpPage-AIS is a web page that is dedicated to #$HelpingAnAgent use the #$WebSite of which the help page is a part.")
(comment antonymsForGenericValue "(#$antonymsForGenericValue SLOT LOW-WU HIGH-WU) means that the #$regularDegree forms of LOW-WU and HIGH-WU denote values at the low and high ends, respectively, of the scale determined by SLOT.")
(comment TheHighCourt-UK "An instance of #$Court-Judicial.  Part of the court system of England and Wales.  The High Court hears civil cases for amounts greater than 15,000 pounds, and also serves as a civil and criminal appellate court for cases from the subordinate courts (e.g. instances of #$CountyCourt-UK).  The High Court is based at the Royal Courts of Justice in central London, but also sits as District Registries all across England and Wales.")
(comment StatutoryDemand "A specialization of #$NormativeSpecification (q.v.).  A #$StatutoryDemand is a formal demand made by a creditor to a debtor for repayment of a debt.")
(comment AffectingAnAccountBalance "A specialization of #$MoneyTransaction.  Instances are transactions that change the balance of an account, positively or negatively.  See #$Account and #$transactionAccount.")
(comment IncreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount "The collection of instances of #$AffectingAnAccountBalance in which the balance (see #$accountBalance) of an account (see #$transactionAccount) is increased, whether by transferring monies into the account (see #$toAccount) as in a deposit to a savings account, or by transferring monies from the account (see #$fromAccount) as happens when one makes a credit card purchase..  Note that #$IncreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount is <b>not</b> disjoint with #$DecreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount, as a single transfer can, and frequently does, involve multiple accounts (as in paying a bill with a check).")
(comment IncreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount "A specialization of #$MoneyTransaction.  Instances are transactions that change the balance of an account, positively or negatively.  See #$Account and #$transactionAccount.")
(comment DecreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount "The collection of instances of #$AffectingAnAccountBalance in which the balance (see #$accountBalance) of an account (see #$transactionAccount) is decreased, whether by transferring monies into the account (see #$toAccount) as in a credit card payment, or by transferring monies from the account (see #$fromAccount) as in a bank withdrawal.  Note that #$DecreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount is <b>not</b> disjoint with #$IncreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount, as a single transfer can, and frequently does, involve multiple accounts (as in paying a bill with a check).")
(comment Sheriff-UK "A specialization of #$LawEnforcementOfficer.  A #$Sheriff-UK is an officer of #$TheHighCourt-UK (q.v.), with similar duties to that of a #$Bailiff (q.v.).  A #$Sheriff-UK however, can be used to enforce #$CountyCourtJudgment-PCWs which exceed 650 pounds, and can levy additional fees on top of the debt, known as poundage.")
(comment DecreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccountBelowZero "A specialization of #$DecreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount.  Instances are transactions that decrease the balance (see #$accountBalance) on some account to a negative amount.  Notable specializations include #$OverdrawingABankAccount.")
(comment Summons-UK "A specialization of #$LegalDocument.  A #$Summons-UK is a document issued by a court in the legal system of England and Wales (e.g. a #$CommonCourt-UK or #$TheHighCourt-UK) that sets out the claim of a creditor and gives a specific time in which a debtor must either pay the debt, or admit or deny that the debt is owed.  Cf. #$Summons-Legal.")
(comment OverpayingTheBalanceDueOnAnAccount "The collection of instances of payments towards an account that are overpayments -- i.e., they set the balance below zero, often resulting in monies being owed the account holder.")
(comment MakingACreditCardOverpayment "A specialization of #$OverpayingTheBalanceDueOnAnAccount.  Instances are credit card payments that bring the balance to below zero.")
(comment WindingUpOrder "The collection of all judicial #$Writs (q.v.) for the seizure and realization of a company's assets, for the benefit of its creditors. In the UK, a #$WindingUpOrder is usually conducted by either The Official Receiver or an #$InsolvencyPractitioner known as the Liquidator.")
(comment preChangeValueOfQuantity "(#$preChangeValueOfQuantity TEMPORAL-THING THING SLOT VALUE) means that the instance of #$TemporalThing TEMPORAL-THING changed the value of SLOT applied to THING from VALUE.  To specify what the value of SLOT applied to THING is changed to, use #$postChangeValueOfQuantity.  #$preChangeValueOfQuantity, #$postChangeValueOfQuantity, and #$changesQuantityByAmount can be used together to perform arithmetical calculations about the value of SLOT applied to THING with respect to TEMPORAL-THING.")
(comment postChangeValueOfQuantity "(#$postChangeValueOfQuantity TEMPORAL-THING THING SLOT VALUE) means that the instance of #$TemporalThing TEMPORAL-THING changed the value of SLOT applied to THING to VALUE.  To specify what the value of SLOT applied to THING is changed from, use #$preChangeValueOfQuantity.  #$preChangeValueOfQuantity, #$postChangeValueOfQuantity, and #$changesQuantityByAmount can be used together to perform arithmetical calculations about the value of SLOT applied to THING with respect to TEMPORAL-THING.")
(comment costBenefitPredForSitTypeInArg "<code>(#$costBenefitPredForSitTypeInArg PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE ARG-NUM)</code> holds just in case any sentence S of the form (PRED ... COL . ARGS) where a specialization COL of SIT-TYPE appears in the ARG-NUMth place of S is a sentence that expresses a fact worth considering when assessing the costs/benefits of playing ROLE in a TYPE.")
(comment productTypeFinancialSummary "An instance of #$SummaryPredicate.  (#$productTypeFinancialSummary TYPE SENTENCE) means that the instance SENTENCE of #$CycLSentence is an interesting fact when considering financial information (typically, pricing) for specializations of TYPE.")
(comment productTypeFacilitates "<code>(#$productTypeFacilitates OBJ-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds just in case instances of OBJ-TYPE make it easier (in some sense) to play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE.  For example, <code> (#$productTypeFacilitates #$CreditCard #$FinancingByBorrowing #$borrower)</code> holds because having a credit card makes it easier to be the borrower in an instance of #$FinancingByBorrowing -- you just use the card, there is no need for you to fill out any form to get the money to make the purchase/cash withdrawal.")
(comment AcquiringAnObject "A subcollection of #$GeneralizedTransfer.  Each instance of this collection is an act in which an agent acquires some tangible or intangible item.  Examples include stealing a sweater from a department store as well as buying a scarf from a boutigue.  Examples where the item is not a tangible good include acquiring the rights to a conceptual work (e.g. a song or story) or  purchasing stock.  Note that all acquirings whether legal or not count as instances of this collection.  For the collection of legal acquisitions of objects see the subcollection of this collection #$AcquiringAnObject-Legally.")
(comment AcquiringAnObject-Legally "A subcollection of #$AcquiringAnObject and #$GainingUserRights.  Each instance of this collection is an act in which an agent legally acquires some tangible or intangible item.  Examples include buying a scarf from a boutigue or  purchasing stock.")
(comment AcquiringAnObject-Illegally "A subcollection of #$AcquiringAnObject.  Each instance of this collection is an act in which an agent illegally acquires some tangible or intangible item.  Examples include stealing a scarf from a boutigue or embezzling from the company pension fund.")
(comment acquisitionTypeOfType "<code>(#$acquisitionTypeOfType ACQUISITION-TYPE OBJECT-TYPE)</code> holds just in case ACQUISITION-TYPE is the collection of instances of #$AcquiringAnObject that are acquirings of instances of OBJECT-TYPE.  This is the corresponding predicate to #$AcquiringFn.")
(comment AcquiringFn "<code>'(#$AcquiringFn OBJ-TYPE)'</code> denotes the subcollection of AcquiringAnObject that corresponds to the collection of all acquirings of instances of OBJ-TYPE.  The is the corresponding function to #$acquisitionTypeOfType. ")
(comment InvestmentPortfolio "A specialization of (#$GroupFn #$InvestmentVehicle).  Each instance of #$InvestmentPortfolio is the group of all investments held by a particular #$Investor.")
(comment DiversifyingInvestments "A specialization of #$Investing.  Each instance of #$DiversifyingInvestments is an event in which an #$Investor deliberately invests in such a way that his or her risk is distributed among various #$InvestmentVehicles.")
(comment enables-RoleInSitTypeRoleInSitType "<code>(#$enables-RoleInSitTypeRoleInSitType SIT-TYPE-1 ROLE-1 SIT-TYPE-2 ROLE-2)</code> holds just in case playing ROLE-1 in instances of SIT-TYPE-1 enables one to play ROLE-2 in instances of SIT-TYPE-2.")
(comment primaryRoleForSituationType "<code>(#$primaryRoleForSituationType SIT-TYPE BIN-ROLE-PRED)</code> holds just in case the most relevant role in a given situation that's an instance of SIT-TYPE is BIN-ROLE-PRED.  For instance, an instance of (#$UsingAFn #$CreditCard) is an instance of both #$UsingADevice and #$Buying.  Given that the #$seller in the event is not the one using the credit card, #$buyer is the most relevant role in the event.")
(comment JobSeekersAllowance-UK "A specialization of #$Allowance.  Each instance of #$JobSeekersAllowance-UK is an allowance available to the unemployed who can work, or are looking for work.")
(comment amountOfAllowance "A predicate relating an instance of #$Allowance to an instance of #$MonetaryValue.  (#$amountOfAllowance ALLOW MONEY) means that ALLOW has the value MONEY.")
(comment allowanceRecipient "A predicate relating an instance of #$Allowance to an instance of #$SocialBeing.  (#$allowanceRecipient ALLOW AGENT) means that AGENT is a recipient of ALLOW.")
(comment allowanceProvider "A predicate relating an instance of #$Allowance to an instance of #$SocialBeing.  (#$allowanceProvider ALLOW AGENT) means that AGENT is a provider of ALLOW.")
(comment AdministrationOrder "A specialization of #$Writ.  Each instance of #$AdministrationOrder is an order issued by a UK County Court.  Such an order requires the party applying for it to pay his debts in full or a percentage of the debts, by monthly instalments.  The total debts of an individual applying for such an order must not exceed 5000 pounds.")
(comment AttachmentOrder "A specialization of #$Writ.  Each instance of #$AttachmentOrder is an order issued by a UK County Court allowing a creditor to sell property and assets of a debtor until the latter's debt to the former is fully paid.")
(comment AttachmentOfEarningsOrder "A specialization of #$Writ.  Each instance of #$AttachmentOfEarningsOrder is an order issued by a UK County Court compelling the employer of a debtor to deduct payments from the debtor's salary. These payments go towards erasing the debt owed by the debtor to his creditor.")
(comment Bailiff-CountyCourt "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$Bailiff-CountyCourt is an officer of the UK County Court who carries out the orders of that court.")
(comment Bailiff-Certificated "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$Bailiff-Certificated is a person who works for a landlord, solicitor, or local council, doing for them what a #$Bailiff-CountyCourt (q.v.) does for a County Court.")
(comment CountyCourtJudgment-PCW "A specialization of #$NormativeSpecification.  Each instance of #$CountyCourtJudgment-PCW is a decree by a UK County Court that a debt is due and payable.")
(comment CountyCourt-UK "A specialization of #$Court-Judicial.  Each instance of #$CountyCourt-UK is a court serving some parish within a UK county (see the collection #$County-Britain).  Instances of #$CountyCourt-UK hear civil cases involving relatively small claims.")
(comment SettingUpADirectDebit "The procedure of setting up a #$DirectDebitInstruction.  See http://www.directdebit.co.uk/general_public/getting_started.php")
(comment DirectDebitForm-IBO "The information bearing object (on-line electronic or hard copy) that instantiates a #$DirectDebitForm-CW.")
(comment CreditCardWithHighAPR "A specialization of #$CreditCard-RevolvingAccount.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card with a high APR (annual percentage rate).  By \"high\" we mean more than 6 or 7 points above the prime rate.")
(disjointWith CreditCardWithHighAPR CreditCardWithLowAPR)
(comment CohabitationSituation "A specialization of #$Situation. Each instance of #$Cohabitating-Married is a situation in which a couple live together.  This includes married and unmarried couples.")
(comment backingInvestment "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$LoanAgreement to an #$InvestmentVehicle.  (#$backingInvestment LOAN INVESTMENT) means that LOAN is backed by INVESTMENT, in the sense that LOAN is made on the understanding that INVESTMENT will eventually be used to pay it off.")
(comment TransitiveADVP-TimeFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly
one complement, an ADVP of time. Example: 'The sale begins this week.'")
(comment AdverbOfManner "The collection of all adverbs of manner, adverbs answering
the question 'how?' Example: 'stupendously' as in 'Fred wrote
stupendously.'")
(comment AdverbOfTime "The collection of all adverbs of time, adverbs answering the
question 'when?'. Example: 'later' as in 'Sally will hand in her paper later.'")
(comment AdverbOfPlace "The collection of all adverbs of place, adverbs answering the question 'where?'. Example: 'there' as in 'Fred lives there.'")
(comment AdverbOfFrequency "The collection of all adverbs of frequency, adverbs abswering the question 'how often?'. Example: 'frequently' as in 'Sally went to the gym frequently.'")
(comment Rights-Abstract "The collection of all natural or legal rights in the abstract as defined in some code of conduct (#$CodeOfConduct).")
(comment sitTypeHasLesserCardinalityWRTSitType "<code>(#$sitTypeHasLesserCardinalityWRTSitType SIT-TYPE-1 COLL SIT-TYPE-2 ROLE)</code> holds just in case individuals playing ROLE in situations that are instances of SIT-TYPE tend to be appropriately related to fewer instances of COLL than individuals playing ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE-2 .  For instance, (#$sitTypeHasLesserCardinalityWRTSitType Cohabitating-Unmarried Rights-Abstract Cohabitating-Married) means that couple who are involved in cohabitation situations who are unmarried tend to have fewer rights than couple who are involved in cohabitation situations who are married.")
(comment Bailiff "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, and a specialization of #$Professional.  Each instance of #$Bailiff is a person authorized to collect a debt owed to a creditor.")
(comment slotCalculationFormula-Addition "An instance of #$TernaryPredicate and #$SlotCalculationFormulaPredicate, used to state a method of calculating the value of a slot (c.f., #$ScalarIntervalSlot) for a given argument through addition.  (#$slotCalculationFormula-Addition SLOT SLOT-1 SLOT-2 . SLOT-N) means that for any valid arg1 for SLOT ARG, the value of VALUE in (SLOT ARG VALUE) can be arrived at by adding the arg2 values of SLOT-1 through SLOT-N with ARG fixed as the arg1 for each slot.")
(disjointWith BinaryPredicate SlotCalculationFormulaPredicate)
(disjointWith UnaryPredicate SlotCalculationFormulaPredicate)
(comment SlotCalculationFormulaPredicate "The collection of predicates that can be used to state formulae for calculating the (arg2) value of an instance of #$ScalarIntervalSlot for some arg1 value, on the basis of the arg2 values of other scalar interval slots with the same arg1 value.")
(comment IncreaseInMonetaryValue "A specialization of #$IncreaseEvent.  Each instance of #$IncreaseInMonetaryValue is an event in which something increases in monetary value.  Note that #$IncreaseInMonetaryValue is a #$rewriteOf (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$IncreaseEvent #$increasesSlot #$monetaryValueOfThing).")
(comment CancellingADirectDebit "The act of cancelling a #$DirectDebitInstruction.  According to http://www.directdebit.co.uk/general_public/faqs.php, if a citizen of the UK needs to cancel a #$DirectDebitInstruction, he or she should simply write their bank or building society, providing the name of the organization being paid, the branch sort code from the checking account, the name or names of the account holder or account holders, the bank or building society account number, and the customer reference number with the organization.  The financial institution then makes the cancellation.  Cancellation of #$DirectDebitInstructions can be made over the telephone or via the internet but written confirmation in these cases may be required.")
(comment DecreaseInMonetaryValue "A specialization of #$DecreaseEvent.  Each instance of #$DecreaseInMonetaryValue is an event in which something decreases in monetary value.  Note that #$IncreaseInMonetaryValue is a #$rewriteOf (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$DecreaseEvent #$decreasesSlot #$monetaryValueOfThing).")
(comment RisingMarket "A specialization of #$Market and #$IncreaseInMonetaryValue.  Each instance of #$RisingMarket is an event in which the things bought and sold in/on a particular #$Market increase in overall monetary value.  See also #$FallingMarket")
(comment FallingMarket "A specialization of #$Market and #$DecreaseInMonetaryValue.  Each instance of #$FallingMarket is an event in which the things bought and sold in/on a particular #$Market decrease in overall monetary value.  See also #$RisingMarket")
(disjointWith RisingMarket FallingMarket)
(comment slotCalculationFormula-Multiplication "An instance of #$SlotCalculationFormulaPredicate, used to state a method of calculating the value of a slot (c.f., #$ScalarIntervalSlot) through multiplication. (#$slotCalculationFormula-Multiplication SLOT-PRODUCT SLOT-1 SLOT-2) means that for any valid arg1 for SLOT-PRODUCT ARG, PRODUCT in (SLOT-PRODUCT ARG PRODUCT) is arrived at by multiplying SLOT-1-ARG2 in (SLOT-1 ARG SLOT-1-ARG2) by SLOT-2-ARG2 in (SLOT-2 ARG SLOT-2-ARG2).")
(comment OnlineBanking "A sub-collection of #$Banking.  This is the collection of online banking activities.  Each instance of this collection is a complex event of one going online, accessing an account, doing some banking sort of action and logging off or otherwise terminating the session.")
(comment slotCalculationFormula-Subtraction "An instance of #$TernaryPredicate and #$SlotCalculationFormulaPredicate, used to state a method of calculating the value of a slot (c.f., #$ScalarIntervalSlot) for a given argument through subtraction.  (#$slotCalculationFormula-Subtraction SLOT MINUEND-SLOT SUBTRAHEND-SLOT) means that for any valid arg1 for SLOT ARG, the value of VALUE in (SLOT ARG VALUE) can be arrived at by subtracting SUBTRAHEND-SLOT-VALUE in (SUBTRAHEND-SLOT ARG SUBTRAHEND) from MINUEND in (MINUEND-SLOT ARG MINUEND).")
(comment AtLocationBanking "A sub-collection of #$Banking.  This is the collection of traditional on-site banking activities.  Each instance of this collection is a complex event of one going to the bank, taking to a bank employee, doing some banking sort of action and leaving or otherwise terminating the session.")
(comment typeHasQuantityComparedToType "(#$typeHasQuantityComparedToType THING-1 VAL THING-2 PRED) means that instances of THING-1,tend to have the quantity VAL wrt PRED, when compared to the value that instances THING-2 would have wrt PRED all other things being equal.")
(comment DerivativeSecurity "A specialization of #$TradeableSecurity.  Each instance of #$DerivativeSecurity is a #$Contract that specifies rights and obligations between the issuer of the security and the holder to receive or deliver assets based on some future event(s).  A notable specialization is #$FinancialOption.")
(comment agentHasOpportunity "(#$agentHasOpportunity AGENT SITUATION-TYPE ROLE) says that the agent AGENT has the opportunity to play the role ROLE in an specialization of #$Situation.")
(comment EndowmentMortgage "A specialization of #$InterestOnlyMortgage.  endowment mortgages are secured by an endowment life insurance policy.")
(comment IdentityTheft "The collection of thefts in which the things stolen are the \"identities\" of the victim.  This means that the performer of an instance of this collection somehow gains unauthorized access to one or more crucial accounts of the victim and purchases items and so forth while posing as the victim.")
(comment UnauthorizedAccessToPersonalInformation "The collection of all events in which a person accesses personal information, such as an address book, calendar, online accounts, or etc. without the owner's permission or authorization.  An important subcollection of this collection is #$IdentityTheft.")
(comment agentTypeProvidesServiceOfType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$Agent-Generic to a specialization of #$ServiceEvent.  <code>(#$agentTypeProvidesServiceOfType AGT-TYPE ACT-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>AGT-TYPE</code> typically provide instances of <code>ACT-TYPE</code> as a service for others.")
(comment PayingABill "A collection of events; a subset of #$Paying.  Every instance of #$PayingABill is a particular paying event in which someone pays a bill such as a utility bill, phone bill, credit card bill, etc.")
(comment Headbutting "A #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$PhysicallyAttackingAnAgent.  Each instance of #$Headbutting is a violent act in which one animal smashes its head into another animal's head or face.  #$Headbutting is a popular fighting technique among barroom brawlers as well as instances of (#$MaleFn #$Sheep).")
(comment CourtJudgment-PCW "A specialization of #$NormativeSpecification.  Each instance of #$CourtJudgment-PCW is a decree by a #$Court-Judicial that a debt is due and payable.")
(comment HeadingABall "A #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$ProjectilePropelling.  Each instance of #$HeadingABall is an action in which an animal hits an airborne #$Ball with its head.  This is often done as part of playing #$Soccer.")
(comment annualEquivalentRate "An instance of #$ScalarIntervalSlot that relates an instance of #$FinancialAccount to an #$IntervalOnNumberLine.  (#$annualEquivalentRate ACCOUNT RATE) means that the annual equivalent rate (AER) for ACCOUNT is RATE. Note that the AER for a #$FinancialAccount is not necessarily the same as the yearly interest rate.")
(comment Spreadbetting "A specialization of #$MakingAnAgreement and #$MoneyTransaction.  Each instance of #$Spreadbetting is a bet concerning the direction in which the price of a stock or other financial instrument will go.  A person making a spread bet will either bet that a stock will exceed the upper value of a given spread of prices within a certain time frame, or bet that the stock will go below the lower value of the spread within that time frame.")
(comment ContractForDifferences "A specialization of #$MakingAnAgreement and #$MoneyTransaction.  Each instance of #$ContractForDifferences allows an investor to bet on the price movement of a stock or other finiancial instrument.  Instances of #$ContractForDifferences are thus similar to instances of #$Spreadbetting (q.v.), although profits from CFDs are subject to capital gains taxes while profits from spreadbetting are not, and one can often deal from inside the quoted spread in a CFD.")
(disjointWith Spreadbetting ContractForDifferences)
(comment SearchBox "A specialization of #$ComputerDisplayTypeInField-Transmitting.  Each instance of #$SearchBox is a type-in field where a user can enter a string of text in order to search for documents or web pages containing or related to that string.")
(comment TransitiveADVP-LocationFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly
one complement, an ADVP of place. Example: 'Sally went there.'")
(comment FrameForClauses "The class of #$SubcategorizationFrames which make sense for clauses, e.g. 'that-clause', 'wh-clause', and so on.")
(comment WHClauseFrameType "Frames used for wh-clauses.  Example: 'whether they were staying', 'what he wanted for lunch', 'why he missed class', and so on.")
(comment WhenClauseFrameType "Frames used for when-clauses.  Example: 'when to leave'.")
(comment AssociationOfPaymentClearingServices "An instance of #$TradeAssociation.  APACS, the UK payments association, is a trade association for institutions delivering payments services to end customers.")
(comment FTSEStockIndex "The collection of all instances of #$StockIndexGroup that are managed by the FTSE Group (c.f., #$FTSEGroup-Organization).")
(comment stockSize-Ask "A predicate used to state the number of shares being offered for sale at the asked market price of a company's #$Stock (of a given class, e.g. common or preferred) at a given time.  (#$stockSize-Ask NUM STOCK EXCHANGE MONEY) means that there are NUM shares of STOCK being offered for sale at the latter's current #$stockPrice-Ask (q.v.) at DATE on the exchange EXCHANGE.  Cf. #$stockSize-Bid.")
(comment IndependentBusiness "The collection of instances of #$Business that are not subsidiary organizations.")
(comment InterestRatePredicate "The collection of predicates used to descrbe interest rates, for example by stating how they are related to certain loans.")
(comment stockSize-Bid "A predicate used to state the number of shares being offered for purchase at the bid market price of a company's #$Stock (of a given class, e.g. common or preferred) at a given time.  (#$stockSize-Bid STOCK NUM DATE EXCHANGE) means that there are NUM shares of STOCK being offered for purchase at the latter's current #$stockPrice-Bid (q.v.) at DATE on the exchange EXCHANGE.  Cf. #$stockSize-Ask.")
(comment stockPrice-Close "A predicate used to state the previous day's closing price of a share of a certain company's #$Stock (of a certain \"class\", e.g. common or preferred).  (#$stockPrice-Close STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PRICE is the price per share for STOCK at the most recent market closing of EXCHANGE prior to DATE.  See also #$stockPrice-Open, #$stockPrice-Ask and #$stockPrice-Bid.")
(comment StockIndexGroupTypeByManagingOrganization "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType that facets #$StockIndexGroup.  Instances are specializations of #$StockIndexGroup, each member of which is created by (see #$createdBy) a common organization.")
(comment partiallyProtectedAgainst-RoleInType "A ternary predicate, an assertion of the form (#$partiallyProtectedAgainst-RoleInType OBJ TYPE ROLE) says that OBJ is partially protected against playing ROLE in some instance of TYPE. The notion of protection here is to be cashed out in terms of an agent's interests or desires being promoted through the prevention of the occurrence of some instance INS of TYPE such that (ROLE INS OBJ).  It is possible that the relevant agent is not OBJ.")
(comment stockPrice-High "A predicate used to state the highest price that a share of a #$PubliclyHeldCorporation's #$StockClass has traded at on the current day.  (#$stockPrice-High STOCKTYPE PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PRICE is the highest price paid for a share of STOCKTYPE so far on the #$CalendarDay that temporally subsumes DATE (i.e. the hightest price paid for such a share between that day's market opening and the end of DATE).  Before the market opens, and on days the market is closed, the high for the last day the market was open remains in effect.  Cf. #$stockPrice-Close.")
(comment computerFileSecuredByIDStringType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$ComputerFile-AIS to an #$IDStringType.  (#$computerFileSecuredByIDStringType FILE ID-TYPE) means that one must enter an appropriate instance of ID-TYPE in order to gain access to FILE.")
(comment InfluencingAnAgentToPlayRoleFn "(#$InfluencingAnAgentToPlayRoleFn SIT-TYPE ROLE) denotes the
collection of events in which an agent is influenced to play the role
ROLE in an instance of the specialization of #$Situation, SIT-TYPE.")
(comment influencingAnAgentToPlayRole "<code>(#$influencingAnAgentToPlayRole SIT-TYPE ROLE INFLUENCING-TYPE)</code> means that <code>INFLUENCING-TYPE</code> is the collection of events in which agents are influenced to play the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of the specialization of #$Situation, <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment stockPrice-Last "A predicate used to state the price that shares of a particular company's stock (of a given \"class\"; e.g. common or preferred) are currently being traded at.  Actually, this price is based on the most recent price-quote for that stock, and quotes are delayed by a set time (e.g. 20-minutes on the London Exchange) from the time of the actual trade.  More precisely, then, (#$stockPrice-Last STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that, as of DATE, the most recent price quoted on EXCHANGE for STOCK is PRICE.  Also see #$stockPrice-Ask and #$stockPrice-Bid.")
(comment stockPrice-Low "A predicate used to state the lowest price that a share of a company's #$Stock (of a given class, e.g. common or preferred) has traded at on the current day.  (#$stockPrice-High STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PRICE is the lowest price paid for a share of STOCK so far on the #$CalendarDay that temporally subsumes DATE (i.e. the lowest price paid for such a share between that day's market opening and the end of DATE).  Before the market opens, and on days the market is closed, the low for the last day the market was open remains in effect.  Cf. #$stockPrice-High.")
(comment stockPrice-Mid "A predicate used to state the midpoint between the \"ask price\" and the \"bid price\" market price of a single share of a company's #$Stock at a given time.  (#$stockPrice-Mid STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PRICE is the average of the #$stockPrice-Ask (q.v.) and the #$stockPrice-Bid (q.v.) for STOCK at DATE on EXCHANGE.")
(comment WH-SententialClausalFrame "This frame is used for wh-clauses having only one complement, a sentence. Example: 'how she did it'.")
(comment spreadForStockInExchangeOnDate "<code>(#$spreadForStockInExchangeOnDate STOCK-TYPE SPREAD DATE EXCHANGE)</code> holds just in case on DATE at EXCHANGE the spread (i.e the difference between the selling and buying price  -- see #$stockPrice-Bid and #$stockPrice-Ask) for stocks of STOCK-TYPE is SPREAD.")
(comment priceChangeIndicator "A #$QuantitySlot relating a specialization of #$Stock to a #$LevelOfChange.  (#$priceChangeIndicator STOCK CHANGE) means that the price of a share of STOCK has undergone CHANGE (where CHANGE is a qualitative measure of the difference between the last reported price of a share and the closing price of a share the previous day).")
(comment priceOfShareAtTime "A #$TernaryPredicate relating a specialization of #$Stock, a #$MonetaryValue, and a #$Date. (#$priceOfShareAtTime STOCK PRICE DATE) means that the price of a share of STOCK on DATE is PRICE.")
(comment numberOfSharesTraded "A #$ScalarIntervalSlot relating a specialization of #$Stock to a #$NonNegativeInteger.  (#$numberOfSharesTraded STOCK NUM) means that NUM of shares of STOCK have been traded today (or on the last day the market was open, if the market is closed today).")
(comment fiftyDayAverageTradingVolume "A #$ScalarIntervalSlot relating a specialization of #$Stock to a #$RationalNumber.  (#$fiftyDayAverageTradingVolume STOCK NUM) means that the average number of shares of STOCK traded per day for the prior fifty days is NUM.")
(comment fiftyTwoWeekHighDate "A #$BinaryPredicate relating a specialization of #$Stock to a #$CalendarDay. (#$fiftyTwoWeekHighDate STOCK DATE) means that the #$fiftyTwoWeekHigh for STOCK was reached on the day DATE.")
(comment fiftyTwoWeekLowDate "A #$BinaryPredicate relating a specialization of   #$Stock to a #$CalendarDay. (#$fiftyTwoWeekLowDate STOCK DATE) means that the #$fiftyTwoWeekLow for STOCK was reached on the day DATE.")
(comment marketCap "An #$QuantitySlot relating a #$LegalCorporation to a #$MonetaryValue.  (#$marketCap CORP VALUE) means that VALUE is the total value of all shares of stock in CORP multiplied by the most recent price per share.")
(comment sharesOutstanding "A #$ScalarIntervalSlot relating a specialization of #$Stock to a #$NonNegativeInteger.  (#$sharesOutstanding STOCK NUM) means that NUM is the number of shares of STOCK available for trading.")
(comment totalDividendsForCompany "A #$QuantitySlot relating a #$LegalCorporation to a #$MonetaryValue.  (#$totalDividendsForCompany CORP DIVIDENDS) means that DIVIDENDS is the amount of money paid out as dividends to the shareholders of CORP.")
(comment dividendPerShare "A #$QuantitySlot relating a specialization of #$Stock to a #$MonetaryValue.  (#$dividendPerShare STOCK DIVIDEND) means that DIVIDEND is the dividend given per share of STOCK.  This number is calculated by dividing the total dividends given by the company (see the predicate #$totalDividendsForCompany) by the total number of shares of STOCK issued by the company.")
(comment FacilitatingSomething "A #$FirstOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$FacilitatingSomething is an #$Event that makes some other event easier to perform or more likely to occur.  A notable specialization is #$ArrangingForSomething.")
(comment FacilitatingFn "A unary #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes a type of #$Event and returns the collection of all events in which that type of event is facilitated, i.e., made easier to perform or more likely to occur.")
(comment BenchmarkingSomething "Each instance of #$BenchmarkingSomething is an event in which a #$Benchmark is selected in order to serve as a standard against which some similar thing is compared.  An example would be the selection of a specification of the performance of #$StandardAndPoors500 as a benchmark against which the performance of one's #$InvestmentPortfolio is compared.")
(comment clauseSemTrans "This predicate expresses the relationship between a word functioning as the head of a clause, a word sense, a subcategorization frame, and a CycL expression used to denote the resulting clause.")
(comment BenchmarkingAnInvestmentPortfolio "A specialization of #$BenchmarkingSomething.  Each instance of #$BenchmarkingAnInvestmentPortfolio is an event in which a #$Benchmark is selected in order to serve as a standard against which the performance of an #$InvestmentPortfolio is compared.")
(comment facilitationTypeOfEventType "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a specialization of #$Event to a specialization of #$FacilitatingSomething.  (#$facilitationTypeOfEventType EVENT-TYPE FAC-TYPE) means that FAC-TYPE is the collection of all events in which instances of EVENT-TYPE are facilitated.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$FacilitatingFn (q.v.).")
(comment averageSpreadForStockExchange "<code>(#$averageSpreadForStockExchange EXCHANGE AVG-SPREAD)</code> holds just in case, in the context, the average spread (see #$spreadForStockInExchangeOnDate) for the stock exchange EXCHANGE is AVG-SPREAD.")
(comment linksToWebPage "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$ComputerDisplayLink to a #$WebPage-AIS.  (#$linksToWebPage LINK PAGE) means that activating LINK will take a user to PAGE.")
(comment Machismo-Pride "A specialization of #$PrideOfMembership.  Each instance of
this collection is the strong sense of masculine pride or superiority.
Behaviorly, this feeling is expressed in expecting traditional roles
for men and women, and forceful male behavior.")
(comment materialPublishedInMediaProduct "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$PublishedMaterial to a #$MediaProduct.  (#$materialPublishedInMediaProduct MATERIAL PRODUCT) means that MATERIAL is published in PRODUCT.")
(comment basicPriceOfType "<code>(#$basicPriceOfType OBJECT-TYPE MONEY)</code> means that to buy an instance of the specialization of #$TemporalThing <code>OBJECT-TYPE</code>, one needs to pay the #$MonetaryValue <code>MONEY</code>, where <code>MONEY</code> can be either a discrete quantity or an interval.  #$basicPriceOfType is a \"type-level\" version of #$basicPrice (q.v.).")
(comment InstantiationOfAISTypeFn "A function which takes a specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure and returns the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings which are physical instantiations of an instance of that collection.  See also #$InstantiationOfAISFn.")
(comment CreditCardInterestFreePeriod "A specialization of #$Situation.  Each instance of #$CreditCardInterestFreePeriod is a temporally continuous situation
that is instantiated under certain conditions after a purchase is made with a credit card.  A necessary condition for such an situation occuring is that, prior to the time the purchase is made, there is no outstanding balance on the account for the card used to make the purchase.")
(comment SearchingAnInformationStore "A specialization of #$LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing.  Each instance of #$SearchingAnInformationStore is an event in which an agent searches an #$InformationStore.  Examples include searching an #$Encyclopedia for entries related to #$WorldWarII, or searching the web (#$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource) for pictures of your favorite #$Celebrity.  A notable specialization is #$ElectronicDataSearching.")
(comment informationStoreSearched "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an instance of #$SearchingAnInformationStore to an #$InformationStore that is searched in that event.")
(comment StandingOrderForm-IBO "The information bearing object (on-line electronic or hard copy) that instantiates a #$StandingOrderForm-CW.")
(comment stockPrice-Open "A predicate used to state the most recent opening price of a share of a particular company's stock (of a certain \"class\", e.g. common or preferred).  (#$stockPrice-Close STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PRICE is the price per share for STOCK at the most recent market opening of EXCHANGE prior to DATE.  See also #$stockPrice-Close.")
(comment timeElapsedSinceLastPriceQuote "A predicate used to state the amount of time that has elapsed since the most recent price-quote for a given company's stock (see #$stockPrice-Last) was released.  (#$timeElapsedSinceLastPriceQuote STOCK DURATION DATE EXCHANGE) means that, as of the start of DATE, DURATION 
amount of time has passed since the most recent price-quote for STOCK was released by EXCHANGE (see #$stockPrice-Last).  Price-quotes for stocks are delayed by a set time (e.g. 20-minutes on the London Exchange) from the time of the actual trade.")
(comment CancellingAStandingOrder "The act of cancelling a #$StandingOrderInstruction, as undertaken by a citizen of the UK.")
(comment stockTypeIssuedBy "(#$stockIssuedBy STOCK-TYPE AGENT) means that STOCK-TYPE is a collection of shares of #$Stock of a common type that are issued by Agent.")
(comment stockTypeListedWith "(#$stockIssuedBy STOCK-TYPE EXCHANGE) means that STOCK-TYPE is a collection of shares of #$Stock of a common type that are listed with EXCHANGE.  To state that a company's stocks are list with exchange use #$stockListedWith.")
(comment StandingOrder "#$StandingOrder is a sub-collection of (#$OnlineActivityTypeFn #$Paying) that is characterized by the creditors having access to a person's accounts so that they can make withdrawals of any amount at any time, provided the have notified the account owner in advance of the withdrawal.")
(disjointWith StandingOrder DirectDebit)
(comment CreditCardWithLongInterestFreePeriod "A specialization of #$CreditCardWithInterestFreePeriod.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card with a long interest free period.  By \"long\" we mean between 6 or 8 weeks.")
(comment CreditCardWithShortInterestFreePeriod "A specialization of #$CreditCardWithInterestFreePeriod.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card with a long interest free period.  By \"short\" we mean between fewer than 4 weeks.")
(disjointWith CreditCardWithLongInterestFreePeriod CreditCardWithShortInterestFreePeriod)
(comment LoyaltyScheme "A #$FirstOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$LoyaltyScheme is an #$Offer which provides rewards for being loyal to some #$CommercialOrganization.  For example, credit card companies sometimes offer cash back for using a certain card, and automobile companies sometimes offer rebates on new cars to existing owners.")
(comment CreditCardInterestFreePeriod-Long "A specialization of #$CreditCardInterestFreePeriod.  Each instance of #$CreditCardInterestFreePeriod-Long is a temporally continuous situation
that is instantiated under certain conditions after a purchase is made with a credit card.  It is the collection of long situations of this type offered by credit card agreements -- usually \"long\" in this context means between 4 and 8 weeks.")
(comment CreditCardInterestFreePeriod-Short "A specialization of #$CreditCardInterestFreePeriod.  Each instance of #$CreditCardInterestFreePeriod-Long is a temporally continuous situation
that is instantiated under certain conditions after a purchase is made with a credit card.  It is the collection of long situations of this type offered by credit card agreements -- usually \"short\" in this context means between 0 and 4 weeks.")
(disjointWith CreditCardInterestFreePeriod-Short CreditCardInterestFreePeriod-Long)
(comment GerundPhraseFrameType "This frame is used for words that take a gerund phrase complement, possibly in addition to other complements.")
(comment thingOffered "An #$ActorSlot that relates an #$Offer to a #$Thing.  (#$thingOffered OFFER THING) means that THING is one of the things that is offered by the #$offerer of OFFER.")
(comment Reward "A #$FirstOrderCollection and specialization of #$TemporalThing.  Each instance of #$Reward is something that is, or is intended to be, given to some agent as a reward, in an act of #$Rewarding.")
(comment offerer "An #$ActorSlot that relates an #$Offer to an #$IntelligentAgent.  (offerer OFFER AGT) means that AGT is does the offering in OFFER.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-PPGerundObjectFrameType "Frames used for verbs that take an NP complement followed by a PP complement having a gerund object. Example 'Fred prevented Sally from leaving'.")
(comment totalInvestmentEarningsForStockTypeBoughtDuring "<code>(#$totalInvestmentEarningsForStockTypeBoughtDuring STOCK-TYPE VALUE TIME-PERIOD)<MT T PAR></code> holds in MT at T to PAR just in case the total earnings of stock of STOCK-TYPE bought during TIME-PERIOD is VALUE as of T (to a granularity of PAR).  Note that TIME-PERIOD refers to the date or time period during which the stocks were bought, not necessarily the period during which they gained or lost value. ")
(comment URLReferentFn "An expression of the form (#$URLReferentFn URL) is used to pick out the instance of #$ComputerDataArtifact that is the designated by the #$UniformResourceLocator URL.  This is a temporally qualifiable relation.")
(comment referentOfURL "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$URLReferentFn.")
(comment WordNetSynsetImportStatus-ReadyForExactMatching "The collection of #$WordNet-Version2_0 synsets that are ready for exact matching with Cyc concepts.")
(comment fosterMother "An instance of #$FamilyRelationSlot and a specialization of
both #$fosterParent and #$mother. (#$fosterMother CHILD MOTHER) means
that the instance of #$FemaleAnimal MOTHER is the foster mother of
CHILD. This means that although MOTHER is fulfilling the caregiving
role of #$mother for CHILD, typically only a temporary arrangement,
MOTHER is not the legal mother of CHILD.")
(comment fosterParent "An instance of #$PersonalAssociationPredicate and
#$FamilyRelationSlot.  <code>(#$fosterParent CHILD PARENT)</code> means that
PARENT is an instance of #$Person filling, typically temporarily, the caregiving
role of parent for CHILD without being the legal parent of CHILD.<p>
For example, in the #$DCSuperheroesMt, it is true that (#$fosterParent
#$ClarkKent MarthaKent).")
(comment fosterFather "An instance of #$FamilyRelationSlot and a specialization of
both #$fosterParent and #$father.  (#$fosterFather CHILD FATHER) means
that the instance of #$MaleAnimal FATHER is the foster father of
CHILD.  This means that although FATHER is fulfilling the caregiving
role of #$father for CHILD, typically only a temporary arrangement,
FATHER is not the legal father of CHILD.")
(disjointWith PaymentPlanWithEqualValueInstallments PaymentPlanWithInstallmentsAtIrregularIntervalsOrForVaryingAmounts)
(comment agreementCOC "(#$agreementCOC AGREEMENT COC) means that COC is the #$CodeOfConduct that obligates each agreeing agent (cf. #$agreeingAgents) in AGREEMENT.")
(comment organizationRecruitsAgentType "<code>(#$organizationRecruitsAgentType ORG
AGENT-TYPE)</code> relates an instance of #$Organization ORG to the
specialization of #$IntelligentAgent from which ORG actively seeks to
recruit members.<p> For example,
<code>(#$organizationRecruitsAgentType #$LebaneseHizballah
#$SunniMuslimPerson)</code> means that #$LebaneseHizballah recruits
its members from the collection of #$SunniMuslimPerson.")
(comment organizationIsRegularServiceProvider "(#$organizationIsRegularServiceProvider AGT-1 ORGANIZATION-TYPE AGT-2) means that   AGT-1 has a relationship with AGT-2, such that if AGT-1 needs a service that is provided by instances of ORGANIZATION-TYPE, by default they will go to AGT-2 first.")
(comment PercentageRate "Each instance of #$PercentageRate is an #$IntervalOnNumberLine taken with respect to an amount of time.  An example of a #$PercentageRate is ((#$PerFn #$Unity #$YearsDuration) (#$Percent 12.9)) which represents the rate of 12.9% per year.  Note that this rate can also be expressed, equivalently, as ((#$PerFn #$Unity #$YearsDuration) 0.129).")
(comment agreementGovernsAccountTenderObject "<code>(#$agreementGovernsAccountTenderObject TENDER-OBJ AGREEMENT)</code> means that the instance of #$LegalAgreement, <code>AGREEMENT</code>, governs the terms of the account drawn upon when the instance of #$FinancialAccountTenderObject <code>TENDER-OBJ</code> is used.  See also #$agreementForAccount and #$accountOfTenderObject.")
(comment loanAgreementRequiresOfCreditor "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a creditor is required, by the terms of a loan agreement, to play a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementRequiresOfCreditor AGREEMENT SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that the #$LoanAgreement <code>AGREEMENT</code> specifies that the creditor is required to play the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment loanAgreementTypeRequiresOfCreditor "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a creditor is required, by the terms of a type of loan agreement, to play a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementTypeRequiresOfCreditor AGREEMENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that entering into an instance of <code>AGREEMENT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$LoanAgreement) requires the creditor to play the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CreditCardWithInterestFreePeriod "A specialization of #$CreditCard-RevolvingAccount.  Each instance of this collection is a credit card with an interest free period (see #$CreditCardInterestFreePeriod).")
(comment loanAgreementRequiresOfBorrower "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a borrower is required, by the terms of a loan agreement, to play a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementRequiresOfBorrower AGREEMENT SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that the #$LoanAgreement <code>AGREEMENT</code> specifies that the borrower is required to play the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>. Cf. #$loanAgreementRequiresOfCreditor.")
(comment loanAgreementTypeRequiresOfBorrower "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a borrower is required, by the terms of a type of loan agreement, to play a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementTypeRequiresOfBorrower AGREEMENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that entering into an instance of <code>AGREEMENT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$LoanAgreement) requires the borrower to play the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.  Cf. #$loanAgreementTypeRequiresOfCreditor.")
(comment loanAgreementForbidsBorrower "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a borrower is forbidden by the terms of a loan agreement, to play a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementForbidsBorrower AGREEMENT SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that the #$LoanAgreement <code>AGREEMENT</code> specifies that the borrower is forbidden from playing the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>. Cf. #$loanAgreementForbidsCreditor.")
(comment loanAgreementForbidsCreditor "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a creditor is forbidden by the terms of a loan agreement, to play a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementForbidsBorrower AGREEMENT SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that the #$LoanAgreement <code>AGREEMENT</code> specifies that the creditor is forbidden from playing the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>. Cf. #$loanAgreementForbidsCreditor.")
(comment loanAgreementTypeForbidsCreditor "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a creditor is forbidden, by the terms of a type of loan agreement, from playing a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementTypeForbidsCreditor AGREEMENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that entering into an instance of <code>AGREEMENT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$LoanAgreement) forbids the creditor from playing the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>. Cf. #$loanAgreementTypeForbidsBorrower.")
(comment loanAgreementTypeForbidsBorrower "This ternary predicate is used to indicate that a borrower is forbidden, by the terms of a type of loan agreement, from playing a particular role in a particular kind of situation.  <code>(#$loanAgreementTypeForbidsBorrower AGREEMENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that entering into an instance of <code>AGREEMENT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$LoanAgreement) forbids the borrower from playing the #$Role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation that is an instance of the subcollection of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.  Cf. #$loanAgreementTypeForbidsCreditor.")
(comment AccruingInterestOnALoan "A specialization of #$IncreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount.  Each instance of #$AccruingInterestOnALoan is an event in which an agent accumulates interest on an outstanding loan balance.")
(comment paymentObligationValue "(#$paymentObligationValue OBLIGATION MONEY) means that MONEY is the instance of #$MonetaryValue that is the value of the payment obligation (see #$PaymentObligation) OBLIGATION.  For example, (#$paymentObligationValue DryCleaningBill001 (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 3.5)) means that the value of drycleaning bill 001 is $3.50.")
(comment obligingAgents "(#$obligingAgents OBLIGATION AGENT) means that the intelligent agent AGENT is owed something (e.g., money) as specified in OBLIGATION, an instance of #$Obligation (a type of #$NormativeSpecification).  See also #$obligatedAgents.  Note that #$obligingAgents and #$obligatedAgents do not stand in the #$negationPreds relation, as OBLIGATION could be broad enough or complicated enough (as in a service contract), where one can play both roles.  However, some obligations, e.g., instances of #$PaymentObligation, are such that no one can stand in both roles simultaneously.")
(comment itemsCompared "(#$itemsCompared COMPARING ITEM-1 ITEM-2) means that ITEM-1 and ITEM-2 are compared in the instance of #$Comparing, COMPARING.")
(comment itemBenchmarkedAgainst "(#$itemBenchmarkedAgainst COMPARING SUBJECT BENCHMARK) means that SUBJECT is compared to BENCHMARK, for purposes of gaining information about SUBJECT.  See also #$comparisonSubject and #$benchmarkRole.")
(comment benchmarkRole "A specializtion of #$itemCompared. (#$benchmarkRole COMPARISON BENCHMARK) means that in the instance COMPARISON of #$Comparing, BENCHMARK plays the role of a benchmark, or standard, against which something else (that which plays the #$comparisonSubject role) is compared.")
(comment comparisonSubject "A specialization of #$evaluee-Direct and #$itemCompared, (#$comparisonSubject COMPARE SUBJECT) means that the instance of #$Comparing COMPARE is, by design, an attempt to gain information about SUBJECT by comparing it with one or more other items.  Contrast with #$benchmarkRole.")
(comment BuyingWhileOnATrip "A collection of events; a subset of #$Buying.  Each instance of this collection is a buying that occurs as a subevent of some #$VacationTrip to a place the #$buyer is not a resident of.")
(comment stockPriceChange-CloseToLast "A predicate used to state the difference in value that a share of a particular company's stock has undergone between the previous day's close and its most-recently quoted price on the current day.  (#$stockPriceChange-CloseToLast STOCK PRICECHANGE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PRICECHANGE is the difference in price between (i) the #$stockPrice-Close for a share of STOCK on EXCHANGE for the day before DATE and (ii) (#$stockPrice-Last STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE).  See also #$stockPercentageChange-CloseToLast.")
(comment stockPercentageChange-CloseToLast "A predicate used to state the difference in value, in terms of percentage, that a share of a particular company's stock has undergone between the previous day's close and its most-recently quoted price on the current day.  (#$stockPriceChange-CloseToLast STOCK PERCENTCHANGE DATE EXCHANGE) means that PERCENTCHANGE is the percentage of increase or decrease in price for a share of STOCK between (i) the #$stockPrice-Close for a share of STOCK on EXCHANGE for the day before DATE and (ii) (#$stockPrice-Last STOCK PRICE DATE EXCHANGE).  See also #$stockPriceChange-CloseToLast.")
(comment sksiSourceActivated "(#$sksiSourceActivated SKS) is true iff SKS has been turned
'activated' for querying. This is not sufficient alone to guarantee
that Cyc can query SKS. In particular, it may the case that SKS has
been activated but the removal module data structures for SKS have not
been registered yet (see #$sksiSourceRegistered). Furthermore, it may
be the case that Cyc cannot establish a connection to SKS (see
#$sksiSourceAccessible). Finally, see also #$sksiSourceQueryable which
checks all three conditions.")
(comment sksiSourceAccessible "(#$sksiSourceAccessible SKS) is true iff it is possible for
Cyc to establish a connection to SKS. That is, i) if SKS is a database
then Cyc should be able to open up an SQL connection to it; ii) if SKS
is a web page then an empty http request to it should succeed (which
basically amounts to being able to open a TCP connection to it); iii)
if SKS is a file hash table then Cyc should be able to open it. See
also #$sksiSourceRegistered, #$sksiSourceActivated, and
#$sksiSourceQueryable.")
(comment sksiSourceRegistered "(#$sksiSourceRegistered SKS) is true iff the SKSI removal
module data structures for SKS have been 'registered'. Note, however,
that source registration is not sufficient to guarantee that it can be
successfully queried from Cyc. Additionally, it must be true that a
connection to the source can be established (See
#$sksiSourceAccessible) and that the removal modules have been
'acivated' (see #$sksiSourceActivated). SKS is queryable (see
#$sksiSourceQueryable) iff all three of these conditions are true.")
(comment sksiSourceQueryable "(#$sksiSourceQueryable SKS) is true
iff (#$and (#$sksiSourceRegistered SKS) (#$sksiSourceActivated SKS)
(#$sksiSourceAccessible SKS)) is true.")
(comment PaymentPlanAccordingToWhichAnyMonthlyBalanceMustBePaidInFull "A specialization of #$PaymentPlanWithInstallmentsAtIrregularIntervalsOrForVaryingAmounts.  Each instance of #$PaymentPlanAccordingToWhichAnyMonthlyBalanceMustBePaidInFull is a #$RepaymentPlan that requires the borrower to pay off his balance in full each month.")
(comment CreditRecord "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$CreditRecord is a record of a person's credit history that is created and maintained by a credit reporting agency.")
(comment Stock-NonUK "Each instance of #$Stock-NonUK is an instance of #$Stock that is (or can be) traded on a non-British stock exchange.")
(comment NationalSavingsAndInvestments-UK "A part of the British government.  Notably, administers the Premium Bonds program.")
(comment StockMarketInvesting "A #$TemporalObjectType and specialization of #$StockTrading.  Each instance of #$StockMarketInvesting is an #$Investing in which someone buys #$Stocks.")
(comment MarketPeak "A specialization of #$Market.  Each instance of #$MarketPeak is an event in which a #$Market reaches a (temporary) peak, i.e. an event in which the market reaches a high value from which it proceeds to decrease to a significant degree (and for a significant amount of time).  Note that instances of #$MarketPeak are not necessarily instantaneous, as the market may stay at its \"peak\" level for an extended period of time.")
(comment MarketTrough "A specialization of #$Market.  Each instance of #$MarketPeak is an event in which a #$Market reaches a (temporary) trough, i.e. an event in which the market reaches a low value from which it proceeds to increase to a significant degree (and for a significant amount of time).  Note that instances of #$MarketTrough are not necessarily instantaneous, as the market may stay at its \"trough\" level for an extended period of time.")
(disjointWith MarketTrough MarketPeak)
(comment performingActionTypeDuringEventTypeFostersSitType "A #$TernaryPredicate that relates an #$Action type to an #$Event type to a #$Situation type.  (#$performingActionTypeDuringEventTypeFostersSitType ACT-TYPE EVT-STYPE SIT-TYPE) means that performing an instance ACT-TYPE while EVT-TYPE is occurring makes it more likely that SIT-TYPE will obtain.  For example, (#$performingActionTypeDuringEventTypeFostersSitType #$TransportInvolvingADriver #$SnowProcess #$VehicleAccident) means that driving while it is snowing makes it more likely that a vehicle accident will occur.")
(comment PermanentInterestBearingShare-Bond "A specialization of #$CorporateBond-Agreement. Each instance of #$PermanentInterestBearingShare-Bond is a bond issued by an instance of #$BuildingSociety.")
(comment CorporateBond-NonInvestmentGrade "A specialization of #$CorporateBond-Agreement.  Each instance of #$CorporateBond-NonInvestmentGrade is a bond issued by a company whose finances are relatively less secure than those of other companies issuing bonds")
(comment ConvertibleBond "A specialization of #$CorporateBond-Agreement.  Each instance of #$ConvertibleBond is a corporate bond that can be converted at a later date into shares of stock in the issuing company.")
(comment CorporateBond-InvestmentGrade "A specialization of #$CorporateBond-Agreement.  Each instance of #$CorporateBond-InvestmentGrade is a bond issued by a large, reputable company.")
(comment informationTransferViaProtocol "<code>(#$informationTransferViaProtocol TRANS PROT)</code> means that the information transfer event <code>TRANS</code> involves communication via the communication protocol <code>PROT</code>.")
(comment FinancialFuture "A type of contract based on interest sensitive financial instruments.")
(comment SellingShort "#$SellingShort is a process where an investor borrows shares in a stock from an owner.  The borrower sells the shares and then buys them back off the market and returns them to the original owner.  If the shares have dropped in price between the selling and the buying, then the investor will make a profit on the transaction.")
(comment eventTypeRequiresAgentTypeForRole "<code>(#$eventTypeRequiresAgentTypeForRole AGENT-TYPE EVENT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds just in case anything playing the role ROLE in EVENT-TYPE is required to be an instance of AGENT-TYPE.  This is intended to be a English parsing/generation friendly way of stating: <code>(#$interArgIsa ROLE 1 EVENT-TYPE 2 AGENT-TYPE)</code>.")
(comment GoldCard "A subcollection of #$CreditCard.  Each instance of #$GoldCard is a credit card.  According to the Motley Fool UK website \"Usually they require a salary over a certain limit and they often entail an annual fee.\".")
(comment PlatinumCard "A subcollection of #$CreditCard.  Each instance of #$PlatinumCard is a credit card.  According to the Motley Fool UK website \"Usually they require a salary over a certain limit and they often entail an annual fee.\".")
(comment BrowserRequestsASecureConnection "A specialization of #$NetworkPropagation and #$ComputerActivity.  Each instance of #$BrowserRequestsASecureConnection is an event in which a running browser requests a SSL connection.")
(comment ExhibitingCourage "Each instance of #$ExhibitingCourage is an #$Action in which an agent exhibits courage -- i.e. the ability to face danger with poise and resolve.")
(comment ProgramSendsSSLCertificate "A specialization of #$NetworkPropagation and #$ComputerActivity.  Each instance of #$ProgramSendsSSLCertificate is an event in which a running program sends a SSL certificate to another process.")
(comment ProgramSendsPublicKey "A specialization of #$NetworkPropagation and #$ComputerActivity.  Each instance of #$ProgramSendsPublicKey is an event in which a running program sends a public key to another process.")
(comment StatementOfAffairs-AccountingReport "A specialization of #$AccountingReport.  Each instance of #$StatementOfAffairs-AccountingReport is a financial document detailing a person's income, outgoing expenses, and debts.")
(comment BrowserReadsSSLCertificate "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of #$BrowserReadsSSLCertificate is an event in which a running program reads an SSL certificate.")
(comment ProgramDevelopsSessionKey "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of #$ProgramDevelopsSessionKey is an event in which a program generates a number and scrambles it using the public key for the session. This is done in such a way that it can only be unscrambled using a different number, the private key.")
(comment studentOverdraftLimit "Some banks offer interest-free overdrafts up to a certain limit for student accounts. (#$studentOverdraftLimit ACCOUNT LIMIT) means that ACCOUNT can be overdrawn by amount LIMIT without incurring interest. See #$OverdrawingABankAccount")
(comment ProgramTransmitsSessionKey "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of #$ProgramTransmitsSessionKey is an event in which a program sends the number it generated in an instance of #$ProgramDevelopsSessionKey.")
(comment ProgramReceivesSessionKey "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of #$ProgramReceivesSessionKey is an event in which a program receives a scrambled session key and unscrambles it with a private key.")
(comment ProgramProcessesCommunicateWithSessionKeyThroughScramblingSystem "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of #$ProgramProcessesCommunicateWithSessionKeyThroughScramblingSystem is an event in which program processes encode and decode their messages by feeding them, along with the session key, through a scrambling system such as Triple DES (Data Encryption Standard).")
(comment costBenefitSentenceForSitType-Quaternary "<code>(#$costBenefitSentenceForSitType-Quaternary SIT-TYPE-1 SIT-TYPE-2 ROLE SENTENCE)</code> holds just in case SENTENCE is a sentence that describes some relevant cost/benefit for individuals who play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE-1 or SIT-TYPE-2.")
(comment isKeepingSecretAboutType "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$KeepingTypeSecretFn")
(disjointWith RevealingInformation ConcealingInformation)
(comment ConcealingInformation "The collection of actions where an agent deliberately acts so as to keep other agents' from gaining some information.")
(comment KeepingTypeSecretFn "An expression of the form (#$KeepingTypeSecreteFn TYPE) represents the sub-collection of #$ConcealingInformation where the type of information is about some instance of TYPE.")
(comment CreditCardStatement "The subcollection of #$FinancialDocument where the subject of the document is an instance of #$CreditCardAccount.")
(comment PersonalIdentificationNumber "A number used for accessing accounts, typically financial accounts.")
(comment AutomobileBreakdownInsurance-RoadsideAndHomeRescue "A specialization of #$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance.  Each instance of #$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance-RoadsideAndHomeRescue provides coverage for labor and towing costs associated with a breakdown at home or on the road.")
(comment AutomobileBreakdownInsurance "A specialization of #$AutomobileInsurance.  Each instance of #$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance is an insurance policy for automobile malfunctions.")
(comment AutomobileBreakdownInsurance-RoadsideRescueAndRecoveryPlus "A specialization of #$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance.  Each instance of #$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance-RoadsideRescueAndRecoveryPlus provides all the coverage of a 
#$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance-RoadsideAndHomeRescue policy, and covers, in addition, either the cost of providing a rental car (or other form of transportation) to get one to one's destination, or the cost of accomodations in a local hotel while one waits for his car to be repaired.")
(comment AutomobileBreakdownInsurance-RoadsideRescue "A specialization of #$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance.  Each instance of #$AutomobileBreakdownInsurance-RoadsideRescue provides coverage for labor and towing costs associated with a roadside breakdown.")
(comment SavingsRelatedShareOption "A collection of #$StockOptions that are distributed by many UK companies to their employees, and linked to monthly savings plans.  SRSOs give holders the right (but not the obligation) to buy shares at a pre-determined price at some future date. They are usually \"exercisable\" from three to ten years after the date they are granted. Also known as Sharesave or Save As You Earn (SAYE).")
(comment InsurancePlan-JointCoverage "A specialization of #$InsurancePlan.  Each instance of #$InsurancePlan-JointCoverage is an insurance plan that covers some agents (see #$insuredAgent) in addition to the #$policyHolder.")
(comment CriticalIllnessInsurance "A specialization of #$MedicalInsurance.  Each instance of #$CriticalIllnessInsurance is an insurance policy that pays out a lump sum in case the person covered suffers from a serious illness, or has to undergo surgery to treat that illness.")
(comment AllEmployeeShareOwnershipPlan "A type of #$EconomicAgreement that some UK companies offer to any employee who wishes to participate.  An AESOP enables an employee to buy company stock with pre-tax income and be given free shares by their employer at the same time.")
(comment costBenefitSummaryOfSitTypeWRTThingInsteadOfThing "<code>(#$costBenefitSummaryOfSitTypeWRTThingInsteadOfThing SIT-TYPE THING-1 THING-2
ROLE SENT)</code> holds just in case SENT is a cost benefit sentence relevant to deciding whether one should use THING-1 to ROLE in SIT-TYPE instead of THING-2.  For example, if SENT is relevant when choosing between AOL and Earthlink as an online provider, then (#$costBenefitSummaryOfSitTypeWRTThingInsteadOfThing (#$ServiceRelatedFn #$Internet) #$AmericaOnlineInc #$EarthLinkNetworkInc  #$providerOfService SENT) holds.")
(comment FinancialOmbudsmanService-UK "A UK #$GovernmentAgency that handles complaints on financial products.")
(comment NoticeOfDisassociation-UK "A specialization of #$LegalDocument.  A type of document one can submit to a UK credit reference agency if                     someone else's credit history is confused with theirs. This is a way to claim certain                       debts don't belong to one.")
(comment PensionRelease "A specialization of #$FinancialActivity.  Each instance of #$PensionRelease is an act of converting a pension (see #$RetirementAccount) into a lump-sum of cash and an annuity.")
(comment IncomeDrawdownRetirement-UK "A specialization of #$PensionRelease (q.v.) available in the UK wherein one delays buying the annuity until the age of 75.  In the meantime, the remaining portion of one's pension fund stays invested and hopefully keeps growing.")
(comment PhasedRetirement-UK "A specialization of #$PensionRelease (q.v.) available in the UK wherein one takes only part of one's #$CompanyPension at the time of retirement, leaving the rest until later.")
(comment HirePurchaseAgreement-UK "A specialization of #$SalesContract pertaining to a method of buying a car on credit in the UK, wherein the finance provider owns the car until the customer has made every repayment.  Cf.  #$PersonalContractPurchase-UK.")
(comment PersonalContractPurchase-UK "A specialization of #$Contract and #$EconomicAgreement pertaining to a method of renting a car in the UK with the option of buying it.  Similar to a #$HirePurchaseAgreement-UK (q.v.), except that the costumer is not required to buy the car at the end of the agreement.")
(comment propertyMortgaged "<code>(#$propertyMortgaged AGREEMENT PROP)</code> means that in the #$EnteringIntoAMortgageAgreement <code>AGREEMENT</code>, the property that is mortgaged is <code>PROPERTY</code>.")
(comment GettingAMortgageOnAHouseToRent "A specialization of #$Investing.  Each instance of #$GettingAMortgageOnAHouseToRent is an event in which someone acquires an instance of #$BuyToLetMortgage in an instance of #$GettingAMortgageOnAHouseToRent, and then procedes to rent the house to someone else.")
(comment InvestingInAHedgeFund "A specialization of #$Investing.  Each instance of #$InvestingInAHedgeFund is a complex event in which a wealthy investor buys into a hedge fund (see #$HedgeFund), and the fund manager uses (typically high-risk, high-payoff) strategies to grow the fund.  Hedge fund managers usually have the prospect of profit due to a high commission rate as motivation for performance.")
(comment TransitiveAdverbFrameType "Frames used for verbs that have a single ADVP complement. Examples include 'runs quickly', 'eats often', and so on.")
(comment TerrorismOntologyConstant "The collection of general constants related to representing the domain of terrorism.")
(comment ContractNote "The collection of \"Contract notes\".  A contract note is a financial statement sent out to investors in the UK after a trading session.  It lists which shares were purchased or sold and the selling and or buying cost.")
(comment RefinedFn "An instance of #$GenlsPreservingFunction. #$RefinedFn takes
for its value a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible, <b>TYPE</b>, and
returns all instances of <b>TYPE</b> that have been refined, which means the
unwanted materials have been removed from <code>(#$UnrefinedFn TYPE)</code> to
leave a purer product.<p> For example, <code>(#$RefinedFn Sugar-Generic)</code> has
been processed to transform instances of #$SugarcanePlant into edible
sugar.")
(comment UnrefinedFn "An instance of #$GenlsPreservingFunction. #$UnrefinedFn
takes for its value a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible <b>TYPE</b> and
denotes all instances of unrefined <b>TYPE</b>.<p> For example,
<code>(#$UnrefinedFn #$Oil)</code> denotes all instances of unrefined oil,
that is, oil that has not undergone a refining process to become an
instance of #$PetroleumProduct-Refined. See also #$RefinedFn and
#$RefiningFn.")
(comment HeavyIndustryFacility "A specialization of #$FactoryBuildingComplex.  Each instance of
this collection is a plant that engages in heavy industry
manufacturing activities.  These industries are those like the
#$OilIndustry, which convert large volumes of raw materials or
partially processed materials into products of higher value.")
(comment refinedMaterialOfType "An instance of #$FunctionalPredicate which relates a type of refined substance, <b>REFINED-COLL</b>, to the type of substance <b>COLL</b> of which <b>REFINED-COLL</b> is the refined form.<p>
For example, <code>(#$refinedMaterialOfType #$PetroleumProduct-Refined
#$Oil)</code> means that #$PetroleumProduct-Refined is the refined
form of #$Oil.")
(comment unrefinedMaterialTypeOfType "An instance of #$FunctionalPredicate which relates a type of
unrefined substance, <b>UNREFINED-COLL</b>, to the type of substance COLL of
which <b>UNREFINED-COLL</b> is the unrefined form.<p>
For example, <code>(#$unrefinedMaterialTypeOfType #$Petroleum-CrudeOil
#$Oil)</code> means that #$Petroleum-CrudeOil is the unrefined form of
#$Oil.  See also #$UnrefinedFn.")
(comment ContentsInsurance "A specialization of #$InsurancePlan.  Each instance of #$ContentsInsurance is an insurance plan that insures against the loss of the contents of one's residence.")
(comment AutomobileAccidentInsurance-ThirdPartyFireAndTheft "A specialization of #$AutomobileInsurance.  Each instance of #$AutomobileAccidentInsurance-ThirdPartyFireAndTheft is an insurance policy that will pay any damage done to someone else in any accident caused by the policy holder's driving. In addition, it will also provide protection in case the policy holder's car is stolen or catches fire.")
(comment IncomeProtectionInsurance "A specialization of #$InsurancePlan.  Each instance of #$IncomeProtectionInsurance is an insurance policy that pays the holder an income if he or she becomes unable to work due to a disability arising from injury or illness.")
(comment AutomobileAccidentInsurance-FullyComprehensive "A specialization of #$AutomobileInsurance.  Each instance of #$AutomobileAccidentInsurance-FullyComprehensive is an insurance policy that will cover the cost of repairs no matter who is to blame for the accident.")
(comment AutomobileAccidentInsurance-ThirdPartyOnly "A specialization of #$AutomobileInsurance.  Each instance of #$AutomobileAccidentInsurance-ThirdPartyOnly is an insurance policy that will pay any damage done to someone else in any accident caused by the policy holder's driving.")
(disjointWith PassivizableFrame ActiveVoiceOnlyFrameType)
(comment ActiveVoiceOnlyFrameType "Frames used for verbs having an active voice construction that cannot be passivized.")
(disjointWith PassivizableFrame PassiveVoiceOnlyFrameType)
(comment PassiveVoiceOnlyFrameType "Frames used for verbs having a passive voice construction with no active voice alternation.")
(comment PassiveVoiceOnlyFrameFn "(#$PassiveVoiceOnlyFrameFn FRAME) returns a passive voice
only version of FRAME. Example: Use (#$PassiveVoiceOnlyFrameFn
(#$PPCompFrameFn #$TransitivePPFrameType #$In-TheWord)) for 'is
located' as in 'The library is located in the east wing.'")
(comment ActiveVoiceOnlyFrameFn "(#$ActiveVoiceOnlyFrameFn FRAME) returns an active voice
only version of FRAME -- it cannot be passivized. Example: use
(#$ActiveVoiceOnlyFrameFn #$TransitiveNPFrame) with the verb 'to bear' when
it takes as subject a #$PlantBLO, as in the construction 'The tree
bore fruit'.")
(comment OnlineBankingSecurity-Technology "A specialization of #$DefenseSystem.  Each instance of #$OnlineBankingSecurity-Technology is a system designed to protect the privacy and integrity of the information transmitted during online banking transactions and activities.")
(comment ProtectionOfOnlineBanking "A specialization of #$ProtectionSituation. Each instance of #$ProtectionOfOnlineBanking is a situation in which the privacy and integrity of the information tranferred during online banking is protected.")
(comment FactoryBuildingComplex "A specialization of #$BuildingCluster.  Each instance of
this collection is a group of buildings, typically one or more
#$FactoryBuildings and the associated administrative and other support
buildings.  Instances of #$FactoryBuildingComplex are involved with
manufacturing products or partially processed materials for futher
manufacturing.")
(comment FinancialSettlementSystem "A collection of systems designed to mediate financial transactions.  The CREST system is a prominent example from the U.K..")
(comment Stock-Cum-Dividend "Each instance of #$Stock-Cum-Dividend is a share of stock that trades with dividend rights.  When a share of this collection is sold just before the date it becomes entitled to a dividend, the share is sold cum-dividend. The purchaser of the share(s) then receives the dividend. ")
(comment DividendReinvestmentPlan "The collection of dividend reinvestment plans (DRiP).  Each instance is a schedule that enables one to reinvest his/her divident earnings with little or no transaction fees.")
(comment agentMakesProfitInTimeInterval "A #$TernaryPredicate that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$MonetaryValue to a #$TimeInterval.  (#$agentMakesProfitInTimeInterval AGENT VALUE INTERVAL) means that AGENT makes VALUE in profits during INTERVAL.  For example, (#$agentMakesProfitInTimeInterval XYZCorp (#$MillionDollars 10) (#$YearFn 2000)) means that XYZ Corp.  made ten million dollars in profits in 2000.")
(comment agentMakesProfitInTimeInterval-BeforeInterestAndTax "A #$TernaryPredicate and specialization of #$agentMakesProfitInTimeInterval that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$MonetaryValue to a #$TimeInterval.  (#$agentMakesProfitInTimeInterval-BeforeInterestAndTax AGENT VALUE INTERVAL) means that AGENT makes VALUE in profits, before interest and taxes, during INTERVAL.  For example, (#$agentMakesProfitInTimeInterval-BeforeInterestAndTax XYZCorp (#$MillionDollars 10) (#$YearFn 2000)) means that XYZ Corp.  made ten million dollars in profits, before interest and taxes, in 2000.")
(comment StockSplit "A specialization of both #$FinancialActivity.  Each instance of #$StockSplit is an event in which a corporation doubles the number of shares of #$Stock it has issued (see #$stockIssuedBy), at the same time halving the value of each share.  Immediately after a #$StockSplit, each shareholder in the company has twice the number of shares s/he had immediately before the split, though the total value of each shareholder's stock remains the same.")
(comment PublicInformationWork "Instances of #$PublicInformationWork contain information intended to educate the public. #$PublicInformationWorks are usually published by government agencies and seek to inform people about issues related to their area of policy. Examples would include tax advice booklets published by the IRS and health-related pamphlets published by the CDC.")
(comment LoanAgreementTypeByMarketSector "A collection of collections. Instances of #$LoanAgreementTypeByMarketSector are collections of #$LoanAgreements that are similar with respect to the target market of the lender.")
(comment standardVariableRate-UK "(#$standardVariableRate-UK THING RATE) means that RATE is the interest rate that commercial banks in the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland are charging their most creditworthy borrowers, such as large corporations. See also #$primeRate-US.")
(comment mortgageArrangementFee "(#$mortgageArrangementFee MORTGAGE FEE) means that the lender of MORTGAGE has charged the #$borrower FEE for administrative costs related to MORTGAGE. Also called an 'Application Fee' or 'Administrative Fee.'")
(disjointWith Term-LifeInsurance Endowment-LifeInsurance)
(comment Term-LifeInsurance "A specialization of #$LifeInsurance.  Each instance of #$Term-LifeInsurance is a life insurance agreement with low premiums that will increase as the insured ages.  When the term of the insurance comes to an end, the insured receives no benefit, in contrast, e.g, with instances of #$Endowment-LifeInsurance (q.v.).")
(comment Churning-StockTrading "A specialization of #$StockTrading and #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal.  Each instance of #$Churning-StockTrading is an event in which a stock broker trades stocks with the sole purpose of earning the commission for making the trade.")
(comment enterpriseValue "(#$enterpriseValue ORG VAL) means that VAL is the sum total of the market value of ORG's debt and equity.")
(comment ISEQStockIndex "The collection of all instances of #$StockIndexGroup that are managed by the #$IrishStockExchange (ISE).")
(comment WithProfitsInsurance "A type of #$InsurancePlan which has both an investment aspect and a coverage aspect, such as an #$Endowment-LifeInsurance.")
(comment LoanNote-Transferable "A specialization of #$AuthorizedAgreement and #$TradeableSecurity.  Each instance of #$LoanNote-Transferable is an agreement that has been recorded in writing as a short-term promise of an issuer to repay a specified principal amount on a particular date, together with interest at a stated rate, payable from a defined source of anticipated revenue. Notes usually mature in a short period of time (usually one year or less) in contrast to bonds (see #$Bond-Agreement).")
(comment FullServiceBrokerageFirm "A specialization of #$BrokerageFirm, instances of which offer customers a full range of services related to commodity-trading, including investment advice.")
(comment FinalSalaryScheme-Pension "A specialization of #$CompanyPension.  Each instance of #$FinalSalaryScheme-Pension is a basic company pension in the UK from which a worker will receive benefits in proportion to his or her final salary at the company.")
(comment internalRateOfReturn "<code>(#$internalRateOfReturn BOND RATE)</code> means that the interest rate on #$Bond-Agreement <code>BOND</code> is <code>RATE</code> expressed as a percentage per lifetime of the bond. This percentage is the interest rate that you are getting if you buy a bond at the current price and hold it until it redeems in however many years' time.")
(comment limitPriceOfStockTypeForAgent-Sell "<code>(#$limitPriceOfStockTypeForAgent-Sell STOCK-TYPE AGENT VALUE)</code> holds just in case the minimum price at which AGENT will sell his/her shares of STOCK-TYPE is VALUE.")
(comment BlueChipStock "Each instance of #$BlueChipStock is a (share of) #$Stock in a large, stable, well-respected company.")
(comment limitPriceOfStockTypeForAgent-Buy "<code>(#$limitPriceOfStockTypeForAgent-Buy STOCK-TYPE AGENT VALUE)</code> holds just in case the maximum price at which AGENT will buy shares of STOCK-TYPE is VALUE.")
(comment londonInterBankOfferRate "The predicate used to state the interest rate that large international banks use to lend money to each other.  It is set by a few banks in London once a day.")
(comment MisSaleOfAnEndowment "A specialization of both #$Fraud and #$Investing.  Each instance of #$MisSaleOfAnEndowment is a sale of an #$Endowment-LifeInsurance in which the seller has defrauded the buyer by failing to explain the greater risk involved with an endowment as compared to an #$InterestOnlyMortgage, with which endowments are often sold together.  Complaints of endowment mis-sales in the UK prompted the #$FinancialServicesAuthority-UK to undertake a full-scale mis-selling enquiry.")
(comment MarketMaker "A financial company (brokerage or bank) that maintains firm, publicly stated prices for both purchase and sale of one or more securities.  At any time, this company is willing to buy or sell at their stated prices.")
(comment ExchangeTradedFund "Funds that track an indices but can be bought and sold by brokers.")
(comment MissellingAFinancialAsset "A #$TemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$MissellingAFinancialAsset is a (#$BuyingFn #$FinancialAsset) event in which the #$seller does not have #$buyer's best interests in mind.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWorkTypeByStyle "A specialization of #$ObjectTypeByStyle and a collection of collections. Each instance of this collection is a collection of #$PropositionalConceptualWorks that are of the same style. Instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWorks share a style if they are of the same genre or some other salient feature, like form. For example, #$Questionnaire-CW is an instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWorkTypeByStyle because its instances share a form, namely that the instances ask questions, or are in what could be considered the 'interrogative style.'")
(comment PropagandaActivity "A specialization of #$HumanActivity and #$CulturalActivity.
Each instance of this collection is an event in which some agent (an
individual or organization) engages in an activity to promote, create,
or distribute instances of #$Propaganda.")
(comment orgCommunicationsTargetsAgentType "<code>(#$orgCommunicationsTargetsAgentType ORGANIZATION
AGENT-TYPE)</code> relates an instance of #$Organization
<b>ORGANIZATION</b> to the specialization of #$IntelligentAgent its
communications target.<p>
For example, <code>(#$orgCommunicationsTargetsAgentType
#$PhilipMorris-Corporation #$HumanChild)</code> means that some communications
originating from #$PhilipMorris-Corporation are specifically aimed to
appeal to or get some message to children.")
(comment expatriateFrom "<code>(#$expatriateFrom REGION PERSON)</code> means that
<b>REGION</b> is the instance of #$GeographicalRegion in which
<b>Person</b> is actaully a citizen of, but currently <b>PERSON</b>
resides in some other instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity.<p> For
example, <code>(#$expatriateFrom Fred #$IrishRepublic)</code> means
that although Fred is a citizen of #$IrishRepublic, he resides in a
different instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity.<p> Please see also
#$ExpatriateCommunity and #$expatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegion.")
(comment ExpatriateCommunity "A specialization of #$Community. Each instance of this
collection is a community of people, who have citizenship in one
country, living in another country with the intent of staying in that
country. See also #$ExpatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegionFn.")
(comment ExpatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegionFn "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction and
#$BinaryFunction.  When applied to an instance of
#$PersonTypeByCulture <b>PERSON-TYPE</b> and an instance of
#$GeographicalRegion <b>AREA</b>, #$ExpatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegionFn returns
the expatriate community of <b>PERSON-TYPE</b> that reside in <b>AREA</b>.<p>
For instance, <code>(#$ExpatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegionFn
#$EthnicGroupOfTamils #$France)</code> is the expatriate community of Tamils
currently residing in #$France.")
(comment expatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegion "An instance of #$TernaryPredicate.
<code>(#$expatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegion COMMUNITY TYPE AREA)</code>
relates <b>COMMUNITY</b>, an instance of #$ExpatriateCommunity, to the
instance of #$PersonTypeByCulture, <b>TYPE</b>, that comprises
<b>COMMUNITY</b> in <b>AREA</b>. Instances of #$ExpatriateCommunity
are groups of people, whose members live in close proximity in
<b>AREA</b> and make up a viable unit within <b>AREA</b> such that
<b>AREA</b> is not the native country for the majority of
<b>COMMUNITY's</b> members.<p> For example,
<code>(#$expatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegion ExpatCommunity001
#$EthiopianPerson #$France)</code> means that ExpatCommunity001 is
located in #$France and it is a community of #$EthiopianPersons.<p> That
the members of <b>COMMUNITY</b> are originally from the same place,
which is different from <b>AREA</b>, provides cohesion to
<b>COMMUNITY</b>. Note that 'originally from' is a vague concept. The
children born within <b>COMMUNITY</b> may or may not identify with the
culture of origin.  See also #$ExpatriateCommunityOfTypeInRegionFn.")
(comment DiscountStockbroker "A specialization of #$Stockbroker.  Each instance of #$DiscountStockbroker is a stockbroker who charges transaction fees lower than those of a typical stockbroker, but who also provides fewer services to his or her customers.")
(comment MortgageRedemptionForm "A specialization of #$Form-StandardizedIBO.      Each instance of #$MortgageRedemptionForm is a form, to be signed by the morgagee,  signifying that a certain #$MortgageAgreement has been fully paid off.")
(comment TenderOffer "An offer by a company to buyback its shares (cf. #$ShareBuyback).")
(comment FT30-StockIndexGroup "An instance of #$StockIndexGroup that was originally conceived as being the UK equivalent to the #$DowJonesIndustrials, but is little quoted now.")
(comment stockEarningsForPeriod "<code>(#$stockEarningsForPeriod STOCKTYPE VALUE PERIOD)</code> means that VALUE is amount the issuing company added to STOCKTYPE shareholders' funds during PERIOD, after all the costs of delivering a product or service have been accounted for.")
(comment assetDepreciationForPeriod "<code>(#$assetDepreciationForPeriod ASSET VALUE PERIOD)</code> means that VALUE is amount that the fixed asset (see #$fixedAssetOf) ASSET has lost in value during PERIOD.")
(comment MoneyPurchasePensionScheme "A type of #$RetirementAccount where holder builds up a pot of cash, which has to be used to buy an annuity.  Also known as a \"defined contribution scheme\".")
(comment PartialOfferTakeover "A specialization of #$Takeover, wherein a bidder only offers to buy a certain percentage of a company's shares.")
(comment BuyingStockCumDividend "A #$TemporalObjectType and specialization of #$StockTrading.  Each instance of #$BuyingStockCumDividend is an event in which someone buys #$Stocks at such a time that they are entitled to receive the next dividend from them.")
(comment TaxDeferredAccount "A specialization of #$FinancialAccount.  Each instance of #$TaxDeferredAccount is an account taxes on which are deferred until the time of withdrawal.")
(comment InAdministration "The financial state of being in Administration.  When a company in financial difficulty is put into administration, an administrator is appointed to run the company so that its debt can be paid off in an orderly fashion.")
(comment InsiderTrading "A specialization of #$StockTrading and #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal.  Each instance of #$InsiderTrading is an event in which someone buys or sells shares with privileged information that would move the price if it were widely known.")
(comment DispositionallyOptimisticSecuritiesTrader "#$DispositionallyOptimisticSecuritiesTrader is an instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$DispositionallyOptimisticSecuritiesTrader is a person, sometimes known as a \"bull\", who behavies as though the value of securities will rise.")
(disjointWith DispositionallyPessimisticSecuritiesTrader DispositionallyOptimisticSecuritiesTrader)
(comment dividendYield "A #$QuantitySlot relating a specialization of #$Stock to a #$RealNumber.  (#$dividendYield STOCK YIELD) means that YIELD is number resulting from dividing the dividend per share (see #$dividendPerShare) by the value of the stock.")
(comment Annualizing "A specialization of #$DoingAnArithmeticOperation.  Each instance of #$Annualizing is an even in which an agent takes an item measured over a certain period and restates it on an annual basis.")
(comment WarrantForSecurities "A specialization of #$Permission.  Each instance of#$WarrantForSecurities is permission, authorized by a cerificate that entitles the holder to purchase a specific quanity of securtities for some agreed upon price which is typically greater than the current market price.")
(comment CapitalGainsTax "The collection of all #$Tax-COCs that are collected on an agent's capital gains.")
(comment totalReturn "#$totalReturn denotes the relation between an investment and the total amount of value it has returned to date.")
(disjointWith SmallCapStock LargeCapStock)
(comment PortfolioManagement "A specialization of #$Investing.  Each instance of #$PortfolioManagement is an event in which a portfolio manager (see #$PortfolioManager) actively looksafter the state of an investment portfolio.")
(comment Intestacy "A specialization of #$Situation. Each instance of #$Intestacy is a situation in which a person dies without a will.")
(comment intialFundManagerFee "The fees that fund managers charge when their funds are purchased.")
(comment endowmentSurrenderValue "A #$QuantitySlot relating an instance of #$Endowment-LifeInsurance to a #$MonetaryValue.  (#$endowmentSurrenderValue ENDOWMENT VALUE) means that VALUE is the value of ENDOWMENT if ENDOWMENT is cashed in before its time.")
(disjointWith SecurityVolatility TangiblePhysicalQuantity)
(comment SecurityVolatility "The degree to which a security share price tends to fluctuate.")
(comment FinancialInterestDisclosure "A specialization of #$Statement.  Each instance of #$FinancialInterestDisclosure is a statement that reveals the financial interests of an agent.  Often these are required to be presented to demonstrate that an agent does not have any conflicts of interest.")
(comment PathfinderProspectus "The collection of instances of #$Prospectus that are distributed prior to any formal offering, primarily in order to generate interest from prospective investors.  These documents publish information about a company or instance of #$CollectivelyManagedFundOrganization without going into details about share price or performance.")
(comment BalanceSheetDay "A specialization of #$RevealingInformation.  Each instance of #$BalanceSheetDay is an event in which an agent (usually a legal corporation) submits its balance sheet (see #$BalanceSheet).")
(comment ClosePeriodAfterBalanceSheetDay "A specialization of #$PreparingFinancialRecords.  Each instance of #$ClosePeriodBeforeBalanceSheetDay is an event that occurs between balance sheet day and the day a company announces its results.")
(comment QuarterlyReport "The collection of all instances of #$ReportOnSituation-CW that are published once every three months.")
(comment LikeForLike-Comparison "A specialization of #$Comparing.  Each instance of #$LikeForLike-Comparison is an event in which retail trade organizations are evaluated in terms of their relative growth.")
(comment QuarterlyFinancialStatement "The collection of all instances of #$QuarterlyReport that are published as financial statements, typically so as to keep investors informed.")
(comment QuarterlyReporting "The collection of all instances of #$Reporting in which one generates a quarterly report (see #$QuarterlyReport).")
(comment LondonInternationalFinancialFuturesAndOptionsExchange "The London International Financial Futures and Options Exchange, an instance of #$StockExchange.")
(comment businessNetProfitForPeriod "(#$businessNetProfitForPeriod BUSINESS VALUE PERIOD) means that VALUE is amount BUSINESS made in sales less all costs directly attributable to those sales (e.g. costs for raw materials and manufacturing labor), charges have been paid and dividends declared. VALUE is added to, or subtracted from if negative, to shareholders' funds at the end of the year.")
(comment exitCharge "An exit charge is a fee charged to the seller (see #$seller) in an instance of #$FinancialInstrumentTrading. (#$exitCharge TRADE FEE) identifies FEE as an exit charge in TRADE.")
(comment ProfitAndLossStatement "The collection of documents that describe the business performance of an agent, usually put out annually.")
(comment Eye-Closed "Each instance of #$Eye-Closed is an #$Eye that is closed -- i.e., completely sheathed by the #$Eyelids of the animal of which the eye is an anatomical part.  See also #$Eye-Open.")
(disjointWith Eye-Closed Eye-Open)
(comment Eye-Open "Each instance of #$Eye-Open is an #$Eye that is (at least partially) open -- i.e., not completely sheathed by the #$Eyelids of the animal of which the eye is an anatomical part.  See also #$Eye-Closed.")
(comment equipmentTypeForStructuredActivity "(#$equipmentTypeForStructuredActivity ACTIVITY EQUIP-TYPE) means that
EQUIP-TYPE is the collection of equipment types whose elements are
used in performances of ACTIVITY (an instance of
#$DevisedStructuredActivity).  This preicate corresponds to the
function #$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn (q.v.).")
(disjointWith Integer TransfiniteCardinal)
(comment TransfiniteCardinal "A specialization of #$Cardinal-Mathematical.  This is the collection of all infinite cardinals: cardinals that are #$greaterThan any integer.  Instances include aleph-0 (see #$PlusInfinity) and #$Aleph-1.")
(comment NonCompetitiveGame "A specialization of #$Game.  Each instance of #$NonCompetitiveGame is a specification of the rules and equipment required for playing a non-competitive game (such as #$RingARosy).")
(disjointWith Atheist Theist)
(comment Theist "Each instance of #$Theist is a #$Person that beliefs in the existence of at least one #$God.  See also #$Atheist.")
(comment believerTypeOfBeliefSystem "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a #$BeliefSystem to the corresponding #$IntelligentAgentTypeByBeliefSystem.  (#$believerTypeOfBeliefSystem SYSTEM AGT-TYPE) means that AGT-TYPE is the collection of all #$IntelligentAgents that have the belief system SYSTEM.  (Cf. #$hasBeliefSystems.)  This is the predicate corresponding to #$BelieverFn (q.v.).")
(comment referenceWorkEntryTitle "(#$referenceWorkEntryTitle WORK STRING) identifies STRING as the title of the instance of #$ReferenceWorkEntry WORK.  For example, (#$referenceWorkEntryTitle WebstersThirdEditionEntryOnTurtle \"turtle\") means that in the third edition of Webster's Dictionary, the entry on the word \"turtle\" appears under the string \"turtle.\"")
(comment Hadith "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork. Each
instance of this collection is the recorded teachings of the Prophet
Mohammed separate from the Qur'an. They are commonly taught as part of
Islamic theology.")
(comment CommunistPartyOfIndiaMarxist "An instance of #$CommunistParty that operates in #$India.")
(comment predHoldsBetweenRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSubSitType "<code>(#$predHoldsBetweenRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSubSitType SITTYPE SUBSITTYPE1 ROLE1 SUBSITTYPE2 ROLE2 TYPE)</code> means that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SITTYPE</code>, where <code>SUBSIT1</code> and <code>SUBSIT2</code> are subsituations of <code>SIT</code> and are instances of <code>SUBSITTYPE1</code> and <code>SUBSITTYPE2</code>, respectively, whatever things of type <code>TYPE</code> play <code>ROLE1</code> in <code>SUBSIT1</code> bear the relation <code>BINPRED</code> to whatever things of type <code>TYPE</code> play <code>ROLE2</code> in <code>SUBSIT2</code>.")
(comment arg7Isa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg7Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the seventh argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG7 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment famousFigureInField "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$Person to a #$FieldOfStudy.  (#$famousFigureInField PERSON FIELD) means that PERSON is famous for his or her work in FIELD.  For example, (#$famousFigureInField #$AlbertEinstein #$Physics) means that Einstein is famous for his work in physics.")
(disjointWith EmptySetOrCollection NonEmptySetOrCollection)
(comment GivingOfTypeFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  This function
takes for its value a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible,
<b>TYPE</b> and returns for its value the collection of
#$GivingSomething events in which an instance of <b>TYPE</b> is the
#$objectGiven.<p>
For example, <code>(#$GivingOfTypeFn #$Automobile)</code> returns the
collection of events in which an agent is given a car.")
(comment givingEventTypeOfType "An instance of #$MacroRelation. <code>(#$givingEventTypeOfType
GIVING-TYPE TYPE)</code> means that the specialization of
#$GivingSomething, <b>GIVING-TYPE</b> is the collection of events in
which an instance of <b>TYPE</b>, a specialization of
#$PartiallyTangible, was the #$objectGiven.<p>
<code>(#$givingEventTypeOfType #$GiftGiving #$Gift)</code> relates the
collection of events #$GiftGiving to the type of thing given, #$Gift.
See also #$GivingOfTypeFn.")
(comment GivingHumanitarianAid "A specialization of #$GivingEconomicAid and
#$HelpingAnAgent.  Each instance of this collection is an event in
which one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible provides another with
#$HumanitarianAssistance.  Generally, this takes the form of food,
clothing, and medical assistance but excludes instances of
#$MoneyTransactions.")
(comment socialQuantityTypeExpressedByInsOfEventType "An instance of #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate that relates
a type of #$InterAgentSupportQuantity, <b>SUPPORT</b>, to
<b>EVENT-TYPE</b>, which are types of #$Events that express
<b>SUPPORT</b>.<p>
As an example, <code>(#$socialQuantityTypeExpressedByInsOfEventType
#$EconomicSupport #$GivingEconomicAid)</code> means that
#$EconomicSupport is expressed in instances of #$GivingEconomicAid.")
(comment MandalParishadTerritorialCouncil "An instance of #$Organization.")
(comment positionNotUserEditable "(#$positionNotUserEditable TEMPLATE POSITION TOPIC) means that when TEMPLATE in invoked under TOPIC, the user will not be able to type information for replaceable position POSITION. In other words, this position will restrict the user to the candidate replacements generated in the drop-down menu.")
(comment NationOfIslam "An instance of #$MuslimOrganization. This spiritual and
political movement began in the U.S. It is controversial movement; one
that diverges from typical Islamic views in key ways. For example, the
NOI believes its founder, Wallace Fard Muhammad, was an incarnate of
God. The NOI also teaches Caucasians are a race of non-human demons
created by an evil scientist named Yakub. These beliefs, among others,
means that many Muslims reject this movement as Islam.")
(comment MillionManMarch "An instance of #$ProtestMarch.  This was a march of African
American men in #$CityOfWashingtonDC on October 16, 1995 to express
unity within the African American male community.  Efforts were made
during this rally to register African Americans to vote.  Notable
speakers at the march included #$MayaAngelou, #$RosaParks, and #$JesseJackson.")
(comment organismKilled-Suicide "An #$ActorSlot and specialization of #$organismKilled and #$performedBy.  (#$organismKilled EVENT ORG) means that ORG deliberately killed itself in EVENT.")
(comment fosterSons "A #$FamilyRelationSlot.  (#$fosterSons PARENT SON) means that SON is a foster son of PARENT.")
(comment fosterDaughters "A #$FamilyRelationSlot.  (#$fosterDaughters PARENT DAUGHTER) means that DAUGHTER is a foster daugher of PARENT.")
(comment pegReferencesType "(#$pegReferencesType LINGUISTIC-PEG TYPE) means that the instance of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg LINGUISITC-PEG contains a reference to the collection TYPE.  For example, where APizza-LinguisticExpressionPeg is a linguistic peg that marks an occurrence of an utterance of the phrase \"a pizza,\" (#$pegReferencesType APizza-LinguisticExpressionPeg #$Pizza) means that that peg contains a reference to the collection #$Pizza.  Note that this is a distinct relationship from the one that a linguistic peg bears to its meaning (see #$pegInterpretations and its specialization-predicates.)")
(comment undamagedActors "An #$ActorSlot.  (#$undamagedActors EVENT THING) means that THING was meaningfully involved in EVENT, but was not damaged in EVENT.  It is equivalent to:
<pre>
(#$and
  (#$actors EVENT THING)
  (#$not (#$damages EVENT THING))).")
(comment CruiseMissile-BGM-109-Tomahawk "Tomahawks are a variety of U.S. submarine or ship-launched land-attack cruise missiles.")
(comment likelyMoreSpecificGeopoliticalEntity "(#$likelyMoreSpecificGeopoliticalEntity NAUT TERM) means that it is likely that NAUT and TERM denote the same geopolitical entity and that TERM is a reifiable or reified representation. Example: (#$likelyMoreSpecificGeopoliticalEntity (#$GeopoliticalEntityNamedFn \"Toronto\" #$Ontario-CanadianProvince) (#$CityNamedFn \"Toronto\" #$Ontario-CanadianProvince))")
(comment unharmedActors "An #$ActorSlot and specialization of #$undamagedActors.  (#$unharmedActors EVENT THING) means that THING was meaningfully involved in EVENT, but was not harmed in EVENT.  It is equivalent to:
<pre>
(#$and
  (#$actors EVENT THING)
  (#$not (#$objectHarmed EVENT THING))).")
(comment ProjectManagement-Reporting-TemplateTopic "An instance of #$FormulaTemplateTopicType. Instances are collections of instances of FormulaTemplate used to report on progress of assignments for project management.")
(comment PrevalentInMotleyFoolUKCorpus "The collection of all instances of #$CycLTerm that denote concepts that are prevalent in the Motley Fool UK corpus.  (See #$MotleyFoolUK-Website, which comprises the corpus.)")
(comment cellMemberInTerroristGroup "(#$cellMemberInTerroristGroup GROUP PERSON) means that PERSON is a member of a #$TerroristCell that is a suborganization of GROUP.")
(comment Jaywalking "A specialization of #$Ambulation.  Each instance of #$Jaywalking is an event in which an agent crosses a street in an illegal or reckless fashion.")
(comment parserTestTarget-Negative "(#$parserTestTarget-Negative TEST TARGET) means that TARGET is an undesired parse for TEST. TEST will fail if TARGET is returned among the answers.")
(comment Machete "An #$ExistingObjectType.  Each instance of #$Machete is a long, broad #$Knife used for hacking down vegetation (or as a weapon).")
(comment lexicalPSCForLanguage "This predicate relates a #$NaturalLanguage to a #$LexicalProblemSolvingContext that describes some of Cyc's lexical knowledge about it.")
(comment CommunicationsOfficer "A #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$CommunicationsOfficer is an #$OfficerInOrganization who specializes in communications.")
(comment PostalWorker "A #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$PostalWorker is a person who works for a #$PostalService.")
(comment Interpreter-Occupation "A #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$Interpreter-Occupation is a multilingual person who makes a living by facilitating communication between agents who speak different languages.")
(comment FreelanceFn "A unary #$SubcollectionDenotingFunction that takes a #$PersonTypeByActivity and returns the collection of all agents who perform that activity professionally as a #$FreelanceWorker.  For example, (#$FreelanceFn #$Photographer) is the collection of all freelance photographers.")
(comment freelance-Pred "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a #$PersonTypeByActivity to the collection of agents who perform that activity professionally as a #$FreelanceWorker.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$FreelanceFn (q.v.).")
(comment InternetCafe-Organization "A #$BusinessTypeByActivityType.  Each instance of #$InternetCafe-Organization is a #$Cafe-Organization that offers internet access in additional to the usual fare of coffee, etc.")
(comment Logging "A #$TemporalStuffType and specialization of #$OutdoorActivity.  Each instance of #$Logging is event in which trees are cut down and harvested for commercial purposes.")
(comment NewspaperEditor "A #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$NewspaperEditor is someone who works as an #$Editor for a #$NewspaperOrganization.")
(comment UNPeacekeeper "The collection of all agents who work as #$Peacekeepers for the #$UnitedNationsOrganization.")
(comment executives "An #$OrganizationalPositionSlot.  (#$executives ORG PERSON) means that PERSON is an executive in ORG.")
(comment ForeignAidOrganization "A #$FirstOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$ForeignAidOrganization is a #$SocialAidOrganization that specializes in providing assistance to citizens of foreign countries -- i.e., countries other than the one(s) in which the organization is based.")
(comment NightWatchperson "A #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$NightWatchperson is a #$SecurityGuard who watches over a facility at night.")
(comment toFacetGLFArc "<code>(#$toFacetGLFArc NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM ARC)</code> means that <code>ARC</code> is the #$SOEFacetingArc that links <code>NODE1</code> to <code>NODE2</code> in <code>SYSTEM</code>, and that <code>ARC</code> has #$facets-Generic as its semantics.")
(comment ToFacetGLFArcFn "(#$ToFacetGLFArcFn NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM) denotes the #$SOEFacetingArc that links NODE1 to NODE2 in SYSTEM.")
(comment TaxAgency "A specialization of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization.  Each instance of #$TaxAgency is a revenue agency that is part of the government of some #$GeopoliticalEntity, and which is concerned primarily with collecting tax money from the residents of that #$GeopoliticalEntity. This collection does not include customs agencies and agencies that collect minor fees only.")
(comment resultDisjointWithArg "A #$MetaFunction.  (#$resultDisjointWithArg FUNC N) means that the value returned by FUNC for any given sequence of arguments is disjoint with the Nth argument in that sequence.
<p>
For example, (#$resultDisjointWithArg #$FormerFn 1) entails that (#$FormerFn #$Teacher) is disjoint with #$Teacher.")
(comment fromFacetGLFArc "<code>(#$fromFacetGLFArc NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM ARC)</code> means that <code>ARC</code> is the #$SOEFacetingArc that links <code>NODE1</code> to <code>NODE2</code> in <code>SYSTEM</code>, and that <code>ARC</code> has (#$InverseBinaryPredicateFn #$isa) as its semantics.")
(comment FromFacetGLFArcFn "(#$FromFacetGLFArcFn NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM) denotes the #$SOEFacetingArc that links NODE1 to NODE2 in SYSTEM.")
(comment former-Pred "(#$former-Pred COL1 COL2) means that COL2 is the collection of former instances of COL1 -- i.e., things that used to be, but no longer are, instances of COL1.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$FormerFn (q.v.).")
(comment specGLFArc "<code>(#$specGLFArc NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM ARC)</code> means that <code>ARC</code> is the #$SOEFacetingArc that links <code>NODE1</code> to <code>NODE2</code> in <code>SYSTEM</code>, and that <code>ARC</code> has #$specs (the inverse of #$genls) as its semantics.")
(comment SpecGLFArcFn "(#$SpecGLFArcFn NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM) denotes the #$SOESpecArc that links NODE1 to NODE2 in SYSTEM.")
(comment DeminingOrganization "An #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType.  Each instance of #$DeminingOrganization is an #$Organization (typically non-profit) whose primary activity is clearing dangerous mines (#$Mine-Weapon).")
(comment ElectionWorker "A #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$ElectionWorker is a person who is currently working as an official facilitator of an #$Election.")
(comment agentOffersRewardForProcurementOfIndividual "A #$TernaryPredicate that relates an #$IntelligentAgent to an #$MonetaryValue to an #$Individual.  (#$agentOffersRewardForProcurementOfIndividual AGENT REWARD INDIVIDUAL) means that AGENT is currently offering REWARD for the procurement (or information leading to the procurement) of INDIVIDUAL.
<p>
For example, (#$agentOffersRewardForProcurementOfIndividual (#$GovernmentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 25000000) #$OsamaBinLaden) means that the U.S. Government is offering 25 million dollars for the procurement (i.e. capture), or information leading to the procurement/capture, of Osama bin Laden.
<p>
Similarly, (#$agentOffersRewardForProcurementOfIndividual Mario (#$Euro 50) MariosWallet) means that Mario is offering a reward of 50 Euro for the return (or information leading to the return) of his wallet.")
(comment OfferingAReward "A specialization of #$Offering-CommunicationAct.  Each instance of #$OfferingAReward is an event in which an agent offers a #$Reward for something.")
(comment rewardOfferedIsForProcurementOf "A #$BinaryRolePredicate.  (#$rewardOfferedIsForProcurementOf OFFER INDIVIDUAL) means that OFFER is an offer of a #$Reward for the procurement of INDIVIDUAL.")
(comment SKSIPragmaticMetaRelation "#$SKSIPragmaticMetaRelation is a collection of #$Relations
which are used to restrict the scope of CycL queries by limiting which
knowledge sources (external, or the current Cyc KB) are applicable to
the query.")
(comment MajorCreditCard "A specialization of #$CreditCard.  Each specialization of #$MajorCreditCard is a major brand of credit card.")
(comment WhiteSupremacism "A #$subBeliefSystem of #$Racism.  #$WhiteSupremacism is the view that the white race (cf. #$EthnicGroupOfCaucasians) is superior to other races.")
(comment CreditCardTypeByBalanceCarryFeature "#$CreditCardTypeByBalanceCarryFeature is a specialization of  #$SecondOrderCollection that strictly facets #$CreditCard.  Each instance of #$CreditCardTypeByBalanceCarryFeature is a specialization of #$CreditCard, instances of which either uniformly allow revolving accounts or uniformly disallow revolving accounts.")
(comment CreditCardWithAnnualFee "A subcollection of #$CreditCard.  Each instance of #$CreditCardWithAnnualFee is a credit card that incurs an annual fee on its account holder.")
(comment CreditCardWithNoAnnualFee "A subcollection of #$CreditCard.  Each instance of #$CreditCardWithNoAnnualFee is a credit card that does not incur an annual fee on its account holder.")
(disjointWith CreditCardWithNoAnnualFee CreditCardWithAnnualFee)
(comment Minibus "A specialization of #$Bus-RoadVehicle.  Each instance of #$Minibus is a small bus designed to carry about eight to twenty passengers.")
(comment CreditCardTypeByGenericInterestRateLevel "A specialization of #$MoneyTenderType.  Each instance of #$CreditCardTypeByGenericInterestRateLevel is a specialization of #$CreditCard-RevolvingAccount.  In particular, each instance of #$CreditCardTypeByGenericInterestRateLevel is a specialization of the collection of credit cards with revolving accounts that is associated with a generic interest rate level, such as \"high\" or \"low\".")
(comment CreditCardTypeByAnnualFeeFeature "#$CreditCardTypeByAnnualFeeFeature is a specialization of #$SecondOrderCollection that strictly facets #$CreditCard.  Each instance of #$CreditCardTypeByAnnualFeeFeature is a specialization of #$CreditCard, instances of which either uniformly charge an annual fee or uniformly do not.")
(comment cardHasAnnualFeeFeature "(#$cardHasAnnualFeeFeature CARD CARD-BY-ANNUAL-FEE-FEATURE) means that the credit card CARD has the annual fee feature CARD-BY-ANNUAL-FEE-FEATURE (i.e., it is an instance of the latter collection -- either #$CreditCardWithNoAnnualFee or #$CreditCardWithAnnualFee).")
(comment cardHasGenericInterestRateLevel "(#$cardHasGenericInterestRateLevel CARD CARD-BY-INTEREST-LEVEL) means that the credit card CARD has the generic interest level CARD-BY-INTEREST-LEVEL (i.e., it is an instance of the latter collection -- either #$CreditCardWithHighAPR or #$CreditCardWithLowAPR).")
(comment Missile-JetPropelled "A #$WeaponType and specialization of #$JetPropelledTransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$Missile-JetPropelled is a #$Missile that is powered by a #$JetEngine.  See also #$Missile-RocketPropelled.")
(comment JetPropelledTransportationDevice "The collection of all #$TransportationDevices that are propelled by #$JetEngines.")
(comment SKSISourceStatusTest "#$SKSISourceStatusTest is a collection of #$SKSITests which are meant to test the current status of external knowledge sources. For instance, the test #$SKSI-WhichSourcesAreCurrentlyUnaccessible returns those top level SKSes to which Cyc cannot currently establish a connection.")
(comment CreditCardAgreementWithNoAnnualFee "The collection of instances of #$CreditCardAgreement that incur no annual fee.  See also #$annualFee and #$CreditCardWithNoAnnualFee.")
(comment CreditCardAgreementTypeByAnnualFeeFeature "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType that facets #$CreditCardAgreement.  It has exactly two instances, #$CreditCardAgreementWithAnnualFee and #$CreditCardAgreementWithNoAnnualFee.")
(comment CreditCardAgreementWithAnnualFee "The collection of instances of #$CreditCardAgreement that incur some annual fee.  See also #$annualFee and #$CreditCardWithAnnualFee.")
(comment IndustryOfTypeFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.
#$IndustryOfTypeFn takes for its value a specialization of
#$TemporalThing, <b>TYPE</b>, and returns the collection of all people
and activities involved with the business of <b>TYPE</b>,
<code>(#$IndustryOfTypeFn TYPE)</code>.<p>Thus,
<code>(#$IndustryOfTypeFn #$Computer)</code> refers to all of the
people and activites involved with the business of computers. This
includes the design, manufacture, and selling of instances of
#$Computer as a whole industry.<p>This function is quite broad; for a
more specific concept of 'industry' as the production of goods, see
also #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn. So, for any given <b>TYPE</b>, only a
subset of design, manufacture, selling, running, owning, etc of
<b>TYPE</b> may apply to <code>(#$IndustryOfTypeFn TYPE)</code>. For
example, <code>(#$IndustryOfTypeFn #$Tourism)</code> may not entail any
aspects of manufacturing.")
(comment industryOfType "A predicate that relates a specialization of
#$MultiIndividualAgent-Intelligent <b>INDUSTRY-TYPE</b> to the specialization
of #$TemporalThing, <b>TYPE</b>, of which <b>INDUSTRY-TYPE</b> is the
business of <b>TYPE</b>.  This is a broad relation, and
<b>INDUSTRY-TYPE</b> will include all of the people and activities for
the business, not just the production of instances of <b>TYPE</b>.")
(comment ManagerTypeOfOrganizationTypeFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.
#$ManagerTypeOfOrganizationTypeFn takes for its value an
specialization of #$Organization, <b>ORGANIZATION</b>, and returns the
subcollection of all #$Managers within <b>ORGANIZATION</b>.<p>For
example, <code>(#$ManagerTypeOfOrganizationTypeFn
McDonaldsRestaurant)</code> denotes the collection of all managers of
instances of #$McDonaldsRestaurant.")
(comment managerTypeOfOrganizationType "An instance of #$FunctionalPredicate and
#$CotemporalPredicate.  <code>(#$managerTypeOfOrganizationType MANAGER-TYPE
ORG-TYPE)</code> relates <b>MANAGER-TYPE</b>, a subcollection of #$Manager,
to a subcollection of #$Organization, <b>ORG-TYPE</b>.
<b>MANAGER-TYPE</b> is the collection of individuals that hold the
position of #$Manager in <b>ORG-TYPE</b>.<p>
For example, <code>(#$managerTypeOfOrganizationType RestaurantManager
#$Restaurant-Organization) relates the collection of individual
managers of #$Restaurant-Organizations.")
(comment AccruingInterestOnABankAccount "The collection of instances of #$AccruingInterest in which interest is credited to a bank account, increasing the holdings of the account holder.  Contrast with #$AccruingInterestOnALoan, which raises the level of debt for the account holder.")
(comment AccruingInterest "A specialization of #$IncreasingTheBalanceOnAnAccount.  Each instance of #$AccruingInterest is an event in which the balance (see #$accountBalance) on an account is increased due to the crediting/charging of interest towards the balance.")
(comment InterestAccrualTypeByAccountType "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType and #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Instances are specializations of #$AccruingInterest, each instance of which involves increasing the balance (see #$accountBalance), through the charging or crediting of interest to a common type of account.  Notable instances include #$AccruingInterestOnASavingsAccount and #$AccruingInterestOnALoan.")
(comment AccruingInterestOnASavingsAccount "The collection of all instances of #$AccruingInterest in which the account that interest is credited to is an instance of #$SavingsAccount.")
(comment physicalFieldXQueryString "This predicate relates a physical field to an XQuery query which is used by the generic web scraper to navigate through one or more xhtml documents and extract the field's value.")
(comment AccruingInterestOnACD "The collection of all instances of #$AccruingInterest in which the account that interest is credited to is an instance of #$CertificateOfDepositAccount.")
(comment UncanonicalizerAssertionFn "#$UncanonicalizerAssertionFn is used by the #$CycUncanonicalizer and should rarely (if ever) need to be seen by users or referenced in assertions entered at the EL level.  It is used by the uncanonicalizer to denote an #$CycLAssertion after it is transformed to its canonical EL formula.")
(comment loanBorrower "(#$loanBorrower LOAN AGENT) means that AGENT is the instance of #$IntelligentAgent who is the borrower with respect to the instance of #$LoanAgreement LOAN.  See also #$borrower, which relates AGENT to the relevant instance of #$BorrowingSomething.")
(comment orgCommunicationTargetsAgentTypeForIncreaseSitType "An instance of #$TernaryPredicate.
<code>(#$orgCommunicationTargetsAgentTypeForIncreaseSitType
ORGANIZATION AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE)</code> means that
<b>ORGANIZATION</b> targets at least one of its communications at
instances of <b>AGENT-TYPE</b> for the purpose of increasing the
number if instances of <b>SIT-TYPE</b> in an instance of
<b>AGENT-TYPE</b> plays a <code>#$doneBy</code> role.<p>Consider for
an example the assertion
<code>(#$orgCommunicationTargetsAgentTypeForIncreaseSitType
#$PhilipMorris-Corporation #$HumanChild #$SmokingACigarette)</code>. If true,
this assertion would mean that the #$PhilipMorris-Corporation
deliberately targets some of its communications to children with the
goal that more children would smoke.")
(disjointWith SmokingAPipe SmokingCigarettes)
(comment SmokingCigarettes "The collection of all actions of #$Smoking #$Cigarettes.  Each instance of this collection has at least one instance of #$SmokingACigarette as a subevent.")
(comment InputStream "The collection of all instantiations of computer input streams (typically an open #$ComputerFileCopy) in which data is read sequentially by a #$ComputerProcessRunning.")
(comment OutputStream "The collection of all instantiations of computer output streams (typically an open #$ComputerFileCopy) in which data is written sequentially by a #$ComputerProcessRunning.")
(comment BufferedWriter "The collection of all instantiations of computer output streams containing characters in which data is written sequentially by a #$ComputerProcessRunning via a buffer.")
(comment BufferedReader "The collection of all instantiations of computer input streams containing characters in which data is read sequentially by a #$ComputerProcessRunning via a buffer.")
(comment LiteralBuilderQueryFn "A unary #$ReifiableFunction that takes a #$Predicate PRED and returns the #$CycLQuerySpecification that is the (official) \"literal builder query\" for PRED, i.e., the (official) builder query of the form (PRED ?ARG1 ... ?ARGn), where n is the arity of PRED.  For example, (#$LiteralBuilderQueryFn #$deviceUsed) denotes the (official) builder query of the form (#$deviceUsed ?ARG1 ?ARG2).")
(comment NominalizationNCRuleFn "(#$NominalizationNCRuleFn EVENTYYPE PRED) denotes a #$NounCompoundRule which covers compounds for which the head denotes EVENTTYPE and is related to the modifier via PRED (often an #$ActorSlot).")
(comment workVisuallyDepicts "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$VisualWork to something that it depicts.  See also #$visuallyDepicts, which relates an instance of #$VisualInformationBearingThing to spatial things depicted in it.")
(comment ToIndividualGLFArcFn "(#$ToIndividualGLFArcFn NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM) denotes the #$SOEToIndividualArc that links NODE1 to NODE2 in SYSTEM.")
(comment fetViewableAssertionsForTerm "<code>(#$fetViewableAssertionsForTerm THING ASSRT TEMPLATE-TYPE)</code> holds just in case ASSRT is a CycL assertion whose form corresponds to some FET template formula that is in some instance of TEMPLATE-TYPE.  This means that the assertion should be viewable via template that's an instance of TEMPLATE-TYPE when THING is loaded as the focal term.")
(comment soeMtFocalGraph "(#$soeMtFocalGraph MT GRAPH) means that MT is the instance of #$SOEGLFGraphDefiningMicrotheory that contains assertions defining the graphical structure of the instance of #$Graph-CW GRAPH.  See also #$soeMtForGraphStructure, which relates MT directly to that structure.")
(comment RelationInstanceExistsCountBuilderQueryFn "(#$RelationInstanceExistsCountBuilderQueryFn BINPRED) denotes the #$CycLQuerySpecification of the form (#$relationInstanceExistsCount BINPRED ?ARG2 ?ARG3 ?N)")
(comment CBLSensationFn "A binary function that returns a #$CBLSensation command and which is composed of the #$CBLMethod and the lexical command sequence number.")
(comment CommonSenseTestType "#$CommonSenseTestType is the collection type of the
specializations of #$CommonSenseTest. Current instances group the
#$CommonSenseTests based on the topic, or type of reasoning
involved.")
(comment graphDepicts "(#$graphDepicts GRAPH SYSTEM) means that the instance GRAPH of #$Graph-CW is a graphical depiction of the instance of #$System, SYSTEM.  Note that if SYSTEM is an instance of #$SpatialThing, then any instantiation INS of GRAPH will visually depict SYSTEM (see #$visuallyDepicts).  Note also that #$graphDepicts is a specialization of #$containsInformationAbout-Focally; thus GRAPH is a depiction of SYSTEM, and not of any proper part of it that INS might also visually depict.")
(comment toIndividualGLFArc "<code>(#$toIndividualGLFLiteArc NODE1 NODE2 SYSTEM ARC)</code> means that <code>ARC</code> is the #$SOEToIndividualArc that links <code>NODE1</code> to <code>NODE2</code> in <code>SYSTEM</code>, and that <code>ARC</code> has (#$InverseBinaryPredicateFn #$isa) as its semantics.")
(comment agentAssignedToReviewTerm "<code>(#$agentAssignedToReviewTerm AGENT THING)</code> holds just in case AGENT was
assigned the content review task of reviewing the assertions on THING.")
(comment relatedTermHasUnreviewedAssertions "<code>(#$relatedTermHasUnreviewedAssertions THING-1 THING-2 AGENT TEMPLATE-TYPE)</code> holds just in case THING-2 is related to THING-1 in an appropriate way and has at least one FET viewable assertion in some instance of TEMPLATE-TYPE that hasn't been reviewed by AGENT.")
(comment RelationInstanceExistsBuilderQueryFn "(#$RelationInstanceExistsBuilderQueryFn BINPRED) denotes the #$CycLQuerySpecification of the form (#$relationInstanceExists BINPRED ?ARG2 ?ARG3)")
(comment UnaryEvaluationPredicate "A collection of unary predicates used to evaluate sentences.")
(comment EmbassyMissionOfCountryFn "(#$EmbassyMissionOfCountryFn COUNTRY) returns the collection of #$Embassy-TheMissions which represent COUNTRY.")
(comment reconsiderFormulaInMicrotheory "(#$reconsiderFormulaInMicrotheory FORMULA MT) tells the system to perform TMS on FORMULA in MT. Note that #$reconsiderFormulaInMicrotheory is an instance of #$ELRelation-OneWay that expands to a #$performSubL sentence.")
(comment evaluationSentenceCorrespondsToAssertion "an instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate.  
<code>(#$evaluationSentenceCorrespondsToAssertion EVALUATION SET-OF-ASSERTIONS)</code> holds just in case in the instance of #$Evaluating, EVALUATION, the assertions that correspond to the sentence evaluated are members of SET-OF-ASSERTIONS.")
(comment nodeInSystem "A specialization of #$pointInSystem (q.v.) that relates #$PathSystems (q.v.) to their \"nodes\".  <code>(#$nodeInSystem NODE SYSTEM)</code> means that <code>NODE</code> is a node in <code>SYSTEM</code>.  The nodes of <code>SYSTEM</code> are distinguished from its other points as follows.
<p>
(i) Every node in <code>SYSTEM</code> is a point in <code>SYSTEM</code>, but only nodes can be either end points of links (see #$linkBetweenInSystem), \"deadend\" points (see #$deadEndInSystem) or \"isolated\" points (i.e. points that are not on any link or loop; see #$isolatedNodeInSystem).  
<p>
(ii) Each point that is not a node must be somewhere on a single link.  That is, for each point <code>POINT</code> in <code>SYSTEM</code>, either <code>(#$pointOnPath POINT LINK)</code> holds for unique link <code>LINK</code> in <code>SYSTEM</code>, or <code>POINT</code> is a node.  Thus every \"intersection\" point (see #$junctionInSystem) in <code>SYSTEM</code> is a node.  See also #$NodesInSystemFn.")
(comment ClassicalMusic-Classical "A specialization of Western #$ClassicalMusic from the \"classical\" period, whose #$genreHeyday lasted from about 1750 to the early part of the 19th century. The classical period saw the development of the string quartet, the sonata form, and the symphony. Representative composers include Mozart, Haydn, and early Beethoven.")
(comment sourcesForTopicInProject "This predicate acts as a switch for Factivore source requirements. (#$sourcesForTopicInProject TOPIC SOURCE-TYPE PROJECT) means that when a Factivore user is logged into the system with a current project of PROJECT, all templates gathered into the user's session under TOPIC will require the user to enter source information, and the sources used will be instances of SOURCE-TYPE. For example, (#$sourcesForTopicInProject #$TKBTemplate-Attack #$FactEntrySourceType-TKB #$TKBProject) means that, if the user's current project is #$TKBProject, the Factivore will require source information for all templates that describe instances of #$TKBTemplate-Attack, and that the sources used will be instances of instances of #$FactEntrySourceType-TKB.")
(comment InternationalAffairs "A field of study.  People who study #$InternationalAffairs study the relationships between international agents (e.g countries and advisory bodies like the U.N.).  An important subfield of this is #$InternationalEconomics.  An example of an organization that teaches this field of study is The Belfer Center for Science and International Affairs: John F. Kennedy School of Government Harvard University.")
(comment ExpressionTypeByPerson "A specialization of #$LinguisticExpressionType.  Instances of this collection facet #$NounPhraseExpressionPeg according to whether the expression is of a first, second , or third person form. Instances include #$FirstPersonExpression, #$SecondPersonExpression, and #$ThirdPersonExpression.")
(comment SecondPersonExpression "Instances of this collection are #$NounPhraseExpressionPegs which are marked for second-person agreement.")
(comment FirstPersonExpression "Instances of this collection are #$NounPhraseExpressionPegs which are marked for first-person agreement.")
(comment ThirdPersonExpression "Instances of this collection are #$NounPhraseExpressionPegs which are marked for first-person agreement.")
(comment MakingCounterfeitCurrency "An instance of #$ActTypeCommonlyConsideredCriminal and specialization of #$Forgery.  Each instance of #$MakingCounterfeitCurrency is an event in which an agent produces instances of (#$ImitationOfCollectionFn #$Currency).")
(comment MediaProgramming "The collection of all acts of deciding which media transmissions will be aired on a given time and day.")
(comment TelevisionProgramming "The collection of all acts of deciding which television transmissions will be aired on a given time and day.  This is a collection of complex actions.  It should not be confused with the transmissions that are aired or the information or conceptual work content transmitted.")
(comment MediaProgrammer "A person who performs instances of #$MediaProgramming as part of his/her job.")
(comment TelevisionProgrammer "A person who performs instances of #$TelevisionProgramming as part of his/her job.")
(comment PsychologicalWarfare "The collection of extended conflict events that are considered \"psychological warfare\".  Each instance of this collection is some complex event in which psychological methods are employed in an effort to win converts to one's side, decrease the morale of the opposing force, etc..")
(comment FactivoreRapidPrototypeTemplate "A spec of #$FormulaTemplate. The collection of formula templates involved in rapid prototyping.")
(comment BallisticMissileLaunch-Complete "The complete flight of a #$BallisticMissile.")
(comment BoostPhase "The boost phase during a #$BallisticMissile's flight.")
(comment BallisticFlightPhase-Missile "The ballistic phase during a #$BallisticMissile's flight.")
(comment ReEntryPhase "The phase during a #$BallisticMissile's flight when it re-enter's the atmosphere.")
(comment PayLoad "The pay load part of a #$Missile.")
(comment RocketBooster "The booster part of a #$Missile.")
(comment CBLEndSessionFn "A binary function that returns a #$CBLEndSession command and which is composed of the #$CBLMethod and the lexical command sequence number.")
(comment CBLBeginSessionFn "A binary function that returns a #$CBLBeginSession command and which is composed of the #$CBLMethod and the lexical command sequence number.")
(comment Interrogation "The collection of interrogation events in which some prisoner or detainee is asked for information.  Often, psychological methods are employed to make the subject more willing to talk.  Interrogations are often performed by persons with some position of authority over the subject.")
(comment CounterInterrogationAct "The collection of acts performed by the subjects of #$Interrogations when they use various methods to try and give false information to the interrogator.")
(comment FundraisingActivity "The collection of all fundraising activities.  Usually performed by organizations or individuals working on behalf of an organization.")
(comment RegressionAnalysis "The collection of analysis events in which one tries to determine the values of certain parameters for a function so that it best fits with some preexisting set of data observations.")
(comment MilitaryTactics-FieldOfStudy "A #$FieldOfStudy.  #$MilitaryTactics-FieldOfStudy is the branch of #$MilitaryScience that is concerned with detailed maneuvers to achieve objectives set by strategy.")
(comment ShockAndAwe-MilitaryTactic "#$ShockAndAwe-MilitaryTactic is the #$MilitaryTactic of attempting induce a state of #$Shock and #$Awe in the enemy, thereby breaking his will to fight.  Shock and awe is typically implemented via a series of spectacular #$MilitaryAttacks geared more toward psychological impact than deadliness.")
(comment ScorchedEarth-MilitaryTactic "#$ScorchedEarth-MilitaryTactic is the #$MilitaryTactic of destroying anything that might be useful to an enemy while retreating from an area.")
(comment MilitaryTactic "A specialization of #$Strategy.  Each instance of #$MilitaryTactic is a method of engaging and defeating an enemy in battle.  Examples include #$ScorchedEarth-MilitaryTactic and #$ShockAndAwe-MilitaryTactic.")
(comment ImplementationOfTacticFn "A unary #$ReifiableFunction that takes a #$MilitaryTactic and returns the collection of all #$PurposefulPhysicalActions that are implementations of that tactic.  For example, (#$ImplementationOfTacticFn #$ShockAndAwe-MilitaryTactic) is the collection of all implementations of the 'shock and awe' military tactic.")
(comment implementationOfTactic-Pred "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a #$MilitaryTactic to the collection of #$PurposefulPhysicalActions that are implementations of that tactic.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$ImplementationOfTacticFn (q.v.).")
(comment CBLSessionStateVariableFn "A binary function that returns a #$CBLSessionStateVariable and which is composed of the #$CBLNode and the name of the session state variable.")
(comment CBLNodeStateVariableFn "A binary function that returns a #$CBLNodeStateVariable and which is composed of the #$CBLNode and the name of the shared state variable.")
(comment effectOfActionIf-Props "A ternary predicate which relates three instances of #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  <code>(#$effectOfActionIf-Props ACTION COND EFFECT)</code> means that if <code>COND</code> is true in the context in which <code>ACTION</code> occurs, then <code>ACTION</code> makes <code>EFFECT</code> true. This predicate was designed to be used in the specification of planning domains (see #$PlanningDomainMicrotheory). <code>ACTION</code> should be an atomic sentence with an #$ActionPredicate as the formula operator (i.e. in the arg0 position). See also the binary predicate #$effectOfAction-Props.")
(comment methodForAction "A binary predicate which relates instances of #CycLSentence-Assertible to instances of #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  <code>(#$methodForAction ACTION ACTION_SEQUENCE)</code> states that <code>ACTION_SEQUENCE</code> describes an appropriate method for carrying out the action described by <code>ACTION</code>. For cases where <code>ACTION_SEQUENCE</code> consists of a series of steps sufficiently atomic that they might be reasoned over by an AI planner (cf. #$PlanningDomainMicrotheory), see the more specialized predicate #$planForTask.")
(comment CyclificationParser "Natural language parsers whose output can be automatically translated to #$CycL.")
(comment CyclifyFn "A function mapping English string to ordered lists of CycL interpretations.")
(comment ConferenceProgramCommittee "A specialization of #$ReviewCommittee.  Each instance is an organization whose responsibility it is to judge or evaluate the submissions to a particular conference or workshop for presentation or publication.")
(comment ArgSometimesIsaPredicate "The collection of ArgTypePredicates (q.v.) that specify argument-types
directly (by referencing certain collections) and impose constraints that
require an argument of a predicate being an instance of a SubLExpressionType
collection at some time.  More precisely, each instance
of ArgSometimesIsaPredicate PRED takes a Relation RELN as its first argument (or
\"arg1\"), and has at least one other argument-place (say the Mth) for
specifying an argument-type for one of RELN's argument-places (say the
Nth). (The value of N might be fixed or might be given by yet another of PRED's
arguments.) Suppose M=2 and N=1. PRED then takes a SubLExpressionType Collection
as its second argument, and a closed atomic sentence (or \"GAF\") of the form
(PRED RELN COL ..) puts a \"sometimes isa\" constraint on RELN's first
argument-place that is based on COL. If PRED is a \"single-argument\" constraint
predicate, the GAF entails that a closed formula of the form (RELN ARG1 ..) is
semantically well-formed only if ARG1 is an instance of 
SubLExpressionType COL in some time interval
(including #$Always-TimeInterval).")
(comment arg1SometimesIsa "An #$ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(#$arg1SometimesIsa RELATION
COLLECTION)</code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything
given as the first argument to <code>RELATION</code> must be an instance of
<code>COLLECTION</code> at some time.  More precisely, if
<code>(arg1SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)</code> holds then in order to
assert <code>(RELATION ARG1 ...)</code>, it must only be the case that there
exists some time interval (including #$Always-TimeInterval) in which
<code>(#$isa ARG1 COLLECTION)</code> holds.")
(comment arg2SometimesIsa "An #$ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(#$arg2SometimesIsa
RELATION COLLECTION)</code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that
anything given as the second argument to <code>RELATION</code> must be an
instance of <code>COLLECTION</code> at some time.  More precisely, if
<code>(arg2SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)</code> holds then in order to
assert <code>(RELATION ... ARG2 ...)</code>, it must only be the case that there
exists some time interval (including #$Always-TimeInterval) in which
<code>(#$isa ARG2 COLLECTION)</code> holds.")
(comment arg3SometimesIsa "An #$ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(#$arg3SometimesIsa
RELATION COLLECTION)</code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that
anything given as the third argument to <code>RELATION</code> must be an
instance of <code>COLLECTION</code> at some time.  More precisely, if
<code>(arg3SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)</code> holds then in order to
assert <code>(RELATION ... ARG3 ...)</code>, it must only be the case that there
exists some time interval (including #$Always-TimeInterval) in which
<code>(#$isa ARG3 COLLECTION)</code> holds.")
(comment arg4SometimesIsa "An #$ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(#$arg4SometimesIsa
RELATION COLLECTION)</code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that
anything given as the fourth argument to <code>RELATION</code> must be an
instance of <code>COLLECTION</code> at some time.  More precisely, if
<code>(arg3SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)</code> holds then in order to
assert <code>(RELATION ... ARG4 ...)</code>, it must only be the case that there
exists some time interval (including #$Always-TimeInterval) in which
<code>(#$isa ARG4 COLLECTION)</code> holds.")
(comment arg5SometimesIsa "An #$ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(#$arg5SometimesIsa
RELATION COLLECTION)</code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that
anything given as the fifth argument to <code>RELATION</code> must be an
instance of <code>COLLECTION</code> at some time.  More precisely, if
<code>(arg3SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)</code> holds then in order to
assert <code>(RELATION ... ARG5 ...)</code>, it must only be the case that there
exists some time interval (including #$Always-TimeInterval) in which
<code>(#$isa ARG5 COLLECTION)</code> holds.")
(comment arg6SometimesIsa "An #$ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(#$arg6SometimesIsa
RELATION COLLECTION)</code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that
anything given as the sixth argument to <code>RELATION</code> must be an
instance of <code>COLLECTION</code> at some time.  More precisely, if
<code>(arg6SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)</code> holds then in order to
assert <code>(RELATION ... ARG6 ...)</code>, it must only be the case that there
exists some time interval (including #$Always-TimeInterval) in which
<code>(#$isa ARG6 COLLECTION)</code> holds.")
(comment ReadingComprehensionKBContentTest "These are KBCTs which test whether Cyc can prove that a particular text answers a particular question.")
(comment CBLProcessBySessionIDFn "(#$CBLProcessBySessionIDFn SESSION-ID) denotes the instance of #$ComputerProcessRunning in the #$CycBehaviorEngine which has been assigned the session-identifying SESSION-ID GUID.")
(comment CBLStateObjectInstanceFn "(#$CBLStateObjectInstanceFn STATE-OBJECT) denotes the current instance of the #$CycBehaviorLanguage state object.")
(comment infelicitousQuerySentence "(#$infelicitousQuerySentence SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE is an inappropriate form question for the #$CycSalientDescriptor to ask. See also #$uninterestingQueryForRelnWithTypeInArg.")
(comment uninterestingQueryForRelnWithTypeInArg "<p>This predicate is a directive for the #$CycSalientDescriptor. (#$uninterestingQueryForRelnWithTypeInArg RELN TYPE ARG) means that for any query on RELN where INS is an instance of TYPE, and INS stands in argument place ARG of RELN, (RELN INS VARIABLE) is an uninteresting question.</p> <p>For example, (#$uninterestingQueryForRelnWithTypeInArg #$eventOccursAt #$MoneyTransaction 1) means that if TRANSACTION is an instance of #$MoneyTransaction, (#$eventOccursAt TRANSACTION WHERE) is an uninteresting question for the #$CycSalientDescriptor to ask.</p>")
(comment uninterestingQueryForRelnWithTermInArg "<p>This predicate is a directive for the #$CycSalientDescriptor. (#$uninterestingQueryForRelnWithTermInArg RELN TYPE ARG) means that for any query on RELN where TERM stands in argument place ARG of RELN, (RELN TERM VARIABLE) is an uninteresting question.</p> <p>For example, (#$uninterestingQueryForRelnWithTermInArg #$eventOccursAt #$InterestAccruingEvent001 1) means that if (#$eventOccursAt #$InterestAccruingEvent001 WHERE) is an uninteresting question for the #$CycSalientDescriptor to ask.</p>")
(comment lawPrescribesActType "A binary #$IntangibleObjectPredicate.  <code>(#$lawPrescribesActType LAW ACTTYPE)</code> means that <code>LAW</code> requires any agent subject to it (see #$subjectToCOC) to perform at least one (and in some cases more, possibly regularly-recurring) instances of <code>ACTTYPE</code>.  This of course does <i>not</i> imply that such acts are performed, since laws are sometimes violated.
<p>
For example, a law might require everyone within a certain age range to register for the miltary draft.  Or a law might require a given parent to make monthly child-support payments to their child's other parent.
<p>
See also #$lawProscribesActType.")
(comment lawProscribesActType "A binary #$IntangibleObjertPredicate.  <code>(#$lawProscribesActType LAW ACTTYPE)</code> means that <code>LAW</code> prohibits any agent subject to it (see #$subjectToCOC) from performing instances of <code>ACTTYPE</code>.  This of course does <i>not</i> imply that no such acts are performed, since laws are sometimes violated.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$lawProscribesActType #$StealingIsIllegal #$Stealing)</code> means that the law #$StealingIsIllegal prohibits stealing.
<p>
See also #$lawPrescribesActType and #$agentProhibitsActType.")
(comment ist-Prohibition "(#$ist-Prohibition MT PROP) means that PROP is prohibited by MT, where MT is a microtheory that corresponds to an instance of #$Obligation via #$contextOfPCW.  This predicate allows the propositional content of prohibitions that apply to actions of agents to be stated in #$CycL.  PROP must be a closed formula.  Statements of the form (#$ist-Prohibition MT PROP) require that PROP mention the variable ?the-agent and/or ?the-action.  If some agent, AGENT, fulfills the role of ?the-agent, and in PROP and AGENT is an #$obligatedAgents for OBLIGATION then (#$agentViolatesObligation AGENT OBLIGATION) is concluded.  If some ACTION can bind to ?the-action in PROP then (#$actionViolatesObligation ACTION OBLIGATION) is concluded.  Once asserted, an #$afterAdding should cause a rule to be added to the system.  This rule will look like (#$implies (#$and PROP (#$obligatedAgents OBLIGATION ?the-agent)) (#$agentViolatesObligation ?the-agent OBLIGATION)).  See also #$ist-Obligation.")
(comment ist-Agreement "The predicate #$ist-Agreement is used to indicate the propositions which have been agreed upon in a particular agreement.  (#$ist-Agreement AGR-MT PROP) means that the #$Agreement that corresponds to the #$Microtheory AGR-MT (via #$contextOfPCW) pertains to (commits its agreeing parties to) making the proposition (#$CycLSentence-Assertible) PROP true. Since each #$Agreement is represented in Cyc as a #$Microtheory, the way that this is expressed is to say that PROP is considered to <i>be</i> true within the microtheory which represents AGR.  PROP may or may not be true in reality (or, thus, according to #$Microtheorys intended to represent reality).
<p>
(#$ist-Agreement AGR-MT PROP) should not be taken to be a simple specialization of (#$ist MT PROP) for cases where MT is an instance of #$Agreement. Whereas #$ist relates any particular microtheory to all assertions that happen to be true in that microtheory, #$ist-Agreement indicates only those assertions in an #$Agreement microtheory which pertain to the agreement itself (and are not just something that happens to be true in it, e.g., that one of the #$agreeingAgents is named \"Joe\").")
(comment obligationOwedTo "Points from an #$Obligation to the agent to whom the obligation is owed.  Note: this slot is not filled for all obligations.  For example, we probably don't want to commit to a particular agent to whom a mother is obliged in nursing her baby.  However, if Fred accepts Sally's request that he clean the toaster then she is the value on the #$obligationOwedTo for FredsToasterCleaningObligationMt.")
(comment ComputerProgramTypeByPlatform "#$ComputerProgramTypeByPlatform is a collection of types of computer programs.  Collections that are instances of #$ComputerProgramTypeByPlatform are collections of programs for which any instance PROG, (#$runsUnderOS PROG OS) is true for some single value of OS.")
(comment onSamePlanetSurfaceAs "This is a very general predicate inter-relating all things on the surface of the same planet.  <code>(#$onSamePlanetSurfaceAs  THINGORPLACE1 THINGORPLACE2)</code> means that the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>THINGORPLACE1</code> and the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>THINGORPLACE2</code> occur on or near the surface of the same planet.  Thus the country denoted by #$France and any instance of the collection #$Bicycle in the #$CityOfPerthAustralia are so related.The relation denoted by #$onSamePlanetSurfaceAs holds between airplanes flying over the earth, people hopping on the earth, and people deep in a mine on the earth, but this relation does not hold between any of the aformentioned entities and a spacecraft deep in outer space, or the Moon, or Andromeda.  Note that for thing T1 to be east of some other thing T2, or southwest of it, etc., it must be the case that T1 is on the same planet as T2.")
(comment cityOfAddress "<code>(#$cityOfAddress LOC CITY)</code> means that the  #$ContactLocation <code>LOC</code> is found in the territory of the #$City <code>CITY</code>. For example, as  #$CycorpHeadquarters is a #$ContactLocation for #$Cycorp, then  (#$cityOfAddress #$CycorpHeadquarters #$CityOfAustinTX) means that the  Cycorp Headquarters building is located in Austin, Texas.  Note that the  arg-constraint on the first argument should be an instance of #$ContactLocation  which serves as a #$pointsOfContact for an agent and not the agent itself.")
(comment programUsed "This predicate is an instance of #$ActorSlot (q.v.) that relates computer programs to the computer activities in which their copies are used.  <code>(#$programUsed ACT PROG)</code> means that a copy of <code>PROG</code> is used in the activity <code>ACT</code>.  For example, (#$programUsed MyEMailSendingThisMorning #$Eudora-TheProgram) means that in MyEMailSendingThisMorning a program I used was #$Eudora-TheProgram.  Note that more that one program may be used in a single computer activity -- the #$arg2Format of #$programUsed is #$SetTheFormat. For example, when I browse the Cyc KB, I typically use #$NetscapeNavigator, #$Emacs-TheProgram, #$AllegroCommonLisp, and of course #$CycProgram.")
(comment searchEngineUsed "An actor slot that is used to relate an electronic data search to the search engine used in it.  <code>(#$searchEngineUsed SEARCH ENGINE)</code> means that in the event <code>SEARCH</code> (an instance of #$ElectronicDataSearching), the search engine used is the #$SearchEngine <code>ENGINE</code>.")
(comment InductiveLogicProgrammingMode "A sub-collection of #$ProgramSpecification.  Instances of #$InductiveLogicProgrammingMode constitute part of the settings for inductive logic programs like #$ALEPH.  Specifically, they serve to increase the efficiency of the system by constraining the search space of possible rules.")
(comment Individual-ILPMode "The sub-collection of #$InductiveLogicProgrammingMode that deal with the representation of argument constraints that are individuals.  Contrast with its sibling collection #$Collection-ILPMode.")
(disjointWith Individual-ILPMode Collection-ILPMode)
(comment Collection-ILPMode "The sub-collection of #$InductiveLogicProgrammingMode that deal with the representation of argument constraints that are collections.  Contrast with its sibling collection #$Individual-ILPMode.")
(comment modeForIOandIndividualType "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$IndividualArgModeFn.")
(comment modeForIOandCollection "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$CollectionArgModeFn.")
(comment SextaryPredicate "A #$PredicateTypeByArity and specialization of (#$ArityRelationFn 6).  Each instance of #$SextaryPredicate is a #$Predicate whose #$arity is 6.")
(comment constantNameAutoGeneratedFromCollection "(#$constantNameAutoGeneratedFromCollection CONSTANT COLLECTION NAME) means that NAME, a present or former name for CONSTANT was automatically generated from COLLECTION.")
(comment Dog "A #$BiologicalSpecies (scientific name 'Canis familiaris') that is a specialization of #$CanineAnimal (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Dog is a canine animal that has either been bred to be a domestic pet (see #$DomesticatedAnimal) or is a wild canine animal that is not an instance of #$Wolf, #$Fox, or any other non-dog specialization of #$CanineAnimal. Note that although #$Dog and #$Wolf are considered distinct #$BiologicalSpecies, instances of the two can and do interbreed successfully. This species classification is therefore unusual, and in some circles, controversial.")
(comment declarationModesThroughArg "An assertion of the form (#$declarationModesThroughArg DEC PRED SYMB LIST N) is used to represent a partial mode declaration relative to the InductiveLogicProgrammingDeclaration DEC. This predicate works in a recursive manner with the predicate declarationModes-Final to generate a complete mode declaration.")
(comment declarationModes-Final "An assertion of the form (#$declarationModes-Final DEC PRED SYMB LIST) is used to state that for the InductiveLogicProgrammingDeclaration DEC, one of its elements, the Predicate PRED, can be given the mode represented by SYMB and LIST, which is itself a list of instances of InductiveLogicProgrammingMode. In short, this allows us to pass out to a Prolog-ComputerLanguage based ILP system a mode declaration in a recognizable format that recognizes arg constraints among CycL predicates. Assertion using the predicate declarationModes-Final are generated in conjunction with assertions using the predicate declarationModesThroughArg.")
(comment languageForSession "(#$languageForSession LANGUAGE SESSION) means that for #$ComputerUserInteractiveSession SESSION, the language used by the session's program (see #$sessionOfProgram) is LANGUAGE. For example, (#$languageForSession #$MSWordSession001 #$FrenchLanguage) means that for the designated session of #$MSWord, the default language is #$FrenchLanguage.")
(comment regionalDialectOfLanguage "(#$regionalDialectOfLanguage LANGUAGE REGION DIALECT) means that DIALECT is the #$LanguageDialect of LANGUAGE indigienous to REGION. For example, (#$regionalDialectOfLanguage #$ItalianLanguage (#$NorthEasternRegionFn #$Italy) #$FriulianDialect) means that Friulian is the a dialect of Italian indigenous to northeatern Italy.")
(comment RegionalDialectOfLanguageFn "(#$RegionalDialectOfLanguageFn LANGUAGE REGION) denotes the #$LanguageDialect of LANGUAGE indigenous to REGION. For example, (#$RegionalDialectOfLanguageFn #$EnglishLanguage #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) denotes American English. See also #$regionalDialectOfLanguage.")
(comment AmericanEnglishDialect "The #$LanguageDialect of the #$EnglishLanguage spoken in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment BritishEnglishDialect "The #$LanguageDialect of the #$EnglishLanguage spoken in the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland.")
(comment manuscriptOfPCW-Type "(#$manuscriptOfPCW-Type PCW-TYPE MANUSCRIPT-TYPE) means that MANUSCRIPT-TYPE is the collection of all #$Manuscript-CWs of instances of PCW-TYPE. For example, (#$manuscriptOfPCW-Type #$Article-PCW MANUSCRIPT-TYPE) means that MANUSCRIPT-TYPE is the collection of all article manuscripts.")
(comment manuscriptOfPCW "(#$manuscriptOfPCW PCW MANUSCRIPT) means that MANUSCRIPT is the #$Manuscript-CW of #$PublishedConceptualWork PCW. For example, (#$manuscriptOfPCW #$TheCognitiveStructureOfEmotions-Book MANUSCRIPT) means that MANUSCRIPT is the manuscript of <i>The Cognitive Structure of Emotions</i>.")
(comment ConceptExtractionTool "The collection of all instances of #$ApplicationProgram that take as input either an instance of textual #$Corpus (whether it be formatted as a string, a list of strings, or a file) and returns (perhaps among other things) a list of words or phrases that denote concepts of significance mentioned in that corpus.")
(comment extractedFromCorpusUsingTool "(extractedFromCorpusUsingTool THING CORPUS TOOL) means that the instance TOOL of ConceptExtractionTool was used to extract (identify a mention of) THING in the instance of Corpus CORPUS. Note that extractedFromCorpusUsingTool is an instance of TemporallyQualifiableRelation. (extractedFromCorpusUsingTool THING CORPUS TOOL) is true at time T iff there is an #$ConceptExtraction event that has completed at T or earlier, such that TOOL is the programUsed, CORPUS is the #$conceptExtractionSource and THING is the #$conceptExtracted.")
(comment genlPredsWRTArgs "A ternary #$MetaPredicate that is used to state that two predicates stand in a #$genlPreds -like relation to each other with respect to a specified correlation between their argument-places.  The first predicate's #$arity might be the same as, greater than, or less than that of the second predicate; and the argument-place correlation is encoded by a list of non-negative integers whose length is equal to the arity of the second predicate.  The encoding scheme is roughly this: the position of a given integer within the list represents that same argument-position within the second predicate, while the size of the integer represents the corresponding argument-position within the first predicate.
<p>
First, suppose that <code>SPECPRED</code>'s arity is greater than or equal to that of <code>GENLPRED</code>.  In that case, each integer in <code>ARGNUMLIST</code> should be greater than 0, and <code>(#$genlPredsWRTArgs SPECPRED GENLPRED ARGNUMLIST)</code> means that, whenever <code>SPECPRED</code> holds of a given argument-sequence <code>SPEC-SEQ</code>, then <code>GENLPREDS</code> holds of the sequence <code>GENL-SEQ</code>, defined as follows: where the <code>I</code>th item in <code>ARGNUMLIST</code> is the integer <code>N</code>, the <code>I</code>th item in <code>GENL-SEQ</code> is the same as the <code>N</code>th item in <code>SPEC-SEQ</code>.  For example,
<pre>
  (#$genlPredsWRTArgs #$touchesWith #$touches (#$TheList 3 2))
</pre>
entails
<pre>
  (#$implies
    (#$touchesWith #$MingXu Steak8 Fork25)
    (#$touches Fork25 Steak8) .
</pre>
Second, suppose that <code>SPECPRED</code>'s arity is less than that of <code>GENLPRED</code>, and the difference in their arities is <code>M</code>.  In that case, the integer 0 should appear in <code>ARGNUMLIST</code> in exactly <code>M</code> different places, and <code>(#$genlPredsWRTArgs SPECPRED GENLPRED ARGNUMLIST)</code> means that, whenever <code>SPECPRED</code> holds of a given argument-sequence <code>SPEC-SEQ</code>, there are <code>M</code> things <code>OBJ-1</code>, ..., <code>OBJ-M</code> such that <code>GENLPREDS</code> holds of the sequence <code>GENL-SEQ</code>, defined as follows: where the <code>I</code>th item in <code>ARGNUMLIST</code> is the integer <code>N</code> (for <code>N</code> > 0), the <code>I</code>th item in <code>GENL-SEQ</code> is the same as the <code>N</code>th item in <code>SPEC-SEQ</code>; and where the <code>I</code>th item in <code>ARGNUMLIST</code> is the <code>J</code>th appearance of 0 in <code>ARGNUMLIST</code> (for 1 <= <code>J</code> <= <code>M</code>), the <code>I</code>th item in <code>GENL-SEQ</code> is <code>OBJ-J</code>.  For example,
<pre>
  (#$genlPredsWRTArgs #$transports #$transportsVia (#$TheList 1 2 0))
</pre>
entails
<pre>
  (#$implies
    (#$transports #$Klein Clutch5)
    (#$thereExists ?X (#$transportsVia #$Klein Clutch5 ?X)) .
</pre>
<p>
See also #$genlPredsWRTTypes.")
(comment candidateModeForArgForDeclaration "An assertion of the form (#$candidateModeForArgForDeclaration PRED MODE N DEC) means that relative to the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination DEC, the #$Predicate PRED's  Nth argument can be adequately constrained with the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingMode MODE. This is a utility predicate in relation to the predicate ")
(disjointWith Agreement MediaSeriesProduct)
(comment bloodAlcoholContent "A #$NumericIntervalSlot that relates an #$Animal to a #$Real0-1.  (#$bloodAlcoholContent ANIMAL N) means that N/1 of ANIMAL's #$Blood currently consists of #$EthylAlcohol.  For example, (#$bloodAlcoholContent Otis (#$Percent 0.2)) means that 1/500 (0.002) of Otis's blood is alcohol.")
(comment FieldType-LogicalOrPhysical "This type-level collection partitions #$Field-LogicalOrPhysical into #$LogicalField and #$PhysicalField.")
(comment ViolentCollision "The collection of instances of #$Colliding in which one or more of the objects involved is damaged as a result.")
(comment homeBuyer "An #$ActorSlot and (typed) specialization of #$buyer.  Where BUYING is an instance of (#$BuyingFn #$HumanResidence) and BUYER is a #$HumanAdult, (#$homeBuyer BUYING BUYER) means that BUYER is a buyer in BUYING.")
(comment portalState "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot and specialization of #$isa.  Where PORTAL is a #$Portal and STATE is a #$PortalTypeByState, (#$portalState PORTAL STATE) means that PORTAL is in the state STATE.")
(comment qualityOfProduct "A #$NonAspectualQuantitySlot that relates an #$Artifact to a #$LevelOfQuality.  (#$qualityOfProduct ARTIFACT LEVEL) means that ARTIFACT's level of quality is LEVEL.")
(comment NonAspectualQuantitySlot "A specialization of #$QuantitySlot (q.v.).  Each instance of #$NonAspectualQuantitySlot is a binary predicate that is used to attribute a property to a thing, by relating it to a #$NonAspectualQuantity (q.v.) of some sort.
<p>
Instances of #$NonAspectualQuantitySlot include #$rigidityOfObject and #$hasGlamour.")
(comment pulseRate "A #$NumericIntervalSlot.  (#$pulseRate ANIMAL NUM) means that ANIMAL's pulse rate is NUM beats per minute.")
(comment supportingObject "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an instance of #$SupportingSomething to a #$PartiallyTangible.  (#$supportingObject SUPPORTING OBJECT) means that OBJECT is supporting something in SUPPORTING.")
(comment objectTypesBought "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$Buying to an #$ObjectType.  (#$objectTypesBought BUYING TYPE) means that an instance of TYPE was bought in BUYING.")
(comment financialState "A (typed) specialization of #$isa that relates an #$IntelligentAgent to a #$SocialBeingTypeByFinancialState.  (#$financialState AGENT STATE) means that AGENT's financial state is STATE.  For instance, (#$financialState #$BillGates #$Wealthy) means that Bill Gates is wealthy.")
(comment dbOwner "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$LogicalTableSchema to a #$SocialBeing.  (#$dbOwner LTS BEING) means that BEING owns LTS.")
(comment causes-SitTypeProp "A #$CausationPredicate that relates a specialization of #$Situation to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$causes-SitTypeProp SIT-TYPE PROP) means that under normal circumstances, an instance of SIT-TYPE will cause PROP to be true.")
(comment taxExemptIncome "A #$QuantitySlot that relates a #$SocialBeing to a #$MonetaryRate.  (#$taxExemptIncome BEING RATE) means that RATE is BEING's tax-exempt income rate.")
(comment supportedObject "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an instance of #$SupportingSomething to a #$PartiallyTangible.  (#$supportedObject SUPPORTING OBJECT) means that OBJECT is supported in SUPPORTING.")
(comment publisher "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$PublishedMaterial to an #$IntelligentAgent.  (#$publisher MATERIAL AGENT) means that AGENT is the publisher of MATERIAL.")
(comment medicalSpecialty "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$MedicalCareProfessional to a #$MedicalSpecialistType.  (#$medicalSpecialty PERSON SPECIALTY) means that PERSON's medical specialty is SPECIALTY.")
(comment agentTortured "An #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$Torture to a #$PerceptualAgent.  (#$agentTortured TORTURE AGENT) means that AGENT is tortured in TORTURE.")
(comment constituentTypes "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to an #$ExistingStuffType.  (#$constituentTypes OBJ TYPE) means that there is an instance INST of TYPE such that (#$constituents OBJ INST).")
(comment situationMonitored "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$Monitoring to a #$Situation.  (#$situationMonitored MONITORING SITUATION) means that SITUATION is a situation that is monitored in MONITORING.")
(comment intendedMaleficiary-ElectronicAttack "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an #$AttackByComputerOperation to an #$Agent-Generic.  (#$intendedMaleficiary ATTACK AGENT) means that AGENT is an intended target of ATTACK.")
(comment bandwidthOfInfoPath "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot that relates a #$Path-InfoTransfer to a #$Bandwidth.  (#$bandwidthOfInfoPath PATH BW) means that the bandwidth of PATH is BW.")
(comment containsMisinformationAbout "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$InformationStore to a #$Thing.  (#$containsMisinformationAbout INFO-STORE THING) means that INFO-STORE contains misinformation about THING.")
(comment bandwidthOfInfoPathType "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot that relates a specialization of #$Path-InfoTransfer to a #$Bandwidth.  (#$bandwidthOfInfoPathType PATH-TYPE BW) means that each instance of PATH-TYPE has a bandwidth of BW.")
(comment sOEArcTypeCompatibleWithNodeAsSource "<code>(#$sOEArcTypeCompatibleWithNodeAsSource NODE ARC-TYPE)</code> means that the #$GLFNode <code>NODE</code> is such that some instance of <code>ARC-TYPE</code> (which is itself a specialization of #$SOEArc) may connect <code>NODE</code> to another node in an SOE graph, with <code>NODE</code> as the source of the link (<i>i.e.</i>, with <code>NODE</code> as the as the second argument in a #$linkFromToInSystem assertion, where the first argument is an instance of <code>ARC-TYPE</code>).")
(comment sOEArcTypeCompatibleWithNodeAsDestination "<code>(#$sOEArcTypeCompatibleWithNodeAsSource NODE ARC-TYPE)</code> means that the #$GLFNode <code>NODE</code> is such that some instance of <code>ARC-TYPE</code> (which is itself a specialization of #$SOEArc) may connect <code>NODE</code> to another node in an SOE graph, with <code>NODE</code> as the destination of the link (<i>i.e.</i>, with <code>NODE</code> as the as the third argument in a #$linkFromToInSystem assertion, where the first argument is an instance of <code>ARC-TYPE</code>).")
(comment linkedByCommPath "A #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate that relates a #$PhysicalDevice to a #$PhysicalDevice.  (#$linkedByCommPath DEVICE1 DEVICE2) means that DEVICE! AND DEVICE2 are linked by some communication path.")
(comment linkedByCommLink "A #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate that relates a #$PhysicalDevice to a #$PhysicalDevice.  (#$linkedByCommLink DEVICE1 DEVICE2) means that DEVICE1 AND DEVICE2 are connected by some communication link.")
(comment pointsConnected "A #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate that relates a #$Thing to a #$Thing.  (#$pointsConnected THING1 THING2) means that THING1 and THING2 are connected by some #$Path-Generic.")
(comment agentTypePosesThreat "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$Agent-Generic to an #$Agent-Generic.  (#$agentTypePosesThreat AGT-TYPE AGT) means that instances of AGT-TYPE pose a threat to AGT.")
(comment subjectOfInspection "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an instance of #$Inspecting to #$SomethingExisting.  (#$subjectOfInspection INSPECTING THING) means that THING is the thing inspected in INSPECTING.")
(comment objectMadeAvailable "An #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$MakingSomethingAvailable to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  (#$objectMadeAvailable MAKING OBJ) means that OBJ is made available in MAKING.")
(comment southeastOf "A #$RelativeLocationalPredicate and #$ELRelation-OneWay.  (#$southeastOf X Y) means that X is southeast of Y (or, equivalently, that Y is northwest of X).")
(comment southwestOf "A #$RelativeLocationalPredicate and #$ELRelation-OneWay.  (#$southwestOf X Y) means that X is southwest of Y (or, equivalently, that Y is northeast of X).")
(comment southOf "A #$RelativeLocationalPredicate and #$ELRelation-OneWay.  (#$southOf X Y) means that X is south of Y (or, equivalently, that Y is north of X).")
(comment westOf "A #$RelativeLocationalPredicate and #$ELRelation-OneWay.  (#$westOf X Y) means that X west of Y (or, equivalently, that Y is east of X).")
(comment bridgeInPath "A #$PhysicalPartPredicate that relates a #$Path-Customary to a #$Bridge.  (#$bridgeInPath PATH BRIDGE) means that BRIDGE is a #$Bridge that is part of PATH.")
(comment MultiplePerformerAction "A specialization of #$MultipleDoerAction (q.v.). Each instance of #$MultiplePerformerAction is an action which must have more than one \"performer\" (see the predicate #$performedBy).  In order for a type of action (i.e. a specialization of #$Action) to be a specialization of #$MultiplePerformerAction, it must be true to assert, for any instance <code>ACT</code> of that type of action, both <code>(#$performedBy ACT X)</code> and <code>(#$performedBy ACT Y)</code>, for some <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code> that are different.  Notable specializations of #$MultiplePerformerAction include #$GettingToKnowSomeone and #$GoingOnADate.")
(comment affectedType-Direct "A #$BinaryPredicate and specialization of #$affectedType that relates an #$Event to a specialization of #$SomethingExisting.  (#$affectedType-Direct EVENT TYPE) means that instances of TYPE are directly affected by EVENT.  See also #$affectedType-Indirect.")
(comment affectedType-Indirect "A #$BinaryPredicate and specialization of #$affectedType that relates an #$Event to a specialization of #$SomethingExisting.  (#$affectedType-Indirect EVENT TYPE) means that instances of TYPE are indirectly affected by EVENT.  See also #$affectedType-Direct.")
(comment after-Underspecified "An #$UnderspecifiedPredicate.  (#$after-Underspecified THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is in some sense after THING2.")
(comment TreeOrganizationalChart "A collection of #$InformationStores and a subcollection of #$OrganizationalChart.  Each instance of #$OrganizationalChart graphically depicts information about the control structure tree of an organization.")
(comment chartOfOrganization "(#$chartOfOrganization ORG CHART) means that #$Organization ORG has CHART as its #$OrganizationalChart.")
(comment chartOfOrganizationTree "(#$chartOfOrganizationTree ORG CHART) means that the tree structured #$Organization ORG has CHART as its tree structured #$OrganizationalChart.")
(comment ComputerUserInteraction-SOE "A specialization of #$ComputerUserInteraction.  Each instance of #$ComputerUserInteraction-SOE is an interaction that occurs during an SOE-driven knowledge authoring session.")
(comment OperatingOnAnSOENode "A specialization of #$ComputerUserInteraction-SOE.  Each instance of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to interact with a node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment DeletingAnSOELink "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOELink.  Each instance of #$DeletingAnSOELink is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to delete a link in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment DeletingAnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$DeletingAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to delete a node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment OperatingOnAnSOELink "A specialization of #$ComputerUserInteraction-SOE.  Each instance of #$OperatingOnAnSOELink is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to interact with a link in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment TheCycOntologyGraph "An instance of #$GLFGraph (q.v.).  This conceptual work is a graphical depiction of #$TheCycOntology.")
(comment focalNodeInSystem "<code>(#$focalNodeInSystem NODE GRAPH)</code> means that <code>NODE</code> is the currently the focal node in the graph <code>GRAPH</code>.")
(comment before-Underspecified "An #$UnderspecifiedPredicate.  (#$before-Underspecified THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is in some sense before THING2.")
(comment without-Underspecified "An #$UnderspecifiedPredicate.  (#$without-Underspecified THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is in some sense without THING2.")
(comment by-Underspecified "An #$UnderspecifiedPredicate.  (#$by-Underspecified THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is in some sense by THING2.")
(comment greaterMassThan "A binary #$ComparisonPredicate that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to a #$PartiallyTangible.  (#$greaterMassThan PT1 PT2) means that PT1 has a greater #$Mass than PT2.")
(comment pseudonym "A #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$ProperNameString.  (#$pseudonym AGT STRING) means that STRING is a pseudonym of AGT.")
(comment plural-Feminine "A #$SpeechPartPredicate that relates a #$LexicalWord to a #$CharacterString.  (#$plural-Feminine WORD STRING) means that STRING is the feminine plural form of WORD.")
(comment plural-Neuter "A #$SpeechPartPredicate that relates a #$LexicalWord to a #$CharacterString.  (#$plural-Neuter WORD STRING) means that STRING is the neuter plural form of WORD.")
(comment singular-Neuter "A #$SpeechPartPredicate that relates a #$LexicalWord to a #$CharacterString.  (#$singular-Neuter WORD STRING) means that STRING is the neuter singular form of WORD.")
(comment plural-Masculine "A #$SpeechPartPredicate that relates a #$LexicalWord to a #$CharacterString.  (#$plural-Masculine WORD STRING) means that STRING is the masculine plural form of WORD.")
(comment singular-Feminine "A #$SpeechPartPredicate that relates a #$LexicalWord to a #$CharacterString.  (#$singular-Feminine WORD STRING) means that STRING is the feminine singular form of WORD.")
(comment pnNonPlural-Generic "A #$GenericSpeechPartPredicate that relates a #$LexicalWord to a #$CharacterString.  (#$pnNonPlural-Generic WORD STRING) means that STRING is the non-plural proper noun form of WORD.")
(comment singular-Masculine "A #$SpeechPartPredicate that relates a #$LexicalWord to a #$CharacterString.  (#$singular-Masculine WORD STRING) means that STRING is the masculine singular form of WORD.")
(comment AddingANewLinkAndNewNodeToAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkAndNewNodeToAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link and node to an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedFacetMemberOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedFacetMemberOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to an as-yet undisplayed facet member of an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedFacetOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedFacetOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to an as yet ungraphed faceting collection of an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedGenlsOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedGenlsOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to an as yet ungraphed generalization of an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedSpecOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedSpecOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to an as yet ungraphed specialization of an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment SOEFromFacetArc "Each instance of #$SOEFromFacetArc connects a faceting collection to tone of its instances. See also #$SOEToFacetArc, which is the collection of arcs that connect collections to the collections that facet them.")
(comment SOEToFacetArc "Each instance of #$SOEToFacetArc connects a collection to a collection that facets it.  See also #$SOEFromFacetArc, which is the collection of arcs that connect faceting collections to their instances.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedCategoryOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkAndNewNodeToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedCategoryOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to an as yet ungraphed collection of which of an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool is to be made an instance.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedInstanceOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkAndNewNodeToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedInstanceOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to an as yet ungraphed instance of an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToACategoryOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToACategoryOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to a node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool from a node which is to be made an instance of that node.")
(comment passportNumber "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$PassportIdentificationNumber.  (#$passportNumber AGT NUMBER) means that NUMBER is AGT's passport identification number.")
(comment driversLicenseIDNumber "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$DriversLicenseNumber.  (#$driversLicenseIDNumber AGT NUMBER) means that NUMBER is AGT's driver's license number.")
(comment creditCardAccountNumber "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$CreditCardNumber.  (#$creditCardAccountNumber AGT NUMBER) means that AGT has a credit card whose credit card number is NUMBER.")
(comment checkingAccountUniqueNumber "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$CheckingAccountNumber.  (#$checkingAccountUniqueNumber AGT NUMBER) means that AGT has a checking account whose checking account number is NUMBER.")
(comment detectionsOf "A #$FunctionalPredicate that relates a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible to a specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  (#$detectionsOf PT-TYPE EVENT-TYPE) means that EVENT-TYPE is the collection of events in which instances of PT-TYPE are detected.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$DetectionFn (q.v.).")
(comment seizes "A binary #$ComplexActionPredicate that relates an #$IntelligentAgent to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  (#$seizes AGT THING) means that there is an instance of #$TakingSomething in which AGT plays the #$performedBy role and THING plays the #$objectTaken role.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAFacetMemberOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAFacetMemberOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new #$SOEFromFacetArc link.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAFacetOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAFacetOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new #$SOEToFacetArc link.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAGenlsOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAGenlsOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new #$SOESpecArc link to a more general collection.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToASpecOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAGenlsOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new #$SOESpecArc link to a more general collection.")
(comment TNTEquivalentDeviceFn "A function that returns a specialization of #$ExplosiveDevice when given an instance of #$ScalarInterval as an argument.  For example, (#$TNTEquivalentDeviceFn (#$Pound-UnitOfMass 1000)) denotes the collection of explosive devices that typically explode with the force of 1000 pounds of TNT (see #$Trinitrotoluene). See also #$tNTEquivalent.")
(comment linkAddedToSOEGraph "<code>(#$linkAddedToSOEGraph ADD LINK)</code> means that in the event <code>ADD</code>, the link added to an SOE graph is <code>LINK</code>.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnInstanceOfAnSOENode "A specialization of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToACategoryOfAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to a node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool from a node which is to be made an instance of that node.")
(comment nodeAddedToSOEGraph "<code>(#$nodeAddedToSOEGraph ADD NODE)</code> means that in the event <code>ADD</code>, the node added to an SOE graph is <code>NODE</code>.")
(comment hasBeenAFocalNodeInSystem "<code>(#$hasBeenAFocalNodeInSystem NODE SYSTEM)</code> means that <code>NODE</code> has been made (on the currently running Cyc image) a focal node in a graphical display of at least a portion of the #$GLFGraph <code>SYSTEM</code>.")
(comment sizeOfObject-Underspecified "A binary #$UnderspecifiedPredicate that relates a #$SpatialThing to a #$MeasurableQuantity.  (#$sizeOfObject-Underspecified OBJ SIZE) means that OBJ is, in some sense, of the size SIZE.")
(comment linkDestination "<code>(#$linkDestination LINKING THING)</code> means that in the linking
together event, <code>LINKING</code> (an instance of
#$LinkingTogether), the  \"directional\" link created is <i>to</i>
<code>THING</code> from some other thing.  See also #$linkSource.")
(comment linkSource "<code>(#$linkSource LINKING THING)</code> means that in the linking
together event, <code>LINKING</code> (an instance of
#$LinkingTogether), the \"directional\" link created is <i>from</i>
<code>THING</code> to some other thing.  See also #$linkDestination.")
(comment AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode and #$LinkingTogether (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to add a new link to an existing node in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment sOEActionTypePermitted "<code>(#$sOEActionTypePermitted COMPONENT GRAPH ACTION-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that an instance of <code>ACTION-TYPE</code> (which is a specialization of #$ComputerUserInteraction-SOE) may (given the current structure and semantics of the graph <code>GRAPH</code> of which <code>COMPONENT</code> is a component) be performed on <code>COMPONENT</code> ( an instance of #$GLFGraphComponent).")
(comment ExchangeOfGreetings "A specialization of #$FaceToFacePresenceCommunicating, #$SociabilityBasedAction, and #$MultiDirectionalCommunication.  In each instance of #$ExchangeOfGreetings, two or more parties greet each other (see #$GreetingSomeone). The greetings in question may be verbal or non-verbal (for instance, a wave of the hand), and the exchange may or may not lead to further communication.")
(comment commutativeInArgs "A variable-arity #$MetaRelation used for stating that a given #$PartiallyCommutativeRelation (q.v.) is \"commutative\" with respect to two or more specified argument-places.
<p>
<code>(#$commutativeInArgs RELN ARGNUM-1 ... ARGNUM-N)</code> means that  <code>RELN</code> is commutative in its <code>ARGNUM-1</code>th, ..., and <code>ARGNUM-N</code>th arguments.  Thus <code>RELN</code> admits unrestricted permutation among  these arguments.  More precisely: (i) if <code>RELN</code> is a #$Predicate that  holds of a given argument-sequence <code>SEQ</code>, then <code>RELN</code> also holds of any other sequence <code>SEQ-PERMUTE</code> obtainable from <code>SEQ</code> by permuting some or all of <code>SEQ</code>'s <code>ARGNUM-1</code>th, ..., and <code>ARGNUM-N</code>th items (while leaving all of <code>SEQ</code>'s other items unchanged).  (ii) if <code>RELN</code> is a #$Function-Denotational that associates a given argument-sequence <code>SEQ</code> with the value <code>VALUE</code>, then <code>RELN</code> also associates any sequence <code>SEQ-PERMUTE</code> (as described above) with <code>VALUE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$commutativeInArgs #$formsBorderBetween 2 3)</code> has as a consequence that whenever a sentence of the form <code>(#$formsBorderBetween BORDER REG1 REG2)</code> holds, so does the corresponding sentence  <code>(#$formsBorderBetween BORDER REG2 REG1)</code>.
<p>
If <code>RELN</code> is commutative in at least two argument-places it is an #$AtLeastPartiallyCommutativeRelation.  If <code>RELN</code> is commutative in <i>all</i> argument-places it is, more specifically, a #$CommutativeRelation.  If <code>RELN</code> is commutative in at least two, but <i> not all</i>,
argument-places it is, instead, a #$PartiallyCommutativeRelation.
<p>
Note that the fact that each argument-place of a given relation commutes with some other argument-place is not sufficient for its being fully commutative.  For example, a partially-commutative quaternary relation might be such that its first and third places commute with each other and its second and fourth places commute with each other.")
(comment AuthoredSOENode-Faceting "A specialization of #$AuthoredSOENode.  Each instance of
#$AuthoredSOENode-Faceting is a node created when a user performs an instance of 
#$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedFacetOfAnSOENode.")
(comment AuthoredSOENode-Individual "A specialization of #$AuthoredSOENode.  Each instance of
#$AuthoredSOENode-Individual is a node created when a user performs an instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedInstanceOfAnSOENode.")
(comment AuthoredSOENode-NonFacetingCollection "A specialization of #$GLFNode.  Each instance of
#$AuthoredSOENode-NonFacetingCollection is a node created when a user performs an instance of #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedSpecOfAnSOENode, #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedGenlsOfAnSOENode,  #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedCategoryOfAnSOENode, or #$AddingANewLinkToAnUngraphedFacetMemberOfAnSOENode
        .")
(comment associatedPaymentPlan "<code>(#$typeAssociatedPaymentPlan TENDER PLAN)</code> means that the use of <code>TENDER</code> (an instance  of #$FinancialAccountTenderObject) requires that its owner repay expenditures according to <code>PLAN</code> (some instance of #$PaymentSchedule).")
(comment suppliedWithTypeAmount "(#$suppliedWithTypeAmount PT COL AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$Collection COL with which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT is supplied.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$suppliedWithTypeAmount is very general.  PT might, for example, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and the range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of supply of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to PT.")
(comment aisFileAbsolutePathname "(#$aisFileAbsolutePathname FILE NAME) means that the #$CharacterString NAME can be used as a #$FilePathname (that is an #$AbsolutePathname) to designate the #$ComputerFile-AIS FILE.  Note that there can be multiple names associated with the same file.  Note also that a single #$ComputerFile-AIS can have multiple corresponding instances of #$ComputerFileCopy stored in different areas of memory or on multiple computers or networks.")
(comment BiDirectionalCommunication "A specialization of #$MultiDirectionalCommunication (q.v.).  Each instance of #$BiDirectionalCommunication is a communication event in which exactly two agents communicate with each other.  That is, both agents play a #$communicatorOfInfo as well as an #$infoCommunicatedTo role with respect to the event; moreover, any information contributed (see #$infoContributed) by either agent is intended to be received (see #$infoGathered) by the other agent. See also #$interCommunicators.")
(comment interCommunicators "A ternary predicate that relates a #$MultiDirectionalCommunication event to two agents that communicate with each other (bi-directionally) in that event.  <code>(#$interCommunicators COMM AGENT1 AGENT2)</code> entails that both <code>AGENT1</code> and <code>AGENT2</code> are a #$communicatorOfInfo as well as an #$infoCommunicatedTo with respect to <code>COMM</code>; moreover, in the course of <code>COMM</code> some piece of information contributed by <code>AGENT1</code> and intended for <code>AGENT2</code> is in fact gathered by <code>AGENT2</code>, and vice versa (see #$infoContributed and #$infoGathered).  
<p>
For example, #$interCommunicators holds when two agents are greeting  (see #$ExchangeOfGreetings) or conversing with (see #$Conversation) each other.
<p>
Note that in some <i>but not all</i> cases, there will be two #$CommunicationAct-Single subevents of <code>COMM</code> such that <code>AGENT1</code> is the #$senderOfInfo and <code>AGENT2</code> the #$recipientOfInfo in one subevent, and vice versa for the other subevent. 
<p>
Note also that the fact that two agents are both #$communicationParticipants in a given #$MultiDirectionalCommunication is <i>not</i> a sufficient condition for their being #$interCommunicators.  For example, if you and I both take part in a group conversation among (say) six people, but we happen not to speak (or nonverbally communicate) to each other at all during the event, then we are not #$interCommunicators.")
(comment infoGathered "A ternary predicate that relates a #$MultiDirectionalCommunication (q.v.) and an agent to information received by the latter in the course of the former.  <code>(#$infoGathered COMM AGENT INFO)</code> means that there is a subevent of <code>COMM</code> that is an #$InformationTransferEvent in which <code>AGENT</code> is a #$recipientOfInfo and <code>INFO</code> is an #$infoTransferred.  
<p>
When it comes to multi-directional communication, #$infoGathered is the \"flip-side\" of #$infoContributed (q.v.).  In successful two-way communication (see #$BiDirectionalCommunication), any information contributed by one party will in turn be gathered by the other party, and vice versa.  In communications among larger groups, however, in which a given party might gather some but not all of the information contributed by the other parties, things can get much more complicated and the foregoing symmetry might not be present.")
(comment objectOfCritique "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$Critique-CW to a #$Thing.  (#$objectOfCritique CRITIQUE THING) means that THING is evaluated or \"critiqued\" in CRITIQUE.")
(comment agreementForAccount "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$LegalAgreement to an #$Account.  (#$agreementForAccount AGREEMENT ACCOUNT) means that AGREEMENT is the agreement governing ACCOUNT.")
(comment possessesCopyOf "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$Agent-Generic to a #$ConceptualWork.  (#$possessesCopyOf AGENT CW) means that AGENT #$possesses a copy (instantiation) of CW.")
(comment properNameStrings "An #$NLPredicate that relates a #$Thing to a #$ProperNameString.  (#$properNameStrings THING STRING) means that STRING is a proper name for THING.")
(comment referenceWorkEntryString "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$ReferenceWorkEntry to a #$CharacterString.  (#$referenceWorkEntryString ENTRY STRING) means that STRING is the text of ENTRY.")
(comment quotedArgument "A specialization of #$opaqueArgument (q.v.).  #$quotedArgument is a binary #$MetaLanguagePredicate used to state that a given argument-place of a given CycL relation-denoting expression is an <i>implicitly quoted</i> context, in the sense that a symbol appearing in that context denotes <i>itself</i> (as opposed to whatever that symbol might denote, if anything, in ordinary non-quoted contexts).  
<p>
<code>(#$quotedArgument REL N)</code> means that in a closed compound expression built from <code>REL</code> -- i.e. a ground atomic sentence (or <i>gaf</i>) if <code>REL</code> is a predicate or a closed non-atomic term (or <i>nat</i>) if <code>REL</code> is a function -- the term (i.e. the CycL expression) <code>EXPR</code> appearing in <code>REL</code>'s <code>N</code>th argument-place is taken to denote <i>itself</i> (i.e. that very expression <code>EXPR</code>).  
<p>
#$quotedArgument thus makes possible a kind of a self-reference in CycL. Relations with quoted argument-places can be used to make statements about particular CycL expressions, without quoting those expressions explicitly (cf. #$Quote).
<p>
For example, the first argument-place of the predicate #$myCreator is quoted and its second argument-place is not.  Thus in the sentence <code>(#$myCreator #$PlanetEarth #$Maeda)</code>, the CycL constant <code>#$PlanetEarth</code> denotes that constant itself (and not the actual planet Earth), while the constant <code>#$Maeda</code> simply denotes the person Maeda (and not a CycL expression).  Hence the above sentence correctly states that Maeda created (i.e. reified) the CycL constant <code>#$PlanetEarth</code>; it does <i>not</i> state the absurdity that he created the planet Earth.  In ordinary non-quoted contexts, of course, <code>#$PlanetEarth</code> denotes the planet and not the constant.
<p>
See also #$quotedCollection and #$NoteAboutUseVersusMention.")
(comment opaqueArgument "A binary #$MetaLanguagePredicate that can be used to state that a given argument-place of a given CycL relation-denoting expression is <i>denotationally opaque</i>.  
<p>
<code>(#$opaqueArgument REL N)</code> means that if in a closed compound expression built from the CycL expression for <code>REL</code> -- i.e. a ground atomic formula (or <i>gaf</i>) if <code>REL</code> is a predicate or a closed non-atomic term (or <i>nat</i>) if <code>REL</code> is a function -- the term appearing in <code>REL</code>'s <code>N</code>th argument-place is replaced with another term having the same denotatum (or truth-value, if the term is a sentence), there is no guarantee that the resulting gaf (or nat) will itself have the same truth-value (or denotatum) as the original.  
<p>
Most argument-places of most relation-denoting expressions do  allow such substitutions to be made freely, and are thus <i>denotationally transparent</i>.  For example, given that (#$equals #$Cicero #$Tully), the truth of <code>(#$residesInRegion #$Cicero #$CityOfRomeItaly)</code> entails the truth of  <code>(#$residesInRegion #$Tully #$CityOfRomeItaly)</code>.  This shows that #$residesInRegion's first argument-place is denotationally transparent. On the other hand, if Caesar were seeking #$Cicero and found him then (<code>#$objectFound-Definite CaesarsSearchForCicero Caesar #$Cicero)</code> would be true; but <code>(#$objectFound-Definite CaesarsSearchForCicero Caesar #$Tully)</code> might nevertheless be false, because Caesar might not know that #$Tully is #$Cicero and thus might not realize that in finding #$Cicero he had found #$Tully.  Having such a realization is a necessary condition for #$objectFound-Definite's holding, which shows that this relation's third argument-place is denotationally opaque.  
<p>
According to one well-known semantics for denotational opacity (viz. #$GottlobFrege's), a term appearing in an opaque context (in most cases) denotes (not its ordinary denotatum, but) what is ordinarily its <i>intensional meaning</i> or <i>sense</i> (or <i>Sinn</i>, in Frege's native German).  
<p>
#$quotedArgument (q.v.) is a specialization of #$opaqueArgument, and a term appearing in a <i>quoted</i> context is interpreted as denoting <i>itself</i> (rather than its usual denotatum).")
(comment TaskFromBugReportFn "A function that takes an instance of #$BugReport and returns the task that solves the reported bug.  Note that #$TaskFromBugReportFn is an instance of #$PartialFunction, as not every bug report describes an actual bug, so there can be cases where no task can be derived from the contents of the report.")
(comment CBLAssignedTask "A specialization #$PurposefulAction that represents the collection of tasks assigned to #$CBLNodes within the running #$CycBehaviorEngine, and are #$performedBy-Uniquely #$Cyc.")
(comment CBLParameterValuesList "A specialization of #$List.  Each instance of #$CBLParameterValuesList is a finite sequence of #$Things whose types are subsumed by corresponding types in the list of formal parameters in a #$CycBehaviorLanguage #$CBLTaskMethod, #$CBLSensationMethod or #$CBLMessageMethod.")
(comment CBLParametersList "A specialization of #$List.  Each instance of #$CBLParameterValuesList is a finite sequence of formal #$CBLParameters for a #$CycBehaviorLanguage #$CBLTaskMethod, #$CBLSensationMethod or #$CBLMessageMethod.")
(comment CBLAssignedTaskFn "A unary function that returns a #$CBLAssignedTask collection for the given task identifier.")
(comment intelligenceOperativeForOrg "(#$intelligenceOperativeForOrg ORG SPY) holds just in case SPY is one of the intelligence operatives in ORG.  This is meant to indicate SPY's status as a covert operative for ORG.  Hence, someone who processes the information obtained is not necessarily an intelligence operative in this sense.")
(comment KillingANART "The collection of events in which an #$IntelligentAgent kills a Cyc constant.")
(comment argGenlsWRTSpec "An assertion of the form (#$argGenlsWRTSpec PRED N COLLECTION SPEC) means that relative to the #$ProgramSpecification  SPEC, the values for the Nth argument of the #$Predicate PRED to sub-collection of the #$Collection COLLECTION.")
(comment predHasInputArgsWRTSpec "An assertion of the form (#$predHasInputArgsWRTSpec PRED N SPEC) means that relative to the #$ProgramSpecification SPEC, the Nth argument of the #$Predicate PRED is considered an 'input' variable.")
(comment predHasOutputArgsWRTSpec "An assertion of the form (#$predHasOutputArgsWRTSpec PRED N SPEC) means that relative to the #$ProgramSpecification SPEC, the Nth argument of the #$Predicate PRED is considered an 'ouput' variable.")
(comment predHasRecallNumberWRTSpec "An assertion of the form (#$predHasRecallNumberWRTSpec PRED NUMBER SPEC) means that relative to the #$ProgramSpecification SPEC, the #$Predicate PRED has a recall number of NUMBER.  NOTE:  The second argument is constrained only to be an instance of #$MathematicalObject since it is possible for some systems to set this value to #$PlusInfinity.")
(comment VerificationOfTruth "A sub-collection of #$Verification.  This is the collection of events in which some agent gathers evidence in an attempt to establish the truth of some entity with propositional content.")
(comment TemplateBasedOntologicalEngineering "Ontological engineering that uses templates to rapidly create assertions that share many common structural features.")
(comment assertionUsedInProcessType "An assertion of the form (#$assertionUsedInProcessType ASSERTION TYPE) means that the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION was used in the performance of an instance of TYPE, some sub-collection of #$PurposefulAction.")
(comment assertionPassedEvaluationType "An assertion of the form (#$assertionPassedEvaluationType ASSERTION TYPE) means that the performance of an instance of TYPE, some sub-collection of #$VerificationOfTruth, was satisfied such that there is confirming evidence of the truth of the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION.")
(comment assertionFailedEvaluationType "An assertion of the form (#$assertionFailedEvaluationType ASSERTION TYPE) means that the performance of an instance of TYPE, some sub-collection of #$VerificationOfTruth, did not uncover evidence for the truth of the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION.")
(comment OperatingOnAnSOEComponent "A specialization of #$InteractingWithAnSOEComponent.  Each instance of #$OperatingOnAnSOEComponent is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to alter the properties (or destroy) a component (i.e., a node or a link) of a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment InteractingWithAnSOEComponent "A specialization of #$InteractingWithAnSOEComponent.  Each instance of #$OperatingOnAnSOEComponent is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to interact with one or more components (i.e., nodes or a links) of a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment EditingACycKB "A specialization of #$EditingAnElectronicDocument.  Each instance of #$EditingACycKB is an event in which an agent alters the content of a Cyc KB by adding assertions, removing assertions, etc.")
(comment RemovingACycLTermFromTheKB "A specialization of #$EditingACycKB.  Each instance of #$RemovingACycLTermFromTheKB is an event in which an #$IntelligentAgent kills a CycL term while editing a CycKB.")
(comment arcCorrespondsToSentence "<code>(#$arcCorrespondsToSentence ARC SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>ARC</code> corresponds to <code>SENTENCE</code>, in that <code>ARC</code> has a certain relation <code>RELN</code> as its semantics, and <code>ARC</code> is a directional link between a source node whose semantics is <code>SEM-NODE1</code> and a destination node whose semantics is <code>SEM-NODE2</code> such that <code>(RELN NODE1 NODE2)</code> holds.")
(comment MeasuringFn "A unary #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes a #$MeasurableScalarIntervalType and returns a specialization of #$MeasuringSomething.  (#$MeasuringFn INTERVAL-TYPE) is the collection of all events in which an instance of INTERVAL-TYPE is measured.  For example, (#$MeasuringFn #$Speed) is the collection of events in which a speed is measured.")
(comment MachineLearning "A collection of events in which a program is running and it could develop new information (in some representational form) based on existing information. This collection is neutral on the success of the process.  Thus, if it may not generate any new information given a particular set of initial data.")
(comment MachineRuleInduction "A sub-collection of #$MachineLearning in which a particular program is trying to develop #$implies rules based on some body of knowledge.")
(comment languageHasRootLexicon "(#$languageHasRootLexicon LANG MT) means that MT is the most general #$LexicalMicrotheory which is specific to the #$NaturalLanguage, LANG.")
(comment ChemicalCompositionIBTFn "#$ChemicalCompositionIBTFn takes as argument any instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType and returns the collection of all #$InformationBearingObjects, such as copies of diagrams and formulas, containing information about the chemical structure of that compound type. For example, (#$ChemicalCompositionIBTFn #$Caffeine) returns the collection of all IBOs presenting diagrams or formulas for the chemical structure of caffeine.")
(comment RequirementsForCertificateFn "#$RequirementsForCertificateFn takes as argument any spec of #$Certificate-IBT and returns the collection of all requirements (instances of #$NeedMicrotheory) which must be met (made true) before a certificate of that kind will be issued.  For example, (#$RequirementsForCertificateFn #$Passport) returns the collection of requirements one must meet before one can be issued a passport.")
(comment DeletingAnSOENodeInGraphFn "(#$DeletingAnSOENodeInGraphFn NODE GRAPH) denotes the collection of events in which a the SOE focuses on the #$GLFNode NODE in the #$GLFGraph GRAPH.")
(comment CBLUnassertFn "A binary function that returns a #$CBLUnassert command and which is composed of the #$CBLMethod and the lexical command sequence number.")
(comment cblNodeDefinitionDate "(cblNodeDefinitionDate NODE-DEFINITION-MT DATE) means that NODE-DEFINITION-MT was last updated at DATE.")
(comment FocusingSOEDisplayOnAnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$FocusingSOEDisplayOnAnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool to make a non-focal node focal in a graph displayed by #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool.")
(comment FocusingSOEDisplayOnSOENodeInGraphFn "(#$FocusingSOEDisplayOnSOENodeInGraphFn NODE GRAPH) denoted the colection of events in which a the SOE focuses on the #$GLFNode NODE in the #$GLFGraph GRAPH.")
(comment AscertainingPermissibleOperationsOnSOENode "A specialization of #$OperatingOnAnSOENode.  Each instance of #$AscertainingPermissibleOperationsOnSOENode is an event in which a user uses #$TheSimpleOntologyEditorTool (SOE) to make determine what sorts of further actions can be performed with the SOE on a certain node in a graph displayed by SOE.")
(comment AscertainingPermissibleOperationsOnSOENodeInGraphFn "(#$AscertainingPermissibleOperationsOnSOENodeInGraphFn NODE GRAPH) denotes the collection of actions in which #$AscertainingPermissibleOperationsOnSOENode is performed on NODE in GRAPH.")
(comment TheFocalNodeInSOEGraph "An instance of #$GLFNode and #$IndexicalConcept.  This is the node that is focal in an SOE graph.  To query for the dispayable structure of a graph where this node is focal, ask #$SOE-WhatIsTheDisplayableGraphGivenCurrentFocalNode.")
(comment QuerySentenceOnlyTestVersionFn "A unary function that takes a fully-specified KB content test (see #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified) to the sentence-only-specified test that is a generalization of it (see #$genlKBContentTests).  (#$QuerySentenceOnlyTestVersionFn TEST) is the #$KBContentTest-QuerySentenceOnly (q.v.) that has the same #$CycLSentence-Askable that TEST has as the value of its #$InferenceSentenceParameter (see #$softwareParameterValueInSpecification), but which has no specified values for any other #$InferenceParameters. 
<p>
#$QuerySentenceOnlyTestVersionFn thus maps different instances of #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified that specify the same query-sentence to the same instance of #$KBContentTest-QuerySentenceOnly.
<p>
See also #$QueryContentOnlyTestVersionFn.")
(comment TheNodeOperatedOnInAnSOEGraph "An instance of #$GLFNode and #$IndexicalConcept.  This is the node that is currently operated on in an SOE graph.")
(comment facets-NearStrict "A #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections and a specialization of #$facets-Generic (q.v.).  (#$facets-NearStrict COL COLTYPE) means that COLTYPE corresponds to one (non-arbitrary) way of dividing (at least some of) COL into disjoint (or \"mostly\" disjoint) subcollections.  The instances of COLTYPE are all \"the same sort\" of subcollection of COL.  For example, #$PersonTypeByOccupation is a near-strict (but not strict) faceting of #$Person: while it is certainly possible for a person to have multiple occupations, it is expected that <i>most</i> people will have no more than one occupation (at a given time).")
(comment sOEArcTypeCorrespondingPredicate "(#$sOEArcTypeCorrespondingPredicate ARC-TYPE PRED) means that PRED is the predicate that corresponds to the SOE arc type, ARC-TYPE.  For example, it is true that (#$sOEArcTypeCorrespondingPredicate #$SOESpecArc (#$InverseBinaryPredicateFn #$genls)).")
(comment LinkagesMtSpindle "An instance of #$MicrotheorySpindle that contains the various #$LinkParserLinkages of #$NLSentences.")
(comment NthLinkParserLinkageFn "An expression of the form (NthLinkParserLinkageFn SENTENCE N) denotes an instance of #$LinkParserLinkage.  Specifically, it represents the (n+1)-th output of the Link Parser with SENTENCE as the input (so for the first parsed output, N = 0).")
(comment ContentMtOfLinkageFn "An expression of the form (ContentMtOfLinkageFn LINKAGE) denotes an instance of Microtheory. Specifically, the content represented by the assertions in the denoted microtheory is the interpretation of at least part of the #$LinkParserLinkage LINKAGE.")
(comment LinkParserLinkage "A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure and #$LinguisticObject.  Each #$LinkParserLinkage is the output of the Link Parser for a particular natural language sentence or a part of it.  There can be more than one instances of #$LinkParserLinkage for the same sentence.  It is a combination of relationships (represented by links) between words of the sentence.")
(comment predicateUnion "A ternary #$MetaPredicate that relates two predicates to the predicate that is by definition their <i>union</i> or <i>disjunction</i>, which holds whenever either of the first two predicates hold.  <code>(#$predicateUnion UNIONPRED PRED1 PRED2)</code> means that, for any sequence  <code>ARGS</code> and any context <code>MT</code>, <code>(UNIONPRED . ARGS)</code> holds in <code>MT</code> if and only if either <code>(PRED1 . ARGS)</code> or <code>(PRED2 . ARGS)</code> holds in <code>MT</code>.  <code>UNIONPRED</code> is thus  a generalization (via #$genlPreds) of both <code>PRED1</code> and <code>PRED1</code>; indeed  <code>UNIONPRED</code> is a <i>nearest possible common generalization</i> of the other two predicates.
<p>
For example, this holds:
<pre>
  (#$predicateUnion #$biologicalOffspring #$biologicalSons #$biologicalDaughters)
</pre>
If either <code>PRED1</code> or <code>PRED2</code> is of fixed arity <code>N</code>, then the other must either be of arity <code>N</code> or be variable-arity, and <code>UNIONPRED</code> is itself of arity <code>N</code>.  If both <code>PRED1</code> and <code>PRED2</code> are variable-arity, then so is <code>UNIONPRED</code>.
<p>
See also the corresponding function #$PredicateUnionFn; and see #$predicateIntersection and #$predicateIsBinaryCompositionOf.")
(comment CommutativeRelation "An instance of #$RelationTypeByLogicalFeature (q.v.) and a specialization of #$AtLeastPartiallyCommutativeRelation (q.v.).  Each instance of #$CommutativeRelation <code>COMRELN</code> is a predicate or function that is commutative in all of its argument-places.  That is, if <code>COMRELN</code> is a predicate (function) that holds among (has a value <code>VAL</code> for) a given sequence of arguments, then <code>COMRELN</code> also holds among (has the same value <code>VAL</code> for) any permutation of that  sequence.  
<p>
Examples of commutative relations include #$PlusFn, #$or, #$bordersOn, #$temporallyIntersects, and #$teammates.  Specialization include #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate.  
<p>
Note that most relations are <i>not</i> commutative.  Cf. the disjoint collection  #$PartiallyCommutativeRelation.")
(disjointWith TranscendentalNumber AlgebraicNumber)
(comment CommunicatingByMeansOfFn "#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn is an instance of #$Function-Denotational that can be used to denote the collection of all instances #$Communicating in which the #$senderOfInfo uses some well-defined subcollection of #$Artifact-Communication.  
<p>
<code>(#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn DEVICE)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$CommunicatingUsingADevice where the #$meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact is some instance of <code>DEVICE</code>, where <code>DEVICE</code> is a specialization of #$Artifact-Communication.")
(comment ThingDescribableAsFn "(#$ThingDescribableAsFn WORD POS) denotes the collection of things which may be in some way be described by the adjectival form of WORD with speeech part POS (where POS is restricted to be some spec of #$Adjective). So, for example, (#$ThingDescribableAsFn #$Editorial-TheWord #$Adjective) denotes the collection of things which may be described as \"editorial\" in some sense.")
(comment infoTransferred-NLString "A specialization of #$transferredAIS (q.v.).  <code>(#$infoTransferred-NLString ITE STRING)</code> means that (i) <code>STRING</code> is a character-string transferred as information in the information-transfer event <code>ITE</code>, (ii) <code>STRING</code> is a meaningful expression of some natural language <code>NL</code>, and (iii) the #$Information-Content <code>CONTENT</code> expressed by <code>STRING</code> with respect to <code>NL</code> (in the context of <code>ITE</code>) is itself information transferred (see #$infoTransferred) in <code>ITE</code>.  
<p>
For example, 

<pre>
  (#$infoTransferred-NLString 
    FDRsFirstInauguralAddress
    \"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself.\")
</pre>
<p>
means that in FDR's first Inaugural Address both the English sentence \"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself\" and the proposition that the only thing we have to fear is fear itself were transferred as information.")
(comment studyOf "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a #$Thing to a specialization of #$Studying.  (#$studyOf THING EVENT-TYPE) means that EVENT-TYPE is collection of all events in which THING (or, if THING is a #$Collection, instances of THING) is/are studied.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$StudyOfFn (q.v.).")
(comment AssigningATask "A specialization of Ordering-CommunicationAct.  Each instance of this collection is an event in which a particular assignment (an instance of #$Assignment-Specification (q.v.)) is assigned to a particular agent or agents.")
(comment StuffFn "(#$StuffFn OBJECT-TYPE) takes an object type as an argument, and returns a \"stuff-like\" version of that object type. (#$StuffFn OBJECT-TYPE) represents a physical portion of a separable, countable object, which is still the same substance, but no longer separable or countable in the same way. For example, a #$Cake is a separable object, but a (#$StuffFn #$Cake) is a non-whole portion of a #$Cake.")
(comment stuffTypeOfObjectType "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot and specialization of #$genls that relates an #$ExistingObjectType to its corresponding #$ExistingStuffType.  (#$stuffTypeOfObjectType OBJECT-TYPE STUFF-TYPE) means that STUFF-TYPE is the \"stuff-like\" version of OBJECT-TYPE.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$StuffFn (q.v.).")
(comment mobTypeOfObjectType "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a specialization of #$Mob to a specialization of #$TemporalThing.  (#$mobTypeOfObjectType MOB-TYPE OBJ-TYPE) means that MOB-TYPE is the collection of all #$Mobs of instances of OBJ-TYPE.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$MobFn (q.v.).")
(comment Specification "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork. Each instance of #$Specification is an abstract work that constitutes a description of the properties of a #$Situation or a #$SomethingExisting, and sometimes even entire collections of such things.  Things are made, bought, and searched for according to specifications, which can be instantiated as printed instructions or as diagrams.  This collection is modally neutral with regard to the descriptive character of its instances. Thus, it includes descriptions of how things are, were, should be, must be, <i>etc</i>.")
(comment Criterion "Each instance of #$Criterion is an action-guiding #$DevisedPracticeOrWork, where the guidance is normative in some sense.  There are two major aspects to this.  First, the instance could represent how something is supposed to be.  These instances belong to the sub-collection #$NormativeSpecification, which is a description of what the properties of some action or entity should be. The second sense, captured by the sub-collection #$EvaluativeCriterion, dictates how to rate the worth or quality of entities.  Overall, instances of #$Criterion inform an agent of how to perform an action, either by directly prescribing the action or its products or by contributing information for an evaluatory action.")
(comment ActionTypeOfAssignmentFn "(#$ActionTypeOfAssignmentFn SPECIFICATION) denotes the collection of purposeful actions (<i>i.e.</i>, the specialization of #$PurposefulAction), instances of which SPECIFICATION specifies should be perfomed.")
(comment unassertForOpenCycBuild "A unary #$MetaKnowledgePredicate.  (#$unassertForOpenCycBuild ASSERTION) means that ASSERTION should be unasserted before compiling an OpenCyc build.")
(comment AssignmentOfTaskFn "A #$UnaryFunction and #$IndividualDenotingFunction, #$AssignmentOfTaskFn is used to convert between two ontologies for the representation of what can alternatively be called 'tasks' and 'assignments'.  This function converts from a task (which is a sub-collection of #$PurposefulAction) to an instance of #$Assignment-Specification.")
(comment CDASubStringAtOffsetWithLengthFn "An expression of the form (#$CDASubStringAtOffsetWithLengthFn FILE STRING START-INDEX LENGTH) denotes a 'relativized' #$SubLString within the #$ComputerFile-Abstract FILE that begins with the offset represented by the #$Integer START-INDEX, has length LENGTH and contains the words of STRING within it.")
(comment DonorFn-Agent "#$DonorFn-Agent takes as argument any instance AGENT of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of all #$LegalAgents who donate money, goods, or services to AGENT. These donations are typically #$CharitableDonations intended to benefit the AGENT who receives them. For example, (#$DonorFn-Agent #$CornellUniversity) denotes the collection of all #$LegalAgents who donate money, good, or services to #$CornellUniversity. If the money, goods, or services are donated as part of a marketing strategy designed to benefit the donating agent, then the donating agent will be an instance of (#$SponsorFn-Agent AGENT) not (#$DonorFn-Agent AGENT).")
(comment OwnerFn-Individual "#$OwnerFn-Individual takes as argument any instance of #$SomethingExisting and returns the collection of instances of #$Agent-Generic owning (having user rights for), in part or entirely, that thing.  For example, (#$OwnerFn-Individual #$NewEnglandPatriots) returns the collection of agents holding part or whole ownership of the Patriots #$FootballTeam.) .")
(comment woodTypeOfPlantType "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a specialization of #$Plant-Woody to the collection of all instances of #$Wood that are derived from that type of plant.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$WoodFn (q.v.).")
(comment pairTypeOfObjectType "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates an #$ObjectType to the collection of all pairs (cf. #$PairOfObjects) of instances of that type.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$PairFn (q.v.).")
(comment protectingTypeOfIndividualType "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a #$FirstOrderCollection COL to the collection of all instances of #$ProtectingSomething in which an instance of COL is protected.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$ProtectingFn (q.v.).")
(comment ExcrementFn "(#$ExcrementFn ORGANISMTYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$ExcretionSubstance deriving from some instance of ORGANISMTYPE.  E.g., (#$ExcrementFn #$Dog) denotes the collection of all instances of dog excrement.")
(comment subFieldsAppliedTo "This relation is the predicate corresponding to
#$FieldAppliedToFn. Specifically, (#$subFieldsAppliedTo FIELD SUBFIELD
TOPIC) means that SUBFIELD is the #$subFields of FIELD which is
devoted to the study of TOPIC.")
(comment ReflexiveBinaryPredicate "The specialization of #$BinaryPredicate whose instances are reflexive relations.  A reflexive binary predicate relates anything that meets the predicate's argument constraints to that thing itself.  Typically, a reflexive predicate has precisely the same constraints on both of its argument-places.
<p>
More precisely: a binary predicate <code>PRED</code> is an instance of #$ReflexiveBinaryPredicate if and only if both (i) for every <code>X</code> that satisfies the constraints on (i.e is an #$admittedArgument for) <i>both</i> argument-places of <code>PRED</code>, <code>(PRED X X)</code> holds and (ii) <code>PRED</code>'s two argument-places are \"co-satisfiable\" with respect to their (single-argument) type constraints (see #$cosatisfiableInArgs and #$NoteOnArgumentCosatisfiabilityRequirement).
<p>
Instances of #$ReflexiveBinaryPredicate include #$physicalParts, #$inRegion, #$genls, and #$equals.")
(comment Only-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances of the form 'only XXX.'")
(comment TheMySentientSystemHost "#$TheHost denotes the current owner/licensee of an individual, running Cyc image that is itself running an instance of the #$MySentientProgram in a production environment. If, for example, COMPANY were to install an image containing the #$MySentientProgram and make it available to their customers, COMPANY would be the #$TheMySentientSystemHost. See also #$MySentientSystemUser.")
(comment termFormulas "A non-assertible #$MetaLanguagePredicate that relates CycL terms to CycL formulas in which they occur.  <code>(#$termFormulas TERM FORMULA)</code> means that <code>TERM</code> occurs as a constituent term in <code>FORMULA</code>.  
<p>
Note that both argument-places of #$termFormulas are implicitly \"quoted\" (see #$quotedArgument). So if the above #$termFormulas sentence is closed (i.e. is a #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence), the CycL expressions it mentions, <code>TERM</code> and <code>FORMULA</code>, actually <i>appear in</i> that sentence -- as names of themselves.  Thus, the sentence 

<pre>  (#$termFormulas #$France (#$bordersOn #$France #$Germany))</pre> 

is true, due to the manifest fact that the term <code>#$France</code> occurs in the sentence <code>(#$bordersOn #$France #$Germany)</code>. 
<p>
Note that <code>FORMULA</code> in the above need not be true (if it's a sentence) or even semantically well-formed.  Note also that, since #$CycLFormula is a specialization of #$CycLTerm, the #$termFormulas relation is reflexive: it holds (trivially) between any CycL formula and itself (see #$ReflexiveBinaryPredicate).
<p>
See also #$assertedTermSentences.")
(comment timeConstraintOfAssignment "(#$timeConstraintOfAssignment ASSIGNMENT TIME) says that the total time constraint for any action that fulfills ASSIGNMENT is TIME.  This predicate is useful for expressing time constraints for tasks or operations, where the task or operation must be completed within a certain amount of time.")
(comment actIsAttemptToFulfillAssignment "(#$actIsAttemptToFulfillAssignment ACT ASSIGNMENT) says that ACT is a performance of a purposeful action that is an attempt to fulfill ASSIGNMENT (an instance of #$Assignment-Specification (q.v.)).")
(comment Allotment "A specialization of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification and #$Assignment-Obligation, the #$FirstOrderCollection #$Allotment refers to the authorized designation of some #$Quantity (of time, money, a material) to bringing about the realization of some #$NormativeSpecification.  This is a very general collection aimed at representing the reservation of some resource. Contrast with #$ResourceRequest, which only indicates a reservation that has been proposed and not approved by the relevant authority.")
(comment TotalAllotmentForFn "An expression of the form (#$TotalAllotmentForFn PURPOSE) is used to denote the instance of #$Allotment that represents the totality of resources that are being dedicated to the #$NormativeSpecification PURPOSE. Its corresponding predicate is #$hasTotalAllotment.")
(comment normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd "The predicate #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd is used for partially specifying the satisfaction conditions for an instance of #$NormativeSpecification  Specifically, it associates an instance of #$NormativeSpecification SPEC with a #$BinaryRolePredicate ROLE and an instance of #$SomethingExisting THING, to state the part of satisfying SPEC involves a situation in which THING fills ROLE.  This predicate works in conjunction with #$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType.  In short, given assertions of the form (#$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType SPEC SIT-TYPE) and (#$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd SPEC ROLE IND), then the satisfaction of SPEC will involve an instance of SIT-TYPE, SIT, such that the assertion (ROLE SIT IND) is true.  This predicate only provides a partial specification because any number of assertions using it or the predicate #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForType can be used with #$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType to represent what needs to be done to satisfy SPEC.  See also #$completeSpecification for more information on constructing rules using these predicates.")
(comment performerInSpec "(#$performerInSpec SPEC AGT) says that part of satisfying SPEC involves an event in which AGT is an #$IntelligentAgent that plays the role #$performedBy.")
(comment assignedOnDate "(#$assignedOnDate TASK DATE) means TASK is assigned on DATE.")
(comment DBSaturationQueryProfilingTest-operatesInRegion1 "#$DBSaturationQueryProfilingTest-operatesInRegion1 is a
collection of three #$ALI_BABAContentTests which profile the
increasing complexity and performance degradation which occurs when
additional #$isa literals are added to the antecedent of the DB Saturation use case #$LDSC-SAICRule-OperatesInRegion.")
(comment objectiveOfTask "(#$objectiveOfTask TASK OBJECTIVE) says that OBJECTIVE has the status of 'task objective' in the planned execution of TASK.  A task objective may be an instance of #$GeographicalRegion, #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable, or #$Artifact, and it may be possible for other kinds of things to play this role as well.")
(comment expectedStartingPoint "This predicate relates a task to the point in time at which it is expected to begin (to be instantiated).  Thus (#$expectedStartingPoint TASK POINT) means that (#$expected-ToBe (#$startingPoint INS POINT)), where INS is any action that is an attempt to fulfill TASK.")
(comment assignmentDeadline "A #$TemporalPredicate and a specialization of #$endingDate that applies to the time-intervals specified in #$Assignment-Specification (see #$assignmentPeriod).  (#$assignmentDeadline ASSIGN DATE) means that the #$Assignment-Specification ASSIGN can be fulfilled no later than the ending of the #$Date DATE.   The end point of DATE is equivalent to the endpoint of the #$assignmentPeriod of ASSIGN.
<p>
Note that not all assignments have deadlines; some are assigned without a deadline specified.  By default, the #$assignmentPeriod of such a predicate is viewed as continuing indefinitely.")
(comment uninterestingForArgTypeInReln "(#$uninterestingForArgTypeInReln TYPE RELATION NUMBER) says that for any instance INS of TYPE and any formula FORMULA of the form (RELATION ... INS ...) where INS appears in the NUMBERth argument place of FORMULA, FORMULA is uninteresting.  See also #$uninterestingForArgInReln.")
(disjointWith DeadAnimal (GroupFn Animal))
(comment LinkParserLinkPredicate "The collection of predicates that denote the relation between instances of #$CycParsingToken as defined by the links of a particular #$LinkParserLinkage.")
(comment InternalSensoryQuantity "A specialization of #$SensoryQuantity.  Each instance of #$InternalSensoryQuantity is a state of a sentient being in which it experiences within itself some level of somatic or psycho-somatic feeling, urge, or impulse.  An internal sensory attribute differs from an `external' one in that the sensing being refers the former to itself and the latter to external objects.  #$InternalSensoryQuantity includes states of feeling thirsty, tired, or in pain, as well as various bodily urges such as the urge to sneeze, burp, or urinate.  Sensory attributes that may occur with more or less intensity are represented by indicating a #$LevelOfPain, #$LevelOfPhysicalPleasure, #$LevelOfStress, and so on.")
(comment VisualSensoryQuantity "A specialization of #$SensoryQuantity. Each instance of #$VisualSensoryQuantity is a sensory quality that can characterize a visual experience.  For example, it might be the subjective impression of a particular shade of blue (see #$ColorSensoryPerception), a certain level of perceived brightness, or a particular subjectively-experienced shape.  In short, a #$VisualSensoryQuantity is any property that can characterize \"how a thing looks\" to the experiencing subject.
<p>
Although typically used to describe experiences involved in #$VisualPerception, note that instances of #$VisualSensoryQuantity are also manifested in dreams and (visual) hallucinations.  And some synesthetics experience visual sensory quantities when presented with stimili not usually related to visual experience (e.g. sounds).")
(comment ColorSensoryQuantity "A specialization of #$VisualSensoryQuantity (q.v.). Instances of #$ColorSensoryQuantity are sensory qualities that characterize visual experience in term of the colors perceived.  For example, the subjective impression of a particular shade of blue is a color sensory quantity.
<p>
If an object that is in fact blue looks (say) purple to me, then my concurrent visual experience displays the #$ColorSensoryQuantity normally associated only with experiences purple objects.")
(comment PicturesFn-Organization "#$PicturesFn-Organization takes instances of #$Organization and returns the collection of all #$VisualInformationBearingThings depicting instances of that #$Organization. For example (#$PicturesFn-Organization #$France) denotes the collection of all pictures of France. For purposes of the #$WebSearchEnhancementProject, the specs of #$Organization that this SubTopicFunction applies to will be limited to those that might be of interest to users of the E-Cyc application.")
(comment resourceAllocationSpecificationOfTask "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$AllotmentOfTaskFn.")
(comment AllotmentOfTaskFn "A #$UnaryFunction and #$IndividualDenotingFunction, #$AllotmentOfTaskFn is used to convert  tasks (sub-collections of #$PurposefulAction) to instances of #$Allotment.")
(comment allocatedObjects "An assertion of the form (#$allocatedObjects ALLOCATION THING) relates an instance of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  Instances of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification represent a reservation (either actual or proposed) on some resource. Such an assertion means that THING is the thing that is reserved in ALLOCATION.")
(comment allottedAgents "A specialization of #$obligatedAgents, #$agreeingAgents and #$specifiedActors (qq.v.) that relates an #$Allotment (q.v.) to the agent(s) to whom it is assigned.  <code>(#$allottedAgents ALLOTMENT AGENT))</code> means that <code>ALLOTMENT</code> is assigned to <code>AGENT</code>.  Depending on the nature of <code>ALLOTMENT</code> (and the actions, or inaction, of <code>AGENT</code> with respect to <code>ALLOTMENT</code>), the assignment might last for a few seconds or for a few years.
<p>
See also #$assigner.")
(comment assigner "A specialization of #$obligationOwedTo and #$agreeingAgents (qq.v.) that relates an #$Assignment-Specification (q.v.) to the agent who assigned it.  (#$assigner TASK ASSIGNER) means that TASK has been assigned to some agent(s) (see #$allottedAgents) by ASSIGNER.
<p>
Note that my informing you that you have a certain assignment does not necessarily make me the #$assigner of that task; for I might be acting on behalf of another agent (e.g. my supervisor or the organization you and I both work for) who is the actual assigner.")
(comment assignmentInfoCutoffDate "(#$assignmentInfoCutoffDate ASSIGN DATE) means that after DATE, no new information gathered will be included in the final product to be delivered at the end of ASSIGNMENT.")
(comment subAssignments "A binary #$NonPhysicalPartPredicate that applies to #$Assignment-Specifications (q.v.).  (#$subAssignments SUPER SUB) means that SUPER has SUB as one of its subordinate tasks.  This implies that (i) the fulfillment of SUPER (see #$actionFulfillsAssignment) depends in part upon the fulfillment of SUB, (ii) each of the #$allottedAgents of SUB must either be an assignee of SUPER or one of the #$groupMembers of (a #$MultiIndividualAgent that is) an assignee of SUPER, and (iii) the #$assignmentDeadline of SUB (if any) cannot be later than that of SUPER.
<p>
The vocabulary for specifying how to satisfy an #$Assignment-Specification is quite flexible on the issue of representing complex assignments.  Specifically, one could break a single assignment down into multiple assignments and relate them using the #$subAssignments vocabulary.  Alternatively, one could have a single #$Assignment-Specification which bears the #$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType to a novel type of #$Situation, where that novel type has a complex sub-event structure.")
(disjointWith ToxicSubstance (FoodOrDrinkForFn HomoSapiens))
(comment versionOfSoftwareDenotedBy "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$SoftwareVersionFn.")
(comment meetsPragmaticRequirement "A #$MetaKnowledgePredicate that is used to express that a pragmatic precondition on a given rule is satisfied.  The predicate takes as arguments a list of CycL variables and an asserted rule (see #$CycLRuleAssertion) in which those variables occur \"free\".  At the EL (\"epistemological level\"), #$meetsPragmaticRequirement sentences are not asserted as GAFs, but appear instead as the consequents of system-generated #$implies rules.  For a given sequence of values for the respective variables <code>VAR1</code>, ..., <code>VARn</code>, <code>(#$meetsPragmaticRequirement (#$TheList VAR1 ... VARn) RULE)</code> means that some pragmatic precondition placed on <code>RULE</code>'s being used by the Cyc inference engine (see #$pragmaticRequirement) is satisfied with respect to those values.
<p>
Let's make this more precise and explicit.  A pragmatic precondition for a rule is written like so:
<p>
<pre>
   (#$pragmaticRequirement CONDITION RULE)
</pre>
<p>
and gets canonicalized into a rule involving #$meetsPragmaticRequirement like so:
<p>
<pre>
   (#$implies
     CONDITION
    (#$meetsPragmaticRequirement (#$TheList VAR1 ... VARn) RULE)),
</pre>
<p>
where <code>VAR1, ..., VARn</code> are all and only the variables that occur free in <code>RULE</code> and thus include all (and possibly only) the variables that occur free in <code>CONDITION</code> (i.e. as <code>RULE</code> and <code>CONDITION</code> explicitly appear in the KB browser, without consideration of their having \"implicit\" initial universal quantifiers).
<p>
The above #$meetsPragmaticRequirement rule is used in inference similarly to an #$abnormal rule.  If <code>CONDITION</code> is not known to hold for a given sequence of values <code><VAL1, ..., VALn></code> for its variables <code><VAR1, ..., VARn></code>, then those values do not \"meet the pragmatic requirement\" for <code>RULE</code>; and hence inference will not proceed using <code><VAL1, ..., VALn></code> with <code>RULE</code>.
<p>
The effect of the foregoing is that any asserted rule <code>RULE</code> is implicitly treated by the Cyc inference engine as if it had the form
<p>
<pre>
 (#$implies
  (#$meetsPragmaticRequirement (#$TheList VAR1 ... VARn) RULE)
   RULE)
</pre>
<p>
(with <code>VAR1, ..., VARn</code> as described above).
<p>
This convention allows the logical content of a rule to be expressed independently of any pragmatic preconditions for its being used in inference.  If a rule has multiple pragmatic requirements, it must meet all of them to be used in inference.
<p>
Also see #$abnormal, which is syntactically similar and has a related  interpretation.")
(comment FullTextOfPCWFn "#$FullTextOfPCWFn takes as argument any #$PropositionalConceptualWork and returns the collection of #$PropositionalCWTexts that contain a full written text of that PCW.  For example, (#$FullTextOfPCWFn #$MobyDickNovel) returns the collection of full texts of Moby Dick (including texts in different languages), and (#$FullTextOfPCWFn RimeOfTheAncientMariner) would return the full texts of this particular poem.")
(comment HoldingHostage "The collection of events in which one or more persons are held hostage.  Each instance of #$HoldingHostages is preceeded by an instance of #$TakingHostage.  Usually, the #$TakingHostage and #$HoldingHostages events are subevents of a more general event (e.g. a bank robbery or a kidnapping) .  During the #$HoldingHostages event, the hostages are in the control of the perpetrators of the event.")
(comment HeldHostageFn "This function takes an instance of #$HoldingHostages and an instance of #$Animal and returns the instance of #$HeldCaptive where that instance is a subevent of the #$HoldingHostages event and the instance of #$Animal is a #$captive in the #$HeldCaptive event.  Note that this is a partial function.  There will only be a value for the pair <HOLDING ANIMAL> when ANIMAL is a #$hostages in HOLDING.")
(comment captivityCorrespondsToHostageTaking "This predicate relates an instance of #$HoldingHostages, HOLD, and an instance of #$Animal, HOSTAGE, to the instance of #$HeldCaptive, CAP, where the following conditions hold:<br><br>

<pre>
   1. (#$hostages HOLD HOSTAGE) 
   2. (#$subEvents HOLD CAP)
   3. (#$captive CAP HOSTAGE)</pre><br><br>

If the above conditions do not hold the function is undefined for that argument pair.  Note: this predicate is the corresponding predicate to #$HeldHostageFn



.")
(comment parseTermForPeg "(#$parseTermForPeg PEG TERM) means that utterance associated with the #$LingisticExpressionPeg PEG was initially parsed to TERM. Because it only reflects the initial parser output, TERM may not reflect the intended content of PEG (e.g., it may be an #$NLTaggedTerm or other i-cycl expression).")
(disjointWith LandBody Promontory)
(comment PhysicalSchema "A specialization of #$Schema-LogicalOrPhysical.  Each instance of #$PhysicalSchema is a schema that models the data types that are admissible in the fields of a knowledge source. Each #$PhysicalSchema is derived from at least one knowledge source (see #$physicalSchemaSourceMap).  Also, each #$PhysicalSchema will have a number of physical fields which corresponds to the columns found in a physical table (see #$physicalFields).  For example, the OFAC database contains three physical tables, which are represented as three #$PhysicalSchemas: #$OFAC-add-PS, #$OFAC-alt-PS, and #$OFAC-main-PS.  See also #$LogicalSchema.")
(comment LogicalSchema "A specialization of #$Schema-LogicalOrPhysical.  Each instance of #$LogicalSchema is a schema that models the logical structure of a source's information content, as well as the CycL \"meaning sentences\" which describe the semantic content of the source.  Each #$LogicalSchema is mapped to some physical schema (see #$logicalPhysicalSchemaMap and #$PhysicalSchema).  Also, each #$LogicalSchema will have a number of logical fields (#$logicalFields) and meaning sentences (#$meaningSentenceOfSchema).")
(comment Schema-LogicalOrPhysical "A specialization of #$CWInfoStructure (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Schema-LogicalOrPhysical is a schema that imposes some structure on the content of knowledge sources.  Its two disjoint specializations are #$LogicalSchema and #$PhysicalSchema (qq.v.).")
(comment StructuredKnowledgeSource-Complex "A specialization of #$StructuredKnowledgeSource (q.v.).  Each instance of #$StructuredKnowledgeSource-Complex isa  a knowledge source that is composed of two or more subordinate knowledge sources.  For example, a database that contains two or more tables is such a knowledge source.  The individual database tables are the atomic components of the database.  For the concept of atomic knowledge sources, see #$StructuredKnowledgeSource-Atomic.")
(comment StructuredKnowledgeSource-Atomic "A specialization of #$StructuredKnowledgeSource.  Each instance of #$StructuredKnowledgeSource-Atomic isa a knowledge sources that cannot be further subdivided into two or more
parts.  For example, a database table is such a knowledge source.  contrast this collection with #$StructuredKnowledgeSource-Complex.")
(comment StructuredKnowledgeSource "A specialization of #$StructuredInformationSource (q.v.).  Each instance of #$StructuredKnowledgeSource is an electronic source of propositional information combined with a conceptual schema that describes its semantic content. Examples include databases, spreadsheets, queryable web pages, and XML or DAML tagged text.")
(comment sentenceImplies "A binary predicate that represents logical entailment in CycL.  <code>(#$sentenceImplies ANTECEDENT CONSEQUENT)</code> means that <code>CONSEQUENT</code> can be derived from <code>ANTECEDENT</code> using purely logical transformations.  For example, this holds by double negation:
<pre>
  (#$sentenceImplies
    (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle)
    (#$not (#$not (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle))) .
</pre>
Note that there are cases in which <code>(#$implies ANTECEDENT CONSEQUENT)</code> is analytically true, or necessarily true in some sense of necessity weaker than logical necessity, such that <code>(#$sentenceImplies ANTECEDENT CONSEQUENT)</code> is false.  For example, whereas:
<pre>
  (#$implies (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle) (#$isa #$Muffet #$Dog))
</pre>
is analytically true or in some sense necessarily true,
<pre>
  (#$sentenceImplies (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle) (#$isa #$Muffet #$Dog))
</pre>
is not true, since the material conditional is not logically valid.
<p>
#$sentenceImplies also differs from #$implies in that whereas #$implies is a #$LogicalConnective (q.v.), #$sentenceImplies is merely a predicate that holds between sentences.  #$sentenceImplies is primarily intended to be used for rules that quantify over CycL sentences.")
(comment SensorOntologyConstant "The collection of constants relating to Sensors and sense perception events.")
(comment argGenlsInputModeForDetermination "An assertion of the form (#$argGenlsInputModeForDetermination PRED N TYPE DET) means that relative to the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination DET, the  Nth argument of the #$Predicate PRED should be a sub-collection of the #$Collection TYPE and that argument position has a mode of an input variable.   The sense of mode here is derived from #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment programDenotesInputModeWith "An assertion of the form (#$programDenotesInputModeWith PROGRAM CHAR) means that the #$CharacterString is used by the #$ComputerProgram-CW for representing an input mode.  Typically, such programs will be written in #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment programDenotesOutputModeWith "An assertion of the form (#$programDenotesOutputModeWith PROGRAM CHAR) means that the #$CharacterString is used by the #$ComputerProgram-CW for representing an output mode.  Typically, such programs will be written in #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment programDenotesConstantModeWith "An assertion of the form (#$programDenotesConstantModeWith PROGRAM CHAR) means that the #$CharacterString is used by the #$ComputerProgram-CW for representing a constant mode.  Typically, such programs will be written in #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment editingTextActedOn "<code>(#$editingTextActedOn EDIT STRING)</code> means that in the #$EditingAnElectronicDocument <code>EDIT</code>, the #$CharacterString <code>STRING</code> is text that was copied, cut or pasted.")
(comment editingTextCopied "<code>(#$editingTextCopied EDIT STRING)</code> means that in the #$EditingAnElectronicDocument <code>EDIT</code>, the #$CharacterString <code>STRING</code> is text that was copied.")
(comment editingTextCut "<code>(#$editingTextCut EDIT STRING)</code> means that in the #$EditingAnElectronicDocument <code>EDIT</code>, the #$CharacterString <code>STRING</code> is text that is cut.")
(comment editingTextPasted "<code>(#$editingTextPasted EDIT STRING)</code> means that in the #$EditingAnElectronicDocument <code>EDIT</code>, the #$CharacterString <code>STRING</code> is text that was pasted.")
(comment GasField-Developed "The collection of regions which are naturally rich in deposits of natural gas and are developed to the point of producing natural gas commercially.  A developed gas field has production facilities on site, such as a gas well or some sort of recovery mechanism.  There will also be means for transporting the natural gas once it has been brought to the surface (by gas tanker or gas pipeline for example).")
(comment DataStream "A specialization of #$ProgramObject.  Each instance of #$DataStream is a stream of data. This includes all streams, including Input and Output streams, as well as Byte and Character streams, and more complex objects such as files.")
(comment PastingDataFromClipboard "A specialization of #$EditingAnElectronicDocument.  Each instance of #$PastingDataFromClipboard is an event in which data (usually text or an image file) is pasted from a \"clipboard\" application data repository to another document.")
(disjointWith CopyingOrCuttingDataToClipboard PastingDataFromClipboard)
(comment fileOperatedOnAtPathname "(#$fileOperatedOnAtPathname OPERATION PATH) means that in the #$FileOperation OPERATION, the file acted on is found at the #$Pathname PATH.")
(comment OpeningAFile "A specialization of #$AccessingAFile.  Each instance of #$OpeningAFile is an event in which a computer file is opened by another program, such as, for example, when Microsoft Word is used to open a \".doc\" file, or when an email client program is used to display an email.")
(comment AdvocacyOrganization "#$AdvocacyOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization (q.v.).  Each instance of #$AdvocacyOrganization is an #$Organization that lobbies or engages in activities with the purpose of advocating a particular position on social, economic, political, environmental matters.  Many instances of #$IdeologicalOrganization (q.v.) are also instances of #$AdvocacyOrganization, though not all advocacy organizations are ideological organizations, since ideological organizations are never motivated solely by self-interest.   Examples of #$AdvocacyOrganization include #$AmericanAssociationOfRetiredPersons, #$SierraClub, #$AmericanMedicalAssociation, and #$StateBarOfTexas.")
(comment CopyingOrCuttingDataToClipboard "A specialization of #$EditingAnElectronicDocument (q.v.).  Each instance of #$CopyingOrCuttingDataToClipboard is an event in which data (usually text or an image file) is copied from a source (usually an open electronic document) and saved to a \"clipboard\" application data repository, from which it can later be pasted elsewhere (<i>e.g.</i>, to another document).")
(comment PicturesFromEventFn "(#$PicturesFromEventFn EVENT) denotes the collection of all pictures that capture some sub-situation (c.f. #$subSituations) of the instance of #$Event, EVENT.  For example (#$PicturesFromEventFn #$WorldWarII) is the collection of all pictures that depict sub-situations of WWII.")
(comment pictureTypeFromEvent "(#$pictureTypeFromEvent PICTURE-TYPE EVENT) means that every picture (c.f., #$VisualInformationBearingThing) of type PICTURE-TYPE depicts some sub-situation (c.f., #$subSituations) of EVENT, an instance of #$Event-Localized.")
(comment PlayOpportunityFn "#$PlayOpportunityFn takes as argument any collection of games and returns the collection of all opportunities (situations in which normal barriers are absent or minimized) to play (perform an instantiation of) that game.  For example, (#$PlayOpportunityFn #$Baseball-TheGame) play a game of baseball.")
(comment sideEffectTypeOfUsingDrugType "(#$sideEffectTypeOfUsingDrugType COLLECTION DRUG-TYPE) identifies COLLECTION as the collection of side effects associated with the use of DRUG-TYPE, a specialization of #$DrugSubstance.")
(comment SideEffectsOfUsingDrugTypeFn "(#$SideEffectsOfUsingDrugTypeFn DRUG-TYPE) denotes the collection of side effects associated with the use of DRUG-TYPE.  Each instance of this collection is a specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition such that, for a user of DRUG-TYPE, there is a reasonable chance of that user developing a case of (playing the #$physiologicalConditionAffects role wrt an instance of) that condition.")
(comment fileCopyActedOn "An #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$FileOperation to a #$ComputerFileCopy.  <code>(#$fileCopyActedOn OPERATION COPY)
</code> means that <code>COPY</code> is accessed in <code>OPERATION</code>.")
(comment fileCopyAccessed "An #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$AccessingAFile to a #$ComputerFileCopy.  (#$fileCopyAccessed ACCESSING COPY) means that COPY is accessed in ACCESSING.")
(comment AgentNowTerminated "A specialization of #$Individual, and an instance of #$HistoricalCollection and #$PostExistenceCollection (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$AgentNowTerminated is an instance of #$Agent-Generic that has terminated. \"(#$isa AGT #$AgentNowTerminated)\" is true only after the ending point of AGT, when \"(#$isa AGT #$Agent-Generic)\" is no longer true.  Instances include defunct organizations and dead animals.")
(comment QueryContentOnlyTestVersionFn "A unary function that takes a given #$KBContentTest (q.v.) to the #$KBContentTest-QueryContentOnly (q.v.) that has the same question-content (see #$kbContentTestQuestion-Content).  <code>(#$QueryContentOnlyTestVersionFn TEST)</code> is the #$KBContentTest-QueryContentOnly that is the most underspecified generalization possible (see #$genlKBContentTests) of TEST.
<p>
See also #$QuerySentenceOnlyTestVersionFn.")
(comment KBContentTest "The collection of all KB content tests including ones that are not structurally specific.  Each instance of this collection is a KB content test that either is associated with a particular CycL formula and microtheory or has a #$genlWorks that is associated with a particularCycL formula and microtheory.  For example, consider all the \"Do people like pain\" common sense tests in the KB.  Each of these is basically asking the same question, but they do so with different, but equivalent, CycL formulas.  Each of these specific queries is the #$genlWorks of a particular (possibly unreified) content test that is not associated with a particular formula.")
(comment operatesInRegion "<code>(#$operatesInRegion AGENT REGION)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> performs (at least once) a task central to her/its job function or group mission in <code>REGION</code>.  Positive examples of this sort of \"operating\" in a region include a company buying assembly materials or selling goods in a region, a #$HumanitarianOrganization performing its mission in a region, and a #$TravelingSalesPerson working in a region.  Negative examples include people who visit a region strictly for personal or hobby-related reasons.  Borderline cases include a #$HumanitarianOrganization which raises money in an area but which does not perform its primary function there, and a #$TerroristGroup which takes sanctuary in a region but which does not conduct terrorist operations there.  See also #$operatesInRegion-BroadestNaturalTerritory as well as #$performsInsAtLocation and rules linking the two predicates.")
(comment groupCardinality "A predicate used to indicate the total number of members there are in a particular group.  <code>(#$groupCardinality GROUP NUM)</code> means that the number of members in the #$Group <code>GROUP</code> is the #$Cardinal-Mathematical <code>NUM</code>.  For example (#$groupCardinality #$SevenWondersOfTheAncientWorld 7).  Cyc infers that the #$groupCardinality of pairs is 2, and dozens, 12. For stating the cardinalities of sets or collections rather than groups, see #$cardinality and #$extentCardinality.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice StationeryProduct)
(comment Plot "The collection of all instances of #$Plan that are the results of some instance of #$Plotting.  A #$Plot is characterized by its having been developed in secrecy, frequently with some insidious motive.")
(comment agentiveNounSemTrans "(#$agentiveNounSemTrans NOUN INT FRAME TRANS) means that the translation of word sense number INT of agentive noun NOUN in frame FRAME is TRANS.")
(comment diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary "A specialization of #$properSubSituationTypes (q.v.) that relates #$DiseaseTypes to #$PhysiologicalConditionTypes that constitute their necessary symptoms.  <code>(#$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary DISTYPE SYMPTYPE)</code> means that each case of <code>DISTYPE</code> involves (as #$properSubSituations) one or more occurrences of <code>SYMPTYPE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary #$Asthma #$AsthmaAttack)</code> holds.
<p>
Occurrences <code>SYMPTYPE</code> are typically more readily identifiable than the occurrences of <code>DISTYPE</code> that subsume them; hence their usefulfulness in diagnosis and in gauging treatment effectiveness.  But note that this is <i>not</i> part of the definition of the predicate #$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-Necessary.
<p>
See also the specialization #$diseaseTypeSymptomTypes-NecessaryAndSufficient.")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic DevisedPracticeOrWork)
(comment incapacitates "<code>(#$incapacitates SIT AGENT ACT-TYPE)</code> means that <code>SIT</code> causes <code>AGENT</code> to be certainly incapable of doing actions that are instances of <code>ACT-TYPE</code>, <i>i.e.</i>, <code>ACT</code> brings it about that the #$derivedProbability of '<code>AGENT</code> would be successful at performing an instance of <code>ACT-TYPE</code> if she tried' is zero. Note that incapacitating factors prevent, but preventing factors need not be incapacitating. An example:
being locked in a closet incapacitates one to play tennis; being a
convicted felon incapacitates one to run for elective offices in most
U.S. states. Negative example: an appointment prevents, but doesn't
incapacitate, me from meeting you at 3pm.")
(comment actionFulfillsAssignment "A specialization of #$obligationFulfilled that applies to #$Assignment-Obligations.  (#$actionFulfillsAssignment ACT TASK) means that the #$Action ACT fulfills or completes TASK.  This implies that (i) ACT is an instance of the type of action specified by TASK, (ii)  the agent(s) to whom the task was assigned (see #$allottedAgents) are all actors in ACT, and (iii) ACT is performed during the time the assignment is in effect (see #$assignmentPeriod).")
(comment normativelyBoundAgents "A #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate that is a generalization of both #$agreeingAgents and #$obligatedAgents (qq.v.).  The predicate #$normativelyBoundAgents relates a normative specification to any agent that it \"normatively constrains\" in some way or other.  Thus, it relates an agreement to the agents who are party to it, a proposal to the agent who proposed it, an obligation to the agents who are subject to it, and so on.
<p>
More precisely: where <code>NORM</code> is a #$NormativeSpecification (q.v.) and <code>AGENT</code> is an #$IntelligentAgent, <code>(#$normativelyBoundAgents NORM AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is normatively constrained with respect to <code>NORM</code>.  <i>Normative constraints</i> are taken here to include commitments, responsibilities, duties, and prohibitions of all sorts -- moral, legal, religious, social, familial, professional, and so on.
<p>
In some cases, the normative constraint derives primarily from some action of <code>AGENT</code>'s that has brought <code>NORM</code> about.  For example, <code>AGENT</code> might enter into an #$Agreement or put forth a #$Proposal, and thereby incur certain commitments or responsibilities.  In other cases, the normative constraint derives primarily from the fact that <code>AGENT</code> is in the scope of some normative principle embodied in <code>NORM</code>.  For example, by virtue of being an employed US citizen, <code>AGENT</code> might be subject to the general #$Obligation #$USIncomeTax.  And still other cases involve constraints deriving from a combination of both of the above sources.")
(comment obligationsViolated "(#$obligationsViolated ACTION OB) means that the #$Action ACTION is in violation of the #$Obligation OB. Note that the class of #$Obligations is very wide, and can include many types of 'obligation,' e.g., etiquette, moral codes, military rules of engagement, etc.  See also #$obligationFulfilled.")
(comment preventsFromPlayingSpecifiedRole "<code>(#$preventsFromPlayingSpecifiedRole SIT OBJ ROLE SPECIFICATION)</code> means that the occurance of the #$Situation <code>SIT</code> prevents <code>OBJ</code> from playing the role <code>ROLE</code> in any situation described by the #$NormativeSpecification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>.")
(comment keyParticipants "(#$keyParticipants SOCIAL AGT) holds just in case AGT was one of the \"key participants\" in SOCIAL.  This means that AGT played a leading role in the event or somehow was importantly involved.")
(comment Agreement "A specialization of #$Policy (q.v.). Each instance of this collection involves two or more parties who agree that certain propositions (which are the contents of a corresponding #$Microtheory -- see the shared note #$AgreementNote) should be true. Making the propositions true may require some action or commitment of resources on the part of one or more of the #$agreeingAgents. Thus, instances of #$Agreement will usually involve some instances of #$Obligation. Instances of #$Agreement and #$Obligation differ, however, in that an #$obligatedAgents is responsible for the truth of all of the propositions over which the obligation holds. In an #$Agreement some agents may not be so responsible. For example, in a loan agreement, the borrower agrees to give the lender back the money, but the borrower is the only #$obligatedAgents for the repayment. Note that #$obligatedAgents need not be among the #$agreeingAgents in the agreement that involves or generates the obligation. Moreover, #$agreeingAgents aren't always #$obligatedAgents; e.g., Wanda and Paul may agree that Paul alone is obligated to do some task. Notable specializations of #$Agreement include #$PeaceAccord, #$LegalAgreement, #$InformalAgreement, #$BusinessPartnershipAgreement, #$WorkAgreement, #$MaintenanceAgreement, #$Reservation and #$Appointment. For assertions about what is \"supposed to be\" true, given some #$Agreement, see #$ist-Agreement.")
(comment NewYearsResolution "A specialization of #$Policy (q.v.).  Each instance of #$NewYearsResolution is the policy of an agent to behave a certain novel (for that agent) way starting on the first day of a new year.  
<p>
New years' resolutions are usually begun with promises to oneself to improve one's own behavior (see #$Promise).")
(comment WeddingVows "A collection of #$Obligations. Each instance of #$WeddingVows is an obligation that a bride or groom accepts as his or her responsibility to conform to upon getting married. Contents generally include love, faithfulness, and not participating in #$ExtraMaritalSexualBehavior. The obligation holds for the length of the marriage, <i>i.e.</i>, it is annulled only by #$Divorce or by the death of one of the spouses.")
(comment TheAutoIncrementingIntegerSequenceGenerator "The #$IndexicalConcept,
#$TheAutoIncrementingIntegerSequenceGenerator denotes the default
#$IntegerSequenceGenerator used by DBMS programs to auto-increment
#$PhysicalFields which are #$autoIncrementingPhysicalFields.")
(comment autoIncrementingPhysicalField "(#$autoIncrementingPhysicalField PF) means that the
#$PhysicalField, PF, is auto-incremented by the DBMS program hosting
its parent database. See also
#$TheAutoIncrementingIntegerSequenceGenerator, which is an
#$IndexicalConcept denoting the #$IntegerSequenceGenerator on the DBMS
which actually generates successive values for the field.")
(comment preventsFromPlayingRoleInType "<code>(#$preventsFromPlayingRoleInType SIT OBJ ROLE SIT-TYPE)</code> means that the occurance of the #$Situation <code>SIT</code> prevents <code>OBJ</code> from playing the role <code>ROLE</code> in any #$Situation of the type <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment normAdopted "<code>(#$normAdopted ADOPT NORM)</code> means that in <code>ADOPT</code> (an instance of #$AdoptingANorm), the norm adopted is the #$NormativeSpecification <code>NORM</code>.")
(comment Agent-Generic "A specialization of #$SomethingExisting.  Each instance of #$Agent-Generic is a being that has desires or intentions, and the ability to act on those desires or intentions.  Instances of #$Agent-Generic may be individuals (see the specialization #$IndividualAgent) or they may consist of several #$Agent-Generics operating together (see the specialization #$MultiIndividualAgent).  Notable specializations of #$Agent-Generic include #$Agent-PartiallyTangible and #$Artifact-Agentive.")
(comment negationPreds "A #$MetaPredicate for stating that two predicates are logical \"contraries\" of one another.  <code>(#$negationPreds PRED1 PRED2)</code> means that if <code>PRED1</code> holds among a given sequence of things, then <code>PRED2</code> does <i>not</i> hold among that sequence (and vice versa).  Thus it is equivalent to 

<pre>  (#$not (#$and (PRED1 . ARGS) (PRED2 . ARGS))) .</pre>  

For example, (#$negationPreds #$owns #$rents) holds, as one cannot both own and rent a given thing at the same time.   
<p>
Note that the argument types of <code>PRED1</code> and <code>PRED2</code> need not be the same, they merely must not be disjoint.  Note also that <code>PRED1</code> and <code>PRED2</code> are constrained (see e.g. #$interArgIsa) either to both having the same fixed-arity (see #$FixedArityRelation) or to both having variable-arity (see #$VariableArityRelations).     
<p>
See also #$genlPreds and #$negationInverse.")
(comment ProgramIdentifierNamespace "This is the collection of all program identifier namespaces.")
(comment ConceptualWorkTypeByCreator "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$ConceptualWork.  Instances are types of conceptual works, all created by the same agent.")
(comment interAgentSupportTypeBasis "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate for #$InterAgentSupportTypeFn. (#$interAgentSupportTypeBasis SUPPORT-TYPE BASIS) means that any positive amount (see #$positiveAmountOf) of the support quantity SUPPORT-TYPE is, by definition, manifested in instances of BASIS, a specialization of #$HelpingAnAgent.  For example, (#$interAgentSupportTypeBasis #$EconomicSupport #$GivingEconomicAid) means that economic support is manifested in the giving of ecomonic aid.")
(comment InterAgentSupportTypeFn "(#$InterAgentSupportTypeFn TYPE) denotes the collection of instances of #$InterAgentSupportQuantity that  For example, (#$InterAgentSupportTypeFn #$GivingEconomicAid) is the collection of all degrees of ecomomic support.")
(comment policyForAgent "<code>(#$policyForAgent POLICY AGENT)</code> means that the #$Policy <code>POLICY</code> is \"for\" the #$IntelligentAgent <code>AGENT</code>, in the sense that <code>AGENT</code> is who is responsible for according with <code>POLICY</code>.  The notion of <i>responsibility</i> here is weaker than obligation: it may be my policy to go to the gym three times a week: in such a case I am not obligated to go to the gym three times a week, but I am in a weak sense still responsible for according with the policy.")
(comment likelySuspects "A predicate used to relate actions to agents who may be perpetrators of those actions (but are not known to be performers of the actions).  <code>(#$likelySuspects ACTION AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is not known to be the performer of <code>ACTION</code>, but nonetheless is considered to be relatively likely to be the performer of <code>ACTION</code>.")
(comment agentTypeGivesSupportToAgentOfCategory "(#$agentTypeGivesSupportToAgentOfCategory GIVER-TYPE RECEIVER CATEGORY) means that there exists at least instance GIVER of GIVER-TYPE such that  (#$givesSupportToAgent GIVER RECEIVER CATEGORY).")
(comment intelligenceOperativeForGovernment "(#$intelligenceOperativeForGovernment OPERATIVE GOVERNMENT) means that OPERATIVE is an instance of #$IntelligenceOperative who does work on behalf of the government GOVERNMENT.  Typically, this means that OPERATIVE stands in the #$intelligenceOperativeForOrg relation to some intelligence agency or military agency that is a sub-organization of GOVERNMENT.  GOVERNMENT need not know of OPERATIVE or even count OPERATIVE among its employees or charges.")
(comment adoptionTypeOfNormByAgent "(#$adoptionTypeOfNormByAgent NORM AGENT ADOPT-TYPE) means that ADOPT-TYPE is the collection of events in which AGENT adopts the norm NORM.")
(comment ArmingAnAgent "The collection of actions in which one or more agents provides working weaponry to another agent.")
(comment CycLAssertion "The collection of semantically well-formed #$CycLSentences asserted to the Cyc Knowledge Base.  Each instance of #$CycLAssertion is either (1) an HL assertion, i.e. a CycL sentence that corresponds to a data structure actually in the Cyc KB), or (2) an EL assertion : an Epistemological Level CycL sentence that can be canonicalized into one or more already extant HL assertions.  #$CycLAssertion is used as a quoted argument type constraint for certain meta-predicates, such as #$overrides.")
(comment middlePartOfInterval "(#$middlePartOfInterval TIME-INTERVAL MIDDLE-PART) means that
MIDDLE-PART is the #$TimeInterval denoted in English by the phrase 'mid-
TIME-INTERVAL,' e.g., 'the mid 1980s.' See the comment on the
corresponding function #$MiddlePartFn.")
(comment temporallyCoexist "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate and the most general #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate; a specialization of #$temporallyIntersects (q.v.).  #$temporallyCoexist relates any two temporally-extended things that presently exist or obtain or are occurring. <code>(#$temporallyCoexist TEMP1 TEMP2)</code> means that the temporal extents of <code>TEMP1</code> and <code>TEMP2</code> both subsume the present time.
<p>
More formally: for any #$TimeInterval <code>TIME</code>,
<pre>
  (#$temporallyCoexist TEMP1 TEMP2)
</pre>
is true at <code>TIME</code> (see #$mtTimeIndex) if and only if both of these:
<pre>
  (#$temporallySubsumes TEMP1 TIME)

  (#$temporallySubsumes TEMP2 TIME)
</pre>
are atemporally true (i.e. true at #$Always-TimeInterval).
<p>
For example, the sentence <code>(#$temporallyCoexist #$GeorgeWBush #$RonaldReagan)</code> was true at the start of 2004 and false after Reagan's death on June 5 of that year.  On the other hand,  the sentence <code>(#$temporallyCoexist #$GeorgeWBush #$GeorgeWashington)</code> has never been true.")
(comment evaluationResultQuotedIsa "A binary #$MetaRelation that holds between relations and collections. #$evaluationResultQuotedIsa is primarily used to indicate that any value returned by a given evaluatable function is a quoted instance of a given collection. Where FUNC is a Function-Denotational, (#$evaluationResultQuotedIsa FUNC COL) means that FUNC returns a quoted instance of COL for any sequence of arguments for which FUNC is defined. That is, (#$quotedIsa (FUNC ARG1 ... ARGn) COL) holds for any sequence <ARG1, ..., ARGN> for which FUNC has a value. For example, '(#$evaluationResultQuotedIsa #$SubstringFn #$SubLString)' holds, and it entails (e.g.) '(#$quotedIsa (#$SubstringFn \"ABC\" 1 2) #$SubLString)'.")
(comment focalSubject "#$focalSubject is a more specialized form of the predicate #$topicRole.  It relates an instance of #$MentalSituation to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  Like #$topicRole it is intended to relate an entity to an event where that entity is the subject of some mental state of some agent in the role of #$deliberateActors in that event.  This is a slightly richer version in that it states that this entity is focal to the event. For example, an unsuccessful assassination attempt might not physically involve a particular agent, nonetheless we want to refer to the target's role in that event.  Further, a lecture could be about a person who died centuries before the time of that lecture.  This is a weak relationship.  Representations should use more specialized versions of this predicate (i.e., the first example should use #$intendedAttackTargets).  Contrast with #$evidence and #$nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation.")
(comment candidateStringsForTopic "This is a very general predicate for relating instances of #$SubLString to the instances of #$Thing with the sense that the instance of #$SubLString might be useful for the purposes of gathering information about #$Thing.  For example, (#$candidateStringsForTopic  GeorgeWBush 'Texas'). This allows us to represent potential relationships (perhaps for machine learning) without committing to an actual connections.")
(comment goodStringsForTopic "This is a very general predicate for relating instances of #$SubLString to the instances of #$Thing with the sense that the instance of #$SubLString is known to be useful for the purposes of gathering information about #$Thing.  For example, (#$goodStringsForTopic GeorgeWBush  'George W. Bush').")
(comment suggestedStrings "An assertion of the form (#$usefulStrings ASSIGN STRING) means that within the instance of #$Assignment-Specificaton ASSIGN, the #$SubLString STRING is known to be a useful set of key words when interacting with data sources.")
(comment ibtContentStrings "An assertion of the form (#$ibtContentStrings IBT STRING) means that topic or, more generally, the information contained in the #$InformationBearingThing IBT is partially captured by the concepts expressed by the  #$SubLString STRING.  This a more general relationship than #$ibtKeyWords, which have a formal role in the characterization of an #$InformationBearingThing.")
(comment ibtKeyWords "An assertion of the form (#$ibtKeyWords IBT STRING) means that the #$InformationBearingThing IBT represents the #$SubLString STRING as a keyword for understanding its topic or content.")
(comment InformationGatheringTypeByTopicType "The instances of #$InformationGatheringTypeByTopicType are used to facet #$InformationGathering.  All of the collections that are instances of #$InformationGatheringTypeByTopicType are such that their instances all share a common value for #$topicOfIndividual.")
(comment candidateStringsForIGType "This is a very general predicate for relating instances of #$SubLString to sub-collections of #$InformationGathering.  In effect, an assertion of the form (#$candidateStringsForIGType TYPE STRING) weakly indicates that there is some evidence that the #$SubLString STRING would be useful for someone engaged in TYPE in that STRING is bears the relationship of #$candidateStringsForTopic to the #$topicOfIndividual for all of the instances of TYPE.  For instance, if Cyc observed someone engaged in an instance of (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$Research #$topicOfIndividual #$Iraq) use the string 'WMD' with a search engine that would justify an assertion of the form (#$candidateStringsForIGType (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$Research #$topicOfIndividual #$Iraq) 'WMD').   A much more meaningful assertion would use the predicate #$goodStringsForIGType.")
(comment goodStringsForIGType "An assertion of the form (#$goodStringsForIGType  TYPE STRING) asserts that the #$SubLString STRING is a useful key word for someone to use if they are performing an instance of TYPE, some sub-collection of #$InformationGathering. gForTopic to the #$topicOfIndividual for all of the instances of TYPE.  For instance, if Cyc observed someone engaged in an instance of (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$Research #$topicOfIndividual #$Iraq) use the string 'Baghdad' with a search engine that would justify an assertion of the form (#$candidateStringsForIGType (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$Research #$topicOfIndividual #$Iraq) 'Baghdad').  This is a #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation.")
(comment stringsUsed "An assertion of the form (#$stringsUsed EVENT STRING) means that during the instance of #$InformationTransferEvent EVENT the #$SubLString STRING was used.  For example, when using a #$SearchEngine, the specific string that is typed in to the engine would play this role in that event.")
(comment sociallySuperiorTo "A specialization of both #$ableToControl and #$influencesAgent.  <code>(#$sociallySuperiorTo SUPERIOR SUBORDINATE)</code> means that <code>SUPERIOR</code> has some type of socially superior position over <code>SUBORDINATE</code> that gives <code>SUPERIOR</code> power over <code>SUBORDINATE</code>.  In many cases, <code>SUPERIOR</code> is able to command and punish <code>SUBORDINATE</code>, and can be held responsible for <code>SUBORDINATE</code>'s actions.  An important specialization of this predicate is #$hasAgents.")
(comment ableToControl "A predicate that relates an agent to some cotemporal thing s/he is able to control.  More precisely, <code>(#$ableToControl AGENT THING)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is in a position of being able to either:
<p>
(i) influence (<i>i.e.</i>, prohibit, enable, or constrain) some significant set of behaviors (or actions or functionings) of <code>THING</code> or <br>
(ii) influence some significant set of behaviors of other agents with respect to <code>THING</code>.  
<p>
For example, Wilbur Post might be able to control some range of his horse Ed's actions in virtue of having the (physical and legal) power to force Ed to walk down this bridle path, stay in that corral, and so on; and Wilbur might also be able to control Ed in the sense of deciding who has access to him (<i>e.g.</i>, deciding who may see Ed and who may ride him).  
<p>
The controlled <code>THING</code> might be a non-living possession of <code>AGENT</code>'s or, as in the above example, another <i>agent</i>.  Since one's ability to control something is rarely comprehensive, <code>(#$ableToControl AGENT THING)</code> can hold despite the fact there  are many behaviors/actions/functionings of <code>THING</code>'s that are beyond <code>AGENT</code>'s control.  Thus, although Wilbur might be able to control which paths Ed is ridden on, where he sleeps, and what he eats, Wilbur might not be able to control such things as Ed's breathing rate, tail swishing, or what he does in the privacy of his stall.  
<p>
Note that <code>AGENT</code>'s being #$ableToControl <code>THING</code> does not entail that <code>AGENT</code> actually exercises this ability.  Note also that <code>AGENT</code>'s merely being able to influence <i>some</i> behavior of <code>THING</code> (or some behavior of another agent's with respect to <code>THING</code>) is not sufficient for her being #$ableToControl <code>THING</code>; <code>AGENT</code> must be able to influence a significant set or range of <code>THING</code>'s behaviors (or of other agents' behaviors with respect to <code>THING</code>) in order to be able to control <code>THING</code> (see #$influencesAgent).  (Unavoidably, the notions of being \"able\" to do something and of a \"significant range\" of a thing's behaviors/actions/functionings are both rather vague.)  For describing events in which an agent actually wields control over something, consider using #$ControllingSomething and #$objectControlled.")
(comment wouldBeEvidenceForPlayingRole "(#$wouldBeEvidenceForPlayingRole AGENT SITUATION ROLE SENTENCE) means that if SENTENCE were true, it would be evidence that (ROLE SITUATION AGENT).  This can be regarded as meaning that if SENTENCE were true, the conditional probability of (ROLE SITUATION AGENT) given SENTENCE would be higher than the prior (or extant) probability of (ROLE SITUATION AGENT).")
(comment fosters-SitTypeSitType "A #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate that relates types of situations to other types of situations, where instances of the latter types are fostered by instances of the former types. <code>(#$fosters-SitTypeSitType SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2)</code> means that the kind of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE1</code> fosters the kind of #$Situation <code>SIT-TYPE2</code>.  Often <code>SIT-TYPE2</code> is a specialization of #$Event and <code>SIT-TYPE1</code> is a specialization of #$Event or #$Action.  Fostering is a looser relation than causation: if <code>SIT-TYPE1</code> causes <code>SIT-TYPE2</code> (#$causes-SitTypeSitType), it certainly fosters it; but a situation-type can foster another without being a cause of it.  While it isn't necessarily the case when <code>(#$fosters-SitTypeSitType SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2)</code> that the occurrence of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE1</code> is typically associated with the occurrence of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE2</code>, it will be the case that the occurrence of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE1</code> is one of the most promising ways of bringing about an occurrence of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE2</code>.")
(comment causes-SitProp "(#$causes-SitProp SIT PROP) means that the situation SIT causes the #$CycLSentence-Assertible PROP to become true.")
(comment EvaluationOfAssertionByOnFn "(#$EvaluationOfAssertionByOnFn ASSERT AGENT SECOND) denotes the instance of #$Evaluating in which ASSERT is evaluated by the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT, as submitted at the time denoted by INT (where INT is a #$PositiveInteger corresponding to the number of seconds elapsed since January 1, 1970).")
(comment assertionEvaluated "(#$assertionEvaluated EVAL SENT) means that, in EVAL, SENT is either the assertion evaluated or is an EL sentence that was evaluated that canonicalizes into two or more assertions.")
(comment evaluationOfAssertionByOn "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate for #$EvaluationOfAssertionByOnFn.  (#$evaluationOfAssertionByOn EVALUATION ASSERT AGENT INT) identifies EVALUATION as the unique instance of #$Evaluating in which AGENT evaluates ASSERT at the time denoted by INT (which is the number of seconds elapsed since January 1, 1970).")
(comment instanceActualizesSubSituationType "The predicate #$instanceActualizesSubSituationType is used to represent the actualization of a specialization of #$Situation's conditional sub-situation types (see, #$candidateProperSubSituationTypes) within an instance of that #$Situation.  Specifically, an assertion of the form (#$instanceActualizesSubSituationType SIT-INSTANCE SUB-SIT-TYPE) means that the SIT-INSTANCE has as a #$subSituations an instance of SUB-SIT-TYPE.  The purpose of this predicate is to allow for the representation of candidate / conditional sub-situation types, but also to represent the actualization of those candidate / conditional scenes within its instances.  This predicate is introduced as a way of reducing the distinct number of situation types which are needed.  Let us focus on the complex event type #$StayingAtCommercialLodging.  A very common, though not essential, sub-event in instances of #$StayingAtCommercialLodging would be the request for and receiving of a wake-up call.  Now, rather than have two event types, one which includes the request and receiving and the other which does not, we can use the predicate #$instanceActualizesSubSituationType to specify rules that dictate the conditions under which instances of a single type will have instances of the requesting and receiving as sub-events.")
(comment goalProvidesMotiveFor "<code>(#$goalProvidesMotiveFor GOAL AGT
ACT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>AGT</code>'s having the goal <code>GOAL</code> would provide her with a motive for acting in the specified way -- <i>i.e.</i>, for playing <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>ACT-TYPE</code>.  Note that <code>(#$goalProvidesMotiveFor GOAL
AGT ...)</code> does not entail that <code>AGT</code> actually has <code>GOAL</code> as a goal -- only that, <i>if</i> she had this goal,
she would be credited (ordinarily) with having a motive for doing
some instance of <code>ACT-TYPE</code>. #$goalProvidesMotiveFor is a specialization of #$providesMotiveFor which focuses on common motivational links
between #$goals and action-types. For further discussion concerning
the notion of 'motive' at work here, see the comment on
#$providesMotiveFor.")
(comment CognitivePredicate "A specialization of #$AgentPredicate.  Each instance of #$CognitivePredicate is a (binary or higher-arity) relation that holds among (at least) an agent and some thing to which the agent has some cognitive connection (perceptual, epistemic, or attitudinal).  Two important specializations of #$CognitivePredicate are #$CognitiveAwarenessPredicate (q.v.), whose instances (e.g. #$tastes, #$knowsAbout) relate an agent to that which the agent perceives or is otherwise aware of, and #$CognitiveAttitudePredicate (q.v.), whose instances (e.g. #$beliefs, #$goals) relate an agent (at least) to an #$CycLSentence-Assertible expressing (all or part of) the content of the agent's belief, goal, etc.")
(comment Pangolin "A specialization of #$Philodota.")
(comment CardinalityOfFn "A unary #$ScalarDenotingFunction that takes a given set-or-collection to a cardinal number.  (#$CardinalityOfFn SETORCOL) equals the cardinality of SETORCOL. For example, (#$CardinalityOfFn #$TheEmptySet) is 0.
<p>
See also the corresponding predicate #$cardinality.")
(comment ShortTermLoan "A #$LoanAgreement is a #$ShortTermLoan (#$loanTermOptions LOAN #$ShortTermLoan) just when the term of the loan (#$loanTermDuration) is short compared to other loans of the same or similar type and size.")
(comment Hypocrite "A #$PersonTypeByMentalFeature instances of which are all and only those agents characterized by #$Hypocrisy: the pretense of having qualities or attitudes (especially virtuous ones) that one does not actually possess.")
(comment BrandishingAWeapon "A sub-collection of both #$Intimidation-CommunicationAct and (#$DisplayingFn #$Weapon), #$BrandishingAWeapon is the collection of events where some agent displays some kind of weapon with the intent of intimidating another agent.")
(comment SingleEventAssignment "A subcollection of #$Assignment-Specification, each instance of #$SingleEventAssignment is characterized by the fact that the expectation is for the performance of a single event.  This should be contrasted with the collections #$IteratedAssignment and #$RegularlyRecurringAssignment.")
(comment definitionInDictionary "(#$definitionInDictionary DICT TERM DEFINITION) means that the structurally specific #$Dictionary DICT contains (see #$containsStructure-CW) the #$TextString TERM and the #$GraphicalStructure DEF, that TERM is one of the terms defined in DICT, and that DEF is the definition of TERM in DICT.")
(comment PCWTypeByGenre "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PCWTypeByGenre is a collection of #$PropositionalConceptualWorks that are of a certain genre.  A conceptual work (a movie, book, play, etc.) may have attributes of several instances of #$PCWTypeByGenre at the same time.  The instances of this collection (broadly) divide up a major portion of #$PropositionalConceptualWork
into subcollections.")
(comment TwoDimensionalArtObjectTypeByGenre "The collection of collections of instances of  #$ConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$TwoDimensionalArtObjectTypeByGenre characterizes certain artistic periods or genres/schools/types of #$TwoDimensionalArtObjects.")
(comment IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn "A unary function that takes a CycL sentence that can be used in a query (see #$CycLSentence-Askable) and returns the intensional meaning appropriate to the question being asked by such a query.  If the question being asked with <code>SENT</code> is a \"<i>Yes/No</i>\" question, (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is a #$Proposition, which is true or false with respect to any given context.  If the question being asked with <code>SENT</code> is a \"<i>what things are such that...</i>\" question  -- i.e. a question that asks for bindings for variables -- (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is an intensional property or \"propositional function\", which has some (possibly empty) extension with respect to any given context.  
<p>
More precisely:  (i) If <code>SENT</code> is a closed sentence, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the #$Proposition that <code>SENT</code> is true.  (ii) If <code>SENT</code> is an implication of the form <code>(#$implies ANTE CONSEQ)</code> such that any variables occurring free in <code>CONSEQ</code> also occur free in <code>ANTE</code>, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the #$Proposition that the universal closure of <code>SENT</code> is true.  (iii) If <code>SENT</code> is an implication of the form <code>(#$implies ANTE CONSEQ)</code> such that some variables occurring free in <code>CONSEQ</code> that do <i>not</i> occur free in <code>ANTE</code>, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the intensional property that holds, in a given context, of exactly those sequences of things that satisfy the open sentence obtained from <code>(#$implies ANTE CONSEQ)</code> by universally quantifying all of the variables occurring free in <code>ANTE</code>.  (iv) Finally, if <code>SENT</code> is an open sentence that is not an implication, then (#$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn <code>SENT</code>) is the intensional property that holds, in a given context, of exactly those sequences of things that satisfy <code>SENT</code>.
<p>
The main purpose of #$IntensionOfQuerySentenceFn is to help relate instances of #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified that ask essentially the same question, but do not have exactly the same sentence as their respective #$InferenceSentenceParameter values.  See also #$kbContentTestQuestion-Content.")
(comment argGenlsConstantModeForDetermination "An assertion of the form (#$argGenlsConstantModeForDetermination PRED N TYPE DET) means that relative to the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination DET, the  Nth argument of the #$Predicate PRED should bea sub-collection of the #$Collection TYPE and that argument position has a constant mode (i.e., for the induction of rules, that argument must have a constant as its value and cannot take a variable).   The sense of mode here is derived from #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment argGenlsOutputModeForDetermination "An assertion of the form (#$argGenlsOutputModeForDetermination PRED N STRING TYPE DET) means that relative to the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination DET, the  Nth argument of the #$Predicate PRED should be a sub-collection of the #$Collection TYPE and that argument position has the mode of an output variable.   The sense of mode here is derived from #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment argIsaConstantModeForDetermination "An assertion of the form (#$argIsaConstantModeForDetermination PRED N TYPE DET) means that relative to the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination DET, the  Nth argument of the #$Predicate PRED should be an instance of the #$Collection TYPE and that argument position has a constant mode (i.e., for the induction of rules, that argument must have a constant as its value and cannot take a variable).   The sense of mode here is derived from #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(disjointWith Hollow Planet)
(comment mtMonad "For microtheories <code>MT</code> and <code>BASE</code>, <code>(#$mtMonad MT MONAD)</code> means that <code>MONAD</code> constitutes the 'base' of <code>MT</code> in the sense that <code>MT</code> is otherwise specified by its values of specific dimensions (see #$MicrotheoryDimensionPredicate).  Another way to look at this is that <code>MONAD</code> constitutes whatever left of <code>MT</code> (or the 'rest' of <code>MT</code>) after having the values of explicit dimensions we can handle.  For example, if one creates a microtheory <code>MT</code> about social life in U.S. during 1990-2000, s/he can simply assert (#$mtMonad MT #$UnitedStatesSocialLifeMt) and (#$mtTimeIndex <code>MT</code> (#$TimeIntervalInclusiveFn (#$YearFn 1990) (#$YearFn 2000))) etc.")
(comment means "A MetaLanguagePredicate (q.v.) that relates #$SubLSExpressions to their meanings: the things in the intended model of the CycL language that those terms denote, refer to, stand for, or express. <code>(#$means TERM THING)</code> means that <code>TERM</code> denotes, refers to, stands for, or expresses <code>THING</code>. <code>TERM</code> will often be explicitly quoted, by being wrapped in the syncategorematic quotation symbol '#$Quote'. For example, the true sentence '(#$means (#$Quote #$Plato) #$Plato)' means that the CycL term 'Plato' means (denotes) the person Plato. (Thus #$means's first argument-place is <i>not</i> \"implicitly quoted\"; cf. #$quotedArgument).
<p>
But note that the first argument of #$means might not be quoted at all. Suppose (e.g.) that the term 'Plato' were the CycL constant most beloved of Cyclists, and that a new constant 'CyclistsFavoriteConstant' were reified and defined so as to reflect this fact. Then 'CyclistsFavoriteConstant' would denote the CycL constant 'Plato', which in turn denotes the man Plato; and so the sentence '(#$means CyclistsFavoriteConstant Plato)' -- which involves no quotation -- would be true.
<p>
Note finally that the sentence '(#$means #$Plato #$Plato)' is of course <i>not</i> true, as it means that the man Plato is a CycL term that denotes the man Plato, which is a patent falsehood since no man is a CycL term and no man denotes anything.
<p>
See also #$expresses, #$denotes, #$hasDenotatum, #$quotedIsa, #$EscapeQuote, and the shared #$NoteAboutQuotingInCycL.")
(comment denotes "A #$MetaLanguagePredicate (q.v.) that relates #$CycLDenotationalTerm to their denotata: the things in the intended model of the CycL language that those terms denote or stand for.  <code>(#$denotes TERM THING)</code> means that <code>TERM</code> denotes <code>THING</code>.  <code>TERM</code> will often be explicitly quoted, by being wrapped in the syncategorematic quotation symbol '#$Quote'.  For example, the true sentence '(#$denotes (#$Quote #$Plato) #$Plato)' means that the CycL term '#$Plato' denotes the person #$Plato.  (Thus #$denotes's first argument-place is <i>not</i> \"implicitly quoted\"; cf. #$quotedArgument).
<p>
But note that the first argument of #$denotes might <i>not</i> be quoted at all.  Suppose (e.g.) that the term '#$Plato' were the CycL constant most beloved of #$Cyclists, and that a new constant 'CyclistsFavoriteConstant' were reified and defined so as to reflect this fact.  Then 'CyclistsFavoriteConstant' would refer to the CycL constant '#$Plato', which in turn denotes the man Plato; and so the sentence '(#$denotes CyclistsFavoriteConstant #$Plato)' -- which involves no quotation -- would be true.
<p>
Note also that not all CycL terms denote, not even all #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerms (q.v.).  For example, the term '(#$BorderBetweenFn #$Canada #$Mexico)' fails to denote anything (except perhaps in certain counterfactual contexts).
<p>
Note finally that the sentence '(#$denotes #$Plato #$Plato)' is of course <i>not</i> true, as it means that the man Plato is a CycL term that denotes the man Plato, which is a patent falsehood since no man is a CycL term and no man denotes anything.
<p>
See also #$means, #$expresses, #$hasDenotatum, #$quotedIsa, #$EscapeQuote, and the shared #$NoteAboutQuotingInCycL.")
(comment Assignment-Obligation "A specialization of both #$Obligation and #$Agreement (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Assignment-Obligation is an obligation to maintain, bring about, or prevent some type of situation.  The agents who have this obligation are the #$allottedAgents and the agents who have given out this obligation are the #$assigner.
<p>
Assignments come in a wide variety of flavors.  The work/action assigned might or might not be part of the assignees' job.  The assignment might be formal or casual, explicit or tacit.  An assignment might take seconds to complete or decades to complete.  A given assignment might be one-off or recurring.  An assignment given to multiple agents might or might not require more-or-less the same thing of each agent, and it might require them to work independently or in concert.  One can take an assignment \"upon oneself\", which means (in effect) assigning it to oneself.")
(comment intraArgReln "An #$ArgConstraintPredicate (q.v.)  that can be used to put a certain kind of binary-relation-based  constraint on a predicate with respect to a given argument-place.   The constraint thereby imposed entails that different CycL terms  can be substituted one for the other in that place (keeping the  predicate's other arguments fixed) while preserving truth only  if the terms' respective denotata stand in the specified  symmetric binary relation.  (Note that this places a necessary, and not a sufficient, condition on such a substitution's preserving  truth.)  
<p>
<code>(#$intraArgReln PRED N BINPRED)</code> means that whenever <code>PRED</code>  holds of two argument-sequences that differ only in their <code>N</code>th  members, then those respective <code>N</code>th members stand in the symmetric  relation <code>BINPRED</code>.  Among the most common predicates to play the  role of <code>BINPRED</code>  in #$intraArgReln sentences asserted to the Cyc  Knowledge Base are #$quantityIntersects, #$intersectsWith, and  #$coextensionalSetOrCollectionOrRelations.  See also  #$argCardinality and #$interArgReln.")
(comment USGSContentTest "#$USGSContentTest is a collection of #$SKSIContentTests which test the content of the #$Usgs-KS database.")
(comment comparativeTypesWRTSpec "This is a hacked up predicate to work around bug 16558.")
(comment PartiallyTangibleTypeByPhysicalFeature "A #$FacetingCollectionType.  Each instance of #$PartiallyTangibleTypeByPhysicalFeature is a collection of individuals who all share a particular physical property.  For example #$RhNegative is the collection of instances of #$Blood such that each is blood that is of type rh-negative.  This collection represents the property \"being blood type rh-negative\" and something has that property just in case they are an instance of that collection.  Note: these collections represent properties that things have or lack in a relatively absolute sense.  For physical properties that admit of dense degress (e.g. #$Flammability -- although something can be flammable in an absolute sense it is by virtue of having a particular degree of flammability.) see #$PhysicalQuantity. ")
(comment lessThan "A #$NumericComparisonPredicate that is a  generalization of the mathematical less-than ( < ) relation to  #$ScalarIntervals (q.v.) of all sorts, including quantitative  intervals as well as point values (see #$ScalarPointValue).   (#$lessThan VALUE1 VALUE2) means that VALUE1 is less than VALUE2  with respect to some scale that they are both on.  More precisely,  there is some #$TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType SCALE that both  VALUE1 and VALUE2 are instances of and either (i) SCALE is a  specialization of #$NumericInterval (e.g. #$RealNumber) and the  maximum (see #$maxQuantValue) of VALUE1 is less than the  minimum (see #$minQuantValue) of VALUE2 or (ii)  (#$followingValueOnScale VALUE1 VALUE2 SCALE) holds.  Note that  #$lessThan is an #$ELRelation (q.v.), and the above sentence would actually canonicalize to (#$greaterThan VALUE2 VALUE1).")
(comment ScienceFairEvent "This is the collection of instances of #$Education at which students display their science projects. Often, these are competitive as the projects may be judged.")
(comment studies "The expression `(#$studies AGENT THING)' means that the intelligent agent
AGENT studies THING. The notion of studying here is akin to what is involved in doing research, though it is broader. For example, reading extant material about THING, if there is such, would in most cases be considered part of studying THING, while it would probably count only as preparation for doing
research. It is important that this notion of studying is distinct from the notion of studying for a test. Studying in the present sense may have no connection to any educational event.  Compare also with #$Studying. The notion here definitely
includes direct encounters with the THING being studied.")
(comment stateOfAffairsObjectedTo "A #$BinaryRolePredicate.  <code>(#$stateOfAffairsObjectedTo OBJECTING SENT)</code> means that the #$senderOfInfo in the instance of #$Objecting-CommunicationAct <code>OBJECTING</code> objects to the state of affairs corresponding to the #$CycLSentence-Assertible <code>SENT</code>.  An example of an assertion that could be made using this predicate is
<p>(#$stateOfAffairsObjectedTo AlicesObjectingToBobsInfidelity <i>P</i>),
<p>
where <i>P</i> abbreviates a #$CycLSentence-Assertible stating that Bob cheats on his wife Alice.")
(comment MillionDollarsPerYear "A function which returns an instance of #$MonetaryRate.  (#$MillionDollarsPerYear 1) equals (#$DollarsPerYear 1000000).  Note, the dollars here are United States dollars.")
(comment actsOnBehalfOf "(#$actsOnBehalfOf AGENT-1 AGENT-2) means that AGENT-1 takes actions on behalf of AGENT-2.  Note that this is a reflexive relation, as every agent takes actions on his or her own behalf.  To make the more substantive claim that AGENT-1 takes actions on behalf of another, use #$hasAgents, which is a spec-inverse of #$actsOnBehalfOf.")
(comment MusicalCompositionTypeByGenre "A #$FacetingCollectionType.  Each instance of #$MusicalCompositionTypeByGenre is a specialization of #$MusicalComposition whose instances are of the same musical genre.")
(comment ComputerGameProgram-Sports "The collection of #$ComputerGamePrograms which simulate some #$Sport.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-LiteraryCriticismGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork 
that are of the literary criticism genre.      ")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-ThrillerGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are of the 
thriller genre. #$AlfredHitchcock's #$Psycho-TheMovie is an example of a 
movie in this genre.      ")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-MusicalGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork (usually movies or plays) that prominently feature singing, 
dancing, and music.               ")
