(comment Granulating-Healing "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Healing. In each #$Granulating-Healing, something forms granulating tissue.")
(comment SplutteringSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Spitting. In each #$SplutteringSomething, someone spits something up in an explosive manner.")
(comment StubbingSomething-IncurringAnInjury "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IncurringAnInjury. In each #$StubbingSomething-IncurringAnInjury, someone strikes something against an object.")
(comment EtiolatingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$EtiolatingSomething, something makes something else pale or sickly.")
(comment EmittingSomeGasOrOdor "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$EmittingAnObject. In each #$EmittingSomeGasOrOdor, something expels (gases or odors).")
(comment PuttingOnAGown "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PuttingOnAClothingItem. In each #$PuttingOnAGown, someone dresses someone else in a gown.")
(comment Jaundice "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$AilmentCondition. In each #$Jaundice, something affects with, or as if with, jaundice.")
(comment RunningDownSomething-IncurringAnInjury "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IncurringAnInjury. In each #$RunningDownSomething-IncurringAnInjury, something injures or kills by running over, as with a vehicle.")
(comment PackingOn-GainingBodyWeight "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GainingBodyWeight. In each #$PackingOn-GainingBodyWeight, someone gains (weight).")
(comment Giving-Offering-CommunicationAct "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Offering-CommunicationAct. In each #$Giving-Offering-CommunicationAct, someone proffers (a body part).")
(comment PackingSomething-MedicalTreatmentEvent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent. In each #$PackingSomething-MedicalTreatmentEvent, someone treats the body or any part of it by wrapping it, as with blankets or sheets, and applying compresses to it, or stuffing it to provide cover, containment, or therapy, or to absorb blood.")
(comment SnuffingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Inhaling. In each #$SnuffingSomething, someone inhales audibly through the nose.")
(comment BrutalizingSomeone "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$PhysiologicalConditionType. In each #$BrutalizingSomeone, something makes someone brutal, unfeeling, or inhuman.")
(comment ConvertingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$ConvertingSomething, someone changes the nature, purpose, or function of something.")
(comment OpalizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$OpalizingSomething, something makes something else opalescent.")
(comment ArterializingSomething-BiologicalEvent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BiologicalEvent. In each #$ArterializingSomething-BiologicalEvent, something changes venous blood into arterial blood.")
(comment SomeSituationAlternating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$SomeSituationAlternating, something goes back and forth; swings back and forth between two states or conditions.")
(comment InterchangeTwoThings "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$InterchangeTwoThings, someone causes something to change places with something else.")
(comment VascularizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BiologicalEvent. In each #$VascularizingSomething, something makes something vascular.")
(comment DecrepitateSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HeatingProcess. In each #$DecrepitateSomething, someone roasts or calcines something so as to cause it to crackle or until crackling stops.")
(comment CracklingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$CracklingSomething, something becomes, or is caused to become, covered with a network of small cracks.")
(comment SuburbanizingSomePlace "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$SuburbanizingSomePlace, something makes some place suburban in character.")
(comment ModulatingAWaveform "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$ModulatingAWaveform, something varies the frequency, amplitude, phase, or other characteristic of (electromagnetic waves).")
(comment AvianizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BiologicalEvent. In each #$AvianizingSomething, someone modifies microorganisms by repeated culture in the developing chick embryo.")
(comment RevolutionizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$RevolutionizingSomething, something changes radically.")
(comment EtiolatingSomething-BiologicalEvent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BiologicalEvent. In each #$EtiolatingSomething-BiologicalEvent, something bleaches and alters the natural development of (a green plant) by excluding sunlight.")
(comment BarbarizingSomeone "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$PhysiologicalConditionType. In each #$BarbarizingSomeone, someone is made crude or savage in behavior or speech.")
(comment AlkalinizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$AlkalinizingSomething, something makes (a substance) alkaline.")
(comment reasonableTrafficableRouteToFor "<code>(#$reasonableTrafficableRouteToFor PATH OBJ AGT)</code> means that <code>PATH</code> is a reasonable route for <code>AGT</code>, between <code>OBJ</code> and <code>AGT</code>. For example, if one were planning to drive a car from Dallas to Los Angeles for no other purpose than to arrive in L.A., it would not make sense to detour through Panama or Canada: reasonabl;e routes would mainly be on trafficable roads mainly east and south of L.A. and mainly west and north of Dallas (since L.A. is to the west and north of Dallas).")
(disjointWith CuttingSomething Drying)
(disjointWith CuttingSomething ComputerProcessRunning)
(disjointWith CuttingSomething RegulatingGasFlow)
(disjointWith GivingSomething AttackOnObject)
(disjointWith GivingSomething HostileSeizure)
(disjointWith BaseballContact HostileSeizure)
(disjointWith BaseballContact CriminalAct)
(disjointWith AttackByComputerOperation TakingHostage)
(disjointWith PurposefulAction Condensation)
(disjointWith CuttingSomething BouncingAnObject)
(comment GeopoliticalEntity "A specialization of #$Organization and of #$LegalAgent and of #$GeographicalAgent; instances of this collection control #$GeographicalRegions.  Each instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity includes a governing body, but is more than just that governing body.  
<p>
Important subcollections include #$Country, #$IndependentCountry, #$State-Geopolitical, #$City, and #$Province.  Instances include #$CityOfTokyoJapan, #$BronxNY-Borough, #$Alaska-State, #$Rwanda, #$Singapore, #$InnerMongolia, #$Somerset-CountyEngland, and #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina.  
<p>
A central feature of this collection is that geopolitical-entities (indeed, all  #$GeographicalAgents) are viewed in two significantly different ways with respect to two different types of geography-related microtheories.  In a \"physical\" geography microtheory (i.e. #$PhysicalGeographyMt and its submicrotheories), geopolitical-entities are clearly distinguished from the regions they control.  (#$TerritoryFn <b>GEO-POL</b>) is used in these contexts to denote the land mass (a #$GeopoliticalRegion) of a given geopolitical-entity <b>GEO-POL</b>.  In a \"dualist\" geography microtheory (i.e. #$DualistGeopoliticalMt and its submicrotheories), on the other hand, geopolitical-entities are viewed as being <i>both</i> agents <i>and</i> land masses (i.e. #$GeographicalRegions).  Thus, there is little need for #$TerritoryFn in the latter sort of context.  (Despite their somewhat paradoxical flavor, dualist microtheories arguably allow Cyc to mimic commonsense reasoning about geopolitical entities and regions more closely than do the stricter physicalist microtheories.)  There are also some \"generic\" geography microtheories (e.g. #$WorldGeographyMt and #$UnitedStatesGeographyMt) which are neutral with respect to the physical and dualist views.  
<p>
Also see the shared-note for this constant.")
(comment trafficableForAgent "(#$trafficableForAgent PATH AGENT) means that AGENT is #$behaviorCapable playing the role of #$performedBy with respect to the
class of instances of #$Movement-TranslationEvent wherein the
PATH has the role #$motionPathway-Partial.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity OpeningPresents)
