(comment ProceedingByStepsIntoANewSituation "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GeneralizedTransfer. In each #$ProceedingByStepsIntoANewSituation, something moves or proceeds as if by steps into a new situation.")
(comment amongThosePresent "This is the active present tense version of #$attendees.  (#$amongThosePresent GATHERING ATTENDEE) is true during TIME, to granularity PAR, if and only if ATTENDEE is actually in attendance at the social gathering GATHERING, throughout TIME to granularity PAR.")
(comment attendees "An instance of #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$SocialGathering to the individuals who attend(ed) that gathering.  To represent attendance-at-a-gathering with temporal qualification, use #$amongThosePresent.")
(comment paraphraseRootMtForLanguage "(#$paraphraseRootMtForLanguage MT LANG) means that MT is the most general instance of #$ParaphraseDataMicrotheory that is specific to the #$NaturalLanguage, LANG.")
(comment iGBackgroundKnowledgeSentences "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$InformationGathering to a (quoted) instances of #$CycLSentence.  (#$iGBackgroundKnowledgeSentences IG SENT) means that the performer of IG goes into IG knowing that SENT is true, and that the purpose of IG, at least in part, is to discover further facts related to the fact that SENT is true.")
(comment NullSpaceRegion-1D "A specialization of #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.) and #$OneDimensionalThing.  #$NullSpaceRegion-1D is the collection of one-dimensional \"null spatial regions\".  There is at most one known instance of #$NullSpaceRegion-1D with respect to any context in which some #$SpaceLines (q.v.) are known to have locations, either absolutely or relatively (see #$LocationalPredicate and its immediate specializations).
<p>
By definition, a 1-D null space region is disconnected from (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions) every 1-D homogeneous space region (i.e. #$SpaceLine), and is the #$spaceRegionComplement of the 1-D \"spatial universe\" (see #$UniversalSpaceRegion-1D).
<p>
The introduction of 1-D null regions into #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory helps to allow the functions #$SpaceRegionComplementFn, #$SpaceRegionProductFn, and #$SpaceRegionDifferenceFn to be defined as #$TotalFunctions.  For example, #$SpaceRegionComplementFn can then be defined on instances of #$UniversalSpaceRegion-1D (q.v.), and #$SpaceRegionProductFn can be defined for pairs of one-dimensional regions that are #$discreteSpaceRegions.  (Also see the comment on #$NullSpaceRegion.)
<p>
See also #$NullSpaceRegion-2D and #$NullSpaceRegion-3D.")
(comment NullSpaceRegion-3D "A specialization of #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.) and #$ThreeDimensionalThing.  #$NullSpaceRegion-3D is the collection of three-dimensional \"null spatial regions\".  There is at most one known instance of #$NullSpaceRegion-3D with respect to any context in which some #$SpaceChunks (q.v.) are known to have locations, either absolutely or relatively (see #$LocationalPredicate and its immediate specializations).
<p>
By definition, a 3-D null space region is disconnected from (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions) every 3-D homogeneous space region (i.e. #$SpaceChunk), and is the #$spaceRegionComplement of the 3-D \"spatial universe\" (see #$UniversalSpaceRegion-3D).
<p>
The introduction of 3-D null regions into #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory helps to allow the functions #$SpaceRegionComplementFn, #$SpaceRegionProductFn, and #$SpaceRegionDifferenceFn to be defined as #$TotalFunctions.  For example, #$SpaceRegionComplementFn can then be defined on instances of #$UniversalSpaceRegion-3D (q.v.), and #$SpaceRegionProductFn can be defined for pairs of three-dimensional regions that are #$discreteSpaceRegions.  (Also see the comment on #$NullSpaceRegion.)
<p>
See also #$NullSpaceRegion-1D and #$NullSpaceRegion-2D.")
(comment LanguageSpecificConceptualUnderspecificationMicrotheory "The collection of instances of #$Microtheory that contain rules for drawing inferences from underspecified representations that reflect grammatical and syntactic properties of a particular language.")
(comment conceptualUnderspecificationMtForLanguage "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that is functional in both argument-places.  #$conceptualUnderspecificationMtForLanguage relates an instance of  #$LanguageSpecificConceptualUnderspecificationMicrotheory to the instance of #$NaturalLanguage that it is specific to.")
