(comment Vasectomy "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Surgery. In each #$Vasectomy, someone removes the vas deferens.")
(comment AutoclavingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$SterilizingSomething. In each #$AutoclavingSomething, someone subjects something to the action of an autoclave.")
(comment AfflictingSomething "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$HurtingSomething-IndisposedCondition. In each #$AfflictingSomething, something causes bodily suffering to something.")
(comment Obstipation "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$Constipation. In each #$Obstipation, something constipates severely.")
(comment Exhaustion "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$FatigueCondition. In each #$Exhaustion, someone wears out completely.")
(comment Overtired "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$FatigueCondition. In each #$Overtired, someone tires excessively.")
(comment Ligation "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BandagingSomething. In each #$Ligation, someone binds something with a bandage or ligature.")
(comment DopingARacehorse "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DopingSomeone. In each #$DopingARacehorse, someone dopes (a racehorse).")
(comment Intoxication "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$Poisoning. In each #$Intoxication, something has an intoxicating effect on some animal, of a drug.")
(comment Hamstringing-CripplingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CripplingSomeone. In each #$Hamstringing-CripplingSomeone, someone cripples someone else by cutting the hamstring.")
(comment MythologizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$MythologizingSomething, someone makes something into a myth.")
(comment AllegorizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$AllegorizingSomething, something makes something else into an allegory.")
(comment SemiProperSpaceRegion "A specialization of #$CompositeSpaceRegion (q.v.).  A #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion is an instance of #$SemiProperSpaceRegion if and only if it has another homogeneous extended space region as a tangential proper part (#$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion).
<p>
Cf. #$ProperSpaceRegion.")
(comment StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion "A subcollection of #$SemiProperSpaceRegion (q.v.).  A homogeneous extended space region is an instance of #$StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion if and only if it has a tangential proper part (see #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion) but does <i>not</i> have any <i>non</i>tangential proper parts (see #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion).  This collection is coextensional with the collection-difference of #$SemiProperSpaceRegion and #$ProperSpaceRegion (q.v.).
<p>
Note that #$ScatteredSpaceRegion is a specialization of #$StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion in #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsVocabularyMt.")
(comment skinOfSpaceRegion "A binary predicate that relates a space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to its \"skin\" in the sense used in the extension of #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory in which atoms are introduced (see #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsMt).  Intuitively, the skin of a space region can be thought of as its one-atom-thick outermost layer or external surface.
<p>
More precisely, <code>(#$skinOfSpaceRegion SKIN REGION)</code> means that, for any space region <b>ANYREGION</b>, <b>ANYREGION</b> is connected to (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) to <b>SKIN</b> if and only if <b>ANYREGION</b> is connected to an #$AtomicSpaceRegion that is a #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion <b>REGION</b>. 
<p> 
See also the corresponding function #$SkinOfSpaceRegionFn.")
(comment identityPreservedUnder "A binary predicate and specialization of #$closedUnder that relates a given #$SetOrCollection to any unary function that behaves as an identity function on it.  <code>(#$identityPreservedUnder SETORCOL FUNC)</code> means that <code>FUNC</code> takes each element <code>ELEM</code> of <code>SETORCOL</code> to <code>ELEM</code> itself.
<p>
For example, #$RoundDownFn is an identity function on #$Integer but not on #$RationalNumber; #$IdentityFn is an identity function on #$Thing.")
(comment ScatteredSpaceRegion "A specialization of #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion (q.v.) and (in #$RCCWithAtomicRegionsVocabularyMt) #$StrictlySemiProperSpaceRegion (q.v.).  This is the collection of scattered, or \"totally disconnected\", space regions.  A homogeneous extended space region is an instance of #$ScatteredSpaceRegion if and only if (i) it is a #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion and (ii) is such that each of its parts (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) is itself either a scattered region or an #$AtomicSpaceRegion (q.v.).
<p>
Whether a given space region is considered as a #$ScatteredSpaceRegion or merely as a #$DisconnectedSpaceRegion may be a matter of context.  For example, with respect to a map on which the stage-cities of the <i>Tour de France</i> are marked with colored dots, the spatial sum of the cities might be viewed as a scattered region; but the French postal service is more likely to view that sum of cities as a partly disconnected region made up of various #$ProperSpaceRegions.")
(comment UserDataMicrotheory "The collection of all instances of #$Microtheory that contain user-specific data.  ")
(comment infoGatheredAbout "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an instance of #$InformationGathering to a #$Thing.  (#$infoGatheredAbout IG THING) means that THING is one of the things about which information is gathered in IG.")
(comment infoGatheredAbout-Primary "A #$BinaryPredicate and specialization of #$infoGatheredAbout and #$topicOfInfoTransfer that relates an instance of #$InformationGathering to a #$Thing.  (#$infoGatheredAbout-Primary IG THING) means that gathering information about THING is one of the primary aims of IG.  Contrast this with #$infoGatheredAbout-Secondary.")
(comment CycTermChooserModule "A #$ComputerProgramModule-CW, the #$CycTermChooserModule conducts a dialog with the user to search for (quoted) instances of #$CycLConstant for the construction of instances of #$CycLFormula.")
(comment CycTermChooserDialogProcess "A #$FirstOrderCollection and a sub-collection of #$GraphicalUserInterfaceProgramRunning, this is the collection of all events in which the #$CycTermChooserModule is providing a dialog interface with some user for the purpose of editing a #$CycLFormula.")
(comment instrumentalAIS "An expression of the form (#$instrumentalAIS ACT AIS) means that the #$AbstractInformationStructure AIS played an instrumental role in the #$Action ACT in the sense of somehow being 'used.' For example, in an instance of #$UsingTheQueryLibraryTool instances of #$KEInteractionFolder (a sub-collection of #$AbstractInformationStructure) can be loaded in the tool to refer to #$CycLQuerySpecifications.")
(comment inputString "An assertion of the form (#$inputString ITE STRING) means that the #$InformationTransferEvent ITE took the #$CharacterString STRING as an input.  For instance, in an instance of #$SyntacticParsing the string that is being parsed would play this role in that event.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByActivityType AcademicDepartmentTypeBySubject)
(comment iGPertinentFCTForType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$FacetingCollectionType to a #$Collection.  (#$iGPertinentFCTForType FCT COL) means that when an instance of #$InformationGathering IG bears #$infoGatheredAbout to an instance INST of COL, then for any instance SPEC of FCT, (#$isa INST SPEC) is pertinent (in the sense of #$iGPertinentSentences) to IG.")
(comment iGPertinentSentences-Closed "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$InformationGathering to a (quoted) instance of #$CycLClosedSentence.  (#$iGPertinentSentences-Closed IG SENT) means the same thing as:
<pre>
(#$and
  (#$iGPertinentSentences IG SENT)
  (#$quotedIsa SENT #$CycLClosedSentence))
</pre>
See also #$iGPertinentSentences-Open.")
(comment iGPertinentSentences-Open "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$InformationGathering to a (quoted) instance of #$CycLOpenSentence.  (#$iGPertinentSentences-Open IG SENT) means the same thing as:
<pre>
(#$and
  (#$iGPertinentSentences IG SENT)
  (#$quotedIsa SENT #$CycLOpenSentence)).
</pre>
See also #$iGPertinentSentences-Closed.")
(comment manpowerAndPersonnelOfficer "A functional role that an agent plays with respect to a
military unit.  The #$manpowerAndPersonnelOfficer is responsible for
insuring that the unit has the manpower and personnel necessary to
perform its assigned task.")
(comment SpatialThingTypeByNumberOfDimensions "A #$TotallyOrderedCollectionType and a specialization of #$SpatialThingTypeByDimensionality; a collection of collections of spatial things.  Each instance of #$SpatialThingTypeByNumberOfDimensions is a subcollection of #$SpatialThing (q.v.) consisting of all and only those things having the same particular number of spatial dimensions.  Instances of this collection include #$ZeroDimensionalThing, #$OneDimensionalThing, #$TwoDimensionalThing, and #$ThreeDimensionalThing.")
(comment RCCBinaryPredicate "A specialization of #$SpaceRegionPredicate.  This is the collection of the fifteen binary predicates defined solely in terms of #$connectedSpaceRegions in the #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory (qq.v.).  For a list of all fifteen instances, see the \"Arg 2\" #$isa assertions on this collection and its specialization #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight (q.v.).  
<p>
Note that it is <i>not</i> the case that every #$RCCConstant that denotes a binary predicate is an #$RCCBinaryPredicate.")
(comment partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse "An #$RCCBinaryPredicate (q.v.) and the inverse of #$partOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION SUBREGION)</code> means that <code>REGION</code> has <code>SUBREGION</code> as a part, in the sense that every #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion that connects (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) with <code>SUBREGION</code> connects with <code>REGION</code>. 
<p>
#$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse is \"partitioned into\" the three specializations: #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse, #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and
#$identicalSpaceRegions.  
<p>
Note that #$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse is the relation called <i>P<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.")
(comment AbandoningASituation "A first-order collection and sub-collection of #$EndingASituation.  #$AbandoningASituation represents a generic form of intentionally stopping a subsuming #$Situation from holding with the implication that the goals or purposes of that larger #$Situation were not realized.  For instance, consider a person who is digging a well and decides to stop that process and perform some other action. The action that constitutes  stopping the digging would be an instance of this collection.")
(comment Omnivore "A specialization of #$Heterotroph (q.v.) and an instance of #$OrganismClassificationType.  Instances of #$Omnivore are those animals whose natural diets consist of both plants (or plant parts or plant-derived products) and animals (or animal parts or animal-derived products).  Thus a human vegetarian is still omnivorous, since meat is part of our \"natural\" diet.  Specializations of this collection include #$Pig, #$Bear-Animal, and #$Person. See also #$Herbivore and #$Carnivore.")
(comment HasPositionRelationship "A specialization of #$InterAgentSituation-TwoAgent. Each instance of this collection is a specific relationship between a #$Person(s) and an #$Organization whereby the former fills a position at the latter. See also #$jobAgreement.")
(comment Cl2Molecule "A specialization of #$Molecule. Each instance of #$Cl2Molecule is a binary chlorine molecule.")
(comment N2Molecule "A specialization of #$Molecule.  Each instance of
#$N2Molecule is a binary nitrogen molecule.")
(comment cycLInputs "An expression of the form (#$cycLInputs CREATE CYCL) means that during the instance of #$IBOCreation CREATE, the quoted instance of #$CycLExpression CYCL was brought into the process at the very beginning and used to some end.  For instance, the formulas contained in instances of #$TKBBuilderQuery are intended to plays this role in an instance of #$ComposingACycQuery. Contrast with #$cycLIntroduced.")
(comment cycLIntroduced "An expression of the form (#$cycLIntroduced  EDIT EXPRESSION) means that the quoted #$CycLExpression EXPRESSION is brought into the instance of #$EditingAnElectronicDocument EDIT at some point after the start of the event.  For instance, during an instance of #$UsingTheQueryLibraryTool, a user might edit the query query (#$isa #$Muffet ?TYPE) to replace the #$CycLVariable ?TYPE with the #$CycLConstant #$Dog.  In that event, #$Dog would play the role of #$cycLIntroduced.  Since instances of #$CycLExpression are abstract and, so, cannot be created or destroyed, this predicate allows us to refer to the expression itself via quotation.  Contrast with #$cycLInputs.  In the example case of editing the query, the #$CycLExpression (#$isa #$Muffet ?TYPE) would play the role of #$cycLInputs since it was an actor from the very beggining of the process. ")
(comment AutogeneratedLeviathanQuery-Uncrippled "The subcollection of #$AutogeneratedLeviathanQuerys that have not been crippled.  These ought to all be answerable, at least in proof-checker mode.")
(disjointWith AutogeneratedLeviathanQuery-Uncrippled AutogeneratedLeviathanQuery-Crippled)
(comment AutogeneratedLeviathanQuery-Crippled "The subcollection of #$AutogeneratedLeviathanQuerys that have been crippled by removing an antecedent literal needed to prove the implication.  These ought to all be unanswerable, at least with reasonable resource constraints.")
(comment Criminologist "The collection of all criminologists, a sub-collection of #$Psychologists who are knowledgeable regarding #$Criminology.")
(comment FlowingContinously "A sub-collection of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance is the act of flowing or streaming; continuous progression.")
(comment Drizzle-RainProcess "A sub-collection of #$RainProcess.  Each instance is a very light rain; stronger than mist but less than a shower.")
(comment Downpour-RainProcess "A sub-collection of #$RainProcess.  Each instance is a heavy rain.")
(comment Fire-CombustionProcess "A sub-collection of #$CombustionProcess.  Each instance is the process of combustion of inflammable materials producing heat and light and (often) smoke.")
(comment SettingSomethingOnFire "A sub-collection of #$ActionOnObject.  Each instance is the act of setting something on fire or something catching fire.")
(comment tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion "An asymmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that is a specialization of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that (i) <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional), (ii) <code>REGION1</code> is a proper part of <code>REGION2</code>, and (iii) there is some space region that externally connects with (see #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions) both <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.
<p>
For example, the space occupied by Texas is a tangential proper part of that occupied by the US, while the space occupied by Oklahoma is a <i>non-</i>tangential proper part of the US-space.

Note that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion and #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion together make a partition of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion.  And see the inverse of the former, #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.
<p>
Note that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>TPP</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.")
(comment nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion "An asymmetric transitive #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that is a specialization of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion and a logical <i>contrary</i> (i.e. #$negationPreds) of #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that (i) <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional), (ii) <code>REGION1</code> is a proper part of <code>REGION2</code>, and (iii) there is <i>no</i> space region that externally connects with (see #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions) both <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.
<p>
For example, the space occupied by Oklahoma is a non-tangential proper part of that occupied by the US, while the space occupied by Texas is a <i>tangential</i> proper part of the US-space.
<p>
Note that #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion and #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion together make a partition of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion.  And see the inverse of the former, #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.
<p>
Note also that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>NTPP</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.")
(comment AutogeneratedHaystackQuery "The collection of all automatically generated \"needle in a haystack\" style of deep inference queries.")
(comment AutogeneratedLeviathanQuery "The collection of all queries created by Project Leviathan's automatic deep inference generator, and actually used as one of the corpora for Project Leviathan.")
(comment KBContentLeviathanQuery "The collection of all instances of #$CycLQuerySpecification that are 'deep-required', i.e. they specify a transformation depth of 2 or more, and were empirically verified to be unanswerable with a transformation depth of 1.")
(disjointWith KBContentLeviathanQuery AutogeneratedLeviathanQuery)
(comment Breveting-PromotingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomeone. In each #$Breveting-PromotingSomeone, someone promotes somebody by brevet, in the military.")
(comment PromotingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ShowingSupportForSomeone. In each #$PromotingSomething, something contributes to the progress or growth of something.")
(comment Undergirding-ShowingSupportForSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ShowingSupportForSomeone. In each #$Undergirding-ShowingSupportForSomeone, someone lends moral support to something.")
(comment Backing-ShowingSupportForSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ShowingSupportForSomeone. In each #$Backing-ShowingSupportForSomeone, someone gives support or their approval to something.")
(comment SwindlingAnAgent "A sub-collection of #$Fraud.  Each instance is the act of swindling by some fraudulent scheme.")
(comment BilkingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Cheating. In each #$BilkingSomeone, someone cheats somebody out of what is due, especially money.")
(comment BeatingSomething-Cheating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Cheating. In each #$BeatingSomething-Cheating, someone avoids paying.")
(comment WhipsawingSomeone-Cheating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Cheating. In each #$WhipsawingSomeone-Cheating, someone victimizes someone else, especially in gambling or negotiations.")
(comment HoodwinkingSomeone-Cheating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Cheating. In each #$HoodwinkingSomeone-Cheating, someone influences someone else by slyness.")
(comment CorruptingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$CorruptingSomeone, someone corrupts someone else morally or by intemperance or sensuality.")
(comment GoverningSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HumanActivity. In each #$GoverningSomething, someone exercises authority over something; as of nations.")
(comment FallingBackOnSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$UsingAnObject. In each #$FallingBackOnSomething, someone has recourse to something.")
(comment ParolingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ReleasingFromConfinement. In each #$ParolingSomeone, someone releases a criminal from detention and places him on parole.")
(comment SocialGroup "A sub-collection of #$Group.  Each instance is a group of people sharing some social relation.")
(comment Gathering-SocialGroup "A sub-collection of #$SocialGroup.  Each instance is a group of persons together in one place.")
(comment Multitude-SocialGroup "A sub-collection of #$Gathering-SocialGroup.  Each instance is a large gathering of people.")
(comment Horde "A sub-collection of #$Multitude-SocialGroup.  Each instance is a vast multitude.")
(comment Fagging-ServingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ServingSomeone-HelpingAnAgent. In each #$Fagging-ServingSomeone, someone acts as a servant for older boys, in British public schools.")
(comment ExercisingAuthoritativeControlOverSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ControllingSomething. In each #$ExercisingAuthoritativeControlOverSomething, something exercises authoritative control or power over something.")
(comment RelaxingTheStrictnessOfSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$RelaxingTheStrictnessOfSomething, some agent makes something less severe or strict.")
(comment SlamDunking-AffectingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$AffectingSomething. In each #$SlamDunking-AffectingSomething, something makes a forceful move against something.")
(comment BorderingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$TouchingEvent. In each #$BorderingSomething, something lies adjacent to another or shares a boundary.")
(comment NeighboringSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BorderingSomething. In each #$NeighboringSomething, something is located near or adjacent to something else.")
(comment Rustication-SystemCondition "A sub-collection of #$SystemCondition.  Each instance is the condition naturally attaching to life in the country.")
(comment RedefiningSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Specifying. In each #$RedefiningSomething, someone gives a new or different definition to something.")
(comment Bridging-ConnectingTogether "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ConnectingTogether. In each #$Bridging-ConnectingTogether, something connects or reduce the distance between something.")
(comment nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse "An asymmetric transitive #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that is a specialization of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and the inverse (see #$elInverse) of #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that (i) <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional), (ii) <code>REGION1</code> has <code>REGION2</code> as a proper part, and (iii) there is <i>no</i> space region that externally connects with (see #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions) both <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.
<p>
For example, the space occupied by the US has that occupied by Oklahoma as a non-tangential proper part, but has the space occupied by Texas as a <i>tangential</i> proper part (see #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse).
<p>
Note that #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse together make a partition of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.
<p>
Note also that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>NTPP<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.")
(comment tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse "An asymmetric #$RCCBinaryPredicate-BaseEight that is a specialization of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and the inverse (see #$elInverse) of #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that (i) <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are space regions (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegions) of the same dimensionality (see #$spatiallyEquidimensional), (ii) <code>REGION1</code> has <code>REGION2</code> as a proper part, and (iii) there is some space region that externally connects with (see #$externallyConnectedSpaceRegions) both <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code>.
<p>
For example, the space occupied by the US has that occupied by Texas as a tangential proper part, but has that occupied by Oklahoma as a <i>non-</i>tangential proper part.
<p>
Note that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse and #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse together make a partition of #$properPartOfSpaceRegion-Inverse. 
<p>
Note also that #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>TPP<sup>-1</sup></i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.")
(comment LeviathanQuery-Blind "The collection of all queries that are part of some blind test suite for Project Leviathan.  These queries are not permitted to be analyzed until the end of the project.")
(disjointWith LeviathanQuery-Training LeviathanQuery-Blind)
(disjointWith SetOrCollectionDenotingFunction IndividualDenotingFunction)
(comment SetOrCollectionDenotingFunction "The subcollection of #$Function-Denotational whose instances, when applied to any appropriate (sequence of) argument(s) on which they are defined, always return instances of #$SetOrCollection.  Instances of this collection include #$SetOrCollectionDifferenceFn.  Notable specializations include  #$CollectionDenotingFunction and #$SetDenotingFunction.")
(comment partOfSpaceRegion "An #$RCCBinaryPredicate (q.v.) that is a specialization of #$overlappingSpaceRegions, #$parts, and #$spatiallySubsumes. <code>(#$partOfSpaceRegion SUBREGION REGION)</code> means that <code>SUBREGION</code> is a part of <code>REGION</code> in the sense that every #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion that connects (see #$connectedSpaceRegions) with <code>SUBREGION</code> connects with <code>REGION</code>. 
<p>
#$partOfSpaceRegion is \"partitioned into\" the three specializations: #$tangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion, #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion and
#$identicalSpaceRegions.  See also #$partOfSpaceRegion-Inverse.
<p>
Note that #$partOfSpaceRegion is the relation called <i>P</i> in #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory.")
(comment FlocculatingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$FlocculatingSomething, something causes something else to become a fluffy or lumpy aggregate.")
(comment TurningSomethingIntoSomethingElse "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$TurningSomethingIntoSomethingElse, something causes something to change or turn into something different; assumes new characteristics.")
(comment BringingAboutSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CreationEvent. In each #$BringingAboutSomething, something makes something possible.")
(comment MakingSomethingPossible "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$MakingSomethingPossible, something makes something else accessible or possible.")
(comment ResidingTemporarilyAtSomeDwellingPlace "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DwellingInAPlace. In each #$ResidingTemporarilyAtSomeDwellingPlace, someone resides temporarily in some dwelling place.")
(comment IllegallyOccupyingADwellingPlace "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DwellingInAPlace. In each #$IllegallyOccupyingADwellingPlace, someone occupies (a dwelling) illegally.")
(comment SomeAnimalsOverpopulatingAPlace "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DwellingInAPlace. In each #$SomeAnimalsOverpopulatingAPlace, some animals cause a place to have too great a population.")
(comment KeepingSomething-RaisingLivingThings "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$RaisingLivingThings. In each #$KeepingSomething-RaisingLivingThings, someone raises living things.")
(comment Lodging "A sub-collection of #$DwellingInAPlace.  Each instance is the act of staying temporarily in a place.")
(comment ShelteringSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MakingSomethingAvailable. In each #$ShelteringSomething, something provides shelter for something.")
(comment SomeRainSprinkling "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$RainProcess. In each #$SomeRainSprinkling, something rains gently.")
(comment Sheeting-Downpour "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Downpour-RainProcess. In each #$Sheeting-Downpour, some rain comes down as if in sheets.")
(comment Sluicing-Downpour "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Downpour-RainProcess. In each #$Sluicing-Downpour, some rain pours as if from a sluice.")
(comment BlowingOut-SettingSomethingOnFire "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$SettingSomethingOnFire. In each #$BlowingOut-SettingSomethingOnFire, something erupts in an uncontrolled manner.")
(comment LightingUp-SettingSomethingOnFire "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$SettingSomethingOnFire. In each #$LightingUp-SettingSomethingOnFire, something starts to burn with a bright flame.")
(comment Flare-CombustionProcess "A sub-collection of #$Fire-CombustionProcess.  Each instance is a sudden burst of flame.")
(comment Blaze-Fire "A sub-collection of #$Fire-CombustionProcess.  Each instance is a strong flame that burns brightly.")
(comment incorrectlyParsedSentence "(#$incorrectlyParsedSentence SENTENCE) means that a reviewer who looked at the #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE felt that the information the sentence expresses is incorrectly parsed from a text source or a text sentence.  For example, (#$objectFoundInLocation #$KuKluxKlan #$BillingsMustangs-BaseballTeam) is an incorrect parse of 'Ku Klux Klan was located in Billings'.  Whether the sentence is correctly/incorrectly parsed depends on a reviewer's subjective judgement, the context within which the claim is being made, and what other information is available to the system.  Also see #$correctlyParsedSentence.")
(comment WordNetWorkflowConstant "The collection of all #$CycLConstants created from the import of concepts from #$WordNet-Version2_0.")
(comment WordNetWorkflowConstant-NotFullyReviewed "The collection of all #$CycLConstants created from the import of concepts from #$WordNet-Version2_0 that have not yet been fully reviewed by a #$HumanCyclist.")
(comment WordNetWorkflowConstant-ScaffoldingGAFsOK "The collection of all #$CycLConstants created from the import of concepts from #$WordNet-Version2_0 that have been reviewed by a #$HumanCyclist who edited and approved the concept's scaffolding assertions.")
(comment PhysicalFeaturePredicate "An instance of #$PredicateType.  Each instance of #$PhysicalFeaturePredicate relates certain #$SpatialThings (q.v.) either to one or more of their physical features (see e.g. the specialization #$PhysicalFeatureBinaryPredicate) or to other spatial things to which they bear certain spatial or physical relations (see e.g. the specialization #$ConnectionPredicate).  Instances of #$PhysicalFeaturePredicate include #$above-Directly, #$physicallyContains, #$touches-Directly, #$temperatureOfObject, and #$spans-Bridgelike.")
(comment touches-Externally "An instance of #$RelativeLocationalPredicate and a specialization of both #$touches-Directly and #$spatiallyDisjoint (qq.v.).  <code>(#$touches-Externally REGION1 REGION2)</code> means that <code>REGION1</code> and <code>REGION2</code> are #$SpatialThings that are directly touching, but do not share any spatial parts.")
(comment BringingOneself-CoercingAnAgent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CoercingAnAgent. In each #$BringingOneself-CoercingAnAgent, someone causes theirself to undertake a certain action, usually used in the negative.")
(comment Inconveniencing-AffectingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$AffectingSomething. In each #$Inconveniencing-AffectingSomething, someone causes inconvenience or discomfort to someone else.")
(comment Branding-MarkingOnASurface "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MarkingOnASurface. In each #$Branding-MarkingOnASurface, someone burns some animal with a branding iron to indicate ownership.")
(comment Regulating-SelectingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$SelectingSomething. In each #$Regulating-SelectingSomething, something brings something into conformity with rules or principles or usage; imposes regulations.")
(comment MakingReparationsForSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. In each #$MakingReparationsForSomething, someone makes reparations or amends for something.")
(comment ControllingSomething-Experimenting "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Experimenting. In each #$ControllingSomething-Experimenting, someone verifies or regulates by conducting a parallel experiment or compares with another standard, of scientific experiments.")
(comment FailingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Evaluating. In each #$FailingSomething, someone judges something unacceptable.")
(comment Enterprise-Project "A sub-collection of #$Project.  Each instance is a purposeful or industrious undertaking (especially one that requires effort or boldness).")
(comment DiscussingSomethingTenatively "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Experimenting. In each #$DiscussingSomethingTenatively, someone circulates or discusses something tentatively; tests the waters with something.")
(comment FieldTestingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Experimenting. In each #$FieldTestingSomething, someone tests something under the conditions under which it will actually be used.")
(comment DemocratizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PoliticalAction. In each #$DemocratizingSomething, someone introduces democratic reforms; of nations.")
(comment NeutralizingSomething-PoliticalAction "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PoliticalAction. In each #$NeutralizingSomething-PoliticalAction, someone makes some entity politically neutral and thus inoffensive.")
(comment DominatingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ExercisingAuthoritativeControlOverSomething. In each #$DominatingSomething, someone has dominance or the power to defeat over something.")
(comment UndertakingSomething-Accept "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Accept. In each #$UndertakingSomething-Accept, someone accepts something as a charge.")
(comment ValetingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ServingSomeone-HelpingAnAgent. In each #$ValetingSomeone, someone serves as a personal attendant to someone.")
(comment DecoratingSomeone-GivingAnAward "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GivingAnAward. In each #$DecoratingSomeone-GivingAnAward, someone awards a mark of honor, as a medal, to someone.")
(comment BenefactingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HelpingAnAgent. In each #$BenefactingSomething, someone helps something as a benefactor.")
(comment Subservience "A sub-collection of #$SystemCondition.  Each instance is the condition of being something that is useful in reaching an end or carrying out a plan.")
(comment SuccoringSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HelpingAnAgent. In each #$SuccoringSomeone, someone helps someone else in a difficult situation.")
(comment ExpeditingSomething-HelpingAnAgent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HelpingAnAgent. In each #$ExpeditingSomething-HelpingAnAgent, someone speeds up the progress of something; facilitates.")
(comment AvailingSomething-HelpingAnAgent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HelpingAnAgent. In each #$AvailingSomething-HelpingAnAgent, something is of use to, is useful to something.")
(comment Caregiving "A sub-collection of #$WorkingEvent.  Each instance is the work of caring for or attending to someone or something.")
(comment Salvation "A sub-collection of #$RescuingSomeone.  Each instance is a saving someone or something from harm of from an unpleasant situation.")
(comment SalvagingSomething "A sub-collection of #$CommercialActivity.  Each instance is the act of saving goods or property that were in danger of damage or destruction.")
(comment ReprievingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$RescuingSomeone. In each #$ReprievingSomeone, someone relieves someone else temporarily.")
(comment Bootstrapping-HelpingAnAgent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HelpingAnAgent. In each #$Bootstrapping-HelpingAnAgent, someone helps theirself, often through improvised means.")
(comment DiscipliningSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Punishing. In each #$DiscipliningSomeone, someone punishes someone else in order to gain control or enforce obedience.")
(comment FosteringSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomething. In each #$FosteringSomething, something promotes the growth of something.")
(comment Spurring-PromotingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomething. In each #$Spurring-PromotingSomething, something incites or stimulates something.")
(comment Helping-PromotingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomething. In each #$Helping-PromotingSomething, something contributes to the furtherance of something.")
(comment Carrying-PromotingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomething. In each #$Carrying-PromotingSomething, someone takes something further or advances something.")
(comment Feeding-PromotingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomething. In each #$Feeding-PromotingSomething, something supports or promote something.")
(comment Contributing-PromotingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomething. In each #$Contributing-PromotingSomething, something is conducive to something.")
(comment armedWithWeapon "(#$armedWithWeapon AGENT WEAPON) means that #$IntelligentAgent AGENT is armed with #$Weapon WEAPON.")
(disjointWith Communicating AttackOnObject)
(comment SpatialThingPredicate "A specialization of #$SpatialPredicate (q.v.).  This is the collection of general spatial predicates that can be used to relate #$SpatialThings of all sorts (and only spatial things).  Thus, any asserted #$argIsa constraint on a #$SpaceRegionPredicate should be to #$SpatialThing itself  (and <i>not</i> to any specialization or generalization of that). Typically, a #$SpatialThingPredicate will also be a binary #$RelativeLocationalPredicate.
<p>
Instances of #$SpatialThingPredicate include #$spatiallySubsumes, #$cospatial, and #$touches-Directly.")
(disjointWith SpaceRegionPredicate SpatialThingPredicate)
(disjointWith SpatialThingPredicate ConnectionPredicate)
(comment Throne-GoverningSomething "A sub-collection of #$GoverningSomething.  Each instance is the position and power of one who occupies a throne.")
(comment ShortChangingSomeone "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$Swindle-TheWord. In each #$ShortChangingSomeone, someone cheats someone by not returning him enough money.")
(comment InfectingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CorruptingSomeone. In each #$InfectingSomething, something contaminates something else with ideas or an ideology.")
(comment LeadingOff-CorruptingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CorruptingSomeone. In each #$LeadingOff-CorruptingSomeone, someone teaches immoral behavior to someone.")
(comment Whoring-CorruptingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CorruptingSomeone. In each #$Whoring-CorruptingSomeone, someone corrupts someone else by lewd intercourse.")
(comment Poisoning-CorruptingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CorruptingSomeone. In each #$Poisoning-CorruptingSomeone, someone spoils something as if by poison.")
(comment Bastardizing-CorruptingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CorruptingSomeone. In each #$Bastardizing-CorruptingSomeone, someone changes something so that its value declines; for example, art forms.")
(comment SuborningSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CorruptingSomeone. In each #$SuborningSomeone, someone incites someone else to commit a crime or an evil deed.")
(comment MisgoverningSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$CorruptingSomeone. In each #$MisgoverningSomething, someone governs badly.")
(comment Dictating-GoverningSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GoverningSomething. In each #$Dictating-GoverningSomething, someone rules  as a dictator.")
(comment dateOfDeathEvent "#$dateOfDeathEvent is a predicate which is intended to be as neutral as possible with respect to various views regarding  life after death and reincarnation.
<p>
There are three main sorts of things, as well as subabstractions of them, which might be said to have a date of death: entities which are Organisms-Whole, entities which are some sort of spiritual thing, and entities which are some kind of composite of the two. In all three cases, the #$dateOfDeathEvent will be the date at which the #$Organism-Whole, or the associated #$Organism-Whole, undergoes a #$Dying event. The #$dateOfDeathEvent of a subabstraction of any of the three would be the #$dateOfDeathEvent of the entity of which it is a subabstraction.
<p>
In #$NaturalismMt only organisms can have a date of death; and every organism
has a single such date.
<p>
There are different rules in #$SpiritualistMt.  In the case of resurrection, an organism can have multiple #$dateOfDeathEvents, but only a single birth event.  In the case of life after death, a soul exists past the death of a body in which it is incarnated.  In the case of reincarnation, a spiritual entity can have multiple #$dateOfDeathEvents, at least one for each incarnation.
<p>
#$dateOfDeathEvent jibes with common sense talk about death, wherein believers in life after death are willing to assert both that Grandpa is in heaven and that Grandpa died on such and such a date.  Of course, this relates to metonomy between the organism, the body, and the soul.  The assertions mean that Grandpa's soul is in heaven, while his body and the Homo sapiens that used to be identified with Grandpa are both dead.
<p>
Note the difference between this predicate and #$dateOfDeath, which ascribes to entities their #$endingDate.")
(comment AttendingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HumanActivity. In each #$AttendingSomething, someone is present at (meetings, church services, university), etc..")
(comment EntailingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BringingAboutSomething. In each #$EntailingSomething, something imposes, involves, or implies something else as a necessary accompaniment or result.")
(comment NecessitatingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BringingAboutSomething. In each #$NecessitatingSomething, something causes something else to be a concomitant.")
(comment HerdingSomeAnimals "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$KeepingSomething-RaisingLivingThings. In each #$HerdingSomeAnimals, someone keeps, moves, or drives animals.")
(comment Sleepover-SocialGathering "A sub-collection of #$SocialGathering.  Each instance is an occasion of spending a night away from home or having a guest spend the night in your home (especially as a party for children).")
(comment InhabitingSomething "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$OccupyingTheWholeOfSomething. In each #$InhabitingSomething, something is present in something else; is inside of something else.")
(comment Harboring-ShelteringSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ShelteringSomething. In each #$Harboring-ShelteringSomething, someone secretly shelters someone else (as of fugitives or criminals).")
(comment ShuttingOffSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DiscontinuingAnActivity. In each #$ShuttingOffSomething, something stems the flow of something.")
(comment Breaking-DiscontinuingAnActivity "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DiscontinuingAnActivity. In each #$Breaking-DiscontinuingAnActivity, someone gives up something.")
(comment ImbricatingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PuttingSomethingSomewhere. In each #$ImbricatingSomething, someone places something so as to overlap.")
(comment EndangeringSomething "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$SomethingExisting. In each #$EndangeringSomething, something poses a threat to something; presents a danger to something.")
(comment RetainingSomethingWithin "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$ContainingSomething. In each #$RetainingSomethingWithin, something holds something else within.")
(comment LiningUp-ArrangingObjects "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ArrangingObjects. In each #$LiningUp-ArrangingObjects, something forms a line.")
(comment StraddlingSomething "A sub-collection of #$Translation-NoLocationChange.  Each instance is the act of sitting or standing astride.")
(comment Siding-SelectingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$SelectingSomething. In each #$Siding-SelectingSomething, someone takes the side of something; is on the side of something.")
(comment Keeping-ProtectingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ProtectingSomething. In each #$Keeping-ProtectingSomething, someone maintains something in safety from injury, harm, or danger.")
(comment FurnishingSomeoneWithAHat "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MakingSomethingAvailable. In each #$FurnishingSomeoneWithAHat, someone furnishes someone with a hat.")
(comment EnfeoffingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$TransferringPossession. In each #$EnfeoffingSomeone, someone puts something else in possession of land in exchange for a pledge of service, in feudal society.")
(comment ThemingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MakingSomethingAvailable. In each #$ThemingSomething, someone provides something with a particular theme or motive.")
(comment SweepingSomethingUnderTheRug "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HidingAnObjectByMovingIt. In each #$SweepingSomethingUnderTheRug, someone conceals something in the hopes it won't be discovered by others.")
(comment MilitaryBattle "A sub-collection of #$Battle.  Each instance is a hostile meeting of opposing military forces in the course of a war.")
(comment SecessionEvent "A sub-collection of #$SeparationEvent.  Each instance is a formal separation from an alliance or federation.")
(comment Retiring-DiscontinuingAnActivity "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DiscontinuingAnActivity. In each #$Retiring-DiscontinuingAnActivity, someone withdraws from active participation in some activity.")
(comment InitiationCeremony "A sub-collection of #$Ceremony.  Each instance is a formal entry into an organization or position or office.")
(comment ReadmitingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$AdmitToMembership. In each #$ReadmitingSomeone, someone is admitted again or anew into an organization.")
(comment FillingAJob "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$EmployeeHiring. In each #$FillingAJob, someone appoints someone to (a position or a job).")
(comment WorkingAsASubstituteForSomeone "A sub-collection of #$ReplacingAnObject.  Each instance is someone working as a substitute for someone else who is ill or on leave of absence.")
(comment Covering-ProtectingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ProtectingSomething. In each #$Covering-ProtectingSomething, someone takes an action to protect something against future problems.")
(comment PackingAGroupWithOnesSupporters "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$FoundingAnOrganization. In each #$PackingAGroupWithOnesSupporters, someone sets up a committee or legislative body with their own supporters so as to influence the outcome.")
(comment AppointingSomeoneSummarily "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$FoundingAnOrganization. In each #$AppointingSomeoneSummarily, someone appoints someone else summarily; commandeers.")
(comment TenuringSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomeone. In each #$TenuringSomeone, someone gives life-time employment to someone.")
(comment PromotingSomeoneFromALowerPosition "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomeone. In each #$PromotingSomeoneFromALowerPosition, someone promotes someone else from a lower position or rank.")
(comment SpotPromotingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomeone. In each #$SpotPromotingSomeone, someone promotes someone else on the spot.")
(comment EnnoblingSomeone "A sub-collection of #$PromotingSomeone.  Each instance is the act of raising someone to the nobility.")
(comment PreferringSomething "A sub-collection of #$PromotingSomeone.  Each instance is the act of preferring someone for a position.")
(comment PreferringACreditor "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Paying. In each #$PreferringACreditor, someone gives preference to one creditor over another.")
(comment VotingInACandidate "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ElectionForOffice. In each #$VotingInACandidate, someone elects some candidate in a voting process.")
(comment CoOption-Election "A sub-collection of #$Election.  Each instance is the selection of a new member (usually by a vote of the existing membership).")
(comment ReelectionForOffice "A sub-collection of #$ElectionForOffice.  Each instance is an election again to the previous position.")
(comment EngagingSomeone-EmployeeHiring "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$EmployeeHiring. In each #$EngagingSomeone-EmployeeHiring, someone asks someone else to represent them; of legal counsel.")
(comment ForcingOutAnEmployee "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DischargeWithPrejudice. In each #$ForcingOutAnEmployee, someone forces out an employee.")
(comment SqueezingOutSomeEmployee "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DischargeWithPrejudice. In each #$SqueezingOutSomeEmployee, something forces out some employee.")
(comment Usurping-ReplacingAnObject "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ReplacingAnObject. In each #$Usurping-ReplacingAnObject, something takes the place of something else.")
(comment Ousting-ReplacingAnObject "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ReplacingAnObject. In each #$Ousting-ReplacingAnObject, something removes and replaces something else.")
(comment ImplementingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$UsingAnObject. In each #$ImplementingSomething, someone applies something in a manner consistent with its purpose or design.")
(comment HiringForWorkOnAShip "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$EmployeeHiring. In each #$HiringForWorkOnAShip, someone hires someone else for work on a ship.")
(comment EmployingStrikeBreakers "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$EmployeeHiring. In each #$EmployingStrikeBreakers, someone employs scabs or strike breakers.")
(comment CollaboratingWithTheEnemy "A sub-collection of #$CooperationEvent.  Each instance is an act of cooperating traitorously with an enemy that is occupying one's country.")
(comment GivingOnesSilientApprovalToSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PromotingSomething. In each #$GivingOnesSilientApprovalToSomething, someone gives their silent approval to something.")
(comment BailingSomeoneOutOfConfinement "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ReleasingFromConfinement. In each #$BailingSomeoneOutOfConfinement, someone releases someone else after a security has been paid.")
(comment Reinstatement "A sub-collection of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  Each instance is the condition of being brought back into original existence, use, function, or position.")
(comment Imprinting "A sub-collection of #$Learning.  Each instance is a learning process in early life whereby species specific patterns of behavior are established.")
(comment NonRechargeableBattery "Batteries which may not be recharged (cf. #$ChargingABattery).")
(comment pretendingTo "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a specialization of #$Action to a specialization of #$Pretending.  (#$pretendingTo ACT-TYPE PRETEND-TYPE) means that PRETEND-TYPE is the collection of all #$Pretendings in which someone pretends to perform an instance of ACT-TYPE.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$PretendingToFn (q.v.).")
(comment PretendingToFn "A reifiable, collection-denoting #$UnaryFunction that takes a specialization of #$Action and returns the collection of all instances of #$Pretending in which someone pretends to perform an instance of that type of action.  For example (#$PretendingToFn #$Reading) is the collection of all events in which someone pretends to read.  See also #$PretendingThatFn.")
(comment pretendingThat "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a (quoted) instance of #$CycLSentence-Assertible to a specialization of #$Pretending.  (#$pretendingThat SENT PRETEND-TYPE) means that PRETEND-TYPE is the collection of all #$Pretendings in which someone pretends that SENT is true.  This is the predicate corresponding to #$PretendingThatFn (q.v.).")
(comment PretendingThatFn "A reifiable, collection-denoting #$UnaryFunction that takes a (quoted) instance of #$CycLSentence-Assertible and returns the collection of all #$Pretending in which someone pretends that SENT is true.  For example (#$PretendingThatFn (#$isa #$Bob #$King-HeadOfState)) is the collection of all events in which someone pretends that Bob is a king.  See also #$PretendingToFn.")
(comment Militating-InfluencingAnAgent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$InfluencingAnAgent. In each #$Militating-InfluencingAnAgent, something has force or influence over something else; brings about an effect or change in something else.")
(comment Reign "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GoverningSomething. In each #$Reign, someone has sovereign power.")
(comment Addressing-GreetingSomeone "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GreetingSomeone. In each #$Addressing-GreetingSomeone, something greets someone else as with a prescribed form, title, or name.")
(comment Unionization "A sub-collection of #$FoundingAnOrganization.  Each instance is an act of forming labor unions.")
(comment OrganizationsAffiliatingWithEachOther "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$OrganizationalTransferIn. In each #$OrganizationsAffiliatingWithEachOther, some organization joins in an affiliation with another organization.")
(comment RejoiningAnOrganization "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$OrganizationalTransferIn. In each #$RejoiningAnOrganization, someone joins an organization again.")
(comment stateHasUSRepresentatives "A predicate that identifies the US Representatives of a given US State.")
(comment stateHasUSSenators "A predicate that identifies the US Senators of a given US State.")
