(disjointWith PoliticalElectionCampaignEvent Election)
(comment PoliticalElectionCampaignEvent "A specialization of #$PoliticalEvent.  This is the collection of election campaigns and the major sub-events that go into running and executing one.")
(comment orgHasProfessingKeyMemberType "(#$orgHasProfessingKeyMemberType ORG MEMBER-TYPE) means that any person who is an instance of MEMBER-TYPE functions as a 'key' member of the organization who professes, and who is required in virtue of their 'key' position to profess, whatever belief system is the #$officialBeliefSystem of ORG.")
(comment agentTypeImpliesBeliefSystem "(#$agentTypeImpliesBeliefSystem AGT-TYPE BELIEF) means that where AGT is any instance of the agent classification type AGT-TYPE, (#$hasBeliefSystems AGT BELIEF).")
(comment TypedSpecPredWithArgSignatureFn "A binary #$PredicateDenotingFunction that takes an <code>N</code>-ary predicate <code>PRED</code> and an <code>N</code>-length list of collections to a predicate that is a typed-specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of <code>PRED</code>, such that each of its argument-places is restricted (beyond the constraints it inherits from <code>PRED</code>) to instances of the respective collection in the list.
<p>
If <code>PRED</code> is an <code>N</code>-ary #$Predicate and <code>ARG-SIGN-LIST</code> an <code>N</code>-length list of #$Collections such that no collection in the list is disjoint with (any of) the #$argIsa -constraint(s) on the corresponding argument-place of <code>PRED</code>, then 
(#$TypedSpecPredWithArgSignatureFn <code>PRED ARG-SIGN-LIST</code>) is the <code>N</code>-ary predicate <code>SPEC</code> such that:
<pre>
  1. PRED is a #$typedGenlPreds of SPEC.
  2. Any #$argIsa or #$argGenl constraint on PRED also holds of the corresponding argument-place of SPEC.
  3. For each member COL<sub>I</sub> of ARG-SIGN-LIST, (#$argIsa SPEC I COL<sub>I</sub>) holds.
</pre>
For example, (#$TypedSpecPredWithArgSignatureFn #$objectStartingDate (#$TheList #$Animal #$Date)) is the predicate #$birthDate.
<p>
As the example shows, a given <code>COL<sub>I</sub></code> might be the same as, or a proper specialization of (see #$genls), an #$argIsa constraint on the <code>I</code>th place of <code>PRED</code>.
<p>
Note that the term <code>(#$TypedSpecPredWithArgSignatureFn PRED ARG-SIGN-LIST)</code> is #$undefined if either (i) the #$lengthOfList of <code>ARG-SIGN-LIST</code> differs from the #$arity of <code>PRED</code> or (ii) 
any of the <code>COL<sub>I</sub></code> in <code>ARG-SIGN-LIST</code> is #$disjointWith any collection <code>CONSTRAINT</code> such that <code>(#$argIsa PRED I CONSTRAINT)</code> holds.
<p>
See also the corresponding predicate #$typedGenlPredWithArgumentSignature.")
(comment typedGenlPredWithArgumentSignature "A ternary predicate that relates a fixed-ary predicate to a typed-specialization of it to a list of collections, such that each of the more specialized predicate's argument-places is restricted (beyond the constraints it inherits from the more general predicate) to instances of the corresponding collection in the list.
<p>
More precisely, <code>(#$typedGenlPredWithArgumentSignature SPECPRED GENLPRED ARG-SIGN-LIST)</code> is true only if all of the following hold:
<pre>
  1. GENLPRED is a #$typedGenlPreds of SPECPRED.
  2. The #$lengthOfList of ARG-SIGN-LIST is equal to the #$arity of both GENLPRED and SPECPRED. 
  3. No member COL<sub>I</sub> of ARG-SIGN-LIST is #$disjointWith any collection CONSTRAINT such that (#$argIsa GENLPRED I CONSTRAINT) holds.
  4. For each member COL<sub>I</sub> of ARG-SIGN-LIST, (#$argIsa SPECPRED I COL<sub>I</sub>) holds.
</pre>
For example, <code>(#$typedGenlPredWithArgumentSignature #$birthDate #$objectStartingDate (#$TheList #$Animal #$Date))</code> holds.
As this shows, a given <code>COL<sub>I</sub></code> might be the same as, or a proper specialization of (see #$genls), an #$argIsa constraint on the <code>I</code>th place of <code>GENLPRED</code>.
<p>
In practice, <code>SPECPRED</code> is defined using the corresponding function #$TypedSpecPredWithArgSignatureFn.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact EcologicalRegion)
(comment Village-Deserted "A specialization of #$GeographicalRegion.  Each instance of #$Village-Deserted is a region that was previously the #$territoryOf a #$Village that has since been deserted.")
(comment objectIDSubschema "(#$objectIDSubschema ODS SET) means that the values taken on by list of indexical denoting terms SET serve together to uniquely determine the idobject of the object that instantiates the #$ObjectDefiningSchema ODS; that is, the membership of SET covaries with ODS instantiations (a change in instantiation entails that at least one field in SET changes its value, and vice versa) and SET is specified as the list of fields intended to uniquify the instantiating object.  This presupposes that every #$elementOf of SET is a #$LogicalField, and #$objectField of the #$ObjectDefiningSchema.")
(comment CommercialPaper "A specialization of #$UnsecuredLoan.  Instances are loan agreement issued by corporations, usually maturing in a very short time (9 months).")
(comment defaultEquivSubSitTypes "This #$SituationTypeRelation expresses a relation that holds between the prescribed substructures of two situations, conditional on one situation being a #$properSubSituations of the other. (#$defaultEquivSubSitTypes SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2 SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2) means that where SIT1 is an instance of SIT-TYPE1 and SIT2 is an instance of SIT-TYPE2 such that (#$properSubSituations SIT1 SIT2), any instance of SUBSIT-TYPE2 that is a #$properSubSituations of SIT2 will be identical with any instance of SUBSIT-TYPE1 that is an #$properSubSituations of SIT1, barring evidence to the contrary.  This is a very strong condition, even for a default, but there are cases for which it is warranted.  For example, consider #$MurderForHire and #$Murder.  It is true that every #$MurderForHire subsumes a #$Murder as a #$properSubSituations.  It is also reasonable to assume that any #$Murder includes a #$Dying as a #$subEvent.  Other things being equal, the default assumption should be that any #$Dying which is known to occur as a proper subsituation of a #$Murder is identical with any #$Dying that is known to occur as a proper subsituation of a #$MurderForHire of which the #$Murder is a part:  thus, (#$defaultEquivSubSitTypes #$MurderForHire #$Murder #$Dying #$Dying).")
(comment defaultSubsumptiveSubSitTypes "This #$SituationTypeRelation expresses a relation that holds between the prescribed substructures of two situations, conditional on one situation being a #$properSubSituations of the other.  More specifically, (#$defaultSubsumptiveSubSitTypes SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2 SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2) means that where SIT1 is an instance of SIT-TYPE1 and SIT2 is an instance of SIT-TYPE2 such that (#$properSubSituations SIT1 SIT2), any proper subsituation of SIT2 that is an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE2 will be a #$subSituations (not necessarily a #$properSubSituations) of any instance of SIT1 that is an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE1.  For example, suppose that a #$HostileSeizure occurs as part of a #$MilitaryOperation, and that it is generally the case that (#$candidateProperSubSituationTypes #$HostileSeizure (#$AcquiringFn #$Weapon)) and also that (#$candidateProperSubSituationTypes #$MilitaryOperation (#$AcquiringFn #$MilitaryHardware)).  It stands to reason that in a #$MilitaryOperation which includes a #$HostileSeizure as a #$properSubSituations, any (#$AcquiringFn #$Weapon) that occurs as part of the seizure should be regarded as a subsituation of any (#$AcquiringFn #$MilitaryHardware) that occurs as part of the #$MilitaryOperation, provided there is no evidence to the contrary;  e.g. evidence that the hardware-aquisition qua military op doesn't temporally subsume the weapon acquisition qua seizure.")
(comment PersonWithoutAVisa "The collection of all persons who are in a country or that country's territorial waters, are not citizens of that country, and do not have a travel visa.")
(comment TradeableSecurityTypeByListingStatus "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType that partitions #$TradeableSecurity into two classes: #$ExchangeTradedSecurity, the collection of securities traded on an official exchange, and #$UnlistedSecurity, the collection of securities that are not so traded.")
(comment UnlistedSecurity "The collection of instances of #$TradeableSecurity that are not traded on an official exchange.")
(comment marketTypeDefiningProductType "<code>(#$marketTypeDefiningProductType MARKET-TYPE TYPE)</code> identifies <code>MARKET-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$Market that are markets for <code>TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$TemporallyExistingThing.  That is, every instance of <code>MARKET-TYPE</code> is characterized by the buying and selling of instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  By definition, <code>MARKET-TYPE</code> is an instance of #$MarketTypeByFocalProductType.")
(comment defaultBaseLexicalMt "<code>(#$defaultBaseLexicalMt LEXICON MT)</code> means that the content of lexical assertions visible from <code>MT</code> are included in LEXICON unless their mts are explicitly excluded from LEXICON (see #$disallowedLexicalMt).")
(comment TrafficObstructionDevice "A specialization of #$ManMadeObstacle and #$PhysicalDevice. Each instance of #$TrafficObstructionDevice is a physical device used to guide or block automobile traffic.  Important specializations include #$TrafficCone and #$TrafficBarrel.")
(comment Obstacle "A specialization of #$EnduringThing-Localized. Each instance of #$Obstacle is a tangible object that can, when suitably situated, impede movement from one place to another.")
(disjointWith PortableObstacle FixedObstacle)
(comment FixedObstacle "A specialization of #$Obstacle and #$Place (qq.v).  Each instance of #$FixedObstacle that is in a fixed location and which is therefore difficult for an average human to move.")
(comment PortableObstacle "A specialization of #$PortableObject and #$Obstacle (qq.v.). Each
instance of #$PortableObstacle is a tangible object that can, (1) when
suitably situated, impede movement from one place to another, and
(2) is light enough for an average human to move easily.")
(comment HumanlyInsurmountableObstruction "A specialization of #$Obstacle (q.v.).  Each instance
of #$HumanlyInsurmountableObstruction is a tangible object that a typical
#$HumanAdult cannot, without aid from technology, pass directly over, through, or under.")
(comment Pit-AirFilled "A specialization of #$Pit-Topographical (q.v.).  Each instance of
#$Pit-AirFilled is a pit that is mainly full of air.")
(comment PanelConstructionBarricadeWithLowestPanelRemoved "A specialization of #$ConstructionBarrier (q.v). Each instance of #$PanelConstructionBarricade is a construction barricade construced of panels of wood.")
(comment TrafficConeBarrierWithLowestBarRemoved "A specialization of #$Barrier-ConstructionArtifact and #$HumanlyHurdlableObject
(qq.v).  Each instance of #$TrafficConeBarrier is a small barrier constructed by placing a bar across the top of two or more traffic cones (see #$TrafficCone).")
(comment ElectricalHazard "A specialization of #$DangerousTangibleThing (q.v.).  Each instance of
#$ElectricalHazard is a hazardous object that treatens to electrocute people who touch it.")
(comment AmmunitionPack "A specialization of #$StorageConstruct and #$PortableObject (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$AmmunitionPack is a container used to store ammunition for projectile weapons.")
(comment FAETestSpecification "The collection of #$KBContentTests created for the Cyc Financial Analyst Environment (or FAE).")
(comment join-left "#$join-left is an #$ELRelation-OneWay designed to approximate a SQL left join in CycL.  It is a #$VariableArityPredicate whose arguments are #$CycLSentence-Askables.  <code>(#$join-left ARG1 ARG2 ... ARGN)</code> expands into a disjunction of increasingly long conjunctions of initial segments of its arguments: <code>(#$or ARG1 (#$and ARG1 ARG2) ... (#$and ARG1 ARG2 ... ARGN))</code>.  So a #$join-left sentence is true just in case some non-empty initial segment of its arguments is true ")
(comment FAEQueryLibraryQuery "The subcollection of #$CycLQuerySpecifications which are not intended to be asked by themselves, but instead are intended to be combined with other builder queries or otherwise added to or constrained.")
(comment FAEQueryLibraryQuery "The collection of instances of #$CycLQuerySpecification that make up the queries of the FAE.")
(disjointWith ObjectDefiningSchema RelationshipDefiningSchema)
(comment RelationshipDefiningSchema "The collection of all #$LogicalSchemas that express relationships between a set of entities. The schemas for the entities are #$ObjectDefiningSchemas.")
(comment FAEQuery-NeedsSanityTest "The collection of queries that were created for (or are used in) the Financial Analyst Environment (FAE), and which need to have corresponding KB content tests which provide a \"sanity check\" for their bindings.")
(comment FAERegressionTest "The collection of #$FAETestSpecifications that are to be used in FAE regression testing.")
(comment MarketTypeByFocalProductTypeFn "<code>(#$MarketTypeByFocalProductTypeFn TYPE)</code> denotes the an instance of  #$MarketTypeByFocalProductType.  In particular, it denotes the collection of all instances of #$Market, each instance of which is defined by the buying and selling of <code>TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$SomethingExisting.")
(comment ObstacleTypeBySizeDimensionRelativeToHuman "A specialization of #$ExistingObjectType.  Each instance of #$ObstacleTypeBySizeDimensionRelativeToHuman is a specialization of #$Obstacle whose instances, in turn, share a general size along a particular dimension relative to humans.  For example, one instance of #$ObstacleTypeBySizeDimensionRelativeToHuman is #$Obstacle-TallWRTHuman.  Each instance of that collection is an obstcle that is tall relative to a human (such obstacle would, generally, be to big to jump onto the top of).")
(comment Obstacle-WideWRTHuman "A specialization of #$Obstacle.  Each instance of #$Obstacle-WideWRTHuman is an object that impedes human movement and which is too wide for a typical human to jump over or to simply duck under. See also #$Obstacle-NarrowWRTHuman.")
(comment Obstacle-NarrowWRTHuman "A specialization of #$Obstacle.  Each instance of #$Obstacle-NarrowWRTHuman is an object that impedes human movement but which a typical human could probably jump over or simply duck under.  Compare with #$Obstacle-WideWRTHuman")
(disjointWith Obstacle-WideWRTHuman Obstacle-NarrowWRTHuman)
(comment Obstacle-DeepWRTHuman "A specialization of #$Obstacle.  Each instance of #$Obstacle-DeepWRTHuman is an object that impedes human movement and which is too deep for a typical human to easily pull themselves out of or stand in and breathe (if the obstacle is filled, e.g. with water). Cf. #$Obstacle-ShallowWRTHuman.")
(comment Obstacle-ShallowWRTHuman "A specialization of #$Obstacle.  Each instance of #$Obstacle-ShallowWRTHuman is an object that impedes human movement and which is too deep for a typical human to easily jump or pull themselves out of or stand in and breathe (if the obstacle is filled, e.g. with water). Cf. #$Obstacle-ShallowWRTHuman.")
(disjointWith Obstacle-DeepWRTHuman Obstacle-ShallowWRTHuman)
(comment Obstacle-TallWRTHuman "A specialization of #$Obstacle.  Each instance of #$Obstacle-TallWRTHuman is an object that impedes human movement and which is too tall for a typical human to jump onto or pull themselves up to the top of. Cf. #$Obstacle-ShortWRTHuman.")
(comment Obstacle-ShortWRTHuman "A specialization of #$Obstacle.  Each instance of #$Obstacle-TallWRTHuman is an object that impedes human movement and which is short enough for a typical human to jump onto or pull themselves up to the top of. Cf. #$Obstacle-TallWRTHuman.")
(disjointWith Obstacle-TallWRTHuman Obstacle-ShortWRTHuman)
(comment Obstacle-WithHumanSizedGapUnderneath "A specialization of #$Obstacle.  Each instance of #$Obstacle-WithHumanSizedGapUnderneath is an object that impedes human movement yet which has a low gap large enough enough for a typical human to crawl through.")
(disjointWith Obstacle-HumanlyGrippableToTop Obstacle-HumanlyNonGrippableToTop)
(comment ObjectSturdyWRTHumanActivity "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$ObjectSturdyWRTHumanActivity is difficult for a human to break using tools commonly available.")
(disjointWith ObjectFragileWRTHumanActivity ObjectSturdyWRTHumanActivity)
(comment Pit-WaterFilled "A specialization of #$Pit-Topographical (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Pit-WaterFilled is a pit that is filled at least nearly to the top
with water.")
(comment Pit-DeepWaterFilled "A specialization of #$Pit-WaterFilled (q.v.).  Each instance of
#$Pit-DeepWaterFilled is a pit that is both deep (too deep for a human
to stand in) and filled at least nearly to the top with water.")
(comment Obstacle-HumanlyNonGrippableToTop "A specialization of #$Obstacle (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Obstacle-HumanlyNonGrippableToTop is an object on which it is not possible for a typical adult humans to safely find hand-holds or foot-holds all the way from the bottom to the top. Cf. #$Obstacle-HumanlyGrippableToTop.")
(comment Obstacle-HumanlyGrippableToTop "A specialization of #$Obstacle (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Obstacle-HumanlyGrippableToTop is an object on which (all the way from the bottom to the top) typical adult humans can safely find hand-holds or foot-holds. Cf. #$Obstacle-HumanlyNonGrippableToTop.")
(comment HighTrafficBarrier "A specialization of #$TrafficObstructionDevice (qq.v).  Each instance of #$HighTrafficBarrier is a device that is intended to be used to block or redirect automobile traffic, and over which a typical adult human can climb but not jump.")
(comment HighConstructionBarrier "A specialization of #$ConstructionBarrier and #$HumanlyInsurmountableObstruction (qq.v). Each instance of #$HighConstructionBarrier is a construction artifact that is used to prevent access to a construction area.  Humans cannot pass over, under, or through such barriers without the aid of technology.")
(comment BarbedWireFence "A specialization of #$Fence (q.v.).  Each instance of #$BarbedWireFence is a fence made with #$BarbedWire.")
(comment HighBarbedWireFence "A specialization of #$BarbedWireFence (q.v.).  Each instance of #$HighBarbedWireFence is a tall fence made with #$BarbedWire.")
(comment HighMastBarricade "Each instance of #$HighMastBarricade is a tall barricade constructed from solid horizontal planks of wood, metal or plastic.  Instances of this collection are constructed to prevent humans form surmounting them.")
(comment HighConstructionBarrierWithLowGap "A specialization of #$ConstructionBarrier (q.v.).  Each instance of #$HighConstructionBarrierWithLowGap is a high construction barrier with a gap near the bottom that is large enough for a human to pass through.")
(comment ListMultiplicityListFn "<code>(#$ListMultiplicityListFn LIST)</code> returns a list of lists of length two, <code>LISTOFLISTS</code>, with the following property: The <code>N</code>th member of <code>LISTOFLISTS</code> is a list of the form <p>
<code>(#$TheList NTH-LIST-MEMBER M)</code><p>
where <code>NTH-LIST-MEMBER</code> is the <code>N</code>th member of <code>LIST</code> and <code>M</code> is the number of occurances of <code>NTH-LIST-MEMBER</code> in the sublist of <code>LIST</code> from <code>1</code> to <code>N</code>.")
(comment classifyingNodeInFilter "<code>(#$classifyingNodeInFilter NODE FILTER)</code> means that <code>NODE</code> is a useful collection for organizing concepts extracted from text or searches done in support of any task of type <code>TASK-TYPE</code> such that <code>(#$conceptNodeCollectionForTaskType FILTER TASK-TYPE)</code>.")
(comment RaisingRevenue "The collection of events in which the revenue (see #$revenue) of an agent is (successfully) raised.")
(comment IssuingASecurity "A specialization of #$MakingSomethingAvailable and (#$AttemptingFn #$RaisingRevenue).  Instances are the events in which instances of #$TradeableSecurity are offered for sale by the issuer (see #$securityIssuedBy).")
(comment securityIssuedBy "<code>(#$securityIssuedBy SECURITY AGENT)</code> means that <code>SECURITY</code> is an instance of #$TradeableSecurity issued by <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment IncomeMeasurePredicate "A collection of binary predicates.  Each instance is an instance of #$QuantitySlot that can be used to represent a measure of an agent's income.")
(comment IssuingADebtInstrument "A specialization of #$IssuingASecurity and (#$AttemptingFn #$FinancingByBorrowing).  Instances are events in which a legal agent (typically a corporation or government, issues securities representing promises of repayment; holders of such securities are thereby creditors (see #$agentHasCreditors) of the issuers.")
(comment highlyRelevantAssertion "A #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate. <code>(#$highlyRelevantAssertion ASSERTION)</code> states that the #$CycLAssertion <code>ASSERTION</code> should be heuristically considered highly relevant to inferences that are performed in a context in which <code>(#$highlyRelevantAssertion ASSERTION)</code> is visible.  See also other instances of #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate.")
(comment monthlyIncome "<code>(#$monthlyIncome AGENT AMOUNT)</code> means that the income (see #$income) for the instance <code>AGENT</code> of #$SocialBeing is <code>AMOUNT</code> per month.")
(comment thingHasSubStringInName "A helper relation that abbreviates a query for an individual based on a substring of their name.")
(comment queryIndirectRegressionTest "(#$queryIndirectRegressionTest QUERY TEST) means that the KB content test TEST is an indirect regression test on one or more bindings of QUERY.")
(comment FolderWithFinancialAnalysisQueriesForSuggestion "Instances of this collection are (abstract) folders which contain queries that may be useful as suggested queries for research.")
(comment FinancialAnalysisTask-Allotment "A specialization of #$Allotment that represents general financial analysis taskings.")
(comment FinancialAnalysisProcess "This constant is currently a stub.")
(comment CAEAnalysisTask "A specialization of #$Allotment that represents general analysis taskings.")
(comment MapFunctionOverListSet "A macro expanded evaluatable function, #$MapFunctionOverListSet is the composition of #$MapFunctionOverSet and #$MapFunctionOverList. If <code>FUNCTION</code> is a #$UnaryFunction and <code>LIST-SET</code> is a set of lists, i.e. an instance of <code>(#$SetOfTypeFn #$List)</code>, then <code>(#$MapFunctionOverListSet FUNCTION LIST-SET</code>) applies <code>FUNCTION</code> to each list member of each element of <code>LIST-SET</code> and returns a new set of lists. ")
(comment agentNetLoss "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate.  Net loss is merely the negative value of net income (see #$netIncome).  So if one has a net income of ($64K) one has a net loss of $64K.  Similarily, if one has a net income of $64K, on has a net loss of ($64K).  Natural language conventions are such that one does not typically talk of negative net losses, or of net losses at all, when the net income is positive.")
(comment relationshipPredicateList "This predicate is the #$predicateUnion of #$explicitRelationshipPredicateList and #$implicitRelationshipPredicateList.")
(comment AntiFn "A partial, unary function that takes a #$BeliefSystem to the  the belief system (if such exists) whose central and characteristic feature is opposition to the former.  For example, (#$AntiFn #$Capitalism) is the belief system of anti-capitalism: the belief system whose central and characteristic feature is opposition to capitalism.")
(comment ExplicitRelationshipDefiningSchemaFn "If <code>PREDICATE</code> is a #$Predicate and <code>ODS-LIST</code> is a list of #$ObjectDefiningSchemas, then <code>(#$ExplicitRelationshipDefiningSchemaFn PREDICATE ODS-LIST)</code> denotes the unique #$RelationshipDefiningSchema which is expressed in the Cyc ontology as logical sentences using <code>PREDICATE</code> and which relates the entities described by the members of <code>ODS-LIST</code>. Note that there are several well formedness conditions between the argument constraints on <code>PREDICATE</code> and the types of entities described by the members of <code>ODS-LIST</code> which must be met in order for the function to have a meaningful dentoatum.")
(comment ArtificialLanguage "A collection that includes all languages created by #$Agent-Generics.  Some examples are computer programming languages, constructed international languages like Esperanto and Ido, and languages of formal logic.  See also #$FormalLanguage.")
(comment FormalLanguage "A specialization of #$Language. Each instance of this collection is a language which is specified and/or created by (not just described by) some instance of #$FormalGrammar-CW.  Prime specializations of this collection are #$ComputerLanguage and #$MathematicalLanguage.  There is considerable overlap between this collection and #$ArtificialLanguage (languages that are created by agents, rather than having evolved), but whereas each constructed language must be constructed by an agent or agents, formal languages need not be.")
(disjointWith NaturalLanguage ArtificialLanguage)
(comment NaturalLanguage "A specialization of #$HumanLanguage and #$InformalLanguage.  Each instance of #$NaturalLanguage is a language that  is used for human communication, and which has evolved naturally.  #$NaturalLanguage is thus disjoint with #$ArtificialLanguage. Instances include dead languages such as Ancient Greek and Latin; but concocted languages such as Esperanto are not included.")
(comment InformalLanguage "A specialization of #$Language. A language is an instance of  #$InformalLanguage if and only if it is <i>not</i> a #$FormalLanguage; i.e. not specified or created by some instance of #$FormalGrammar-CW (q.v.).  A prime specialization of this collection is #$NaturalLanguage.  Note that an #$ArtificialLanguage (q.v.) might be formal or informal.")
(disjointWith InformalLanguage FormalLanguage)
(comment structureLanguages "<code>(#$structureLanguages STRUCTURE LANGUAGE)</code> means that textual portions of the instance <code>STRUCTURE</code> of #$GraphicalStructure are written in <code>LANGUAGE</code>, an instance of #$Language.  To talk about the primarly language of a structure, use #$structurePrimaryLanguage.")
(comment ComputerLanguage "A specialization of #$ArtificialLanguage-Formal.  Each instance of #$ComputerLanguage is designed expressly for the purpose of creating expressions that are in some sense interpretable by computers. This may mean that the expressions are used to program computers (for which, see the specialization #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage), to facilitate interaction between pieces of software, or to indicate how to represent pieces of text (for which, see #$MarkupLanguage). Machine and assembly languages are also included in this category.")
(comment Esperanto "The prototypical #$InternationalAuxiliaryLanguage, devised by L. L. Zamenhof and introduced in 1887.")
(comment Interlingua "A #$ConstructedHumanLanguage.")
(comment BasicEnglish "A #$ConstructedHumanLanguage.")
(comment commonShareholders "<code>(#$commonShareholders CORPORATION AGENT)</code> means that the instance <code>AGENT</code> of #$SocialBeing is a shareholder (see #$shareholders) in the legal corporation (see #$LegalCorporation) <code>CORPORATION</code> with at least one share of common stock (see #$CommonStock).  Common shareholders have voting rights in the companies whose stock they hold.")
(comment hasVotingRightsInOrganization "<code>(#$hasVotingRightsInOrganization AGENT ORGANIZATION)</code> means that the instance <code>AGENT</code> of #$SocialBeing is able to vote in (some) elections held by and affecting the organization <code>ORGANIZATION</code>.  This is a very general relation, and does not specify what kinds of elections or what kinds of affects these elections have, or the degree to which <code>AGENT</code>'s \"say\" in such an election matters from the perspective of the organization.")
(comment ConstructedHumanLanguage "A specialization of #$HumanLanguage, #$ArtificialLanguage-Informal, and #$DevisedStructuredActivity (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$ConstructedHumanLanguage is an artificially constructed language that can be used for everyday conversation.  The collection is thus disjoint with both #$NaturalLanguage and #$FormalLanguage.  Note, however, that a #$ConstructedHumanLanguage <i>might</i> evolve over time in a more-or-less \"natural\" manner, despite its artificial origin.")
(comment preferredShareholders "<code>(#$preferredShareholders CORPORATION AGENT)</code> means that the instance <code>AGENT</code> of #$SocialBeing is a shareholder (see #$shareholders) in the legal corporation (see #$LegalCorporation) <code>CORPORATION</code> with at least one share of preferred stock (see #$PreferredStock).  Unlike common shareholders (see #$commonShareholders and #$CommonStock), preferred shareholders (typically) do not have voting rights in the companies whose stock they hold.  However, they are entitled to a dividend and are ahead in line of common shareholders in case of liquidation (but behind creditors (see #$agentHasCreditors and #$bondHolders).")
(comment ConvertibleSecurity "The collection of instances of #$TradeableSecurity that contain an option (see #$subObligations and #$OptionTransactionAgreement) to covert the security into another security of a different type.")
(comment TradeableSecurityTypeByConvertibility "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType that partitions #$TradeableSecurity into two classes: #$ConvertibleSecurity, the collection of securities that contain an option (see #$OptionTransactionAgreement and #$subObligations) to convert that security into another security of a different type; and #$NonconvertibleSecurity, the collection of securities that do not contain any such option.")
(comment ConvertiblePreferredStock "A specialization of #$ConvertibleSecurity.  Each instance of #$ConvertiblePreferredStock is a share of preferred stock that can be converted at a later date into shares of common stock in the issuing company.")
(comment VisualWork "A specialization of #$ConceptualWork. Each instance of #$VisualWork is an abstract work that is intended to be instantiated in a medium that is experienced primarily visually. The textual component of an instance of #$VisualWork, if any, is secondary to its visual component.  Instances of #$VisualWork may contain textual components, but the content of an instance of #$VisualWork could not be completely expressed in text (thus a #$VisualWork is very unlikely to be a #$TextualPCW). Important specializations of #$VisualWork include #$VideoConceptualWork and #$VisualArtifact-CW.")
(disjointWith VisualWork AudioConceptualWork)
(comment schemaIntegrationPredicateForInputExplicitRDSSet "This relates a schema integration to a predicate and the set of explicitly defined relationship defining schemas relating source object defining schemas using the predicate. That is, <code>(#$schemaIntegrationPredicateForInputExplicitRDSSet INTEGRATION PREDICATE SOURCE-RDS-SET)</code> means that:<p>
1. <code>SOURCE-RDS-SET</code> is the set of explicitly defined #$RelationshipDefiningSchemas that state relationships between the input object defining schemas in <code>INTEGRATION</code>;<p>
2. <code>PREDICATE</code> is the predicate that states the meaning of the relationship between the participating object defining schemas.")
(comment schemaIntegrationTypeForInputExplicitRDSSet "This predicate relates each of the object schema types for a schema integration to the set of explicitly represented relationship defining schemas that relate some object defining schema of the given type. That is, <code>(#$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputExplicitRDSSet INTEGRATION TYPE RDS-SET)</code> means that in the schema integration <code>INTEGRATION</code>, each #$RelationshipDefiningSchema in the set <code>RDS-SET</code> relates some #$ObjectDefiningSchema of type <code>TYPE</code> (determined via #$schemaIsa). See also #$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputImplicitRDSSet.")
(comment schemaIntegrationTypeForInputImplicitRDSSet "This predicate relates each of the object schema types for a schema integration to the set of relationship defining schemas that implicitly relate (See #$ImplicitRelationshipDefiningSchemaFn) some object defining schema of the given type. That is, <code>(#$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputImplicitRDSSet INTEGRATION TYPE RDS-SET)</code> means that in the schema integration <code>INTEGRATION</code>, each #$RelationshipDefiningSchema in the set <code>RDS-SET</code> implicitly relates some #$ObjectDefiningSchema of type <code>TYPE</code> (determined via #$schemaIsa). See also #$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputExplicitRDSSet.")
(comment schemaIntegrationTypeForInputRDSSet "This predicate is the #$predicateUnion of #$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputExplicitRDSSet and #$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputImplicitRDSSet.")
(comment schemaIntegrationPredicateForInputRDSSet "This predicate is the predicateUnion of #$schemaIntegrationPredicateForInputExplicitRDSSet and #$schemaIntegrationPredicateForInputImplicitRDSSet.")
(comment Now-Indexical "#$Now-Indexical is the current time point. Whenever \"(#$IndexicalReferentFn #$Now-Indexical)\" is used in an assertion, that non-atomic term is replaced with an expression denoting the time of the assertion.
<p>
For example, if one were to assert this sentence at 2:30 p.m. on July 16, 2006:
<p>
<code>(#$awareOf #$BillClinton (#$IndexicalReferentFn #$Now-Indexical))</code>
<p>
the assertion that would be added to the kb would have this as its sentence:
<p>
<code>(#$awareOf #$BillClinton
           (#$MinuteFn 30
               (#$HourFn 14
                   (#$DayFn 16
                       (#$MonthFn July
                           (#$YearFn 2006))))))</code>
<p>
See also #$Now.")
(comment convertiblePreferredShareholders "<code>(#$convertiblePreferredShareholders CORPORATION AGENT)</code> means that the instance <code>AGENT</code> of #$SocialBeing is a shareholder (see #$shareholders) in the legal corporation (see #$LegalCorporation) <code>CORPORATION</code> with at least one share of convertible preferred stock (see #$ConvertiblePreferredStock).  Such shareholders have the option to convert their preferred shares for common shares (see #$CommonStock), giving them the ability to benefit from future increases in (common) stock prices while collecting dividends in the present.")
(comment ImageUniformResourceLocator "The collection of all instances of #$UniformResourceLocator that are urls for image files.")
(comment ImageURLFn "<code>(#$ImageURLFn STRING)</code> denotes the instance of #$ImageUniformResourceLocator whose corresponding pathname is the string <code>STRING</code>.")
(comment imageURLPathname "<code>(#$imageURLPathname URL STRING)</code> identifies <code>STRING</code> as the full pathname of the instance <code>URL</code> of #$ImageUniformResourcelocator.")
(comment urlPathname "<code>(#$uRLPathname URL STRING)</code> identifies <code>STRING</code> as the full pathname of the instance <code>URL</code> of #$UniformResourcelocator.")
(comment Now "#$Now is a special #$TimePoint: it is the current moment from the perspective of Cyc's inference engine.  If one asks <code>(#$indexicalReferent #$Now ?X)</code> the inference engine will return an answer in which ?X is bound to whatever the time is according to the central processing unit on which the inference engine is running.  Thus #$Now does not vary with the microtheoretical context in which one asks (#$indexicalReferent #$Now ?X).  Instead the referent of #$Now varies from moment to moment down to the resolution of #$Cyc's central processing unit. It is appropriate to use #$Now as the time interval that qualifies the context of  query. See also #$Now-Indexical, which is more appropriate to use with assertions than with queries.")
(comment explicitRelationshipPredicateList "A predicate that uniquely identifies an explicitly defined #$RelationshipDefiningSchema by a #$Predicate and a list of #$ObjectDefiningSchemas which correspond to the entities that participate in the relationship. <code>(#$explicitRelationshipPredicateList RDS PREDICATE ODS-LIST)</code> means that <code>RDS</code> is the logical schema that describes the relationship that holds between the entities described by the members of <code>ODS-LIST</code>. The relationship is expressed in the Cyc ontology as sentences using <code>PREDICATE</code>. The order of the #$ObjectDefiningSchemas in <code>ODS-LIST</code> determines the order in which the entities appear in <code>PREDICATE</code> sentences. In addition, there are several necessary conditions for <code>RDS</code>es to be well defined using this predicate. See also the corresponding function #$ExplicitRelationshipDefiningSchemaFn and the exceptions (#$exceptWhen meta assertions) on its generating rule.")
(comment schemaIntegrationPredicateForTargetExplicitRDS "This predicate is the analogue of #$schemaIntegrationTypeForTargetODS, however it relates a schema integration to a predicate and the relationship defining schema relating target object defining schemas using the predicate. That is, <code>(#$schemaIntegrationPredicateForTargetExplicitRDS INTEGRATION PREDICATE TARGET-RDS)</code> means that:<p>
1. <code>TARGET-RDS</code> is a #$RelationshipDefiningSchema that states a relationship between two or more target object defining schemas in <code>INTEGRATION</code>;<p>
2. <code>PREDICATE</code> is the CycL predicate that states the relationship between the object defining schemas participating in the relationship.")
(comment MarketTypeByFacilitatingVenueOrSystem "A second order collection and instance of #$FacetingCollectionType, #$MarketTypeByFacilitatingVenueOrSystem is the collection of all specialization of #$Market, each instance of which is such that its instances are faciliated by a common market venue or trading system, such as the New York Stock Exchange (see #$NewYorkStockExchange) or the OTC Bulletin Board Service (#$OTCBulletinBoardService).")
(comment MarketFacilitationVenueOrSystem "The collection of all \"markets\" <i>qua</i> organizations (such as the NYSE (see #$NewYorkStockExchange)) or systems for trading (e.g., NASDAQ (see #$NASDAQSecuritiesTradingSystem)) that serve to give structure to various markets.")
(disjointWith ConceptualWorkSeries-Periodic (CollectionDifferenceFn ConceptualWorkSeries ConceptualWorkSeries-Periodic))
(comment mtOfEvaluation "(#$mtOfEvaluation EVAL MT) holds just in case (#$thereExists ?OBJECT (#$ist MT (#$objectOfEvaluation EVAL ?OBJECT)))")
(comment corporateCompetitors "(#$corporateCompetitors COMPANY-1 COMPANY-2) means that COMPANY-1 and COMPANY-2 are direct competitors.")
(comment WedgeSurface "A specialization of #$PolyhedralSurface (q.v.).  Each instance of #$WedgeSurface is the two-dimensional, non-planar, unbounded surface of a #$Wedge (q.v.); it is the spatial sum of five flat externally-connected polygons, two of which are (mutually-congruent) #$Triangles and three of which are #$Rectangles.")
(disjointWith SmallBuilding LargeBuilding)
(comment IKRISTranslationLanguage "The collection of Languages that need to have their vocabulary and any structural differences mapped into CycL for the purposes of the IKRIS project.")
(comment |isit:Participants| "A variable arity predicate from the IKRIS scenario inner theory.  This predicate is designed to translate assertions made with fluents and holds, occurs, etc. into ICL.  The number of arguments it takes is determined by the orignal fluent predicate it was translated from plus one for the situation generated.  For example a sentence in the native KANI KB like this:

 <pre>(holds (ownerOf Bob Car01) April_1_2006)</pre> 

would be translated into ICL as 

<pre> (thereExists ?S 
       (and 
        (isa ?S kani:ownerOf)
        (t:during ?S kani:April_1_2006)
        (isit:Participants ?S Bob Car01)))</pre> 

This predicate has been recreated in CycL so we can convert sentences like the one above into proper CycL.  For example there will be support to convert the above ICL sentence into the CycL that follows:

<pre>  (thereExists ?S
        (and 
         (isa ?S OwningSomething)
         (ownerInSituation ?S Bob)
         (thingOwnedInSit ?S Car01)
         (temporallySubsumes (DayFn 1 (MonthFn April (YearFn 2006))) ?S)))</pre>



 
 .")
(comment keyStatsForMemberCorporation "(#$keyStatsForMemberCorporation SET-OR-COLL CORP CHANGE DV) holds just in case CORP is an instance of SET-OR-COLL and the change in stock price for CORP since last close is CHANGE and DV is the \"dollar value meaning it is the amount of money spent on CORP's stock on an average day.")
(comment Polyhedron "A specialization of #$ThreeDimensionalGeometricThing and #$SimplyConnectedThing (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Polyhedron is a 3-D, simply-connected, geometrically-describable object whose entire surface (see #$PolyhedralSurface) is a finite, unbounded #$SurfaceRegion that is the spatial sum of several (i.e. four or more) polygons (see #$Polygon).")
(comment elementOf "A very general binary predicate that relates a thing to any set or collection (see #$SetOrCollection) that it is a member or element of. <code>(#$elementOf THING SETORCOL)</code> means that <code>THING</code> is an element of <code>SETORCOL</code>.  
<p>
#$elementOf is a more general relation than #$isa.  Whereas #$isa is used exclusively to talk about membership in #$Collections,  #$elementOf can also be used to talk about membership in mathematical sets (see #$Set-Mathematical).")
(comment convexHullOf "A binary predicate that relates a given two- or three-dimensional spatial thing to its intangible \"convex hull\".  If <b>OBJECT</b> is a #$TwoDimensionalThing, then <code>(#$convexHullOf HULL OBJECT)</code> means that <b>HULL</b> is the entire one-dimensional boundary (see #$ClosedLinearObject) of the minimal convex 2-D space region that #$spatiallySubsumes <b>OBJECT</b> (see #$ConvexSpaceRegion and #$Surface).  If <b>OBJECT</b> is a #$ThreeDimensionalThing, then <code>(#$convexHullOf HULL OBJECT)</code> means that <b>HULL</b> is the entire closed two-dimensional surface (see #$ClosedSurfaceRegion) of the minimal convex 3-D space region that subsumes <b>OBJECT</b>.  
<p>
Note that the dimensionality of <b>HULL</b> is always one less than that of <b>OBJECT</b>.  Also note that, while <b>OBJECT</b> might or might not be a #$SpatiallyContinuousThing, <b>HULL</b> is spatially-continuous in either case.
<p>
See also the corresponding function #$ConvexHullFn.  To describe the whole convex space region bounded by a given object's convex hull, use #$convexSpaceRegionSubsuming-Minimal.")
(comment SpaceRegion-Empirical "A specialization of #$SpaceRegion, #$SpatialThing-Localized, and #$IntangibleExistingThing (qq.v.).  Instances of #$SpaceRegion-Empirical are intangible regions of space located in the empirically observable universe.  A space region might or might not be connected (see #$SpatiallyContinuousThing).  It might be partially or completely filled with (occupied by) #$PartiallyTangibles, or it might be completely empty (but cf. #$FreeSpaceRegion).  In any case, the space region itself is not to be confused with a physical object or other spatially localized (non-space-region) thing that might happen to be #$cospatial with it.  A given space region can be characterized fully merely by specifying its location and dimensions.  Thus (although this is not the case with spatial things in general), space regions are identical (#$equals) if and only if they are #$cospatial.  #$SpaceRegion-Empirical is in a way the spatial analogue of #$TimeInterval, whose own instances can be fully characterized by specifying their temporal properties; these two collections can be used, respectively, to talk about space and time as \"dimensions\".  Specializations of #$SpaceRegion-Empirical include #$Point-Empirical, #$LineSegment-Empirical, #$Surface-Empirical, and #$SpaceChunk-Empirical.")
(comment companyIsInIndustry "(#$companyIsInIndustry COMPANY INDUSTRY) means that the #$CommercialOrganization COMPANY is in the #$Industry-Localized INDUSTRY.")
(disjointWith DoorInABuilding-Exterior DoorInABuilding-Interior)
(comment DoorInABuilding-Interior "A specialization of #$DoorInABuilding.  Each instance of #$DoorInABuilding-Interior is an interior door of a building.  That is, each instance of this collection is a door that covers a portal leading from one area in the interior of a building to another interior area.  These doors are often lighter and less durable than exterior doors (see #$DoorInABuilding-Exterior).")
(comment DoorInABuilding-Exterior "A specialization of #$DoorInABuilding.  Each instance of #$DoorInABuilding-Exterior is an exterior door of a building.  That is, each instance of this collection is a door that covers a portal leading from the interior of a building to the outside.  These doors are often heavier and more weatherproof than interior doors (see #$DoorInABuilding-Interior).")
(comment Door-OutdoorRegionToOutdoorRegion "A specialization of #$DoorwayCovering.  Each instance of #$Door-OutdoorRegionToOutdoorRegion is a doorway covering for a doorway in a structure that separates two outdoor regions.  Such doors may be found in such stuctures as large outdoor walls.")
(disjointWith Door-OutdoorRegionToOutdoorRegion DoorInABuilding)
(disjointWith TimeIndependentCollection TimeDependentCollection)
(disjointWith TextString (CollectionDifferenceFn CharacterString TextString))
(comment ImplicitRelationshipDefiningSchemaFn "This function identifies a #$RelationshipDefiningSchema that is implicitly defined by a meaning sentence in some #$ObjectDefiningSchema. The first argument of #$ImplicitRelationshipDefiningSchemaFn is determined by the meaning sentence predicate and the second argument is a list of the object defining schemas and logical fields that correspond to the arguments of the meaning sentence template. See also the corresponding predicate, #$implicitRelationshipPredicateList.")
(comment implicitRelationshipPredicateList "This predicate is similar to #$explicitRelationshipPredicateList, as it uniquely identifies a #$RelationshipDefiningSchema, however in this case the schema is only 'implicit' as a relationship between some #$ObjectDefiningSchema, <code>ODS</code> and one or more of its logical fields that references some other #$ObjectDefiningSchema, <code>OTHER-ODS</code> in one of <code>ODS</code>'s meaning sentences. In this case, we record the meaning sentence predicate that participates in the relationship, together with a list of the object defining schemas and logical fields that participate in the relationship, where the order of the list reflects the order in which they appear as arguments to the meaning sentence template. That is, <code>(#$implicitRelationshipPredicateList IMPLICIT-RDS PREDICATE LIST)</code> means that <code>IMPLICIT-RDS</code> is the #$RelationshipDefiningSchema that is implicitly defined by some meaning sentence of <code>ODS</code> and <code>LIST</code> is the list of the object defining schemas and logical fields corresponding to the arguments of the meaning sentence.")
(comment DividendPaymentObligation "A specialization of #$PaymentObligation.  Instances are obligations to make dividend payments to the holder of a security.")
(comment ObjectWithSSPSIDFn "<code>(#$ObjectWithSSPSIDFn INT)<code> denotes the SSPS ('static spatial perception service' for the Urban Combat game) object in the current context that has the SSPS id number <code>INT</code>.")
(comment missionStartLocation "<code>(#$missionStartLocation MISSION LOC)<code> means that the mission <code>MISSION</code> commences at the location <code>LOC</code>.")
(comment missionGoalLocation "<code>(#$missionGoalLocation MISSION LOC)<code> means that the mission <code>MISSION</code> has the goal of terminating at the location <code>LOC</code>.")
(comment missionGoalLocationType "<code>(#$missionGoalLocationType MISSION LOC-TYPE)<code> means that the mission <code>MISSION</code> has the goal of terminating at a location that is an instance of <code>LOC-TYPE</code>.")
(comment missionActionOnTypeWithFeatures "<code>(#$missionActionOnTypeWithFeatures MISSION ACT-TYPE LIST-OF-COLS)<code> means that the mission <code>MISSION</code> requires an instance of <code>ACT-TYPE</code> to have as the #$objectActedOn some thing which is an instance of each of each of the collections in <code>LIST-OF-COLS</code>.")
(comment missionCodeWords "<code>(#$missionCodeWords MISSION THING STRING)<code> means that in the mission <code>MISSION</code> the string <code>STRING</code> is code for <code>THING</code>.")
(comment MilitaryCommandSuccessionPolicy "A specialization of #$OrganizationPolicy (q.v.).  Each instance of #$MilitaryCommandSuccessionPolicy is a specification of how command should be transferred in the even that a command succession is required.")
(comment NormalCommandSuccession "An instance of #$MilitaryCommandSuccessionPolicy.  According to #$NormalCommandSuccession, the highest ranking most senior personnel take command before lower-ranking, less senior personnel.")
(comment commandSuccession "<code>(#$commandSuccession MISSION POLICY)<code> means that in the mission <code>MISSION</code> the military command succession policy is <code>POLICY</code>.")
(comment authorizedWeaponUse "<code>(#$authorizeWeaponUse MISSION WEAPON-TYPE TARGET-TYPE)<code> means that in the mission <code>MISSION</code>, instances of <code>TARGET-TYPE</code> are authorized to be targeted by weapons that are instances of <code>WEAPON-TYPE</code>.")
(comment missionMapID "<code>(#$missionMapID MISSION ID-STRING)<code> means that in the mission <code>MISSION</code>, a critical map is denoted by <code>ID-STRING</code>.")
(comment FindingAndDefusingExplosiveDevice "Each instance of this collection is an event in which one or more
agents find and defuse an explosive device before it is otherwise detonated.")
(comment OvercomingObstacles "Each instance of this collection is an event in which an agent
overcomes one or more obstacles.")
(comment RadioSilence "Each instance of this collection is an event in which an agent
purposefully maintains radio silence.")
(comment UrbanArea-HighDensity "A specialization of #$UrbanArea (q.v.).  Each instance of #$UrbanArea-HighDensity is a geographical region the whole of which (more or less) is characterized by typically \"urban\" features, and which, furthermore, has extremely many of these features per unit land. Cf. #$UrbanArea-MediumDensity.")
(disjointWith UrbanArea-HighDensity UrbanArea-MediumDensity)
(comment missionEnvironmentType "<code>(#$missionEnvironmentType MISSION LOC-TYPE)<code> means that in the mission <code>MISSION</code> the environment is of the type <code>LOC-TYPE</code>.")
(comment MilitarySignalOperationsInstructions "A specialization of #$OrganizationPolicy (q.v.).  Each instance of #$MilitarySignalOperationsInstructions is a specification of what sort of code to use in signal communications.")
(comment StandardSOI "An instance of #$MilitarySignalOperationsInstructions (q.v.).
#$StandardSOI specifies that ordinary SOI to use.")
(comment missionSignalOperationInstructions "<code>(#$missionSignalOperationInstructions MISSION SOI)<code> means that in the mission <code>MISSION</code> the signal operations instructions to be followed are <code>SOI</code>.")
(comment missionStartTime "<code>(#$missionSignalOperationInstructions MISSION SOI)<code> means that in the mission <code>MISSION</code> the signal operations instructions to be followed are <code>SOI</code>.")
(comment missionTeamCommanderLocation "<code>(#$missionTeamCommanderLocation MISSION LOCATION)<code> means that during the mission <code>MISSION</code> the team commander for the mission is at <code>LOCATION</code>.")
(comment missionTaskForceCommanderLocation "<code>(#$missionTaskForceCommanderLocation MISSION LOCATION)<code> means that during the mission <code>MISSION</code> the task force commander for the mission is at <code>LOCATION</code>.")
(comment missionMainCommandPostCommanderLocation "<code>(#$missionTaskForceCommanderLocation MISSION LOCATION)<code> means that during the mission <code>MISSION</code> the main command post for the mission is at <code>LOCATION</code>.")
(comment obligationHasPriorityOverObligationForAgent "<code>(#$obligationHasPriorityOverObligationForAgent PRIOR-OBLIGATION OBLIGATION AGENT)</code> means that the instance <code>AGENT</code> of #$IntelligentAgent is obliged to fufill the instance <code>PRIOR-OBLIGATION</code> of #$Obligation before fufilling the distinct instance of #$Obligation <code>OBLIGATION</code>.  Thus this predicate entails the existence of a third obligation that specifies which obligation takes priority.")
(comment SpatialOrderingPredicate "A specialization of both #$SpatialPredicate and #$OrderingPredicate (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$SpatialOrderingPredicate is an antisymmetric, transitive, binary predicate that can be used for ordering a #$PhysicalSeries (or other series of spatial objects) in such a way that the predicate relates each element of the series to each subsequent element.")
(comment OrderingPredicate "A specialization of #$AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate, #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate, and #$ObjectPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$OrderingPredicate is an antisymmetric, transitive, binary predicate that can be used for ordering a #$Series (q.v.) in such a way that the predicate relates each member of the series to each subsequent member.  An ordering predicate can also be used for similarly ordering the instances of a #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder (q.v.).
<p>
For spatial predicates that can be used to order #$PhysicalSeries, see the specialization #$SpatialOrderingPredicate.")
(comment seriesMemberType "<code>(#$seriesMemberType SERIES COL)</code> means that each of the #$seriesMembers of <code>SERIES</code> is an instance of the collection <code>COL</code>.")
(comment listMemberType "A binary predicate that relates a #$List to a collection that each of the list's members is an instance of. 
<code>(#$listMemberType LIST COL)</code> means that <code>LIST</code> is a list of instances of <code>COL</code>.  See also the corresponding function, #$ListOfTypeFn.")
(comment seriesDefiningMemberType "(#$seriesDefiningMemberType SERIES TYPE) identifies TYPE as the instance of #$Collection that defines SERIES as a SERIES of a given type.  Thus, for any instances of #$Series SERIES, a thing THING is a member of that SERIES (i.e., (#$seriesMembers SERIES THING) holds) if and only if THING is a part of SERIES (i.e., (#$parts SERIES THING)) and THING is an instance of TYPE.")
(disjointWith EventSeries-Noncontinuous PhysicalSeries)
(comment MostCapturedFn "A collection denoting unary function.  (#$MostCapturedFn COLL) denotes the subcollection of COLL that consists of the instances that have the most number of persons captured in the event.  There could be more than one \"most captured in\" event in because of ties.  Most often though, this will return a collection with a single instance.")
(comment TermSuppressedAtTheTopLevelOfCycInference "A specialization of #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerm.  Each instance of #$TermSuppressedAtTheTopLevelOfCycInference is a CycL term that, by default (with standard inference parameter settings), is filtered from the set of results returned by the Cyc inference engine as the result of a query. For example, because #$TheTerm is a specialization of #$TermSuppressedAtTheTopLevelOfCycInference, this query:
<p>
<pre>
(new-cyc-query
  '(#$isa ?PRES #$UnitedStatesPresident)
  '(#$MtSpace #$CurrentWorldDataCollectorMt-NonHomocentric 
  (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn 
   (#$MonthFn #$June 
     (#$YearFn 1995)) #$TimePoint))
  `(:INFERENCE-MODE :MINIMAL
    :MAX-TIME 30
    :PROBABLY-APPROXIMATELY-DONE 0.9500000000000001
    :ANSWER-LANGUAGE :HL
    :CONTINUABLE? T)
)
</pre>
<p>
Will return this result only:
<p> 
<code>
#$BillClinton
</code>
<p>
Whereas, if the inference parameter <code>:allow-indeterminite-results</code> is set to <code>t</code>, these answers will be returned:
<p>
<code>
#$BillClinton
(#$TheFn #$UnitedStatesPresident)
</code>
<p>
This collection is a useful tool for preventing Cyc from sounding like a \"wise guy\" by answering questions with trivial and uninformative correct answers.")
(comment TermExemptFromUniqueNamesAssumption "A specialization of #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerm.  Each instance of #$TermExemptFromUniqueNamesAssumption is a CycL term that is not by default assumed to be #$different all other terms.")
(comment GeographicalQuantity "A specialization of #$TangiblePhysicalQuantity.     Each instance of #$GeographicalQuantity is a #$PhysicalQuantity that can only characterize a #$GeographicalRegion.")
(comment Temperature "A specialization of #$TangiblePhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Temperature is a degree of \"hotness\" -- or, more precisely, the potential for heat transfer -- that some tangible thing might have.  An instance of #$Temperature might be either a fixed point-value, such as 98.6 degrees Fahrenheit (cf. #$UnitOfTemperature), or a range, such as #$HumanHabitableTemperature or #$TooHotToTouch.")
(comment StandardPressure "The standard air pressure range that humans live in -- what one finds on terrestrial earth, inside houses, and so forth.  #$StandardPressure is approximately (#$PoundsPerSquareInch 14).")
(comment WeatherQuantity "#$WeatherQuantity is the collection of all particular quantities of weather related measurements.  For example, (#$LowAmountFn #$Raininess) is an instance of this collection and is a low amount on the conventional \"raininess\" scale.  All instances of this collection are measurements exclusively along some weather dimension ( e.g. \"raininess\", \"cloudiness\", etc.) the broadest predicate that can be used to relate these quantities to an instance of #$OutdoorLocation is #$hasWeatherQuantity.  In most cases more specific predicates should be used (c.f. #$raininessOfRegion and #$cloudinessOfRegion).")
(comment PhysicalQuantity "A specialization of #$ScalarQuantity (q.v.). Each #$PhysicalQuantity is a quantity that can (at least in principle) be the measure of a physical, spatial, or temporal aspect of an individual.  Specializations include #$Time-Quantity, #$Mass, and #$Area.
<p>
For those physical quantities that only characterize <i>tangible objects</i>, see the specialization #$TangiblePhysicalQuantity.  See also #$hasPhysicalQuantity.")
(comment hasPhysicalQuantity "(#$hasPhysicalQuantity OBJ QUANT) means that OBJ has the quantity QUANT, which is an instance of #$PhysicalQuantity, possibly along some implicit dimension.  This predicate relates things to their physical properties measured as a quantity.  For instance, #$Distance is a physical quantity that is always a measure along some dimension: height, length, or width. (#$hasPhysicalQuantity OBJ (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 2)) holds just in case OBj measures 2 feet along some dimension or other (i.e. it is either 2 feet high, 2 feet wide, or two feet long.")
(comment Relaxation "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType and a specialization of #$FeelingAttribute.  Each instance of #$Relaxation is some level  of an agent's feeling of being at ease and untroubled.")
(comment typeEvokes "(#$typeEvokes TYPE QUANT-OF-FEELING) When an abstract agent perceives or thinks about objects of type TYPE, the agent is caused to the feel the emotion type to the degree specified by QUANT-OF-FEELING.  Most often the second argument to this relation will be formed by an instance of #$FeelingAttribute wrapped with a generic value function.")
(comment attitudeTowardsObject "(#$attitudeTowardsObject AGT OBJ QUANT) means that the #$SentientAnimal AGT has the quantity of feeling described by QUANT (see #$FeelingAttribute) about the #$Individual.  By `attitude' we mean a possibly latent and/or long-lasting feeling.  To refer to feelings that AGT experiences immediately and consciously towards OBJ, use #$feelsTowardsObject-Ternary.")
(comment SetOfCollectionSpecializationListsFn "A function which takes a set of collections and returns a set 
of lists of collections where the members of each list in the resulting 
set are elements of the input set, ordered by #$genls. That is, each list in the set returned represents one path through the #$genls graph from the first member of the list to the last member using only members of the input set. Here are some examples:
<p>
(#$equals
(#$SetOfCollectionSpecializationListsFn
(#$TheSet #$Book-CW #$PublishedConceptualWork #$University
#$Organization))
(#$TheSet
(#$TheList #$Book-CW #$PublishedConceptualWork)
(#$TheList #$University #$Organization))))
</p>  
<p>
(#$equals  
(#$SetOfCollectionSpecializationListsFn
(#$TheSet #$Roadway #$Facility-Generic #$InfrastructureProduct))
(#$TheSet
(#$TheList #$Roadway #$Facility-Generic)
(#$TheList #$Roadway #$InfrastructureProduct)))
</p>
See also #$SetOfPredicateSpecializationListsFn, which performs the analogous transformation for sets of predicates, using the #$genlPreds graph.")
(comment SetOfPredicateSpecializationListsFn "A function which takes a set of predicates and returns a set of lists of predicates where the members of each list in the resulting set are elements of the input set, ordered by #$genlPreds. That is, each list in the set returned represents one path through the #$genlPreds graph from the first member of the list to the last member using only members of the input set. Here is an example:
<p>
(#$equals
  (#$SetOfPredicateSpecializationListsFn
    (#$TheSet #$eventOccursAt #$performedBy #$actors #$objectActedOn))
  (#$TheSet
    (#$TheList #$eventOccursAt #$actors)
    (#$TheList #$objectActedOn #$actors)
    (#$TheList #$performedBy #$actors))</p>  

See also #$SetOfCollectionSpecializationListsFn, which performs the analogous transformation for sets of collections, using the #$genls graph.")
(comment memberOfTuple "A binary predicate that relates a given #$Tuple to any of the items in that tuple.  <code>(#$memberOfTuple MEMBER TUPLE)</code> means that <code>MEMBER</code> is a  member of <code>TUPLE</code>.  Where <code>TUPLE</code> is an instance of #$List (q.v.), the more specialized predicate #$memberOfList will apply as well.  
<p>
See also #$tupleIndexSet and #$tupleMemberIndex.")
(comment hasNumberOfValuesOfTypeViaPred "(#$hasNumberOfValuesOfTypeViaPred INS BIN-PRED TYPE POS-INTEGER) holds just in case INS is related to POS-INTEGER number of instances of TYPE via performing events that stand in BIN-PRED to those instances of TYPE.  For example, If Martha Stewart has baked  NUM cakes, then

 <pre>(#$hasNumberOfValuesOfTypeViaPred #$MarthaStewart #$outputsCreated #$Cake NUM)</pre>
<br>
holds.")
(comment memberHasLargestNumberOfValuesofTypeViaPred "(#$memberHasLargestNumberOfValuesofTypeViaPred COLL INS BIN-PRED TYPE POS-INTEGER) holds just in case INS is the instance of COLL in which no other instance of COLL is related to more instances of TYPE via performing events that stand in BIN-PRED to those instances of TYPE and POS-INTEGER is the number of instances those events are related to.  For example, If Martha Stewart has baked NUM cakes and that is more than any other person has baked, then

 <pre>(#$memberHasLargestNumberOfValuesofTypeViaPred #$Person 
         #$MarthaStewart #$outputsCreated #$Cake NUM)</pre>
<br>
holds.<br>Note that this relation allows for ties.")
(disjointWith Relation FieldOfStudy)
(disjointWith Relation Title)
(disjointWith MusicalCompositionTypeByGenre PersonTypeByOccupation)
(disjointWith ArtisticTypeByStyle PersonTypeByOccupation)
(comment TruthFunction "A major subcollection of #$Relation that subsumes the collections #$Predicate, #$LogicalConnective, and #$Quantifier (qq.v.). Truth-functions, or rather the expressions that represent or denote them, are used to form sentences.  More precisely, any CycL expression that denotes an instance of #$TruthFunction (and only such an expression) can appear in the \"0th\" argument-position (i.e. as the term immediately following the opening parenthesis) of a #$CycLSentence.  
<p>
The name 'TruthFunction' derives in part from the fact that the sentences thus formed (if semantically well-formed and quantificationally closed; see #$CycLSentence-Assertible and #$CycLClosedSentence) are the kind of expression that can be true or false (with respect to a given context and interpretation). Though not really functions (cf. #$Function-Denotational), many #$TruthFunctions are \"truth-functional\" in the sense that the truth-value of a (closed, semantically well-formed) sentence <code>(RELN ARG1..ARGN)</code> built using a truth-function <code>RELN</code> is uniquely determined (with respect to a given context) by <code>RELN</code> together with the argument(s) <code>ARG1..ARGN</code> to which it is applied.  For example, the sentence <code>(#$mother #$ChelseaClinton #$HillaryClinton)</code> is made true (in the actual world) by the fact that Chelsea Clinton's mother is Hillary Clinton.")
(comment denotes-TypeType "A binary predicate that relates a type of denoting expression (i.e. a specialization of #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerm) to a collection.  <code>(#$denotes-TypeType EXPR-TYPE COL)</code> means that each instance of <code>EXPR-TYPE</code> denotes (see #$denotes) some instance of <code>COL</code>, and no instance of <code>COL</code> is denoted by a CycL term that is not an instance of <code>EXPR-TYPE</code>.")
(comment totalFunctionOn "A binary predicate that relates a given function (see #$Function-Denotational) to any #$SetOrCollection that it is a \"total function\" on (cf. #$TotalFunction).  <code>(#$totalFunctionOn FUNC SETORCOL)</code> means that <code>FUNC</code> returns a value for any (sequence of) element(s) of <code>SETORCOL</code> taken as argument(s).  
<p>
More precisely: where the #$arity of <code>FUNC</code> is <code>N</code>, then <code>(#$totalFunctionOn FUNC SETORCOL)</code> is true if and only if for any <code>N</code>-length sequence of elements of <code>SETORCOL</code> (<code>THING<sub>1</sub>, ..., THING<sub>N</sub></code>), there is some <code>VALUE</code> such that this holds:
<pre>
  (#$equals VALUE (FUNC THING<sub>1</sub> ... THING<sub>N</sub>)) .
</pre>
Where <code>FUNC</code> is a #$VariableArityFunction it is the same, except that  
the above must hold of every sequence of elements of <code>SETORCOL</code> whose length is between the #$arityMin and the #$arityMax of <code>FUNC</code> (inclusive).
<p>
Typically, <code>FUNC</code> will be a #$PartialFunction (or at least not known to be a #$TotalFunction) and <code>SETORCOL</code> a proper subset of the set/collection of all #$admittedArguments to <code>FUNC</code>.
<p> 
For example, #$QuotientFn is a total function on both #$PositiveInteger and #$NegativeInteger, but not on #$Integer (since dividing by 0 is undefined).")
(comment relationDomain "A #$MetaRelation predicate that associates each instance of #$Relation with its domain: the set of all sequences of things that the relation relates to something.  For example, the domain of #$likesAsFriend is the set of (length one sequences of) sentient animals who like some sentient 
animal or other, and the domain of #$DifferenceFn is the set of all pairs of #$ScalarIntervals (since #$DifferenceFn relates each such pair to the result of subtracting its second member from its first member).  <code>(#$relationDomain RELATION DOMAIN)</code> means that the domain of <code>RELATION</code> is <code>DOMAIN</code>.  
<p>
More precisely (and following standard mathematical practice): if the #$relationalArity (q.v.) of <code>RELATION</code> is <code>N</code> (for <code>N</code> > 1), <code>DOMAIN</code> is the set of all (<code>N</code>-1)-length #$Lists consisting of the first N-1 items of some list in the #$relationExtension (q.v.) of <code>RELATION</code>; if <code>RELATION</code> is unary it has no domain, and #$relationDomain is undefined for such a <code>RELATION</code>.  
<p>
Though defined for polyadic relations generally, <code>DOMAIN</code> will normally be of particular interest only when <code>RELATION</code> is a function (i.e. an instance of  #$Function-Denotational), in which case <code>RELATION</code> relates each  element of <code>DOMAIN</code> to exactly one thing (which, in turn, is an element  of the #$relationRange of <code>RELATION</code>).  See also #$DomainOfFunctionFn.")
(comment AbstractThing "The collection that is by definition the intersection of #$AtemporalThing and #$AspatialThing (qq.v.).  A given thing is an instance of #$AbstractThing just in case it is \"abstract\", in the sense of having neither temporal nor spatial extent or location.  Specializations of #$AbstractThing include #$SetOrCollection, #$Number-General, #$Relation, and #$Proposition (qq.v.).  Note that a set or collection is considered an abstract thing even if its elements are not abstract.")
(comment Microtheory "A specialization of #$AspatialInformationStore and #$AbstractIndividual (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Microtheory is an atemporal, aspatial, informational thing that represents a context in Cyc.  Each microtheory (or 'mt') serves to group a set of assertions together that share some common assumptions; the assertions in an mt constitute the content of that mt.  Note that each assertion in the Cyc knowledge base must be explicitly stated to be true in at least one microtheory.  Assertions stated to be true in one mt will also be true  (by inference) in more specialized mts that depend on the content of that mt.  For example, if something is true in the #$HumanSocialLifeMt (q.v.), then it should by default be true in the more specialized #$UnitedStatesSocialLifeMt (q.v.).  Specialized microtheories are related to the more general microtheories on which they depend by the predicate #$genlMt (q.v.).  Note that every query is made in some mt, and the answer one gets to a query depends on the mt in which it is asked, since the only assertions which can be used to answer a query in an mt are those  explicitly stated to be true in that mt, or in some more general mt.  See also the predicate #$ist, which is used to relate an assertion to the microtheories in which it is true.")
(comment MapFunctionOverSetList "A macro expanded evaluatable function, #$MapFunctionOverSetList is the composition of #$MapFunctionOverList and #$MapFunctionOverSet. If <code>FUNCTION</code> is a #$UnaryFunction and <code>SET-LIST</code> is a list of sets, i.e. an instance of <code>(#$ListOfTypeFn #$Set-Mathematical)</code>, then <code>(#$MapFunctionOverSetList FUNCTION SET-LIST</code>) applies <code>FUNCTION</code> to each element of each set in <code>LIST-SET</code> and returns a new list of sets. ")
(comment MapFunctionOverSetOfSets "A macro expanded evaluatable function, #$MapFunctionOverSetOfSets is the composition of #$MapFunctionOverSet with itself. If <code>FUNCTION</code> is a #$UnaryFunction and <code>SET-OF-SETS</code> is a #$SetOfSets, then <code>(#$MapFunctionOverSetOfSets FUNCTION SET-OF-SETS</code>) applies <code>FUNCTION</code> to each element of each set in <code>SET-OF-SETS</code> and returns a new set of sets.")
(comment MapFunctionOverListOfLists "A macro expanded evaluatable function, #$MapFunctionOverListOfLists is the composition of #$MapFunctionOverList with itself. If <code>FUNCTION</code> is a #$UnaryFunction and <code>LIST-OF-LISTS</code> is a list of lists, then <code>(#$MapFunctionOverListOfLists FUNCTION LIST-OF-LISTS</code>) applies <code>FUNCTION</code> to each member of each list in <code>LIST-OF-LISTS</code> and returns a new list of lists.")
(comment RadioTransceiver "A #$RadioTransceiver is a #$Radio that has both a #$RadioTransmitter and a #$RadioReceiver as proper physical parts. That is, it is a radio that can both transmit and receive radio signals.")
(comment AirGroundRadioTransceiver "An #$AirGroundRadioTransceiver is a #$RadioTransceiver that is intended to transmit and receive radio signals between air and land based information terminals.")
(comment generatePhrase "(generatePhrase TERM STRING) is a convenience wrapper for (evaluate STRING (GeneratePhraseFn TERM)), under the assumption that STRING is a variable and TERM is bound.")
(comment IKRISInnerTheoryVocabularyTerm "The collection of constants created that correspond to defined terms in the ICL/IKL inner theory.")
(comment |isit:instanceOf| "an IKRIS inner theory term.  This term is like #$isa, but in the inner theory is not specific to collections.  For instance in PSL activity types are abstract types that have \"occurrences\" but not instances.  So, if PSI:running is a PSL activity type, (isit:instanceOf RUNNING-01 PSI:running) is how you would represent, in the inner theory, RUNNING-01 as an occurrence of PSI:running.  Generally, during an import of ICL/IKL into CycL this predicate will be converted to #$isa and the PSL activity type mapped to a specialization of Situation.  In this case, PSI:running maps to #$Running .")
(comment |isit:EventType| "An IKRIS inner theory term.  It is defined by the following axiom:

<pre>

    (#$forAll ?X
        (#$implies 
          (isit:EventType ?X)
          (#$thereExists ?Y 
            (#$and 
              (#$genls ?Y #$Event)
              (#$forAll ?E 
                (#$equiv (#$isa ?E ?Y) (isit:instanceOf ?E ?X))))))))</pre>
<br>
Bascially, anything that has the property isit:EventType is such that there is some spec of event that it is coextensional with


.")
(comment |isit:StateType| "An IKRIS inner theory term.  It is basically a unary predicate version of the collection of all specializations of StaticSituation (c.f. (#$SpecsFn #$StaticSituation))


.")
(comment RestructuringSomething "A #$FirstOrderCollection and specialization of #$PurposefulAction and #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$RestructuringSomething is an event in which an agent deliberately modifies the structure of something, such as the financial structure of a corporation or the plot structure of a novel.")
(comment intersectionType "A #$MetaFunction predicate that relates a given #$UnaryIntersectionFunction (q.v.) to the collection that the function \"intersects\" with another collection, taken as argument, to yield a corresponding value.  <code>(#$intersectionType INTFUNC COL)</code> means that <code>INTFUNC</code> maps any admitted argument <code>ARG</code> (which will itself be a collection) to the collection that is the #$collectionIntersection of <code>COL</code> and <code>ARG</code>.  For example, <code>(#$intersectionType #$JuvenileFn #$JuvenileAnimal)</code> implies that (#$JuvenileFn #$Dog) is the collection-intersection of #$JuvenileAnimal and #$Dog, i.e. the collection of juvenile dogs.")
(comment NeutralElectricalCharge "An instance of both #$ElectricalCharge and #$ScalarNullValue (qq.v.).  #$NeutralElectricalCharge is the electrical charge posessed by things that have neither a positive nor a negative charge.")
(disjointWith ExternalPartOfBuilding (CollectionDifferenceFn PartOfBuilding ExternalPartOfBuilding))
(comment EcotoneRegion "An #$EcotoneRegion is a transition area between two adjacent #$Ecosystems. It may appear on the ground as a gradual blending of the two communities across a broad area, or it may manifest itself as a sharp boundary line.
<p>
Changes in the physical environment may produce a sharp boundary, as in the example of a #$Shoreline or the region between areas of #$Forest and #$ForestClearing. Elsewhere, a more gradually blended interface area will be found, where organisms from the #$BiologicalSpecies from each community will be found together as well as organisms of #$BiologicalSpecies unique to the #$EcotoneRegion. #$MountainRanges often create such #$EcotoneRegions, due to the wide variety of climatic conditions experienced on their slopes. They may also provide a boundary between species due to the obstructive nature of their terrain. 
<p>
#$WetlandRegions are examples of #$EcotoneRegions, as they are the interfaces between terrestrial and aquatic #$Ecosystems.")
(disjointWith Tool-PowerTool (CollectionDifferenceFn Tool Tool-PowerTool))
(comment ExternallyPoweredDevice "A collection of #$PoweredDevices, classified by the main way of supplying the force needed to operate them.  An instance of #$ExternallyPoweredDevice has energy supplied from outside, such as #$Electricity supplied from an electric grid or a #$SolarCell or mechanical force such as a #$Cable pulling a cable car.  Cf. #$SelfPoweredDevice.")
(comment stateOfDevice "This predicate is used to identify the state of operation that a particular device is in.  (#$stateOfDevice DEV STATE) means that the #$PhysicalDevice DEV is in the #$DeviceTypeByState STATE.  Thus, (#$stateOfDevice HAL #$Device-Off) says that the computer HAL is switched off.")
(comment BeingSomewhere "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$Situation. Each instance of #$BeingSomewhere is the situation in which some particular thing is located at a certain place.")
(comment standingInBinaryRelation "This is the predicate corresponding to #$StandingInBinaryRelationFn (q.v.).")
(comment TerrorismOWLExportBinaryPredicate "Instances of this collection are binary predicates whose extent we want to export in any OWL export of terrorism data.  Typically the export will be constrained as follows:
<pre>
        (1) There will be some query to retrieve the individuals we want to export information about -- generally a query that pulls back terrorist agents and acts.
        (2)  Any instances of #$Collection involved in assertions with the individuals that satisfy the query mentioned in (1) using the predicates from this collection or the predicates that are instances of #$OwlExportableRelation should have their top level OWL definitions included in the export and the assertion should be exported. (use specializations of this collection for less than a full terrorism data export.</pre>

Consider the following examples.  Example 1: Assume that #$affiliatedWith is an instance of TerrorismOWLExportBinaryPredicate.  Further assume that PERSON1 and PERSON2 are both bindings for the query in (1).  If (#$affiliatedWith PERSON1 PERSON2) is asserted, then export that assertion.  Example 2: #$relationInstanceExists is an instance of #$OwlExportableRelation, #$organismKilled is an instance of #$TerrorismOWLExportBinaryPredicate and ATTACK1 is an instance of the query in (1).  If (#$relationInstanceExists #$organismKilled ATTACK1 MilitaryPerson) is asserted, then export that assertions and provide the top level definition of MilitaryPerson.")
(comment HashDollar "The two-character string '#$'.")
(comment TheStJoeCompany "The St. Joe Company -- a real estate company traded on the #$NewYorkStockExchange.")
(comment SIInternationalInc "SI International, Inc., a NASDAQ-traded defense contractor.")
(comment WynnResortsLtd "A publicly traded corporation that owns and manages hotels and casinos.")
(comment PlainsAllAmericanPipelineLP "A publicly traded company in the oil industry.")
(comment VertrueInc "Vertrue Inc, a leading direct marketing company specializing in development and marketing of membership service programs.")
(comment VishayIntertechnologyInc "Vishay Intertechnology Inc, is one of the largest manufacturers of discrete semiconductors and electronics components. Its listed on the New York Stock Exchange.")
(comment VisteonCorp "Visteon Corporation, is an automotive parts company spun off from the Ford Motor Company. Its listed on New York Stock Exchange")
(comment VitalImagesInc "Vital Images, Inc is a leading provider of enterprise-wide advanced visualization and analysis software solution. Its listed on Nasdaq")
(comment VonageHoldingsCorporation "Vonage is a leading provider of broadband telephone services. Its listed on New York Stock Exchange.")
(comment WisconsinEnergyCorp "Wisconsin Energy Corporation, provides electrical service for customers, primarily located in southeastern and eastern Wisconsin as well as Upper Peninsula of Michigan. Its listed on New York Stock Exchange.")
(comment PinnacleAirlinesCorporation "An airline company traded on NASDAQ.")
(comment NSGroupInc "A manufacturing company traded on NYSE.")
(comment NuSkinEnterprisesInc "A drug company traded on NYSE.")
(comment OshkoshTruckCorp "A consumer goods company traded on NYSE.")
(comment ParkerDrillingCo "A basic materials company traded on NYSE.")
(comment quantitySlotForArg1 "(#$quantitySlotForArg1 <code>SLOT</code>
<code>THING> <code>COMPLEX-SLOT</code>) means that <code>SLOT</code>
is the <code>#$QuantitySlot</code> which results from restricting the first
argument of <code>COMPLEX-SLOT</code> to <code>THING</code>.  See the
corresponding function <code>#$QuantitySlotForArg1Fn</code>.")
(comment subcollectionOfWithRelationFrom "<code>(#$subcollectionOfWithRelationFrom SUPER-COL PREDICATE THING SUB-COL)</code> means that <code>SUB-COL</code> is the collection of all instances <code>INSTANCE</code> of <code>SUPER-COL</code> for which <code>(PREDICATE THING INSTANCE)</code> holds. See the function that corresponds to this predicate, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn.")
(comment NSFInferenceTest "A sub-collection of <code>#$KBContentTest-FullySpecified</code>. <code>#$NSFInferenceTest</code> is the collection of KB content tests designed to test knowledge extracted from the Event Learner, and more specifically, knowledge associated with the oil price seed event.")
(comment SupplyRateOfToFn "<code>(#$SupplyRateOfToFn COMMODITY)</code> denotes a function that maps an instance RECIPIENT of <code>#$PartiallyTangible</code> to the supply rate (see <code>#$supplyRate</code>) of COMMODITY to RECIPIENT.")
(comment PriceOfInRegionFn "<code>(#$PriceOfInRegionFn COMMODITY)</code> denotes a function that maps an instance PLACE of <code>#$PartiallyTangible</code> to the price (see <code>#$priceChargedFor</code>) charged for COMMODITY in PLACE.")
(comment candidateTriggerSituationTypes "<code>(#$candidateTriggerSituationTypes SIT-TYPE TRIGGER-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$Situation) may be partially triggered by instances of <code>TRIGGER-TYPE</code> (cf. #$TriggeringSomething).")
(comment climateCycleTypeHasCharacteristicWeatherEventType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a #$ClimateCycleType to a specialization of #$WeatherEvent.  <code>(#$climateCycleTypeHasCharacteristicWeatherEventType CCT WET)</code> means that instances of <code>CCT</code> are characterized by frequent occurrences of instances of <code>WET</code>.")
(comment DebtSecurity "A specialization of #$LoanAgreement and #$TradeableSecurity.  Each instance of #$DebtSecurity is an agreement to repay money borrowed by the issuer.")
(comment DepositoryReceipt "A specialization of #$TradeableSecurity, the purpose of which is to facilitate the trade of stocks in companies traded on an exchange in one polity, among investors of a distinct polity.  A depository receipt confers ownership of some number of shares of stock (see #$Stock) to its holder, and can be traded, like stocks, on an exchange in the issuing polity.")
(disjointWith Equity-Security LoanAgreement)
(comment Equity-Security "The collection of instances of #$TradeableSecurity, ownership of which confers ownership in some company.")
(comment DepositoryReceiptTypeByPolityOfIssue "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$DepositoryReceipt into collections with a shared polity of issue.")
(comment DemandRateForByFn "<code>(#$DemandRateForByFn COMMODITY)</code> denotes a function that maps an instance CONSUMER of <code>#$PartiallyTangible</code> to the demand rate (see <code>#$demandRate</code>) for COMMODITY by CONSUMER.")
(comment polityOfIssue "<code>(#$polityOfIssue SECURITY POLITY)</code> means that <code>SECURITY</code> is an instance of #$TradeableSecurity issue in such a way that its trade will take place on an exchange in, and subject to the laws of, the instance <code>POLITY</code> of #$GeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment polityOfIssue "<code>(#$polityOfIssue SECURITY POLITY)</code> means that <code>SECURITY</code> is an instance of #$TradeableSecurity issue in such a way that its trade will take place on an exchange in, and subject to the laws of, the instance <code>POLITY</code> of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  Typically, this will mean that the issuer of <code>SECURITY</code> (see #$securityIssuedBy) is headquartered in <code>POLITY</code> though this is more dictated by spatio-temporal convenience rather than logic.")
(comment ILPNonSyntheticTestDataMicrotheory "A specialization of #$DataMicrotheory.  Each instance of #$ILPNonSyntheticTestDataMicrotheory is a ssociated with a non-synthetic ILP (inductive logic programming) test. See the wiki page http://wiki.cyc.com/wiki/index.php/ILP_test_calls_to_Aleph for a complete list of tests.")
(comment EarningsFigure "A specialization of #$MonetaryValue.  Membership in this collection is dependent on occurrence as an argument in a true sentence whose arg0 is an instance of #$IncomeMeasurePredicate.")
(comment corpDilutedLossPerShare "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$corpDilutedLossPerShare CORPORATION AMOUNT)</code> means <code>(#$corpDilutedEarningsPerShare CORPORATION (#$MinusFn AMOUNT))</code>.")
(comment dilutedLossPerShare-ForStockType "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate, <code>(#$dilutedLossPerShare-ForStockType STOCK VALUE)</code> means the same things as <code>(#$dilutedEarningsPerShare-ForStockType STOCK (#$MinusFn VALUE))</code>.")
(comment SalmedixInc "A wholly-owned subsidiary of Cephalon, Inc., that makes cancer drugs.")
(comment ExportRateOfByFn "<code>(#$ExportRateOfByFn COMMODITY)</code> denotes a function that maps an instance EXPORTER of <code>#$GeographicalRegion</code> to the export rate (see <code>#$exportRate</code>) for COMMODITY by EXPORTER.")
(comment corpDilutedAdjustedEPS "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation. <code>(#$corpDilutedAdjustedEPS COMPANY AMOUNT)</code><T> means that <code>AMOUNT</code> is the amount that would be earned (i.e. profit) by <code>COMPANY</code> per diluted share during the time interval T (but not necessarily any sub-interval of T), if all amortization and exceptional costs to  were added back to <code>COMPANY</code>'s profits.")
(comment ForcadosOilTerminal "The Forcados oil terminal in the Niger Delta, including the port facilities and harbor.")
(comment ExpenseFigure "A specialization of #$MonetaryValue.  Membership in this collection is dependent on occurrence as an argument in a true sentence whose arg0 is an instance of #$ExpensePredicate.")
(comment expenseForType "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation.  <code>(#$expenseForType AGENT TYPE AMOUNT)</code><T> means that at the interval T (but not necessarily at any sub-interval of T), <code>AMOUNT</code> is the amount of money (#$MonetaryValue, q.v.) that counts as <code>AGENT</code>'s total expenses for instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  See #$expenseDuringPeriodForType for a temporally decontextualized version of #$expenseForType.")
(comment JohnstonAtoll-Territory "#$JohnstonAtoll-Territory is an unincorporated #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, now administered by the Fish and Wildlife Service.")
(comment BouvetIsland-Territory "#$BouvetIsland-Territory is a #$Territory of the #$Norway.")
(comment WakeIsland-Territory "#$WakeIsland-Territory is an unincorporated #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica")
(comment NavassaIsland-Territory "#$NavassaIsland-Territory is an unincorporated #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, now administered by the Fish and Wildlife Service.")
(comment yearHasEnumerationOnCalendar "<code>(#$yearHasEnumerationOnCalendar YEAR NUMBER CALENDAR)</code> means that the instance <code>YEAR</code> of #$CalendarYear is the <code>NUMBER</code>th year on <code>CALENDAR</code>, an instance of #$CalendarSystem.")
(comment CalendarYearTypeFn "<code>(#$CalendarYearTypeFn NUMBER)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$CalendarYear that, by conventions for enumerating calendar years, are enumerated as a year of number <code>NUMBER</code>.   For example, both the year 2001 on the Julian calendar (see <code>(#$YearFn 2001)</code>) and <code>(#$FiscalYearFn AGENT 2001)</code> (for any appropriate value of <code>AGENT</code>) are instances of <code>(#$CalendarYearTypeFn NUMBER)</code>.")
(comment calendarYearTypeEnumeration "<code>(#$calendarYearTypeEnumeration YEAR-TYPE NUMBER)</code> identifies <code>YEAR-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$CalendarYear that are enumerated as year number <code>NUMBER</code> on some calendar.")
(comment QuarterTypeOfYearTypeFn "<code>(#$QuarterTypeOfYearTypeFn N YEAR-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all <code>N</code>th quarters of <code>YEAR-TYPE</code>, a collection of years (see #$CalendarYear).  For example, <code>(#$QuarterTypeOfYearTypeFn 3 (#$CalendarYearTypeFn 2001))</code> denotes the collection of third quarters of any year that is enumerated as the 2001th year on a calendar (see #$CalendarSystem).")
(comment quarterTypeOfYearType "<code>(#$quarterTypeOfYearType QUARTER-TYPE N YEAR-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>QUARTER-TYPE</code> as the collection of <code>N</code>th quarters of any year that is an instance of <code>YEAR-TYPE</code>, a sub-collection of #$CalendarYear.")
(comment TromelinIsland-ControlledLand "#$TromelinIsland-ControlledLand is a #$ControlledLand of #$France.")
(comment PalmyraAtoll-Territory "#$PalmyraAtoll-Territory is an incorporated #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, administered mostly by the Fish and Wildlife Service, though nine acres are administered by the Office of Insular Affairs.")
(comment GloriosoIslands-ControlledLand "#$GloriosoIslands-ControlledLand is a #$ControlledLand of #$France.")
(comment HeardIslandAndMcDonaldIslands-Territory "#$HeardIslandAndMcDonaldIslands-Territory is a #$Territory of #$Australia.")
(comment WallisAndFutuna-Territory "#$WallisAndFutuna-Territory is a #$Territory of #$France.")
(comment CoralSeaIslands-Territory "#$CoralSeaIslands-Territory is a #$Territory of #$Australia.")
(comment EuropaIsland-ControlledLand "#$EuropaIsland-ControlledLand is a #$ControlledLand of #$France.")
(comment HowlandIsland-Territory "#$HowlandIsland-Territory is a #$Territory of #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, administered by the Fish and Wildlife Service.")
(comment Guam-Territory "#$Guam-Territory is a #$Territory of #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, administered by the Office of Insular Affairs.")
(comment JuanDeNovaIsland-ControlledLand "#$JuanDeNovaIsland-ControlledLand is a #$ControlledLand of #$France.")
(comment MidwayIslands-Territory "#$MidwayIslands-Territory is a #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, administered by the Fish and Wildlife Service.")
(comment NorfolkIsland-Territory "#$NorfolkIsland-Territory is a #$Territory of #$Australia.")
(comment CorporationSole "The collection of all 'corporation soles' as defined in common law countries.  A #$CorporationSole is an individual #$Person who acts directly as a corporation (it is not a #$SoleProprietorship).   This form is used principally as the means of holding assets of a church or state under the control of one person, such as a bishop or king.  It also provides a means of passing the assets and authority of the entity to a successor.  One prominent example of a #$CorporationSole is the #$TheBritishCrown.")
(comment TheCrownInTheRightOfTheUnitedKingdom "#$TheCrownInTheRightOfTheUnitedKingdom is a #$CorporationSole consisting of the property and authority of the ruler of the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland.  The only member of this organization at a given time is the person who is the current king or queen or the UK.  Since 6 February, 1952, that person has been #$QueenElizabethII.")
(comment JanMayen-Territory "#$JanMayen-Territory is a #$Territory of #$Norway.")
(comment FaroeIslands-AdministrativeDivision "#$FaroeIslands-AdministrativeDivision is a self-governing administrative division of the Kingdom of #$Denmark.")
(comment JarvisIsland-Territory "#$JarvisIsland-Territory is an unincorportated #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment KingmanReef-Territory "#$KingmanReef-Territory is an unincorportated #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment BakerIsland-Territory "#$BakerIsland-Territory is an unincorportated #$Territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment BasicProbabilityTheoryMt "A #$Microtheory containing rules that express basic principles of probability.")
(comment conflateToInSystem "A predicate used to construct specialized lexicons for a classification system, such as an ontology (see #$Ontology) or taxonomy (see #$Taxonomy).  <code>(#$conflateToInSystem THING-1 THING-2 SYSTEM)</code> means that for purposes of mapping natural language to nodes in the system <code>SYSTEM</code>, natural language references to <code>THING-1</code> should be interpreted as references to <code>THING-2</code>.  For example, <code>(#$conflateToInSystem #$CalendarQuarter #$FiscalQuarter #$InvestmentRelatedThingTaxonomy)</code> means that references to #$CalendarQuarter (e.g., \"quarter\") should be understood as referring to #$FiscalQuarter.  Such assertions result in additions to the lexicon for the system in question, which also makes it possible for the system and lexicon to be separated from the Cyc KB as a bundle, preserving the mappings in question.")
(comment argIsaOutputModeForDetermination "<code>(#$argIsaOutputModeForDetermination PRED N TYPE DET)</code> means that relative to the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination <code>DET</code>, the  <code>N</code>th argument of the #$Predicate <code>PRED</code> should be an instance of the #$Collection <code>TYPE</code> and that argument position has a mode of an output variable.  The sense of \"mode\" here is derived from #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment argIsaInputModeForDetermination "<code>(#$argIsaInputModeForDetermination PRED N TYPE DET)</code> means that relative to the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination <code>DET</code>, the  <code>N</code>th argument of the #$Predicate <code>PRED</code> should be an instance of the #$Collection <code>TYPE</code> and that argument position has a mode of an input variable. The sense of \"mode\" here is derived from #$Prolog-ComputerLanguage.")
(comment focalArgumentOfDeterminationTarget "<code>(#$focalArgumentOfDeterminationTarget DET INT)</code> means that the target predicate of the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination represents that entity (i.e., #$Individual, #$Collection, etc.) which is of focal interest for generating rules relative to some induction process.")
(comment negationPredsWRTArgs "<code>(#$negationPredsWRTArgs PRED-1 PRED-2 LIST)</code> means that the two predicates <code>PRED-1</code> and <code>PRED-2</code> stand in a #$negationPreds -like relation to each other with respect to a specified correlation among their argument-places.  The two predicates, though both of fixed arity (see #$FixedArityRelation), might have identical or different #$arity; in the latter case, <code>PRED-1</code>'s #$arity is required to be higher than that of <code>PRED-2</code>.  The argument-place correlation between <code>PRED-1</code> and <code>PRED-2</code> is encoded in <code>LIST</code>, a list of non-negative integers whose length is equal to the arity of <code>PRED-2</code>.  The position of an integer within the list represents that same argument-position within <code>PRED-2</code>, while the size of the integer represents the corresponding argument-position within <code>PRED-1</code>.
<p>Thus <code>(#$negationPredsWRTArgs PRED-1 PRED-2 LIST)</code> means that whenever <code>PRED-1</code> holds of a given argument sequence <code>SEQUENCE-1</code>, then #$negationPreds holds of the sequence <code>SEQUENCE-2</code>, defined as follows: Where the <code>I</code>th item in <code>LIST</code> is the integer <code>N</code>, the <code>I</code>th item if <code>SEQUENCE-2</code> is the same as the <code>N</code>th item in <code>SEQUENCE-1</code>.  For example,
<pre>
  (#$negationPredsWRTArgs #$touchesWith #$spatiallySeparated (#$TheList 3 2))</pre>
entails
<pre>
  (#$not
    (#$and
      (#$touchesWith #$MingXu Steak8 Fork25)
      (#$spatiallySeparated Fork25 Steak8))).</pre>")
(comment companyEarnings "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation, <code>(#$companyEarnings COMPANY AMOUNT)</code><T> means that at the time period T (but not necessarily at any proper sub-interval of T), the earnings of the company <code>COMPANY</code> are <code>AMOUNT</code>, an instance of #$MonetaryValue.  The earnings of a company are arrived at by subtracting certain expenses and taxes from revenues.  As such, #$companyEarnings is #$netIncome as applied to instances of #$Business.  This sense of \"earnings\" can be contrasted to the related notion of \"earnings\" as applied to individual people, which refers to the money (typically, the gross) earned through employment or investments.")
(comment MultiplyAdministeredGeopoliticalEntity "Each instance of #$MultiplyAdministeredGeopoliticalEntity is a #$GeographicalAgent that is not an independent nation, but is under the control of or claimed by more than one other #$GeopoliticalEntity, either in cooperation or in dipute.  Examples include #$Antarctica-ControlledLand, which is administered by the 45 nations that are members of the Antarctic Treaty, and #$SpratlyIslands-ControlledLand, which is claimed entirely by each of #$China-PeoplesRepublic, #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina and #$Vietnam, and in part by several other nations.")
(comment Antarctica-ControlledLand "#$Antarctica-ControlledLand is a #$GeopoliticalEntity controlled cooperatively by the 45 member nations of the Antarctic Treaty.")
(comment SpratlyIslands-ControlledLand "#$SpratlyIslands-ControlledLand is a #$GeopoliticalEntity occupying a region that includes hundreds of islands in the #$SouthChinaSea (the #$SpratlyIslands).  Each of #$China-PeoplesRepublic. #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina and #$Vietnam claim the entire territory, and other nations claim portions of it.")
(comment ParacelIslands-ControlledLand "#$ParacelIslands-ControlledLand is a #$GeopoliticalEntity occupying a region that includes several islands in the #$SouthChinaSea (the #$ParacelIslands).  Each of #$China-PeoplesRepublic. #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina and #$Vietnam claim the entire territory.")
(comment ProductionRateOfByFn "<code>(#$ProductionRateOfByFn COMMODITY)</code> denotes a function that maps an instance REGION of <code>#$GeographicalRegion</code> to the production rate (see <code>#$productionRateOfRegion</code>) of COMMODITY within REGION.")
(comment PossibleWorld-Specification "A #$FirstOrderCollection and specialization of #$Specification.  Each instance of #$PossibleWorld-Specification is a maximal consistent (with respect to some set of atomic propositions closed under certain logical operations) specification of a way that things might be.
<p>
Note that philosophers and other theorists have widely diverging accounts of what possible worlds are.  This collection represents but one such account.")
(comment SAP-Company "A large software company based in Germany, traded on NYSE  as \"SAP\" (as an ADR).")
(disjointWith DepositoryReceipt Stock)
(comment physicalSchemaFieldWithName "A fully functional ternary predicate relating a physical schema, physical field, and a string. <code>(#$physicalSchemaFieldWithName SCHEMA FIELD NAME)</code> means that:
<p>
1. <code>FIELD</code> is a physical field of <code>SCHEMA</code> (See #$physicalFields);
<p>
2. <code>FIELD</code> is named <code>NAME</code> (See #$fieldName-SKS);
<p>
See also the function corresponding to the second argument of this predicate, #$PhysicalFieldFn.")
(comment PhoenixIslands-AdministrativeDivision "#$PhoenixIslands-AdministrativeDivision is one of the #$FirstOrderAdministrativeDivisions of #$Kiribati.")
(comment LineIslands-AdministrativeDivision "#$LineIslands-AdministrativeDivision is one of the #$FirstOrderAdministrativeDivisions of #$Kiribati.")
(comment physicalSchemaFieldIndexicalWithName "A fully functional ternary predicate relating a physical schema, physical field indexical, and a string. <code>(#$physicalSchemaFieldWithName SCHEMA FIELD-INDEXICAL NAME)</code> means that:
<p>
1. <code>FIELD-INDEXICAL</code> is a physical field indexical of <code>SCHEMA</code> (See #$physicalFieldIndexicals);
<p>
2. <code>FIELD-INDEXICAL</code> is associated with a unique #$PhysicalField named <code>NAME</code> (See #$indexicalForPhysicalField and #$fieldName-SKS);
<p>
See also the function corresponding to the second argument of this predicate, #$ThePhysicalFieldValueFn.")
(comment conceptFilterSpecifications "<code>(#$conceptFilterSpecifications FILTER SPECIFICATION)</code> means that <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, an instance of #$ConceptFilterSpecification, is one of the specifications for the concept filter (see #$ConceptFilter), <code>FILTER</code>.")
(comment CycLConstant-CreatedForKaniImport "The collection of constants created for the Kani system import of knowledge for the IKRIS CAPSTONE demo.  This only includes constants that were hand created for this effort and not constants that were automatically created during the import process.")
(comment kbCompatibleSentence "<code>(#$kbCompatibleSentence SENT)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is a
well-formed CycL sentence that does not contradict currently known
facts.  See also #$consistent.  #$kbCompatibleSentence is differnt
from #$consistent in that it is provable via transformation by the Cyc
inference engine.")
(comment DegreeOfLiquidity "A specialization of #$ScalarQuantity.  Instances are degrees to which instances of an an asset-type can be sold on a market.")
(comment PublicPlace "A specialization of #$Place.  Each instance of #$PublicPlace is a place that is generally accessible to the public.  If it is a place of business, accessibility might be restricted to normal business hours.")
(comment Councilor "The collection of all members of #$Council-Organizations (q.v.).")
(comment ElectricalRelay "A specialization of #$ElectricalSwitch.  Each instance of #$ElectricalRelay is an electrical device in which current flowing through it in one circuit can switch on and off a current in a second circuit.")
(comment objectHurdled "<code>(#$objectHurdled EVENT LOC)</code> means that in the #$JumpingOverSomething event <code>EVENT</code>, the thing being hurdled is <code>LOC</code>.")
(comment objectClimbed "<code>(#$objectClimbed EVENT LOC)</code> means that in the #$Climbing event <code>EVENT</code>, the thing being scaled is <code>LOC</code>.")
(comment adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicActionCollection "<code>(#$adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicActionCollection TYPE
ACTION-COL)</code> means that <code>TYPE</code> is the instance of
#$ObjectTypeByAdultHumanlyDoableAction, instances of which can be the
#$objectActedOn in instances of <code>ACTION-COL</code>.  For example,
(#$adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicActionCollection
#$HumanlyHurdlableObject #$JumpingOverSomething) means that instances
of #$HumanlyHurdlableObject are capable of being the #$objetActedOn in
instances of #$JumpingOverSomething that are done by ordinary adult humans.")
(comment adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicRoleOfObject "<code>(#$adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicRoleOfObject TYPE BIN-ROLE)</code> means the objects which are instances of <code>TYPE</code> play the role <code>BIN-ROLE</code> in instances of the action collection performed by adult humans that bears the relation #$adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicActionCollection to <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicRoleOfHuman "<code>(#$adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicRoleOfHuman TYPE BIN-ROLE)</code> means that adult humans play the role <code>BIN-ROLE</code> in instances of the action collection performed by adult humans that bears the relation #$adultHumanlyDoableCharacteristicActionCollection to <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment ObjectTypeByAdultHumanlyDoableAction "A specialization #$FirstOrderCollection,  Each instance of #$ObjectTypeByAdultHumanlyDoableAction is a collection of objects on which ordinary adult humans can, under normal conditions, do actions of a certain sort.  For example, #$HumanlyHurdlableObject is an instance of #$ObjectTypeByAdultHumanlyDoableAction.  It is the collection of objects that, in ordinary circumstances, ordinary adult humans can overleap.")
(comment physicalFieldIndexicals "(#$physicalFieldIndexicals SCHEMA INDEXICAL) means that INDEXICAL is an indexical used to denote the value in a row for a physical field in the physical schema, SCHEMA. This predicate is a #$typedGenlPreds of #$schemaFieldIndexicals. See also #$physicalFields for a similar predicate for relating a physical field to a physical schema.  Assertions using this predicate are typically inferred from forward rules.")
(comment predFindsNearest "<code>(#$predFindsNearest KB-PRED BIN-PRED)</code> means that <code>KB-PRED</code> is a \"nearest\" version of <code>BIN-PRED</code>.  For example, (#$predFindsNearest #$nearestGenls #$genls) is true, as is (#$predFindsNearest #$nearestIsa #$isa).")
(comment IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources "#$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources is the collection of all #$CWCreation events in which two or more #$StructuredKnowledgeSources are integrated to produce a new #$StructuredKnowledgeSource that is capable of storing all of the data stored in the input sources.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputLFHasTargetLF "This predicate relates an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources event with a #$LogicalField that is part of one of the input schemas and its corresponding logical field in the appropriate target schema. That is, <code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputLFHasTargetLF INTEGRATION INPUT-LF TARGET-LF)</code> means that:
<p>
1. <code>INPUT-LF</code> is a logical field in some #$ObjectDefiningSchema, <code>INPUT-ODS</code>;
<p>
2. <code>INPUT-ODS</code> is an element of some input schema set, <code>INPUT-ODS-SET</code> that is related to a target schema, <code>TARGET-ODS</code>, via #$schemaIntegrationInputODSSetHasTargetODS;
<p>
3. <code>TARGET-LF</code> is a logical field in <code>TARGET-ODS</code>;
<p>
4. <code>INPUT-LF</code> and <code>TARGET-LF</code> share the same field type and multiplicity. See #$logicalSchemaFieldOfTypeWithMultiplicity.
<p>
This predicate is used to determine the mapping from source schema meaning sentences to target schema meaning sentences.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputODSSetSubsumptionList "This predicate relates an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources to a list of length at least two of sets of #$ObjectDefiningSchemas, where each set in the list is set of input schemas for the integration all of the same type. (See #$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputODSSet). The list is ordered by the respective type corresponding to each set, using #$SetOfCollectionSpecializationListsFn. That is, <code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputODSSetSubsumptionList INTEGRATION INPUT-ODS-SET-LIST)</code> is calculated as follows:
<p>
1. Find the <code>ODS-TYPE-SET</code> for <code>INTEGRATION</code> using #$schemaIntegrationObjectFieldTypeSet;
<p>
2. Apply #$SetOfCollectionSpecializationListsFn to <code>ODS-TYPE-SET</code> to obtain <code>TYPE-SPECIALIZATION-LIST-SET</code>;
<p>
3. Take an element, <code>TYPE-SPECIALIZATION-LIST</code>, of <code>TYPE-SPECIALIZATION-LIST-SET</code> of length at least two (to avoid pathological and uninteresting cases);
<p>
4. Replace each member, <code>TYPE</code>, of <code>TYPE-SPECIALIZATION-LIST</code> with its corresponding <code>INPUT-ODS-SET</code>, found by looking up on #$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputODSSet.
<p>
This predicate is used in further analysis of the input schemas to determine the correct set of logical fields and meaning sentences for their corresponding target schemas, and to properly record schema inheritence in the target model (see #$odsExtendsODS)..")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputODSSetHasTypeMultiplicityListSet "This predicate relates a set of #$ObjectDefiningSchemas that are all input schemas of the same type for an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources event (see #$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputODSSet) to the set of multiplicity lists (see #$ListMultiplicityListFn) of the schemas' respective logical field type lists (See #$logicalSchemaFieldTypeList). That is, <code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputODSSetHasTypeMultiplicityListSet INTEGRATION INPUT-ODS-SET INPUT-ODS-TYPE-MULTIPLICITY-LIST-SET)</code> means that: <p>
1. The elements of <code>INPUT-ODS-SET</code> are all input object defining schemas in <code>INTEGRATION</code>; 
<p>
2. <code>INPUT-ODS-TYPE-MULTIPLICITY-LIST-SET</code> is the set of lists of length two obtained by first taking the <code>TYPE-LIST</code> for each of the elements of <code>INPUT-ODS-LIST</code> (obtained from the arg2 of #$logicalSchemaFieldTypeList), applying the function #$ListMultiplicityListFn to <code>TYPE-LIST</code> to obtain <code>TYPE-MULTIPLICITY-LIST-LIST</code>, applying #$SetOfListMembersFn to <code>TYPE-MULTIPLICITY-LIST-LIST</code> to obtain <code>TYPE-MULTIPLICITY-LIST-SET</code> and then finally taking the set union of the <code>TYPE-MULTIPLICITY-LIST-SET</code>s over all elements of <code>INPUT-ODS-SET</code>.
<p>
This predicate is used in further analysis of the input schemas to determine the correct set of logical fields and meaning sentences for their corresponding schemas.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputReifiedMappingSet "This predicate relates an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources, <code>INTEGRATION</code>, to the set of all #$ReifiedMappings that are related (via #$subKS, #$logicalSchemaSourceMap, #$logicalFields, and #$logicalFieldMapping) to some 'input' knowledge source (determined by #$schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet). It collects all of the #$ReifiedMappings used to translate the values of some #$LogicalField of some #$LogicalSchema that is related to some #$subKS of some member of the <code>INTEGRATION</code>'s input set of knowledge sources.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputRDSSetHasTargetRDS "This predicate is the analogue for #$RelationshipDefiningSchemas of #$schemaIntegrationInputODSSetHasTargetODS. <code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputRDSSetHasTargetRDS INTEGRATION INPUT-RDS-SET TARGET-RDS)</code> means that in the SKS schema integration <code>INTEGRATION</code> (see #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources), <code>TARGET-RDS</code> is the relationship defining schema in the target knowledge source that unifies all of the input relationship defining schemas in <code>TARGET-RDS-SET</code>.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputODSSet "This predicate relates an instance of #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources to the set of all #$ObjectDefiningSchemas that are related (via #$subKS and #$logicalSchemaSourceMap) to some 'input' knowledge source (determined by #$schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet).")
(comment schemaIntegrationPredicateForInputImplicitRDSSet "This predicate is analogous to #$schemaIntegrationPredicateForInputExplicitRDSSet, however it relates an instance of #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources with a #$Predicate and the set of <i>implicitly defined</i> #$RelationshipDefiningSchemas for which the predicate expresses the meaning of the relationship in #$CycL.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputODSSetHasTargetODS "<code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputODSSetHasTargetODS INTEGRATION INPUT-ODS-SET TARGET-ODS)</code> means that in the SKS schema integration <code>INTEGRATION</code> (see #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources), <code>TARGET-ODS</code> is the object defining schema in the target knowledge source that unifies all of the input object defining schemas in <code>INPUT-ODS-SET</code>.")
(comment schemaIntegrationTargetSubSKS "If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources and <code>SKS</code> is a #$StructuredKnowledgeSource, then <code>(#$schemaIntegrationTargetSubSKS INTEGRATION SKS)</code> means that <code>SKS</code> is one of perhaps several structured knowledge sources that are part of (see #$subKS) the 'top-level' structured knowledge source that is the target of <code>INTEGRATION</code>. See #$schemaIntegrationTargetSKS.")
(comment TargetSubSKSForODSFn "The function corresponding to the third argument of #$schemaIntegrationODSHasTargetSubSKS. That is, if <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources and <code>ODS</code> is an #$ObjectDefiningSchema, then <code>(#$TargetSubSKSForODSFn INTEGRATION ODS)</code> denotes the target sub-knowledge source associated with <code>ODS</code> in <code>INTEGRATION</code>.")
(comment schemaIntegrationODSHasTargetSubSKS "If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources, <code>ODS</code> is an #$ObjectDefiningSchema, and <code>SKS</code> is a #$StructuredKnowledgeSource, then <code>(#$schemaIntegrationODSHasTargetSubSKS INTEGRATION ODS SKS)</code> means that <code>SKS</code> is the target sub-knowledge source of <code>INTEGRATION</code> (see #$schemaIntegrationTargetSubSKS) that is associated with the target object defining schema <code>ODS</code>. See #$schemaIntegrationTypeForTargetODS.")
(comment TargetODSOfTypeFn "The function corresponding to the third argument of #$schemaIntegrationTypeForTargetODS. If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources event and <code>COLL</code> is a collection, then <code>(#$TargetODSOfTypeFn INTEGRATION COLL)</code> denotes the #$ObjectDefiningSchema of type <code>COLL</code> associated with the <code>INTEGRATION</code> event.")
(comment schemaIntegrationTypeForTargetODS "If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources, <code>COLL</code> is a #$Collection, and <code>ODS</code> is an #$ObjectDefiningSchema, then <code>(#$schemaIntegrationTypeForTargetODS INTEGRATION COLL ODS)</code> means that <code>ODS</code> is the target object defining schema of type <code>COLL</code> (see #$schemaIsa) in the schema integration event <code>INTEGRATION</code>.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputReifiedMappingTypeSet "If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources and <code>INPUT-SET</code> is the set of input sources to be integrated (see #$schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet), then <code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputReifiedMappingTypeSet INTEGRATION TYPE-SET)</code> means that <code>TYPE-SET</code> is the set of types such that a field associated with some element of INPUT-SET has that type and has values that are specified by a #$ReifiedMapping.

Typically, the elements of <code>INPUT-SET</code> are related to some element of <code>TYPE-SET</code> as follows: For each <code>TOP-KS</code> element of <code>INPUT-SET</code> find its 'parts' via #$subKS. For each of these parts, find the element of <code>TYPE-SET</code> by looking up on #$sourceCMLSFieldType.")
(comment schemaIntegrationObjectTypeFromODS "(#$schemaIntegrationObjectTypeFromODS INTEGRATION COLL SOURCE-ODS) means that the instance of #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources, INTEGRATION, must produce a table that defines an object that is an instance of COLL and that the need to do so is motivated by the source knowledge source having an non-ReifiedMapping schema that defines this sort of object.")
(comment schemaIntegrationObjectFieldTypeSet "If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources and <code>INPUT-SET</code> is the set of input sources to be integrated (see #$schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet), then <code>(#$schemaIntegrationObjectFieldTypeSet INTEGRATION TYPE-SET)</code> means that <code>TYPE-SET</code> is the set of the object field types associated with some element of <code>INPUT-SET</code>. 
<p>
Typically, the elements of <code>INPUT-SET</code> are related to some element of <code>TYPE-SET</code> as follows: For each <code>TOP-KS</code> element of <code>INPUT-SET</code> find its 'parts' via #$subKS. For each of these parts, find the element of <code>TYPE-SET</code> by looking up on #$objectFieldTypeForSource.")
(comment schemaIntegrationTypeForInputODSSet "If <code>INTEGRATION</code> is an #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources, <code>INPUT-ODS-SET</code> is the set of input object defining schemas to be integrated (see #$schemaIntegrationInputODSSet), and <code>TYPE</code> is one of the object field types associated with <code>INTEGRATION</code> (see #$schemaIntegrationObjectFieldTypeSet), then <code>(#$schemaIntegrationTypeForInputODSSet INTEGRATION TYPE ODS-SET)</code> means that each element of <code>INPUT-ODS-SET</code> is an object defining schema (see #$ObjectDefiningSchema) of type <code>TYPE</code> (see #$schemaIsa) that is associated with some element of <code>INPUT-SET</code>.")
(comment schemaIntegrationTargetSKS "<code>(#$schemaIntegrationTargetSKS INTEGRATION TARGET)</code> means that <code>TARGET</code> is the target, or fused #$StructuredKnowledgeSource that is the product of the knowledge source integration event <code>INTEGRATION</code>. See also #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources and #$schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet.")
(comment schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet "<code>(#$schemaIntegrationInputSKSSet INTEGRATION SKS-SET)</code> means that <code>SKS-SET</code> is the set of source, or input #$StructuredKnowledgeSources that are integrated in <code>INTEGRATION</code>. See slso #$IntegratingASetOfKnowledgeSources and #$schemaIntegrationTargetSKS.")
(comment programHasProcessRunningType "This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$ProgramProcessFn.")
(comment ObjectTypeByTaste "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ObjectTypeByTaste is a collection of instances of #$PartiallyTangible that share some particular qualitative taste.  Some important instances are #$SaltyTaste, #$BitterTaste, #$SweetTaste, and #$SourTaste.  Instances of #$ObjectTypeByTaste can also be functionally denoted using #$TasteFn, e.g., (#$TasteFn #$Pizza) returns the collection of all instances of #$PartiallyTangible that have the taste of pizza.")
(comment InformationCenter "Any single-site organization that provides free information on a walk-in basis.  Examples include an information counter at an airport and a tourist information office in a city.")
(comment ILPProgramProcess "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of
#$ILPProgramProcess is a computer process in which an inductive logic
programming program (e.g. #$ALEPH-ILPProgram) is performing induction
to discover rules.")
(comment determinationOfILPProcess "<code>(#$determinationOfILPProcess ILP-PROCESS DETERMINATION)</code>
means that <code>DETERMINATION</code> enumerates the predicates that
are investigated during <code>ILP-PROCESS</code>.")
(comment modeDeclarationStrategyOfILPProcess "<code>(#$determinationOfILPProcess ILP-PROCESS STRATEGY)</code>
means that <code>STRATEGY</code> is the context from which mode declarations are calculated for <code>ILP-PROCESS</code>.")
(comment infoStoreOfILPProcess "<code>(#$infoStoreOfILPProcess ILP-PROCESS INFO-STORE)</code> means that
<code>INFO-STORE</code> is the information repository used with
<code>ILP-PROCESS</code>.")
(comment VillageLeader "A specialization of #$Mayor each instance of which is the leader of a #$Village.  In the muslim world, a village leader is known as a \"mukhtar\".")
(comment RetirementHome "A specialization of #$ApartmentBuilding.  Each instance of #$RetirementHome is a building consisting of multiple individual residences designed specifically for the elderly.  Retirement homes typically also have communal dining and socializing areas.")
(comment FighterPlane-F117 "The #$FighterPlane-F117 Nighthawk is the first operational stealth fighter jet, first delivered to the US Air Force in 1982 by Lockheed.")
(comment NasdaqCompositeIndex "A broad based index of securities, each of which is traded on the NASDAQ over-the-counter system.")
(comment cycLFormulaOutputByILPProcess "<code>(#$cycLFormulaOutputByILPProcess PROCESS FORMULA)</code> means that
<code>FORMULA</code> is a #$CycLFormula output by <code>PROCESS</code> (an instance of #$ILPProgramProcess).")
(comment PeaceWall "A specialization of #$Wall-Vertical.  Each instance of #$PeaceWall is a wall or fence decorated (with paintings, murals, tiles, etc.) for the purpose of advocating peace.")
(comment DigitalAudioFilePlayer "A specialization of #$AudioEquipment and #$MediaPlayingDevice.  Each instance of #$DigitalAudioFilePlayer is a device whose intended purpose is to play digital audio files.")
(comment IPod "An instance of #$ProductTypeByBrand.  Each instance of #$IPod is a portable digital media playing device manufactured by #$AppleInc.")
(comment NonVolatileMemory "A specialization of #$ComputerStorageDevice. Each instance of #$NonVolatileMemory is a computer storage device that has the ability to retain data even when not powered.")
(comment VolatileMemory "A specialization of #$ComputerStorageDevice. Each instance of #$VolatileMemory is a computer storage device that must be powered in order to retain data.")
(disjointWith NonVolatileMemory VolatileMemory)
(comment FlashMemory "A specialization of #$ComputerStorageDevice. Each instance of #$FlashMemory is a computer storage device that non-volatile computer memory device that can be electrically erased and reprogrammed .")
(disjointWith FlashMemory MagneticComputerStorageDevice)
(comment omitFromILP "<code>(#$omitFromILP TERM)</code> means that the #$CycLIndexedTerm <code>TERM</code> should not be included in ILP predicate determinations.")
(comment dontUseLexicalAssertionForParaphraseInApplication "<code>(#$dontUseLexicalAssertionForParaphraseInApplication LEX-AS APP)</code> means that when doing paraphrase in the context of <code>APP</code>, <code>LEX-AS</code> should not be used.")
(comment queryHasVeryHighPertinenceForType "<code>(#$queryHasVeryHighPertinenceForType QUERY TYPE)</code> means that the #$CycLQuerySpecification <code>QUERY</code> contains information that would be appropriate, interesting, or othewise useful to ask about instance of <code>TYPE</code>, some #$Collection.")
(comment AstronomicalObject "A specialization of #$InanimateObject-Natural.  The collection of all things of the types studied by astronomers.  Each instance of #$AstronomicalObject is a (usually quite large) natural, inanimate object that is located in the physical universe and is not on the surface of the Earth.  (But note that #$PlanetEarth itself <i>is</i> an instance of this collection.)  An 
#$AstronomicalObject might be either an individual heavenly body (see 
#$AstronomicalBody) or a group or system made up of such bodies (see e.g. 
#$Galaxy and #$PlanetarySystem).  See also the specialization 
#$CelestialObject, instances of which are visible from the Earth.")
(comment FindOrCreateConstantNamedFn "A #$CycL wrapper around the SubL function <code>CYC-FIND-OR-CREATE-NEW-PERMANENT</code>. Evaluating <code>(#$FindOrCreateConstantNamedFn NAME)</code> either finds and returns the #$CycLConstant named <code>NAME</code>, or creates a new constant named <code>NAME</code> and returns it.")
(comment BalconyDoorway "A specialization of #$Doorway.  Each instance of #$BalconyDoorway is a doorway between the interior of a building and a balcony of that building.")
(comment BalconyDoor "A specialization of #$DoorInABuilding-Exterior.  Each instance of #$BalconyDoor is a door that covers a #$BalconyDoorway (q.v.).")
(comment GarageDoorway "A specialization of #$Doorway.  Each instance of #$GarageDoorway is a doorway between the interior of a garage and the outdoors.")
(comment StaphylococcusAureus "A species of #$Staphylococcus (q.v.).  Each instance of  #$StaphylococcusAureus is bacterium, capable of surviving on the skin or in the nose of an otherwise healthy #$HomoSapiens.")
(comment MethicillinResistantStaphylococcusAureus "A variety of of #$StaphylococcusAureus (q.v.).  Methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus is resistant to treatment by antibiotics, even methicillin.")
(comment OilExportTerminal "The collection of #$OilTerminals where oil
is transferred to a conveyance for exporting.")
(comment TemporaryJobEmploymentAgency "Each instance of #$TemporaryJobEmploymentAgency is an #$EmploymentOrganization that helps job-seekers find #$TemporaryJobPositions.")
(comment ElectionCommittee "The collection of instances of #$Committee-Organization that are organized in connection with some #$Election, either (a) to run the #$PoliticalElectionCampaign of an #$ElectoralCandidate for an office or (b) to try to help pass or defeat a certain ballot measure.")
(comment FictionalContext "A #$MicrotheoryType that is a specialization of #$PropositionalInformationThing (qq.v.). Most instances of #$FictionalContext represents things explicitly from the point of view of some work of fiction (see #$FictionalPCW).  But there are exceptions.  There can be a context derived from a government report in a fictional work that is itself a fictional context (e.g. the context of a report from the resurrected Soviet Union in a new political thriller from Tom Clancy is a fictional context).  But the report itself, in the context of the fictional work, is nonfiction. Presumably, since the report does not actually exist, it is neither fiction nor nonfiction in the context of the actual world. 
<p>
In general, a #$FictionalContext is assumed to include many assertions that are widely believed to be false or questionable.  Such assertions might or might not be about actually-existing things.  For example, the fictional context associated with the Sherlock Holmes stories contains assertions about London as well as assertions about Holmes.
<p>
Note that the work associated with a given fictional context must have been created intentionally, and not by error or chance or gradual evolution and accretion in a culture.
<p>
Cf. #$NonfictionalContext.")
(comment FictionalOrMythologicalContext "A specialization of #$ConjecturalContext.  Most instances of #$FictionalOrMythologicalContext are microtheories which are derived from the contents of fictional or mythological works or legends.  There are exceptions having to do with fictional accounts of nonfiction works -- Zeus's \"state of the Heavens\" address, in the context of Greek mythology, is a nonfiction report, but any context derived from it will be a #$FictionalOrMythologicalContext.")
(comment NonfictionalContext "A #$MicrotheoryType that is a specialization of #$PropositionalInformationThing (qq.v.). Each instance of #$NonfictionalContext is an informational microtheory that represents things explicitly from the point of view of some work of nonfiction (see #$NonfictionalPCW). 
<p>
Note that it is possible for a #$NonfictionalContext to contain a large number of statements that are false in the actual world since many nonfiction works contain a large number of incorrect/false statements.
<p>
Cf. #$FictionalContext.")
(disjointWith LaboratoryEquipment SportsEquipment)
(comment LaboratoryEquipment "A specialization of #$Artifact-NonAgentive and #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$LaboratoryEquipment is a toll or piece of equipment used by scientists to perform or record experiments in laboratories.  Examples include #$TestTubes and #$BunsenBurners.")
(comment TestTube "Cylinder like containers for keeping liquids, usually in labs.")
(disjointWith BunsenBurner GasStoveBurner)
(comment BunsenBurner "A specialization of #$CombustionHeatingElement and #$LaboratoryEquipment.  Bunsen burners are laboratory devices designed to safely burn continuous streams of flammable gas.")
(comment HeatingElement "A collection of focussed heat producing devices.  An instance of #$HeatingElement may be a heating coil, stove top burner, #$BunsenBurner, etc.  Heating elements are among the #$physicalParts of many kinds of heating devices, such as #$Ovens, heaters, toasters, #$CoffeeMakers, etc.")
(comment PetriDish "Small flat dish - a piece of scientific glassware - used in scientific experiments and study.")
(comment Aspirator-LaboratoryEquipment "A specialization of #$LaboratoryEquipment.  Each instance of #$Aspirator-LaboratoryEquipment is a device used to produce vacuum by means of the Venturi effect.")
(comment WaterAspirator-LaboratoryEquipment "A specialization of #$Aspirator-LaboratoryEquipment.  Each instance of #$WaterAspirator-LaboratoryEquipment is a device with which liquid water is used to produce a vacuum by means of the Venturi effect.")
(comment SteamEjector-LaboratoryEquipment "A specialization of #$Aspirator-LaboratoryEquipment.  Each instance of #$SteamEjector-LaboratoryEquipment is a device with which water vapor is used to produce a vacuum by means of the Venturi effect.")
(comment AirEjector-LaboratoryEquipment "A specialization of #$Aspirator-LaboratoryEquipment.  Each instance of #$AirEjector-LaboratoryEquipment is a device with which high pressure air is used to produce a vacuum by means of the Venturi effect.")
(comment Vacuum "A specialization of #$FreeSpaceRegion whose instances are connected regions of completely empty space (i.e. space that contains absolutely no tangible material) located in the empirically observable universe.")
(disjointWith ElectronMicroscope Microscope-Optical)
(comment Microscope-Optical "A specialization of #$Microscope.  Each instance of #$Microscope-Optical is a microscope that uses a refractive lens to magnify the visual image of a small object.")
(comment ScanningElectronMicroscope "A specialization of #$ElectronMicroscope.  Each instance of #$ScanningElectronMicroscope is a microscope that scans the surface of an object with a fine electron beam and measuring reflection to produce a magnified image of the scanned object.")
(disjointWith ScanningElectronMicroscope TransmissionElectronMicroscope)
(comment TransmissionElectronMicroscope "A specialization of #$ElectronMicroscope.  Each instance of #$TransmissionElectronMicroscope is a microscope that passes electrons completely through the sample being examined, thereby gaining information about the sample's crystallography through diffraction.")
(disjointWith Microscope-Optical ScanningProbeMicroscope)
(comment ScanningProbeMicroscope "A specialization of #$Microscope.  Each instance of #$ScanningProbeMicroscope is a microscope that generates a micrograph by rastering a physical probe across the surface of a sample.")
(comment AtomicForceMicroscope "A specialization of #$ScanningProbeMicroscope.")
(disjointWith ScanningTunnelingMicroscope AtomicForceMicroscope)
(comment ScanningTunnelingMicroscope "A specialization of #$ScanningProbeMicroscope.  Each instance of #$ScanningTunnelingMicroscope is a microscope that generates a micrograph by rastering an electrical probe over the surface of the sample to detect a weak electric current flowing between the tip of the probe and the surface of the sample.")
(disjointWith AtomicForceMicroscope MagneticForceMicroscope)
(disjointWith ScanningTunnelingMicroscope MagneticForceMicroscope)
(comment MagneticForceMicroscope "A specialization of #$ScanningProbeMicroscope. Each instance of #$MagneticForceMicroscope is a microscope that produces an image from measuring the magnetic interaction between a sample and a tip.")
(comment LaboratoryThermometer "Thermometers that are normally used for scientific purposes.")
(disjointWith LaboratoryThermometer MedicalThermometer)
(disjointWith MeatThermometer MedicalThermometer)
(disjointWith LaboratoryThermometer MeatThermometer)
(comment MeatThermometer "A specialization of #$Thermometer.  Each instance of #$MeatThermometer is a thermometer designed to measure the internal temperature of meat.")
(disjointWith CandyThermometer MedicalThermometer)
(disjointWith LaboratoryThermometer CandyThermometer)
(comment CandyThermometer "A specialization of #$Thermometer.  Each instance of #$CandyThermometer is a thermometer used to measure the temperature of a cooking sugar solution. Candy thermometers are similar to meat thermometers (see #$MeatThermometer) but they can read higher temperatures.")
(disjointWith MeatThermometer CandyThermometer)
(comment FumeHood "A specialization of #$LaboratoryEquipment. Each instance of #$FumeHood is a sheild to designed to limit exposure to hazardous fumes.")
(comment Photometer "A specialization of #$MeasuringDevice.  Each instance of #$Photometer is a device used to measure the intensity of light.")
(comment Spectrophotometer "A specialization of #$LaboratoryEquipment and #$Photometer (qq.v.). Each instance of #$Spectrophotometer is a photometer that measures light intensity as a function of its wavelength.")
(comment Colorimeter "A specialization of #$MeasuringDevice.  Each instance of #$Colorimeter is a device used in chemistry to determine the absorbance of a solution at a particular frequency of visible light.")
(comment Calorimeter "A specialization of #$MeasuringDevice.  Each instance of #$Calorimeter is a device used  to measure the heat of chemical reactions.")
(comment MicrotiterPlate "A specialization of #$LaboratoryEquipment. Each instance of #$MicrotiterPlate is a plate with small indentations, or \"wells\" that are used as small test tubes.")
(comment Beaker-LabGlassware "A specialization of #$LaboratoryEquipment. Each instance of #$Beaker-LabGlassware is a cylindrical glass or plastic container, open at the top with a flat bottom.  Beakers ore typically graduated.")
(comment LaboratoryGlassware "A specialization of #$LaboratoryEquipment.  Each instance of #$LaboratoryGlassware is glassware desgned to be used in a laboratory setting, for experiments.  Important specializations include #$TestTube and #$Flask-LabGlassware.")
(comment MotorOil "A specialization of #$Oil and #$Lubricant.  Each instance of #$MotorOil is some portion of oil initially intended to be used for lubrication by various kinds internal combustion engines.")
(comment MotorOil-PetroliumDerived "A specialization of #$MotorOil and #$PetroleumProduct-Refined.  Each instance of #$MotorOil-PetroliumDerived  a motor oil derived from petrolium.  Cf. #$MotorOil-Synthetic.")
(disjointWith MotorOil-PetroliumDerived MotorOil-Synthetic)
(comment MotorOil-Synthetic "A specialization of #$MotorOil.  Each instance of #$MotorOil-Synthetic is  a motor oil consisting of artificially-synthesized compounds.  Cf. #$MotorOil-PetroliumDerived.")
(comment Beeswax "A specialization of #$Wax.  Beeswax is a product of #$Honeybees, who use it to build honey comb cells as spaces in which to raise their young and to store and honey and pollen.  People harvest beeswax to make polishes and candles, among other things.")
(comment availableFrom-Type "<code>(#$availableFrom-Type OBJ TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>TYPE</code> are available from <code>OBJ</code>.  For example (#$availableFrom-Type #$Sothebys-CommercialOrganization #$ArtObject) means that art objects are available from Sotheby's (see #$brokersProductType), and <code>(#$availableFrom-Type PecanTree001 (#$FruitFn #$PecanTree))</code> means that pecans are available from pecan tree 001.")
(comment availableFrom "<code>(#$availableFrom OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that <code>OBJ2</code> is available from <code>OBJ2</code>.  For example <code>(#$availableFrom PecanTree001 Pecan007)</code> means that <code>Pecan007</code> is available from <code>PecanTree001</code> and <code>(#$availableFrom #$EbayInc FireTruck001)</code> means <code>FireTruck001</code> is available from Ebay.")
(comment productOfAnimal "<code>(#$productOfAnimal ANIMAL PRODUCT)</code> means that <code>ANIMAL</code> is the source of <code>PRODUCT</code>.  For example <code>(#$productOfAnimal Sheep001 Wool001)</code> means that Sheep001 is the source of Wool001.")
(comment TransNeptunianObject "The collection of all objects that reside in the solar system beyond #$PlanetNeptune.")
(disjointWith TransNeptunianObject Asteroid)
(comment Rubber "A collection of material that is solid and flexible, and used to make bouncing balls and galoshes, among other things.  Some ruber is synthetic (see #$Rubber-Synthetic, and some is not (see #$Rubber-TheNaturalStuff).")
(comment Neoprene "A specialization of #$Rubber-Synthetic.  #$Neoprene was invened at DuPont and is based on polychloroprene.")
(comment ButylRubber "A specialization of #$Rubber-Synthetic.  Butyl rubber is a synthetic rubber also known as \"polyisobutylene\".")
(disjointWith Neoprene ButylRubber)
(comment relativeDensity "<code>(#$relativeDensity STUFF1 TEMP1 STUFF2 TEMP2 RATIO)</code> means that the ratio of <code>STUFF1</code>'s density at <code>TEMP1</code> to <code>STUFF2</code>'s density at <code>TEMP2</code> is <code>RATIO</code>. This concept is also known as \"specific gravity\".")
(comment apiGravity "#$apiGravity is a specific gravity scale used for petroleum liquids based on the relative density of the liquid to water at 60 degrees Fahrenheit. It was developed by the #$AmericanPetroleumInstitute.")
(comment CoastlineFn "<code>(#$CoastlineFn REG)</code> denotes the entirety of the coastline of the region <code>REG</code>. This may involve a few discontinuous pieces, as with (#$CoastlineFn #$Spain). The coastline of a region may include the coast of an #$InlandSea, if that inland sea provides easy access to #$EarthsOceanSea. For example, #$Iran's piece of the #$CaspianSea does not count as part of the (#$CoastlineFn #$Iran), since the #$CaspianSea provides no ocean access; but #$Ukraine's border with the #$BlackSea does count as part of the (#$CoastlineFn #$Ukraine), since the #$BlackSea provides access to the #$MediterraneanSea.")
(comment KeyOfLock "A specialization of #$RigidPortableObject and #$Device-UserPowered.  Each instance of #$KeyOfLock is a key intended to open a certain lock or locks.")
(disjointWith KillingByOrganism ProducingMusicalSound)
(disjointWith Country Band-MusicGroup)
(disjointWith InternationalOrganizationOfCountries OrganizationOfPeopleOnly)
(comment Fault-Topographical "A specialization of #$LandTopographicalFeature and #$Crevice.  Each instance of #$Fault-Topographical is a fracture in the Earth's crust in which the adjacent surfaces are displaced with respect to each other in a direction parallel to the fracture.  Faults are caused by a shifting or dislodging of the Earth's crust. Energy release during rapid slippage along faults causes earthquakes (see #$Earthquake).")
(comment CanOpener "The collection of can openers.  Important specializations include #$ManualCanOpener and #$ElectricCanOpener (qq.v).")
(disjointWith ManualCanOpener ElectricCanOpener)
(comment BottleOpener "The collection of bottle openers.")
(comment LemonZester "A specialization of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice.  Lemon zesters are used to remove lemon zest from lemon skins.")
(comment GarlicPress "A specialization of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice.  Garlic presses are used to crush garlic.")
(comment CheeseGrater "A specialization of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice.  Cheese graters are used to shred cheese.")
(comment instanceDiffersFromPrototypicalInstance-Addition "(#$instanceDiffersFromPrototypicalInstance-Addition INST TYPE SCRIPT ADDITION) means that the assertion ADDITION references INST, and when INST is compared with a protototypical instance of TYPE generated by propagating the assertions in SCRIPT to deductive closure, no comparable assertion (an assertion formed by substituting occurrences of the prototype for occurrences of INST) is found for the prototype.")
(comment instanceDiffersFromPrototypicalInstance-Lacuna "(#$instanceDiffersFromPrototypicalInstance-Lacuna INST TYPE SCRIPT LACUNA) means that when INST is compared with a prototypical instance of TYPE generated by propagating the assertions in SCRIPT to deductive closure, the assertio LACUNAE is found referencing the prototypical instance, and no comparable assertion (an assertion formed by substituting occurrence of INST for occurrences of the prototype) is found for INST.")
(comment instanceDiffersFromPrototypicalInstance-Conflict "Where CONFLICT is an ordered pair of assertions, (#$instanceDiffersFromPrototypicalInstance-Conflict INST TYPE SCRIPT CONFLICT) means that the pair of assertions in CONFLICT is such that the first assertion references INST, and the second assertion is in the deductive closure produced by forward-propagating the assertions in SCRIPT on a hypothesized instance of TYPE, and if INST were substituted for the hypothesized instance occurring in the second assertion, a contradiction would result.")
(comment Crumpling "A collection of events.  A #$Crumpling event is an event of #$ShapeChangeWithoutRemovingMaterial in which some particular sheetlike object (e.g., a piece of paper, a cloth sheet, or a fender) is crumpled.")
(comment Crumpled "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing.  Each instnce of #$Crumpled is an object that has gone through a #$Crumpling - no longer sheet-shaped, but now wrinkled and probably roughly ball-shaped.")
(comment Crushed-Fragmented "A specialization of (#$GroupFn #$PartiallyTangible).  Each instance of  #$Crushed-Fragmented is a group of things that were parts of larger objects that went through a #$PulverizationEvent. Such groups consist of pieces of those objects.")
(comment crushedFormOfType "(#$crushedFormOfType CRUSHED TYPE) means that CRUSHED the crushed form of TYPE, that instances of CRUSHED are all derived from some instance or instances of TYPE via a #$PulverizationEvent.")
(comment Epilogue-PCW "A specialization of #$TextualPCW.  Each instance of #$Epilogue-PCW is a short passage intended to be published at the end of a larger literary work.")
(disjointWith Epilogue-PCW Prologue-PCW)
(comment Prologue-PCW "A specialization of #$TextualPCW.  Each instance of #$Epilogue-PCW is a short passage intended to be published at the beginning of a larger literary work.")
(comment SoftwareAgent "The collection of all software agents. A software agent is a complex object consisting in a physical platform (a machine or a network of machines that is a Universal Turing Machine-equivalent) with at least one associated #$ComputerProcessRunning, such that said process can be interpreted as operations on internal propositional representations that confer an ability to make assertions to and requests of other instances of #$SoftwareAgent. 'Associating' a software agent with an instance of #$ComputerProcessRunning is analogous to 'associating' an animal agent with an instance of #$BiologicalEvent that is the event of its mental and physiological processes.")
(comment AlmondTree "A type of #$FruitTree, instances of which yield almonds.")
(comment HazelTree "A type of #$FruitTree, instances of which yield almonds.")
(comment EdibleNut "The nuts that people typically eat.This is the commonsense, not botanical definition, so #$EdibleNut has specializations such as (#$SeedFn #$PeanutPlant).")
(comment IAUStandardsAndDefinitionsMt "An instance of #$TheoryMicrotheory whose contents reflect the definitions and standards for usage of terms in the field of astronomy as established by the #$InternationalAstronomicalUnion.")
(disjointWith PlanetInTheSolarSystem DwarfPlanet)
(comment PlanetInTheSolarSystem "An instance of #$ConventionalClassificationType  defined by the #$InternationalAstronomicalUnion as the collection of celestial bodies such that each instance 1) orbits the sun (see #$TheSun), 2) has sufficient gravity to force it into having a round shape, and 3) has \"cleared\" the area around its orbit of other bodies.  Contrast with #$DwarfPlanet.")
(comment most "A binary #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  <code>(#$most SOC1 SOC2)</code> means that more than #$half of the elements of <code>SOC1</code> are elements of <code>SOC2</code>.
<p>
Note that <code>(#$most SOC1 SOC2)</code> holds trivially when <code>SOC1</code> is empty; for in that case, 100% of the elements of <code>SOC1</code> are elements of <code>SOC2</code>.")
(disjointWith DwarfPlanet MoonOfAPlanet)
(comment MusicalComposition-Chant "The collection of #$MusicalCompositions that are considered 'classical', rather than popular. In the sphere of influence of Western Europe, instances are members of a tradition that started with the rise of counterpoint and modern conceptions of harmony around the 17th century.")
(comment namedAfter "A binary predicate that relates one instance  of #$Thing to another.  <code>(#$namedAfter NAMED SOURCE)</code> means that a commonly used term for <code>NAMED</code> is derived from a commonly used term for <code>SOURCE</code>.  Many things may be named after a single thing.  For example, #$WashingtonMonumentInWashingtonDC and #$Washington-State are both named after #$GeorgeWashington.  Also, one thing can be named after more than one other thing.  For example, #$ZermeloFraenkelSetTheory is named after #$AdolfFraenkel and #$ErnstZermelo.")
(comment GregorianChantMusic "The collection of all Gregorian chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Gregorian chant music.")
(comment AmbrosianChantMusic "The collection of all Ambrosian chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Ambrosian chant music.")
(comment MozarabicChantMusic "The collection of all Mozarabic chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Mosarabic chant music.")
(comment BeneventanChantMusic "The collection of all Mozarabic chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Mosarabic chant music.")
(comment CityState "The collection of geopolitical entities that are cities and states. Currently a singleton in Cyc, its unique element being
#$VaticanCity.")
(comment capitalCity "The predicate #$capitalCity is used to relate a geopolitical entity to its capital.  <code>(#$capitalCity GEO CITY)</code> means that <code>CITY</code> is the capital city of the #$GeopoliticalEntity <code>GEO</code>.  #$capitalCity is an #$AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate, because whenever <code>(#$capitalCity X Y)</code> and <code>(#$capitalCity Y X)</code> are both true, <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code> are identical (e.g. in the case of #$CityStates, such as #$VaticanCity). Examples: the #$capitalCity of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica is the #$CityOfWashingtonDC; the #$capitalCity of #$AmericanSamoa is #$CityOfPagoPagoSamoa.  Note: to relate an instance of #$State-Geopolitical to its capital, use the more specialized predicate #$capitalCityOfState.")
(comment CycLSentence "The collection of syntactically well-formed sentences of the CycL language.  Each instance of #$CycLSentence consists of a CycL expression denoting an instance of #$TruthFunction (e.g. an instance of #$Predicate or #$SententialRelation) followed by one or more CycL terms (see #$CycLTerm), with the entire sequence enclosed in parentheses.  
<p>
For example, (#$isa #$Collection #$Thing) and (#$genls ?FOO #$SpatialThing) are both CycL sentences.  Note that #$CycLSentences <i>need not</i> obey arity constraints (see #$arity) or other semantic constraints (such as argument type constraints; see #$ArgTypePredicate).  Thus, for example, (#$genls ?FOO #$SpatialThing #$EiffelTower) is a CycL sentence.
<p>
#$CycLSentences are also called \"logical formulas\", and are to be distinguished from \"denotational formulas\" (which are also known as \"NAT\"s; see #$CycLNonAtomicTerms).  Note that this notion of a CycL sentence is broader than the notion of \"sentence\" standardly used in formal logic, where a sentence is defined as a <i>closed</i> well-formed formula: CycL sentences may be <i>open</i> (i.e. they may contain free variables; see the specialization #$CycLOpenSentence).")
(comment assertionSentence "<code>(#$assertionSentence ASSERTION SENT)</code> means that in the #$CycLAssertion <code>ASSERTION</code>, the statement asserted is what is represented by the CycL sentence (more precisely, the #$CycLSentence-Assertible) <code>SENT</code>.  Note that each assertion will have exactly one corresponding sentence (though it's worth noting that after canonicalization this sentence may appear in the browser in another, albeit logically equivalent, form -- particularly if it 'polycanonicalizes', cf. #$MetaAssertionsForPolycanonicalizingAssertions).
<p>
Note, however, that some instances of #$CycLSentence-Assertible may correspond to more than one #$CycLAssertion. For example, the formula (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle) might appear in the following:
<p>
(#$ist #$SportsMt (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle)) and
(#$ist #$CyclistsMt (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle)).
<p>
In other words, since any given #$CycLAssertion is asserted in the Cyc KB in a particular microtheory, any time an #$CycLSentence-Assertible is asserted in multiple microtheories the resulting assertions in each of those microtheories will share the common sentence. See also #$assertionTruth, #$assertionStrength  and #$assertionMt.")
(comment assertionVerifiedByInduction "<code>(#$assertionVerifiedByInduction PROG-CW ASSERTION)</code> means that <code>ASSERTION</code> is determined to have a true sentence by a running process of <code>PROG-CW</code>, and that <code>ASSERTION</code> was already present in the Cyc KB, prior to the running of the inductive process that verified it.")
(comment assertionDiscoveredByInduction "<code>(#$assertionDiscoveredByInduction PROG-CW ASSERTION)</code> means
that the sentgence of <code>ASSERTION</code> is determined to be true by
the program <code>PROG-CW</code>, and <code>ASSERTION</code> was not present in the Cyc KB prior to being discovered by <code>PROG-CW</code>.")
(comment assertionSupportedByILPProcess "<code>(#$assertionSupportedByILPProcess ILP-PROCESS ASSERTION)</code> means
that <code>PROG-CW</code> discovered a sentence strictly more specific
than the sentence corresponding to the existing KB assertion <code>ASSERTION</code>. <code>ASSERTION</code> is therefore supported by <code>PROG-CW</code>.")
(comment ChristianMonophonicChantMusic "A specialization of #$ChantMusic.  Christian monophonic chant music is the collection of sequences of sounds that constitute traditional songs used in the liturgies of Christian Churches.")
(comment ChristianMonophonicChantMusic-EasternOrthodox "A specialization of #$ChantMusic.  Christian monophonic chant music is the collection of sequences of sounds that constitute traditional songs used in the liturgies of the Eastern Orthodox Catholic Church.")
(comment ChristianMonophonicChantMusic-RomanCatholic "A specialization of #$ChantMusic.  Christian monophonic chant music is the collection of sequences of sounds that constitute traditional songs used in the liturgies of the Eastern Orthodox Catholic Church.")
(comment ArmenianChantMusic "The collection of all Armenian chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Armenian chant music.")
(comment ByzantineChantMusic "The collection of all Byzantine chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Byzantine chant music.")
(comment RussianChantMusic "The collection of all Russian chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Russian chant music.")
(comment SyrianChantMusic "The collection of all Russian chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Syrian chant music.")
(comment GallicanChantMusic "The collection of all Gallican chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Gallican chant music.")
(comment OldRomanChantMusic "The collection of all Old Roman chant music -- sequences of sounds that constitute Celtic chant music.")
(comment MariachiBand "The collection of all bands that play #$MariachiMusic.")
(comment ShieldVolcano "A specialization of #$Volcano (q.v.) Each instance of #$ShieldVolcano is a wide volcano with shallow sloping sides.  Such volcanoes are characterized lava flows with low viscosity. ")
(comment CinderCone "A specialization of #$Volcano (q.v.) Each instance of #$CinderCone is volcano that extrudes mainly scoria and pyroclastics that build up around the vent.")
(comment ExtinctVolcano "A specialization of #$Volcano (q.v.) Each instance of #$ExtinctVolcano is a volcano that is no longer expected to erupt.")
(comment orbitalPeriod "<code>(#$orbitalPeriod OBJ PERIOD)</code> means that there is a primary object aroud which <code>OBJ</code> orbits regularly, and that a complete orbit around that primary object takes <code>OBJ</code> the amount of time <code>PERIOD</code>.")
(comment Orbiting "Elements of #$Orbiting are events in which an #$objectMoving moves along a #$motionPathway-Complete which is a roughly eliptical path through #$OuterSpace around some #$AstronomicalBody and does so periodically.  For example, a spacecraft in orbit #$orbits in such an event.  If the #$OrbitalPath is roughly circular, this event is also an instance of #$MovingInACircle.")
(comment AstronomicalUnit "A #$UnitOfDistance. One astronomical unit is equal to approximately 93 million miles, or 149,597,870,691 meters.")
(comment orbitalEccentricity "<code>(#$orbitalEccentricity OBJ NUM)</code>
indicates that <code>NUM</code> is the eccentricity of the orbital path of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment orbitalInclination "<code>(#$orbitalInclination OBJ ANG-DIST)</code> indicates that <code>ANG-DIST</code> is the inclination of the orbital path of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment MountainBreeze "A specialization of #$Breeze and #$KatabaticWind (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$MountainBreeze is a wind process that blows down from a mountain into a plane or valley. Cool peaks (relative to the lower regions below) tend to transport air downward.")
(comment AnabaticWind "A specialization of #$WindProcess (q.v.).  Each instance of #$AnabaticWind is a wind process that blows up a slope to a high region from a plane or valley.")
(disjointWith KatabaticWind AnabaticWind)
(comment ValleyBreeze "A specialization of #$Breeze and #$AnabaticWind (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$ValleyBreeze is a breeze that blows up a mountain from a plane or valley.")
(comment WindProcessTypeByCompassFromDirection "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$WindProcess whose instances all have the same direction of translation.")
(comment KatabaticWind "A specialization of #$WindProcess (q.v.).  Each instance of #$KatabaticWind is a wind process that blows down a slope from a high region (such as a mountain, hill or glacier) into a plane or valley. ")
(comment Tramontane "A specialization of #$KatabaticWind-Cold (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Tramontane is a wind process that blows from the northwest to the southeast in the south of France and North Catalonia.  A similar process is the #$Mistral.")
(comment KatabaticWind-Cold "A specialization of #$KatabaticWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$KatabaticWind-Cold is a cold wind that blows cold from a high to a low region.  Contrast this collection with #$FoehnWind.")
(comment Breeze "A specialization of #$WindProcess.  Each instance of #$Breeze is a very light wind.")
(comment WindProcessTypeByStrength "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$WindProcess whose instances are all of the same strength.")
(comment FoehnWind "A specialization of #$KatabaticWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$FoehnWind is a warm wind that blows from a high to a low region.  Contrast this collection with #$KatabaticWind-Cold.")
(comment ChinookWind "A specialization of #$FoehnWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ChinookWind is a warm wind that typically blows from the Rocky Mountains toward the Canadian Prairies or the Great Plains.")
(comment SantaAnaWind "A specialization of #$FoehnWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$SantaAnaWind is a warm dry wind that typically blows in Southern California weather during autumn and early winter.")
(comment Mistral "A specialization of #$KatabaticWind-Cold  (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Mistral is a cold and strong northwesterly wind along the coast of the Gulf of Lyon in southern France.")
(comment NorwesterWind "A specialization of #$FoehnWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$NorwesterWind is a warm dry wind that typically blows over New Zealand's South Island.")
(comment WindProcessTypeByLocation "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$WindProcess whose instances all occur at the same location.")
(comment OnShoreWind "A specialization of #$WindProcess (q.v.).  Each instance of #$OnShoreWind is a wind process that blows from the land to the sea.")
(comment OffShoreWind "A specialization of #$WindProcess (q.v.).  Each instance of #$OffShoreWind is a wind process that blows from the sea to the land.")
(comment LandBreeze "A specialization of #$OnShoreWind and #$Breeze (q.v.).  Each instance of #$LandBreeze is a breeze that blows from the land.")
(comment SeaBreeze "A specialization of #$OnShoreWind and #$Breeze (q.v.).  Each instance of #$LandBreeze is a breeze that blows from the land.")
(comment PrevailingWind "A specialization of #$WindProcess (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PrevailingWind is a long-enduring wind process with a trend to blow a particular general direction.face.")
(comment TradeWind "A specialization of #$PrevailingWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TradeWind is a a prevailing wind in the tropics.  They blow from high-pressure areas in the horse latitudes towards low-pressure areas in the vicinity of the equator.")
(comment Westerlies-PrevailingWind "A specialization of #$PrevailingWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TradeWind is a a prevailing wind in the tropics.  They blow from high-pressure areas in the horse latitudes towards low-pressure areas in the vicinity of the equator.")
(comment PolarEasterlies-PrevailingWind "A specialization of #$PrevailingWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TradeWind is a prevailing wind which on Earth blows from high-pressure areas of the polar highs at the north and south poles towards the low-pressure areas of the polar fronts at around 60 degrees latitude.")
(comment JetStream "A specialization of #$PrevailingWind (q.v.).  Each instance of #$JetStream is a fast and narrow air current that occurs high above the surface of the Earth, just under the #$Tropopause-PlanetEarth.")
(comment Sirocco "A specialization of #$WindProcess.  Each instance of #$Sirocco is a strong southerly to southeasterly wind in the Mediterranean that blows in from the Sahara.")
(comment Bora-Wind "A specialization of #$KatabaticWind-Cold  (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Bora-Wind is a cold northern to north-eastern wind in the Adriatic, Greece, Russia or Turkey.")
(comment DustDevil "The collection of small whirlwinds that contain dust or sand.  Elements are not as strong as elements of #$CycloneAsObject.")
(comment BalkanCountry "An instance of #$CountryTypeByGeneralRegion.  This is the collection of all countries that are located in the #$Balkans-Region.")
(comment CentralEuropeanCountry "The collection of nation-states in the Central region of Europe.")
(comment SouthernEuropeanCountry "The collection of nation-states in the Southern region of Europe.")
(comment BalticState "An instance of #$CountryTypeByGeneralRegion.  This collection includes three instances: Latvia, Lithuania, and Estonia.")
(comment BlindAnimal "A specialization of #$AnimalBLO (q.v.).  Each instance of #$BlindAnimal is an animal that is unable to see.")
(comment FertileAnimal "Able to reproduce. This is different than #$SexuallyMature, although we expect that #$SexuallyMature animals are fertile.  For example, a male may have all the primary and secondary sexual characteristics after puberty but can be infertile due to disease or accident.  Moreover, women past menopause are #$SexuallyMature animals but are not #$FertileAnimals.")
(comment PregnantAnimal "A specialization of #$FertileAnimal.  Each instance of #$PregnantAnimal is an animal that is currently the #$bodilyDoer in a #$Pregnancy.")
(comment exceptionalAtActivityType "<code>(#$exceptionalAtActivityType AGENT ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> has the ability level of an exceptional performer of the action-type <code>ACTIVITY-TYPE</code>.")
(comment poorAtActivityType "<code>(#$poorAtActivityType AGENT ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> has the ability level of an poor performer of the action-type <code>ACTIVITY-TYPE</code>.")
(comment goodAtActivityType "<code>(#$goodAtActivityType AGENT ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> has the ability level of an at least good performer of the action-type <code>ACTIVITY-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Whispering "A collection of actions; each of which is the action of speaking softly without vibration of the vocal cords.")
(comment Shouting "A collection of actions; each of which is the action of speaking very loudly.")
(disjointWith Whispering Shouting)
(comment Speaking "A specialization of #$Talking (which includes non-verbal talking such as the use of sign-language) and #$MakingAnOralSound. The collection of actions generating utterances (cf. #$SpokenUtterance-IBT) which are speech. Hence, #$Speaking normally includes only those utterances using some #$Language as a communication convention, unlike other utterances such as #$Booing and #$Cheering. It is also a #$SingleDoerAction -- for events where two or more agents are involved in spoken communication, see #$SpokenCommunicating.")
(comment SpeakingTypeByLoudness "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Speaking whose instances are all of the same loudness.")
(comment Stratovolcano "A specialization of #$Volcano (q.v.) Each instance of #$Stratovolcano is a tall conical volcano caused by the subduction of #$TectonicPlates.  Active stratovolcanoes are characterized by frequent eruptions, with highly viscous lava flows that harden quickly.")
(comment SkippingWithTwoLegs "A specialization of #$Locomotion-TwoLegged.  Each instance #$SkippingWithTwoLegs is an event in which a biped locomotes by giving a little hop on alternating feet.")
(comment lowToMediumAmountOf "The instance of #$GenericValuePredicate (q.v.) that corresponds to (see #$correspondingGenericValuePredicate) the generic-value function #$LowToMediumAmountFn (q.v.).  <code>(#$lowToMediumAmountOf QUANTTYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the #$GenericQuantity that corresponds to a <i>low-to-medium amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$lowToMediumAmountOf #$Happiness (#$LowToMediumAmountFn #$Happiness))</code> holds.  And <code>(#$levelOfCompatibility OLDTHING NEWTHING #$lowToMediumAmountOf)</code> holds just in case <code>OLDTHING</code> and <code>NEWTHING</code> are compatible to a low-to-medium degree.")
(comment highToVeryHighAmountOf "The instance of #$GenericValuePredicate (q.v.) that corresponds to (see #$correspondingGenericValuePredicate) the generic-value function #$HighToVeryHighAmountFn (q.v.).  <code>(#$highToVeryHighAmountOf QUANTTYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the #$GenericQuantity that corresponds to a <i>high-to-very-high amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$highToVeryHighAmountOf #$Happiness (#$HighToVeryHighAmountFn #$Happiness))</code> holds.  And <code>(#$levelOfCompatibility OLDTHING NEWTHING #$highToVeryHighAmountOf)</code> holds just in case <code>OLDTHING</code> and <code>NEWTHING</code> are compatible to a high-to-very-high degree.")
(comment WindowPane "A specialization of #$PlateGlass. Each instance of this collection is a sheet of transparent material (usually made of glass) in a #$WindowPortal. These days, a window generally has just one window pane.")
(comment mediumToHighAmountOf "The instance of #$GenericValuePredicate (q.v.) that corresponds to (see #$correspondingGenericValuePredicate) the generic-value function #$MediumToHighAmountFn (q.v.).  <code>(#$mediumToHighAmountOf QUANTTYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the #$GenericQuantity that corresponds to a <i>medium-to-high amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$mediumToHighAmountOf #$Happiness (#$MediumToHighAmountFn #$Happiness))</code> holds.  And <code>(#$levelOfCompatibility OLDTHING NEWTHING #$mediumToHighAmountOf)</code> holds just in case <code>OLDTHING</code> and <code>NEWTHING</code> are compatible to a medium-to-high degree.")
(comment AlmostFn "<code>(#$AlmostFn SCALAR)</code> is the #$ScalarInterval whose #$followingValue and #$negationQuantities is <code>SCALAR</code>.")
(comment KMFOntologyTerm "The collection of terms created for the KMF ontology mapping.  Many instances are special case collections that closely correspond to the KMF OWL classes and properties.  Those special case terms that prove generally useful will be renamed and be available for general use.")
(comment ObjectFragileWRTHumanActivity "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$ObjectFragileWRTHumanActivity is an object that requires very little force to break.")
(comment subcollectionOfAndSubsetOf "A ternary #$SetOrCollectionPredicate that relates two #$Collections and a #$Set-Mathematical such that the first collection is the largest subcollection of the second that is a #$subsetOf the set.  <code>(#$subcollectionOfAndSubsetOf SUB COL SET)</code> means that <code>SUB</code> is, by definition, the collection of all and only those instances of <code>COL</code> that are also elements of <code>SET</code>.  
<p>
See also the corresponding function #$CollectionSubsetFn.")
(comment TakingControlOfAGroupOfFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$TakingControlOfAGroupOfFn TYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$TakingControlOfAGroup in which the #$objectOfControlTransfer is an instance of (#$GroupFn TYPE).")
(comment citizenTypeOfGeopoliticalEntity "(#$citizenTypeOfGeopoliticalEntity GEOPOL-ENTITY CIT-TYPE) means that CIT-TYPE is the collection of all people who are citizens of GEOPOL-ENTITY.")
(comment southEasternRegion "(#$southEasternRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `southeastern region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `southeastern region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment northEasternRegion "(#$northEasternRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `northeastern region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `northeastern region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment centralRegion "(#$centralRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `centraln region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `central region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment metropolitanAreaOf "(#$metropolitanAreaOf CITY AREA) means that AREA is the `metropolitan region' of CITY.")
(comment predHoldsBetweenProperSubSits "(#$predHoldsBetweenProperSubSits SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2 BIN-PRED) means that if SIT is an instance of SIT-TYPE, SUBSIT1 is an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE1, SUBSIT2 is an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE2, and (#$properSubSituations SIT SUBSIT1) and (#$properSubSituations SIT SUBSIT2), then (BIN-PRED SUBSIT1 SUBSIT2).")
(comment HoldingHostageForRansom "The collection of all instances of #$HoldingHostages wherein the characteristic (#$AttemptingFn #$Extortion) consists in one or more ransom demands (#$DemandingARansom).  The hostage-holders may or may not receive the ransom they request, and the victim may or may not be released.")
(comment SeizingAndHoldingCaptive "The collection of all events in which one or more living organisms are forcibly seized (cf. (#$HostileSeizureOfTypeFn #$Organism-Whole)) and held captive (cf. #$HeldCaptive).")
(comment SeizingAndHoldingHostage "A specialization of #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal.  In
each instance of #$SeizingAndHoldingHostage, an agent seizes and
subsequently holds as hostage(s) one or more #$Persons.  Instances
of this collection thus have instances of both #$HostileSeizure and #$HoldingHostages as sub-events.  Note that the seizure may occur as part
of a #$KidnappingSomeone -- where the person seized is subsequently
transported to an unknown or inaccessible location -- or may simply
consist of gaining control over the person by threat of force (e.g.,
holding someone at gunpoint while issuing demands).  Typically, the
purpose of the #$perpetrator is to coerce other agents --
who have a #$positiveVestedInterest in the #$hostages -- to accede to some
demand.  See, for example, the specialization #$SeizingAndHoldingHostageForRansom.")
(comment SeizingAndHoldingHostageForRansom "The collection of all events in which one or more living organisms are forcibly seized and held in a hostage-holding wherein one or more ransom demands are made.")
(comment HeldCaptive "A configuration that holds when at least one animal is in the captivity of another.  The captive(s) may be under direct physical control of the captor, or may be held by devices that the captor controls.")
(comment Entertainer-PerformanceContributor "An instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$Entertainer-PerformanceContributor is a person who contributes to the performance aspect of an entertainment event.  Thus #$Entertainer-PerformanceContributor is a generalization of #$Entertainer (the collection of entertainers), but is not identical to it.  A canonical example of a person who is an instance of this collection but not #$Entertainer would be  a professional athlete.  Such a person works in the entertainment industry (see #$EntertainmentIndustry), not as an entertainer (in the sense of #$Entertainer) <i>per se</i>, but as someone who practices his or her craft with a focal goal of contributing to an individual or team victory, and, in doing so, contributes to the execution (performance) of an entertainment event.  The entertainment of the audience is a by-product the athlete's actions, and is not his or her focal concern.")
(comment structureInUrbanArea "This predicate relates a structure to the urban area in which it is located.  (#$structureInUrbanArea STRUCT AREA) means that STRUCT is located in AREA.  For instance, (#$structureInUrbanArea #$ArcDeTriomphe (#$TerritoryFn #$CityOfParisFrance))  means that the Arc de Triomphe is located in the geographical extent of Paris, France, which  is (in the context of the assertion) an urban area.")
(comment northWesternRegion "(#$northWesternRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `northwestern region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `northwestern region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment southWesternRegion "(#$southWesternRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `southwestern region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `southwestern region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment exclusiveEconomicZoneOf "(#$exclusiveEconomicZoneOf GEO-ENTITY ZONE) means that ZONE is the region of the sea designated as the exclusive economic zone of GEO-ENTITY, in accordance with U.N provisions.")
(comment maritimeClaimOf "(#$maritimeClaimOf GEO-ENTITY ZONE) means that ZONE is the belt of sea which forms the maritime claim of some coastal entity ENT. U.N. regulations specify how countries may figure their maritime claims. Typically, a country has control over the waters, ocean bed, and subsoil of its maritime claim region, as well as to the airspace over it.")
(comment contiguousZoneOf "(#$contiguousZoneOf GEO-ENTITY ZONE) means that ZONE picks out the region of the sea designated as the contiguous zone of ENT, in accordance with U.N provisions.")
(comment SexualProductOrServiceEvent "This is the collection of all #$Artifacts and #$ServiceEvents intended for the sexual entertainment of users, viewers, or participants.  In many societies, because of their explicit sexual nature, such things are particularly unsuitable for non-adults.  The collection includes, but is not limited to, #$InformationBearingThings that present sexually explicit content as entertainment (e.g., movies with an #$XRating), #$Events with high sex-relevant content (e.g., lap dances, #$Prostitution events), and #$PersonalProducts used by adults for #$SexualGratification (e.g., #$SexToys, #$Whips, hand cuffs).")
(comment territorialSeaOf "(#$territorialSeaOf GEO-ENTITY ZONE) means that ZONE is  the region of the sea designated as the territorial sea of GEO_ENTITY, in accordance with U.N provisions.")
(comment ReifiableFunction "A specialization of #$Function-Denotational.   Each instance of #$ReifiableFunction is denoted by a CycL constant that can stand in the 0th (or \"arg0\") position in a #$CycLReifiableNonAtomicTerm  (q.v.).  For example, #$GovernmentFn is a reifiable function, so the term  `(#$GovernmentFn #$France)' is a reifiable non-atomic term (or \"NAT\").   And since this particular term actually _is_ reified in the Cyc Knowledge  Base, it is, more specifically, a #$CycLNonAtomicReifiedTerm (or \"NART\").   The NART `(#$GovernmentFn #$France)' is treated more or less the same as if  it were a CycL constant (named, say, `GovernmentOfFrance').  Similary, the constant for #$GovernmentFn can be applied to the constant (or other  reified or reifiable term) for _any_ instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity to form a reifiable NAT that denotes that region's government; and should this NAT appear in a sentence that is asserted to the KB, it will thereby become a NART. Note, however, that not all NATs are such that it is desireable that  they should become reified (i.e. become NARTs) if they appear in  assertions; for more on this see #$UnreifiableFunction.")
(comment graduatesOfType "(#$graduatesOfType ED-ORG-TYPE GRAD-TYPE) means that GRAD-TYPE is the collection of graduates of educational organizations of instances of ED-ORG-TYPE.")
(comment AttendingSchoolFn "This function takes as its sole argument a type of educational institution and returns the collection of actions of attending that type of school.  For example, (#$AttendingSchoolFn #$HighSchool) is the  collection of all attendings of any high school.  An instance of this collection is any action in which a student enrolled in a high school attends that school.  Since one may attend high school without graduating, an element of this collection need not be a complete high school education.")
(comment embassyMissionTypeOfCountry "(#$embassyMissionTypeOfCountry COUNTRY MISSION-TYPE) means that MISSION-TYPE is the collection of embassies which represent COUNTRY.")
(comment electedMemberType "(#$electedMemberType ORG AGENT-TYPE) means that AGENT-TYPE is the collection of elected members of ORG.")
(comment BalletDancing "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the ballet style.")
(comment TapDancing "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in thetap style.")
(comment BallroomDancing "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the ballroom style.")
(comment CountryAndWesternDancing "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the country and western style.")
(comment SalsaDancing "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the salsa style.")
(comment EroticDancing "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are intende to be erotic.")
(comment LapDancing "A specialization of #$EroticDancing.  Lap dances are erotic dances offered in some strip clubs.  They are performed under circumstances in which the patron is seated, and the dancer is either in immediate contact or within a very short distance of the patron.")
(comment numInstancesOfCollStandInPredToValue "(#$numInstancesOfCollStandInPredToValue BIN-PRED COLL THING NUM) holds just in case the number of instances, INS, of COLL such that (BIN-PRED INS THING) is NUM.")
(comment Organization-SelfDirecting "The collection of all #$Organizations that are, to a very large degree, self-directing in the sense that they determine the where and how in actions they or their agents perform.  This is not to say that there are not individuals members of the organization who actually do the directing, rather it merely means that for any action in which it is correct to assert that the organization or their agents performed it, it is also correct to assert that the organization was the #$directingAgent of the action.")
(comment CardinalityFn "An individual denoting unary function.  This is primarily used as a modifier for #$QueryMacroPredicates.  To calculate the known cardinality of a collection use #$extentCardinality.")
(comment LiquidFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  #$LiquidFn takes as an argument a collection COL, membership in which is based only on physical and/or chemical composition and not on any other property (see #$TangibleStuffCompositionType).  (#$LiquidFn COL) is the collection of elements of COL that are in liquid form (i.e., are instances of #$LiquidTangibleThing), including elements having #$Liquid-StateOfMatter, but also including various mixtures that behave like liquids (see the comment on #$LiquidTangibleThing).  For example, a quantity of water as dispensed from a faucet is an instance of (#$LiquidFn #$Water); a glass of apple juice, in its drinkable state, is an instance of (#$LiquidFn (#$JuiceFn (#$FruitFn #$AppleTree))).")
(comment liquidForm "(#$liquidForm TANGIBLE-TYPE LIQUID-TYPE) means that LIQUID-TYPE is the collection of TANGIBLE-TYPE in liquid form.")
(comment solidForm "(#$solidForm TANGIBLE-TYPE SOLID-TYPE) means that SOLID-TYPE is the collection of TANGIBLE-TYPE in solid form.")
(comment gaseousForm "(#$gaseousForm TANGIBLE-TYPE GASEOUS-TYPE) means that GASEOUS-TYPE is the collection of TANGIBLE-TYPE in gaseous form.")
(comment chemicalWeaponForm "(#$chemicalWeaponForm STUFF-TYPE WEAPON-TYPE) means that WEAPON-TYPE is the collection of STUFF-TYPE in weapon form.")
(comment TangibleStuffStateType "A #$SecondOrderCollection and a specialization of #$ExistingStuffType (q.v.). Each instance of #$TangibleStuffStateType is a collection of pieces of tangible stuff that are all in the same distinct physical state, where the notion of  \"physical state\" is a naive (as in #$NaivePhysicsMt) concept of a distinctive physical structure and/or texture.  Some instances of #$TangibleStuffStateType  have distinctive chemical compositions, such as #$Diamond; but for collections  that are distinguished <i>solely</i> on the basis of chemical composition, see  #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  #$TangibleStuffStateType includes both (i) collections of substances that can exist only in one distinct physical state  (e.g. #$Diamond again) and (ii) collections of pieces of stuff that by definition are in a certain distinct state (e.g. ice).  Instances of #$TangibleStuffStateType include #$Foam, #$Rubble, and (#$LiquidFn #$Water).  Note that #$Water per se is <i>not</i> an instance of #$TangibleStuffStateType, since some water is in a gaseous state or a solid state.")
(comment vaporForm "(#$vaporForm STUFF-TYPE VAPOR-TYPE) means that VAPOR-TYPE is the collection of STUFF-TYPE in vapor form.")
(comment weaponizedForm "(#$weaponizedForm STUFF-TYPE WEAPON-TYPE) means that WEAPON-TYPE is the collection of STUFF-TYPE in weaponized form.")
(comment antiWeaponType "(#$antiWeaponType HARDWARE-TYPE WEAPON-TYPE) means that ARTIFACT-TYPE is the collection of artifacts intended to be used against instances of WEAPON-TYPE.")
(comment powderedTypeOfType "(#$powderedTypeOfType TANGIBLE-TYPE POWDER-TYPE) means that POWDER-TYPE is the collection of powdered instances of TANGIBLE-TYPE.")
(comment juiceTypeOfType "(#$juiceTypeOfType STUFF-TYPE JUICE-TYPE) means that JUICE-TYPE is the collection of STUFF-TYPE juice.")
(comment stuffTypeUsedIsConsumedInEventType "<code>(#$stuffTypeUsedIsConsumedInEventType EVENT-TYPE STUFF-TYPE)</code> means that if an instance of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> is used in an instance <code>EVENT</code> of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>, a portion of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> is consumed in <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment relationAllOnly "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to two collections.  <code>(#$relationAllOnly BINPRED COL1 COL2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, only instances of  <code>COL2</code>, say <code>INST2</code>, are such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<pre>
(#$implies
  (#$and
    (#$isa ?INST1 COL1)
    (BINPRED ?INST1 ?INST2))
  (#$isa ?INST2 COL2)) .
</pre>
So #$relationAllOnly (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.
<p>
For example, '(#$relationAllOnly #$eatsWillingly-Instance #$Herbivore #$PlantBLO)' means that every herbivore willingly eats only plants or parts thereof.  See also #$relationOnlyAll and #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")
(comment mediators "<code>(#$mediators OCCUR AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> participates deliberately in the #$SocialOccurrence <code>OCCUR</code>, and, by doing so, helps facilitate <code>OCCUR</code>.  For example, #$mediators would relate a judge to the trial he or she oversees, or a selling agent (see the specialization #$sellingAgent) to a sale he or she helps to bring about.")
(comment predicateIsComposedOfThroughArg2Positions "<code>(#$predicateIsComposedOfThroughArg2Positions  COMP-PRED PRED-1 PRED-2)</code> means that the binary predicate <code>COMP-PRED</code> is the composition of the binary predicates <code>PRED-1</code> and <code>PRED-2</code> such that if <code>(#$predicateIsComposedOfThroughArg2Positions COMP-PRED PRED-1 PRED-2)</code>, then <code>(COMP-PRED X Z)</code> if and only if there is something, <code>Y</code>, such that <code>(PRED-1 X Y)</code> and <code>(PRED-2 Z Y)</code>.")
(comment predicateIsComposedOfThroughArg1Positions "<code>(#$predicateIsComposedOfThroughArg1Positions  COMP-PRED PRED-1 PRED-2)</code> means that the binary predicate <code>COMP-PRED</code> is the composition of the binary predicates <code>PRED-1</code> and <code>PRED-2</code> such that if <code>(#$predicateIsComposedOfThroughArg1Positions  COMP-PRED PRED-1 PRED-2)</code>, then <code>(COMP-PRED X Z)</code> if and only if there is something, <code>Y</code>, such that <code>(PRED-1 Y X)</code> and <code>(PRED-2 Y Z)</code>.")
(comment genlPredsWRTTypes "<code>(#$genlPredsWRTTypes BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL1 COL2)</code> means that if <code>(BINPRED1 INS1 INS2)</code> where <code>INS1</code> is an instance of <code>COL1</code> and <code>INS2</code> is an instance of <code>COL2</code>, then <code>(BINPRED2 INS1 INS2)</code>. 
<p>
#$genlPredsWRTTypes facilitates the expresssion of pseudo-#$genlPreds relationships between #$BinaryPredicates <code>BINPRED1</code> and <code>BINPRED2</code> when their argument constraints are not in the appropriate #$genls relationship for <code>(#$genlPreds BINPRED1 BINPRED2)</code> to be asserted.  
<p>
At a more specific level, #$genlPredsWRTTypes can serve as a useful rule macro predicate.  For instance, suppose we wanted to say that all people of a certain nationality, Italian, for instance, are, as a general rule, acquainted with all of their neighbors.  We could assert <code>(#$genlPredsWRTTypes #$neighbors #$acquaintedWith #$ItalianPerson #$Person)</code>.  If there is a bi-directional #$genlPreds for the given argument types, use the more specific #$equivPredsWRTTypes.  See also #$genlInverseWRTTypes.")
(comment mate "An #$InterAnimalRelationPredicate that is a specialization of both #$sexualPartners and #$positiveVestedInterest.  <code>(#$mate ANIMAL1 ANIMAL2)</code> means that <code>ANIMAL1</code> and <code>ANIMAL2</code> are long-term companions.  More general than #$spouse, #$mate can also be used to specify a person's \"significant other\", including one's boyfriend, girlfriend, or partner in a homosexual relationship.
<p>
An  assumption in the #$UnitedStatesSocialLifeMt is that a person has at most one mate at any given time.")
(comment sexualPartners "<code>(#$sexualPartners IND1 IND2)</code> is true, if, and only if, <code>IND1</code> and <code>IND2</code> regularly engage in #$SexualBehavior in a context specified by time interval or microtheory. <code>IND1</code> and <code>IND2</code> must both be instances of #$Animal. A negative borderline case is #$Masturbating (somebody engaging in sexual behavior with him/herself), which is ruled out by the fact that the predicate is an #$IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate")
(comment StrictlyFunctionalPredicate "A specialization of #$FunctionalPredicate (q.v.) whose instances are those predicates that are in  a strict sense \"functional\" in at least one argument-place (see #$strictlyFunctionalInArgs and #$singleEntryFormatInArgs).  That is, given any sequence of legal arguments placed in such a predicate's other argument positions, there is at most one argument such that, when it is placed in the predicate's functional position, the resulting formula is true.  
<p>
More precisely: Suppose <code>PRED</code> is an <code>N</code>-ary instance of #$FunctionalPredicate that is functional in its <code>K</code>th place.  Given any (<code>N</code>-1)-tuple <code><O(1),.., O(K-1), O(K+1),.., O(N)></code> consisting of things that are, respectively, legal arguments for (i.e. satisfy all argument-constraints on) the <code>N</code>-1 argument-places in <code>PRED</code> other than its <code>K</code>th-place, there is at most one thing -- call it <code>O(K)</code> -- such that <code>(PRED O(1)..O(N))</code> is true.  For example, #$biologicalMother is functional in its second argument-place, since every animal has one and only one biological mother.  Note that it might be the case that, for some ways of fixing <code>PRED</code>'s other arguments, there will be <i>nothing</i> that would yield a true formula when put into PRED's functional argument-place; for example, while a country has at most one dictator (see #$dictator), some countries have no dictator.  A binary #$StrictlyFunctionalPredicate that is strictly functional in its second argument is an instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot (q.v.).")
(comment singleEntryFormatInArgs "An instance of #$SpecificEntryFormatPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$singleEntryFormatInArgs PRED N)</code> means that, for any particular way of fixing the other arguments to <code>PRED</code> besides the <code>N</code>th, there is at most one thing such that, if taken as the <code>N</code>th argument, <code>PRED</code> holds of those arguments.  That is, if the sequences <code><... ARGN ...></code> and <code><... ARGN-PRIME ...></code> differ at most in their <code>N</code>th items and both <code>(PRED ... ARGN ...)</code> and <code>(PRED ... ARGN-PRIME ...)</code> hold, then <code>ARGN = ARGN-PRIME</code> (see #$equals).  For example, #$singleEntryFormatInArgs holds of #$biologicalMother with respect to its second argument-place, since an animal can only have one biological mother.  A predicate with a single-entry format argument-place is thus a #$StrictlyFunctionalPredicate (q.v.) that is \"functional\" with respect to that argument-place (see #$strictlyFunctionalInArgs).  Contrast with #$openEntryFormatInArgs.")
(comment pulverizingSomethingOfType "(#$pulverizingSomethingOfType TYPE PULV-TYPE) means that PULV-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$PulverizationEvent in which the #$objectActedOn is an instance of TYPE.")
(comment ransomDemanded "<code>(#$ransomDemanded HOST AMOUNT)</code> means that in the event <code>HOST</code> (an instance of #$DemandingARansom), the ransom demanded by the kidnappers is <code>AMOUNT</code>.  See also #$HoldingHostageForRansom.")
(comment sightseeingsOf "(#$sightseeingsOf relates an instance of #$Artifact to the collection of all instances of #$Sightseeing of which it is the subject.")
(comment partsPartition-Binary "(#$partsPartition-Binary WHOLE PART-1 PART-2) says that PART-1 and ?PART-2 form a partition of WHOLE.  In other words, PART-1 and PART-2 have no parts in common, and together, PART-1 and PART-2 form WHOLE in its entirety.")
(comment officialNavy "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$Organization to instances of #$Navy.   <code>(#$officialNavy ORG NAVY)</code> means that the official navy of <code>ORG</code> is <code>NAVY</code>.  See also #$NavyFn.")
(comment officialArmy "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$Organization to instances of #$Army-BranchOfService.  <code>(#$officialArmy ORG ARMY)</code> means that the official army of <code>ORG</code> is <code>ARMY</code>.  See also #$ArmyFn.")
(comment indexicalReferent "(#$indexicalReferent INDCONCEPT THING) means that in the context of the assertion, the #$IndexicalConcept INDCONCEPT has the referent THING.  This is a #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot, in keeping with the idea that the predicate will return one and only one 'value' for the second argument place at any given point in context space.  However, be advised that the arg2 will change from context to context.")
(comment businessGrossProfitForPeriod "<code>(#$businessGrossProfitForPeriod BUSINESS VALUE PERIOD)</code> means that <code>VALUE</code> is amount <code>BUSINESS</code> made in sales less all costs directly attributable to those sales (e.g. costs for raw materials and manufacturing labor).")
(comment grandfathers "A #$FamilyRelationSlot relating an #$Animal to his or her grandfathers.  If <code>(#$grandfathers ANIM GF)</code>, then <code>GF</code> is the male parent (#$father) of one of the parents of <code>ANIM</code>.  In the case of #$NonHumanAnimals, there is a line of direct biological descent from <code>GF</code> to <code>ANIM</code>.  However, in the case of humans, because the #$children relationship can also arise due to a variety of social arrangements in addition to birth (e.g., #$Adoption, marriage, fostering), a person and their grandfathers may not be biologically related.")
(comment biologicalMother "A #$FamilyRelationSlot
that relates a given #$Animal to its female biological parent.
<code>(#$biologicalMother OFFSPRING FEMALE)</code> means that <code>FEMALE</code> is the female biological parent of <code>OFFSPRING</code>.  Cf. #$mother.")
(comment biologicalGrandfathers "A #$FamilyRelationSlot
that relates a given #$Animal to its male biological grandparents.
<code>(#$biologicalGrandfathers PROGENY MALE)</code> means that <code>MALE</code> is a male biological grandparent of <code>PROGENY</code>.  Cf. #$biologicalGrandfathers.")
(comment biologicalGrandmothers "A #$FamilyRelationSlot
that relates a given #$Animal to its female biological grandparents.
<code>(#$biologicalGrandmothers PROGENY FEMALE)</code> means that <code>FEMALE</code> is a female biological grandparent of <code>PROGENY</code>.  Cf. #$biologicalGrandfathers.")
(comment minimizeExtent "An instance of both #$MetaKnowledgePredicate and #$MetaPredicate (qq.v.) that is used to state that the Cyc system will \"assume\" that a (sequence of) thing(s) is not in the extension (see #$relationExtension) of a given predicate if the #$CycInferenceEngine is unable to prove that it is.  
<p>
<code>(#$minimizeExtent PRED)</code> means that, for any sequence of things <code><THING1, ..., THINGn></code> such that <code>(PRED THING1 ... THINGn)</code> holds, the fact that this holds is either expressed by some GAF (i.e. a \"ground atomic formula\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) that is asserted in the Cyc Knowledge Base or is deducible via the inference engine from what is in the KB.  
<p>
The practical import of a #$minimizeExtent assertion is that it reflects an underlying assumption that if the inference engine cannot prove some given sentence of the form <code>(PRED ARG1 ... ARGN)</code>, then that fact constitutes an argument for its negation <code>(#$not (PRED ARG1 ... ARGN))</code>; and, if the \"negation by failure\" inference parameter is turned on, the inference engine will actually conclude that this negation is true.  Note that a #$minimizeExtent assertion is weaker than the corresponding #$completeExtentEnumerable (q.v.) assertion would be, in that the latter does not require that the inference engine attempt to deduce <code>(PRED ARG1 ... ARGn)</code> before concluding that it is not true.  See also #$minimizeExtentForArg and the shared #$NoteOnClosedWorldAssumption.")
(comment extentCardinality "<code>(#$extentCardinality SETORCOL N)</code> means that there are <code>N</code> terms in the currently represented extent of #$SetOrCollection <code>SETORCOL</code>.  See also #$cardinality.")
(comment MostWoundedFn "A collection denoting unary function.  (#$MostCapturedFn COLL) denotes the subcollection of COLL that consists of the instances that have the most number of persons wounded in the event.  There could be more than one \"most wounded in\" event in because of ties.  Most often though, this will return a collection with a single instance.")
(comment DetectingSomething "An instance of #$DetectingSomething is an event in which something is determined to be an instance of a particular collection.")
(comment DetectionOfCollaborationOpportunityFn "An instance of #$ReifiableFunction that signifies the detection of a potential collaboration opportunity between two or more CAE users. For example, (#$DetectionOfCollaborationOpportunityFn (#$TheSet (#$TheList USER1 CONCEPT1) (#$TheList USER2 CONCEPT2)) DATE) means that, on DATE, Cyc discovered a potential collaboration opportunity between users USER1, working on topic CONCEPT1, and USER2, working on topic CONCEPT2.")
(comment potentialCollaboratorConcept "(#$potentialCollaboratorConcept COL-OP USER CONCEPT) means that Cyc has detected a potential collaboration opportunity, COL-OP, between the CAE user USER, working on topic CONCEPT and other CAE users.")
(comment cwGenre "(#$cwGenre WORK GENRE) states that the #$ConceptualWork ?WORK has the #$ArtisticTypeByStyle GENRE. For example,  (#$cwGenre #$GoneWithTheWind-TheBook (#$GenreFn #$LiteraryWork-CW #$PropositionalConceptualWork-RomanceGenre)) states that the book 'Gone With The Wind' has the attribute of being of the romance genre.")
(comment AreaIlluminatedByMoonlight "A specialization of #$OutdoorLocation which subsumes areas illuminated directly or indirectly by #$Moonlight.")
(comment weather "The predicate #$weather is used to describe the weather at a particular outdoor location.  <code>(#$weather LOC WEATHER)</code> means that the #$OutdoorLocation <code>LOC</code> is an instance of the #$OutdoorLocationTypeByWeather <code>WEATHER</code>.  For example, to say that it's snowy in Lake Tahoe, we would say: (#$weather #$LakeTahoe #$SnowyArea).  Note that multiple sorts of conditions can characterize the weather at a given region at a given time; thus the truth of (#$weather #$LakeTahoe #$SnowyArea) does not rule out the possiblity of (#$weather #$LakeTahoe #$CloudyArea) also being true.")
(comment ambientCondition "The predicate #$ambientCondition is used to describe the ambient conditions at a particular outdoor location.  <code>(#$ambientCondition LOC COND)</code> means that the #$OutdoorLocation <code>LOC</code> is an instance of the #$OutdoorLocationTypeByAmbientCondition <code>COND</code>.")
(comment PavedPath "A subcollection of #$Paved.  #$PavedPath is the collection of surfaces, such as roads, sidewalks, and floors, that are covered with concrete, asphalt, stones or bricks, etc. The paved surface is generally #$Smooth and has some degree of #$Hardness.")
(comment PavedPath "A subcollection of #$Paved.  #$PavedPath describes 
surfaces, such as roads, sidewalks, and floors, that are covered with
concrete, asphalt, stones or bricks, etc. The paved surface is generally
#$Smooth and has some degree of #$Hardness.")
(comment UnpavedPathArtifact "This is the collection of unpaved instances of #$PathArtifact, i.e. the opposite collection (see #$oppositeCollections) of #$PavedPath. See its two main specializations: #$UnimprovedSurface-PathArtifact and #$ImprovedSurface-PathArtifact.")
(comment oppositeCollections "This specialization of disjointWith (q.v.) relates incompatible collections that are \"direct opposites\" of each other. <code>(#$oppositeCollections COLL1 COLL2)</code> means that <code>COLL1</code> is the \"directly opposite\" collection of <code>COLL2</code> (and vice versa). The sense of \"opposite\" intended here is intuitively familiar, but difficult to define precisely.")
(comment OutdoorLocationByIlluminationLevel "A collection of collections and a specialization of
#$OutdoorLocationTypeByAmbientCondition. Each instance of
#$OutdoorLocationByIlluminationLevel is a collection of
OutdoorLocations with similar levels of illumination. Such levels are
conventionally specified by percentage of full daylight.")
(comment sourceOfDirectIllumination "<code>(#$sourceOfDirectIllumination OBJ SOURCE)</code> means that <code>SOURCE</code> is a direct illumination source for <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment ProductTypeByBrandVersion "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ProductTypeByBrandVersion is a collection of all instances of a particular version of a #$ProductTypeByBrand. The level of specificity here can vary.  For example, VolkswagenJetta and VolkswagenJettaGTI would both be instances of #$ProductTypeByBrandVersion, since both pick out not just a #$ProductTypeByBrand (#$VolkswagenCar) but a specific, named version of that #$ProductTypeByBrand.  However, since it is a more specific subset, VolkswagenJettaGTI would be a spec of VolkswagenJetta.  Those instances of #$FormalProductType in which the product specification is restricted to a single #$brandNameOfProductType, such as PetcoGroomingPoodlePuppyCut are also instances of #$ProductTypeByBrandVersion.")
(comment AthleteTypeBySport "#$AthleteTypeBySport is a collection of collections. Each element is a collection of #$Athletes who play the same #$Sport, for example, #$TennisPlayer. Since a #$Person can play more than one #$Sport, the instances of #$AthleteTypeBySport need not be disjoint. The motivation for creating this collection is to make use of a faceting of #$Athlete to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment Tutoring "A kind of #$Teaching, typically performed one-on-one or at least with a small student-to-teacher ratio.")
(comment gameTypeForSystemTYpe "<code>(#$gameTypeForSystemType COMP-TYPE PROG-TYPE)</code> means that <code>PROG-TYPE</code> is the collection of games that that can be played on <code>COMP-TYPE</code>.")
(comment JobFilled "A specialization of #$JobPosition.  Each instance of #$JobFilled is a filled job position. This means that there is both a #$Person currently standing in the #$personWithJobPosition relation to the #$JobPosition, and an #$Organization standing in the #$orgWithJobPosition to the #$JobPosition.")
(comment subOrganizations "The predicate #$subOrganizations relates a particular organization to one of its sub-organizations -- i.e., a smaller organization which is part of it or which it somehow subsumes. <code>(#$subOrganizations ORG SUBORG)</code> holds both when <code>SUBORG</code> is only one organizational level down from <code>ORG</code>, e.g., (#$subOrganizations #$NationalLeague-Baseball #$NationalLeagueEast-Baseball), and when it is several levels down the hierarchy.")
(comment DancingTypeByStyle "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$DancingTypeByStyle is a collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are
all of a particular style.")
(comment MentalState "A specialization of #$MentalSituation whose instances 
are relatively enduring mental <i>states</i>, such as beliefs (and other propositional attitudes) and moods of particular agents, as opposed to the more dynamic mental <i>events</i> (see #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent) such as thinking, perceiving, and experiencing pain.  (Note that, while generally more long-lived than a mental event, a mental state might exist for only a fraction of a second; e.g. \"For one fleeting moment the quarterback believed his team had won the game\".)")
(comment animalMentalState "<code>(#$animalMentalState ANIMAL STATE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>ANIMAL</code> is in the mental state <code>STATE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment deviceDamageState "<code>(#$deviceDamageState DEVICE STATE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>DEVICE</code> is in the damage state <code>STATE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment RetailOutletCategoryType "A collection of collections.  Each element of #$RetailOutletCategoryType is a collection of #$RetailStores which all sell products in the same market category.  The collections #$GroceryStore, #$RecordedMusicStore, #$Bookstore, and #$SportingGoodsStore are elements of #$RetailOutletCategoryType.")
(comment expertRegarding "<code>(#$expertRegarding AGT X)</code> means that the knowledge about <code>X</code> that the agent <code>AGT</code> has is extensive.  This predicate is stronger than #$knowsAbout in the sense that <code>(#$expertRegarding AGT X)</code> implies <code>(#$knowsAbout AGT X)</code>, but the converse does not in general hold.  For example, while many Americans know about #$Basketball-TheGame, few are experts regarding #$Basketball-TheGame.  See also #$fieldsOfCompetence and #$domainsOfSpecialization.")
(comment NarrativeTVShowTypeByGenre "#$NarrativeTVShowTypeByGenre is a collection of collections. Each element of #$NarrativeTVShowTypeByGenre is a collection of instances of #$NarrativeTVShow-CW that have the same narrative genre, for example #$TVActionShow. This collection was created to make use of a faceting of #$NarrativeTVShow-CW to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment regionalAffiliation "<code>(#$regionalAffiliation AGENT REGION)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> identifies or is identified by others with <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment EntertainerTypeByActivity "#$EntertainerTypeByActivity is a collection of collections. Each instance of #$EntertainerTypeByActivity is a collection of #$Entertainers who perform the same kind of activity. For example, #$Magician, #$Actor, and #$MusicalPerformer are instances of #$EntertainerTypeByActivity. This collection can be used to generate English questions to aid classification in a clarification dialogue. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed. Since instances of #$Entertainer can engage in more than one activity of this sort, the elements of #$EntertainerTypeByActivity need not be disjoint.")
(comment appropriateSeasonForObjectUse "<code>(#$appropriateSeasonForObjectUse OBJ SEASON)</code> means that it is appropriate to use <code>OBJ</code> in its intended functionality during <code>SEASON</code>.")
(comment geoPoliticalAffiliation "<code>(#$regionalAffiliation AGENT GEO-POL)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> identifies or is identified by others with <code>GEO-POL</code>.")
(comment RestaurantTypeByState "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$RestaurantTypeByState is a collection of instances of #$Restaurant-Organization that all have in common being in the same state.")
(comment ArmyFn "A unary function that returns an instance of #$Army-BranchOfService when given an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity as an argument.  <code>(#$ArmyFn COUNTRY)</code> denotes the instance of #$Army-BranchOfService that belongs to <code>COUNTRY</code>.  See also the corresponding predicate, #$officialArmy.")
(comment NavyFn "A unary function that returns an instance of #$Navy when given an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity as an argument. <code>(#$NavyFn COUNTRY)</code> denotes the instance of Army-BranchOfService that belongs to <code>COUNTRY</code>. See also the corresponding predicate, #$officialNavy.")
(comment PersonTypeBySexualBehavior "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of (#$FrequentPerformerFn #$SexualBehavior) whose instances are all of the same sexual behavior.")
(comment dutyStatus "<code>(#$dutyStatus PERSON DUTY-STATUS)</code> means that the duty status of <code>PERSON</code> is <code>DUTY-STATUS</code>.")
(comment GeometricShapeType "A specialization of #$SpatialThingTypeByShape (q.v.).  Each instance of #$GeometricShapeType is a type of #$GeometricallyDescribableThing (q.v.) whose own instances are all and only those things that have a common shape that is characterizable in relatively simple geometric terms.  An instance of a given geometric shape-type is a geometrically-describable object, which might either be intangible or tangible (though in the latter case it must be three-dimensional).
<p>
For example, #$Sphere is the collection of all spherical object; it includes both spherical space regions and crystal balls.  Similarly, #$Circle is the collection of all two-dimensional circles; all of its instances are <i>intangible</i>, since tangible objects are by their nature three-dimensional.
<p>
Specializations of #$GeometricShapeType include #$TwoDimensionalShapeType and #$ThreeDimensionalShapeType.")
(comment Helix "A #$GeometricShapeType and a specialization of #$Spiral (q.v.).  This is the collection of all helices, tangible or abstract.  Each instance of #$Helix is a spiral (i.e. a curved #$LinearObject that makes one or more turns about an axis) such that each turn about the axis is the same size, and the successive turns \"proceed\" linearly in the general direction parallel to the axis.  Thus, a helix can fit on the surface of a cylinder having that same axis.  
<p>
Examples of helices include some wire springs and the frieze on #$TrajansColumn.
<p>
Cf. #$DoubleHelix.")
(comment LineSegment-Straight "A #$GeometricShapeType and a specialization of #$LineSegment, #$LinearObject-Straight, and #$LinearObject-Bounded (qq.v.).  This is the collection of straight line segments.  Each instance of #$LineSegment-Straight is a portion of a #$Line-Straight, having two end points and containing all colinear points between those end points.")
(comment Knot "A #$GeometricShapeType and a specialization of #$LinearObject-NonPlanar and #$LinearObject-Finite (qq.v.).  This is the collection of all knots, whether tangible or intangible.")
(comment L-Shaped "An instance of #$GeometricShapeType.  Each instance of #$L-Shaped it a spatial thing whose shape resembles that of a typical inscription of the Latin uppercase letter 'L'.  It might be one-, two-, or three-dimensional; tangible or intangible.")
(comment SectorShapedObject "A #$GeometricShapeType and thus a specialization of #$GeometricallyDescribableThing.  This is the collection of all  sector (i.e. \"pie-slice\") shaped objects, whether tangible or intangible.   A two-dimensional #$SectorShapedObject is bounded by two line segments with a common vertex and by an arc of a circle whose center is that vertex.  A three-dimensional #$SectorShapedObject has two parallel, congruent surfaces that are 2-D sector-shaped.")
(comment Ray-Geometrical "A #$GeometricShapeType and a specialization of #$LinearObject-Straight (q.v.).  The collection of all geometric rays, or half-lines.  Each instance of #$Ray-Geometrical has a single end point and contains all the points on a #$Line-Straight (containing the end point) that lie in a given direction from that point.  Any given straight line can be divided at any point incident in it into two rays.")
(comment MetricUnitOfMeasure "An instance of #$UnitOfMeasureTypeBySystem and a specialization of #$InternationalUnitOfMeasure.  Each instance of #$MetricUnitOfMeasure is a #$UnitOfMeasure that can be given an <i>exact</i> definition in terms of instances of #$SIUnitOfMeasure-Base (q.v.).  #$MetricUnitOfMeasure is a generalization of #$SIUnitOfMeasure, since some units of measure (e.g. #$MetricTon, #$Liter, #$MinutesDuration) can be defined in terms of SI base units only by introducing a numerical factor other than 1, which is forbidden by SI (and all other \"coherent\" systems of measurement--see #$UnitOfMeasureTypeBySystem-Coherent), but not by the \"metric system\" in the colloquial sense, which is what this collection is intended to represent.")
(comment WhiteHairedHuman "The collection of all #$HomoSapiens with #$White-HairColor evident on the head.  The color may be natural or dyed, and it may include woven hair.  Removable wigs are excluded from consideration in determining this class of people.  See also #$GrayHairedHuman.")
(comment GrayHairedHuman "The collection of all #$HomoSapiens with #$Gray-HairColor evident on the head.  The color may be natural or dyed, and it may include woven hair.  Removable wigs are excluded from consideration in determining this class of people.  See also #$WhiteHairedHuman.")
(comment colorOfHairOnHead "<code>(#$colorOfHairOnHead HUMAN HAIR-COLOR)</code> means <code>HUMAN</code> has hair on its head that is largely <code>HAIR-COLOR</code>.")
(comment optimumCellEnlargementTemperatureOfType "<code>(#$optimumCellEnlargementTemperatureOfType BACTERIUM-TYPE TEMP)</code> means <code>TEMPERATURE</code> has <code>TEMP</code> as an optimal call enlargement temperature.")
(comment ActionTypeByLegality "A collection of collections that indicate the legality of actions.  Instances of this collection include #$LegalAction, #$IllegalAction, and #$QuestionablyLegal.")
(comment derivedFrom "<code>(#$derivedFrom PRODUCT MATERIAL)</code> means that <code>PRODUCT</code> has been made from <code>MATERIAL</code> by an irreversible process; e.g., an element of #$Table-PieceOfFurniture may have been #$derivedFrom an instance of #$MapleTree.  
<p>
Note that #$derivedFrom is <i>not</i> transitive: A particular Door121 may be derived from OakTree53, SandMob442, and several other things.  Subsequently, someone may break down the door and make Mallet0234 out of some of the  wood and a WindowPane120825 out of some (or all) of the glass. Both Mallet0234  and WindowPane120825 are #$derivedFrom Door121, but Mallet0234 is not  #$derivedFrom SandMob442, nor is WindowPane120825 #$derivedFrom OakTree53.")
(comment SingletonSetOrCollection "A #$SetOrCollectionTypeByCardinality.  Each instance of #$SingletonSetOrCollection is a #$SetOrCollection with exactly one element.")
(disjointWith ConvertibleSecurity NonconvertibleSecurity)
(comment ComputerGameTypeByOperatingSystem "Each instance of #$ComputerGameTypeByOperatingSystem is a kind of #$ComputerGameProgram whose instances all run on a particular #$OperatingSystem.")
(comment ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$ElementStuffType.  Each instance of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons is a specialization of #$ElementStuff which is defined <i>only</i> by the atomic composition of its instances -- neither the isotopic composition or physical state of the substances, nor any other additional feature, determines membership in an instance of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons.  All that matters is that the instances of that collection are entirely composed of atoms having a particular number of protons in each atomic nucleus.  Thus, the collection #$Carbon is an instance of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons, but neither the collection #$Diamond nor the collection #$Graphite is (even though they are subcollections of #$Carbon), because their members have additional qualifications.")
(comment EfficientPathfindingQuery "The collection of all queries that are part of some test corpus for the Efficient Pathfinding project.")
(comment EfficientPathfindingTest "The collection of all KB content tests that are part of some test suite for the #$EfficientPathfindingProject.")
(comment EfficientPathfindingProofByCasesQuery "The collection of all Efficient Pathfinding queries that test proof by cases (disjunctive assumption) reasoning.")
(comment FOLificationQuery "The collection of the 8 queries that were used as the test corpus for the paper \"First-Orderized ResearchCyc: Expressivity and Efficiency in a Common-Sense Ontology\" by Deepak Ramachandran, #$Pace, and #$Goolsbey.")
(comment EfficientPathfindingProofByCasesTest "The collection of all Efficient Pathfinding tests that test proof by cases (disjunctive assumption) reasoning.")
(comment FOLificationTest "The collection of the 8 tests that were used as the test corpus for the paper \"First-Orderized ResearchCyc: Expressivity and Efficiency in a Common-Sense Ontology\" by Deepak Ramachandran, #$Pace, and #$Goolsbey.")
(comment SalientDescriptorFETTerm "The collection of CycL terms that are in the function extent of #$SalientDescriptorFETFn.  This is a pragmatically motivated collection used to speed up forward inference on a particular rule.  The rule is in the #$salientAssertions of #$SalientDescriptorFETTerm.")
(comment SalientDescriptorFETTypeTerm "The collection of CycL terms that are in the function extent of #$SalientDescriptorFETForTypeFn.  This is a pragmatically motivated collection used to speed up forward inference on a particular rule.  The rule is in the #$salientAssertions of #$SalientDescriptorFETTypeTerm.")
(comment SentencesInducedByProgramFn "<code>(#$SentencesInducedByProgramFn PROG PRED-SET MT)</code> denotes <code>SENT-SET</code> which is the set of quoted CycL sentences that the program <code>PROG</code> has sufficient evidence to induce, given the visible extent from <code>MT</code> of each of the predicates in the list <code>PRED-SET</code>.")
(comment sentencesInducedByProgram "<code>(#$sentencesInducedByProgram PROG PRED-SET MT SENT-SET)</code> means that, given the extent in microtheory <code>MT</code> of each of the predicates in the list <code>PRED-SET</code>, the program <code>PROG</code> has sufficient evidence to induce the quoted sentences in <code>SENT-SET</code>.")
(comment dateOfPotentialCollaborationOpportunityDetection "(#$dateOfPotentialCollaborationOpportunityDetection COL-OP DATE) means that the potential collaboration opportunity, COL-OP, has been detected by Cyc on date DATE.")
(comment CycLSubLSymbol "The collection of syntactically well formed CycL expressions which denote symbols inthe SubL language. Examples of SubL symbols include (#$SubLQuoteFn GENLS) and (#$SubLQuoteFn CYC-SYSTEM-NON-VARIABLE-SYMBOL-P).")
(comment cancerOf "<code>(#$cancerOf REGION-TYPE CANCER)</code> means <code>CANCER</code> is the collection of cancers found in <code>REGION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CancerFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  <code>(#$CancerFn REGION-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all cancers found in the specialization of #$AnimalBLO, <code>REGION-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$CancerFn #$Throat) is the collection of all throat cancers.")
(comment Leading-BringingAboutSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BringingAboutSomething. In each #$Leading-BringingAboutSomething, something results in something else.")
(comment sentencesInducedByProgram-OverSubsetsOfPopulatedPreds "<code>(#$sentencesInducedByProgram-OverSubsetsOfPopulatedPreds PROG PRED-COUNT COMBO-COUNT MT SENTENCE-SET))</code> means that, after the ILP program <code>PROG</code> iterates through the extent in microtheory <code>MT</code> of each of the <code>PRED-COUNT</code> predicates in the sets of size <code>COMBO-COUNT</code>, <code>PROG</code> has sufficient evidence to induce the sentences in the set <code>SENTENCE-SET</code>.  
<p>
At the code level, the size of <code>PRED-COUNT</code> is typically set to 6, and the size of <code>COMBO-COUNT</code> is typically set to 3.  These are generally the values that should be passed: using any other values could be very expensive.")
(comment sentencesInducedByProgram-InMt "<code>(#$sentencesInducedByProgram-OverSubsetsOfPopulatedPreds PROG MT SENTENCE-SET))</code> means that, after the ILP program <code>PROG</code> iterates through the extent in microtheory <code>MT</code> of each of the 6 predicates in the sets of size 3 or less, <code>PROG</code> has sufficient evidence to induce the sentences in the set <code>SENTENCE-SET</code>.  
<p>
See also #$sentencesInducedByProgram-OverSubsetsOfPopulatedPreds, which allows one to adjust the values that this predicate assumes will be 6 and 3 (the number of most-populous predicates found, and the maximumsize of the subsets passed to ILP.")
(comment SentencesInducedByProgram-InMtFn "<code>(#$SentencesInducedByProgramFn-InMtFn PROG MT)</code> denotes <code>SENT-SET</code> which is the set of quoted CycL sentences that the program <code>PROG</code> has sufficient evidence to induce, given that it iterates over the sets of cardnality 3 of the 6 most populous preds in <code>MT</code>.")
(comment SentencesInducedByProgram-OverSubsetsOfPopulatedPredsFn "<code>(#$SentencesInducedByProgram-OverSubsetsOfPopulatedPredsFn
 PROG PRED-COUNT COMBO-COUNTMT)</code> denotes <code>SENT-SET</code> which is the set of quoted CycL sentences that the program <code>PROG</code> has sufficient evidence to induce, given that it iterates over the sets of cardnality <code>COMBO-COUNT</code> of the <code>PRED-COUNT</code> most populous preds in <code>MT</code>.")
(comment placeName-WithRegion "(#$placeName-WithRegion PLACE STRING) means that
STRING is the name for PLACE including the name of the
GeopoliticalEntity that PLACE is a part of. Example: (#$placeName-WithRegion #$CityOfAustinTX \"Austin, Texas\")")
(disjointWith Relation Tuple)
(disjointWith Organization-NonGeopoliticalEntity Technology-Artifact)
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntity (CollectionDifferenceFn Organization GeopoliticalEntity))
(disjointWith Organization-NonGeopoliticalEntity GeopoliticalEntity)
(comment Organization-NonGeopoliticalEntity "The collection of organizations that are not instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  This will include most of the instances of organization other than governments and countries.")
(comment PoolHall-Organization "The collection of all pool hall organizations -- the businesses where people gather to play games of pool.")
(disjointWith PersonByStudentStatus PersonTypeByActivity)
(disjointWith Color PersonTypeByActivity)
(comment DecisionSupportOntologyTerm "The collection of terms created for the Decision Support SBIR.  Many instances are special case collections that closely correspond to the KMF OWL classes and properties.  Others are more general terms designed to be used in rules that enable DS demo queries.  For the collection of terms created specifically for the mapping to the KMF ontology see #$KMFOntologyTerm.")
(comment minQuantityInBinPredDamagesObjectType "(#$minQuantityInBinPredDamagesObjectType BIN-PRED VALUE OBJECT-TYPE) means that in situations where INS is an instance of OBJECT-TYPE and (BIN-PRED INS VALUE2) holds where VALUE2 is greater than or equal to VALUE, it is highly likely that INS will suffer non-trivial damage.")
(comment durationUntilStormLandfallInFacility "(#$durationUntilStormLandfallInFacility STORM FACILITY DURATION) means that STORM is due to hit FACILITY within DURATION according to the source associated with the microtheory in which the sentence is asserted.  For instance, if the Patrick Airforce Base weather services state that the storm is due to hit the base in 72 hours, then this predicate holds of the storm, Patrick Airforce Base and (#$HoursDuration 72). ")
(comment DecisionSupportExternalSource1 "A microtheory designed to simulate a call to an external data source.")
(comment TerroristAttack-Maritime "The collection of all instances of #$TerroristAttack in which a group of terrorists carries out an attack on a #$BodyOfWater, using a #$Watercraft of some kind as a primary #$instrument-Generic.  This class includes 'boat bombings', like the #$AttackOnUSSCole-2000, as well as acts of terrorism involving piracy (see #$TerroristAttack-FeaturesPiracy).")
(comment TerroristOperationWithRecruitmentAndTraining "The collection of terrorist operations culminating in an attack, in which recruitment and training of the attackers precedes the attack proper, possibly by a period of months or years.")
(comment TerroristAttack-BlockingTransportArtery "The collection of all terrorist attacks wherein a #$TerroristGroup causes disruption by creating a #$BarrierSituation in a thoroughfare that is widely used for commercial and/or military transport, such as a highway, a subway, a river, a harbor, or a strait.")
(comment TerroristAttack-FeaturesHijacking "The collection of every #$TerroristAttack which feature a hijacking carried out as a means to another, larger end which is the actual goal and culmination of the attack.")
(comment TerroristAttack-FeaturesPiracy "The collection of all terrorist attacks in which an instance of #$Piracy-AtSea figures as a significant subevent.")
(comment TermUnacceptableForQueryStringMapping "The collection of terms that are deemed bad candidates for being instantiated in or mapped to returned builder queries from CAE search strings.")
(disjointWith Organization (CollectionDifferenceFn SomethingExisting Organization))
(comment OrganizationOfIndividuals "The collection of organizations who have only instances of #$IndividualAgent as members.")
(disjointWith OrganizationOfIndividuals OrganizationOfOrganizations)
(comment omitArgIsa "<code>(#$omitArgIsa RELN N)</code> means that the relation <code>RELN</code> is not asserted to have a non-quoted argument constraint in its <code>N</code>th argument position, due to limitations of the Cyc system.  Since every relation relates things to other things, in principle every argument position for every relation should have an #$argIsa constraint; however, asserting some #$argIsa constraints will cause certain Cyc tests to fail.")
(comment SubLAtomicTerm "The collection of all atomic denotational terms in the CycL language that are not explicitly represented in CycL (i.e. they are neither #$CycLConstants nor #$CycLVariables) but are represented in SubL, the underlying implementation language of the Cyc system.  \"Atomic\" here means not constructable from other terms via the SubL syntax.  Examples include the terms '212', ':NOUN', '#x', and 'VARIABLE-P'. Do not confuse this collection with #$SubLAtom, most of whose instances, while they are expressions of SubL, are <i>not</i> part of CycL.  Note that this collection, like most instances of #$CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\".")
(comment SubLListOrAtom "A subcollection of #$SubLSExpression. The collection #$SubLListOrAtom contains both the list-denoting expressions (see #$SubLList) and the atomic expressions (see #$SubLAtom) of SubL, the underlying implementation language for the Cyc System.  Note that #$SubLListOrAtom is a \"quoted-collection\".")
(comment organismKilledOrInjuredIn "(#$organismKilledOrInjuredIn EVENT ORGANISM) means that ORGANISM was killed or injured in EVENT.  This is the common generalization of #$animalInjuredIn and #$organismKilled.")
(comment subGroups "<code>(#$subGroups GROUP SUBGROUP)</code> means that:
<p>
(1) all #$groupMembers of <code>SUBGROUP</code> are members of <code>GROUP</code>;<br>
(2) if <code>SUBGROUP</code> is different from <code>GROUP</code>, then the members of <code>SUBGROUP</code> constitute a #$Group in their own right that is some sort of specialization within <code>GROUP</code>, and<br> 
(3) if a new member were to join <code>SUBGROUP</code>, by doing so it would also become a member of <code>GROUP</code>. 
<p> Examples: the stars in #$BigDipper-Asterism constitute one of the #$subGroups of #$MilkyWay-Galaxy; the Democrats in the House of Representatives in a given year constitute a subgroup of the group of #$USRepresentatives for that year.  Counter-example: the group of Democrats in the House of Representatives and the group of people currently located in the territory of the #$DistrictOfColumbia -- even if every member of the first group is a member of the second, and it isn't totally happenstance, a member of <code>SUBGROUP</code> could cease membership in <code>GROUP</code> without ceasing membership in <code>SUBGROUP</code>.")
(comment genls-SpecDenotesGenlInstances "An instance of #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections (q.v.) and a specialization of #$generalizations. #$genls-SpecDenotesGenlInstances relates a collection (see #$Collection) to those collections which denote instances of it. More precisely, (#$genls-SpecDenotesGenlInstances SUBCOL SUPERCOL) means that SUPERCOL is a quoted supercollection of SUBCOL: anything that is quoted instance of (see #$quotedIsa) SUBCOL is an instance (see #$isa) of SUPERCOL. For example, (#$genls-SpecDenotesGenlInstances #$List-Extensional #$List) holds.")
(comment NewtonsFirstLawMt "An instance of #$LawOfNatureMicrotheory (q.v.).  #$NewtonsFirstLawMt is the context in which #$NewtonsFirstLaw is asserted.")
(comment LawOfConservationOfMomentum "An instance of #$LawOfNature (q.v.). The #$LawOfConservationOfMomentum states that the total momentum of an isolated system of bodies remains constant.")
(comment LawOfConservationOfMomentum-Specification "An instance of #$LawOfNatureSpecification (q.v.). #$LawOfConservationOfMomentum-Specification states that the total momentum of an isolated system of bodies remains constant.")
(comment LawOfConservationOfAngularMomentum "An instance of #$LawOfNature (q.v.). The #$LawOfConservationOfAngularMomentum states that the total angular momentum of a rotating body remains constant if the net torque acting on it is zero.")
(comment LawOfConservationOfAngularMomentum-Specification "An instance of #$LawOfNatureSpecification (q.v.). #$LawOfConservationOfAngularMomentum-Specification states that the total angular momentum of a rotating body remains constant if the net torque acting on it is zero.")
(comment LawOfUniversalGravitation "An instance of #$LawOfNature (q.v.). The #$LawOfUniversalGravitation states that when two masses gravitationally interact, they attract each other with forces of equal magnitude.")
(comment LawOfUniversalGravitation-Specification "An instance of #$LawOfNatureSpecification (q.v.). #$LawOfUniversalGravitation-Specification states that when two masses gravitationally interact, they attract each other with forces of equal magnitude.")
(comment LawOfConservationOfMechanicalEnergy "An instance of #$LawOfNature (q.v.). The #$LawOfConservationOfMechanicalEnergy states that if only conservative forces are acting, the total mechanical energy of a system neither decreases nor increases in any process, rather it is conserved.")
(comment LawOfConservationOfMechanicalEnergy-Specification "An instance of #$LawOfNatureSpecification (q.v.). #$LawOfConservationOfMechanicalEnergy-Specification states that if only conservative forces are acting, the total mechanical energy of a system neither decreases nor increases in any process, rather it is conserved.")
(comment basicDataForCollection "A #$BasicDataPredicate that relates a #$Collection to a #$List of three instances of #$Set-Mathematical.  (#$basicDataForCollection COLLECTION (#$TheList PARAPHRASE-SET COL-SET OTHER-SET)) means that:
<p>
a) PARAPHRASE-SET is a set of paraphrase strings for COLLECTION.
<p>
b) COL-SET is a set of notable collections of which COLLECTION is an instance or specialization.
<p>
c) OTHER-SET is a set of other salient terms related to COLLECTION.")
(comment TestForProprietaryTermTagging "tests in this collection should be queried before a ResearchCyc KB branch to ensure the terms that come back as bindings are all marked as proprietary terms.  Note, this step needn't be done by hand, a script could be written to automatically run the queries and make the proper proprietary assertions.")
(comment Resistor "A specialization of #$TwoTerminalElectricalDevice (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Resistor is a two-terminal electrical component that can resists an electric current by producing a voltage drop between its terminals.")
(comment DeviceTypeByState "A subcollection of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState.  Each instance of #$DeviceTypeByState is a collection of devices in a similar state.  Each instance represents a particular state a device could be in.  Instances of #$DeviceTypeByState include #$Device-On and #$OffHook.")
(comment ClosingSomething "This is the collection of all actions in which a #$PartiallyTangible something is closed.  The #$objectOfStateChange must be such that it has the states of #$OpenPortal and #$ClosedPortal, and an instance of this collection involves the object going from the #$OpenPortal state to the #$ClosedPortal.  Cf. #$OpeningSomething.")
(comment chargeOfObject "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot that relates an object to its net electrical charge.  (#$chargeOfObject OBJECT CHARGE) means that OBJECT has
the #$ElectricalCharge CHARGE.")
(comment capacitance "<code>(#$capacitance OBJ C)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> has electrical capacitance <code>C</code>.")
(comment stateOfDeviceInSituation "(#$stateOfDeviceInSituation SIT DEV STATE) means that during the #$Situation SIT the #$PhysicalDevice DEV is in the #$DeviceTypeByState STATE.")
(comment stateOfPortalInSituation "(#$stateOfPortalInSituation SIT PORTAL STATE) means that during the #$Situation SIT the #$Portal DEV is in the #PortalTypeByState STATE.")
(comment ElectricalCircuit "A specialization of #$ElectricalNetwork and #$PhysicalDevice (q.v.). Each instance of #$ElectricalCircuit is an electrical network that has a closed loop which entails that it involves a return path for the current that flows through the network.")
(comment ElectricalNetwork "A specialization of #$CustomarySystemOfLinks and #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$ElectricalNetwork is an interconnected group of electrical elements such as voltage sources, switches, resistors and capacitors.")
(comment OhmsLawMt "An instance of #$LawOfNature (q.v.). #$OhmsLawMt contains propositional information to the effect that in an electrical circuit, the current is directly proportional to the potential difference.")
(comment totalVoltageSuppliedToCircuit "(#$totalVoltageSuppliedToCircuit C V) menas that V is the total voltage supplied to the circuit C by all its sources of voltage (see #$voltage suppliedBySource).")
(comment currentInCircuit "(#$currentInCircuit C I) menas that I is the total current in the circuit C.")
(disjointWith SoftDrink HumanPathogen)
(comment Inductor "An electrical device used to produce magnetic flux from an electric current.")
(comment ElectricalInductance "#$ElectricalCapacitance is a physical quantity.  It is an amount of electricity.")
(comment inductance "<code>(#$inductance OBJ IND)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> has electrical inductance <code>IND</code>.")
(comment between-Entirely "An instance of #$RelativeLocationalPredicate.  <code>(#$between-Entirely THIS THAT MID)</code> means that <code>MID</code> fills the space separating <code>THIS</code> and <code>THAT</code>, and is directly between them.")
(comment electricForceBetween "(#$electricForceBetween OBJ1 OBJ2 CHARGE) means that CHARGE is the electric force between OBJ1 and OBJ2.")
(comment cloneOfSKS "(#$cloneOfSKS ORIGINAL-SKS CLONED-SKS) means that CLONED-SKS is a cloned copy of ORIGINAL-SKS.  If the SKS was cloned perfectly, the two knowledge sources will differ only in #$constantName (including #$constantNames of #$subKSs) and #$structuredKnowledgeSourceName.")
(comment sksFusionSources "(#$sksFusionSources FUSED-SKS SOURCE-SKS-LIST) means that the knowledge sources in SOURCE-SKS-LIST were fused to create FUSED-SKS.")
(comment WordSenseDisambiguationMt "The microtheory that contains rules to disambiguate word senses. Each rule in this microtheory concludes bound #$isLicensedBy or #$isDislicensedBy literals")
(comment averageLinearVelocityOfPrimaryObjectMoving "<code>(#$averageLinearVelocityOfPrimaryObjectMoving MOVE VEL)</code> means in the #$MovementEvent <code>MOVE</code> where the primary moving object (see #$primaryObjectMoving) is <code>OBJ</code>, <code>VEL</code> is the average linear velocity of <code>OBJ</code>.  The average linear  velocity of an object in an event is the change in the object's displacement (see #$totalDisplacement) divided by the time elapsed (see #$duration) during the event.")
(comment angularDisplacement "<code>(#$angularDisplacement ROTATION DISP)</code> means that in the event <code>ROTATION</code>, the #$primaryObjectMoving underwent an angular displacement of <code>DISP</code>.")
(comment averageAngularVelocityOfPrimaryObjectMoving "<code>(#$averageLinearVelocityOfPrimaryObjectMoving MOVE VEL)</code> means in the #$Movement-Rotation <code>MOVE</code> where the primary moving object (see #$primaryObjectMoving) is <code>OBJ</code>, <code>VEL</code> is the average angular velocity of <code>OBJ</code>.  The average angular velocity of an object in an event is the change in the object's angular displacement (see #angularDisplacement) divided by the time elapsed (see #$duration) during the event.")
(comment Accelerating "A specialization of #$MovementEvent.  Each instance of #$Accelerating is an event in which the angular or linear velocity of the object moving changes.")
(comment averageRateOfRotationOfPrimaryObjectMoving "<code>(#$averageRateOfRotationOfPrimaryObjectMoving ROTATION RATE)</code> means in the #$Movement-Rotation <code>ROTATION</code> where the primary moving object (see #$primaryObjectMoving) is <code>OBJ</code>, <code>RATE</code> is the average rate of rotation of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment constantLinearAccelerationOfPrimaryObjectMoving "<code>(#$constantLinearAccelerationOfPrimaryObjectMoving MOVE ACCEL)</code> means in the #$MovementEvent <code>MOVE</code> where the primary moving object (see #$primaryObjectMoving) is <code>OBJ</code>, #$Acceleration <code>ACCEL</code> is the constant acceleration of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment initialRateOfRotationOfPrimaryObjectMoving "<code>(#$initialRateOfRotationOfPrimaryObjectMoving ROTATION RATE)</code> means in the #$Movement-Rotation <code>ROTATION</code> where the primary moving object (see #$primaryObjectMoving) is <code>OBJ</code>, <code>RATE</code> is rate of rotation of <code>OBJ</code> at the start of <code>ROTATION</code>.")
(comment terminalRateOfRotationOfPrimaryObjectMoving "<code>(#$terminalRateOfRotationOfPrimaryObjectMoving ROTATION RATE)</code> means in the #$Movement-Rotation <code>ROTATION</code> where the primary moving object (see #$primaryObjectMoving) is <code>OBJ</code>, <code>RATE</code> is rate of rotation of <code>OBJ</code> at the end of <code>ROTATION</code>.")
(comment constantAngularAccelerationOfPrimaryObjectMoving "<code>(#$constantAngularAccelerationOfPrimaryObjectMoving ROTATION RATE)</code> means in the #$Movement-Rotation <code>ROTATION</code> where the primary moving object (see #$primaryObjectMoving) is <code>OBJ</code>, <code>RATE</code> is rate angularAcceleration of <code>OBJ</code> throughout <code>ROTATION</code>.")
(comment TurningOffPoweredDevice "A specialization of #$ChangingDeviceState.  Each instance of #$TurningOffPoweredDevice is an event in which the #$stateOfDevice of some instance of #$PhysicalDevice changes from #$Device-On to #$Device-Off.")
(comment vulnerableIn "<code>(#$vulnerableIn SITUATION OBJECT RESULT-TYPE)</code> means that when in situation <code>SITUATION</code>, existing object <code>OBJECT</code> is vulnerable to hardships of type <code>RESULT-TYPE</code>.  The purpose of #$vulnerableIn is to represent vulnerabilities that stem from being in a particular situation, and presumably from playing some sort of role in that situation.  It is the situation taken as a whole, including the important background conditions, that pose the vulnerability, not some object exclusively.  Given this sense of vulnerability, and so as to distinguish this predicate from #$vulnerableTo and the like, we characterize <code>RESULT-TYPE</code> from <code>OBJECT</code>'s perspective.  <code>RESULT-TYPE</code> should therefore be a 'passive' term.")
(comment energySourceForEvent "This predicate is used to identify a particular source of energy used in a particular event.  <code>(#$energySourceForEvent EVENT ENERGYSOURCE)</code> means that <code>ENERGYSOURCE</code> provides (some of) the energy used in <code>EVENT</code>. <code>ENERGYSOURCE</code> might be a battery, the sun, a person, etc.  See also #$providesPowerFor.")
(comment intendedPrimaryFunction "A specialization of  both #$primaryFunction and #$intendedBehaviorCapable (qq.v.) that is used to indicate the primary or typical use a given  artifact (see #$Artifact-Generic) was designed to serve.  <code>(#$intendedPrimaryFunction ARTIFACT SITTYPE ROLE)</code> means that:
<p>
(i) the primary function of <code>ARTIFACT</code> is to play <code>ROLE</code> in situations of  the type <code>SITTYPE</code> and <br>
(ii) <code>ARTIFACT</code> was intended by its designer  primarily to play <code>ROLE</code> in <code>SITTYPE</code>s.
<p>
For example, the  intended primary function of a #$MammographyProvider is to  provide service (see #$providerOfService) in  #$MammographicBreastCancerScreenings; and the intended primary function of a #$Pump-Mechanical is to cause things to move  (see #$providerOfMotiveForce) in #$ConveyingMaterials events. Most artifacts have just one intended primary function, but  some have more than one.  For example, a clock-radio has two intended primary functions: displaying the current time of day  and converting transmitted radio signals into audible sounds.   Note that in #$SimpleDeviceFunctioningMt, however, it is  assumed that every #$PhysicalDevice has only one intended  primary function.")
(comment WordProcessingProgram "A specialization of #$TextEditorProgram. Each instance of #$WordProcessingProgram is a computer programs whose primary function is the production, manipulation, and editing of text (instances of #$CharacterString). This collection includes programs that can be run in batch mode (i.e. not driven by user input). For solely interactive word processors, see #$WordProcessingProgram-Interactive, and #$WordProcessingProgram-Visual.")
(comment PersonnelManagementProgram "An instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction. Each instance of #$PersonnelManagementProgram a computer program whose primary function is to gather, organize and manage information about employees.")
(comment ManagingPersonnelData "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$ManagingPersonnelData is an even in which someone gathers organizes or usefully manipulates information about the employees of a company.")
(comment KMFSalientSituationType "Each instance of this collection is a specialization of #$Situation that is pertinent to the KMF domain.")
(comment pairwisePropertyOfCollection "(#$pairwisePropertyOfCollection MODIFIER COLLECTION THING) states that THING is the property described by MODIFIER.  This is a very general predicates and its meaning in a given context is determined by what stands in its arg1.  For example, 

    <pre>
        (#$pairwisePropertyOfCollection #$Longest-Between COLLECTION DURATION)</pre>

means that DURATION is the longest empty duration between members of COLLECTION.  That is, it looks at the instances of COLLECTION and for each sequential pair it calculates the duration between them and returns the longest duration as the value for DURATION.  Note that COLLECTION must be a collection of temporal things for which the start and end dates are known.
.")
(comment pairwisePropertyOfCollection-IncludeReferenceEntities "A quaternary #$QueryMacroPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$pairwisePropertyOfCollection-IncludeReferenceEntities MODIFIER COLLECTION THING SET)</code> states that <code>THING</code> is the property described by <code>MODIFIER</code> and <code>SET</code> is a set of instances of <code>COLLECTION</code> that jointly satisfy the final comparision in terms of <code>MODIFIER</code>.  This is a very general predicate and its meaning in a given context is determined by what stands in its arg1.  For example, 
<pre>
  (#specifiedPropertyOfCollection-IncludeReferenceEntities #$Longest-Between COLLECTION DURATION SET)
</pre>
means that <code>DURATION</code> is the longest duration between (the respective ending and starting points of) sequential intances of <code>COLLECTION</code>, and <code>SET</code> is a set of sequential instances that have <code>DURATION</code> between them.  (Note that, in this case, <code>COLLECTION</code> must be a collection of temporal things for which the start and end dates are known.)")
(comment PairwiseModifierType "A collection of terms that serve as argument places in instances of #$QueryMacroPredicate.  The terms in this collection allow one to bring back the results of a pairwise comparison between members of a set or collection.")
(comment specifiedPropertyOfCollectionMember "(#$specifiedPropertyOfCollectionMember MODIFIER COLLECTION THING) states that THING is the member of collection that has the property described by MODIFIER.  For instance, if MODIFIER=#$DeadliestFn, then THING will be the event in which more people were killed than any other event in COLLECTION
.")
(comment SpecifiedValueModifierType "A collection of terms that serve as argument places in instances of #$QueryMacroPredicate.  The terms in this collection allow one to bring back a member of a collection or set that has the a particular type of value in some specified property, e.g. \"most killed\", \"most wounded\", etc.")
(comment collectivePropertyOfCollection "(#$specifiedPropertyOfCollectionMember MODIFIER COLLECTION THING) states that THING is the member of collection that has the property described by MODIFIER.  For instance, if MODIFIER=#$DeadliestFn, then THING will be the event in which more people were killed than any other event in COLLECTION
.")
(comment CollectivePropertyModifierType "A collection of terms that serve as argument places in instances of #$QueryMacroPredicate.  The terms in this collection allow one to bring back some value that is a function of the members of a collection taken as a whole.  For example, #$CardinalityFn allows one to return the number of members of the collection..")
(comment victim "(#$victim EVT AGENT) means that AGENT was a victim in EVT.  This is a very general predicate in that there are many ways to be a victim in an event.  For instance one could be a person killed in an rock slide, the animal wounded in a hunting event, the organization that is the object of a hostile take-over, etc.")
(comment urlOfCW "<code>(#$urlOfCW WORK URL)</code> means that an electronic encoding or instantiation of <code>WORK</code> (see #$ElectronicFn and #$ComputerFileCopy) is available on the #$Internet at the web address <code>URL</code>.")
(comment DecisionSupportOwlExportTerm "The collection of terms included in the owl export of the enriched KMF deployed ontology.")
(comment DecisionSupportOwlExportTerm-WithSuggestedDownwardClosure "The collection of terms included in the owl export of the enriched KMF deployed ontolgy with selected downward closure terms.")
(comment stormWindSpeedMax "<code>(#$stormWindSpeedMax STORM SPEED)</code> means that <code>STORM</code> involves wind speeds of up to <code>SPEED</code>.")
(comment HVACSystem "A specialization of #$ClimateControlDevice and #$ElectricalDevice.  Each instance of #$HVACSystem is a sysytem used to regulate the heating, air conditioning and ventilation in a building.")
(comment KeylessEntryCardReader "A specialization of #$ElectricalDevice.  Each instance of #$KeylessEntryCardReader is an electrical device that supports the ability to unlock a door without a key, but rather with a radio signal from a card.")
(comment KeylessEntry "A specialization of #$EnteringAnHOC.  Each instance of #$KeylessEntry is an event in which an agent uses a #$KeylessEntryCardReader to open a door and enter a building.")
(comment functionalityCompromised "(#$functionalityCompromised SIT-TYPE) means that the ability for things to act in a situation of SIT-TYPE is provably compromised.  If some type TYPE of object is such that its instances are defeasibly capable of playing some role in instances of SIT-TYPE, that functionality is compromised if some instance of TYPE is provably incapable of playing that role in SIT-TYPE.")
(comment ClimateControl "Each instance of #$ClimateControl is an event in which air temperature is purposefully heated or cooled, or in which air quality or humidity is altered.")
(comment residenceOfOrganization "The predicate #$residenceOfOrganization indicates the #$GeographicalAgent in whose territory a particular organization has its main offices.  <code>(#$residenceOfOrganization ORG GEOGAGENT)</code> means that the #$Organization <code>ORG</code> has its chief office on the territory of <code>GEOGAGENT</code>.  <code>GEOGAGENT</code> is typically a #$City but may be a larger or smaller #$GeographicalAgent.  For example, the #$residenceOfOrganization of the #$UnitedStatesFederalGovernment is the #$CityOfWashingtonDC.
<p>
Use #$hasHeadquartersInRegion to refer to a #$GeographicalRegion, such as #$ManhattanIsland, that is the location of the main offices.")
(comment Agent-NonGeographical "A specialization of #$Agent-Generic and #$EnduringThing-Localized (qq.v.).  #$Agent-NonGeographical is the collection of all spatially-located agents that are not geographical (cf. #$GeographicalAgent).  Specializations include #$EmbodiedAgent, #$CommercialOrganization, and #$LegalCorporation.")
(comment numberOfInstancesOfCollPerInstanceOfDateType "(#$numberOfInstancesOfCollPerInstanceOfDateType DATE-TYPE DATE EVENT-TYPE NUM) holds of every NUM such that NUM is the number of instances of EVENT-TYPE that occur in DATE where DATE is an instance of DATE-TYPE.")
(comment FloatingInASubstance "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$FloatingInASubstance is an event in which an object floats (is suspended) in a liquid or gaseous substance.")
(comment FloatingInLiquid "A specialization of #$FloatingInASubstance (q.v.).  Each instance of #$FloatingInLiquid is an event in which something floats in a liquid.")
(comment intendedBehaviorCapable "A #$SituationTypeTernaryPredicate that is used to describe the functions a given artifact (see #$Artifact-Generic) is, by design, capable of serving. <code>(#$intendedBehaviorCapable ARTIFACT SITTYPE ROLE)</code> means that (i) <code>ARTIFACT</code> can play <code>ROLE</code> in situations or events of type <code>SITTYPE</code> (see #$behaviorCapable) and (ii) <code>ARTIFACT</code> is intended by its designer to play  <code>ROLE</code> in situations or events of type <code>SITTYPE</code>.  Note that a given artifact  can be intended to be capable of serving more than one function.  (In  contrast, such things typically have just one <i>primary</i> function; see #$primaryFunction.)  For example, a wall calendar is intended to be  capable both of being hung on a wall and of being legible; a vacuum  cleaner is meant to serve both as a device (see #$deviceUsed) and --  in virtue of its dust bag -- as a container (see #$containerUsed) in #$Vacuuming events.")
(comment contextOfAgentOnTheRecord "A #$FunctionalSlot that relates intelligent agents to the microtheories that contain the propositions they go on the record as endorsing. <code>(#$contextOfAgentOnTheRecord AGENT CONTEXT TIME)</code> means that <code>CONTEXT</code> is the context that contains all the propositions endorsed by <code>AGENT</code> on the record (and their closure) at <code>TIME</code>.")
(comment TerroristAttackTargetTypeType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$TerroristAttackTargetTypeType is a collection a specialization of which, TYPE, appears in a (#$relationInstanceExists #$intendedAttackTargets FOO TYPE) assertion for some FOO.  The instances which have been selected offer the most complete coverage of the collections appearing in those assertions.  It is useful, but not necessary, to think of this collection as a near faceting of the (non-reified) collection of things targeted in terrorist attacks.")
(comment numberOfInstancesOfCollRelatedToInstancesOfType "(#$numberOfInstancesOfCollRelatedToInstancesOfType TYPE INSTANCE TYPE2 NUM BIN-PRED) holds of every NUM such that NUM is the number of instances of TYPE2 that have BIN-PRED to INSTANCE where INSTANCE is an instance of TYPE.  For example, the relevant property for #$Country is #$eventOccursAt while the relevant property for #$TerroristGroup-Islamist is #$performedBy.  If #$Country replaced TYPE and the query were run with some given specialization of #$Event for TYPE2 with INSTANCE and NUM open, it would return pairs of Countries and numbers such that the number is the number of instances of EVENT-TYPE that occurred in that country.  Similarly, a query with #$TerroristGroup-Islamist replacing THING will net you pairs of terrorist groups that are instances of #$TerroristGroup-Islamist and the number of attacks they have performed.  Note that this predicate will only be well-defined for those types (and their specializations) that we have specifically supported.")
(comment numberOfInstancesOfCollRelatedToSpecsOfType "(#$numberOfInstancesOfCollRelatedToSpecsOfType TYPE INSTANCE TYPE2 NUM BIN-PRED) holds of every NUM such that NUM is the number of instances of TYPE2 that have BIN-PRED to INSTANCE where INSTANCE is a specialization of TYPE.  For example, if BIN-PRED is #$intendedAttackTargets and TYPE is #$GovernmentalBuilding, the running the query with a specified subcollection of #$Event fro TYPE2 will return pairs consisting of a specialization of #$GovernmentalBuilding and the number of instances of the event type that targeted that type of building.  Note that although arg3 takes any sort of collection, It is mostly designed for use with collections of events")
(comment CAEUserCreatedCollection "This is the collection of collections created by users of the CAE.")
(comment numberOfInstancesOfCollRelatedToInstancesOfType-Inverse "(#$numberOfInstancesOfCollRelatedToInstancesOfType TYPE INSTANCE TYPE2 NUM BIN-PRED) holds of every NUM such that NUM is the number of instances of TYPE2 in which (BIN-PRED INSTANCE INSTANCE-OF-TYPE2) holds where INSTANCE is an instance of TYPE.")
(comment suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg "<pre>(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg PRED COLL-1 N COLL-2 M)</pre> holds just in case COLL-1 is the collection of terms that are suitable suggestions for substitution into arg N of PRED when an instance of COLL-2 stands in arg M.

<br><br>
For example,   
<br><br>
(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg #$relationInstanceExists #$CasualtyPredReplacement 1 #$AgentCasualtyPredicate 1)
<br><br>
 means that instances of #$CasualtyPredReplacement should be offered up as suggested replacements in arg1 of #$relationInstanceExists literals when an instance of #$AgentCasualtyPredicate appears in arg1 of the literal.

Note that if you just want to specify the suggested replacements regardless of the terms appearing in other argument positions you can assert:

<pre>(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg PRED COLL-OF-REPLACEMENTS N #$Predicate 0)</pre>.")
(comment suggestionsForPredRelativeToGenlsInArg "<pre>(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToGenlsInArg PRED COLL-1 N COLL-2 M)</pre> holds just in case COLL-1 is the collection of terms that are suitable suggestions for substitution into arg N of PRED when an specialization of COLL-2 stands in arg M.

<br><br>
For example,   
<br><br>
(#$suggestionsForPredRelativeToIsaInArg #$isa #$TerroristAttackTacticType 2 #$AttackOnObject 2)
<br><br>
 means that instances of #$TerroristAttackTacticType should be offered up as suggested replacements in arg1 of #$isa literals when an specialization of #$AttackOnObject appears in arg1 of the literal.")
(comment GenericAgentRelatingBinaryPredicate "A collection of binary predicates that can relate individuals or groups to individuals or groups.  Predicates that are restricted in either argument place to either #$Group or #$IndividualAgent will not be instances of this collection.")
(comment possibleSuspects "(#$possibleSuspects EVT AGT) means that there is some reason to believe that AGT has performed EVT.  Usually this entails there being some positive connection between EVT and AGT (e.g. AGT is known to perform acts of that type in the area) and there is a lack of conclusive evidence refuting the connection between EVT and AGT (e.g. it is not the case that the attack occurred before the existence of AGT or after AGT's existence).")
(comment KMFOntologyObjectFn "(#$KMFOntologyObjectFn ONT ID COL) denotes the object defined by ONT, identified by ID, and of type COL.")
(comment MakingBiologicalToxins "This is the collection of events in which some biological toxin is manufactured.")
(comment SA2Missile "A type of surface-to-air missile.")
(comment SA3Missile "A type of surface-to-air missile.")
(comment FactGatheringGoal "The goal-category of wanting to gather facts, e.g. from a corpus such as the world wide web.")
(comment isaOrGenls-ForPragmaticsOnly "A generalization of #$isa and #$genls.  This predicate is not suitable for knowledge representation.  It's only purpose is to get around the fact that we can't make disjunctive pragmaticRequirements.")
(comment FactGatheringForbiddenPredicate "A sub-collection of #$Predicate.  Each instance of #$FactGatheringForbiddenPredicate is a predicate which should not be used for fact gathering.")
(comment factGatheringUnspecifiableArgPosition "(#$factGatheringUnspecifiableArgPosition PRED INTEGER) means that when constructing sentences to use to gather facts with PRED in the arg0 position, it is not feasible to specify arg INTEGER, leaving other positions open.")
(comment FactGatheringTypicallyUnspecifiedSetOrCollection "The collection #$FactGatheringTypicallyUnspecifiedSetOrCollection is a sub-collection of #$SetOrCollection.  Each instance of this collection is such that if it is the argIsa argument constraint for the Nth argument position for a predicate P, then that predicate position is one which should not be the only specified position when the constructing knowledge acquisition goals with P in the arg0 position.")
(comment LawEnforcementOfficer "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, and a specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$LawEnforcementOfficer is a person whose job is to detect and stop people engaged in illegal activities.  The collection #$LawEnforcementOfficer includes members of local, state, and special police (e.g., transit police) forces, as well as federal agents (e.g., members of border patrols, national security agents).  Consequently, a given instance of #$LawEnforcementOfficer typically also belongs to one of the following collections: #$StateEmployee, #$LocalGovernmentEmployee, or #$NationalGovernmentEmployee (see #$PublicSectorEmployee).")
(comment CycBasedFactGatheringProcess "A specialization of #$ComputerActivity. Each instance of #$CycBasedFactGatheringProcess is an event in which a #$Cyc based process attempts to find facts in a corpus on data outside of the Cyc knowledge base.  For example, such a process might involve a number of #$StringBasedSearching sub-events based on knowledge acquisition goals that Cyc knows about.  These string-based searches, in turn might have a number of #$ObtainingAStringBasedSearchResult sub-events, which, when parsed, could provide Cyc with knowledge of facts.")
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntityOrRegion (CollectionDifferenceFn PartiallyTangible GeopoliticalEntityOrRegion))
(comment predicateListForDeterminationHasAllArgIsas "<code>(#$predicateListForDeterminationHasAllArgIsas DET LIST-OF-PREDS)</code> means that for the #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination <code>DET</code>, the list <code>LIST-OF-PREDS)</code> has all of its argument constraints, via #$argIsa, asserted.")
(comment cycVariableBindingSelectionGoalOfType "<code>(#$cycVariableBindingSelectionGoalOfType QUOTED-SENTENCE SET-OR-COLLECTION GOAL-CATEGORY)</code> means that #$Cyc has the goal of type <code>GOAL-CATEGORY</code> of knowing what elements of <code>SET-OR-COLLECTION</code> can be substituted for the single open variable in the quoted <code>SENTENCE</code> to result in a true sentence.")
(comment FactGatheringCAEUsableFETTemplateTopic "A specialization of #$CAEUsableFETTemplateTopic.  Each instance is a template topic vetted for use both with theCAE and with fact-gathering.")
(comment FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery "The collection of queries used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology.")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-CAETemplateBased "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are derived from fields in the Cyc fact-entry tool.")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-WordSenseDisambiguationBased "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are derived from predicates known to be useful for word sense disambiguation.")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-FactSheetBased "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are derived from fields in Cyc fact sheets.")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-ForNERExperiment "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are deemed useful for named entity recognition experiments.")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-InstancesOfFactGatheringPredicate "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are derived from predicates that re instances of the collection #$FactGatheringPredicate (q.v.)")
(comment CycBasedFactGatheringProcessNamedFn "(#$CycBasedFactGatheringProcessNamedFn NAME-STRING) denotes the #$CycBasedFactGatheringProcess named NAME-STRING.")
(comment TheFactGatheringFocalTerm "A quoted instance of #$IndexicalConcept.  This indexical concept is used in particular instances of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-CAETemplates-SpecificTerm "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are generated by looking at a single focal term and determining which CAE templates are pertinent to that term.")
(comment mentorOf "<code>(#$mentorOf PERSON MENTOR)</code> means that <code>MENTOR</code> is the mentor of <code>PERSON</code>, in the sense that <code>MENTOR</code> is a teacher or trusted counselor or advisor of <code>PERSON</code>.")
(comment protegeOf "<code>(#$protegeOf PERSON PROTEGE)</code> means that <code>PROTEGE</code> is the protege of <code>PERSON</code>.")
(comment protegeOf "<code>(#$professorOf PERSON PROFESSOR)</code> means that <code>PROFESSOR</code> is the professor of <code>PERSON</code>.")
(comment Pedestrian "The collection of people (Homo Sapiens) that are travelling by foot.  This corresponds to the commonsense notion of a pedestrian.  Note that this is not equivalent to someone who is currently moving by foot (c.f. #$Locomotion-TwoLegged).  Someone that is walking a short distance from a store to their car would not necessarily be considered a pedestrian.")
(comment ByWheeledVehicle "(#$modeOfTravel AGENT ByWheeledVehicle) means that AGENT is
capable of (has the necessary equipment for, etc.) travelling by
wheeled vehicle, and can be expected to travel by such means in the
situation at hand, should AGENT do any travelling at all. ")
(comment ByFoot "(#$modeOfTravel AGENT ByFoot) means that AGENT is capable of
travelling by foot, and can be expected to travel by such means in the
situation at hand, should AGENT do any travelling at all.")
(comment ByTrackedVehicle "(#$modeOfTravel AGENT ByTrackedVehicle) means that AGENT is
capable of (has the necessary equipment for, etc.) travelling by
tracked vehicle, and can be expected to travel by such means in the
situation at hand, should AGENT do any travelling at all.")
(comment WordSenseDisambiguationPredicate "A specialization of #$Predicate.  Each instance of #$WordSenseDisambiguationPredicate is a predicate used to disambiguate word senses.  Typically, these predicates will be specializations of #$isLicensedBy (q.v.).")
(comment MilitaryPlace "A location that used by military organizations on a regular basis and generally administered or controlled by military personnel.  Typical specializations include military bases, military posts, military checkpoints, etc.  A negative example of an instance would be a night club frequented by members of a nearby army base.")
(comment familyName "<code>(#$familyName PERSON STRING)</code> means that #$Person <code>PERSON</code> is known by the #$HumanFamilyNameString <code>STRING</code> as his or her family name (surname).  E.g., (#$familyName #$Lenat \"Lenat\").  A person rarely has more than one family name at any one time.  Family names may change as a result of certain actions, such as marriages, deaths, etc., in various cultures.  In current (20th Century) Western cultures, #$familyNames are the same as #$lastNames, while in many Eastern cultures (Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Vietnamese) they are #$firstNames.")
(comment AssistantPredFn "(#$AssistantPredFn ROLE) returns the #$OrganizationalPositionSlot of being assistant to an agent playing the #$OrganizationalPositionSlot ROLE in a system.  This means that if the player PLAYER of the functional role SYSROLE in SYSTEM is required by that role to play an actor role in a certain event, whoever plays the role of (#$AssistantPredFn SYSROLE) in SYSTEM is required to assist PLAYER.")
(comment Assistant "The collection of persons who are assistant something-or-others as their occupation.  This is a very general collection and its specs include assistant managers, assistant chiefs of staff and so forth.  Normally the instances of this collection are denoted via #$AssistantFn.")
(comment AssistantFn "(#$AssistantFn POS-TYPE) returns the #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg that is the position of being the assistant POS-TYPE.  For example, (#$AssistantFn #$HealthInspector) denotes the collection of people who are assistant health inspectors.  Note: not every instance of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg has a non-empty #$AssistantFn collection -- e.g. there probably are no assistant chaos theorists.  Also, recursive applications of this function should be avoided.")
(comment CampaignManager "the Manager of a #$PoliticalElectionCampaign.")
(comment spokesmanFor "(#$spokesmanFor AGENT INTEL-AGENT) means that #$IntelligentAgent INTEL-AGENT is the #$Spokesman for AGENT. A #$Spokesman is authorized by some agent to speak on behalf of that
agent to other agents or the public.")
(comment spokesmanForIndividual "<code>(#$spokesmanForIndividual SPOKES INDIV)</code> means that <code>SPOKES</code> is a spokesman for <code>INDIV</code>.  See also #$spokesmanFor.")
(comment eventCasualtyDataSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Event to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$eventCasualtyDataSentence EVENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact about the casualties in/of EVENT.  See also #$CasualtyPredicate.")
(comment specInversesRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTTypeInArg "<code>(#$specPredsRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTTypeInArg PRED TERM-SUMMARY-PRED TYPE N)</code> means that if a thing <code>THING</code> is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, then any assertions in which an inverse specialization of <code>PRED</code> occurs in arg 0 and <code>THING</code> occurs as arg <code>N</code> should appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment countryCodeTrigraph "(#$countryCodeTrigraph PLACE CODE) means that CODE is an internationally recognized three-letter abbreviation for the name of PLACE, according to the ISO-3166-1 standard")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-FactSheetBased-SpecificTerm "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are generated by looking at a single focal term and determining which fact-sheet displayed predicates are pertinent to that thing.")
(comment FactGatheringPSQ-ForNERExperiment-SpecificTerm "A specialization of #$FactGatheringPartialSentenceQuery.  Each instance of this collection is a query used to collect partial sentences to be passed to the Cyc-based fact gathering technology, where the partial sentences are generated by looking at a single focal term and where the partial sentences are deemed useful for named entity recognition experiments.")
(comment Function-Denotational "A specialization of #$Relation (q.v.) and the collection of all functions.  Each instance of #$Function-Denotational is a many-one relation that represents, with respect to any given context, a mapping from one set of things (the function's #$relationDomain) to another set of things (its #$relationRange).  As a many-one relation, a function maps each thing in its domain to exactly one thing in its range.  A function might be unary, binary, ternary, etc. (see #$arity; but cf. #$relationalArity), depending on whether the members of its domain are singletons, ordered pairs, ordered triples, etc.  In general, the domain of an N-ary function with respect to a given context is a set of ordered N-tuples (construed in CycL as #$Lists of length N).  The function is said to take the items from any of these N-tuples as its N <i>arguments</i> and to return a member of its range as its corresponding <i>value</i> (see #$valueOfFunctionForArgs).  There are also functions that are not of any particular fixed arity; see #$VariableArityFunction.
<p>
For example, #$GovernmentFn is the unary function that takes each #$GeopoliticalEntity to its #$RegionalGovernment, and #$PlusFn is the variable-arity function that takes any sequence of two or more #$ScalarIntervals
(q.v.) to their arithmetic sum.
<p>
Note that the domain and range (i.e. the extension) of a given function might vary from context to context.  For example, as the government of a country can change over time, #$GovernmentFn will in such cases map the same country to different governments with respect to different times.  Thus, an instance of #$Function-Denotational is closer to what is sometimes called a \"function-in-intension\" than to the purely set-theoretical notion of a \"function-in-extension\".
<p>
CycL terms that denote functions can be used to form non-atomic terms (or \"NATs\"; see #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm).  Specifically, when such a function-denoting expression is appropriately combined with other expressions (i.e. the former is in the 0th argument position and the latter are of the correct number and type) the resulting expression is a new CycL term (a NAT) that may then freely appear as a component in other CycL expressions.  The NAT will itself denote the value (if any) of the function denoted by the former expression for the sequence of arguments denoted, respectively, by the latter expressions.  For example, #$GovernmentFn is a unary function, and so the CycL constant '#$GovernmentFn' requires one syntactic argument (such as the constant '#$France') to form a NAT (in this case, the expression '(#$GovernmentFn #$France)').  This NAT, which denotes the government of France, can in turn serve as a syntactic argument in any CycL expression in which a term for an instance of #$RegionalGovernment can legally occur.
<p>
Important subcollections of #$Function-Denotational include #$IndividualDenotingFunction (whose instances always return instances of #$Individual), #$CollectionDenotingFunction, #$SetDenotingFunction, and #$FunctionDenotingFunction (which is itself a subcollection of the first).  NATs formed using terms that denote instances of #$FunctionDenotingFunction denote instances of #$Function-Denotational themselves.  Thus, like most other things, functions can be denoted in CycL either by constants  (e.g. '#$GovernmentFn') or -- although this is less common -- by NATs (e.g.  '(#$FunctionToArg 2 #$biologicalMother)').
<p>
An important partition of #$Function-Denotational is into #$TotalFunction and #$PartialFunction (qq.v.).
<p>
Note that #$Function-Denotational does not include any of the so-called #$TruthFunctions (q.v.): #$Predicates, #$Quantifiers, or #$LogicalConnectives. For these relations (as construed in CycL) are not really functions at all, even though it can be heuristically useful to think of them as if they were functions from sequences of arguments to truth values.")
(comment Predicate "A specialization of #$TruthFunction (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Predicate is either a property of things (see #$UnaryPredicate) or a relationship holding between two or more things.  Like other truth-functions, predicates, or rather the expressions that represent or denote them, are used to form sentences.  More precisely, any CycL expression that denotes an instance of #$Predicate (and only such an expression) can appear in the \"0th\" (or \"arg0\") position (i.e. as the term following the opening parenthesis) of a #$CycLAtomicSentence (q.v.).  Important specializations of #$Predicate include #$UnaryPredicate, #$BinaryPredicate, #$TernaryPredicate, #$QuaternaryPredicate, and #$QuintaryPredicate.  Note that, despite its name, #$Predicate is a collection of <i>relations</i>, and not a collection of expressions that represent or denote such relations.")
(comment Cyc101QueryToolDemoQuery "A specialization of #$CommonSenseTest.  Each instance of this collection is a commonsense test useful for illustrating a particular aspect of the query tool's behavior.")
(comment nodesForSetConceptFilter "(#$nodesForConceptFilter NODE FILTER) means that NODE can be displayed (and its instances as well) in the the concept panel during tasks of the type correlated with FILTER.")
(comment CoEquivalenceBinaryPredicate "A specialization of  #$IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate, #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate, and  #$QuasiTransitiveBinaryPredicate (qq.v.).  A binary predicate <code>PRED</code> is a #$CoEquivalenceBinaryPredicate if and only if <code>PRED</code> is irreflexive, symmetric, and <b><i>quasi-transitive</i></b>.  This collection consists of exactly all of the instances of #$QuasiTransitiveBinaryPredicate that are also symmetric and irreflexive.
<p>
Note that a necessary condition on <code>PRED</code>'s being a co-equivalence predicate is that its two argument-places must be co-satisfiable; see #$cosatisfiableInArgs and #$NoteOnArgumentCosatisfiabilityRequirement.
<p>
Instances of #$CoEquivalenceBinaryPredicate include #$cohabitants, #$connectedTerminals, and #$twins.
<p>
Cf. #$EquivalenceRelation.")
(comment QueryMacroPredicateEventTypeInArgPosition "The collection of #$QueryMacroPredicates that make sense to suggest as statistical queries when one of the focal concepts is a collection of events (Attacks in the terrorism domain).")
(comment QueryMacroPredicateAgentTypeInArgPosition "The collection of #$QueryMacroPredicates that it makes sense to offer up a query based on the predicate when the user has selected an agent-type")
(comment suggestedOpenPositionForPred "(#$suggestedOpenPositionForPred PRED NUM) means that we should not try to instantiate the NUM argument place in PRED when we generate a query using PRED.")
(comment QueryMacroPredicateAgentInArgPosition "The collection of #$QueryMacroPredicates that it makes sense to offer up a query based on the predicate when the user has selected an agent")
(comment Analyst-PertinentConcept "An instance of #$ConceptTypeByDomain.  Generally speaking, instances of #$Analyst-PertinentConcept are concepts and relations such as are used by intelligence analysts reasoning about threat situations.  Specifically, all core concepts in this domain (see #$coreConceptOfDomain) are either 1) #$BinaryPredicates referenced in AKB Fact Entry Templates, 2) #$TernaryPredicates referenced in AKB Fact Entry Templates, 3:)#$FirstOrderCollections that are asserted to be #$argIsas of #$BinaryPredicates referenced in AKB Fact Entry Templates, 4) #$FirstOrderCollections that are asserted to be #$argIsas of #$TernaryPredicates referenced in AKB Fact Entry Templates, 5) #$FirstOrderCollections that are asserted to be #$argGenls of #$TernaryPredicates referenced in AKB Fact Entry Templates, or 6) concepts or relations that are instances of instances of #$TKBInterfaceCollection.")
(comment defaultValueForPredInArg "(#$defaultValueForPredInArg PRED NUM THING) means that when generating queries using PRED you should generate them with THING in arg-NUM.")
(comment requiredBoundArgInQuerySearch "(#$requiredBoundArgInQuerySearch PRED NUM) means that in order for a literal involving PRED in arg0 to be offered up as a query search result the NUMth argument place must be bound with an extracted/selected concept or provided by a #$defaultValueForPredInArg GAF")
(comment StatisticalPredicate "Instances of this collection are predicates that express \"statistical\" relations.  They often compare the members of one or more collections and relate those collections to a number of some sort.")
(comment ComputerDataArtifact "The collection of all pieces of computer data stored in hardcopy form or in computer memory. This collection includes all such information, such as data streams (e.g., bits or bytes of data in addressable memory) and more complex objects such as files in a filesystem (see the specialization of this collection, #$ComputerFileCopy).  Instances of #$ComputerDataArtifact are  <i>non-agentive</i> existing things; thus computer processes and software agents are not instances of this collection.  Instances of #$ComputerDataArtifact are actual physical objects  which encode information (e.g., via ink on paper or magnetic domains, holes in a piece of paper, or voltage fluctuations in a device corresponding to bits or bytes).")
(comment ComputerDataArtifact-Generic "The collection of all pieces of computer data. This collection includes all such information, such as data streams (e.g., bits or bytes of data in addressable memory) and more complex objects such as files in a filesystem (see the specialization of this collection, #$ComputerFileCopy).  Instances of #$ComputerDataArtifact-Generic are  <i>non-agentive</i> existing things; thus computer processes and software agents are not instances of this collection.  Instances of #$ComputerDataArtifact-Generic encode information, but are not necessarily physical objects (see #$ComputerDataArtifact).")
(comment campaignManagerOf "<code>(#$campaignManagerOf MANAGER CAMPAIGNER)</code> means that <code>MANAGER</code> is the campaign manager of <code>CAMPAIGNER</code> in some instance of #$PoliticalElectionCampaign.")
(comment PersonTypeByPositionInOrg "A collection of collections.  A #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg is a collection representing a type of position in an organization.  More precisely, each instance of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg is the collection of instances of #$Person who typically hold that position within some #$Organization or other.  For example, #$Scout is the collection of all persons who are scouts -- e.g.  people who lead people through wilderness areas or jungles.  #$Scout is an instance of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg because typically a scout performs those duties within the context of their employment with some organization or other.  Some other instances of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg are #$Mayor, #$CampaignManager, #$Director-Movie, #$BaseballShortstop, and #$Secretary.  Obviously, which position-types are filled in a given organization partly depends on the type of organization it is; thus cities have mayors while business firms do not.
<p>
Note that #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg is _not_ a specialization of #$PersonTypeByOccupation (q.v.); the latter categorizes workers according to the kinds of activities they perform at work rather than the positions organization members hold in their respective organizations.  The typical activities of a vice president of a toy manufacturer (e.g.) are likely to be very unlike those of the vice president of a stamp club.  An instance of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg need not be a spec of #$PersonWithOccupation.
<p>
Since every action is taken to be performed as part of one's job in #$JobMt, #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg <i>is</i> a specialization of #$PersonTypeByOccupation there.")
(comment argN "A predicate that relates a CycL term and an  integer (representing an argument-position) to a CycL formula in  which the term appears (in that position). <code>(#$argN TERM N FORMULA)</code> means that <code>TERM</code> occurs in the <code>N</code>th argument-position within <code>FORMULA</code>. For example, the sentence `(#$argN #$Dog 1 (#$genls #$Dog #$Mammal))' holds.  Note that #$argN's first and third argument-places are both \"quoted\" (see #$quotedArgument); thus in the context of the above  #$argN sentence the constituent term `#$Dog' denotes  <i>itself</i>  (rather than the collection of dogs), and similarly for the  constituent #$genls sentence.")
(comment governmentalMinister "<code>(governmentalMinister ORG MINIST)</code> means that <code>MINIST</code> is a minister in <code>ORG</code>.  Cf. specializations, such as #$financeMinister and #$defenseMinister.")
(comment unknownDeceased "(#$unknownDeceased ANIMAL) means that ANIMAL is not known (by the Cyc system) to be deceased.  This predicate is not assertible.")
(comment Treatise "A collection of #$ProseLiteraryWork-CW instances that deal formally and systematically with a single subject.")
(comment Tract-CW "A collection of short #$Treatise instances that typically deal with religious subjects and are published in #$Pamphlet form.")
(comment Procedure-Specification "A type of #$Protocol that specifies a series of actions to be performed in a certain order in a certain type of situation, with an intended result.")
(comment EarliestFn "A collection denoting unary function.  (#$EarliestFn COLL) denotes the subcollection of COLL that consists of the earliest known instance of COLL (A collection of events) -- there could be more than one \"earliest\" because of ties.  Most often though, this will return a collection with a single instance.")
(comment TotalEclipse "A type of #$Eclipse-CelestialEvent in which the #$Shadow of the intervening body either falls completely on the other body or completely covers it.")
(comment LatestFn "A collection denoting unary function.  (#$LatestFn COLL) denotes the subcollection of COLL that consists of the latest known instance of COLL (A collection of events) -- there could be more than one \"latest\" because of ties.  Most often though, this will return a collection with a single instance.")
(comment threatToTypePossiblyPresentInRegion "(#$threatToTypePossiblyPresentInRegion THREAT-TYPE THREATENED-TYPE REGION) means that there is some possibility that an instance of THREAT-TYPE could be used to damage or otherwise harm an instance of THREATENED-TYPE in REGION.")
(comment sitTypePosesThreatToType "(#$sitTypePosesThreatToType SIT-TYPE TYPE) means that the occurrence of any instance of SIT-TYPE poses a (possibly mitigable) threat to instances of TYPE.  Generally this holds when SIT-TYPE is the collection of situations in which there are objects which can harm instances of type which are in possession of an entity with the desire and ability to use them.")
(comment SituationTypeSuchThatFn-New "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction that allows one to specify subcollections of #$Situation in terms of sentences that truly describe any situation of the relevant type.  For example, (#$SituationTypeSuchThatFn-New (#$and  (#$postureOfAnimal #$BillClinton #$SittingPosture) (#$objectFoundInLocation #$BillClinton TheOvalOffice))) denotes the collection of all situations in which Bill Clinton is sitting somewhere in the Oval Office.")
(comment KnowledgeManagementTechnology-Artifact "The collection of all pieces of technology used primarily for knowledge management (information storage and retrieval).")
(comment SemanticallyEnabledKnowledgeTechnology-Artifact "The collection of pieces of knowledge-management technology that use real-world knowledge to perform knowledge-management tasks.")
(comment JointResearchCentre-ResearchLab "The Joint Research Centre, a research laboratory that provides support for the entire European Union.")
(comment EuropeanCommission "The executive branch of the European Union.")
(comment GeorgeWBush "An instance of #$UnitedStatesPresident. 43rd President of the United States; son of George Herbert Walker Bush (born in 1946).")
(comment KingHusseinBinTalalAlHashimi "An instance of #$HomoSapiens. King of Jordan credited with creating stability at home and seeking peace with Israel (1935-1999).")
(comment HongKong "An instance of #$Colony-GeopoliticalEntity. Formerly a Crown Colony on the coast of southern China in Guangdong province; leased by China to Britain in 1842 and returned in 1997; one of the world's leading commercial centers.")
(comment (BelieverFn DemocraticRepublicanIdeology) "A sub-collection of #$Agent-NonGeographical. Each instance is an advocate of democratic principles.")
(comment MikhailGorbachev "An instance of #$HeadOfPoliticalParty. Soviet statesman whose foreign policy brought an end to the Cold War and whose domestic policy introduced major reforms (born in 1931).")
(comment ColinPowell "An instance of #$USSecretaryOfState-Federal. United States general who was the first Black to serve as Chief of Staff; later served as Secretary of State under President George W. Bush (born 1937).")
(comment TheWhiteHouse "An instance of #$House-Modern. The government building that serves as the residence and office of the President of the United States.")
(comment StudentVisa-Document "A specialization of Visa-Document. Each instance of Visa-Document is a document issued by the government of some country to one (or more) person(s), authorizing that person (or those persons) to enter that country and remain for a certain period of time while engaging in study.")
(comment ObtainingAStudentVisa "The act of obtaining a student visa.")
(comment ObtainingAVisa "The act of obtaining a visa.")
(comment NationalRifleAssociation "An instance of #$Lobby-PoliticalOrganization. A powerful lobby that advocates the right to own and bear arms and rejects any gun regulation by the government.")
(comment Critic "A sub-collection of #$Person. Each instance is a person who is professionally engaged in the analysis and interpretation of works of art.")
(comment Victory "A sub-collection of #$Event. Each instance is a successful ending of a struggle or contest.")
(comment CardiacValveType "This is the collection of the different types of cardiac valves.  This includes only those found in the CCG XML file CardiacValve.xml.  CCF classifies what value an instance of #$CCFCardiacValveReference is about with their OWL property \"ptrec:CardiacValve\" .")
(comment Stenosis-Condition "A condition in which there is an abnormal narrowing of a blood vessel or other tubular body part.")
(comment Regurgitation-Circulatory "A condition in which the blood flow in a blood vessel is opposite from normal.")
(comment MedicalAnalysisTask "A specialization of #$Allotment that represents general medical research and analysis taskings.")
(comment analysisTask "<code>(#$analysisTask SPECIFICATION TASK)</code> relates a CAE specification to the specific task (#$Allotment) of that specification.")
(comment cAEQuerySearchFilter "<code>(#$cAEQuerySearchFilter SPECIFICATION FILTER)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, FILTER should be used to filter concepts from a user search when trying to find appropriate query components.  In the current implementation, FILTER is limited to being an instance of #$DecisionTreeConceptFilter, though there is no particlar ontological reason not to be broaden it to ConceptFilter.")
(comment analystNotebookEnabled "<code>(#$analystNotebookEnabled SPECIFICATION #$True)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, the #$CycAnalyticEnvironment-TheProgram should attempt to use Analyst Notebook for displaying graphs, where applicable. An arg2 of #$False means that the CAE should not be used at all.")
(comment defaultQueryMt "<code>(#$defaultQueryMt SPECIFICATION MT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, any queries that do not come with a pre-specified #$Microtheory should be asked from MT.")
(comment queryLibraryRootFolder "<code>(#$queryLibraryRootFolder SPECIFICATION FOLDER)</code> means that in the #$CycAnalyticEnvironment-TheProgram specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, the program should start populating the query library folder from FOLDER.")
(comment factEditorFocalType "<code>(#$factEditorFocalType SPECIFICATION COLL)</code> means that in the #$CycAnalyticEnvironment-TheProgram specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, data entry forms for instances of COLL should be made available to the user by default.")
(comment coGenlInverseWRTTypes "<code>(#$coGenlInverseWRTTypes PRED-1 PRED-2 TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> means that if:<br><br> 1) <code>(PRED-1 INS-1 INS-2)</code>, <br>2) <code>(#$isa INS-1 TYPE-1)</code>, <br>3) <code>(#$isa INS-2 TYPE-2)</code><br><br> then it follows that <br>4) <code>(PRED-2 INS-2 INS-1)</code>.<br> <br> Moreover, 1) follows from the conjunction of 2), 3), and 4).")
(comment provinces "<code>(#$provinces COUNTRY PROVINCE)</code> identifies <code>PROVINCE</code> as one of the provinces of the country <code>COUNTRY</code>.")
(comment MinistryOfCulture "The collection of instances of #$Ministry responsible for protecting or advancing a culture or cultures of a region.")
(comment HospitalVisit "A specialization of #$VisitingASite.  Instances of #$HospitalVisit are events in which some individual checks into a hospital for some length of time.  If the visit include a nights stay, then it also counts as an instance of #$Lodging.")
(comment Ulna "The #$Collection of all #$Forearm bones called 'ulna' by the medical profession.  Each #$Ulna lies within a #$Forearm and connects the #$Elbow to the #$Wrist.")
(comment averagePrecipitation "The average quantity per year of precipitation falling in this geographical region, converted to equivalent measures of rain.            This is the rate averaged over a long period of time, so that the          irregularity is averaged out.")
(comment IntervalMaxFn "<code>(#$IntervalMaxFn SCALAR)</code> returns an interval of the same type as <code>SCALAR</code> whose maximum value is the maximum value of <code>SCALAR</code> and whose minimum value is minus infinity.  For example, (#$IntervalMaxFn (#$Mile 3)) is the same as `the interval from negative infinity miles to three miles'. [Technical Note: if that expression were to denote a strictly absolute, as opposed to a relative-or-absolute, distance, then it would mean `the interval from 0 miles to 3 miles'.]   (#$IntervalMaxFn (#$Unity 1)) is the same as `the interval from negative infinity to 1', in other words, `no greater than one'.")
(comment IntervalMinFn "<code>(#$IntervalMinFn SCALAR)</code> returns an interval of the same type as <code>SCALAR</code> whose minimum value is the minimum value of <code>SCALAR</code> and whose maximum value is #$PlusInfinity.  For example, (#$IntervalMinFn (#$Mile 3)) is the same as `the interval from three miles to an infinite number of miles', in other words, `at least three miles'.")
(comment synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes-Inverse "A predicate used to indirectly map concepts from external data sources into Cyc, even though the target concept has not been reified. <code>(#$synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes RELN SOURCE STRING TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means that the string <code>STRING</code>, as it occurs in the data source <code>SOURCE</code>, denotes a binary predicate <code>PRED</code> such that <code>(#$coGenlInverseWRTTypes RELN PRED TYPE1 TYPE2)</code>.")
(comment genericCycLMappingToSourceString "The most general predicate for representing mappings of terms from data sources into Cyc. <code>(#$genericCycLMappingToSourceString THING SOURCE STRING)</code> means that there is some mapping of a denotation of <code>STRING</code> as it occurs in <code>SOURCE</code> to a concept, represented in Cyc, that is closely related to THING.  This mapping might be one in which <code>STRING</code> denotes <code>THING</code> (a \"true\" mapping -- see #$synonymousExternalConcept), or one in which <code>STRING</code> maps to a concept not reified in Cyc, but to a concept that can be characterized in terms of operations on <code>THING</code> (see, e.g., #$synonymousExternalPred-Inverse, #$synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes, and #$synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes-Inverse).")
(comment synonymousExternalPred-Inverse "A ternary predicate that relates an instance of #$BinaryPredicate to a term that occurs in a data source, <code>(#$synonymousExternalPred-Inverse PRED SOURCE STRING)</code> means that the predicate <code>PRED</code> is the co-inverse of a predicate <code>OTHER-PRED</code> (i.e., <code>(#$inverseBinaryPredicateOf PRED-1 PRED-2)</code> holds) such that, within the data source <code>SOURCE</code>, the string <code>STRING</code> denotes <code>OTHER-PRED</code>.")
(comment synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes "A predicate used to indirectly map concepts from external data sources into Cyc, even though the target concept has not been reified. <code>(#$synonymousExternalPredWRTTypes PRED-1 SOURCE STRING TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means that the string <code>STRING</code>, as it occurs in the data source <code>SOURCE</code>, denotes a binary predicate <code>PRED-2</code> such that <code>(#$equivPredsWRTTypes PRED-1 PRED-2 TYPE1 TYPE2)</code>.")
(comment synonymousExternalConcept "<code>(#$synonymousExternalConcept THING SOURCE STRING)</code> means that as it occurs in the external data source <code>SOURCE</code>, the string <code>STRING</code> denotes <code>THING</code>.")
(comment Cardiomyopathy "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition. Each instance of #$Cardiomyopathy is a deterioration of the function of a myocardium (muscle tissue of the heart).")
(comment Endocarditis-Infection "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType and a specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Endocarditis is an inflammation of an #$Endocardium.")
(comment MeasuringSomething "A specialization of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction.  Each instance of #$MeasuringSomething is an event in which an agent uses a physical device to measure some physical attribute of a tangible object.  The last part of such an event involves the perception (and perhaps recording) of a result of the measurement (see the predicate #$measurementResult) by some instance of #$PerceptualAgent.  See also the function #$MeasuringFn.")
(comment VascularStent "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$VascularStent is a wire mesh tube used to repair damaged arteries.")
(comment DiseaseType-AtrialDisorder "The collection of diseases that are considered atrial disorders.")
(comment DiseaseAfflictingPartFn "(#$DiseaseAfflictingPartFn ORGANISM-PART) denotes a collection of diseases instances of which affect instances of ORGANISM-PART, a spec of #$OrganismPart, in their victims. See #$ailmentTypeAfflictsPartType.")
(comment AtrialDisorder "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$AtrialDisorder is a disease that afflicts the #$Atrium.")
(comment CardiacAssistDeviceProcedure "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$CardiacAssistDeviceProcedure is an event in which a #$CardiacAssistDevice is either removed (see #$CardiacAssistDeviceRemoval) or inserted (see #$CardiacAssistDeviceInsertion).")
(comment CardiacAssistDeviceRemoval "A specialization of #$CardiacAssistDeviceProcedure.  Each instance of #$CardiacAssistDeviceRemoval is an event in which a #$CardiacAssistDevice is removed from a patient.")
(comment CardiacAssistDeviceInsertion "A specialization of #$CardiacAssistDeviceProcedure.  Each instance of #$CardiacAssistDeviceInsertion is an event in which a #$CardiacAssistDevice is inserted into a patient.")
(comment CardiacAssistDevice "A specialization of #$MedicalDevice.  Each instance of #$CardiacAssistDevice is a mechanical device designed to support a failing heart.")
(comment CoronaryArteryProcedureNonCongenital-Surgical "The collection of all surgical procedures that involve the #$CoronaryArtery.")
(comment BloodTransfusionEvent "An event in which an
amount of blood from one or more donors (typically from a blood bank or similar organization) is transfused into another organism. A
#$BloodTransfusionEvent will have a #$BloodTransfusionProcess subEvent.
This unit is not cooextensive with #$BloodTransfusionProcess, since a
#$BloodTransfusionEvent will have other #$subEvents, such as inserting the
IV needle into the recipient's vein.")
(disjointWith ChronicLungDisease UpperRespiratoryDistress)
(comment MyocardialScar "A specialization of #$Scar.  Each instance of #$MyocardialScar is a scar on a heart.")
(comment Clot "Each instance of #$Clot is a lump of matter of some sort.")
(comment Thrombus "The collection of blood clots formed within a vessel that remain attached to the locations where they formed.")
(comment BloodClot "The collection of blood clots.")
(comment SurgeryLesion "The collection of lesions received during surgery.")
(comment HeartAttack "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType, and a specialization of #$HeartCondition. #$HeartAttack denotes the collection of all physiological conditions in which some region of the heart muscle is damaged due to an inadequate supply of oxygen. Note that #$HeartAttack is different from #$CardiacArrest, which denotes the collection of all physiological conditions in which the heart has stopped beating or is otherwise unable to pump a quantity of blood sufficient to sustain vital organs.")
(comment HibernatingIschemicMyocardium "A specialization of #$HeartCondition.  Each instance of #$HibernatingIschemicMyocardium is a condition in which segments of the myocardium exhibit abnormal contractile function.")
(comment Myocardium "The collection of all myocarrdia.  A #$Myocardium is the  muscle tissue of the #$Heart.")
(comment rtvPanelEnabled "<code>(#$rtvPanelEnabled SPECIFICATION BOOLEAN)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, the #$relatedToVia query panel is enabled when BOOLEAN is #$True, and disabled otherwise.")
(comment PulmonaryArtery-Generic "The collection of all pulmonary arteries.  A #$PulmonaryArtery-Generic carries #$DeoxygenatedBlood from the right ventricle of the #$Heart to or within the #$Lungs.  For the left and right (main) pulmonary arteries see #$PulmonaryArtery-Main.")
(comment Dyslipidemia "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Dyslipidemia is a disruption in the normal amount of lipids in the #$Blood.")
(comment AmaurosisFugax "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition. Each instance of #$AmaurosisFugax is a temporary loss of vision in one eye caused by decreased blood flow to the retina.")
(comment Hemoptysis "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType.   Each instance of #$Hemoptysis is a condition involving coughing up blood or blood-stained sputum.")
(comment Orthopnea "A specialization of #$Dyspnea.  Cases of #$Orthopnea are shortnesses of breath experienced when in a prone position.")
(comment Trepopnea "A specialization of #$Dyspnea.  Cases of #$Trepopnea are shortnesses of breath experienced when lying on one side, but not the other.")
(comment Palpitation "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition.  Each instance of #$Palpitation is an awareness of the beating of the heart, especially with regard to whether it is irregular or abnormally slow or rapid.")
(comment Cryoprecipitate "Cryoprecipitate is a blood transfusion product prepared from plasma which also contains fibrinogen, von Willebrand factor, factor VIII, factor XIII and fibronectin.")
(comment DiagonalCoronaryArtery "A specialization of #$CoronaryArtery.  Each instance of #$DiagonalCoronaryArtery is diagonals is a branch of the #$LeftAnteriorDescendingArtery-Coronary that runs diagonally away from it and towards the left front of the #$Heart.")
(comment CerebrovascularNeurologicAttack "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$CerebrovascularNeurologicAttack is an event in which the neurological functioning of the brain is affected by a problem with the cerebrovascular circulatory system.  Important specializations include: #$Stroke-PhysiologicalCondition, #$TransientIschemicAttack, and #$ReversibleIschemicNeurologicDeficit.")
(disjointWith TransientIschemicAttack Stroke-PhysiologicalCondition)
(disjointWith TransientIschemicAttack ReversibleIschemicNeurologicDeficit)
(disjointWith ReversibleIschemicNeurologicDeficit Stroke-PhysiologicalCondition)
(comment organTransplanted "<code>(#$organTransplanted TRANSPLANT ORGAN)</code> means that in the #$TransplantSurgery event <code>TRANSPLANT</code>, the organ transplanted is <code>ORGAN</code>.")
(comment NorvascProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by #$PfizerInc.")
(comment Inotrope "A specialization of #$DrugProduct.  Each instance of #$Inotrope is a drug that increases or decreases the force of muscular contractions. #$NegativelyInotropicAgents weaken the force of muscular contractions, and #$PositivelyInotropicAgents increase the strength of muscular contraction.")
(comment PositivelyInotropicAgent "A specialization of #$Inotrope.  Each instance of #$PositivelyInotropicAgent is a drug product that increases the strength of muscular contraction.")
(comment NegativelyInotropicAgent "A specialization of #$Inotrope.  Each instance of #$PositivelyInotropicAgent is a drug product that increases the strength of muscular contraction.")
(disjointWith PositivelyInotropicAgent NegativelyInotropicAgent)
(comment ChemicalSubstanceType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  Each instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType is a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible whose instances are defined <i>only</i> by their chemical composition -- not by their physical state or any other property. Instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType can be of two varieties:  
<p>
(1) Collections whose instances are completely uniform with each other in terms of chemical composition; this includes (a) the chemical elements -- such as #$Carbon, #$Oxygen, and #$Hydrogen -- which are instances of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons (thus, the latter is a specialization of #$ChemicalSubstanceType), and (b) chemical compounds constituted of more than one substance chemically bonded, e.g., #$Water, #$Caffeine, and #$IronOxide, which are instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies 
<br>
(2) Substances which have a general chemical specification, that is, whose instances do not have exactly the same chemical composition but fall within certain specifications, e.g., #$DNAStuff. 
<p>
Note that collections that are <i>not</i> instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType include collections of substances which have some component which is of overriding significance in some context, so that in everyday language such substances are frequently referred to by the name of their important component (e.g., \"penicillin\" applied to a tablet containing penicillin), but which have significant admixtures of other substances. Thus, #$Penicillin is an instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType, but the collection of tablets containing penicillin and including other ingredients is not.  Also, specializations of #$Mixture, such as #$Lemonade, are <i>not</i> instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType, because mixtures are determined by their physical state rather than solely by their chemical composition.")
(comment Nitrate "A specialization of #$IonicCompound.  Each instance of #$Nitrate is a partially tangible substance composed of molecules each of which has at least one #$NitrateIon and one other positively charged ion.")
(disjointWith SportsPlayingArea Weapon)
(disjointWith WaterMain Weapon)
(disjointWith Spillway Weapon)
(disjointWith Weapon FlyingFreehold)
(disjointWith Framework-SupportingStructure Weapon)
(disjointWith Partition-ConstructionArtifact Weapon)
(disjointWith Weapon RetailBusinessStand)
(disjointWith Weapon TransformerSubstation)
(disjointWith CustomsCheckpoint Weapon)
(disjointWith Weapon SwimmingPool)
(disjointWith StepOfStairs Weapon)
(disjointWith Weapon NaturalGasProcessingPlant)
(disjointWith Weapon Railing)
(disjointWith Weapon StageForPerformances)
(disjointWith WindowPane Weapon)
(disjointWith HandRail Weapon)
(disjointWith Weapon ElectricPowerGrid)
(disjointWith Weapon Bar-Place)
(disjointWith Weapon AstronomicalObservatory)
(disjointWith Weapon MemorialMarker)
(disjointWith Weapon Curb)
(comment MineShaftEntrance "The collection of surface openings to mine shafts (see #$MineShaft).")
(comment Adit "The collection of instances of #$MineShaftEntrance that are oriented vertically, so that miners and equipment need not be lowered into the mine, but can instead walk or be carted to it.")
(comment Dopamine "A specialization of #$Neurotransmitter and #$Hormone.")
(comment CommonCarotidArtery "A specialization of #$SystemicArtery.  The common carotid artery supplies the head and neck with blood.  It is a paired structure: there are two common carotid arteries in the body, one for each side. The right common carotid originates in the neck from the brachiocephalic trunk, whereas the left common carotid arises from the aortic arch.")
(comment BrachiocephalicArtery "The collection of all brachiocephalic trunks (or arteries).  Each #$HomoSapiens has one #$BrachiocephalicArtery, which branches off of the #$AscendingAorta towards the right side of the body.  The #$BrachiocephalicArtery is a #$SystemicArtery which #$branchesInto the right #$CommonCarotidArtery (which serves the head) and the right #$SubclavianArtery.  Another name for #$BrachiocephalicArtery is 'innominate artery'.")
(comment SubclavianArtery "The collection of all subclavian arteries.  The proximal ends of the right and left #$SubclavianArtery connect to the matching #$BrachiocephalicArtery.  The distal ends of a #$SubclavianArtery becomes the #$AxillaryArtery.")
(comment AorticArch "The collection of all aortic arches.  An #$AorticArch is the horizontal section of an #$Aorta following the #$AscendingAorta and preceding the #$DescendingAorta.  Each #$BrachiocephalicArtery (or trunk), left #$CommonCarotidArtery and left #$SubclavianArtery branches off of an #$AorticArch.")
(comment AorticCoarctation "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType. Aortic coarctation is narrowing of the aorta where the ductus arteriosus inserts.")
(comment BrachiocephalicVein "The collection of all brachiocephalic #$Veins.  The proximal ends of the right and left #$BrachiocephalicVeins connect to the #$SuperiorVenaCava.  The distal ends of the #$BrachiocephalicVeins become the #$SubclavianVeins.")
(comment SubclavianVein "The collection of all subclavian #$Veins.  The proximal ends of the right and left #$SubclavianVeins connect to the #$BrachiocephalicVeins.  The distal ends of the #$SubclavianVeins become the #$AxillaryVeins at the level of the #$FirstRibs.")
(comment AorticRoot "The collection of all aortic roots.  An #$AorticRoot is the section of the #$Aorta immediately next to the #$AorticValve.")
(comment AortaAscendingAboveRoot "The collection of all portions of the #$AscendingAorta beyond the #$AorticRoot.")
(disjointWith AortaAscendingAboveRoot AorticRoot)
(comment InferiorVenaCava "The collection of all inferior vena cavas.  An #$InferiorVenaCava is the main #$Vein in the #$Abdomen that empties into the right atrium.  It is formed by the junction of the proximal ends of the right and left #$CommonIliacVeins.  The #$InferiorVenaCava returns all #$Blood from the lower body to the #$Heart.")
(comment VenaCava "A specialization of #$SystemicVein.  Each instance of #$VenaCava is a vein that empties directly into the heart.")
(comment AtrialFibrillationProcedure-Surgical "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$AtrialFibrillationProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed to correct the condition of #$AtrialFibrillation.")
(comment ResectionProcedure-Surgical "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$ResectionProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed to remove part or all of an organ or other structure or tissue.")
(comment CystCondition "The condition of having a #$Cyst -- an abnormal growth characterized by a sac-like membrane.")
(disjointWith Cyst Organ)
(comment Cyst "A specialization of #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of #$Tumor is an abnormal tissue mass found in an animal.  Instances of #$Tumor include both malignant (cancerous -- see the collection #$Cancer) and benign (non-cancerous) growths which have no normal physiological cause or function.")
(comment Biopsy-SurgicalProcedure "A medical care event involving the removal of cells or tissues for examination.")
(comment Septum-Heart "The collection of all septums that are the dividing walls between the right and left sides of the heart.")
(comment Ultrasound "A specialization of #$Sound.  Each instance of #$Ultrasound is a sound wave having a #$Frequency (q.v.) greater than 20,000 cycles per second, a frequency which is above the range of human hearing.")
(comment Echocardiogram "A specialization of #$MedicalTesting.  Each instance of #$Echocardiogram is an application of ultrasound imaging to monitor the #$Heart.")
(comment Electrocardiogram "A specialization of #$MedicalTesting.  Each instance of #$Electrocardiogram is the use of an #$EKGMonitor to test the #$Heart.")
(comment Thrombolysis "A specialization of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent.  Each instance of #$Thrombolysis is the breakdown of blood clots by pharmacological means.")
(comment Thrombosis "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Thrombosis is the condition of having a blood clot inside a blood vessel, obstructing the flow of blood through the circulatory system.")
(comment Defibrillator "A specialization of #$MedicalDevice.  Each instance of #$Defibrillator is a medical device desinged to deliver a therapeutic electrical current to the heart to induce a normal heart rhythm.")
(comment Cardioversion "A specialization of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent.  Each instance of #$Cardioversion is an event in which abnormal atrial or ventricular rhythms are converted back to normal sinus rhythm.")
(comment InflammationFn "(#$InflammationFn ORGANISM-PART) denotes a collection of ailments constitued by inflammation of ORGANISM-PART, a specialization of #$OrganismPart. See also #$ailmentTypeAfflictsPartType.")
(comment Myocarditis "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType and a specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Myocarditis is an inflammation of a #$Myocardium.")
(comment CardiacValveProsthesis "A specialization of #$MedicalDevice.  Each instance of #$CardiacValveProsthesis is a medical device designed to replace a native heart valve.")
(comment artificialBodyPartOfType "<code>(#$artificialBodyPartOfType ARTIFICIAL-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means that <code>ARTIFICIAL-TYPE</code> is the collection of artificial body parts that are artificial versions of instances of the collection <code>PART-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ArtificialBodyPartOfTypeFn "<code>(#$ArtificialOrganOfTypeFn ORGAN-TYPE)</code> is the collection of artificial versions of the specialization of #$Organ, <code>ORGAN-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$ArtificialOrganOfTypeFn #$Heart) is the collection of artificial hearts.")
(comment LegalCode "A specialization of #$GovernmentCOC.  Each instance of #$LegalCode is a code of conduct consisting of all the laws that hold in some instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  One notable instance of #$LegalCode is #$UnitedStatesCode.")
(comment OfficeOfTheLawRevisionCounsel "The organization that publishes the United States Code (see #$UnitedStatesCode).")
(comment UnitedStatesCodeTitle "The collection of subdivisions of #$UnitedStatesCode by topic. There are fifty of these, plus some appendices.")
(comment CodesOfConductDataMt "An instance of #$DataMicrotheory, used for representing basic facts about instances of #$CodeOfConduct.")
(comment or "A #$LogicalConnective that represents disjunction in #$CycL. It is a #$VariableArityRelation, taking an arbitrary number of instances of #$CycLSentence-Assertible as arguments.  (#$or P Q ... Z) is true if and only if at least one of the sentences P, Q, ..., or Z is true.")
(comment CardiacCatheterization-Diagnostic "A specialization of #$MedicalCareEvent.  Each instance of #$CardiacCatheterization is a diagnostic test performed by inserting a catheter into a chamber or vessel of the #$Heart.")
(comment Chapter-PCW "The collection of all chapters of larger, subdivided #$TextualPCWs.  An example would be Chapter 4 of the #$AdventuresOfHuckleberryFinn.  See also the predicate #$chapters, which relates individual instances of #$Chapter-PCW to the works that contain them.")
(comment chapters "<code>(#$chapters WORK CHAPTER)</code> means the instance <code>CHAPTER</code> of #$Chapter-PCW is a chapter of the instance of #$TextualPCW <code>WORK</code>.")
(comment ChapterOfWork-OrdinalFn "A term of the form <code>(#$ChapterOfWork-OrdinalFn WORK N)</code> denotes the
<code>N</code>th chapter of <code>WORK</code>, an instance of #$TextualPCW. The 2nd
argument of this function should correspond to the ordinal number explicitly
assigned to the chapter in the book, but it need not: in some books, for
instance, chapters are not numbered. In such cases, the arg2 corresponds to
the actual sequential order of the chapters.")
(disjointWith Chapter-PCW Section-PCW)
(comment SectionOfWork-OrdinalFn "A term of the form <code>(#$SectionOfWork-OrdinalFn WORK N)</code> denotes the <code>N</code> top level section of <code>WORK</code> (as opposed to a sub-section of <code>WORK</code>.  If a <code>WORK</code> is not subdivided into numbered sections then this function is undefined.")
(comment cocTitles "<code>(#$cocTitles COC TITLE)</code> identifies <code>TITLE</code> as a title (a high-level #$subWorks) of <code>COC</code>, an instance of #$CodeOfConduct and #$TextualPCW.")
(comment Aneurysm "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Aneurysm is a localized dilation of a blood vessel.")
(comment SaccularAneurysm "A specialization of #$Aneurysm.  Each instance of #$SaccularAneurysm is an aneurysm that resembles a small sack.  Contrast this with the collection #$FusiformAneurysm, which is the collection of aneurysms shaped like spindles.")
(comment MitralValve "A specialization of #$HeartValve.  Each instance of #$MitralValve is a #$Valve at the #$Portal from the left #$AuricleOfHeart into the left #$VentricleOfHeart which prevents #$Blood from passing back into the #$AuricleOfHeart during systole.")
(comment HemolyticAnemia "A specialization of #$Anemia.  Hemolytic anemia is anemia caused by hemolysis, which is  the abnormal breakdown of red blood cells.")
(comment ThoracicCavity "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$ThoracicCavity is a chamber of a body that is protected by the #$ChestWall (the #$RibCage and associated skin, muscle, and fascia).")
(comment ChestWall "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$ChestWall is the part of a #$Chest-BodyPart that is the boundary of the #$ThoracicCavity.")
(comment appendixes "<code>(#$appendixes WORK APPENDIX)</code> identifies <code>APPENDIX</code>, an instance of #$Appendix-PCW, as an appendix of <code>WORK</code>, an instance of #$TextualPCW.  See also #$appendix-DocumentPartOf, which relates a work to the structure of its appendix(es).")
(comment RadialArtery "The collection of all radial arteries.  The proximal end of the #$RadialArtery connects to the #$BrachialArtery, passes through the #$Forearm and then ends in the #$Hand.")
(comment ReplacementSurgery "A specialization of #$SurgicalTreatment (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ReplacementSurgery is a surgery event in which part of a body is replaced.  An instance of this collection could be a transplant (replacement by donated organ -- see the specialization, #$TransplantSurgery), or it could involve replacement of a body part with artificial substitute.")
(comment OpenHeartSurgery "A specialization of #$MajorSurgery.  Each instance of #$OpenHeartSurgery is a surgery involving procedures that require direct action on the #$Heart.")
(comment TransplantSurgery "A specialization of #$ReplacementSurgery.  Each instance of #$TransplantSurgery is surgery in which a part of a body is transplanted (e.g., one organ may be replaced with a donor organ).")
(comment HeartTransplantSurgery "A specialization of #$MajorSurgery and #$TransplantSurgery.  Each instance of #$HeartTransplantSurgery is a surgical operation in which a whole donor heart is used to replace the patient's existing heart.")
(comment LungTransplantSurgery "A specialization of #$TransplantSurgery.  Each instance of #$LungTransplantSurgery is a surgical operation in which a #$Lung is transplanted..")
(comment HeartTransplantProcedure-Surgical "A specialization of #$TransplantProcedure-Surgical .  Each instance of #$HeartTransplantProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure in which a #$Heart is transplanted.")
(comment KidneyTransplantProcedure-Surgical "A specialization of #$TransplantProcedure-Surgical .  Each instance of #$KidneyTransplantProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure in which a #$Kidney is transplanted.")
(comment LiverTransplantSurgery "A specialization of #$TransplantSurgery.  Each instance of #$LiverTransplantSurgery is a surgical operation in which a #$Liver is transplanted..")
(comment PancreasTransplantSurgery "A specialization of #$TransplantSurgery.  Each instance of #$PancreasTransplantSurgery is a surgical operation in which a #$Pancreas is transplanted.")
(comment Tracheostomy-SurgicalProcedure "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$Tracheostomy-SurgicalProcedure is a surgical procedure performed on the neck to open a direct airway through an incision in the #$Trachea.")
(comment EvaluatablePredicate "A specialization of both #$EvaluatableRelation and #$Predicate (qq.v.).   Each instance of #$EvaluatablePredicate is a  predicate associated (via #$evaluationDefn) with a piece of HL (\"heuristic level\") code that computes the resulting truth-value when the predicate is applied to legal 
arguments. These truth-values can, of course, be computed only when all of the predicate's argument positions are bound: thus Cyc inference will not generate viable inference tactics for non-fully-bound literals with evaluatable predicates in the arg 0 position.  As one might expect, most evaluatable predicates are mathematical or syntactic in nature; for numbers, sets, lists, and strings are the sorts of things that are related in various ways that can be calculated 
algorithmically.  Examples include #$greaterThan and #$substring. Thus the sentence `(#$greaterThan 3 1)' evaluates to (and so if used to ask a query will return the answer) `#$True'.")
(comment Fistula "A specilaization of #$PhysicalConnection-Configuration and #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of #$Fistula is an abnormal connection between organs or vessels that do not normally connect.")
(comment FistulaCondition "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition .  Each instance of #$FistulaCondition is a physiological condition in which a #$Fistula is present.")
(disjointWith Translation-RandomTrajectory DirectedTranslation)
(comment Translation-RandomTrajectory "The collection of all instances of single-trajectory translations (#$Translation-SingleTrajectory) in which the associated #$Trajectory is what physicists and engineers sometimes refer to as a 'random walk':  i.e., where the vector of the trajectory (the direction and speed of motion, with direction defined as the directed slope tangential to the graph at a given point) is essentially unpredictable, notwithstanding the availablity of information about the vector at previous points along the trajectory.  Usually, a #$Translation-RandomTrajectory comes about because the motion in question is the statistical summation of forces deriving from the microscopic state of the medium in which the #$primaryObjectMoving is fully or partly immersed.Examples include the Brownian motion of a particle suspended in water or some other fluid, or the path of a photon making its way from the core of the sun to the photosphere (constantly being absorbed and re-emitted on a random vector by the surrounding plasma:  takes about 100 years after its creation by nuclear fusion in the core to escape).")
(comment Drifting "The collection of all random path translations in which the #$primaryObjectMoving is suspended in a fluid, i.e. a liquid or a gas.  Examples include the movement of a toy baloon on the breeze (but not necessarily the movement of a manned hot-air balloon or a dirigible!) or the movement of the Mary Celeste at the time she was discovered.")
(comment TransportationDeviceTypeByCrewedStatus "A #$FacetingCollectionType that partitions #$TransportationDevice into 'manned' and 'unmanned' collections (see #$Manned-CrewAttribute and #$Unmanned-CrewAttribute).")
(comment Manned-CrewAttribute "The collection of all 'manned' #$TransportationDevices, i.e., all #$TransportationDevices which have assigned 'crew' who are present 'on' the device.")
(comment Unmanned-CrewAttribute "The collection of all 'unmanned' #$TransportationDevices, i.e., all #$TransportationDevices for which no assigned 'crew' is physically present 'on' the device.")
(disjointWith Manned-CrewAttribute Unmanned-CrewAttribute)
(comment RenalDisease "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$RenalDisease is an ailment condition afflicting a #$Kidney.")
(comment CardiacTamponade "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$CardiacTamponade is a condition in which liquid rapidly accumulates in the #$Pericardium.")
(comment PhoneNumber "A specialization of #$ContactInfoString. Each instance of #$PhoneNumber is a character string that can be used to call a particular #$Telephone or telephone-like device, such as a #$Pager or #$FaxMachine.")
(comment InteratrialSeptum "The collection of all interatrial septa.  An individual #$InteratrialSeptum is the partition separating the left and right atria (see #$Atrium) of the #$Heart.")
(disjointWith AtrioventricularValve SemilunarValve)
(comment AtrioventricularValve "A specilization of #$HeartValve.  Each instance of #$AtrioventricularValve is a heart vlave that is located between an atrium and a ventricle.  For example, mitral valves are atrioventricular valves because they are found between right atria and left ventricles.")
(comment SemilunarValve "A specialization of #$HeartValve.  Each instance of #$SemilunarValve is a valve positioned on the pulmonary artery or the aorta. Semilunar valves do not have chordae tendinae and are more similar to valves in veins than they are to the other class of heart valves, #$AtrioventricularValves.")
(comment relationExistsUniqueAll "<code>(#$relationExistsUniqueAll PRED COL1 COL2)</code> means that, for every instance of <code>COL2</code>  (such as <code>INS2</code>), there is exactly one instance of <code>COL1</code> (<code>INS1</code>) such that <code>(PRED INS1 INS2)</code> holds.  This is the same as <code>(#$relationExistsCountAll PRED COL1 COL2 1)</code>.")
(comment TricuspidValveCusp-Anterior "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$TricuspidValveCusp-Anterior is a large cusp of the #$TricuspidValve, located between the atrioventricular orifice and the conus arteriosis of a #$Heart.")
(comment TricuspidValveCusp-Posterior "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$TricuspidValveCusp-Posterior is a cusp of the #$TricuspidValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment TricuspidValveCusp-Septal "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$TricuspidValveCusp-Septal is a cusp of the #$TricuspidValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment MitralValveCusp "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$MitralValveCusp is a cusp of the #$MitralValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment MitralValveCusp-Anterior "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$MitralValveCusp-Anterior is a large cusp of the #$MitralValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment MitralValveCusp-Posterior "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$MitralValveCusp-Posterior is a cusp of the #$MitralValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment TricuspidValveCusp "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$TricuspidValveCusp is a cusp of the #$TricuspidValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment AorticValveCusp "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$AorticValveCusp is a cusp of the #$AorticValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment AorticValveCusp-Posterior "A specialization of #$AorticValveCusp.  Each instance of #$AorticValveCusp-Posterior is a posterior cusp of the #$AorticValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment AorticValveCusp-Right "A specialization of #$AorticValveCusp.  Each instance of #$AorticValveCusp-Right is a right cusp of the #$AorticValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment AorticValveCusp-Left "A specialization of #$AorticValveCusp.  Each instance of #$AorticValveCusp-Left is a left cusp of the #$AorticValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment AbnormalProtusion-Biological "Each instance of this collection is an abnormal growth attached to some organism's body part that protrudes from it.")
(disjointWith Vegetation-AbnormalOutgrowth Organ)
(comment Vegetation-AbnormalOutgrowth "A specialization of #$OrganismPart.  An outgrowth located on some body part.  In cardiac medicine it refers to any of the warty excrescenses on the valves of the heart typically composed of various tissue elements.")
(comment PapillaryMuscle "A specialization of #$SmoothMuscle.  Papillary muscles are muscles of the #$Heart that limit the movements of the #$MitralValve and #$TricuspidValves.  Primarily, papillary muscles prevent these valves from being inverted.")
(disjointWith HeartValveDysfunction HeartDisease-NonValvular)
(comment Section-PCW "The collection of all sub-works of instances of #$TextualPCW explicitly identified within the work (through numbering or some other indicator) as \"sections.\"  In CycL, this relationship is reified as #$textualPCWSections; membership in this collection is defined in terms of this relationship.  These sub-works typically appear in instances of #$Article-PCW, #$Chapter-PCW, or in textual instances of #$CodeOfConduct.  By definition, this collection excludes certain types of sub-works, such as #$Chapter-PCW, which are often, literally, numbered sections, but merely sections in the sense of #$textualPCWSubSections, and not in the sense of \"section\" intended to be represented here.  Also excluded from this collection are sub-works of works explicitly identified as \"parts,\" -- a category typically used to distinguish these sub-works from chapters, sections, appendixes, and the like.")
(comment textualPCWSections "<code>(#$textualPCWSections PCW SECTION)</code> identifies <code>SECTION</code> as a sub-work of the #$TextualPCW <code>PCW</code> that is explicitly identified as a \"section\" (versus a \"chapter\" or \"part\" or other sub-work category) of that work.  See also #$Section-PCW, the collection of all values of <code>SECTION</code>.")
(comment textualPCWSubSections "<code>(#$textualPCWSubSections LARGER-WORK SUB-WORK)</code> relates <code>LARGER-WORK</code>, an instance of #$TextualPCW, to <code>SUB-WORK</code>, a distinct instance of #$TextualPCW that is a sub-work (see #$subWorks) of <code>LARGER-WORK</code> that is recognizably so due to stylistic or structural features that, usually by design, are intended to set it apart as a somewhat self-contained work.  Examples include chapters in books, articles in magazines or journals, and the sections and sub-sections of an article that are typically demarcated with titles or some sort of numbering scheme.<br><br>#$textualPCWSubSections is to be distinguished from its specialization, #$textualPCWSections, which is used relates an instance of #$TextualPCW to a #$textualPCWSubSections that is explicitly identified as a \"section\" (as opposed to some other category, such as a chapter).")
(comment textualPCWSubSectionIDString "<code>(#$textualPCWSubSectionIDString PCW ID-STRING)</code> means that the instance <code>PCW</code> of #$TextualPCW is a #$textualPCWSubSections of some larger work such that <code>PCW</code> has been assigned an ID string </code>ID-STRING</code> that serves to both identify <code>PCW</code> and order it among other, similar sub-sections of the same work.  For example, <code>#$textualPCWSubSectionIDString 16USC-ChapterIA \"IA\")</code> relates Chapter IA of Title 16 of the United States Code to the string \"IA,\" which serves both as a way to identify that chapter and to order it among other chapters of Title 16.")
(comment PulmonaryValve "A specialization of #$SemilunarValve. Each instance of #$PulmonaryValve is a valve at the #$Portal from the right #$VentricleOfHeart into the #$PulmonaryTrunk (which leads to the #$Lungs) which prevents #$Blood from passing back from the pulmonary arteries into the #$Heart.")
(comment PulmonaryValveCusp "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$PulmonaryValveCusp is a cusp of the #$PulmonaryValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment PulmonaryValveCusp-Left "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$PulmonaryValveCusp-Left is a cusp of the #$PulmonaryValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment PulmonaryValveCusp-Right "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$PulmonaryValveCusp-Right is a cusp of the #$PulmonaryValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment PulmonaryValveCusp-Anterior "A specialization of #$CuspOfHeartValve.  Each instance of #$PulmonaryValveCusp-Anterior is an anterior cusp of the #$PulmonaryValve of a #$Heart.")
(comment PulmonaryAutograft "A specilaization of #$HeartValve.  Each instance of #$PulmonaryAutograft a #$PulmonaryValve that has been surgically placed in the position where the patient's own diseased #$AorticValve was removed.")
(comment HeartValve "The collection of all #$Heart #$Valves.  Each instance of this collection is #$Valve at a #$Portal for a #$BloodVessel connected to the #$Heart, or is a #$Valve separating a ventricle (#$VentricleOfHeart) and auricle.  The human #$Heart has a #$MitralValve, #$TricuspidValve, #$AorticValve, #$PulmonaryValve, and a #$CoronaryValve.")
(comment subSectionIndexingStrings "<code>(#$subSectionIndexingStrings CW ID-STRING)</code> means that the string <code>ID-STRING</code> is an indexing string used to reference <code>CW</code>, a sub-work of some conceptual work.")
(comment MildPhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn "A #$UnaryFunction that takes a #$PhysiologicalConditionType to a mild form of that type.  For example (#$MildPhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn #$NasalCongestion) denotes the collection of mild cases of nasal congestion.")
(comment hairCoverage "<code>(#$hairCoverage ANIMAL PART-TYPE ANIMAL-BY-AMOUNT-OF-HAIR-TYPE)</code> means that the <code>ANIMAL-PART-TYPE</code> of <code>ANIMAL</code> has the level of hair coverage indicated by <code>ANIMAL-BY-AMOUNT-OF-HAIR-TYPE</code>.")
(comment MildPhysiologicalCondition "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionTypeByDegreeOfSeverity. Each instance of #$MildPhysiologicalCondition is a mild condition.")
(comment MildToModeratePhysiologicalCondition "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionTypeByDegreeOfSeverity. Each instance of #$MildToModeratePhysiologicalCondition is a mild to moderate condition.")
(comment ModeratePhysiologicalCondition "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionTypeByDegreeOfSeverity. Each instance of #$ModeratePhysiologicalCondition is a moderate condition.")
(comment ModerateToSeverePhysiologicalCondition "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionTypeByDegreeOfSeverity. Each instance of #$ModeratePhysiologicalCondition is a moderate to severe condition.")
(comment SeverePhysiologicalCondition "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionTypeByDegreeOfSeverity. Each instance of #$ModeratePhysiologicalCondition is a severe condition.")
(comment PhysiologicalConditionTypeByDegreeOfSeverity "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalConditionType.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of physiological conditions with a particular degree of severity (e.g., mild, moderate, or severe).  Note that although moderate cancer might be more threatening to general heaalth than a severe cold, it is still (according to the notion of \"severity\" at hand) correct to say of someone with moderate cancer and a severe cold, \"His cold is more severe than his cancer, but of course he's more worried about his cancer because it is <i>cancer</i>, after all.\"  There may be another notion of \"physiological condition type by degree of severity\" in terms of which cancer (no matter how severe), for example, is always more severe than nasal congestion (no matter how severe), but this is not that notion.")
(comment MildToModeratePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn "A #$UnaryFunction that takes a #$PhysiologicalConditionType to a mild-to-moderate form of that type.  For example (#$MildToModeratePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn #$NasalCongestion) denotes the collection of mild to moderate cases of nasal congestion.")
(comment ModeratePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn "A #$UnaryFunction that takes a #$PhysiologicalConditionType to a moderate form of that type.  For example (#$ModeratePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn #$NasalCongestion) denotes the collection of moderate cases of nasal congestion.")
(comment SeverePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn "A #$UnaryFunction that takes a #$PhysiologicalConditionType to a severe form of that type.  For example (#$SeverePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn #$NasalCongestion) denotes the collection of moderate to severe cases of nasal congestion.")
(comment ModerateToSeverePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn "A #$UnaryFunction that takes a #$PhysiologicalConditionType to a moderate to severe form of that type.  For example (#$ModerateToSeverePhysiologicalConditionOfTypeFn #$NasalCongestion) denotes the collection of moderate to severe cases of nasal congestion.")
(comment AtrialFibrillation "A specialization of #$AtrialDisorder.  The condition of atrial fibrillation is characterized by an atrium that beats irregularly and possibly rapidly, as contrasted with #$AtrialFlutter, which is characterized by a heartbeat that is regular and rapid.")
(comment AtrialFlutter "A specialization of #$AtrialDisorder.  The condition of atrial flutter is characterized by an atrium that beats rapidly but regularly, as contrasted with #$AtrialFibrillation, which is characterized by a heartbeat that is irregular and possibly rapid.")
(comment lawOfGeoEntity "<code>(#$lawOfGeoEntity LAW GEO-ENTITY)</code> means that the instance <code>LAW</code> of #$Law is a law generated by and (at least in principle) enforced by <code>GEO-ENTITY</code>, an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment LawsOfGeoEntityFn "<code>(#$LawsOfGeoEntityFn GEO-ENTITY)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$Law that are generated and (at least in principle) enforced by <code>GEO-ENTITY</code>, an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity. This function is to be contrasted with #$LawsInTerritoryFn, which returns the collection of laws that are, roughly speaking, \"in place\" within a geographical area.  Because one geo-entity (say, the state of Arkansas) might be a #$geopoliticalSubdivisions of another (say, the United States), the laws <i>of</i> the smaller entity (in the sense of #$LawsOfGeoEntityFn) might be a proper subset of the laws <i>in</i> its territory (which include the laws of the larger geopolitical entity).  Thus the following relationship holds, though not necessarily the converse: <code>(#$genls (#$LawsOfGeoEntityFn GEO-ENTITY) (#$LawsInTerritoryFn (#$TerritoryFn GEO-ENTITY)))</code>.")
(comment NthUSCongressFn "<code>(#$NthUSCongressFn N)</code> denotes the <code>N</code>th United States Congress, where <code>N</code> corresponds to the number of election-induced congress \"turnovers.\" Thus each application of #$NthUSCongressFn returns a distinct timeslice (see #$properTimeSlices) of the US Congress.")
(comment encodes "<code>(#$encodes STORE-1 STORE-2)</code> means that the instance <code>STORE-1</code> of #$InformationStore encodes (contains a codification of) <code>STORE-2</code>, a distinct instance of #$InformationStore.  Where the substantive content of <code>STORE-1</code> just is that of <code>STORE-2</code>, use the more specific #$codificationOf.")
(comment codificationOf "<code>(#$codificationOf CODIFICATION STORE)</code> means that the instance <code>CODIFICATION</code> of #$InformationStore is a codification of <code>STORE</code>, a distinct instance of #$InformationStore.  To count as a codification, the substantive content of <code>CODIFICATION</code> must be the same as that of <code>STORE</code>, which is to say that although there will (almost certainly) be some information in one that is not in the other, there is an interpretation of the content of <code>STORE</code> that is also an interpretation of the content of <code>CODIFICATION</code>.  To give an example, consider the United States Code (see #$UnitedStatesCode), which is a codification of the body of US public law: although the code contains information (e.g, internal cross-references and references to the law, information about the ordering of sections, titles, and chapters), the substantive content of the law (its legal prescriptions and prohibitions) is identical to the substantive content of the code.   What counts as the \"substantive\" content is a matter of interpretative convention.")
(comment CardiacValveRing "A specialization of #$Implant-Medical.  Each instance of #$CardiacValveRing is a medical implant device designed to be used in cardiac valve repair.")
(comment Valvuloplasty-MedicalProcedure "A specialization of  #$MedicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$Valvuloplasty-MedicalProcedure is a surgical procedure performed to ensure the cusps of heart valves close properly.")
(comment Commissurotomy "A specialization of #$Valvuloplasty-MedicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$Commissurotomy is a surgical procedure performed to ensure the cusps of heart valves close properly, when they had been failing to close due to becoming stif or fusing together.")
(comment temporallyBetween "<code>(#$temporallyBetween TEMP-THING EARLY LATE)</code> means that <code>TEMP-THING</code> starts after the end of<code> EARLY</code> and ends before the start of <code>LATE</code>.  <code>EARLY</code> and <code>LATE</code> are restricted to instances of #$TemporallyExtendedThing.")
(comment QualitativeTimeOfDay "An instance of #$RegularlyRepeatedEventType. Each instance of #$QualitativeTimeOfDay is a celestial event such as a dawn (see #$Dawn), a morning (see #$Morning), an evening (see #$Evening), etc.  On #$PlanetEarth, qualitative times of day are synchronized with the rotation of the earth about its axis, but the absolute timing of qualitative times of day depends upon such factors as the season and the observer's location on the planet's surface.")
(comment PostSurgicalCare "A specialization of #$MedicalCareEvent.  Each instance of #$PostSurgicalCare is an event in which a post-op patient undergoes post-operative medical care.")
(comment PreSurgicalCare "A specialization of #$MedicalCareEvent.  Each instance of #$PreSurgicalCare is an event in which a pre-op patient undergoes pre-operative medical care.")
(comment UnitedStatesCodeSection "The collection of all sections of the United States Code.  Each section of the code corresponds to a law or to a section of a law passed by congress.")
(comment Resolution "A resolution represents a formal description of some policy that should be adopted by the #$Government that accepts it as part of a #$CreatingALegalAgreement.")
(comment LegislativeAct "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork, #$LegislativeAct is the collection of all acts put forth by a legislative body as part of the process of introducing or revising laws.")
(comment ActOfParliament "The collection of all instances of #$LegislativeAct  put forth by an instance of #$Parliament.")
(comment ActOfCongress "The collection of all instances of #$LegislativeAct  put forth by the United States Congress (see #$USCongress).")
(comment NthActOfCongressFn "A partial function from integers to an instance of #$TemporalThing. <code>(#$NthActOfCongressFn CONGRESS-NUM ACT-NUM)</code> denotes the temporal thing <code>ACT</code> such that from its starting date onward, it has the following properties: It is an instance of #$ActOfCongress, it was the creation of the <code>CONGRESS-NUM</code>th United States Congress (see #$NthUSCongressFn), and it was the <code>ACT-NUM</code>th act of that congress.  This function is useful for on-the-fly reification of Congressional acts, as they are enumerated by congressional session number and ordinal -- e.g., \"Pub. Law 104 17\" refers to the 17th law act of the 104th congress, representable with this function-term as <code>(#$NthActOfCongressFn 17 104)</code>.")
(comment Asystole "A specialization of #$HeartCondition.  Each instance of #$Asystole is a condition of having a #$Heart with no cardiac electrical activity, i.e. no contractions of the #$Myocardium and no cardiac output or blood flow.")
(comment HeartBlock "A specialization of #$HeartCondition.  Each instance of #$HeartBlock is blockage at any level of the electrical conduction system of a heart.")
(comment HeartBlock-FirstDegree "A specialization of #$HeartBlock.  Each instance of #$HeartBlock-FirstDegree is a heart block condition with little clinical significance.  Most instances of #$HeartBlock-FirstDegree are instances of #$AVBlock.")
(comment AVBlock "A specialization of #$HeartBlock.  Each instance of #$AVBlock is a heart block that occurs within the atrioventricular node of a #$Heart.")
(comment HeartBlock-SecondDegree "A specialization of #$HeartBlock.  Each instance of #$HeartBlock-SecondDegree is a heart block condition in which one or more (but not all) of the atrial impulses fail to conduct to the ventricles due to impaired conduction. There are two distinct types of second degree AV block: type 1 and type 2.")
(comment EctopicHeartbeat "A specialization of #$CardiacArrhythmia.  Each instance of #$EctopicHeartbeat is an irregularity of heart rate and heart rhythm involving extra or skipped heartbeats.")
(comment synonymousExternalConceptWRTPredicate "<code>(#$synonymousExternalConceptWRTPredicate THING SOURCE PRED STRING)</code> means that when <code>THING</code> stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to any other thing, the string <code>STRING</code> (when it occurs in the data source <code>SOURCE</code>) denotes <code>THING</code>.")
(comment defaultParsingMt "<code>(#$defaultParsingMt SPECIFICATION MT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, MT is the appropriate #$Microtheory to use when performing natural language generation.")
(comment ForestServiceHandbook "The collection of all Forest Service handbooks, each instance of which forms a part of the Forest Service Directive System, the codification of all the policies and procedures of the U.S. Forest Service.")
(comment TheForestServiceDirectiveSystem "An instance of #$CompiledConceptualWork, the Forest Service Directive System is the codification of the policies and procedures of the USDA Forest Service (see #$UnitedStatesForestService) and consists of the Forest Service Manual (see #$ForestServiceManual) and the Forest Service Handbooks (see #$ForestServiceHandbook).")
(comment ForestServiceManual "The Forest Service Manual, a major component of the Forest Service Directive System.")
(comment nonFunctionalExternalSynonomy "<code>(#$nonFunctionalExternalSynonomy ASSERT)</code> means that the synonymous external concept assertion declared by <code>ASSERT</code> is non-functional, in the sense that there is an additional valid synonymous external concept assertion, <code>ASSERT2</code>, such that both <code>ASSERT</code> and <code>ASSERT2</code> map the same things to different external concepts in a single external knowledge source.")
(comment ContentOfFileFn "(#$ContentOfFileFn FILE-PATH) returns the string that is the content of the text file specified by FILE-PATH.  Note that FILE-PATH can be a relative or an absolute pathname.")
(comment conceptFilterDecisionTree "(#$conceptFilterDecisionTree FILTER DECISION-TREE-STRING) relates a particular #$DecisionTreeConceptFilter to the string representation of the corresponding decision-tree that is being used the concept filter.")
(comment ConceptFilterFromDecisionTreeFn "(#$ConceptFilterFromDecisionTreeFn DECISION-TREE-STRING) returns the #$DecisionTreeConceptFilter defined by DECISION-TREE-STRING, i.e. the string representation of the corresponding decision tree.")
(disjointWith AcquiredHeartDisease CongenitalHeartDisease)
(comment PericardialCyst "A specialization of #$Cyst.  Each instance of #$PericardialCyst is a cyst of the #$Pericardium.")
(comment ChronicLungDisease "A specialization of #$LungDisease and #$ChronicCondition.  Each instance of #$ChronicLungDisease is a chronic ailment condition that affects some #$Lung.")
(comment IntracoronaryInjectionOfThrombolyticAgent "Intracornoary refers to the use of a catheter to inject a thrombolytic agent into the heart.")
(comment ThrombolyticAgent "A drug that is able to dissolve a clot (thrombus) and reopen an artery or vein. ")
(comment principalInvestigator "An instance of #$ActorSlot, <code>(#$principalInvestigator PROJECT AGENT)</code> means that there is some period of time, subsumed by the project <code>PROJECT</code> during which <code>AGENT</code> is the principle investigator of <code>PROJECT</code>.")
(disjointWith InformalAgreement TextualPCW)
(disjointWith ChallengeCostShareAgreement LoanAgreement)
(disjointWith Entitlement Proposal)
(disjointWith Prohibition Proposal)
(comment cocSpecifications "The most general predicate used to relate a code of conduct (see #$CodeOfConduct), such as a law (#$Law) or religious norm (#$ReligiousNorm), to the prohibitions (#$Prohibition), entitlements (#$Entitlement), and obligations (#$Obligation) it contains, and without which it would not count as a code of conduct in any meaningful sense.  This predicate, which is constrained in its arg2 to take any instance of #$NormativeSpecification, is more tightly constrained by virtue of being the union  (see #$predicateUnion) of #$cocProhibitions, #$cocEntitlements, and #$cocObligations, which relate a code of conduct to its prohibitions, entitlements, and obligations, respectively.")
(comment cocEntitlements "<code>(#$cocEntitlements COC ENTITLEMENT)</code> means that <code>ENTITLEMENT</code> is one of the entitlements contained in <code>COC</code>, an instance of #$CodeOfConduct.")
(comment cocProhibitions "<code>(#$cocProhibitions COC PROHIBITION)</code> means that <code>PROHIBITION</code> is one of the prohibitions contained in <code>COC</code>, an instance of #$CodeOfConduct.")
(comment cocObligations "<code>(#$cocObligations COC OBLIGATION)</code> means that <code>OBLIGATION</code> is one of the obligations contained in <code>COC</code>, an instance of #$CodeOfConduct.")
(comment CodeOfConduct "A specialization of #$NormativeSpecification and #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$CodeOfConduct is specification of obligations, entitlements, or prohibitions of agents.")
(comment ChallengeCostShareProgramProject "The collection of all instances of #$Project that are authorized via an instance of #$ChallengeCostShareAgreement.")
(comment entitledAgents "<code>(#$entitledAgents ENTITLEMENT AGENT)</code> identifies <code>ENTITLEMENT</code> as one of the entitlements, or rights, of the intelligent agent <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment restrictedAgents "<code>(#$restrictedAgents PROHIBITION AGENT)</code> identifies <code>PROHIBITION</code> as one of the restrictions on the entitlements of the intelligent agent <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment Prohibition "The collection of all prohibitions, or restrictions on the entitlements (see #$Entitlement) of agents.")
(comment derivedObligation "<code>(#$derivedObligations SPEC OBLIG)</code> means that the instance of #$Obligation <code>OBLIG</code> is motivated by, gets its normative force from, or has as its purpose the satisfaction of the #$NormativeSpecification <code>SPEC</code>, typically an instance of #$Agreement or #$CodeOfConduct.  This is a distinct relation from #$normativeSpecificationParts which would express a partonomic relation between the content of <code>SPEC</code> and the content of <code>OBLIG</code>.")
(comment derivedEntitlements "<code>(#$derivedObligations SPEC RIGHT)</code> means that the instance of #$Entitlement <code>RIGHT</code> is motivated by, gets its normative force from, or has as its purpose the satisfaction of the #$NormativeSpecification <code>SPEC</code>, typically an instance of #$Agreement or #$CodeOfConduct.  This is a distinct relation from #$normativeSpecificationParts which would express a partonomic relation between the content of <code>SPEC</code> and the content of <code>RIGHT</code>.")
(comment derivedProhibitions "<code>(#$derivedProhibitions SPEC PROHIBITION)</code> means that the instance of #$Prohibition <code>PROHIBITION</code> is motivated by, gets its normative force from, or has as its purpose the satisfaction of the #$NormativeSpecification <code>SPEC</code>, typically an instance of #$Agreement or #$CodeOfConduct.  This is a distinct relation from #$normativeSpecificationParts which would express a partonomic relation between the content of <code>SPEC</code> and the content of <code>PROHIBITION</code>.")
(comment entitlementSitType "<code>(#$entitlementSitType RIGHT TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>RIGHT</code> of #$Entitlement is an entitlement of its #$entitledAgents to play a role or roles (specifiable via #$entitlementRoles) in situations of type <code>TYPE</code>.")
(disjointWith ChallengeCostShareAgreement InternationalAgreement)
(comment ChallengeCostShareAgreement "The collection of all instances of #$WrittenLegalAgreement that authorize a government agency such as the #$NationalParkService and the #$UnitedStatesForestService to partner with a non-federal cooperator in an instance of #$ChallengeCostShareProgramProject.")
(comment federalIdentifierNumber "<code>(#$federalIdentifierNumber DOC STRING)</code> identifies the instance <code>DOC</code> of #$Document as the document with the Federal Identifier Number <code>STRING</code>, a string (and typically not a number-string) used by the US Federal Government for tracking.")
(comment agreementAuthorization "<code>(#$agreementAuthorization AGREEMENT AUTHORITY)</code> means that the #$agreeingAgents in the instance <code>AGREEMENT</code> of #$Agreement are authorized to enter into <code>AGREEMENT</code> by <code>AUTHORITY</code>, an instance of #$InformationStore, typically a code of conduct such as an instance of #$Law or a set of policies.  Hence <code>(#$agreementAuthorization AGREEMENT AUTHORITY)</code> entails that <code>(#$authorizationFor AUTHORITY ACTION)</code>, where <code>ACTION</code> is the instance of #$MakingAnAgreement that produced <code>AGREEMENT</code>.   Note that not all agreements will have this property.")
(comment CollectionAgreement "A specialization of #$EconomicAgreement.  Instances are agreements authorizing one party to collect monies or objects of value from another.")
(comment CooperativeAgreement "A specialization of #$EconomicAgreement.  Instances are agreements authorizing a government agency to direct monies or objects of value to an entity (who is not a member or sub-organization of the aforementioned government)--a \"cooperator\"--in order to stimulate work beneficial to the public.")
(comment CooperativeFireProtectionAgreement "A specialization of #$EconomicAgreement.  Instances are agreements authorizing a government agency to direct monies or objects of value to an entity (who is not a member or sub-organization of the aforementioned government)--a \"cooperator\"--in order to stimulate work beneficial to the public.")
(comment Anticoagulant "A specialization of #$DrugProduct.  Each instance of #$Anticoagulant is a portion of a drug that, when taken in a recommended dosage, can prevent or reduce the clotting of blood.")
(comment SickleCellAnemia "A specilaization of #$SickleCellDisease and #$Anemia.  Each instance of #$SickleCellAnemia is a type of anemia characterized by misshappen red blood cells.")
(comment CongenitalHeartProcedure-Surgical "The collection of surgical procedures that are performed to correct congenital defects or problems.")
(comment Catheter "A flexible tube designed for insertion into body cavities or vessels for the purpose of allowing the passage of fluids between the body and outside sources.")
(comment termPhrases "(#$termPhrases TERM CONSTRAINT STRING) means that STRING is a word or
phrase that denotes TERM and that meets CONSTRAINT. CONSTRAINT is an
instance of #$TermPhrasesConstraint (q.v.).  For example, CONSTRAINT
may be an instance of #$SpeechPartPredicate (such as #$singular or
#$gerund); an instance of #$SpeechPart (such as #$Noun or
#$Verb); or an instance of #$StringIndexingSlot (such as
#$nameString).  If CONSTRAINT is a predicate, assertions on its
spec-preds will also be searched: thus, the query (#$termPhrases TERM
#$nameString ?STRING) will also return strings asserted of TERM using
#$preferredNameString.  Similarly, if CONSTRAINT is a collection,
assertions related to its specializations will be searched: thus, the
query (#$termPhrases TERM #$ProperNoun ?STRING) will return
#$ProperCountNouns and #$ProperMassNouns that refer to TERM.  If
CONSTRAINT is #$ProperNameString, assertions on predicates whose
arg2Isa #$ProperNameString will be searched.  If CONSTRAINT is
#$CharacterString, no constraints will be imposed, and all lexifications
of TERM are returned.")
(comment LexiconSliceMicrotheory "A #$LexiconSliceMicrotheory is a kind of #$LexicalDataMicrotheory that includes only selected content from a particular lexicon or set of lexicons.")
(comment AbandoningAVesselsCrew "The collection of all criminal actions in which the crew of a hijacked vessel is forcibly removed from the vessel and left somewhere by the pirates who are #$perpetrators of the #$Hijacking (cf. (#$HijackingAFn #$Watercraft).  Cases where the crew is 'marooned' on some land mass as well as cases where they are set adrift on a #$Raft or some other conveyance are included.")
(comment RestoringAnObject "A specialization of #$ImprovementEvent.  This is the collection of events in which the #$objectImproved begins the process in a degraded state--i.e., it had previously been in a useful or otherwise \"good\" state--and is improved by having much or all of its positive or useful qualities restored.")
(comment RestoringAnEcologicalRegion "A specialization of #$RestoringAnObject.  Instances of this collection restore damaged instances of #$EcologicalRegion, such as polluted rivers or lands damaged by tornadoes.")
(comment MineRehabilitation "Mine rehabilitation, or mine reclamation is the process of rehabilitating lands that have been damaged by instances of #$Mining.")
(comment NationalForest "The collection of all instances of #$Forest whose use is regulated by an agency of an instance of #$IndependentCountry.")
(comment planHypotheticalInstanceOfType "<code>(#$planHypotheticalInstanceOfType SPEC INS TYPE)</code> means that <code>INS</code> is a hypothesized instance of <code>TYPE</code> generated for reasoning about the consequences of carrying out <code>SPEC</code>, an instance of #$GoalOrientedSpecification.")
(comment planHypotheticals "<code>(#$planHypotheticals SPEC THING)</code> means that <code>THING</code> is a hypothesized object generated for reasoning about the consequences of carrying out <code>SPEC</code>, an instance of #$GoalOrientedSpecification.")
(comment SubEventRoleFn "A function from predicates to predicates, <code>(#$SubEventRoleFn ROLE)</code> denotes the instance of #$BinarySituationPredicate that holds of its arguments <code>ARG1</code> and <code>ARG2</code> just in case there is a sub-event <code>SUB</code> (see #$subEvents) of <code>ARG1</code> such that <code>(ROLE SUB ARG2)</code>. As such <code>(#$SubEventRoleFn ROLE)</code> denotes a generalization of <code>ROLE</code> (see #$genlPreds).")
(comment LandRehabilitation "A specialization of #$RestoringAnEcologicalRegion, where the region restored is also an instance of #$LandTopographicalFeature. This is not to be confused with land reclamation in the sense of creating an area of land where one had not existed before.")
(comment NationalForestsInFn "<code>(#$NationalForestsInFn ENTITY)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$NationalForest that spatially intersect (see #$spatiallyIntersects) with the territory of <code>ENTITY</code>, an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  Where <code>ENTITY</code> is an instance of #$IndependentCountry, the forests will be spatially subsumed (see #$spatiallySubsumes) by <code>ENTITY</code>.")
(comment nationalForestsIn "<code>(#$nationalForestsIn FOREST-TYPE ENTITY)</code> identifies <code>FOREST-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$NationalForest that are in--entirely or partly--the territory of <code>ENTITY</code>, an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment GoalOrientedSpecification "The collection of instances of #$NormativeSpecification that describe a goal to be achieved.  In many cases (as in instances of #$Plan), steps for achieving that goal are also described.")
(comment areaHazards "<code>(#$areaHazards AREA DANGER)</code> identifies <code>DANGER</code> as one of the instances of #$DangerousTangibleThing found in the geographical region <code>AREA</code> that negatively impact the general level of safety for agents in <code>AREA</code>.")
(comment regionLevelOfSafeness "<code>(#$regionLevelOfSafeness REGION SAFENESS)</code> identifies the level of safeness of any arbitrarily selected instance of #$Action taken in <code>REGION</code>, an instance of #$GeographicalRegion.  As such #$regionLevelOfSafeness is defined in terms of #$levelOfSafeness, which relates actions to instances of #$Safeness.")
(comment proposalAddressesProblem-Prop "A binary predicate used to describe instances of #$GoalOrientedSpecification. <code>(#$proposalAddressesProblem-Prop SPEC SENTENCE)</code> means that the specification <code>SPEC</code> has among its goals some state of affairs that either renders false or lessons the impact from the fact that <code>SENTENCE</code> is true.")
(comment HypothesizedPlanInstantiationMtFn "<code>(#$HypothesizedPlanInstantiationMtFn PLAN)</code> denotes the instance of #$HypotheticalContext that describes the hypothetical instantiation of the actions described in <code>PLAN</code>, an instance of #$GoalOrientedSpecification.")
(comment planInstantiationHypothesisMt "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$HypothesizedPlanInstantiationMtFn , <code>(#$planInstantiationHypothesisMt PLAN MT)</code> identifies <code>MT</code> as the instance of #$HypotheticalContext that describes the hypothetical instantiation of the actions described in <code>PLAN</code>, an instance of #$GoalOrientedSpecification.")
(comment ReservingPassageOnAVessel "The act of reserving passage on a #$Watercraft.")
(comment Hematoma "A lump or swelling in some tissue or organ in the body filled with blood.")
(comment specificationBenefitsAgent "<code>(#$specificationBenefitsAgent SPEC AGENT)</code> identifies <code>AGENT</code> as an instance of #$Agent-Generic who benefits/would benefit from the terms set forth in the instance <code>SPEC</code> of #$NormativeSpecification. <code>SPEC</code> will typically be an instance of #$GoalOrientedSpecification, such as a plan or proposal, or an instance of #$Agreement; in either case, situation-types are described in <code>SPEC</code> that, were they instantiated, some benefit befalls <code>AGENT</code> as a consequence of the terms of <code>SPEC</code>.  <code>AGENT</code> need not be explicitly mentioned in or even aware of <code>SPEC</code> in order to benefit (as that benefit might occur as an unintended consequence).  However, typically, when agents craft specifications such as plans or agreements, they attempt to ensure that #$specificationBenefitsAgent holds of the specification and themselves.")
(disjointWith RDFTripleStore-Physical HumanAccessibleIBO)
(comment RDFTripleStore-Physical "A specialization of both #$InformationBearingObject and #$StructuredKnowledgeSource.  Each instance of #$RDFTripleStore-Physical is an IBO (either hardcopy or electronic) that stores RDF triples.")
(comment hostDBNameForSKS "This predicate relates a structured knowlege source to the name of hosting database.  If the structured knowledge source just is the database, then use the more specific #$structuredKnowledgeSourceName.")
(comment structuredKnowledgeSourceUsesService "(#$$structuredKnowledgeSourceUsesService SKS SERVICE-PROGRAM) means that the API to SERVICE-PROGRAM is how SKS is accessed.")
(comment baseNamespaceForSKS "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate, used to identify a structured knowledge source with a base URI.")
(comment CardiacFlutter "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$CardiacFlutter is a condition afflicting a region of the heart in which that region beats regularly and rapidly.  Contrast this collection with the similar #$CardiacFibrillation, which is characterized by a heartbeat that is irregular and possibly rapid.")
(comment CardiacFibrillation "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$CardiacFibrillation is a condition afflicting a region of the heart in which that region beats irregularly and possibly rapidly.  Contrast this collection with the similar #$CardiacFlutter, which is characterized by a heartbeat that is regular and rapid.")
(comment formulaTemplateGloss-Alternate "(#$formulaTemplateGloss-Alternate TEMPLATE STRING) means that STRING is an alternate gloss for TEMPLATE. To specify the primary gloss for a template, use #$formulaTemplateGloss.")
(comment OrganismPart "A specialization of both #$PhysicalPartOfObject and #$BiologicalLivingObject. Each instance of #$OrganismPart is a part of an organism.  It may be an anatomical part or a pathological part such as a tumor.  This collection includes the gross anatomical parts and microscopic anatomical parts of every individual of every species.")
(comment situationTypeAffectsOrganismPartType "(#$situationTypeAffectsOrganismPartType EVTTYPE PARTTYPE) says that instances of EVTTYPE generally affect instances of PARTTYPE.  For example, (#$situationTypeAffectsOrganismPartType #$HairCuttingEvent #$MobOfHair-Mammal) says that haircutting events affect the hair.")
(comment USDAFSCanEnterIntoAgreementsToDoCooperativePollutionAbatement "The legal right of the US Secretary of Agriculture to enter into cooperative agreements on behalf of the US Forest Service, quoting 16 USC 565a-1, \"to construct, operate, and maintain cooperative pollution abatement equipment and facilities.\"")
(comment agreementBasedOnProposal "<code>(#$agreementBasedOnProposal AGREEMENT PROPOSAL)</code> identifies <code>PROPOSAL</code> as the instance of #$GoalOrientedSpecification on which the instance <code>AGREEMENT</code> of #$Agreement is based.  In particular, the terms of <code>PROPOSAL</code> are essentially those of <code>AGREEMENT</code>, and the instance of #$MakingAnAgreement which spawned <code>AGREEMENT</code> (see #$agreementCreated) just is the event of the relevant parties deciding to agree on the terms of <code>PROPOSAL</code>.")
(comment USDAFSCanEnterIntoAgreementsToDoForestryProtection "The legal right of the US Secretary of Agriculture to enter into cooperative agreements on behalf of the US Forest Service, quoting 16 USC 565a-1, \"to perform forestry protection, including fire protection, timber stand improvement, debris removal, and thinning of trees.\"")
(comment entitlementRolePlayerConstraints "A predicate used to encode constraints on a class of situations licensed by an instance of #$Entitlement. <code>(#$entitlementRolePlayerConstraints ENTITLEMENT ROLE PRED THING)</code> means that if <code>ENTITLEMENT</code> is an entitlement that licenses the bringing about of some situation <code>SIT</code>, anything that plays the role <code>ROLE</code> in <code>SIT</code> will bear the relationship <code>PRED</code> to <code>THING</code>.  Otherwise, <code>SIT</code> is not licensed by <code>ENTITLEMENT</code>.")
(comment ReplacementSurgicalProcedure "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ReplacementSurgicalProcedure is a specific procedure in which part of a body is replaced.  An instance of this collection could be a transplant procedure, or it could involve replacement of a body part with an artificial substitute.")
(comment CandidaTropicalis "A species of #$Candida.")
(comment CandidaZeylanoides "A species of #$Candida.")
(comment CandidaAlbicans "A species of #$Candida.")
(comment CandidaKrusei "A species of #$Candida.")
(comment MycobacteriumLeprae "A subset of #$Bacterium, #$MycobacteriumLeprae is the collection of bacteria that can cause #$Leprosy.")
(comment InfectionTypeByPathogenType "A collection of Collection. Elements of #$InfectionTypeByPathogenType are specs of #$Infection of which instances share the common property of being caused by pathogenic organisms of the same type. See #$pathogenCausesConditionType, #$InfectionDueToFn.")
(comment pathogenTypeCausesInfectionType "(#$pathogenTypeCausesInfectionType PATHOGENTYPE INFECTIONTYPE) means that under ordinary circumstances, instances of PATHOGENTYPE are capable of causing an #$InfectionType  of the type INFECTIONTYPE in a host organism.")
(comment LeftCoronaryArtery-MainTrunk "A specialization of #$CoronaryArtery.  The left main trunk is the portion of the left coronary artery that branches from the #$Aorta and branches into the left anterior descending coronary artery and the  left circumflex cornoary artery.")
(comment typeCommonColors "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate.  <code>(#$typeCommonColors TYPE COLOR)</code> means that the instance <code>COLOR</code> of #$Color is a common color for instances of the collection <code>TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$SpatialThing-Localized.  For example, <code>(#$typeCommonColors #$FireTruck #$RedColor)</code> and <code>(#$typeCommonColors #$FireTruck #$YellowColor)</code> are both true, as fire trucks typically come in red or yellow.")
(comment proposalMeetsSomeAuthorizationConditions "A predicate that relates instances of #$GoalOrientedSpecification to instances of #$CodeOfConduct that, at least on some level of analysis, are potential sources of authorization for that specification. <code>(#$proposalMeetsSomeAuthorizationConditions PROPOSAL COC)</code> means that the specification <code>PROPOSAL</code> meets at least one necessary condition for being authorized by the code of conduct <code>COC</code>.  This is consistent with <code>PROPOSAL</code> violating some other condition imposed by <code>COC</code>, ruling it out as an authority.")
(comment proposalViolatesSomeAuthorizationConditions "<code>(#$proposalViolatesSomeAuthorizationConditions PROPOSAL COC)</code> means that the specification <code>PROPOSAL</code> violates at least one necessary condition for being authorized by the code of conduct <code>COC</code>.")
(comment agreementAuthorizationCondition "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate, <code>(#$agreementAuthorizationCondition AUTHORITY PRED THING)</code> means that any instance <code>INS</code> of #$Agreement authorized by <code>AUTHORITY</code> is such that <code>(PRED INS THING)</code>.")
(comment isolatedSurgicalProcedureOfType "<code>(#$isolatedSurgicalProcedureOfType PRO PRO-TYPE)</code> means that the #$SurgicalProcedure <code>PRO</code> is an instance of <code>PRO-TYPE</code> and that the #$Surgery during which <code>PRO</code> is performed is not known to involve any notable surgical procedures other than <code>PRO</code>.")
(comment Pre-opDiagnosisType "A collection of all the different types of values allowed by #$pre-opDiagnosis .")
(comment Lollipop "A specialization of #$Candy.  Each instance of #$Lollipop is a small candy attached to the end of a short stick.")
(comment Gumdrop "A specialization of #$Candy.  Each instance of #$Gumdrop is a small chewy candy that is shaped like a truncated cone and coated in granulated sugar.")
(comment NaturalResourceManagement "The collection of events in which the natural resources of some region are maintained and their use allocated in a way that supports maintainence.")
(comment UtahDivisionOfOilGasAndMining "the State of Utah, Department of Natural Resources, Division of Oil, Gas and Mining")
(comment UtahAbandonedMineReclamationProgram "The State of Utah's abandoned mine reclamation program")
(comment Program "A specialization of #$Project.  Instances are projects whose purpose is to launch and support projects with a common goal.")
(comment projectTypeGoalState "The predicate that coresponds to the function #$ProjectTypeByGoalState.  <code>(#$projectTypeGoalState PROJECT-TYPE SITUATION-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>PROJECT-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$Project whose goal is to bring about an instance of <code>SITUATION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ProjectTypeByGoalStateFn "<code>(#$ProjectTypeByGoalStateFn SITUATION-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$Project whose goal is to bring about an instance of <code>SITUATION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment programTypeFocalProjectType "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$ProgramTypeByFocalProjectTypeFn.  <code>(#$programTypeFocalProjectType PROGRAM-TYPE PROJECT-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>PROGRAM-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$Program whose purpose it is to spawn and support projects of type <code>PROJECT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ProgramTypeByFocalProjectType "A collection of specializations of #$Program.  Each instances is such that the purpose of each of its instances is to bring about a common type of #$Project.")
(comment ProgramTypeByFocalProjectTypeFn "<code>(#$ProgramTypeByFocalProjectTypeFn PROJECT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$Program whose goal is to bring about an support (typically many) instance(s) of <code>PROJECT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment agreementGrantor "A highly technical specialization of #$agreeingAgents.  The 'grantor' of an agreement is a government entity who has specific authorization from statuatory law to play the role of #$agreeingAgents in an agreement.")
(comment agreementCollaborators "A highly technical specialization of #$agreeingAgents.  The 'collaborator' of an agreement is a agent who has agreed to work with the #$agreementGrantor of that agreement to achieve a common goal.")
(comment proposedAgreementSlotForAgent "<code>(#$proposedAgreementSlotForAgent PROPOSAL SLOT AGENT)</code> means that if <code>AGREEMENT</code> is the instance of #$Agreement that results from the instance <code>PROPOSAL</code> of #$Proposal, then <code>AGENT</code> will stand in the <code>SLOT</code> relation to <code>AGREEMENT</code>.")
(comment DepartmentOfNaturalResources "An instance of #$DepartmentTypeByFunction.  Instances are departments focused on #$NaturalResourceManagement.")
(comment orgDivisions "A specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of #$subordinateOrganizations.  #$orgDivisions relates an organization to its divisions.")
(comment UtahDepartmentOfNaturalResources "the State of Utah Department of Natural Resources.")
(comment purposeOf-EventSitType "<code>(#$purposeOf-EventSitType EVENT SITUATION-TYPE)</code> means that the purpose of performing the event <code>EVENT</code> is/was/will be to bring about an instance of a situation of type <code>SITUATION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ProjectTypeByGoalState "A collection that facets (see #$facets-Generic) the collection #$Project into subcollections.  Each instance is a class of projects, every instance <code>INS</code> of which share a common situation type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that <code>(#$purposeOf-EventSitType INS SIT-TYPE)</code>.")
(comment AgreementAgentSlot "The class of binary predicates that relate an instance of #$Agreement in the arg1 position to an instance of #$IntelligentAgent in the arg2, where the relation denotes some role that the agent has with respect to the agreement.  Instances include #$signatories and #$agreeingAgents.")
(comment planHypotheticalAgreement "<code>(#$planHypotheticalAgreement PROPOSAL THING)</code> means that <code>THING</code> is hypothesized to be the agreement based on the proposal <code>PROPOSAL</code> in the #$planInstantiationHypothesisMt for <code>PROPOSAL</code>.  Note that the CycL term that represents <code>THING</code> is an instance of #$IndeterminateTerm; <code>THING</code> is not assumed to be a real instance of #$Agreement outside of the hypothetical context where it is defined as such.")
(comment HypotheticalAgreementFromPlanFn "CycL terms of the form <code>(#$HypotheticalAgreementFromPlanFn PROPOSAL)</code> are instances of #$IndeterminateTerm that are hypothesized to be instances of #$Agreement such that the #$agreementBasedOnProposal stands between them and <code>PROPOSAL</code>, an instance of #$Proposal.  The referents of such terms are not assumed to be agreements anywhere outside of the #$planInstantiationHypothesisMt for the proposal.")
(comment isolatedIndividualTypeOfType "<code>(isolatedIndividualTypeOfType TYPE ISO-TYPE)</code> means that <code>ISO-TYPE</code> is the collection of isolated instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment agreementAuthorizationIsaCondition "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate, <code>(#$agreementAuthorizationIsaCondition AUTHORITY PRED COLL)</code> means that any instance <code>INS</code> of #$Agreement authorized by <code>AUTHORITY</code> and any thing <code>THING</code> such that <code>(PRED INS THING)</code>, <code>(#$isa THING COLL)</code> must hold.  Otherwise, <code>AUTHORITY</code> cannot authorize <code>INS</code>.")
(disjointWith GovernmentOfCountry USStateGovernmentOrganization)
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure ClinicalExam-HistoryAndPhysical)
(disjointWith CoronaryArteryGraftDistalAnastomosis Organism-Whole)
(disjointWith CoronaryArteryGraftSegment Organism-Whole)
(disjointWith MedicalPatient (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet CoronaryArteryGraftDistalAnastomosis CoronaryArteryGraftSegment)))
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure CardiacCatheterization-Diagnostic)
(comment DiabetesMellitus "A specialization of #$LifeThreateningCondition.   Diabetes melitus isa a metabolic disorder characterized by high blood sugar.  There are three major types of diabetes mellitus: type 1, or \"juvenile\" diabetes (see #$DiabetesMellitus-Type1), type 2, or \"adult onset\" diabetes (see #$DiabetesMellitus-Type2), and gestational diabetes (see #$GestationalDiabetes).")
(comment DiabetesMellitus-Type1 "A specialization of #$DiabetesMellitus, also known as \"juvenile diabetes\".")
(comment DiabetesMellitus-Type2 "A specialization of #$DiabetesMellitus, also known as \"adult onset diabetes\".")
(comment GestationalDiabetes "A specialization of #$DiabetesMellitus which may be acquired during and as a consequence of pregnacy.")
(comment USCanLendEmployeesToForeignGovernments "The legal right of the Director of the US Information Agency to assign government employees with the requisite expertise or skills to do work on behalf of a requesting foreign government.")
(comment FishlakeNationalForest "Fishlake National Forest, located in Utah.")
(comment managesRegion "#$managesRegion relates an instance of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization, typically a sub-organization of a #$RegulatoryAgency, to an instance of #$EcologicalRegion that the sub-organization manages.")
(comment managesRegion-Directly "A specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$managesRegion, <code>(#$managesRegion-Directly ORG REGION)</code> identifies <code>ORG</code> as the instance of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization that is directly in charge of managing the ecological region <code>REGION</code>.  <code>ORG</code> might be one of many organizations for which #$managesRegion holds wrt <code>REGION</code>, but it is the sole organization directly responsible for <code>REGION</code>. For example, the Federal Government manages each national forest, which it does indirectly through the National Forest Service, which manages each forest indirectly, by having a dedicated sub-organization for each forest; these sub-organizations manage their respective forests directly.")
(comment FillmoreRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Fishlake National Forest in Utah. (See #$FishlakeNationalForest.)")
(comment BeaverRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Fishlake National Forest in Utah. (See #$FishlakeNationalForest.)")
(comment RichfieldRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Fishlake National Forest in Utah. (See #$FishlakeNationalForest.)")
(comment ManagingOrgOfRegionFn "<code>(#$ManagingOrgOfRegionFn REGION)</code> identifies the government organization directly responsible (see #$managesRegion-Directly) for the management of the instance <code>REGION</code> of #$EcologicalRegion.")
(comment Dilatation-PhysiologicalCondition "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Dilatation-PhysiologicalCondition is a condition involving the dilatation of a body part of the affected organism.")
(comment CardiacValveDilatation "A specialization of #$Dilatation-PhysiologicalCondition.  Each instance of #$CardiacValveDilatation is a condition involving a dilated #$HeartValve.")
(comment agentCommonEnablingAuthorities "This predicate relates an intelligent agent to the legal authorities (see #$LegalCOC) that the agent typically uses to legally justify many of its actions (in particular, those actions that require legal justification).")
(comment timeIntervalInclusive "This predicate relates two instances of #$TemporalThing to the (longest) instance of #$TimeInterval between, and including, them.  <code>(#$timeIntervalInclusive INTERVAL EARLIER LATER)</code> means that <code>INTERVAL</code> is the time interval that starts when <code>EARLIER</code> begins and ends when <code>LATER</code> ends.  <code>LATER</code> must begin after <code>EARLIER</code> begins.")
(disjointWith Operation LocomotionEvent)
(disjointWith Operation (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(disjointWith Operation PreparingFoodOrDrink)
(disjointWith Operation MakingAPlan)
(comment SurgicalProcedure "A specialization of #$Surgery (q.v.).  #$SurgicalProcedure is the collection of all surgical procedures.  Generally, a surgical procedure is a subevent of a surgery event.  A surgery may have many surgical procedures as immediate subevents and surgical procedures themselves may have surgical procedures as subevents.")
(comment Operation "A specialization of #$MedicalCareEvent.  Each instance of #$Operation is a medical care event in which a medical professional cuts a part of a living body, either to examine what's inside (a diagnostic, exploratory surgery) or to treat an ailment (an instance of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent).  Generally, an operation will have one or more proper sub-events that is an instance of #$Surgery (or, specifically, #$SurgicalProcedure (q.v.)).")
(disjointWith MedicalProcedure-NonSurgical Surgery)
(comment MedicalProcedure-NonSurgical "A specialization of #$MedicalCareEvent.  #$MedicalProcedure-NonSurgical is the collection of all medical procedures that are not surgical in nature.")
(comment collectionAndSpecsInConceptFilter "(#$collectionAndSpecsInConceptFilter COLLECTION FILTER) means that COLLECTION and all its specs are included in FILTER.")
(comment FederalHighwayAdministration "The Federal Highway Administration, the division of the US Department of Transportation responsible for the federal highway system.")
(comment HighwayDevelopmentAndMaintenanceActionType "A collection of collections.  Instances are types of purposeful actions that involve or support the development, improvement, or maintenance of highways.")
(comment USDACanHelpStatesHelpStateOrPrivateForestersManageTheirForests "The legal right of the Department of Agriculture to enter into agreements with state agencies to help them help private or public (but non-federal) foresters protect and manage their forests.")
(disjointWith NationalForest (CollectionDifferenceFn Forest NationalForest))
(disjointWith (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn Forest geographicalSubRegions (TerritoryFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica)) (CollectionDifferenceFn Forest (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn Forest geographicalSubRegions (TerritoryFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica))))
(comment proposalVersionOfRole "<code>(#$proposalVersionOfRole COERCED-ROLE ROLE)</code> identifies <code>COERCED-ROLE</code> as the predicate such that <code>(COERCED-ROLE PLAN THING)</code> if and only if the instance <code>PLAN</code> of #$GoalOrientedSpecification specifies that <code>THING</code> play the role <code>ROLE</code> in the planned instantiation of the #$eventTypePlanned in <code>PLAN</code>.")
(comment ProposedRolePlayerFn "<code>(#$ProposedRolePlayerFn ROLE)</code> denotes the instance <code>PRED</code> of #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate such that <code>(PRED PLAN THING)</code> holds just in case the instance <code>PLAN</code> of #$GoalOrientedSpecification specifies that <code>THING</code> is to play <code>ROLE</code> in the instantiation of <code>PLAN</code>'s #$eventTypePlanned.")
(comment ecoRegionBenefited "A specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$beneficiary-Generic, <code>(#$ecoRegionBenefited ACTION REGION)</code> means that the instance <code>ACTION</code> of #$Action benefited the instance <code>REGION</code> of <code>#$EcologicalRegion</code>.")
(disjointWith LegalGovernmentOrganization-NonUS USStateGovernmentOrganization)
(disjointWith LegalGovernmentOrganization-NonUS USFederalGovernmentOrganization)
(disjointWith (NationalForestsInFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica) (CollectionDifferenceFn Forest (NationalForestsInFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica)))
(comment instancesMutuallyInconsistentWRTPred "<code>(#$instancesMutuallyInconsistentWRTPred TYPE PRED)</code> means that for any two distinct instances of <code>TYPE</code> <code>INS-1</code> and <code>INS-2</code>, <code>(PRED INS-1 THING)</code> entails <code>(#$not (PRED INS-2 THING))</code>.")
(comment ForestServiceOrganizationConceptFilter "A #$ConceptFilter designed to identify the #$UnitedStatesForestService and its suborganizations.")
(comment ForestServiceGrantProposalConceptFilter "The collection of all concept filters designed to identify targets of concept extraction in the context of grant proposals for the #$UnitedStatesForestService.")
(comment CommonForestProblem "The collection of all common problems with managed forests, i.e. things that forest managers worry about.")
(comment VentilationShaft "The collection of all more-or-less vertical passages through which harmful gases can ventilate out of (or outside air into) a relatively enclosed space.")
(comment temporallyBetween-Inclusive "<code>(#$temporallyBetween-Inclusive TEMP-THING EARLY LATE)</code> means that <code>TEMP-THING</code> starts no earlier than when <code>EARLY</code> begins and ends no later than when <code>LATE</code> ends. <code>LATE</code> must begin after <code>EARLY</code> begins.")
(comment normativeSpecificationDescribesRelnToIns "The predicate #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRelnToIns is used for partially specifying the satisfaction conditions for an instance of #$NormativeSpecification  Specifically, it associates an instance of #$NormativeSpecification <code>SPEC</code> with a #$BinaryPredicate <code>RELN</code> and an instance of #$Thing <code>THING</code>, to state the part of satisfying SPEC involves a situation <code>SIT</code> such that <code>(RELN SIT THING)</code>.  This predicate works in conjunction with #$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType, which specifies the #$isa constraints for <code>SIT</code>; indeed <code>(#$normativeSpecificationDescribesSituationType SPEC TYPE)</code> is equivalent to and shorthand for <code>(#$normativeSpecificationDescribesRelnToIns SPEC #$isa TYPE)</code>.  See #$completeSpecification for more information on how to characterize the satisfaction conditions for a normative specification.  See also #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRoleForInd, which is a more specific version of #$normativeSpecificationDescribesRelnToIns, dealing with instances of #$BinaryRolePredicate and #$SomethingExisting.")
(comment affectsNegatively "The most general predicate used to relate a temporal thing to other temporal things that affect it in a way that is contrary to that thing's interests, well-being, or continued existence. <code>(#$affectsNegatively THING-1 THING-2)</code> means that the instance <code>THING-1</code> of #$TemporalThing harms, degrades, thwarts, disturbs, decreases the functionality of, or is otherwise bad for <code>THING-2</code>.   When possible, a more specific predicate (e.g., #$maleficiary, #$objectHarmed, #$negativeVestedInterest) should be used.")
(comment Description-PCW "A sub-collection of #$PropositionalConceptualWork. Each instance is a highly-focused work that characterizes (ascribes properties to) an object.")
(comment SubworkWithTitleFn "<code>(#$SubworkWithTitleFn WORK STRING)</code> denotes sub-work of the work <code>WORK</code> whose title is <code>STRING</code>.")
(comment subworkIsNthOfType "<code>(#$subworkIsNthOfType SUB-WORK WORK N TYPE)</code> identifies <code>SUB-WORK</code> as the <code>N</code>th sub-work of the conceptual work <code>WORK</code> of type <code>TYPE</code>. The value of <code>N</code> is determined by the structure of <code>WORK</code> (see #$correspondingAIS) and the conventions for interpreting such structures.")
(comment NthSubworkOfTypeFn "<code>(#$NthSubworkOfTypeFn WORK N TYPE)</code> denotes the <code>N</code>th sub-work of type <code>TYPE</code> in the conceptual work <code>WORK</code>.   The value of <code>N</code> is determined by the structure of <code>WORK</code> (see #$correspondingAIS) and the conventions for interpreting such structures.")
(comment DescriptionTypeByFocus "An instance of #$FacetingCollecionType, each instance is a subcollection of #$Description-PCW whose instances all describe an object of the same type.  (Note that since #$Description-PCW is the collection of all descriptions of any instance of the type #$Thing, #$Description-PCW is an instance of this collection.)")
(comment ProblemDescription "An instance of #$DescriptionTypeByFocus.  Each instance is a description of a problem, or of what the author purports in the work to be a problem.")
(comment thingDescribed "<code>(#$thingDescribed PCW THING)</code> means that <code>THING</code> is described in the instance <code>PCW</code> of #$PropositionalConceptualWork.")
(comment GoalDescriptionPCW "An instance of #$DescriptionTypeByFocus.  Each instance is a description of a problem, or of what the author purports in the work to be a problem.")
(comment descriptionAscribesRelnToIns "<code>(#$descriptionAscribesRelnToIns DESCRIPTION RELN THING)</code> means that the instance <code>DESCRIPTION</code> of #$Description-PCW is such that its description of <code>DESCRIBED-THING</code> (see #$thingDescribed) contains the claim that <code>(RELN DESCRIBED-THING THING)</code>.")
(comment descriptionAscribesRelnToType "<code>(#$descriptionAscribesRelnToType DESCRIPTION RELN TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>DESCRIPTION</code> of #$Description-PCW is such that its description of <code>DESCRIBED-THING</code> (see #$thingDescribed) contains the claim that <code>(#$relationInstanceExists RELN DESCRIBED-THING TYPE)</code>.")
(comment startsNoEarlierThanStartingOf "(#$startsNoEarlierThanStartingOf TEMPTHING1 TEMPTHING2) means that TEMPTHING1 starts to exist or occur either at the same time as, or after, TEMPTHING2 starts to exist or occur.  That is, (#$startsNoEarlierThanStartingOf TEMPTHING1 TEMPTHING2) means that either (#$temporallyCooriginating TEMPTHING1 TEMPTHING2) or (#$startsAfterStartingOf TEMPTHING1 TEMPTHING2).")
(comment MantiLaSalNationalForest "Manti-La Sal National Forest, located in Utah.")
(comment UintaNationalForest "Uinta National Forest, Utah's first national forest.")
(comment WasatchCacheNationalForest "Wasatch-Cache National Forest, located in Utah.")
(comment DixieNationalForest "Dixie National Forest, the largest national forest in Utah.")
(comment logicalResultSetCardinality "This predicate is used by the SKSI code to estimate the cost of querying the fields of a logical schema.  More precisely, let SCHEMA denote a logical schema, let LF-1, LF-2, ..., LF-N, denote the logical fields of SCHEMA, and let SELECT_SET and WHERE_SET denote two disjoint subsets of (#$TheSet LF-1 LF-2 ... LF-N). Then (#$logicalResultSetCardinality SCHEMA SELECT_SET WHERE_SET NUM) means that NUM is the average cardinality of the result set returned from a query in which the fields in SELECT_SET left unbound and the fields of WHERE_SET are bound.")
(disjointWith CoronaryArteryBypassGraft-SurgicalProcedure (CollectionDifferenceFn CoronaryArteryProcedureNonCongenital-Surgical CoronaryArteryBypassGraft-SurgicalProcedure))
(comment NearlyFunctionalBinaryPredicate "Something is \"nearly functional\" just in case the overwhelming majority of the cases are such that given a fixed arg1 there is just one thing it is related to in arg2.")
(comment TopLevelProblemDescription "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are top-level descriptions of some problem.  For any instance <code>INS</code> of #$TopLevelProblemDescription, there is at least one distinct instance <code>INS-2</code> of #$ProblemDescription that is a elaboration on <code>INS</code> (in a shared context, such as a larger document of which <code>INS</code> and <code>INS-2</code> are both sub-works), and there is no instance <code>INS-3</code> of #$ProblemDescription that <code>INS</code> is an elaboration on.")
(comment TopLevelGoalDescription "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are top-level descriptions of some goal.  For any instance <code>INS</code> of #$TopLevelGoalDescription, there is at least one distinct instance <code>INS-2</code> of #$GoalDescriptionPCW that is a elaboration on <code>INS</code> (in a shared context, such as a larger document of which <code>INS</code> and <code>INS-2</code> are both sub-works), and there is no instance <code>INS-3</code> of #$GoalDescriptionPCW that <code>INS</code> is an elaboration on.")
(comment topLevelDescriptionType "<code>(#$topLevelDescriptionType DESCRIPTION-TYPE TOP-LEVEL-DESCRIPION-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TOP-LEVEL-DESCRIPION-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of <code>DESCRIPTION-TYPE</code> that are \"top-level\" descriptions relative to some instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWork of which <code>TOP-LEVEL-DESCRIPION-TYPE</code> is a sub-work.  To be a \"top-level\" description in this sense means that within the larger work, there is at least one description of type <code>DESCRIPTION-TYPE</code> that is an elaboration on (see #$elaboration-RST) the top-level description, and that there are no descriptions of type <code>DESCRIPION-TYPE</code> upon which the top-level description elaborates.")
(comment elaboration-Enumeration "<code>(#$elaboration-Enumeration INFO-STORE LIST)</code> means that <code>LIST</code>, an instance of either #$List-CW or #$List-Information is an elaboration of the content of <code>INFO-STORE</code> by virtue of being an enumeration of a number of specific points, each of which elaborates on that content.")
(comment conceptFilterCandidateForDocumentType "<code>(#$conceptFilterCandidateForDocumentType FILTER DOC-TYPE)</code> means that when doing targeted concept extraction on documents of type <code>DOC-TYPE</code>, the instance <code>FILTER</code> of #$ConceptFilter is a useful filter to apply.")
(comment pcwCandidateTemplateWithConceptFilter "<code>(#$pcwCandidateTemplateWithConceptFilter PCW TEMPLATE FILTER-SPEC)</code> means that when attempting to do concept-extraction from the instance <code>PCW</code> of #$TextualPCW in order to complete the CycL formula <code>TEMPLATE</code>, use the instance <code>FILTER-SPEC</code> of #$ConceptFilterSpecification.")
(comment SamHouston "Sam Houston, famous and deceased politician, who served as President of Texas, governor of Texas, US Senator from Texas, and governor of Tennessee.")
(comment ProposalWritingAssistanceTemplate "Instances of this collection are templates to guide the reification of instances of #$GoalOrientedSpecification used by applications that help the author(s) compose them.  Each instance should be associated via #$creationTemplateForType with a specific subcollection of #$GoalOrientedSpecification; the template used to adequately cyclify the proposal will be selected by virtue of its specific type.")
(comment SKSIOnlyPredicate "The collection of predicates whose extent is in some stuctured knowledge source that Cyc is mapped to.  The inference engine will not attempt to apply any non-sksi modules to instances of this collection .")
(comment sectionTypeHasTitle "<code>(#$sectionTypeHasTitle WORK-TYPE SECTION-TYPE STRING)</code> means that every instance of <code>WORK-TYPE</code>, a type of #$ConceptualWork, has exactly one #$subWorks of type <code>SECTION-TYPE</code> with title <code>STRING</code>.")
(comment SurgicalIncision-Sternotomy-Partial "A #$Sternotomy, in which the #$Sternum is bisected longitudinally, but the two halves are not completely separated.")
(comment SurgicalIncision-Sternotomy-Full "A #$Sternotomy, in which the entire #$Sternum is bisected (typically longitudinally).")
(comment SurgicalIncision-Sternotomy-Transverse "Instances are #$Sternotomy procedures in which the #$Sternum is cut from side to side as opposed to longitudinally.")
(comment SurgicalIncision-Xiphoid "A surgical incision of the chest wall near the #$XiphoidProcess.")
(comment SurgicalIncision-Subclavian "A surgical incision of the chest wall under one of the #$Clavicles.")
(comment SurgicalIncision-ParasternalRightVertical "Instances are vertical incisions of the right side of the chest wall near the sternum.")
(comment SurgicalIncision-ParasternalLeftVertical "Instances are vertical incisions of the left side of the chest wall near the sternum.")
(comment GreenMountainNationalForest "Green Mountain National Forest, Vermont's only National forest.")
(comment PatientTypeByPreoperativeStatus "A collection of collections; a subset of #$BLOTypeByPhysiology.  Each instance of #$PatientTypeByPreoperativeStatus describes a human patient's preoperative status. ")
(comment medicalEventUsedPerfusionTechnique "Refers to the methods used to divert the blood circulation from the heart, and provide circulation to other parts of the body during Open Heart Surgery.")
(comment selectedEnablingAuthority "<code>(#$selectedEnablingAuthority PROPOSAL AUTHORITY)</code> means that the author of the instance <code>PROPOSAL</code> of #$Proposal has selected <code>AUTHORITY</code>, an instance of #$InformationStore, typically a code of conduct such as an instance of #$Law or a set of policies, to serve as the official authorization for the agreement based on <code>PROPOSAL</code> (see #$agreementAuthorization).")
(comment CherokeeNationalForest "Cherokee National Forest in Tennessee.")
(comment ClinchRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$JeffersonNationalForest.)")
(comment EasternDivideRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$JeffersonNationalForest.)")
(comment GlenwoodRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$JeffersonNationalForest.)")
(comment geographicalDistricts "(#$geographicalDistricts SUPER SUB) means that <code>SUB</code> is a geograhpical sub-region of <code>SUPER</code> that has been desginated a district for administrative purposes.")
(comment PedlarRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$GeorgeWashingtonNationalForest.)")
(comment JamesRiverRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$GeorgeWashingtonNationalForest.)")
(comment USDAFSSouthernRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the southern-most FS lands in the US.")
(comment LeeRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$GeorgeWashingtonNationalForest.)")
(comment NorthRiverRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$GeorgeWashingtonNationalForest.)")
(comment WarmSpringsRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Jefferson National Forest. (See #$GeorgeWashingtonNationalForest.)")
(comment JamesRiver "A river in Virginia.")
(disjointWith AcquiredValvularHeartDisease CongenitalHeartDisease)
(comment definiteDescriptions "<code>(#$definiteDescriptions IND STRING)</code> means that <code>IND</code> is the unique satisfier of the description <code>STRING</code>, and thus that <code>STRING</code> designates <code>IND</code>.
<p> 
Keep in mind that, strictly speaking, definite descriptions are not names, one major difference being that descriptions do not designate rigidly.  Thus any use of #$definiteDescriptions in the KB should either be time-indexed, by using #$holdsIn (or some other predicate); placed in an Mt where the assertion in question is guaranteed to be true; or otherwise monitored for 
staleness and removed whenever the assertion becomes false.")
(comment proposalAddressesProblem-Type "A binary predicate used to describe instances of #$GoalOrientedSpecification. <code>(#$proposalAddressesProblem-Type SPEC TYPE)</code> means that the specification <code>SPEC</code> has among its goals some state of affairs that either renders empty or lessens the impact from the fact there exist instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  In many cases, a value for <code>TYPE</code> can be derived from a sentence of the form <code>(#$proposalAddressesProblem-Prop SPEC PROP)</code>.")
(comment USDAFSSouthwesternRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the FS lands in the southwestern US.")
(comment USDAFSPacificSouthwesternRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the FS lands in California and Hawaii.")
(disjointWith USDAFSRegion RegionallyPartitionedUSDAFSRegion)
(comment USDAFSAlaskaRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the FS lands in Alaska.")
(comment USDAFSIntermountainRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the FS lands in the USDAFS-designated 'intermountain' region.")
(comment USDAFSPacificNorthwestRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the FS lands in Washington and Oregon.")
(comment USDAFSRockyMountainRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the FS lands in the USDAFS-designated 'rocky mountain' region.")
(comment countryOfNationality "'(#$countryOfNationality NATION ALITY)' means that the #$PersonTypeByNationality ALITY is associated with the #$Country NATION, that is, a person who belongs to ALITY is either a citizen of, or a participant in the #$NationalCulture of, NATION.")
(comment AshleyNationalForest "Ashley National Forest, located (mostly) in Utah.")
(comment HiawathaNF-Eastside "The forest, once designated as Marquette National Forest, now the eastern portion of Hiawatha National Forest.")
(comment IronRiverRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Ottowa National Forest in northern Michigan. (See #$OttowaNationalForest.)")
(comment BessemerRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Ottowa National Forest in northern Michigan. (See #$OttowaNationalForest.)")
(comment KentonRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Ottowa National Forest in northern Michigan. (See #$OttowaNationalForest.)")
(comment OntonagonRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Ottowa National Forest in northern Michigan. (See #$OttowaNationalForest.)")
(comment WatersmeetRangerDistrict "An area of forest that makes up part of Ottowa National Forest in northern Michigan. (See #$OttowaNationalForest.)")
(comment USDAFSEasternRegion-Org "The sub-organization of the USDA Forest Service in charge of the FS lands in the USDAFS-designated 'eastern' region.")
(comment OttowaNationalForest "A national forest in Michigan's upper peninsula.")
(comment HiawathaNationalForest "A national forest in Michigan's upper peninsula.")
(comment HiawathaNF-Westside "The western portion of Hiawatha National Forest.")
(comment TerrestrialFunctioningObject "The collection of objects, such as humans, roller coasters, and hamburgers, that function best, if at all, when in an environment similar to that found on the earths surface, immersed in air.")
