(comment exceptMt "(#$exceptMt MT) means that (#$except ASSERTION) is true for all ASSERTIONs asserted in MT. In other words, in the current microtheory ASSERTION is not known to be true.  If ASSERTION is a rule, it will not fire.")
(comment collectionIsaBackchainRequired "<code>(#$collectionIsaBackchainRequired COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
means that rules that conclude
<p>
<code>(#$isa <anything> COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
must be used in order to prove literals of the form
<p>
<code>(#$isa <anything> COLLECTION)</code>.
<p>
This directs the inference engine to use such rules even if HL predicate transformation is disabled.  See also #$backchainRequired for the analogue of this predicate applicable to predicates rather than collections.")
(comment collectionGenlsBackchainRequired "<code>(#$collectionGenlsBackchainRequired COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
means that rules that conclude
<p>
<code>(#$genls <anything> COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
must be used in order to prove literals of the form
<p>
<code>(#$genls <anything> COLLECTION)</code>.
<p>
This directs the inference engine to use such rules even if HL predicate transformation is disabled. See also #$backchainRequired for the analogue of this predicate applicable to predicates rather than collections.")
(comment collectionBackchainRequired "<code>(#$collectionBackchainRequired COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
means that rules that conclude
<p>
<code>(#$isa <anything> COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
must be used in order to prove literals of the form
<p>
<code>(#$isa <anything> COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
and rules that conclude
<p>
<code>(#$genls <anything> COLLECTION)</code>
<p>
must be used in order to prove literals of the form
<p>
<code>(#$genls <anything> COLLECTION)</code>.
<p>
This directs the inference engine to use such rules even if HL predicate transformation is disabled.  See also #$backchainRequired for the analogue of this predicate applicable to predicates rather than collections.")
