(comment StreptococcusMilleriGroupMemberType "The three species of <i>Streptococcus</i>, <i>S. anginosus</i>, <i>S. constellatus</i>, and </i>S. intermedius</i> whose instances make up the <i>S. milleri</i> group of bacteria.")
(comment laterThan "#$laterThan is similar to #$greaterThan, but takes #$Dates as arguments.  <code>(#$laterThan LATE-DATE EARLY-DATE)</code> is true when <code>LATE-DATE</code> and <code>EARLY-DATE</code> are #$Dates, and <code>LATE-DATE</code> starts after <code>EARLY-DATE</code> is over.  #$laterThan is evaluatable.")
(comment ImplantOrRevisionOfAnEPSDevice "includes any implant or revision of an EPS device either in an EPS lab or during an operation.")
(comment LowerRespiratoryTract "The lower portion of the respiratory tract.")
(comment UpperRespiratoryTract "The upper portion of the respiratory tract.")
(comment Bloodstream "An instance of #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType.  Instances are the total physical extent of blood (see #$Blood) inside an individual animal, as it moves through blood vessels (see #$BloodVessel) in the body.")
(comment objectRemaining "<code>(#$objectRemaining SEPARATION OBJECT)</code> means that <code>OBJECT</code> remains at its previous location in <code>SEPARATION</code>, an instance of #$SeparationEvent.")
(comment FluidFlow-Separation "The collection of instances of #$FluidFlow-Translation events in which some part of a portion of fluid moves and separates from that original portion.")
(comment objectsSeparated "An instance of #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$SeparationEvent to each of the objects separated from one another in that event.")
(comment SerratiaOdorifera "A collection of bacteria of the <i>Serratia</i> genus, typically non-pathogenic.")
(comment Sphingomonadaceae-Family "A collection of instances of #$Bacterium, the Sphingomonadaceae are a family under the Protobacteria phylum.")
(comment Sphingomonas "A collection of instances of #$Bacterium, <i>Sphingomonas</i> is a genus under the <i>Sphingomonadaceae</i> family.")
(comment Bacteroidetes-Phylum "The Bacteriodetes phylum in the bacteria kingdom.")
(comment Bacteroidales-Order "The <i>Bacteriodales</i> order in the bacteria kingdom, the most studied class of bacteria.")
(comment Prevotellaceae-Family "The <i>Prevotellaceae</i> family of bacteria.")
(comment Prevotella "A genus in the bacteria kingdom.  Instances are gram-negative, rod-shaped bacteria.")
(comment Prevotella "A genus in the bacteria kingdom.  Instances are gram-negative, rod-shaped bacteria. <i>Prevotella</i> can cause infections in the mouth.")
(comment StreptococcusBovis "A species of #$Streptococcus.")
(comment StreptococcusGroupABacterium "A collection of instances of #$Streptococcus with a similar cell wall structure.  Instances are divided into highly pathogenic species responsible for common and dangerous strep infections.")
(comment StreptococcusGroupBBacterium "A collection of instances of #$Bacterium with a common cell wall structure.  Instances divide into pathogenic species of #$Streptococcus that can cause such infections as pneumonia and meningitis.  Infants and the elderly are particularly susceptible to infections caused by instances of this collection.")
(comment StreptococcusGroupCBacterium "A collection of instances of #$Bacterium with a common cell wall structure.  Instances divide into pathogenic species of #$Streptococcus that cause infections in chickens and in several types of mammals, particularly cows, horses, and moose.")
(comment AlphaHemolyticBacterium "An instance #$BacteriumTypeByHemolysisDisplayTendency.  When colonies of instances of this class of bacteria are grown on blood agar plates, they tend to cause a greenish darkening of the agar.")
(comment BetaHemolyticBacterium "An instance #$BacteriumTypeByHemolysisDisplayTendency.  When colonies of instances of this class of bacteria are grown on blood agar plates, they break the red blood cells down completely, causing the red agar to become clear.")
(comment GammaHemolyticBacterium "The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium that do not break down red blood cells.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByHemolysisDisplayTendency "A specialization of #$OrganismClassificationType, this collection partitions #$Bacterium into classes based on how colonies of bacteria grown on blood agar plates display levels of hemolysis.")
(comment StreptococcusGroupCMemberType "A collection of species of the <i>Streptococcus</i> genus.  Instances are such that their instances possess the Group C antigen, a structural characteristic of the cell wall.")
(comment StreptococcusGroupBMemberType "A collection of species of the <i>Streptococcus</i> genus.  Instances are such that their instances possess the Group B antigen, a structural characteristic of the cell wall.")
(comment StreptococcusGroupAMemberType "A collection of species of the <i>Streptococcus</i> genus.  Instances are such that their instances possess the Group A antigen, a structural characteristic of the cell wall.")
(comment HiatalHernia "A specialization of #$DigestiveDisorder. Each instance of #$HiatalHernia is a condition in which the upper portion of the stomach protrudes into the chest cavity through the esophageal hiatus, an opening of the diaphragm.")
(comment medicalEventPerfusionTime "<code>(#$medicalEventPerfusionTime CARE-EVENT TIME)</code> means that in <code>CARE-EVENT</code>, perfusion was used for a period with the duration <code>TIME</code>.")
(comment Lactobacillaceae "A family of gram-positive bacteria.")
(comment Lactobacillales-Order "An order of gram positive bacterium, used in the fermenation of wine, yogurt, and other products.")
(comment Enterococcaceae "A family of gram-positive bacteria.")
(comment ExchangeOfGunfire "The collection of all #$ConflictEvents consisting primarily in an exchange of gunfire between aggrieved parties, which may be single individuals or groups of persons.  By 'exchange' we mean that the parties are firing at each other, using instances of #$Gun-Portable, with the intent to cause bodily injury or death:  we stipulate further that this is primarily what the event consists in.  At a minimum, every #$ExchangeOfGunfire consists in at least two instances of #$ShootingAGun-Portable:  where A and B are #$opponentsInConflict in the exchange, and are both persons, there must be at least one shooting at B by A and one shooting at A by B, and where A and B are groups of persons, at least one member of A must shoot at at least one member of B and at least one member of B must shoot at at least one member of A.  The shootings need not occur in any particular order and may be simultaneous.  Casualties are possible but not necessary.  Classic examples include the shootout at the Okay Corral and Butch and Sundance's last stand.")
(comment CandidaKefyr "A species of #$Candida.")
(comment CandidaLusitaniae "A species of #$Candida.")
(comment CandidaGuilliermondii "A species of #$Candida.")
(comment Eurotiomycetes "A class of fungi under #$Ascomycota-Division.")
(comment Eurotiales "An order of fungi under the <i>Eurotiomycetes</i> class.")
(comment Onygenales "An order of fungi under the <i>Eurotiomycetes</i> class.")
(comment Trichocomaceae "A family of fungi of the <i>Eurotiales</i> order.")
(comment Aspergillus "A genus of fungi under the <i>Trichocomaceae</i> family and a type of mold.")
(comment Penicillium "A genus of fungi under the <i>Trichocomaceae</i> family.")
(comment PenicilliumChrysogenum "The species of <i>penicillium</i> used to make penicillin.")
(comment Micrococcaceae "A family of gram-positive sphere-shaped bacteria.")
(comment Rhizobiaceae-Family "A collection of instances of #$Bacterium, the <i>Rhizobiaceae</i> are a family under the <i>Protobacteria</i> phylum, whose instances dwell in soil.")
(comment Rhizobium "A genus of bacteria under the <i>Rhizobiaceae</i> family.")
(comment RhizobiumRadiobacter "A species of gram-negative bacteria that lives in soil.")
(comment ProvidenciaStuartii "The species of <i>Providencia</i> bacteria most commonly associated with infections in humans.")
(comment Peptostreptococcus "A genus of gram-positive, anaerobic, non-spore-forming bacteria.")
(comment PeptostreptococcusMagnus "A highly pathogenic species of bacteria.")
(comment Mycobacterium "A genus of bacteria of the <i>Mycobacteriaceae</i> family.  Its species are frequently highly pathogenic and can cause serious infections that are hard to treat with antibiotics, such as leprosy and tuberculosis.")
(comment MycobacteriumFortuitum "A pathogenic species of <i>Mycobacterium</i> found in soil and tap water.  It can cause serious infections, such as menigitis and endocarditis.")
(comment EnterobacterAgglomerans "A pathogenic species of bacteria that typically infects plants, but can also cause infections in animals.")
(comment EnterobacterAsburiae "A somewhat rare species of bacteria of the <i>Enterobacter</i> genus.")
(comment EnterobacterSakazakii "A species of bacteria of the <i>Enterobacter</i> genus.")
(comment CitrobacterAmalonaticus "A species of bacteria of the <i>Citrobacter</i> genus that dwel in soil, water, and human intestine.  <i>Citrobacter amalonaticus</i> rarely is responsible for human infections, but does occasionaly cause urinary tract infections.")
(comment CitrobacterDiversus "A species of bacteria of the <i>Citrobacter</i> genus.")
(comment Flavobacteriaceae "A family of bacteria of the <i>Flavobacteriales</i> order.")
(comment Flavobacteriales "An order of bacteria under the <i>Bacteroidetes<i> phylum.")
(comment Capnocytophaga "A biological genus of bacteria.  One of its species, <i>C. canimorsus</i> is commonly found in the mouths of dogs that can cause zoonotic infections.")
(disjointWith StaphylococcusAureus CoagulaseNegativeStaphylococcus)
(comment Coagulase "An enzyme produced by members of the species <i>Staphylococcus aureus</i>, its presence or absence in blood cultures is used to distinguish <i>Staphylococcus aureus</i>-instances from other instances of <i>Staphylococcus</i>.")
(comment CoagulaseNegativeStaphylococcus "The collection of instances of #$Staphylococcus that do not produce coagulase (see #$Coagulase).  Since <i>S. aureus</i> is the only species of <i>Staphylococcus</i> that does produce coagulase, this is extensionally the collection of all instances of #$Staphylococcus  that are not also instances of instances of #$StaphylococcusAureus.")
(comment Aeromonadaceae-Family "A family of rod-shaped bacteria of the <i>Proteobacteria</i> phylum.")
(comment Aeromonas "A genus of bacteria of the <i>Aeromonadaceae</i>, instances of which are gram-negative rods.")
(comment EnterobacterGergoviae "A species of bacteria of the <i>Enterobacter</i> genus.")
(comment EubacteriumLentum "A species of bacteria of the <i>Eubacterium</i> genus.")
(comment EubacteriumLimosum "A species of bacteria of the <i>Eubacterium</i> genus.")
(comment Eubacterium-Genus "The genus <i>Eubacterium</i> of the <i>Propionibacteriaceae</i> family of bacteria, not to be confused with the collection #$Bacterium, which is also sometimes referred to as \"eubacterium.\"")
(comment DiphtheroidBacterium "The collection of all instances of #$Corynebacterium (a genus of bacteria) that are members of species that are non-pathogenic.")
(comment Acinetobacter "The <i>Acinetobacter</i> genus under the <i>Moraxellaceae</i> family of bacteria.")
(comment AcinetobacterLwoffi "A species of bacteria of the <i>Acinetobacter</i> genus.")
(comment AcinetobacterBaumanni "A species of bacteria of the <i>Acinetobacter</i> genus.")
(comment StenotrophomonasMaltophilia "A pathogenic species of bacteria of the <i>Stenotrophomonas</i> genus. Infections in humans with uncompromised immune systems are rare, but hard to treat, as this species is resistant to antibiotics.")
(comment Propionibacteriaceae-Family "A family of bacteria under the <i>Actinomycetales</i> order.")
(comment Propionibacterium "The <i>Propionibacterium</i> genus of the <i>Propionibacteriaceae</i> family in the Bacteria kingdom.")
(comment Pichia "A genus of fungi.")
(comment PantoeaAgglomerans "A species of bacteria of the genus <i>Pantoea</i>.")
(comment Paecilomyces "A genus of fungi under the <i>Trichocomaceae</i> family.")
(comment Listeria "A genus of bacteria.  One notable species is <i>Listeria monocytogenes</i>, which is pathogenic to humans.")
(comment Listeriaceae-Family "The <i>Listeriaceae</i> family of bacteria, under the order <i>Bacillales</i>.")
(comment Pantoea "The <i>Pantoea</i> genus of bacteria in the <i>Enterobacteriaceae</i> family.")
(comment Xanthomonadaceae-Family "A family of rod-shaped bacteria.")
(comment Stenotrophomonas "A genus of rod-shaped, gram-negative bacteria of the <i>Xanthomonadaceae</i> family.")
(comment Hafnia "A genus of bacteria in the <i>Enterobacteriaceae</i> family.")
(comment dataForValveOfEventRecordsStenosisSite "<code>(#$dataForValveOfEventRecordsStenosisSite VALVE-DATA EVENT STENOSIS-SITE-TYPE)</code> means that according to the <code>VALVE-DATA</code> associated with <code>EVENT</code> (an instance of #$CardiacCatheterization, #$Echocardiogram) the focal valve has the stenosis site <code>STENOSIS-SITE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment dataForValveOfEventRecordsStenosisSeverity "<code>(#$dataForValveOfEventRecordsStenosisSeverity VALVE-DATA EVENT STENOSIS-SEVERITY)</code> means that according to the <code>VALVE-DATA</code> associated with <code>EVENT</code> (an instance of #$CardiacCatheterization or #$Echocardiogram) the focal valve has the stenosis severity <code>STENOSIS-SEVERITY</code>.")
(comment Methylobacterium "A genus of bacteria under the <i>Methylobacteriaceae</i> family.")
(comment Methylobacteriaceae-Family "A family of bacteria under the <i>Proteobacteria</i> phylum.")
(comment Moraxella "The <i>Moraxella</i> genus under the <i>Moraxellaceae</i> family of bacteria.")
(comment Moraxellaceae-Family "A collection of instances of #$Bacterium, the <i>Moraxellacaeae</i> are a family under the <i>Proteobacteria</i> phylum.")
(comment HaemophilusInfluenzae "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are found in the mucous membranes of
the upper respiratory tract in humans.  Infection of type of bacterium is of two types: an acute, invasive infection, where it is the primary pathogen and those infections in which it is a secondary pathogen.   It is a major cause of meningitis in children, see (#$InfectionFn #$Meninges), and occasionally cause upper respiratory infections in adults and children.")
(comment Trichosporan "A genus of yeasts.")
(comment TrichosporanBeigelii "A species of yeast of the genus <i>Trichosporan</i> that sometimes causes infections in humans.")
(comment Geotrichum "A genus of yeasts.")
(comment GeotrichumCapitatum "A species of yeast of the genus <i>Geotrichum</i> that sometimes causes infections in humans.")
(comment Flavobacterium "A genus of bacteria under the <i>Flavobacteriaceae</i> family.")
(comment Fusobacteria-Phylum "The <i>Fusobacteria</i> phylum in the bacteria kingdom.")
(comment FusobacteriumNucleatum "A species of bacteria of the <i>Fusobacterium</i> genus.")
(comment Fusobacterium "A genus of pathogenic, gram-negative bacteria.")
(comment Comamonadaceae "A collection of instances of #$Bacterium, the <i>Comamonadaceae</i> are a family under the <i>Proteobacteria</i> phylum.")
(comment Delftia "The <i>Delftia</i> genus under the <i>Comamonadaceae</i> family of bacteria.")
(comment DelftiaAcidovorans "A species of bacteria of the <i>Delftia</i> genus.")
(comment Cryptococcus "A genus of pathogenic fungi.")
(comment CryptococcusNeoformans "A species of fungus that can cause menigitis in humans who have a weakened immune system.")
(comment Citrobacter "A subcollection of #$Bacterium, <i>Citrobacter</i> is a genus under the <i>Enterobacteriaceae</i> family.")
(comment Chryseobacterium "A genus of bacteria of the <i>Flavobacteriaceae</i> family.")
(comment Alcaligenaceae-Family "A family of bacteria of the <i>Proteobacteria</i> phylum.")
(comment Alcaligenes "A genus of the <i>Alcaligenaceae</i> family of bacteria.")
(comment AlcaligenesXyloxidans "A species of bacteria of the genus <i>Alcaligenes</i>.")
(comment HaemophilusParainfluenzae "A typically non-pathogenic species of bacteria of the <i>Haemophilus</i> genus.")
(comment StreptococcusGroupGBacterium "A collection of instances of #$Streptococcus with a similar cell wall structure.  Instances are divided into species that make up <i>Streptococcus</i> Group G.")
(comment Flavimonas "A collection of instances of Bacterium, Flavimonas was once recognized as a genus, but later deemed identical to the genus Pseudomonas.")
(comment Pneumovirus "A genus of viruses whose instances cause respiratory infections.")
(comment RespiratorySyncytialVirus "A type of virus that is a common cause of lower respiratory tract infections.  For most people, symptoms of such infections are mild; however, in infants (especially those born prematurely), these infections can be quite serious, requiring hospitalization and sometimes causing death. Infants who experience serious RSV infections frequently go on to develop asthma.")
(comment Acidaminococcaceae-Family "A family of bacteria of the <i>Firmicutes</i> phylum, distinguished from other <i>Firmicutes</i> by virtue of being gram-negative.")
(comment Veillonella "A genus of the <i>Acidaminococcaceae</i> family of bacteria.")
(comment VeillonellaParvula "A species of bacteria of the <i>Veillonella</i> genus that is rarely pathogenic, but occasionally causes osteomyelitis in humans.")
(comment PseudomonasFluorescens "A species of bacteria of the <i>Pseudomonas</i> genus.  It is used to make yogurt and the antibiotic Mupirocin.")
(comment HospitalCareEventWithAdmissionOnSameDayAsElectiveSurgery "A specialization of #$HospitalCareEvent. Each instance of #$HospitalCareEventWithAdmissionOnSameDayAsElectiveSurgery is a hospital care event in which a patient is admited on the same day as their elective surgery.")
(disjointWith TermUnacceptableForQueryStringMapping TermAcceptableForQuerySearch-InstantiationOnly)
(comment MinimallyInvasiveProcedureOrOperation "if the operation or procedure used a minimally invasive approach, then it is an instance of this collection.")
(comment DateInitialSecondFn "<code>(#$DateInitialSecondFn DATE)</code> returns a date representing the first second of <code>DATE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$DateInitialSecondFn (#$YearFn 2007))</code> evaluates to <code>(#$SecondFn 0 (#$MinuteFn 0 (#$HourFn 0 (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 2007))))))</code>.  For the last second see #$DateFinalSecondFn.")
(comment DateFinalSecondFn "<code>(#$DateFinalSecondFn DATE)</code> returns a date representing the last second of <code>DATE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$DateFinalSecondFn (#$YearFn 2007))</code> returns <code>(#$SecondFn 59 (#$MinuteFn 59 (#$HourFn 23 (#$DayFn 31 (#$MonthFn #$December (#$YearFn 2007))))))</code>.  For the first second see #$DateInitialSecondFn.")
(disjointWith InformationStore ScalarOrVectorInterval)
(comment CardioPulmonaryBypassOperation "A specialization of #$Operation.  Each instance is a surgery during which CPB is used.  These are also known as \"off-pump\" surgery.")
(disjointWith BeatingHeartSurgery CardioPulmonaryBypassOperation)
(comment BeatingHeartSurgery "A specialization of #$Operation.  Each instance is a surgery during which the heart is not stopped from beating.  These are also known as \"off-pump\" surgeries.")
(comment VentricularAssistDevice "A specialization of #$CardiacAssistDevice.  Each instance of #$VentricularAssistDevice is a mechanical device designed to support a failing heart by assisting the ventricles.")
(comment argIsaArg "(#$argIsaArg PRED N M) means that for a formula involving PRED in arg0 to be well formed the Nth argument to PRED must be an instance of the Mth argument.  This is especially useful in enforcing disjointness constaints for specPreds of #$isa.")
(comment GroupRoleFn "<code>(#$GroupRoleFn ROLE)</code> denotes the binary situation predicate <code>PRED</code> such that if <code>(PRED SITUATION GROUP)</code>, then for each member <code>MEMBER</code> of <code>GROUP</code>, there is a sub-situation <code>SUB</code> of <code>SITUATION</code> such that <code>(ROLE SUB MEMBER)</code>.")
(comment groupVersionOfRole "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$GroupRoleFn, <code>(#$groupVersionOfRole PRED ROLE)</code> identifies <code>PRED</code> as the binary situation predicate such that if <code>(PRED SITUATION GROUP)</code>, then for each member <code>MEMBER</code> of <code>GROUP</code>, there is a sub-situation <code>SUB</code> of <code>SITUATION</code> such that <code>(ROLE SUB MEMBER)</code>.")
(comment PrimarySurgery "A specialization of #$Operation.  Each instance of #$PrimarySurgery is a surgery performed on a patient who has had no prior surgeries.")
(comment owlExportTermFromContextsWithIsaFilters "<code>(#$owlExportTermFromContextsWithIsaFilters SET-OF-MTS SET-OF-COLS THING)</code> means that <code>THING</code> is a term suitable for OWL export because it is mentioned in an assertion in one of the contexts in <code>SET-OF-MTS</code>, and is not an instance of any collection that is an element of <code>SET-OF-COLS</code>.")
(comment medicalEventHasAssociatedData "Relates a medical event to a data node that specifies further information about the event or procedure.")
(comment AortaDissection "A kind of affliction affecting the aorta. Each instance of aortic dissecton is a condition in which the afflicted person has a tear in the wall of the aorta.  This condition will typically lead to a rapid death.")
(comment MarfansSyndrome "A specialization of #$GeneticDisorder.  Each instance of #$MarfansSyndrome is a genetic physiological condition characterized by long limbs and a cluster of disorders of the heart valves and aorta.")
(comment existentiallyCloseVariablesOfType "(#$existentiallyCloseVariablesOfType COLL) means that variables appearing in query search fragments that are constrained to be instances of COLL should be existentially closed.  The binding should appear at the widest scope.")
(comment surgicalProcedureUsedRepairProcedure "states the type of repair procedure used during the heart valve repair procedure.")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure Diagnosing)
(comment IndustryOfRegionFn "(#$IndustryOfRegionFn INDUSTRY-TYPE REGION) is the #$Industry-Localized of type INDUSTRY-TYPE 'belonging to' REGION -- that is, its income contributes to the Gross National Product of the nation containing REGION.  If a private industry, it pays taxes to the national government of REGION. Not all of the industry's facilities are necessarily located in REGION.  For instance, it may have factories in countries where labor is cheaper.  See also #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn which denotes types of industries characterized by what kind of products they create. See also the corresponding predicate #$industryOfRegion")
(comment EthnicGroupOfTubu "Rugged mountain peope who live predominantly in the southwest of #$Chad.  They have a reputation for being fierce fighters, and are feared by many.")
(disjointWith HospitalCareEvent Infection)
(comment GroupOfPersonTypeByCultureFn "<code>(#$GroupOfPersonTypeByCultureFn PERSON-TYPE)</code> denotes the group consisting of all and only instances of the #$PersonTypeByCulture, <code>PERSON-TYPE</code>.")
(comment groupOfPersonTypeByCulture "<code>(#$groupOfPersonTypeByCulture PERSON-TYPE GROUP)</code> means that <code>GROUP</code> is the group consisting of all and only instances of the #$PersonTypeByCulture, <code>PERSON-TYPE</code>.")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure HospitalCareEvent)
(comment agentPlaysRoleInEventsDuring-Count "(agentPlaysRoleInEventsDuring-Count ROLE AGENT COLL DATE INT) means that the agent AGENT played the role ROLE in exactly INT events that were instances of COLL during the time period DATE.")
(comment providerPerformsProceduresDuring-Count "(providerPerformsProceduresDuring-Count ROLE SURG PROC-TYPE DATE INT) means that the surgeon or group of surgeons SURG played the role ROLE in exactly INT surgical procedures that were instances of COLL during the time period DATE.")
(comment factSheetLinksForQuerySearchStringsEnabled "<code>(#$factSheetLinksForQuerySearchStringsEnabled SPECIFICATION BOOLEAN)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, the CAE should display fact-sheet links for terms identified in query search strings if and only if BOOLEAN is #$True.")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure MakingAMedicalIncisionInABLO)
(comment vascularProcedureSite "(#$vascularProcedureSite PRO SITE) states that the vascular procedure, PRO, was a procedure involving an instance of SITE in the patient.")
(comment vascularProcedureName "States the more specific name of the other vascular or aortic procedure that was performed.")
(comment Warlord "A military leader controlling a subnational region with loyal forces, often in defiance of a weak national government.")
(comment Myxoma "Tumors found in the heart.")
(comment AtrialMyxoma "Tumors found in the left or right atrium of the heart.")
(comment termSummaryPredicateLabel "<code>(#$termSummaryPredicateLabel PRED LABEL)</code> means that a textual summary of a term <code>TERM</code> containing sentences such that <code>(PRED TERM SENTENCE)</code> should be labeled <code>LABEL</code>.")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure PrimarySurgery)
(disjointWith PrimarySurgery MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment objectPlacedInCABG "related a CABG procedure to the graft implant placed during that procedure.")
(comment comorbidConditions "<code>(#$comorbidConditions CONDITION-1 CONDITION-2)</code> means that the instances <code>CONDITION-1</code> and <code>CONDITIION-2</code> of #$AilmentCondition are comorbid, meaning they are present in the same organism at the same time.  More formally, if <code>(#$comorbidConditions CONDITION-1 CONDITION-2)</code> holds at some time <code>t</code>, then <code>t</code> intersects the temporal extents of both conditions such that there exists an organism <code>ORG</code> such that both <code>(#$ailmentConditionAffects CONDITION-1 ORG)</code> and <code>(#$ailmentConditionAffects CONDITION-2 ORG)</code>.")
(comment deviceTypeTreatsConditionType "A binary predicate that relates types of #$MedicalDevices to the conditions the device is commonly used to treat.  This does not necessarily mean that the devices are approved for treatment of the condition, merely that one of the common uses of the device is to treat the condition.")
(comment Anchorage "The place in a harbor where ships lie at anchor.")
(comment Anchor "A heavy metal device equipped with hook-like arms designed to prevent #$Watercraft from travel when let down to the seafloor and at the same time secured to the vessel, typically by chain or heavy rope.")
(comment patientAgeDuringMedicalEvent "<code>(#$patientAgeDuringMedicalEvent PAT EVT TIME-QUANT)</code> means that the #$MedicalPatient <code>PAT</code> is of the age <code>TIME-QUANT</code> at the time of the start of the event <code>EVT</code>.")
(comment sksiLaterThan "#$sksiLaterThan is similar to #$laterThan, but is intended to only be solved via an external knowledge source.  <code>(#$sksiLaterThan LATE-DATE EARLY-DATE)</code> is true when <code>LATE-DATE</code> and <code>EARLY-DATE</code> are #$Dates, and <code>LATE-DATE</code> starts after <code>EARLY-DATE</code> is over.")
(comment infectionOnsetDate "<code>(#$infectionOnsetDate INFECTION DATE)</code> means that the starting date (see #$startingDate) of the infecting event (see #$InfectingEvent) that resulted in the instance <code>INFECTION</code> of #$Infection is <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment ThoracicAortaProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ThoracicAortaProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a #$ThoracicAorta.")
(comment AbdominalAortaProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$AbdominalAortaProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on an #$AbdominalAorta.")
(comment AirwayProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$AirwayProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on an airway.")
(comment AtrialProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$AtrialProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on an atrium of a heart.")
(comment CardiacProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$CardiacProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a #$Heart.")
(comment CardiacSeptumProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$CardiacSeptumProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a cardiac septum.")
(comment ChestWallProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ChestWallProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a chest wall.")
(comment DiaphragmProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$DiaphragmProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a diaphragm.")
(comment HeartValveProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$HeartValveProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a heart valve.")
(comment HeartVentricleProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$HeartVentricleProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a ventricle of a heart.")
(comment PericardialProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PericardialProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a pericardium.")
(comment PleuraProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PleuraProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a pleura.")
(comment PulmonaryProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PulmonaryProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a lung.")
(comment RenalProcedure-Surgical "An instance of #$SurgicalProcedureTypeByOrganismPartTypeActedOn (q.v.).  Each instance of #$RenalProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure performed on a kidney.")
(disjointWith RedoProcedure MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment PatientBloodAnalysis "A specialization of #$InformationGathering.  Instances are events in which blood is drawn from an animal and one or more instances of #$BloodTest are run to rule out or diagnose medical problems.")
(comment IsolatedIndividualTypeOfTypeFn "(#$IsolatedIndividualTypeOfTypeFn TYPE) denotes the collection of instances of TYPE that are set or kept apart from other instances of TYPE.")
(comment conditionAffectsPartType "<code>(#$conditionAffectsPartType COND-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means that the #$PhysiologicalConditionType <code>COND-TYPE</code> affects <code>PART-TYPE</code>, which is a typically a type of organism part, or a type of medical implant.")
(comment USAirForceWing "#$USAirForceWing is the collection of all wings within the #$UnitedStatesAirForce.")
(comment Regurgitation-MitralValve "The condition in which some blood flows the wrong direction through the #$MitralValve")
(comment NativeHeartValveDisease "A specialization of #$HeartCondition, each instance of #$NativeHeartValveDisease is a condition in which a native heart valve (i.e. not an implant) is diseased.")
(comment ProstheticHeartValveDisease "A specialization of #$AcquiredHeartDisease, each instance of #$ProstheticHeartValveDisease is a condition in which a prosthetic heart valve is diseased.")
(comment cAEQuerySearchFilterSpecification "<code>(#$cAEQuerySearchFilterSpecification SPECIFICATION FILTER-SPEC)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, FILTER-SPEC should be used to filter concepts from a user search when trying to find appropriate query components.")
(comment CindySheehan "Cindy Sheehan, a famous American anti-war activist.")
(comment OpportunisticHumanPathogenType "A collection of collections.  Each instance is a collection of microorganisms (typically a species or genus) that typically poses little threat to healthy humans, but which can cause infections in humans with a compromised immune system.")
(comment OpportunisticInfection "The collection of all instances of #$Infection caused by typically non-pathogenic microorganisms that were able to infect the host organism because the organism has a compromised immune system.")
(comment ExplanationWorthyConcept "The collection of concepts that are worthy of explanation in any given context.  Typically, these concepts are not so esoteric that people are incapable of understanding them, but the average person is likely to not know exactly what these concepts mean.")
(comment caeQueryLibraryDefaultDisjunctionFreeELVarsPolicy "<code>(#$caeQueryLibraryDefaultDisjunctionFreeELVarsPolicy SPECIFICATION VALUE)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, the inference engine setting for :DISJUNCTION-FREE-EL-VARS-POLICY should by default be VALUE for any query.")
(comment opportunisticHumanPathogen-Type "A collection of collections.  Each instance is a collection of microorganisms (typically a species or genus) that typically poses little threat to healthy humans, but which can cause infections in humans with a compromised immune system.")
(comment folderHasContentsOrder "(#$folderHasContentsOrder FOLDER CONTENTS-LIST) is syntactic sugar for a set of #$higherPriorityInFolder assertions (N - 1 assertions when CONTENTS-LIST is of length N), which are used by the Query Library to control the order in which the contents of FOLDER are displayed.  Each list member of CONTENTS-LIST must be a resource (via #$folderContainsResource) in FOLDER, and CONTENTS-LIST must not include duplicates.")
(comment deeperGenTemplateRecipe "<code>(#$deeperGenTemplateRecipe RECIPE DEEPER-RECIPE)</code> means that <code>DEEPER-RECIPE</code> is one (of potentially many) <code>#$GenTemplateRecipe</code> whose linguistic representation is deeper (i.e., more syntactically complex or more semantic) than <code>RECIPE</code>, but produces the same strings in at least some cases")
(comment generateArgOfRelnWithForm "<code>(#$generateArgOfRelnWithForm ARGNUM RELN FORM)</code> means that the <code>ARGNUM</code>th argument to <code>RELN</code> should be paraphrased in natural language using a phrase with the syntactic agreement specified by <code>FORM</code>.")
(comment OrganSystem "An instance of #$OrganismPartType.  Each instance of #$OrganSystem is a group of organs (see #$Organ) that are part of a single organism and, by applying conventions accepted in the field of anatomy, are considered to be related in a way that warrants treating the group as a cohesive anatomical part in its own right.  Organ systems are frequently classified as such due to function (see, e.g., #$UrinarySystem).  However, in some cases, they are classified because of common developmental origin in embryos (see, e.g., #$GenitourinarySystem.)")
(comment ConventionalOrganSystemType "A collection of specializations of #$OrganSystem.  Instances are the types of organ systems that are recognized as such by the classification conventions of biologists and anatomists.  Examples thus include the cirulatory system (see #$CirculatorySystem), but exclude what might (from a biologist's perspective) appear to be arbitrary types of organ systems, such as the collection of all organ systems belonging to red-haired mammals nickaned \"Gerry.\"  An important specialization of this collection is #$OrganSystemTypeByFunction.")
(comment OrganSystemTypeByFunction "A collection of specializations of #$OrganSystem, classified by the biological function those systems perform.")
(comment MajorSurgery "A specialization of #$SurgicalTreatment.  Each instance of #$MajorSurgery is a surgery event that requires procedures involving general anesthesia, typically also involving opening the body cavity or the skull.")
(comment querySentenceForTermSummaryPredicate "<code>(#$querySentenceForTermSummaryPredicate SUMMARY-PRED FOCAL-TERM QUERY-SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>QUERY-SENTENCE</code> is a query sentence whose answers, if any, will reveal facts about <code>FOCAL-TERM</code> in the summary category covered by <code>SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment pathTypeConveysType "<code>(#$pathTypeConveysType PATH-TYPE COLL)</code> means that all properly working instances of the type <code>PATH-TYPE</code> can carry or bear instances of the type <code>COLL</code>. All properly working instances of #$Path-InfoTransfer, for instance, can carry instances of #$AspatialInformationStore.  See also #$pathConveysType.")
(comment pathConveysType "<code>(#$pathConveysType PATH COLL)</code> means that the particular instance of path <code>PATH</code> can carry instances of the type <code>COLL</code>, provided that <code>PATH</code> is functioning properly or in good repair.  For instance, a telephone line might carry information, a road might carry vehicles, etc. See also #$pathTypeConveysType.")
(comment above-Generally "<code>(#$above-Generally OVER-OBJ UNDER-OBJ)</code> means that the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>OVER-OBJ</code> is more or less above the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>UNDER-OBJ</code>. To be more precise: if <code>OVER-OBJ</code> is within a cone-shaped set of vectors within about 45 degrees of #$Up-Directly pointing up from <code>UNDER-OBJ</code> (see #$Up-Generally), then <code>(#$above-Generally OVER-OBJ UNDER-OBJ)</code> holds. This is a more general predicate than #$above-Directly (q.v.), but it is a more specialized predicate than #$above-Higher (q.v.). It probably most closely conforms to the English word \"above.\"")
(comment emitter "This predicate, a specialization of #$providerOfMotiveForce and #$fromLocation (qq.v.), is used to identify the source of an emission.  <code>(#$emitter EMIT OBJ)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> provides the force involved in making the #$objectEmitted move from <code>OBJ</code> to someplace outside of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment RocketEngine "A collection of #$Engines used to propel  #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice, of which they are generally a part.  Rocket engines are driven by reaction propulsion.")
(comment RocketPropelledTransportationDevice "The collection of all #$TransportationDevices propelled by rocket engines which includes earth-to-orbit and moon-to-orbit devices, aircraft, weapons and some unusual instances of automobiles.  Rocket engines are self-contained in that they do not need oxygen from the atmosphere to burn fuel and therefore are the only engines capable of space travel.  #$Weapons which are commonly called rockets are here defined as #$Missiles that are also #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevices (see #$Missile-RocketPropelled).")
(comment Missile-RocketPropelled "A #$WeaponType and specialization of both #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice and #$Missile (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Missile-RocketPropelled is a #$Missile that is powered by a #$RocketEngine.  See also #$Missile-JetPropelled.")
(comment LaunchingASelfPoweredProjectile "A specialization of #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion (q.v.).  Each instance of #$LaunchingASelfPoweredProjectile is an event in which a self-propelled projectile is launched.")
(comment LaunchingAMissile "A specialization of #$LaunchingASelfPoweredProjectile.  Each instance of #$LaunchingAMissile is an event in which some instance of #$Missile is launched.")
(comment LaunchingARocket "A specialization of #$LaunchingASelfPoweredProjectile. Each instance of #$LaunchingARocket is an event in which some instance of #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice is launched.")
(comment RocketRange "A specialization of #$GeographicalRegion (q.v.).   Each instance of #$RocketRange is a large area associated with a rocket launching site, including all of the area over which rockets launched from that site are expected to fly. Typically, tracking stations and other support technology are established within the range.")
(comment RocketFlight "A specialization of #$FlyingViaAirTransportationDevice. Each instance of #$RocketFlight is an event in which a rocket flies.")
(comment RocketFlight-SubOrbital "A specialization of #$RocketFlight. Each instance of #$RocketFlight-SubOrbital is an event in which a rocket flies sub-orbitally.")
(comment RocketFlight-Orbital "A specialization of #$RocketFlight. Each instance of #$RocketFlight-SubOrbital is an event in which a rocket files orbitally around a planetary body.")
(disjointWith RocketFlight-SubOrbital RocketFlight-Orbital)
(disjointWith BiologicalProcess Orbiting)
(comment RocketFlight-EscapeVelocity "A specialization of #$RocketFlight. Each instance of #$RocketFlight-EscapeVelocity is an event in which a rocket files away from a planetary body with sufficient velocity to escape that body's gravitational pull.")
(disjointWith RocketFlight-Orbital RocketFlight-EscapeVelocity)
(comment departureFacilityForType "<code>(#$departureFacilityForType FACILITY TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used for departures and loading of instances of <code>TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE</code>.  Note that the first argument is an individual, whereas the second is a collection (usually a collection of vehicles).  For example, (#$departureFacilityForType #$CapeCanaveralAirForceStation #$Airplane).")
(comment arrivalFacilityForType "<code>(#$arrivalFacilityForType FACILITY TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used for arrivals and unloading of instances of <code>TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE</code>.  Note that the first argument is an individual, whereas the second is a collection (usually a collection of vehicles).")
(comment arrivalFacilityAppropriateForTransporter "<code>(#$arrivalFacilityAppropriateForTransporter FACILITY TRANSPORTER)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used for arrivals and unloading of transporter types such as those that <code>TRANSPORTER</code> is an instance of.")
(comment departureFacilityAppropriateForTransporter "<code>(#$departureFacilityAppropriateForTransporter FACILITY TRANSPORTER)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used for departures and loading of transporter types such as those that <code>TRANSPORTER</code> is an instance of.")
(comment RocketLaunchFacility "A specialization of #$TransportFacility. Each instance of #$RocketLaunchFacility is a structure built for the purpose of launching rockets (see #$LaunchingARocket).")
(comment SeaportFacility "The collection of working port facilities that are owned and/or managed by a single organization (private or public).  Each element of #$SeaportFacility is either in the working port part of some element of #$PortCity, or is in a #$NavalShipBase. (See #$Seaport.) Instances of #$SeaportFacility have both tangible and intangible aspects.")
(comment departureAndArrivalFacilityForType "<code>(#$departureAndArrivalFacilityForType FACILITY TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used for arrivals, loading, unloading and departures of instances of <code>TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE</code>.  Note that the first argument is an individual, whereas the second is a collection (usually a collection of vehicles).  For example, (#$departureAndArrivalFacilityForType OHareAirport #$Airplane).")
(comment departureAndArrivalFacilityAppropriateForTransporter "<code>(#$departureAndArrivalFacilityAppropriateForTransporter FACILITY TRANSPORTER)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used for arrivals, loading, unloading and departures of transporter types such as those that <code>TRANSPORTER</code> is an instance of.")
(comment portFacilityForType "<code>(#$portFacilityForType FACILITY TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used as a port facility (see #$PortFacility) for instances of <code>TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE</code>.  Note that the first argument is an individual, whereas the second is a collection (usually a collection of vehicles).")
(comment PortFacility "A specialization of #$TransportFacility.  Each instance of #$PortFacility is an transport facility owned and/or managed by a single organization (private or public), typically built to support the loading, unloading, launching (or departure) and arrival of transports of certain kinds.  Some ports serve only to support some of these functions: for example, some ports support only loading and launching of transports (see, for example, #$SpaceLaunchFacility).  Specific kinds of port tend to support specific kinds of transports: space ports support spacecraft, sea ports support ships, and airports support aircraft.")
(comment AirForceStation-Grounds "A subcollection of #$GroundsOfOrganization and #$MilitaryFacility; each is controlled by a #$subOrganizations of an air force and is the #$orgFacilities of some #$AirForceStation-MilitaryOrganization.")
(comment AirForceStation-MilitaryOrganization "A specialization of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization (q.v.). This is the collection of military organizations that run air force stations (cf. #$AirForceStation-Grounds).")
(disjointWith CartPath SpaceLaunchFacility)
(disjointWith SpaceLaunchFacility Roadway)
(disjointWith SpaceLaunchFacility Airport-Physical)
(disjointWith SpaceLaunchFacility RailroadStation)
(comment WesternRange-RocketRange "The Western Range is a rocket range (see #$RocketRange) that consists of the launch head at VAFB and extends along the west coast of the continental US westward through the Pacific and Indian Oceans.")
(comment portFacilityAppropriateForTransporter "<code>(#$portFacilityAppropriateForTransporter FACILITY TRANSPORTER)</code> means that the individual #$TransportFacility <code>FACILITY</code> is designed and used for either arrivals and unloading or departures and loading of transporter types such as those that <code>TRANSPORTER</code> is an instance of.")
(comment RocketFlight-Liftoff "A specialization of #$RocketFlight. Each instance of #$RocketFlight-Liftoff is an event in which a rocket files, caused by some instance of #$LaunchingARocket.")
(comment EasternRange-RocketRange "The Eastern Range is a rocket range (see #$RocketRange) that consists of the launch head at Cape Canaveral Air Force Station; primary facilities on Patrick Air Force Base, Kennedy Space Center, Malabar Annex, Jonathan Dickinson Missile Tracking Annex, and facilities at Antigua, Argentia and Ascension; and secondary facilities at Wallops Island, Virginia, and Newfoundland, as well as all land sea and air space within reach of a launch vehicle in the Atlantic, Pacific and Indian Oceans.")
(comment SpaceLaunchFacility "A specialization of #$PortFacility (q.v.). Each instance of #$SpaceLaunchFacility is a port built for #$Spacecraft.")
(comment AirForceAnnex-MilitaryOrganization "A specialization of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization (q.v.). This is the collection of military organizations that run air force annexess (cf. #$AirForceAnnex-Grounds).")
(comment AirForceFacility "A subcollection of #$GroundsOfOrganization and #$MilitaryFacility; each instance of #$AirForceFacility is controlled by a #$subOrganizations of an #$AirForce.  An important specialization is #$AirForceBase-Grounds.  Other instances are annexes (see #$AirForceAnnex-Grounds), as well as radar or telemetry stations.")
(comment temporallyContains "<code>(#$temporallyContains LONG SHORT)</code> means that <code>SHORT</code> #$startsDuring <code>LONG</code>,
#$endsDuring <code>LONG</code>, and is temporally subsumed by <code>LONG</code>.")
(comment temporalBoundsContain "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate and a specialization of #$temporalBoundsSubsume (q.v.). <code>(#$temporalBoundsContain LONGER SHORTER)</code> means that the temporal boundaries of <code>LONGER</code> strictly contain those of <code>SHORTER</code>.  In other words, <code>LONGER</code> starts before <code>SHORTER</code> and ends after it: the #$startingPoint of <code>LONGER</code> is some positive, non-zero amount of time earlier than the #$startingPoint of <code>SHORTER</code>, and the #$endingPoint of <code>LONGER</code> is some positive, non-zero amount of time later than the #$endingPoint of <code>SHORTER</code>.
<p>
Note that if <code>LONGER</code> is an instance of #$TemporallyContinuousThing, then <code>(#$temporalBoundsContain LONGER SHORTER)</code> further implies <code>(#$temporallySubsumes LONGER SHORTER)</code>.
<p>
See also the specialization #$temporallyContains.")
(comment temporalBoundsSubsume "<code>(#$temporalBoundsSubsume LONGER SHORTER)</code> means that <code>LONGER</code> contains <code>SHORTER</code>.  <code>SHORTER</code> starts no sooner than the start of <code>LONGER</code> and ends no later than the end of <code>LONGER</code>.  Thus they can have one or two of the same endpoints.   That is, the #$startingPoint of <code>LONGER</code> is a finite amount of time earlier than the #$startingPoint of <code>SHORTER</code>, and the #$endingPoint of <code>LONGER</code> is a finite amount of time later than the #$endingPoint of <code>SHORTER</code>.   Naturally, #$temporalBoundsSubsume is a stronger relation than #$temporalBoundsIntersect.  If <code>LONGER</code> is an instance of #$TemporallyContinuousThing, then <code>(#$temporalBoundsSubsume LONGER SHORTER)</code> further implies <code>(#$temporallySubsumes LONGER SHORTER)</code>.")
(comment startsDuring "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that is a  specialization of both #$startsAfterStartingOf and #$temporalBoundsIntersect (qq.v.), and that relates a given temporal thing (see #$TemporalThing) to  another such that the first starts to exist or occur at some time between  the start and the end of the existence or occurrence of the second.
<p>
<code>(#$startsDuring SECONDTHING FIRSTTHING)</code> means that the start (see  #$startingPoint) of <code>SECONDTHING</code> is properly contained within the temporal  bounds (see #$temporalBoundsContain) of <code>FIRSTTHING</code>.  
<p>
Note that this does  <i>not</i> entail that <code>SECONDTHING</code> and <code>FIRSTTHING</code> <i>intersect</i> in time (see  #$temporallyIntersects); but they will intersect if (e.g.) <code>FIRSTTHING</code>  is temporally continuous (see #$TemporallyContinuousThing).")
(comment relationAllAll-Different "<code>(#$relationAllAll-Different PRED TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> means that for every instance, <code>INS1</code>, of <code>TYPE-1</code> and for every instance of <code>TYPE-2</code>, <code>INS2</code>, such that <code>(#$different INS1 INS2)</code>, <code>(PRED INS1 INS2)</code> holds.")
(comment TrivialityContext "The collection of #$DeclarativeContexts that contain knowledge about what a type of #$IntelligentAgent or individual #$IntelligentAgent considers trivial, in the sense of obviously or unquestionably true.")
(comment trivialityContextForIndividual "<code>(#$trivialityContextForIndividual IND CONTEXT)</code> means that <code>CONTEXT</code> is the <code>#$TrivialityContext</code>  that contains knowledge about what <code>IND</code> considers trivial, in the sense of obviously or unquestionably true.")
(comment trivialityContextForType "<code>(#$trivialityContextForType TYPE CONTEXT)</code> means that <code>CONTEXT</code> is the <code>#$TrivialityContext</code>  that contains knowledge about what instances of <code>TYPE</code> consider trivial, in the sense of obviously or unquestionably true.")
(comment IrrelevanceContext "The collection of #$DeclarativeContexts that contain knowledge about what a type of #$IntelligentAgent or individual #$IntelligentAgent considers irrelevant, in the sense of arcane or incomprehensible.")
(comment irrelevanceContextForIndividual "<code>(#$irrelevanceContextForIndividual IND CONTEXT)</code> means that <code>CONTEXT</code> is the <code>#$IrrelevanceContext</code> that contains knowledge about what <code>IND</code> considers irrelevant, in the sense of arcane or incomprehensible.")
(comment irrelevanceContextForType "<code>(#$irrelevanceContextForType TYPE CONTEXT)</code> means that <code>CONTEXT</code> is the <code>#$IrrelevanceContext</code> that contains knowledge about what instances of <code>TYPE</code> consider irrelevant, in the sense of arcane or incomprehensible.")
(comment NewYorkSun-Newspaper "An instance of #$NewspaperSeries.")
(comment subSystems "<code>(#$subSystems SUPER SUB)</code> means that <code>SUB</code> isa a part of <code>SUPER</code> that can stand by themselves, i.e. have independent existence and still be more or less the same, e.g. the amp in a stereo system or the console of a computer, or the physical protocol in a layered protocol. However, the handle of a cup would typically not be a considered a subsystem of the cup, for it it were removed, it would cease to be a handle of anything. What qualifies as a subsystem of a larger system is often context dependent.")
(comment Communications-ERInstrumentationSupersystem "An instance of #$EasternRangeInstrumentationSupersystem.  The purpose of Communications is to provide the extensive communication infrastructure required by the ER for normal operation.")
(comment properSubSystems "A specialization of #$subSystems and #$properParts (qq.v.). <code>(#$properSubSystems SUPER SUB)</code> means that <code>SUB</code> is a system that is part of the larger system, <code>SUPER</code>, can stand by itself, i.e. have independent existence from <code>SUPER</code> and still be more or less the same. Eg. the amp in a stereo system or the console of a computer. However, the handle of a cup would not typically be considered a subsystem.")
(comment MajorCommandOfUSAirForce "A specialization of #$UnitedStatesMilitaryOrganization.  Each instance of #$MajorCommandOfUSAirForce is one of the major commands of the #$UnitedStatesAirForce.")
(comment AirForceSpaceCommand-US "Air Force Space Command is a major command of the United States Air Force (see #$MajorCommandOfUSAirForce) with headquarters at Peterson Air Force Base, Colorado (see #$AFBase-Peterson-Grounds-Colorado).")
(comment AirForceBase-US-Grounds "A subcollection of #$AirForceBase-Grounds; each is controlled by #$UnitedStatesAirForce.")
(comment NumberedAirForce-US "A specialization of #$UnitedStatesMilitaryOrganization. Each instance of #$NumberedAirForce-US is one of the numbered air forces of the #$UnitedStatesAirForce.")
(disjointWith MajorCommandOfUSAirForce NumberedAirForce-US)
(comment SatelliteNavigationSystem-Global "A specialization of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$SatelliteNavigationSystem-Global is a satellite navigation system with global coverage.")
(comment GPSReceiver "A specialization of #$SatelliteReceiver.  Each instance of #$GPSReceiver  The collection of navigational products that use the #$GlobalPositioningSystem in determining the position of the user on earth. These devices are composed of an antenna tuned to the frequencies transmitted by the GPS satellites, receiver-processors and a highly-stable clock. They may also include a display for providing location and speed information to the user.")
(comment NavigationDevice "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$NavigationDevice is a device used for #$Navigating, i.e., for taking the bearings and plotting the course of someone or something travelling -- often in some transportation device -- through some medium.  Notable specializations of #$NavigationDevice include #$Sextant, #$Compass and #$GPSReceiver.")
(comment NavigationBeacon "A specialization of #$NavigationDevice.  Each instance of #$NavigationBeacon is fixed artifact on or near the #$EarthsTopographicSurface that  provides a geodetic reference point for the navigation of airborne, seafaring, land-based, or orbiting transportation.")
(comment SatelliteTransmission-Uplink "The collection of events in which a #$SatelliteTransmitter located
at a #$SatelliteEarthStation sends a #$SatelliteTransmission via 
#$MicrowaveRadiation to a #$CommunicationsSatellite in orbit around
the Earth.  In order to be able to transmit signals to an orbiting
satellite, the #$SatelliteEarthStation must be located in the 
#$GeographicalFootprint of the #$CommunicationsSatellite.")
(comment SatelliteTransmission-Downlink "The collection of events in which a #$SatelliteTransmitter located
on a #$CommunicationsSatellite orbiting the Earth sends a 
#$SatelliteTransmission via
#$MicrowaveRadiation to a #$SatelliteEarthStation on Earth located
within the #$GeographicalFootprint of the #$CommunicationsSatellite.")
(comment NavigationSatellite "A specialization of #$Satellite-Device.  Each instance of #$NavigationSatellite is a satellite used as part of a #$SatelliteNavigationSystem.")
(comment GPSSatellite "A specialization of #$NavigationSatellite.  Each instance of #$GPSSatellite is a satellite used as part of the #$GlobalPositioningSystem.")
(comment GPSSatelliteTransmission-Downlink "A specialization of #$SatelliteTransmission-Downlink.  Each instance of #$GPSSatelliteTransmission-Downlink is an event in which a transmitter on a #$GPSSatellite orbiting the Earth sends a transmission toward the Earth.")
(comment SatelliteNavigationSystem "A specialization of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$SatelliteNavigationSystem is a range of satellites that transmit signal which allow small electronic receivers to determine their locations.")
(comment USAirForceStaffAgency "The collection of US Air Force staff agencies.  Each instance is an organization with a particular focused set of responsibilities, often at a level below that of e.g. a wing (see #$USAirForceWing).")
(comment KMFOWLInstance "The collection of Skolemized entities that are the subjects and members of the KMF OWL classes in the KMF triple store.")
(comment KMFOWLClass "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$KMFOWLClass is a collection that corresponds to one of the classes in the KMF OWL ontology.")
(comment ruleConclusionsTrivial "<code>(#$ruleConclusionsTrivial RULE)</code> means that anything concluded from RULE is obvious -- seemingly tautologous or nearly so.")
(comment KMFOWLProperty "The collection of binary predicates that correspond to the KMF OWL properties.")
(comment KMFOWLPropertyTypeByArg2Isa "A faceting collection for #$KMFOWLProperty.  Each instance of this collection is a specialization of #$KMFOWLProperty with a specific notable #$arg2Isa constraint.")
(comment KMFOWLProperty-RelationToString "A specialization of #$KMFOWLProperty (q.v.).  Each instance of #$KMFOWLProperty-RelationToString is a binary relation that corresponds to a KMF OWL property whose arg2 constraint is a specialization of #$CharacterString.")
(comment KMFOWLProperty-RelationToBoolean "A specialization of KMFOWLProperty (q.v.). Each instance of KMFOWLProperty-RelationToString is a binary relation that corresponds to a KMF OWL property whose arg2 constraint is a specialization of #$TruthValue.")
(comment KMFOWLProperty-RelationToScalarPointValue "A specialization of KMFOWLProperty (q.v.). Each instance of KMFOWLProperty-RelationToString is a binary relation that corresponds to a KMF OWL property whose arg2 constraint is a specialization of #$ScalarPointValue.")
(comment KMFOWLProperty-RelationToKMFOWLInstance "A specialization of KMFOWLProperty (q.v.). Each instance of KMFOWLProperty-RelationToString is a binary relation that corresponds to a KMF OWL property whose arg2 constraint is a collection that is an instance of #$KMFOWLClass.")
(comment rangeStations "<code>(#$rangeStations RANGE SITE)</code> means that <code>SITE</code> is a station for the rocket range, <code>RANGE</code>.")
(comment rangeLaunchStations "<code>(#$rangeLaunchStations
 RANGE SITE)</code> means that <code>SITE</code> is a rocket launch station for the rocket range, <code>RANGE</code>.")
(comment properlyGeographicallySubsumes "<code>(#$properlyGeographicallySubsumes GEO-THING-1 GEO-THING-2)</code> holds just in case either of the following hold:
<p>
(1) <code>GEO-THING-1</code> has as a #$properGeographicalSubRegions either <code>GEO-THING-2</code> or the territory (c.f. #$territoryOf) of <code>GEO-THING-2</code>.
<p>
(2) <code>GEO-THING-1</code> has as a #$geopoliticalSubdivision <code>GEO-THING-2</code> or the territory of <code>GEO-THING-1</code> has as a #$properGeographicalSubRegions <code>GEO-THING-2<</code>.
<p>
An example of this relation holding from case (1) would be (#$properlyGeographicallySubsumes #$NorthernHemisphere-Region #$Israel). An example of this relation holding from case (2) would be (#$properlyGeographicallySubsumes #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$MississippiRiver).")
(comment coastlineOf "<code>(#$coastlineOf GEO-THING COAST)</code> means that <code>COAST</code> is the entire coastline of <code>GEO-THING</code>.")
(comment properGeographicalSubRegions "<code>(#$properGeographicalSubRegions SUPER SUB)</code> means that <code>SUPER</code> and <code>SUB</code> are both elements of #$GeographicalRegion, the area <code>SUB</code> lies wholly within the region <code>SUPER</code> (see #$inRegion), and <code>SUPER</code> is different from <code>SUB</code>.  <code>SUPER</code> may or may not completely surround <code>SUB</code>, as they may share an outer boundary (e.g., the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica and  #$Texas-State in the #$WorldGeographyDualistMt).   Note that, if either argument to #$geographicalSubRegions is an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity, the assertion must be made in #$WorldGeographyDualistMt or a more specialized microtheory.   To relate two instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity, use the predicate #$geopoliticalSubdivision, if it applies.  See also #$surroundsHorizontally and #$bordersOn.")
(comment geographicalSubRegionTypes "<code>(#$geographicalSubRegionTypes REGION-TYPE SUBREGION-TYPE)</code> means that every geographical region, or feature that is an instance of the collection <code>REGION-TYPE</code>, has at least one geographical subregion (via #$geographicalSubRegions) which is an instance of the collection <code>SUBREGION-TYPE</code>.  For example, \"every mountain has a summit\" may be expressed as (#$geographicalSubRegionTypes #$Mountain #$Summit).")
(comment properGeographicalSubRegionTypes "<code>(#$properGeographicalSubRegionTypes REGION-TYPE SUBREGION-TYPE)</code> means that every geographical region, or feature that is an instance of the collection <code>REGION-TYPE</code>, has at least one proper geographical subregion (via #$properGeographicalSubRegions) which is an instance of the collection <code>SUBREGION-TYPE</code>.  For example, \"every mountain has a summit\" may be expressed as (#$properGeographicalSubRegionTypes #$Mountain #$Summit).")
(comment properPhysicalPartTypes "A #$RuleMacroPredicate and a specialization of #$physicalPartTypes.  Where <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code> are both specializations of #$PartiallyTangible, <code>(#$properPhysicalPartTypes TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> has an instance of <code>TYPE2</code> as a proper physical part.  For example, (#$properPhysicalPartTypes #$RoseBouquet #$RoseFlower).
<p>
Most assertions with #$properPhysicalPartTypes are default true, because it is generally possible for some instances of a collection to lack parts of a type that most instances of that collection always have.  For example, (#$properPhysicalPartTypes #$Finger #$Fingernail) is default true, even though a some fingers might lack fingernails as parts.
<p>
Cf. #$normalWholeTypeForPartType, which is used to relate typical part types to the whole types of which they are ordinarily parts.")
(comment projectSeedlings "<code>(#$projectSeedlings PROJECT SEEDLING)</code> means that the instance <code>SEEDLING</code> of #$Project was a seedling effort done to support the successful launch of the project <code>PROJECT</code>.")
(comment resourceTypeRequiredForSituationType "#$resourceTypeRequiredForSituationType is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. (#$resourceTypeRequiredForSituationType THING-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means that, in the context of the assertion, instances of SIT-TYPE require some instance of THING-TYPE in order to occur.")
(comment AtlasIIRocket "A specialization of #$AtlasRocket. The maiden flight of an Atlas II rocket was on December 7, 1991, and the last flight of an Atlas II was on August 31, 2004.")
(comment MilitaryEvent "The collection of all military events, including #$War, #$Battles, #$Explosions, and military #$Training.  Note that these events need not be organized or planned, just connected to the military in some way.")
(comment MilitarySpaceLaunchOperation "A specialization of #$MilitaryOperation. Each instance of #$MilitarySpaceLaunchOperation is a complex event during which a military organization prepares a rocket (see #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice) and rocket-supporting systems (e.g. a #$RocketRange) for transportation in outer space (see #$SpaceTransportationEvent).  Each instance involves preparation events, and, in those cases where the prepartation events are successful, a rocket launch (see #$LaunchingARocket).  Each instance that involves a rocket launch also involves additional post-launch events, during which the rocket travels toward outer space and is tracked by facilities at the stations on the launch site's rocket range.  Completely succesful instances of this collection terminate when the launch vehicle no longer needs to be tracked by the launching agent, for example when the launch vehicle for the spaceflight has been expended or has safely landed at its destination.")
(comment companyQuarterlyEarnings "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation, <code>(#$companyQuarterlyEarnings COMPANY AMOUNT)</code><T> means that at the calendar quarter T (but not necessarily at any proper sub-interval of T), the earnings of the company <code>COMPANY</code> are <code>AMOUNT</code>, an instance of #$MonetaryValue.  The earnings of a company are arrived at by subtracting certain expenses and taxes from revenues.  As such, #$companyQuarterlyEarnings is #$netIncome as applied to instances of #$Business.  This sense of \"earnings\" can be contrasted to the related notion of \"earnings\" as applied to individual people, which refers to the money (typically, the gross) earned through employment or investments.")
(comment contextOfPCWInterpretation "A #$FunctionalPredicate that relates conceptual works, agents that interpret them, and a time to the propositions that are in the interpretations. <tt>(#$contextOfPCWInterpretation PCW CONTEXT AGENT TIME)</tt> means that CONTEXT is the context that contains all the propositions endorsed by AGENT on the record (and their closure) at TIME as part of the inteprpretation of PCW.")
(comment ContextOfPCWInterpretationFn "A ternary function that returns an instance of #$Microtheory when given a #$PropositionalConceptualWork, an #$IntelligentAgent, and a time interval as arguments. (#$ContextOfPCWInterpretationFn PCW AGENT TIME) denotes the microtheory containing the propositions (and their upward closure) that AGENT goes on the record at TIME as claiming that PCW contains.  Essentially, it is the the interpretation by AGENT of PCW at TIME, or at least the portion of the interpretation that AGENT is willing claim.")
(comment Festival "The collection of large, organized and festive social gatherings.  Festivals often involve leisurely activities such as dancing, drinking, eating, and listening to or making music.  This collection includes   traditional, community-wide #$Party-Celebrations commemorating events or times of special religious or other historical significance.")
(comment attemptsToDoActType "<code>(#$attemptsToDoActType ATTEMPTS ACT-TYPE)</code> means that <code>ATTEMPTS</code> is the collection of attempts to do acts of type <code>ACT-TYPE</code>.  Note that while some attempts are failures, some may be successful, so that <code>ATTEMPTS</code> and <code>ACT-TYPE</code> are not necessarily disjoint.")
(comment PreparingForSitTypeFn "<code>(#$PreparingForSitTypeFn SITTYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$PreparingForSituation that are preparings for instances of <code>SITTYPE</code> (which is itself some specialization of #$Situation). For example,  (#$PreparingForSitTypeFn #$VacationTrip) denotes the collection of all actions of preparing for a vacation trip.")
(comment refrainingsFromSituationType "<code>(#$refrainingsFromSituationType SITTYPE REFRAINS)</code> means that <code>REFRAINS</code> is the collection of refrainings from instances of <code>SITTYPE</code>.")
(comment preparationsForSituationType "<code>(#$preparationsForSituationType SITTYPE PREPS)</code> means that <code>PREPS</code> is the collection of preparations for instances of <code>SITTYPE</code>.")
(comment RocketLaunchOperation "The collection of events in which rockets and systems supporting rocket flight are prepared for a launch; in cases where the launch is successful, instances of this collection involve rocket launches and monitored portions of the rocket flight as well.")
(comment intendedRocketFlightAzimuth "<code>(#$intendedRocketFlightAzimuth LAUNCH-OP DIRECTION)</code> means that <code>DIRECTION</code> is the intended direction in which the rocket launched during <code>LAUNCH-OP</code> will fly.")
(comment AtlasVLaunchOperation08012008Mt "A microtheory to contain information about #$AtlasVLaunchOperation08012008.")
(comment AtlasVLaunchOperation08012008 "An example instance of #$MilitarySpaceLaunchOperation involving an #$AtlasVRocket intended to be launched on January 8, 2008.")
(comment rangeRequired "<code>(#$rangeRequired LAUNCH-OP RANGE)</code> means that <code>RANGE</code> is the range required to be involved in monitoring the flight of the rocket launched in <code>LAUNCH-OP</code>.")
(comment focalRocketOfLaunchOperation "<code>(#$focalRocketOfLaunchOperation LAUNCH-OP ROCKET)</code> means that <code>ROCKET</code> is the focal rocket involved in <code>LAUNCH-OP</code>.")
(comment DecisionSupport-InferenceTest "The collection of reified inference tests for the Decision Support project.")
(comment rangeStationRequired "<code>(#$rangeStationRequired LAUNCH-OP STATION)</code> means that <code>STATION</code> is one of the range stations required to be involved in monitoring the down-range flight of the rocket launched in <code>LAUNCH-OP</code>.")
(comment easternRangeDesignator "<code>(#$easternRangeDesignator DEV ID)</code> means that <code>ID</code> is the ERD for <code>DEV</code>.  Each ERD identification string has a field that references, in order, each of the supersystem, station, facility and specific system, with a backslash seaprating each of those fields.")
(comment DegreeOfRangeNecessity "A specialization of #$ScalarQuantity.  Each instance of #$DegreeOfRangeNecessity is a quantity of necessity for a launch that can be attributed to a range component.")
(comment rangeSystemRequiredToDegreeForLaunchOperation "<code>(#$rangeSystemRequiredToDegreeForLaunchOperation SYSTEM LAUNCH-OP DEGREE)</code> means that <code>SYSTEM</code> is required to <code>DEGREE</code> for <code>LAUNCH-OP</code>,")
(comment primaryRangeUser "<code>(#$primaryRangeUser RANGE AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is a primary user of <code>RANGE</code>, in the sense that  <code>AGENT</code> is responsible for overseeing the rocket launches using <code>RANGE</code>.")
(comment LiquifiedPetroleumGas "Each instance of this collection is some amount of #$NaturalGas that has been liquified.")
(comment MooringBuoy "The collection of all #$Buoys whose primary function is to serve as anchor points for vessels.")
(comment RadarDetection "A specialization of #$DetectingSomethingPhysical.  Each instance of #$RadarDetection is an event in which a #$RadarDevice is used to detect a physical object.")
(comment RadarDetectionOfERLaunchedRocket "A specialization of #$RadarDetection.  Each instance of #$RadarDetectionOfERLaunchedRocket is an event in which a #$RadarDevice is used to detect a rocket launched over the Eastern Range.")
(comment TelemetryDetection "A specialization of #$DetectingSomethingPhysical.  Each instance of #$TelemetryDetection is an event in which a #$TelemetryDetectionDevice is used to detect a physical object.")
(comment LPGTankerShip "The collection of all instances of #$TankerShip dedicated to transport of #$LiquifiedPetroleumGas.")
(comment ReportingACrimeToALawEnforcementAgent "The collection of all instances of #$StatingSomething in which the #$senderOfInfo makes a statement to a #$LawEnforcementAgent that includes the propositional content that there is a crime pre-existing with respect to the report.")
(comment uniquelyBehaviorCapable "<code>(#$uniquelyBehaviorCapable OBJ SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is the unique object that would be capable (in the sense of #$behaviorCapable (q.v.)) of playing <code>ROLE</code> in any instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>. <code>(#$uniquelyBehaviorCapable OBJ SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> does not imply that <code>OBJ</code> actually can play <code>ROLE</code> in <i>every</i> instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> -- it means only that if anything can play such a role, only <code>OBJ</code> can do so.  However, specific circumstances during some instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> may prevent even <code>OBJ</code>  from playing the role  <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment GivingAnAlarmSignal "The collection of all communicative acts (see #$CommunicationAct-Single) in which an #$AlarmSignal is the primary #$ibtGenerated.")
(comment JumpingOverboardFromAVessel "The collection of all #$Jumping actions in which someone deliberately jumps off a #$Watercraft and into a #$BodyOfWater in which the #$Watercraft is currently floating.")
(comment PortAuthority "The collection of all #$LawEnforcementOrganizations whose areas of jurisdiction are harbors/anchorages and their associated port facilities.  Instances are charged with enforcing maritime law and insuring right-of-way is maintained within the harbor, and also with carrying out some customs-related functions, e.g., inspecting cargo.")
(comment watchOnVessel "A #$BinaryPredicate for identifying who is standing watch on a particular vessel.")
(comment inProgressTerm "(#$inProgressTerm TERM) states that TERM will either be treated as #$retainTerm or #$ephemeralTerm at the KB cleanup step of the build process. Which of these two it is will depend on whether at KB cleanup time, more will be known about the term than just the #$inProgressTerm assertion. The predicate is designed for use by knowledge acquisition tools that have no way of knowing whether a term created during a user interaction will ever be fleshed out by the user.")
(comment infectionCausedByOrganismType "<code>(#$infectionCausedByOrganismType INFECTION-INSTANCE ORGANISM-TYPE)</code> means that the #$Infection <code>INFECTION-INSTANCE</code> is caused by instances of <code>ORGANISM-TYPE</code> (a type of #$Organism-Whole).")
(comment infectingPathogen "<code>(#$infectingPathogen INFECTING PATHOGEN)</code> means that the #$MicroorganismMob <code>PATHOGEN</code> is transmitted from the #$infectingSource in an #$InfectingEvent to the newly infected host, which is the #$infectingActsOn in the <code>INFECTING</code>.")
(comment contaminant "An #$ActorSlot used to identify the contaminants in an instance of #$ContaminationEvent. <code>(#$contaminant CONTAMINATION THING)</code> means that in the #$ContaminationEvent, <code>CONTAMINATION</code>, something is contaminated by <code>THING</code>, an instance of #$PartiallyTangible.")
(comment lengthOfList "This predicate relates a list to its length. <code>(#$lengthOfList LIST N)</code> means that the #$List <code>LIST</code> is a list of exactly <code>N</code> members.  Thus, for example, (#$lengthOfList (#$TheList #$Dog #$Whale) 2) holds.")
(comment cardinality "<code>(#$cardinality SETORCOL N)</code> means that the #$SetOrCollection <code>SETORCOL</code> has <code>N</code> members. For instance, (#$cardinality #$TheEmptySet 0). Note that the concept of cardinality is clearest for finite sets; only in special branches of mathematics does one speak of the cardinality of infinite sets. See also #$extentCardinality and #$groupCardinality.")
(comment setOrCollectionDifference "This is the predicate corresponding to
#$SetOrCollectionDifferenceFn. <code>(#$setOrCollectionDifference SOC1
SOC2 DIFFERENCE)</code> means that <code>DIFFERENCE</code> is the #$SetOrCollection containing all elements of <code>SOC1</code> which are not elements of <code>SOC2</code>.")
(comment SetOrCollectionDifferenceFn "<code>(#$SetOrCollectionDifferenceFn A B)</code> denotes the instance of #$SetOrCollection that is, by definition, the set or collection of things that are elements of <code>A</code>, but not elements of <code>B</code>. ")
(comment Rumen "A specialization of #$InternalOrgan.  Each instance of #$Rumen is an organ which is part of the digestive system (see the collection #$DigestiveSystem) of some ruminant.")
(comment X-Men "The group of #$Superheroes known as \"the X-Men.\"")
(comment ruleRequiredForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$ruleTrivialForJustificationParaphrase RULE)</code> means that when
<code>RULE</code> is used in a transformation proof, a paraphrase of that proof should explicitly mention <code>RULE</code>, as a human would have a hard time reconstructing the line of reasoning without it.")
(comment sentenceTrivialForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$sentenceTrivialForJustificationParaphrase SENTENCE)</code> means
that when <code>SENTENCE</code>, an instance of #$CycLSentence, is used in a
transformation proof, it is deemed trivial. It is unnecessary to
explicitly mention <code>SENTENCE</code> as a support for returned bindings,
because a human would regard it as obvious.")
(comment ruleHighlyRelevantForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$ruleTrivialForJustificationParaphrase RULE)</code> means that when <code>RULE</code> is used in a transformation proof, a paraphrase of that proof should explicitly mention <code>RULE</code>, and that paraphrase should print the rule in a manner that emphasizes the rule (e.g by printing the rule in bold or italic).")
(comment sentenceRequiredForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$sentenceRequiredForJustificationParaphrase SENT)</code> means that when <code>SENT</code> is used in a transformation proof, a paraphrase of that proof should explicitly mention <code>SENT</code>.).")
(comment sentenceHighlyRelevantForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$sentenceHighlyRelevantForJustificationParaphrase SENT)</code> means that when <code>SENT</code> is used in a transformation proof, a paraphrase of that proof should explicitly mention <code>SENT</code>, and that paraphrase should print the sentence in a manner that emphasizes the sentence (e.g by printing the sentence in bold or italic.).")
(comment assertionTrivialForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$assertionTrivialForJustificationParaphrase ASSERTION)</code> means
that when <code>ASSERTION</code>, an instance of #$CycLAssertion, is used in a
transformation proof, it is deemed trivial. It is unnecessary to
explicitly mention <code>ASSERTION</code> as a support for returned bindings,
because a human would regard it as obvious.")
(comment objectRequiresNCapabilitiesOfTypeToSupportRoleInType "<code>(#$objectRequiresNCapabilitiesOfTypeToSupportRoleInType OBJ N SET EVENT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> requires other systems to provide at least <code>N</code> many of the capabilities in the set <code>SET</code> in order itself to play the role <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised "<code>(#$behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised OBJ SITTYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is incapable of playing <code>ROLE</code> in any instance of <code>SITTYPE</code>, as a consequence of malfunctioning or being a defective instance of its type. Thus, <code>(#$behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised EddieTheAdultEagle #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)</code> means that <code>EddieTheAdultEagle</code> is incapable of flying, though this must be due to some particular thing being wrong with Eddie, since it is generally true that <code>((#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$Eagle #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)</code> . Cf. #$behaviorIncapable and #$functionalityCompromised.")
(comment Aardvark "A specialization of #$Mammal.  Aardvarks are medium-sized mammals native to Africa. Their name comes from Afrikaans for \"earth pig\".")
(comment startsDurationAfterEndingOf "A ternary #$TemporalPredicate that is used to state how long one #$TemporalThing starts after another ends.  <code>(#$startsDurationAfterEndingOf AFTER TIME BEFORE)</code> means that <code>AFTER</code> starts duration <code>TIME</code> after <code>BEFORE</code> ends.  That is, the #$startingPoint (q.v.) of <code>AFTER</code> is after the #$endingPoint (q.v.) of <code>BEFORE</code>, by an interval of #$Time-Quantity <code>TIME</code>.
<p>
See also #$startsAfterEndingOf and #$startsDurationAfterStartingOf.")
(comment startsDurationAfterStartingOf "A ternary #$TemporalPredicate that is used to state how long one #$TemporalThing starts after another starts.  <code>(#$startsDurationAfterStartingOf AFTER TIME BEFORE)</code> means that <code>AFTER</code> starts duration <code>TIME</code> after <code>BEFORE</code> starts.  That is, the #$startingPoint (q.v.) of <code>AFTER</code> is after the starting point of <code>BEFORE</code>, by an interval of #$Time-Quantity <code>TIME</code>.
<p>
See also #$startsAfterStartingOf and #$startsDurationAfterEndingOf.")
(comment startsDurationAfterStartOfInSituationType "<code>(#$startsDurationAfterStartOfInSituationType SIT-TYPE AFTER-TYPE TIME BEFORE-TYPE)</code> means that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$Situation), if instances <code>AFTER</code> and <code>BEFORE</code> of <code>AFTER-TYPE</code> and <code>BEFORE-TYPE</code> occur as subsituations, then <code>AFTER</code> starts <code>TIME</code> after <code>BEFORE</code> starts.")
(comment endsDurationAfterStartOfInSituationType "<code>(#$endsDurationAfterStartOfInSituationType SIT-TYPE AFTER-TYPE TIME BEFORE-TYPE)</code> means that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$Situation), if instances <code>AFTER</code> and <code>BEFORE</code> of <code>AFTER-TYPE</code> and <code>BEFORE-TYPE</code> occur as subsituations, then <code>AFTER</code> ends <code>TIME</code> after <code>BEFORE</code> starts.")
(comment |owl:Ontology| "The collection of all ontologies represented in #$OWL-WebOntologyLanguage.")
(comment SWEETOntology "A collection of ontologies that are part of the Semantic Web for Earth and Environmental Terminology (SWEET).")
(comment TanningSalon "A localized (one site) commercial organization where customers can get an accelerated sun tan (e.g. by spraying or using tanning beds.")
(comment launchFromERHasStationCompromisedWRTCapability "<code>(#$launchFromERHasStationCompromisedWRTCapability OP FACILITY FUNC-TYPE)</code> means that the rocket launch operation <code>OP</code> involves a range station <code>FACILITY</code> whose functionality, <code>FUNC-TYPE</code> is compromised in a manner that impacts the implementation of <code>OP</code>.")
(comment knowsAbout "<code>(#$knowsAbout AGENT THING)</code> means that the #$IntelligentAgent <code>AGENT</code> knows something about <code>THING</code>.  This predicate represents more than simple awareness, but exactly what is known -- the content of <code>AGENT</code>'s knowledge about <code>THING</code> -- is not specified.  For example, (#$knowsAbout #$MichaelJordan #$Basketball-TheGame).
<p> 
Note: many commonsense rules can conclude <code>(#$knowsAbout AGENT THING)</code> -- e.g., those having to do with <code>AGENT</code>'s occupation, college degrees, city of residence,... in fact, almost any assertion about <code>AGENT</code> can lead to presumptions that he/she probably #$knowsAbout something.  #$knowsAbout in turn can serve (weakly) in arguments about whether or not <code>AGENT</code> #$knows (q.v.) specific common assertions involving <code>THING</code>, and in arguments about whether or not <code>AGENT</code> #$knowsValue (q.v.) of some particular predicate applied to <code>THING</code>, etc.  See also #$expertRegarding.")
(comment OWLOntologyFn "An instance of #$ReifiableFunction. Given an #$OWLOntology -denoting #$UniformResourceIdentifier as its single argument, #$OWLOntologyFn returns the corresponding ontology term.")
(comment owlOntologyURI "A predicate relating an imported #$OWLOntology with its URI.")
(comment NailSalon "A localized (one site) commercial organization where customers can get a manicure (i.e., nails trimmed and polished.")
(comment repairTypeOfType "<code>(#$repairTypeOfType OBJ-TYPE REPAIR-TYPE)</code> means that <code>REPAIR-TYPE</code> is the collection of events in which <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> is repaired.")
(comment Sucralose "An artificial sweetening agent used in soft drinks and other prepared foods.")
(comment OfficeOfAChiefOfSafety "The 45th and 30th Space Wings (#$FortyFifthSpaceWing and #$ThirtiethSpaceWing, respectively) feature several offices reporting to the officers serving those organizations in the capacity of #$chiefOfAirWingSafety.  Offices include Mission Flight Control, Operations Support and Analysis, Systems Saftey, and Operations Safety.")
(comment MaxQuantValueFn "<code>(#$MaxQuantValueFn QUANTITY)</code> returns a point value which is the maximal quantity that is subsumed by <code>QUANTITY</code>.  For example, (#$MaxQuantValueFn (#$Meter 2 5)) returns (#$Meter 5).  See also #$MinQuantValueFn.")
(comment MinRangeFn "An instance of both #$VariableArityRelation and #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to instances <code>QUANTITY1</code>, ..., <code>QUANTITYN</code>  of #$ScalarInterval, #$MinRangeFn yields an instance of #$ScalarInterval that is the largest interval subsumed by each of <code>QUANTITY1</code> through <code>QUANTITYN</code>.  
<p>
For example, (#$MinRangeFn  (#$Meter 1 3) (#$Meter 2 4)) is (#$Meter 2 3). 
<p>
Note that if one of the instances <code>QUANTITY1</code>, ..., <code>QUANTITYN</code> fails to intersect with at least one of the other instances, then the result of applying #$MinRangeFn to <code>QUANTITY1</code>, ..., <code>QUANTITYN</code> is undefined (for example, both (#$MinRangeFn (#$Meter 1 1.5) (#$Meter 2 4) (#$Meter 0 5)) and (#$MinRangeFn (#$SecondsDuration 3 5) (#$Meter 1 4)) are undefined).  See also #$MaxRangeFn.")
(comment DateBeforeFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction. When applied to an instance <code>DATE</code> of #$Date and an instance <code>DUR</code> of #$Time-Quantity, #$DateBeforeFn returns the instance of #$Date which is <code>DUR</code> amount of time (truncated to the resolution of <code>DATE</code>) before <code>DATE</code>. 
<p>
For example, (#$DateBeforeFn (#$YearFn 1950) (#$DecadesDuration 1)) is (#$YearFn 1940) and (#$DateBeforeFn (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1950))) (#$HoursDuration 23)) is still (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1950))). See also #$DateAfterFn, #$TimeElapsedFn.")
(comment DateAfterFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance <code>DATE</code> of #$Date and an instance <code>DUR</code> of #$Time-Quantity, #$DateAfterFn returns the instance of #$Date which has the same duration as <code>DATE</code> and is <code>DUR</code> amount of time after the end of <code>DATE</code> (with the starting time truncated to the resolution of <code>DATE</code>).  
<p>
For example, (#$DateAfterFn (#$YearFn 1950) (#$DecadesDuration 1)) is (#$YearFn 1961), (#$DateAfterFn (#$YearFn 1950) (#$MonthsDuration 1)) is (#$YearFn 1951), and  (#$DateAfterFn (#$DayFn 31 (#$MonthFn #$December (#$YearFn 1999))) (#$HoursDuration 47)) is (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 2000)))  See also #$DateBeforeFn, #$TimeElapsedFn.")
(comment behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised-WithRoot "<code>(#$behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised OBJ SITTYPE ROLE ROOT)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is incapable of playing <code>ROLE</code> in any instance of <code>SITTYPE</code>, as a consequence of malfunctioning or being a defective instance of its type due to the further malfunctioning of <code>ROOT</code>, which provides critical sub-functionality for <code>OBJ</code>. Thus, <code>(#$behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised EddieTheAdultEagle #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy EddiesLeftWing)</code> means that <code>EddieTheAdultEagle</code> is incapable of flying due to some particular thing being wrong with Eddie's left wing, whereas it is generally true that <code>((#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$Eagle #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)</code> . Cf. #$behaviorIncapable and #$functionalityCompromised.")
(comment launchFromERHasStationCompromisedWRTCapability-WithRoot "<code>(#$launchFromERHasStationCompromisedWRTCapability OP FACILITY FUNC-TYPE OBJ)</code> means that the rocket launch operation <code>OP</code> involves a range station <code>FACILITY</code> whose functionality, <code>FUNC-TYPE</code> is compromised in a manner that impacts the implementation of <code>OP</code>, due to a problem with <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment scheduledStartDateOfSitOfTypeInScriptedSitOfType "<code>(#$scheduledStartDateOfSitOfTypeInScriptedSitOfType
SUB-SIT-TYPE SIT SIT-TYPE SCHED-DATE)</code> means that 
<code>SCHED-DATE</code> is the date that an instance <code>INST</code> of <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> is scheduled to occur, at which time <code>INST</code> will be a sub-situation of <code>SIT</code>, which is itself an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> that has <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> as at least a candidate sub-situation type (see #$candidateSubSituationTypes).")
(comment situationRequiresRepairOfObjToStartByDateForFutureStageOfType "<code>(#$situationRequiresRepairOfObjToStartByDateForFutureStageOfType SIT OBJ DATE FUTURE-SIT-TYPE)</code> means that in order to have an instance of <code>FUTURE-SIT-TYPE</code> occur as a sub-situation of <code>SIT</code>, repair of <code>OBJ</code> must start by <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment TermFromOntologyFn "(#$TermFromOntologyFn ONTOLOGY) denotes the collection of terms created for the mapping of ONTOLOGY into Cyc. Many instances are special case terms that closely correspond to the OWL classes and properties. Those special case terms that prove generally useful may be renamed and made available for general use.")
(comment launchSpaceLiftCommander "(#$launchSpaceLiftCommander LAUNCH PERSON) means that on the day of LAUNCH, PERSON exercises final decision authority over the launch wing with controlling authority (see #$controllingLaunchAuthority-USAF over LAUNCH.  Responsibilities include approval to proceed with countdown and final clear to launch prior to liftoff.  The player of this role is accountable for public safety during the launch, and, in the event the mission is for the DOD, for the mission's success or failure.")
(comment launchOperationsDirector "(#$launchOperationsDirector LAUNCH PERSON) means that on the day of LAUNCH, PERSON is responsible for coordinating and executing Range countdown operations.  Based on overall range operational readiness, the #$launchOperationsDirector makes a go/no-go recommendation to the #$launchSpaceLiftCommander.")
(comment launchRangeOperationsCommander "(#$launchRangeOperationsCommander LAUNCH PERSON) means that on the day of LAUNCH, PERSON is responsible for providing command and control of range operations capability, and for passing operations-related information to the SLCC and OD.  Here 'operations related' is defined as anything that affects range operations and safety capability.  The #$launchRangeOperationsCommander also provides go/no-go status for the range to the #$launchOperationsDirector.")
(comment launchRangeControlOfficer "(#$launchRangeControlOfficer LAUNCH PERSON) means that PERSON is the focal point of communications between the launch range and user during the countdown for LAUNCH.  This responsibility includes coordinating instrumentation configuration and testing and associated anomaly resolution activities with technical contracts.  The #$launchRangeControlOfficer also recommends changes to the range operations capability to the #$launchRangeOperationsCommander, and notifies the #$seniorMissionFlightControlOfficer of any range status changes.  Responsibility for determining range capability is delegated to the #$launchRangeControlOfficer when the #$launchRangeOperationsCommander is not on console.  Also, the #$launchRangeControlOfficer relays the range clear to launch to the launch agency.")
(comment launchAerospaceControlOfficer "(#$launchAerospaceControlOfficer LAUNCH PERSON) means that during LAUNCH, PERSON is responsible for monitoring the status of aircraft in and around the launch restricted area for the launch range, insures that support aircraft are at pre-planned mission support positions prior to liftoff, and reports activity status and recommends final go/no-go to the #$seniorMissionFlightControlOfficer and #$launchRangeOperationsCommander.  Also, when a #$missionFlightControlOfficer issues an order that 'break away' instructions be sent to a support aircraft, the #$launchAerospaceControlOfficer directs the flight radar unit to relay these instructions.")
(comment launchMissionDirector "")
(comment launch_AFLD-AFSD "(#$launch_AFLD-AFSD LAUNCH PERSON) means that  PERSON manages Air Force and contractor team activities to ensure all booster, spacecraft and facility systems are ready for launch.  'AFLD' stands for 'Air Force Launch Director' and 'AFSD' for 'Air Force Site Director':  the two positions are ordinarily held concurrently and combined into one role.")
(comment MalfunctionTypeByActionTypeCompromised "This type level collection defines a covering on #$Malfunction.  Each instance of #$MalfunctionTypeByActionTypeCompromised is a collection of instances of #$Malfunction, such that every instance of the collection compromises the same kind of activity on the part of the system experiencing the #$Malfunction in question.")
(comment MalfunctionOfTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$MalfunctionOfTypeFn ?ACTION-TYPE) denotes the class of all instances of #$Malfunction in which the system experiencing the #$Malfunction is prevented from playing an #$instrumentalRole in activities of type ?ACTION-TYPE.")
(comment actionTypeCompromisedByMalfunctionType "The canonical corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$MalfunctionOfTypeFn, reified to avoid the phenomenon of 'skipping the predicate' in some important inference paths.")
(comment malfunctionAffectsSitType "A very general predicate:  (#$malfunctionAffectsSitType MALFUNCTION SIT-TYPE) means that the fact of MALFUNCTION's occurrence either prevents a relevant instance of SIT-TYPE from happening absent corrective action, or at least bears on the outcome of one or more instances of SIT-TYPE in such a way that said instance or instances will be 'unsuccessful' unless corrective action is taken.")
(comment LexicalMappingStrength "Formality attributes apply to individual word senses of words or phrases.")
(comment PrimaryLexicalMapping "Interpretations of words or phrases which are considered to be primary mappings. A mapping is a primary mapping the phrase would be expected to evoke the concept out of context.  Some words and phrases can have more than one primary mapping (e.g. 'bat' means either baseball bat or the flying mammal), but most words have only one primary mapping.  If a meaning is only evoked with the help of contextual clues, it should not be a #$PrimaryLexicalMapping, but is instead one of the other instances of #$LexicalMappingStrength.")
(comment ContextuallyDependentLexicalMapping "Interpretations of words or phrases which are only evoked by contextual clues.  For example, the phrase 'Utah' means, acontextually, #$Utah-State, but can mean #$UtahJazz in a basketball context.  Thus, the mapping from 'Utah' to #$UtahJazz is a #$ContextuallyDependentLexicalMapping.")
(comment VanishinglyRareLexicalMapping "Interpretations of words or phrases which are extremely rare, such as the mapping from 'A' to #$Adenine-Base.  In practice, this will likely only be used on phrases that are extremely common and regularly misunderstood by #$Cyc.")
(comment strengthOfLexicalMapping "(#$strengthOfLexicalMapping ASRTN STRENGTH) means that the lexical mapping in the #$CycLNLSemanticAssertion ASRTN has the strength STRENGTH.")
(comment currentStageOfTypeInScriptedSitOfType "<code>(#$currentStageOfTypeInScriptedSitOfType SUB-SIT SUB-SIT-TYPE SIT SIT-TYPE)</code> means that:
<br>
(1) <code>SUB-SIT</code> is the currently occurring situation which is a sub-situation of <code>SIT</code>;
<br>
(2) <code>SIT</code> is of the type <code>SIT-TYPE</code>;
<br>
(3) <code>SUB-SIT</code> is of the type <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code>; and
<br>
(3) <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> is at least a candidate sub-situation type (see #$candidateSubSituationTypes) of <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment fieldEncodingOverrideForComparisonOperatorArg "This predicate defines how a logical field in a logical schema is interpreted and given a physical value in a corresponding physical schema when a specified value appears in a specific comparison predicate argument position.  This overrides the default behavior of assuming that a comparison predicate uses the same encoding for each argument and that when one argument is bound it can use the variable in the other to find a relevant meaning sentecen and logical field indexical with an encoding.")
(comment Endarterectomy-SurgicalProcedure "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$Endarterectomy-SurgicalProcedure is a surgical procedure performed in order to remove the atheromatous plaque in the lining of an artery. When this removal is performed as an endovascular procedure through a catheter it is called an \"atherectomy\".")
(comment Euro "The official currency of the Eurozone, which as of 2007, consists of the European states of Austria, Belgium, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Portugal, Slovenia, and Spain.")
(comment currencyCode "<code>(#$currencyCode UNIT CODE)</code> means that the ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the currency <code>UNIT</code> is <code>CODE</code>.")
(comment TravelAndTourismConceptFilter "An instance of #$ConceptFilter specifically designed to return only those concepts likely to be generally useful in the travel and tourism domain.")
(comment PatientIDString "A subcollection of #$UniqueID, each instance of this collection is an ID string that identified a medical patient in a medical record.")
(comment conditionsCommonlyCooccur "(#$conditionsCommonlyCooccur INDEP DEP) means that if someone has a case of INDEP, it would not be surprised for a case of DEP to cooccur.  In some cases, this relation holds in both direction (e.g. both (#$conditionsCommonlyCooccur X Y) and (#$conditionsCommonlyCooccur Y X) might be true), but that is by no means required.")
(comment dateOfEvent-CAE "(#$dateOfEvent-CAE EVT DATE) means that EVT happens during DATE.  This entails that DATE temporally subsumes (either properly or not) EVT.")
(comment termExpansionExpected "(#$termExpansionExpected TERM) indicates that assertions using TERM should be expanded into any and all possible component meanings.  For example, (#$isa #$HafezAlAssad (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn #$Person #$president #$Syria)) would be 'expanded' into (#$president #$Syria #$HafezAlAssad).  Typically, this expansion will happen via rules in the KB, but it could just as easily be a directive that the inference engine takes into account when determine how to perform inference over assertions using these terms.")
(comment causeOfDeathEvent "<code>(#$causeOfDeathEvent DYING CAUSE-SIT-TYPE)</code> means that some instance of <code>CAUSE-SIT-TYPE</code> is the particular situation that causes the individual involved in <code>DYING</code> to die.")
(disjointWith HeartValveRelatedProblem HeartDisease-NonValvular)
(comment interArgDependentCardinality "An instance of both #$ArgCardinalityPredicate and #$InterArgConstraintPredicate (qq.v.) that can be used to put a conditional argument-cardinality constraint on a specified argument-place of a predicate, dependent upon the type of thing occupying that or another specified argument-place.
<p>
(#$interArgDependentCardinality PRED M COL1 N COL2 CARD) means that when PRED's Mth argument is an instance of COL2, INS1, then, however the rest of the arguments are fixed, there is at most CARD things, INS2, that are instances of COL3 that stand in PRED to INS1.  For example, a relation like currentlyFieldedPlayerForTeam that relates a sports team in arg1 to a player in arg2 that is playing in a game the team is involved in the current context might have the following cardinality restriction
<p>
<code>(#$interArgDependentCardinality currentlyFieldedPlayerForTeam 1 BaseballTeam 2 Outfielder 3) </code><p>
This would entail that in a given context there are at most 3 outfielders playing in a game for a given team.  The most useful assertions of this type are when CARD=1.  In cases like those, simplification modules can utilize this information to unify distinct variables that may have arisen from independent transformations.")
(comment Sepsis "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Sepsis is a severe ailment condition resulting in an inflammatory state caused by an infection.")
(comment WordSequenceItem "Something that can be in a #$WordSequence. Abstractly, a string or set of strings.")
(comment WordSequenceFn "A #$ReifiableFunction that returns an abstract sequence of #$WordSequenceItem arguments.")
(comment StringsOfWordSequenceFn "An #$EvaluatableFunction that returns the set of all strings composed by concatenating in order (separated by spaces) one string represented by each of its #$WordSequenceItem arguments.")
(comment WordStringsFn "An #$EvaluatableFunction. (#$WordStringsFn WU PRED) denotes the set of all strings STRING such that (PRED WU STRING) holds.")
(comment CompoundWordFn "(CompoundWordFn WORDS WORD) denotes the compound word headed by WORD, preceded by one of the word-sequence strings denoted by WORDS.")
(comment CompoundWordFn-HeadInitial "(#$CompoundWordFn-HeadInitial WORD WORDS) denotes the compound word headed by WORD, followed by one of the word-sequence strings denoted by WORDS.")
(comment CompoundWordFn-HeadMedial "(#$CompoundWordFn-HeadMedial LEADING-WORDS WORD FOLLOWING-WORDS) denotes the compound word headed by WORD, preceded by LEADING-WORDS and followed by FOLLOWING-WORDS.")
(comment dayBetweenDate-Inclusive "(#$dayBetweenDate-Inclusive DATE1 DAY DATE2) means that DAY is a calendar day that is temporally subsumed by the date range that starts at the beginning of the first day of DATE1 through the last day of DATE2.")
(comment dateFinalSecond "(#$dateFinalSecond DATE SECOND) means that SECOND is the final second of date.  E.g. if DATE = July, 2004, then SECOND = 11:59:59 July 31, 2004.")
(comment caeQueryLibraryDefaultMaxProductivity "<code>(#$caeQueryLibraryDefaultMaxProductivity SPECIFICATION INT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, the inference engine productivity limit should be INT.")
(comment SlovenianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Slovenia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment situationAffectsBodyPart "(situationAffectsBodyPart SIT PART) says that SIT affects #$OrganismPart PART.  For example, (#$situationAffectsBodyPart HairCuttingEvent001 MobOfHair001) says that MobOfHair001 is affected by HairCuttingEvent001.")
(comment SurgicalProcedureNonCongenital "The collection of surgical procedures that are not instances of #$CongenitalHeartProcedure-Surgical")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedureNonCongenital CongenitalHeartProcedure-Surgical)
(comment CreditCardAssociation "A specialization of #$CommercialServiceOrganization, each instance of which sets the terms for banks who issue or collect payments on, and merchants who accept, credit cards of a particular brand (see #$CreditCardTypeByBrand).  Notable instances include VISA, MasterCard, Discover Financial Services, and American Express.  A credit card association may either have members who issue credit cards (as is the case with VISA and MasterCard), or it may be a bank that issues its own brand (as is the case with Discover and American Express).  Credit card asociations of the first type are instances of #$CreditCardAssociation-Cooperative; associations of the second type are instances of #$CreditCardAssociation-SelfIssuing.")
(comment CreditCardAssociation-Cooperative "A specialization of #$CommercialServiceOrganization, each instance of which sets the terms for banks who issue or collect payments on, and merchants who accept, credit cards of a particular brand (see #$CreditCardTypeByBrand).  Notable instances include VISA, MasterCard, Discover Financial Services, and American Express.  A credit card association may either have members who issue credit cards (as is the case with VISA and MasterCard), or it may be a bank that issues its own brand (as is the case with Discover and American Express).  Credit card asociations of the first type are instances of #$CreditCardAssociation-Cooperative; associations of the second type are instances of #$CreditCardAssociation-SelfIssuing.")
(comment CreditCardAssociation-SelfIssuing "A collection of instances of #$BankOrganization and #$CreditCardAssociation.  Instances are banks, such as Discover Financial Services and American Express, who issue their own brand of credit card.  Contrast with instances of #$CreditCardAssociation-Cooperative, such as VISA and MasterCard, whose cards are issued by any of thousands of member banks.")
(comment cardIssuingBank "<code>(#$cardIssuingBank ACCOUNT BANK)</code> identifies <code>BANK</code> as the instance of #$BankOrganization that is the issuer of the instance <code>ACCOUNT</code> of #$CreditCardAccount.  <code>BANK</code> is responsible for billing the #$accountHolder, though a distinct bank may play the role of #$acquiringBank, i.e., the bank responsible for receiving the customer's payments.")
(comment associationForCard "<code>(#$associationForCard CARD ASSOC)</code> identifies <code>ASSOC</code> as the instance of #$CreditCardAssociation who controls the rights to the brand of credit card of which <code>CARD</code> is an instance.")
(comment MasterCardAccount "The collection of instances of #$CreditCardAccount whose #$accountOfTenderObject is an instance of #$MasterCard.")
(comment VisaCardAccount "The collection of instances of #$CreditCardAccount whose #$accountOfTenderObject is an instance of #$VISACard.")
(comment DiscoverCardAccount "The collection of instances of #$CreditCardAccount whose #$accountOfTenderObject is an instance of #$DiscoverCard.")
(comment AmExCardAccount "The collection of instances of #$CreditCardAccount whose #$accountOfTenderObject is an instance of #$AmExCard.")
(comment CreditCardAccountTypeByCardBrand "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType.  Instances are collections of #$CreditCardAccount that are accounts for instances of a common #$CreditCardTypeByBrand.")
(comment internalPowerSource "This relation is intended to capture the comparatively vague concept of the 'power source' of a #$SelfPoweredDevice.  More specifically (#$internalPowerSource DEVICE SOURCE) means that when DEVICE exhibits some motion that is part of its intended behavior, a causal explanation of this motion can be given that treats SOURCE as one of the principle physical causes and origins of this motion.  The scope of the predicate is thus extremely broad. E.g., a car's battery can be considered to be an #$internalPowerSource, but so can the car's engine.  The only provisos are that the 'source' so identified must be a #$properPhysicalParts of the device it helps power, and that the device in question must, accordingly, be a #$SelfPoweredDevice.")
(comment providesPowerFor "(#$providesPowerFor SUPPLY CONSTRUCT) means that SUPPLY provides power for CONSTRUCT.")
(comment associationForCardBrand "An instance of #$FunctionalPredicate, #$associationForCardBrand relates an instance of #$CreditCardTypeByBrand to the instance of #$CreditCardAssociation whose brand of card it is.")
(comment primaryFunction "A specialization of #$behaviorCapable (q.v.) that is used to specify a primary or particularly important function that a given object serves.  <code>(#$primaryFunction OBJ SITTYPE ROLE)</code> means that the primary function of <code>OBJ</code> is to play <code>ROLE</code> in situations of the type <code>SITTYPE</code>.  <code>OBJ</code> might be a natural object that has a primary function (e.g the primary function of a heart is to  pump blood), or <code>OBJ</code> might be an artifact that was intentionally  designed to have the primary function that it does (e.g. the primary function of a wall clock is to show the current time of day).  For cases of the latter sort, consider the more specialized predicate #$intendedPrimaryFunction.  Note that, while most things have one primary function, some have more than one.  For example, one might  claim that the two primary functions of a lung are to take in oxygen and to expell carbon dioxide.  For things that have only one main function, consider the specialization #$soleFunction.")
(comment TermOfService "A specialization of #$Situation, instances of which are characterized by an agent holding a particular position within an organzation at the granularity of a single 'term,' where the temporal bounds of a 'term' are conventially-defined so as to be consistent with the charactersitic relation continuing beyond the scope of the term (e.g., Bill Clinton was US President for 8 consecutive years, but served 2 terms).")
(comment NthTermInOrgRoleFn "<code>(#$NthTermInOrgRoleFn AGENT N ORG ROLE)</code> denotes the <code>N</code>th term that <code>AGENT</code> served in the role of <code>ROLE</code> in the organziation <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment agentNthTermInOrgRole "The predicate that corresponds to (see #$functionCorrespondsToPredicate) #$NthTermInOrgRoleFn, <code>(#$agentNthTermInOrgRole AGENT N TERM ORG ROLE)</code> means that <code>TERM</code> is the <code>N</code>th instance of #$TermOfService in which <code>AGENT</code> served as/played the role of <code>ROLE</code> in the organization <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment textSupportsConclusion-CycL "<code>(#$textSupportsConclusion-CycL STRING CYCL)</code> means that the text-string <code>STRING</code> has a natural interpretation from which the truth of the CycL sentence <code>CYCL</code> follows.")
(comment behaviorIncapable "<code>(#$behaviorIncapable OBJ SITTYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is incapable of playing <code>ROLE</code> in any instance of <code>SITTYPE</code>.  Thus, <code>(#$behaviorIncapable HarryThePenguin #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)</code> means that <code>HarryThePenguin</code> is incapable of flying.   Cf. #$behaviorCapable and #$behaviorIncapable-CapabilityCompromised.")
(comment focalRocketTypeOfLaunchOperation "<code>(#$focalRocketOfLaunchOperation LAUNCH-OP ROCKET-TYPE)</code> means that <code>ROCKET-TYPE</code> is the type of focal rocket involved in <code>LAUNCH-OP</code>.")
(comment rangeSystemRequired "<code>(#$rangeSystemRequired LAUNCH-OP SYSTEM)</code> means that <code>SYSTEM</code> is one of the systems required to be involved in monitoring the down-range flight of the rocket launched in <code>LAUNCH-OP</code>.")
(comment Ontology "The collection of organized conceptual structures in which types of things form a generalization hierarchy and in which properties are defined to hold between instances of the types of things.  An example is the #$Cyc ontology. ")
(comment owlRootClass "A predicate relating an #$OWLOntology to each of its unsubsumed #$OWLClass members.")
(comment firstMateOfCrew "(#$firstMateOfCrew CREW MATE) means that MATE holds the position of 'first mate' among CREW.")
(comment firstMateOfVessel "(#$firstMateOfVessel VESSEL MATE) means that, at the time of the assertion, MATE serves in the capacity of 'first mate' on VESSEL).")
(comment ShipsFirstMate "A #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg, and a specialization of #$CrewMemberOnShip.  Each instance of #$ShipsFirstMate is a #$firstMateOfVessel on some #$Watercraft, and a #$firstMateOfCrew in some ship's crew, within the temporal scope of the '#$isa' assertion.")
(comment secondMateOfCrew "(#$secondMateOfCrew CREW MATE) means that MATE holds the position of 'second mate' among CREW.")
(comment secondMateOfVessel "(#$secondMateOfVessel VESSEL MATE) means that, at the time of the assertion, MATE serves in the capacity of 'second mate' on VESSEL).")
(comment ShipsSecondMate "A #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg, and a specialization of #$CrewMemberOnShip.  Each instance of #$ShipsSecondMate is a #$secondMateOfVessel on some #$Watercraft, and a #$secondMateOfCrew in some ship's crew, within the temporal scope of the '#$isa' assertion.")
(comment masterOfCrew "(#$masterOfCrew CREW MASTER) means that MASTER holds the position of 'ship's master' among CREW.")
(comment masterOfVessel "(#$masterOfVessel VESSEL MASTER) means that, at the time of the assertion, MASTER serves in the capacity of 'ship's master' on VESSEL).")
(comment ShipsMaster "A #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg, and a specialization of #$CrewMemberOnShip.  Each instance of #$ShipsMaster is a #$masterOfVessel on some #$Watercraft, and a #$masterOfCrew in some ship's crew, within the temporal scope of the '#$isa' assertion.")
(comment captainOfCrew "(#$captainOfCrew CREW CAPTAIN) means that CAPTAIN holds the position of captain among CREW.")
(comment captainOfVessel "(#$captainOfVessel VESSEL CAPTAIN) means that, at the time of the assertion, CAPTAIN serves in the capacity of captain on VESSEL).")
(comment dutyOfficerOfTask "(#$dutyOfficerOfTask TASK OFFICER) means that OFFICER is the individual charged with carrying out TASK, in an official capacity as a crewmember on board an oceangoing vessel whereon TASK is carried out.")
(comment KnowledgeAcquisitionProgram "The collection of software programs designed to extract knowledge from some source (e.g., a person or a document), and store that knowledge away in a form that makes it amenable to integration in some formalized knowledge store.")
(comment infoStoreSentenceStatusResolutionMt "<code>(#$infoStoreSentenceStatusResolutionMt STORE MT)</code> identifies <code>MT</code> as the instance of #$Microtheory that contains assertions reflecting the resolution of the status of CycL sentences (e.g, their truth or falsity) as determined by the instance <code>STORE</code> of #$InformationStore.")
(comment occursDuringHospitalization "This relates a patient's #$HospitalCareEvent to the patient's events that occur in the hospital during that hospitalization.")
(comment bridgingPredicateForPredicate "(#$bridgingPredicateForPredicate PRED-BASE PRED-BRIDGE (#$TheSet ARG1, ... , ARGN))  means that PRED-BRIDGE is the consequent of a transformation rule that, essentially, transforms into PRED-BASE in order to generate bindings.  The third argument will be a set of lists that determine the correspondence between the argument positions in PRED-BASE and PRED-BRIDGE.  The first item in the list corresponds to the argument position of PRED-BASE and the second item in the list corresponds to the argument position of the PRED-BRIDGE.  For example, (#$bridgingPredicateForPredicate #$rdf-type #$isa (#$TheSet (#$TheList 1 1) (#$TheList 2 2))) means that, in certain contexts #$isa literals are solved by transforming into #$rdf-type and the arg1 of #$rdf-type corresponds to arg1 is #$isa and arg2 of #$rdf-type corresponds to arg2 of #$isa. ")
(comment PreoperativeStatusTypeByUrgencyAndCondition "Each instance of #$PreoperativeStatusTypeByUrgencyAndCondition is a specialization of #$PreoperativePatientStatus with a particular urgency and a particular type of #$PhysiologicalCondition.")
(comment PreoperativeStatusFn "<code>(#$PreoperativeStatusFn URGEN COND-TYPE)</code> denotes the subcollection of #$PreoperativePatientStatus where an operation with the urgency <code>URGEN</code> is performed for some condition <code>COND-TYPE</code>.  
<p>
For example, <code>(#$PreoperativeStatusFn #$EmergentSurgery #$HeartAttack)</code> denotes the collecton of preoperative statuses where emergency surgery for heart attacks is indicated..")
(disjointWith Operation PreoperativePatientStatus)
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure Operation)
(comment StreamingStructuredKnowledgeSource "A specialization of both #$InformationBearingObject and #$StructuredKnowledgeSource. Each instance of StreaminStructuredknowledgeSource is an electronic IBO that dynamically streams structured information.")
(disjointWith CoronaryArteryGraftDistalAnastomosis CoronaryArteryGraftSegment)
(comment bypassConduitHasCorrespondingCoronaryArteryGraftDistalAnastomosis "Relates a graft segment to a data node that specifies information about the graft distal anastomosis.")
(comment DeltaIIRocket "A specialization of #$DeltaRocket.  The Delta II rockets have been part of the Delta rocket family since 1989.")
(comment DeltaIVRocket "A specialization of #$DeltaRocket.")
(disjointWith DeltaIIRocket DeltaIVRocket)
(disjointWith AtlasRocket DeltaRocket)
(comment RADAR-ApplicationArchitectureMt "The microtheory for describing the architecture of #$RADAR-TheCycBasedApplication.")
(comment RecordMtByUserTaskAndApplicationFn "<code>(#$RecordMtByUserTaskAndApplicationFn USER TASK PROGRAM)</code> denotes the context in which data is stored about the session involving the software application <code>PROGRAM</code> by <code>USER</code> while <code>USER</code> is working on <code>TASK</code>.")
(comment RADARSessionRecordMicrotheory "A specialization of #$SoftwareInteractionSessionRecordMicrotheory.  Each instance of #$RADARSessionRecordMicrotheory stores information about some use of #$RADAR-TheCycBasedApplication.")
(comment RADARInteractionSession " A specialization of #$RADARInteractionSession.  Each instance of #$RADARInteractionSession is a session in which #$RADAR-TheCycBasedApplication is used.")
(comment missionOfRADARSession "<code>(#$missionOfRADARSession SESSION MISSION)</code> means that the #$RADARInteractionSession deals focally with #$MilitarySpaceLaunchOperation.")
(comment sessionHasParameterizedQuerySentenceForDEEP "<code>(#$sessionHasParameterizedQuerySentenceForDEEP SESSION PARAM-SET SENT)</code> means that during <code>SESSION</code>, <code>SENT</code> must be posted to DEEP, with the parameters listed in <code>PARAM-SET</code>.")
(comment DEEPQuery-Historical "An instance of #$DEEPSubscriptionParameter.  DEEP subscriptions with this parameter should set the DEEP flag which indicates that historical values should be retrieved.")
(comment DEEPQuery-Ephemeral "An instance of #$DEEPSubscriptionParameter.  DEEP subscriptions with this parameter should be retracted after they get answers.")
(comment DEEPSubscriptionParameter "A specialization of #$SoftwareParameter.  Each instance of #$DEEPSubscriptionParameter is a parameter for subscriptions to be posted to DEEP.")
(comment temporalUpdateRequiredForArg "<code>(#$temporalUpdateRequiredForArg PRED N)</code> means that when there is a temporally qualified assertion in a context with monadic <code>MT-1</code> with <code>PRED</code> in the arg0 position and <code>TERM</code> in the <code>Nth</code> position, then if there is reason to make an additional assertion in a context with monadic <code>MT-2</code> (where <code>MT-2</code> inherits from <code>MT-1</code>) with <code>PRED</code> in the arg0 position and <code>TERM</code> in the <code>Nth</code> position, and where the temporal qualification of the existing assertion is open-ended toward the future, then the temporal qualification of the existing assertion needs to be temporally closed off before the novel assertion can be made.  For example,  given
<p>
<code>(#$temporalUpdateRequiredForArg #$president 1)</code>
<p>
then if we have this assertion in the Cyc KB:
<p>
  <code>(#$ist #$HistoricalPeopleDataMt (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn (#$TimeIntervalBetweenFn (#$YearFn 2000) #$Now) #$TimePoint) (#$president #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$GeorgeWBush))</code>
<p>
if we wish to add a new assertion with #$president in the arg0 position and #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica in the arg1 position, and <code>NEW-PRESIDENT</code> in the arg2 position (where <code>NEW-PRESIDENT</code> is #$different from #$GeorgeWBush) in a temporal context that starts at time <code>T</code> where <code>T</code> is later than (#$YearFn 2000), then the previous assertion must first be updated to:
<p>
 <code>(#$ist #$HistoricalPeopleDataMt (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn (#$TimeIntervalBetweenFn (#$YearFn 2000) T) #$TimePoint) (#$president #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$GeorgeWBush))</code>
<p>
before we can assert:
<p>
 <code>(#$ist #$HistoricalPeopleDataMt (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn (#$TimeIntervalBetweenFn T #$Now) #$TimePoint) (#$president #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica NEW-PRESIDENT))</code>
")
(comment Imipenem-Cilastatin "A type of anitbiotic.")
(comment Antibiotic "drug substances with anti-bacterial, anti-fungal, or anti-parasitical activity")
(comment Amikacin "A type of anitbiotic.")
(comment RADARKBEventTerm "A specialization of#$CycLTerm.  RADAR registers an event listener for all quoted instances of #$RADARKBEventTerm.")
(comment Daptomycin "A type of anitbiotic.")
(comment termOfUnit "An #$InferenceRelatedBookkeepingPredicate (q.v.) that appears in system-generated assertions.  #$termOfUnit relates unreified reifiable non-atomic terms (\"NATs\") to indexed data structures reified by the system.  #$termOfUnit GAF (see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) assertions
are added by the system when an unreified reifiable NAT first appears in a CycL sentence that is added to the knowledge base.  When such a NAT is first used in a sentence, the Cyc system automatically creates an indexed data structure to reify the NAT.  A name is automatically assigned to the new data structure by the Cyc system.  (Typically, this name is character-for-character identical to the unreified reifiable NAT itself; but one should not be misled by this into thinking that #$termOfUnit is a specialization of #$equals.)  The predicate #$termOfUnit relates the system-generated data structure to the original NAT.  <code>(#$termOfUnit DATA-STRUCTURE NAT)</code> means that the data structure <code>DATA-STRUCTURE</code> was created to reify the value of the non-atomic term <code>NAT</code>, and that <code>NAT</code> refers to <code>DATA-STRUCTURE</code>, which in turn denotes something in the range of the function in the 0th (or \"arg 0\") position of <code>NAT</code>.
<p>
For example, if an assertion such as (#$isa (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile) #$ProductType) introduced the unreified reifiable NAT (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile) in the Cyc knowledge base, the system would create a data structure to reify the value of (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile).  The system would assign the name `(#$RepairingFn #$Automobile)' to the newly-created data structure.  The system would also associate the newly-reified data structure with the unreified refiable NAT by means of the #$termOfUnit assertion (#$termOfUnit (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile) (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile)).
<p>
Note that #$termOfUnit assertions are made in the #$BaseKB because the relation between a NAT and the data structure reified for it is meant to hold in all contexts.  
<p>
One should view #$termOfUnit assertions as bits of bookkeeping knowledge that are very rarely, if ever, entered into the Cyc knowledge base by hand. See #$retainTerm -- the predicate to use to create a NART that one wishes to remain in the Cyc KB even if no substantive additional assertions are made about it. NARTs that have only #$termOfUnit assertions made about them are removed from the KB at build time.")
(comment isolatedProcedureOfTypeWithLoneProcedureOfType "<code>(#$isolatedProcedureOfTypeWithLoneProcedureOfType PRO PRO-TYPE ISO-TYPE)</code> means that the #$SurgicalProcedure <code>PRO</code> is an instance of <code>PRO-TYPE</code> and that the #$Surgery during which <code>PRO</code> is performed is not known to involve any other surgical procedures other than an instance of ISO-TYPE.")
(comment DEEPReportMicrotheory "A specialization of #$Microtheory.  Each instance of #$DEEPReportMicrotheory contains information about a single report from a DEEP tuple.")
(comment dEEPReportOfSessionWithIDAndDate "<code>(#$dEEPReportOfSessionWithIDAndDate SESSION ID DATE MT)</code> means that <code>MT</code> is the microtheory containing information represnting the content of a DEEP tuple, where that tuple has the identification string <code>ID</code> and was received by RADAR at <code>DATE</code> during <code>SESSION</code>.")
(comment DEEPReportOfSessionWithIDAndDateFn "<code>(#$DEEPReportOfSessionWithIDAndDateFn SESSION ID DATE)</code> denotes the microtheory containing information represnting the content of a DEEP tuple, where that tuple has the identification string <code>ID</code> and was received by RADAR at <code>DATE</code> during <code>SESSION</code>.")
(comment riversides "(#$riversides BANK RIVER) means that BANK is one of the banks/sides of RIVER.  Note that RIVER is not restricted to being a #$River, but can be any specialization of #$Stream, including #$River.")
(comment SurgicalProcedureType-General "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  This is the collection of surgical procedure types that are very general like #$CardiacProcedure-Surgical.")
(comment sourceQueryForEnumeratedCollection "(#$sourceQueryForSimpleQuery SOURCE-QUERY USER-CREATED-COLLECTION) means that the results of running SOURCE-QUERY were saved as the enumerated collection USER-CREATED-COLLECTION.")
(comment specInversesIrrelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTTypeInArg "<code>(#$specPredsIrrelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTTypeInArg PRED TERM-SUMMARY-PRED TYPE N)</code> means that if a thing <code>THING</code> is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, then any assertions in which an inverse specialization of <code>PRED</code> occurs in arg 0 and <code>THING</code> occurs as arg <code>N</code> should NOT appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment ThoracicAbdominalAorta "comment needed")
(disjointWith CardiacValveDonor (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet CoronaryArteryGraftDistalAnastomosis CoronaryArteryGraftSegment)))
(disjointWith MedicalPatientOrDonor (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet CoronaryArteryGraftDistalAnastomosis CoronaryArteryGraftSegment)))
(disjointWith HeartValveRepairOrReplacement (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepairOrReplacement))
(comment IrritableBowelSyndrome "Irritable bowel syndrome (IBS), also called spastic colon, is a chronic (long-lasting) disorder of the colon, or large intestine. It is the most common gastrointestinal disorder. It affects women twice as often as men and usually begins in early adult life. Although the disorder can cause much distress, it is not life-threatening and does not lead to life-threatening disease.")
(comment RocketPropelledDevice "The collection of all devices designed to execute directed translations through a controlled application of Newton's Second Law, i.e., the principle that every reaction has an equal and opposite reaction.  In practice, this means that instances of #$RocketPropelledDevice obtain their motive power from the forcible ejection of mass, usually in the form of violently expanding gasses from a contained explosion, in the direction opposite the motion of the vehicle.  #$RocketPropelledDevices include all #$RocketEngines, as well as all devices which incorporate #$RocketEngines, including, e.g., bottle rockets as well as rockets designed for transport (see #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice).")
(comment RocketTypeByStageConfiguration "A faceting of #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice.  Each instance is a specialization of #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice whose instances are all vehicles with a common number of rocket stages.")
(comment Rocket-MultiStage "The collection of all multi-stage rockets.  Every instance of #$Rocket-MultiStage is a physical 'stack' of instances of #$Rocket-SingleStage, each of which is an instance of #$RocketStage by virtue of being a physical part of a #$Rocket-MultiStage.")
(comment NStageRocketFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for faceting #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevice by the number of rocket stages in the vehicle.")
(comment numberOfRocketStagesForRocketType "The corresponding predicate (see #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$NStageRocketFn.")
(comment RocketStage "The collection of all instances of #$Rocket-SingleStage that are components in instances of #$Rocket-MultiStage at some phase of their existence.")
(disjointWith Operation HospitalCareEvent)
(disjointWith HeartRhythmMonitorContainingThing HospitalCareEvent)
(comment Requirement "A first-order collection and a specialization of #$Obligation.  Each instance of #$Requirement is an obligation to ensure that a particular capability is provided.")
(comment RangeRequirement "A first-order collection and a specialization of #$Requirement.  Each instance of #$RangeRequirement is an obligation on the part of Space Wing personnel to ensure that a particular capability is provided, where this obligation is imposed by the Space Wing on itself (contrast with #$RangeCustomerRequirement).  Generally, the relevant capabilities are pertinent to a specific operation.")
(comment RangeCustomerRequirement "A first-order collection and a specialization of #$Requirement.  Each instance of #$RangeCustomerRequirement is an obligation on the part of Space Wing personnel to ensure that a particular capability is provided, where this obligation is imposed by a Range customer on the Space Wing (contrast with #$RangeCustomerRequirement).  Generally, the relevant capabilities are pertinent to a specific operation.")
(comment Capability "A first-order collection and a specialization of #$TemporalThing.  Each instance of #$Capability is an attribute that objects or agents can have.  Having an instance of the collection #$Capability indicates that an entity can play a role in a type of situation.  When an object OBJ has a capability, that does not entail that OBJ can unquestionably play the corresponding role in every such situation, since extrinsic factors may prevent it from doing so; for example, if OBJ is a tool, it may be in the wrong location or operated by a person lacking the requisite skills.")
(comment ComplexCapability "A first-order collection and a specialization of #$Group and #$Capability.  Each instance of #$ComplexCapability is a group of capabiliteis and also itself a capability.  For example, the ability to play golf is a complex capability, whose group members include both the capability to putt balls and the capability to drive balls.")
(comment capabilityRequired "<code>(#$capabilityRequired REQUIREMENT CAPABILITY)</code> means that <code>CAPABILITY</code> is a capability demanded by <code>REQUIREMENT</code>.")
(comment subCapability "<code>(#$subCapability COMPLEX-CAPABILITY CAPABILITY)</code> means that <code>CAPABILITY</code> is a member of the group of capabilities, <code>COMPLEX-CAPABILITY</code>.")
(comment complexCapabilityCardinality "<code>(#$complexCapabilityCardinality COMPLEX-CAPABILITY INTEGER)</code> means that <code>COMPLEX-CAPABILITY</code> has exactly <code>INTEGER</code> direct sub-capabilities.")
(comment minSubCapabilities "<code>(#$minSubCapabilities COMPLEX-CAPABILITY INTEGER)</code> means that <code>COMPLEX-CAPABILITY</code>, in order to be actualized, must draw upon at least <code>INTEGER</code> of its direct sub-capabilities.")
(comment technologyAssigned "<code>(#$technologyAssigned REQUIREMENT SYSTEM)</code> means that <code>SYSTEM</code> has been allocated to fulfill <code>REQUIREMENT</code>.")
(comment operationOfRequirement "<code>(#$operationOfRequirement REQUIREMENT OPERATION)</code> means that <code>REQUIREMENT</code> is a requirement for <code>OPERATION</code>.")
(comment strengthOfRequirement "<code>(#$strengthOfRequirement REQUIREMENT DEGREE)</code> means that <code>REQUIREMENT</code> is required to degree <code>DEGREE</code>.")
(comment hasCapabilityStatus "(#$hasCapabilityStatus THING CAP) means that THING has the capability represented by the instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability CAP.  That is, the statement holds just in case THING is an instance of CAP.")
(comment hasCapability "<code>(#$hasCapability OBJ CAP)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> has the capability <code>CAP</code>.")
(comment RocketEngineTypeByFuelType "A faceting collection on #$RocketEngine.  It includes two instances:  #$RocketEngine-LiquidFueled and #$RocketEngine-SolidFueled.")
(comment RocketEngine-LiquidFueled "One of the two main instances of #$RocketEngineTypeByFuelType.  Instances of #$RocketEngine-LiquidFueled use a combustible liquid fuel, such as #$Hydrazine and a liquified oxidant, e.g. (#$LiquidFn #$Oxygen), which are explosively combined in acombustion chamber to provide thrust.")
(comment RocketEngine-SolidFueled "One of the two main instances of #$RocketEngineTypeByFuelType.  Instances of #$RocketEngine-SolidFueled burn a solid fuel core combined with oxidant and a reactive catalyst to provide thrust.  The best-known examples are probably the solid-fuel #$RocketBoosters that support launches of the Space Shuttle.")
(comment SolidRocketBooster "The class of all #$RocketBoosters featuring solid-fuel engines (#$RocketEngine-SolidFueled).")
(disjointWith SolidRocketBooster LiquidRocketBooster)
(comment LiquidRocketBooster "The class of all #$RocketBoosters featuring liquid-fuel engines (#$RocketEngine-LiquidFueled).")
(comment PayloadFairing "The collection of fairings, or aerodynamically streamlined covers, used to protect the payload in some kinds of #$RocketLaunchOperation.  Fairings are commonly used when the payload being launched is a satellite or more generally, an unmanned instrumentation package.")
(comment cabgHasBypassConduitToCoronaryArtery "Relates a CABG to the bypass conduit type and the coronary artery type bypassed.")
(comment latitude "<code>(#$latitude THING ANGULAR-DISTANCE)</code> means that the #$SpatialThing <code>THING</code> is located at the north latitude <code>ANGULAR-DISTANCE</code>, in the sense that either the whole of <code>THING</code> lies at this latitude or <code>THING</code> has a proper part which lies at this latitude.  Thus if <code>THING</code> is, for instance, a large geographical region, there can be more than one true assertion of the form <code>(#$latitude THING X)</code>.  Some examples of assertions about latitude are:  
<p>
(#$latitude #$EarthsEquator (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 0)),<br> 
(#$latitude #$AxialNorthPoleOfEarth (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 90)), and <br>
(#$latitude #$AntarcticCircle (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure -66.5)).  
<p>
As the last example indicates, latitudes of things in the southern hemisphere are expressed using negative real numbers.")
(comment longitude "<code>(#$longitude THING ANGULAR-DISTANCE)</code> means that the #$SpatialThing <code>THING</code> is located at the east longitude <code>ANGULAR-DISTANCE</code>, in the sense that either the whole of <code>THING</code> lies at this longitude or <code>THING</code> has a proper part which lies at this longitude.  Thus if <code>THING</code> is, for instance, a large geographical region, there can be more than one true assertion of the form <code>(#$longitude THING X)</code>.  Some examples of assertions about longitude are:  
<p>
(#$longitude #$PrimeMeridian-Greenwich (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 0)) and <br> (#$longitude #$CityOfAustinTX (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure -97.7)).  
<p>
As the last example indicates, longitudes of things in the western hemisphere are expressed using negative real numbers.  We adopt the convention that the longitude of the north and south poles is 0 degrees.")
(disjointWith PrimaryProcedure MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment locatedInBoundingBoxWithCoordinates-Minimal "A specialization of #$locatedInBoundingBoxWithCoordinates (q.v.).   <code>(#$locatedInBoundingBoxWithCoordinates-Minimal PLACE LAT-MAX LON-MIN LAT-MIN LON-MAX)</code> means that the bounding box specified by the corner points <code>LAT-MAX</code>, <code>LON-MIN</code>, <code>LAT-MIN</code> and <code>LON-MAX</code> is the smallest bounding box that can be constructed to fully contain <code>PLACE</code>.")
(comment obstacleInLocationBlocksPathForType "<code>(#$obstacleInLocationBlocksPathForType OBJ PATH TYPE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is an obstacle to the traversal of <code>PATH</code> for all instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment AbsoluteCycProblemStoreFn "(#$AbsoluteCycProblemStoreFn CYC-IMAGE SUID) denotes the problem store whose system-internal ID is SUID, and that was created by CYC-IMAGE.")
(comment CycImageFn "(#$CycImageFn COMPUTER ID) denotes the #$CycImage that is running or ran on COMPUTER under the image name ID. ID must be sufficient to uniquely identify a single image among all images ever run on COMPUTER.")
(comment queryInferences "(#$queryInferences QUERY-SPEC INFERENCE) means that INFERENCE was run according to the parameters specified by QUERY-SPEC.")
(comment problemStoreSnapshotPathnames "(#$problemStoreSnapshotPathnames PROBLEM-STORE PATHNAME) means that PATHNAME designates a file that constitutes a record of the state of PROBLEM-STORE at some point in its existence.")
(comment inferenceTimeToFirstAnswer "<code>(#$inferenceTimeToFirstAnswer INFERENCE HOW-LONG)</code> means that <code>INFERENCE</code> found its first set of bindings <code>HOW-LONG</code> after it started.")
(comment inferenceTimeToLastAnswer "<code>(#$inferenceTimeToLastAnswer INFERENCE HOW-LONG)</code> means that <code>INFERENCE</code> found its last set of bindings <code>HOW-LONG</code> after it started.")
(comment inferenceStartTime "<code>(#$inferenceStartTime INFERENCE TIME)</code> means that <code>INFERENCE</code> started at <code>TIME</code>.")
(comment inferenceBindings "<code>(#$inferenceBindings INFERENCE BINDING-SETS)</code> means that the variable bindings found by <code>INFERENCE</code> are those in <code>BINDING-SETS</code>.")
(comment UserScheduledQueryFolderForTaskFn "(#$UserScheduledQueryFolderForTaskFn AGENT ALLOTMENT) denotes the instance of #$KEInteractionFolder that contains queries scheduled by AGENT relative to ALLOTMENT.")
(comment UserCompletedQueryFolderForTaskFn "(#$UserCompletedQueryFolderForTaskFn AGENT ALLOTMENT) denotes the instance of #$KEInteractionFolder that contains queries completed at the request of AGENT relative to ALLOTMENT.")
(comment AortaProcedure-ExceptionSpecification "The collection of aorta procedures that do not count against certain procedures being classified as \"isolated\".")
(comment RadarSpecificationPredicate "A collection of predicates useful for stating the specifications of instances of #$RadarDevice.")
(comment RadarSpecificationPredicate-Transmitter "A collection of predicates useful for stating the specifications of the transmitters of instances of #$RadarDevice.")
(comment RadarSpecificationPredicate-Receiver "A collection of predicates useful for stating the specifications of the receivers of instances of #$RadarDevice.")
(comment RadarSpecificationPredicate-AntennaPedestal "A collection of predicates useful for stating the specifications of the antenna pedestals of instances of #$RadarDevice.")
(comment frequencyRangeOfTransmitter "<code>(#$frequencyRangeOfTransmitter TRANS FREQ)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, transmits in the frequency <code>FREQ</code>.")
(comment frequencyStabilityOfTransmitter "<code>(#$frequencyStabilityOfTransmitter RAD FREQ)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has a frequency drift of <code>FREQ</code>.")
(comment fineTuningRangeOfTransmitter "<code>(#$fineTuningRangeOfTransmitter TRANS FREQ)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has a fine tuning range of <code>FREQ</code>.")
(comment pulseRepetitionFrequencyOfTransmitter "<code>(#$pulseRepetitionFrequencyOfTransmitter TRANS FREQ)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has a pulse repetition frequency of <code>FREQ</code>.")
(comment peakPowerOfTransmitter "<code>(#$peakPowerOfTransmitter TRANS POWER)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has a peak power of <code>POWER</code>.")
(comment averagePowerOfTransmitter "<code>(#$averagePowerOfTransmitter TRANS POWER)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has an average power of <code>POWER</code>.")
(comment powerProgrammingRangeOfTransmitter "<code>(#$powerProgrammingRangeOfTransmitter TRANS POWER)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has an average power of <code>POWER</code>.")
(comment pulseWidthAvaliableForOfTransmitter "<code>(#$pulseWidthAvaliableForOfTransmitter TRANS TIME)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has an available pulse width of <code>TIME</code>.")
(comment frequencyRangeOfReceiver "<code>(#$frequencyRangeOfReceiver RECEIVER FREQ)</code> means that the radio receiver <code>RECEIVER</code>, an instance of #$RadioReceiver, receives in the frequency range <code>FREQ</code>.")
(comment intermediateFrequencyOfReceiver "<code>(#$intermediateFrequencyOfReceiver RECEIVER FREQ)</code> means that the radio receiver <code>RECEIVER</code>, an instance of #$RadioReceiver, has an intermediate frequency of <code>FREQ</code>.")
(comment pulseWidthOfReceiverAt6dB "<code>(#$pulseWidthOfReceiverAt6dB RECEIVER RATIO)</code> means that the radio receiver <code>RECEIVER</code>, an instance of #$RadioReceiver, has an available pulse width of <code>RATIO</code>.")
(comment dynamicRangeOfReceiver "<code>(#$dynamicRangeOfReceiver RECEIVER INTERVAL)</code> means that the radio receiver <code>RECEIVER</code>, an instance of #$RadioReceiver, has a dynamic range of <code>INTERVAL</code>.  Typically, <code>INTERVAL</code> will be expressed in decibels (see #$Decibel).")
(comment SuperheterodyneReceiver "A specialization of #$RadioReceiver.  Each instance of #$SuperheterodyneReceiver is a radio receiver that applie the superheterodyne principle to selectively recover information from radio waves of a particular frequency.")
(comment radarUsesReceiverType "<code>(#$radarUsesReceiverType RADAR RECEIVER-TYPE)</code> means that the radar <code>RADAR</code>, an instance of #$RadarDevice, has a receiver component of the type <code>RECEIVER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment AntennaPedestalMount "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$AntennaPedestalMount is a device that is used to control the orientation of an antenna.")
(comment AntennaPedestalMount-ElevationOverAzimuth "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$AntennaPedestalMount-ElevationOverAzimuth is an antenna pedestal mount that facilitates symmetrical loading. It locates a point in the sky by elevation in degrees above the horizon, and azimuth in degrees clockwise (eastward) from true north.")
(comment antennaPedestalAzimuthSlewRate "<code>(#$antennaPedestalAzimuthSlewRate RADAR SPEED</code> means that the radar <code>RADAR</code>, an instance of #$RadarDevice, has an antenna pedestal with an azimuth slew rate of <code>SPEED</code>.")
(comment antennaPedestalAzimuthAcceleration "<code>(#$antennaPedestalAzimuthAcceleration RADAR ACCEL</code> means that the radar <code>RADAR</code>, an instance of #$RadarDevice, has an antenna pedestal with an azimuth acceleration of <code>ACCEL</code>.")
(comment antennaPedestalElevationSlewRate "<code>(#$antennaPedestalElevationSlewRate RADAR SPEED</code> means that the radar <code>RADAR</code>, an instance of #$RadarDevice, has an antenna pedestal with an elevation slew rate of <code>SPEED</code>.")
(comment Paganism-Religion "A sub-collection of #$Religion. Each instance is one of various religions other than Christianity or Judaism or Islam.")
(comment NativeOrBypassReimplantation-ExceptionSpecification "The collection of certain reimplantation procedures that don't count against certain procedures being considered isolated.")
(comment AortaProcedureOrIABPProcedure-ExceptionSpecification "The collection of aorta or IABP procedures that do not count against certain procedures being classified as \"isolated\".")
(comment AtlasVPayloadFairing "The collection of all payload fairings of all #$AtlasVRockets.")
(comment AtlasVSRB "The class of solid rocket booster used in launching the AtlasV series 400 and series 500 rockets.")
(comment Centaur-AtlasRocketStage "The collection of second stage boosters customarily used in conjunction with the Atlas Common Core rocket booster (CCRB) in Atlas stack assemblies.")
(comment OneEngineCentaur-AtlasRocketStage "The collection of all instances of #$Centaur-AtlasRocketStage with one engine.")
(comment TwoEngineCentaur-AtlasRocketStage "The collection of all instances of #$Centaur-AtlasRocketStage with two engines.")
(comment atlasVPayloadFairingType "A typed spec-pred of #$hasPhysicalPartTypes, this predicate relates a given instance of #$AtlasVRocket to the class of #$AtlasVPayloadFairing that it possesses.")
(comment atlasVCentaurUpperStageType "A typed spec-pred of #$hasPhysicalPartTypes, this predicate relates a given instance of #$AtlasVRocket to the class of #$Centaur-AtlasRocketStage that it possesses.")
(comment atlasVNumberOfSRBs "A predicate relating an instance of #$AtlasVRocket to the number of #$AtlasVSRB instances attached to its common core booster. Atlas V series 400 and series 500 launch vehicles have between 0 and 5 SRBs.")
(comment Ocean "A specialization of #$Sea. Each instance of #$Ocean is one of the oceans of the world.  This includes #$EarthsOceanSea, the interconnected expanse of salt water covering 71% of the Earth's surface, and of which the other oceans are subregions.  Examples: #$AtlanticOcean, #$ArcticOcean, #$IndianOcean, #$PacificOcean.")
(comment AtlasVRocket "A specialization of #$AtlasRocket.  The Atlas V rockets are the successors to the Atlas II and Atlas IV vehicles. The Atlas V rocket had its maiden flight on August 21, 2002, and as of mid-2007, is one of the rockets most commonly used by the USAF.")
(comment PulmonaryFunctionTest "A specialialization of #$MedicalTesting.  each instance of this collection is a test or series of tests that measure the ability of the lungs to take air in and out and how well they deliver oxygen to the bloodstream.")
(comment Exclusion-SurgicalProcedure "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ClosingSomething. In each #$Exclusion-SurgicalProcedure, someone binds something or closes it off with a staple or ligature.")
(comment GroupingTheResultsOfAQuery "A specialization of #$CollectingInformation.  Each instance is an action in which an agent groups together some set of information from a query.  Typically the information is stored in such a way that the meaning of the items so grouped is preserved.")
(comment YearOfDateFn "Where DATE is a #$Date referencing one and only one #$CalendarYear, (#$YearOfDateFn DATE) returns the particular #$CalendarYear that DATE references.  Thus, e.g., (#$YearOfDateFn (#$DayFn 31 (#$MonthFn #$October (YearFn 2007)))) evaluates as (#$YearFn 2007).")
(comment MonthOfDateFn "Where DATE is a #$Date referencing one and only one #$CalendarMonth, (#$MonthOfDateFn DATE) returns the particular #$CalendarMonth referenced in DATE.  For example, (#$MonthOfDateFn (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 2008)))) evaluates as (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 2008)).")
(comment BloodstreamMorbidity "An instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType.  Each instance of #$Bleeding-TheCondition is a #$PhysiologicalCondition characterized by instances of #$Bleeding-TheAction (q.v.).")
(comment SeverityScoreString "A subcollection of #$UniqueID, each instance of this collection is an ID string that identified a medical patient in a medical record.")
(comment UniformResourceIdentifier "A specialization of #$IDString.  A #$UniformResourceIdentifier (URI) is a compact string of characters for identifying an abstract or physical resource.  The URI syntax is defined by http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2396.txt and is a world wide web standard.")
(comment ConceptDenotingString "A specialization of #$IDString.  instances of #$ConceptDenotingString are URIs or other strings that identify individuals or collections in the context of a particular ontology.")
(comment SurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceRemoval "A specialization of #$CardiacAssistDeviceRemoval.  Each instance of #$SurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceRemoval is an event in which a #$CardiacAssistDevice is removed from a patient during an operation.")
(comment NonSurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceRemoval "A specialization of #$CardiacAssistDeviceRemoval.  Each instance of #$NonSurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceRemoval is an event in which a #$CardiacAssistDevice is removed from a patient during an event other than an operation.")
(comment NonSurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceInsertion "A specialization of #$CardiacAssistDeviceInsertion.  Each instance of #$NonSurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceInsertion is an event in which a #$CardiacAssistDevice is inserted into a patient during an event other than an operation.")
(comment SurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceInsertion "A specialization of #$CardiacAssistDeviceInsertion.  Each instance of #$SurgicalCardiacAssistDeviceInsertion is an event in which a #$CardiacAssistDevice is surgically inserted into a patient.")
(comment procedureOperationUsedCPB "Refers to whether cardio-pulmonary bypass was employed during the surgery in which the procedure was performed.")
(comment Intra-aorticBalloonPumpRemovalOrInsertion-ExceptionSpecification "The collection of IABP or aorta procedures that don't count against certain procedures being considered isolated.")
(comment RevascularizationorIABPProcedure "The collection of specific revascularization or IABP procedures that are allowed to accompany certain CCF surgical procedures and still be considered isolated.")
(comment generateSupplementalFormulasForElements-TermGenls "(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls TERM SET) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  The appropriate formula, at this point is determined by whether INS is a collection or a predicate.  If INS is a collection, then (#$isa ?X INS) is the appropriate formula.  If INS is a predicate with arity N, then (INS ?VAR1, ..., VARN)is the appropriate formula.  At that point, any formulas resulting from the instantiation of terms from the valid terms set should be placed in the \"supplemental fragments\" folder.")
(comment generateSupplementalFormulasForElements-TermIsa "(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls TERM SET) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  The appropriate formula, at this point is determined by whether INS is a collection or a predicate.  If INS is a collection, then (#$isa ?X INS) is the appropriate formula.  If INS is a predicate with arity N, then (INS ?VAR1, ..., VARN)is the appropriate formula.  At that point, any formulas resulting from the instantiation of terms from the valid terms set should be placed in the \"supplemental fragments\" folder.")
(comment AtlasVCommonCoreBooster "The collection of all first stage boosters used in launching contemporary #$AtlasVRockets.")
(comment AtlasV-400Series "The collection of all instances of #$AtlasVRocket consisting in an Atlas V common core booster (CCB) surmounted by a #$Centaur-AtlasRocketStage and a payload protected by an #$AtlasV-400SeriesPayloadFairing.")
(comment AtlasV-400SeriesPayloadFairing "The collection of all #$AtlasVPayloadFairings that are 4 meters in diameter, i.e., the atomic #$rewriteOf (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$AtlasVPayloadFairing #$diameterOfObject (#$Meter 4)).  #$AtlasV-400SeriesPayloadFairings in turn are subdivided into three subclasses based on length:  the 12.0 meter large payload fairing (LPF), the 12.9 meter extended payload fairing (EPF), and the 13.8 meter superextended payload fairing (XEPF).")
(disjointWith TruthValue List)
(comment PathologyOrEtiologyInRecordEventFn "(#$PathologyOrEtiologyInRecordEventFn EVT  DATA AILMENT-TYPE) denotes the diagnosis of AILMENT-TYPE during or prior to EVT according to DATA.")
(comment PathologyOrEtiologyInRecordEventFn "(#$PathologyOrEtiologyInRecordEventFn EVT DATA AILMENT-TYPE) denotes the particular occurence of an instance of AILMENT-TYPE as diagnosed during EVT according to DATA.")
(comment BentallProcedure "A specialization of #$Replacement-SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$BentallProcedure is a replacement of an #$AscendingAorta with a tube graft that contains a prosthetic valve.  Reimplementation of coronary arteries into the graft is part of the procedure as well.")
(comment ReplacementWithValvedConduit-SurgicalProcedure "A specialization of #$Replacement-SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$ReplacementWithValvedConduit-SurgicalProcedure is a replacement of a vessel with a valved conduit.  A subset of these procedures are considered Bentall procedures when the vessel affected is the ascending aorta and there is a concomitant aortic valve replacement as well as a reimplantation of the coronary arteries.")
(comment DefinedSurgicalProcedureType "The collection of types of surgical procedures that are defined in terms of other procedures and properties.")
(comment Myectomy "The excision of some part of a muscle.")
(comment SeptalMyectomy "A myectomy of the cardiac septum.  A common treatment for hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.")
(comment TerritoryFn "The function #$TerritoryFn, applied to some instance <code>GEO-AGENT</code> of #$GeographicalAgent, denotes the spatial region of the earth occupied by <code>GEO-AGENT</code>, usually demarcated by natural or artificial boundaries.  Sometimes these boundaries are determined by a political process (as in the case that <code>GEO-AGENT</code> is a #$GeopoliticalEntity).  Note that this geographical region can be fluid over time, expanding and contacting as the geographical agent's borders change.  Note also that the temporal extent of (#$TerritoryFn <code>GEO-AGENT</code>) is equal to the temporal extent of <code>GEO-AGENT</code>.  So, if you want to refer to Hungary's territory in 1900, you could do so with (#$TerritoryFn HungaryIn1900).")
(comment GeographicalRegion-Declared "The collection of all instances of #$GeographicalPlace whose physical extent is determined by the boundary declarations of some intelligent agent.  Instances include plots of real estate, such as individual homesteads, commercial zones, and educational districts; the territory (see #$territoryOf) any geopolitical entity (see #$GeopoliticalEntity) such as a country, province, state, township, etc.; and even playing fields (e.g., a football field) and their parts (e.g., the \"red zone\" the \"end zone,\").  In many cases, especially in regions of any large size, an instance of #$GeographicalRegion-Declared will be administered or managed by some intelligent agent -- these all belong to the sub-category #$GeographicalRegion-Administered.")
(comment mostRecentEventOfTypeForPatient "<code>(#$mostRecentEventOfTypeForPatient EVT TYPE)</code> means that <code>EVT</code> is the most recent of the type <code>TYPE</code> for the patient acted on in <code>EVT</code>.")
(comment USNationalForestDistrict "The collection of districts (see #$geographicalDistricts) of national forests.")
(comment UnitedStatesAdministeredEcoRegionType "A collection of subcollections of #$EcologicalRegion-Administered.  Each instance is a type of region, instances of which are 1) of a common biome type (see #$BiomeType), and 2) administered at a national level by the USDA Forest Service.  This collection has four instances: (#$NationalForestsInFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) #$USNationalForestDistrict, #$USNationalGrassland, and #$USNationalGrasslandDistrict.")
(comment conflateMembersOfSetWhenGeneratingHierarchicalOrderingsForSpecs "(#$conflateMembersOfSetWhenGeneratingHierarchicalOrderingsForSpecs COLL SET) means that when generating hierarchical diagrams from suggestions of specs of COLL, then the trees generated from the members of SET should be merged into one diagram.")
(comment conflateMembersOfSetWhenGeneratingHierarchicalOrderingsForInstances "(#$conflateMembersOfSetWhenGeneratingHierarchicalOrderingsForInstances COLL SET) means that when generating hierarchical diagrams from suggestions of instances of COLL, then the trees generated from the members of SET should be merged into one diagram.")
(comment DillonRangerDistrict-Montana "Dillon Ranger District in Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest in Montana")
(comment valveProsthesisTypeExplanted "Relates a heart valve replacement to the broad type or the manufacturer's model number of the prosthetic cardiac valve that is being explanted during surgery.")
(comment valveProsthesisTypeImplanted "Relates a heart valve replacement to the broad type or the manufacturer's model number of the prosthetic cardiac valve that is being implanted during surgery.")
(comment suggestionGenlClassOrderedBy "(#$suggestionGenlClassOrderedBy TERM REL NUM) means that if a specialization of TERM has suggestions generated for it, then it is reasonable to generate alternate hierarchical suggestion views with those suggestions using REL as the ordering relation.  One example use is in generating hierarchical drop down menus for the CAE or FET.  Arg3 indicates the direction of the ordering, e.g. terms ordered via #$genls are typically ordered more general to more specific; from arg2 to arg1, while terms ordered via #$physicalPartTypes are ordered from whole to part; from arg1 to arg2.")
(comment suggestionIsaClassOrderedBy "(#$suggestionIsaClassOrderedBy TERM REL NUM) means that if an instance of TERM has suggestions generated for it, then it is reasonable to generate alternate hierarchical suggestion views with those suggestions using REL as the ordering relation.  One example use is in generating hierarchical drop down menus for the CAE or FET.  Arg3 indicates the direction of the ordering, e.g. terms ordered via #$genls are typically ordered more general to more specific; from arg2 to arg1, while terms ordered via #$physicalPartTypes are ordered from whole to part; from arg1 to arg2")
(comment PennsylvaniaBureauOfOilAndGasManagement "the State of Pennsylvania, Department of Environmental Protection, Bureau of Oil and Gas Management")
(comment PennsylvaniaDepartmentOfEnvironmentalProtection "the Pennsylvania Department of Environmental Protection")
(comment RentalAgreement "A specialization of #$EconomicAgreement and #$TemporaryUserRightsAgreement.  Each instance of #$RentalAgreement is an agreement between the owner of a property and a renter who, according to the terms of the agreement, will have temporary user rights over the property.")
(comment renter "<code>(#$renter AGREEMENT AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is the agent who agrees to be a renter of property as specified in the rental agreement, <code>AGREEMENT</code>.")
(comment lessee "<code>(#$lessee AGREEMENT AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is the agent who agrees to lease property as specified in the lease agreement, <code>AGREEMENT</code>.")
(comment lessor "<code>(#$lessor AGREEMENT AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is the agent who agrees to act as a lessor as specified in the lease agreement, <code>AGREEMENT</code>.")
(comment RealEstateLeaseAgreement "A specialization of #$LeaseAgreement.  Each instance is a lease agreement that transfers temporary user rights of real estate.")
(comment genlsDown "#$genlsDown is a supported predicate that will generate the transitive specialization closure of a term in arg2, but will only generate the reflexive closure of a term in arg1.  Fully bound uses are treated exactly like #$genls.  For example, (#$genlsDown ?X #$Dog) will yield all the specialization of #$Dog as values for ?X, but (#$genlsDown #$Dog ?X) will only yield #$Dog as a value for ?X.")
(comment CardiacValvePart "the collection of parts of cardiac valves and the surrounding infrastructures.")
(disjointWith TechnologyOrganization MedicalCareProvider)
(comment USCodeFilter-Chapter37 "The code filter used to focus concept-extraction against Chapter 37 of the US Code.")
(comment DEEPQuery-Hybrid "An instance of #$DEEPSubscriptionParameter.  DEEP subscriptions with this parameter should retieve historical and \"live\" datapoints.")
(comment OceanZoneInstance-WholeOcean "The collection of all terrestrial oceanic zones, that is, those regions of Earth's oceans which are defined by physical parameters associated with the extent to which light penetrates the water column.")
(comment above-Completely "(#$above-Completely HIGHER LOWER) means that every point that is #$spatiallySubsumed by HIGHER is further from some 'grounded' reference level (such as seal level or the local surface of the Earth) than every point that is spatiallySubsumed by LOWER.")
(comment EarthsWholeOceansCoastalZone "Oceanic layer consisting of waters lying above the continental shelves")
(comment EarthsWholeOceansEuphoticZone "Oceanic layer consisting of the contiguous region of #$EarthsOceanSea where light can penetrate with sufficient intensity to sustain photosynthetic organisms.  This is the warmest region of ocean water, and has the highest levels of dissolved oxygen.")
(comment EarthsWholeOceansBathyalZone "Oceanic layer consisting of the contiguous region of #$EarthsOceanSea between the point where light can no longer penetrate with sufficient intensity to sustain photosynthesis and the point where all visible light ceases to penetrate.")
(comment EarthsWholeOceansAbyssalZone "The deepest layer of #$EarthsOceanSea, whose upper boundary is defined by the point at which visible light ceases to penetrate.")
(comment FreshWaterStratificationZoneType "A type-level collection:  each instance is a specialization of #$FreshWaterStratificationZone.")
(comment FreshWaterStratificationZone "The class of all freshwater stratification zones, i.e., layers of water characterized by a typical temperature, oxygen content, and nutrient level, with abrupt changes in these parameters at the boundaries.")
(comment LittoralZone "The class of all littoral zones of freshwater bodies.  In a typical #$FreshWaterLake, the littoral zone begins with very shallow water near the shoreline.  The zone boundary is defined as the depth at which rooted plants cease to grow.")
(comment LimneticZone "The class of all limnetic zones of freshwater bodies.  In a typical #$FreshWaterLake, the limnetic zone consists of the region of open water through which sunlight can penetrate.")
(comment ProfundalZone "The class of all profundal zones of freshwater bodies.  In a typical (and sufficiently deep) #$FreshWaterLake, the profundal zone is defined as the area between the point where sunlight ceases to penetrate and the point at which water ceases to significantly convect.")
(comment BenthicZone "The class of all benthic zones of freshwater bodies.  In very deep #$FreshWaterLakes (e.g., #$LakeBaikal), the benthic zone is a layer of water that begins at the deepest point at which convection cells penetrate:  in consequence, #$BenthicZone instances are very still and very cold, with extremely low levels of dissolved oxygen.")
(comment LittoralZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify a #$LittoralZone instance for a particular body of water.  Thus, (#$LittoralZoneFn WATER-BODY) denotes the #$LittoralZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment LimneticZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify a #$LimneticZone instance for a particular body of water.  Thus, (#$LimneticZoneFn WATER-BDOY) denotes the #$LimneticZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment ProfundalZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify a #$ProfundalZone instance for a particular body of water.  Thus, (#$ProfundalZoneFn WATER-BODY) denotes the #$ProfundalZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment BenthicZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify a #$BenthicZone instance for a particular body of water.  Thus, (#$BenthicZoneFn WATER-BODY) denotes the #$BenthicZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment littoralZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$LittoralZoneFn.")
(comment limneticZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$LimneticZoneFn.")
(comment profundalZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$ProfundalZoneFn.")
(comment benthicZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$BenthicZoneFn.")
(comment synonymousExternalConceptWRTPredicate-HasSpellingChange "<code>(#$synonymousExternalConceptWRTPredicate-HasSpellingChange THING SOURCE PRED STRING)</code> means that in the latest OWL ontology, THING is a new OWL class such that when THING stands in the relation PRED to any other thing, the string STRING (when it occurs in the data source SOURCE) denotes THING, and STRING is different from the old controlled vocabulary string that was used.")
(comment CauseOfDeathFn "<code>(#$CauseOfDeathFn AIL-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of situations in which some instance of <code>AIL-TYPE</code> has caused the death of an individual.  Generally, but with some exceptions, this function will take a specialization of #$AilmentCondition as its argument.")
(comment HemodynamicPressureReading "A specialization of #$MeasuringSomething,  Each instance of #$HemodynamicPressureReading is an event in which the energy imparted to the blood by contraction of the left ventricle is measured.")
(comment Water "An instance of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies and a specialization of #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$Water is one piece of some (pure or impure) portion of the chemical compound H2O.  Instances of #$Water may be in a gaseous, liquid, or solid state (see #$stateOfMatter); they may be salty or not, drinkable or not.  Examples include portions of the ocean, such as the #$BayOfBiscay and the #$BayOfBengal (see also #$SeaWater); bodies of fresh water, such as #$NiagaraFalls and the #$GangesRiver; quantities of chlorinated water (see #$PoolWater); and the contents of bottles of tonic water (see #$SeltzerWater).  Any portion of liquid that consists mostly of water but differs from it in one or more important properties (as does e.g. urine, coffee, and lemonade) is not itself an instance 
of #$Water, but has an instance of #$Water as its main constituent (see #$mainConstituent).  For the specialization of #$Water whose instances are 
pure, see (#$PureFn #$Water).")
(comment baseForm "(baseForm WORD STRING) means that STRING is one of the base forms for WORD.  Most words have only one base form, but multiple base forms are necessary in some cases.  For example, some prefixes are just as valid with or without a hyphen.  In these cases, there will be two valid #$baseForm values.  For example, 're-implant' and 'reimplant' are both good base forms for (#$WordWithPrefixFn #$Re-ThePrefix #$Implant-TheWord).  In general, #$baseForm should only be asserted for less-preferred base forms, while the preferred base form should be asserted with #$preferredBaseForm.")
(comment InorganicMaterial "A specialization of #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$InorganicMaterial is a tangible thing wholly composed of one or more types of inorganic molecule.  Instances of #$InorganicMaterial usually didn't originate as parts or products of living things.  Notable specializations of #$InorganicMaterial include #$Mineral, #$Metal, and #$Glass.")
(comment addElementsToValidTermSet-Genls "(#$addElementsToValidTermSet-Genls  TERM SET) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should be added to the valid term set.  This is useful when you want a particular trigger term to add certains terms to the valid term set where they can have formulas generated for them or used for instantiation into other formulas.")
(comment addElementsToValidTermSet-Isa "(#$addElementsToValidTermSet-Isa  TERM SET) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should be added to the valid term set.  This is useful when you want a particular trigger term to add certains terms to the valid term set where they can have formulas generated for them or used for instantiation into other formulas.")
(comment eventHasHemodynamicPressureReading "Relates a medical evaluation to a hemodynamic pressure reading that occurred during the evaluation.")
(comment opportunityCostForAgent "(#$opportunityCostForAgent AGENT PRODUCT-TYPE UNIT COST) means that the 'opportunity cost' to AGENT (i.e., the cost assessed in terms of lost or bypassed opportunities) of generating one UNIT of PRODUCT-TYPE is COST.")
(comment absoluteAdvantageInProduction "(#$absoluteAdvantageInProduction GEO-AGENT REGION PRODUCT-TYPE) means that, of every #$GeopoliticalEntity found in REGION, GEO-AGENT has the lowest production cost in producing units of PRODUCT-TYPE (see #$productionCostForAgent).")
(comment comparativeAdvantageInProduction "(#$comparativeAdvantageInProduction GEO-AGENT REGION PRODUCT-TYPE) means that, of every #$GeopoliticalEntity with territory in REGION, GEO-AGENT has the lowest opportunity cost in producing a unit of PRODUCT-TYPE (see #$opportunityCostForAgent).")
(comment productionCostForAgent "(#$productionCostForAgent AGENT PRODUCT-TYPE UNIT COST) means that in the context of the assertion, the cost in resources to agent of producing one UNIT of PRODUCT-TYPE is COST.")
(comment (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn StentPlacement objectActedOn-Type CommonCarotidArtery) "the placement of a stent into the carotid artery")
(comment (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn StentPlacement objectActedOn-Type CoronaryArtery) "placement of a stent inside one of the the patient's coronary arteries.")
(comment MedicalTreatmentFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance CONDITION of #$PhysiologicalConditionType, #Medical$TreatmentFn returns the collection of medical treatment events in which an instance of CONDITION is treated (so that the collection in question is a specialization of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent).  For example, (#$MedicalTreatmentFn #$HeartCondition) is the collection of all events in which some heart condition is medically treated.")
(comment HerniaRepairProcedure-Surgical "The collection of surgical hernia repair procedures.")
(comment RemovalFn "<code>(#$RemovalFn OBJ-TYPE)</code> denotes the class of #$RemovingSomething instances in which some instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> is removed from its previous position.")
(comment removalTypeOfType "(<code>#$removalTypeOfType OBJ-TYPE REMOVAL-TYPE)</code> means that in each instance of <code>REOMOVAL-TYPE</code>, some instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> is removed.")
(comment Cycle-Situation "The collection of all instances of #$Situation that are 'cyclical' in the sense of featuring iterated phases or scenes.  #$Cycle-Situations may be be serial or parallel (cf. #$Cycle-Serial and #$Cycle-Parallel) and may have a well-defined termination point or not (cf. #$Cycle-DefiniteTerminus and #$Cycle-IndefiniteTerminus).  All cycles, though, are characterized by repetition of a definable sequence of stages.")
(comment Cycle-Parallel "The collection of all instances of #$Cycle-Situation that can be subdivided into iterated stages which run in parallel.  For example, consider an instantiation of the Krebs cycle in a particular cell's metabolism.  At any given time, instantiations of all of the scenes or 'stages' of the cycle are likely to be running in the cell concurrently:  however the metabolic output of any instantiation of any given stage will be 'fed into' an instantiation of the next stage in the cycle.  This is the hallmark of a #$Cycle-Parallel.")
(comment Cycle-DefiniteTerminus "The collection of all instances of #$Cycle-Situation for which a definite termination point for the cycle can be identified.")
(disjointWith Cycle-DefiniteTerminus Cycle-IndefiniteTerminus)
(comment Cycle-IndefiniteTerminus "The collection of all instances of #$Cycle-Situation for which it is not possible or practical to specify a well-defined temporal endpoint for local reasoning.  For example, the #$WaterCycle-Terrestrial for the whole of #$PlanetEarth will end at some future date a few billions of years into the future when the #$Sun starts burning #$Carbon and the oceans boil, but for purposes of temporally 'local' reasoning, the cycle can be regarded as non-terminating.")
(comment WorkCycle "The collection of all thermodynamic cycles (instances of #$Cycle-Situation) in which potential energy is stored and then released in a controlled fashion over the course of the cycle.")
(comment BiologicalCycle "The collection of every #$WorkCycle which occurs as part of the life function of some #$BiologicalLivingObject.")
(comment EcologicalCycle "The class of all complex biochemical #$Cycle-Situations wherein biochemical substances such as #$Nitrogen, #$Phosphorus, #$Oxygen, #$Water, etc., move through the biosphere or a subset thereof (an #$Ecosystem) in a controlled storage and release of potential energy resulting from the interaction of multiple environmental agents.")
(comment cyclicalProcessTypeFocus "(#$cyclicalProcessTypeFocus CYCLE-CLASS FOCUS-CLASS) means that, in any instance of CYCLE-CLASS, there is an instance of FOCUS-CLASS that is in some way physically integrated into every output and every input of each stage within the cycle.  For example, consider the (#$NitrogenCycleFn #$ContinentOfNorthAmerica).  This is an instance of #$NitrogenCycle, and features instances of the characteristic stages associated with #$NitrogenCycles: #$NitrogenFixation, #$Nitrification, #$NitrogenAssimilation, etc..  Although free #$Nitrogen is emphatically not an input or output of every stage instantiation, #$Nitrogen or a chemical compound containing #$Nitrogen is involved in every stage of the process, and #$Nitrogen itself can be regarded as the principle role player in the narrative thread of the cycle's description.  Thus, #$Nitrogen is regarded as the #$cyclicalProcessTypeFocus of the #$NitrogenCycle.")
(comment WaterCycleOfRegionFn "A #$UnaryFunction used in denoting regionally constrained instances of #$WaterCycle-Terrestrial.")
(comment NitrogenCycleOfRegionFn "A #$UnaryFunction used in denoting regionally constrained instances of #$NitrogenCycle-Terrestrial.")
(comment PhosphorusCycleOfRegionFn "A #$UnaryFunction used in #$denoting regionally constrained instances of #$PhosphorusCycle-Terrestrial.")
(comment OceanStratificationZone "The collection of all hydrological layers in planetary oceans, as distinguished by characteristic boundary features.")
(comment OceanStratificationZoneType "A type-level collection:  each instance is an #$OceanStratificationZone.")
(comment CoastalZone "The #$Collection of all oceanic layers consisting of waters lying above continental shelves.")
(comment EuphoticZone "The collection of all oceanic layer where light can penetrate with sufficient intensity to sustain photosynthetic organisms.  The #$EuphoticZone instance for a given ocean is the warmest region of ocean water, and has the highest levels of dissolved oxygen.")
(comment BathyalZone "The collection of all oceanic layers consisting of the region of the water column between the point where light can no longer penetrate with sufficient intensity to sustain photosynthesis and the point where all visible light ceases to penetrate.")
(comment AbyssalZone "The collection of all oceanic layers defined by the point in the water column of a given #$Ocean where light ceases to penetrate entirely.  #$AbyssalZone instances are normally characertized by extremely cold temperatures and low levels of dissolved oxygen.")
(comment CoastalZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify a #$CoastalZone instance for a particular #$Ocean.  Thus, (#$CoastalZoneFn WATER-BODY) denotes the #$CoastalZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment EuphoticZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify a #$EuphoticZone instance for a particular #$Ocean.  Thus, (#$EuphoticZoneFn WATER-BODY) denotes the #$EuphoticZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment BathyalZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify a #$BathyalZone instance for a particular #$Ocean.  Thus, (#$BathyalZoneFn WATER-BODY) denotes the #$BathyalZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment AbyssalZoneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reify an #$AbyssalZone instance for a particular #$Ocean.  Thus, (#$AbyssalZoneFn WATER-BODY) denotes the #$AbyssalZone instance belonging to WATER-BODY.")
(comment coastalZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$CoastalZoneFn.")
(comment euphoticZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$EuphoticZoneFn.")
(comment bathyalZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$BathyalZoneFn.")
(comment abyssalZoneOf "The corresponding predicate of #$AbyssalZoneFn.")
(comment MarketSupplyFn "A function which returns the quantity of instances of a given #$ExistingObjectType and specialization of #$Product that suppliers in a #$Market are willing to provide for a specific #$MonetaryValue.  More specifically, (#$MarketSupplyFn MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE PRICE) denotes the total quantity of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE that suppliers in MARKET are willing to supply for PRICE. Thus, e.g. (#$MarketSupplyFn (#$MarketFn #$Automobile (#$YearFn 2008) #$Italy) #$LamborghiniP400Car (#$USDollar 60000)) denotes how many Lamborghini P400s will be supplied in the 2008 Italian automobile market for a price of $60,000 per car.")
(comment MarketDemandFn "A function which returns the quantity of instances of a given #$ExistingObjectType and specialization of #$Product that consumers in a #$Market are willing to buy for a specific #$MonetaryValue. More specifically, (#$MarketDemandFn MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE PRICE) denotes the total quantity of instances of PRODUC-TYPE that consumers in MARKET are willing to buy for PRICE.  Thus, e.g. (#$MarketDemandFn (#$MarketFn #$Automobile (#$YearFn 2008) #$LosAngeles) #$LamborghiniP400Car (#$USDollar 60000)) denotes how many Lamborghinis will/would be purchased by consumers in the 2008 L.A. auto market for a price of $60,000 per car.")
(comment MarketSupplyInUnitsFn "A funtion which returns the quantity of instances of a given #$ExistingStuffType, as measured by a specified #$UnitOfMeasure, that suppliers in a given #$Market will supply for a given monetary value.  More specifically, (#$MarketSupplyInUnitsFn MARKET STUFF-TYPE UNIT PRICE) denotes the number of UNITs of STUFF-TYPE that suppliers in MARKET will supply for PRICE.  Thus, e.g., (#$MarketSupplyInUnitsFn (#$MarketFn #$Oil (#$YearFn 2008) #$SaudiArabia) #$Petroleum-CrudeOil #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume (#$Dollar 110)) denotes the number of barrels of crude oil that the 2008 Saudi oil market will supply for a price of $110.00.")
(comment MarketDemandInUnitsFn "A funtion which returns the quantity of instances of a given #$ExistingStuffType, as measured by a specified #$UnitOfMeasure, that consumers in a given #$Market will demand for a given monetary value.  More specifically, (#$MarketDemandInUnitsFn MARKET STUFF-TYPE UNIT PRICE) denotes the number of UNITs of STUFF-TYPE that consumers in MARKET will demand for PRICE.  Thus, e.g., (#$MarketSupplyInUnitsFn (#$MarketFn #$Oil (#$YearFn 2008) #$LosAngeles) #$Petroleum-CrudeOil #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume (#$Dollar 110)) denotes the number of barrels of crude oil that the 2008 Los Angeles oil market will demand for a price of $110.00.")
(comment EconomicLaw "The collection of all true propositions constituing general, law-like economic principles used to describe and predict economic trends.")
(comment LawOfSupply "The #$LawOfSupply states that as the price of a good within a market increases, the quantity of that good supplied within a given period will increase, other things being equal.")
(comment LawOfDemand "The #$LawOfDemand states that, as the price of a good rises within a given market, the quantity of that good demanded by consumers within the market falls.")
(comment marketQuantitySupplyForPrice "The corresponding predicate of #$MarketSupplyFn.")
(comment marketQuantitySupplyInUnitsForPrice "The corresponding predicate of #$MarketSupplyInUnitsFn.")
(comment ruleAssertionCorrespondsToLawSpecification "<code>(#$ruleAssertionCorrespondsToLawSpecification ASSERT LAW)</code> means that the #$LawOfNature, <code>LAW</code>, is expressed in CycL as the #$CycLRuleSpecification, <code>ASSERT</code>.")
(comment CycLAssertionSpecification "A specialization of #$ProgramStepSpecification.  Each instance of #$CycLAssertionSpecification is a description of an assertion.  It may be an actual asserted sentence in the Cyc KB, or it may be a description of how an assertion should function in the KB or in some Cyc-based application.  At a minimum, this description should include the CycL assertion that constitutes the specification, via #$assertionOfSpecification.  Other parameters can also be represented, e.g., applications whose functionalities are supported by the assertion.")
(comment assertionOfSpecification "(#$assertionOfSpecification SPEC ASSERT) means that the #$CycLAssertionSpecification SPEC is expressed in CycL as the #$CycLAssertion, ASSERT.")
(comment specificationExpressesProposition "(#$specificationExpressesProposition SPEC PROP) means that the #$CycLAssertionSpecfication SPEC describes a #$CycLAssertion that expresses the #$Proposition PROP.")
(comment LawOfSupply-SpecificationForObjects "A CycL specification of the #$LawOfSupply, applied to #$Product classes which are instances of #$ExistingObjectType.")
(comment LawOfSupply-SpecificationForStuffs "A CycL specification of the #$LawOfSupply, applied to #$Product classes which are instances of #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment LawOfDemand-SpecificationForObjects "A CycL specification of the #$LawOfDemand, applied to #$Product classes which are instances of #$ExistingObjectType.")
(comment LawOfDemand-SpecificationForStuffs "A CycL specification of the #$LawOfDemand, applied to #$ProductClasses which are instances of #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment marketQuantityDemandInUnitsForPrice "The corresponding predicate of #$MarketDemandInUnitsFn.")
(comment CardiacValveProsthesisType-Other "The collection of types of functionally defined valve prostheses that need an alternate defining rule for #$valveProsthesisTypeImplanted/Explanted.")
(comment WaterCycle-Terrestrial "The collection of all hydrologic cycles (cf. #$HydrologicCycle) occurring at or near the #$EarthsTopographicSurface.  Most involve the biological processes of living systems in one form or another.")
(comment ArtesianTransport "The collection of all natural processes in which water is transported underground through artesian channels from one point under (or within) the #$EarthsTopographicSurface to another.")
(comment VegetableTranspiration "The collection of all processes of transpiration in multicellular plant life growing on the surface of the #$PlanetEarth, wherein water is drawn through the vegetable tissues by evaporative perfusion, eventually escaping to #$TheEarthsAtmosphere as water vapor.")
(comment HydrologicInfiltration "The collection of all processes wherein water infiltrates or perfuses through the upper layers of soil in #$EarthsTopographicSurface and penetrates to the level of artesian channels in the bedrock.")
(comment HydrologicExfiltration "The collection of all processes wherein water perfuses up from the level of bedrock through the upper layers of #$EarthsTopographicSurface, to flow freely at the surface in the form of artesian springs and wells.")
(comment AtmosphericWaterVaporTransport "The collection of all processes wherein water circulates freely in Earth's atmosphere in the form of water vapor.")
(comment NitrogenCycle-Terrestrial "The collection of all processes wherein #$Nitrogen is cycled through the terrestrial biosphere in the form of atmospheric gas (#$GaseousFn Nitrogen) and #$NitrousOxide, as well as in chemical #$Nitrate and #$PotassiumNitrite compounds, #$Ammonia, and #$AmmoniumIons")
(comment NitrogenFixationProcess "The collection of processes whereby atmospheric nitrogen is incorporated or 'fixed' into ammonia and nitrate compounds where it can be used by #$BiologicalLivingOrganisms.  Nitrogen fixation is implemented on a small scale by some meteorological processes, and on a large scale by soil bacteria, often species associated with the roots of legumes such as soybeans or clover.")
(comment AmmoniumAssimilationProcess-Autotrophic "The collection of processes wherein plants absorb ammonia, ammonium ions, and nitrate ions through their roots and convert them into compounds that can be consumed by heterotrophs.")
(comment NitrogenAssimilation-Heterotrophic "The collection of processes wherein heterotrophs or groups consume vegetable material and take up #$Nitrogen in the process.")
(comment AmmonificationProcess "The collection of processes whereing decay bacteria convert dead organisms into #$Ammonia and #$AmmoniumIons.")
(comment DenitrificationProcess "The collection of processes wherein specialized bacteria, usually anaerobic bacteria, convert #$Ammonia into #$Nitrites and #$Nitrates, and thence into #$Nitrogen and #$NitrousOxide which are released into the atmosphere in gaeous form.")
(comment NitrificationProcess-Bacterial "The collection of processes whereby soil bacteria convert #$AmmoniumIons into #$Nitrates.")
(comment AmmoniumAssimilationProcess-Autotrophic "The collection of processes wherein #$Autotrophs (usually #$Plants) absorb ammonia, ammonium ions, and nitrate ions through their roots and convert them into compounds that can be consumed by heterotrophs.")
(comment EcosystemOfRegionFn "")
(comment ecosystemOfRegion "The corresponding predicate of #$EcosystemOfRegionFn")
(comment agentInEcosystem "")
(comment componentInSystem-FunctionalRole "The most general Cyc #$SystemRolePredicate, analogous in the #$SystemRolePredicate hierarchy to #$actors in the #$ActorSlot hierarchy. (#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means simply that AGENT plays some functional role in SYSTEM that is otherwise unspecified.")
(comment BicameralLegislativeOrganization "A specialization of #$LegislativeOrganization.  Each instance of #$BicameralLegislativeOrganization is a legislature consisting of two legislative chambers.")
(comment Parliament "#$Parliament is a specialization of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization and #$LegislativeOrganization.  Each instance of #$Parliament is a legislative body of a government which adheres to a parliamentary system (see #$ParliamentaryGovernment).")
(comment PhilosophicalLiteraryWork "A specialization of #$ProseLiteraryWork-CW.  Each instance is a literary work intended to contibute to the field of philosophy.")
(comment LegalCode-ModernWestern "A specialization of #$LegalCode and #$GovernmentCOC-ModernWestern. Each instance of this collection is a #$LegalCode in use in modern western countries.")
(comment RatifyingSomething "A specialization of #$PoliticalEvent and #$AdoptingANorm (qq.v.).  This is the collection of all acts of ratifying an #$Agreement or #$CodeOfConduct (qq.v.).   Each instance of #$RatifyingSomething is an political action in which an #$Organization formally sanctions or approves some proposed agreement or code.  In many cases, the ratifying organization is the #$governingBody of some larger subsuming group, and the agreement/code concerns the members of the larger group.
<p>
In some cases, ratification by the relevant organization is a necessary and sufficient condition for the agreement/code's taking effect at all.  For example, a city council might ratify a proposed municipal law (or not), and an electorate might ratify a certain ballot measure (or not).  In other cases (such as instances of #$RatifyingAnInternationalAgreement), a particular organization's ratifying the agreement/code is just a necessary and sufficient condition for <i>that organization's</i> being bound (see #$normativelyBoundAgents) by the agreement/code, which other groups may independently decide to ratify.")
(comment BritishColoniesThatFormedTheUnitedStates "A sub-collection of #$Colony-GeopoliticalEntity. Each instance is one of the 13 British colonies that formed the original states of the United States.")
(comment RatificationOfAgreementByAgentFn "<code>(#$RatificationOfAgreementByAgentFn AGENT AGREEMENT)</code> denotes the ratification of <code>AGREEMENT</code> by <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment firstPublicationDate-CW "<code>(#$firstPublicationDate-CW WORK DATE)</code> means that the #$ConceptualWork <code>WORK</code> was first published on #$Date <code>DATE</code>.  Publication here means the distribution of more than one copy of a work to the public or an identifiable subset of the public consisting of more than a few members.  Note that publication here does not imply that a particular #$ConceptualWork has been printed or physically distributed (a work may be electronically distributed).  To have a publication date implies that a #$ConceptualWork has been made available to, or accessible by, the public or a portion of the public.  Publication date is not the same as creation date (see #$workCreationDate).  A #$ConceptualWork that has been created, but not made available to anyone except the creator of the work, has not been published and has no #$firstPublicationDate-CW.  The #$firstPublicationDate-CW of a #$ConceptualWork is necessarily the same as the #$publicationDate-IBO of the first instantiation of that #$ConceptualWork that is published. ")
(comment workCreationDate "<code>(#$workCreationDate WORK DATE)</code> means that <code>WORK</code> was completed on <code>DATE</code>.  Generally, <code>DATE</code> will be before the date on which <code>WORK</code> is published, if it is published.")
(comment ratificationEventOfAgreementByAgent "(#$ratificationEventOfAgreementByAgent AGENT AGREEMENT EVENT) means that AGREEMENT is ratified by AGENT during EVENT.")
(comment AutocatalyticProcess "The collection of all self-organizing processes consisting in multiple and often-interlinked thermodynamic work cycles whereby a #$FunctionalSystem is maintained over time within its own operational parameters.  Examples include the metabolism of an #$Organism-Whole, the economy of a nation-state (considered as a myriad of preferential buying-selling interactions), or the skein of interlinked biochemical processes realizing an #$Ecosystem.")
(comment autocatalyticProcessImplementsSystem "The corresponding predicate of #$AutocatalyticProcessOfSystemFn.")
(comment producerOfResourceTypeInSystem "(#$producerOfResourceTypeInSystem AGENT RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM) implies that (#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT), that, where AUTOCATALYSIS is the #$autocatalyticProcessImplementsSystem of SYSTEM, AGENT is capable of being the #$doneBy of makings of instances of RESOURCE-TYPE that are part of AUTOCATALYSIS, and that there exists a CONSUMER (which could be equivalent to AGENT but need not be) such that (#$consumerOfResourceTypeInSystem CONSUMER RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM).")
(comment TheEarthsBiosphere "The whole biosphere of #$PlanetEarth, considered as a total #$Ecosystem.")
(comment resourceTypeInSystem "(#$resourceTypeInSystem RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM) means that, within the (possibly temporal) context of the assertion, there is at least one CONSUMER such that (#$consumerOfResourceTypeInSystem CONSUMER RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM).")
(comment renewableResourceTypeInSystem "(#$renewableResourceTypeInSystem RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM) means that within the (possibly temporal) context of the assertion, there exists at least one PRODUCER such that (#$producerOfResourceTypeInSystem PRODUCER RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM).")
(comment nonRenewableResourceTypeInSystem "(#$renewableResourceTypeInSystem RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM) means that within the (possibly temporal) context of the assertion, there exists no PRODUCER such that (#$producerOfResourceTypeInSystem PRODUCER RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM).")
(comment systemHasAccessTo "A #$FunctionalSystem predicate that is intended to capture the difficult concept of systemic 'access':  generally speaking (#$systemHasAccessTo SYSTEM RESOURCE) means that it is possible that (#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM RESOURCE).")
(comment Resource "The collection of all #$Individuals INST such that there is a #$FunctionalSystem SYSTEM and a #$Collection TYPE such that (#$systemHasAccessTo SYSTEM INST), (#$isa INST TYPE), and (#$resourceTypeInSystem TYPE SYSTEM).")
(comment RenewableResource "The collection of #$Individuals INST such that there is a #$FunctionalSystem SYSTEM and a #$Collection TYPE such that (#$renewableResourceTypeInSystem TYPE SYSTEM), (#$isa INST TYPE), and (#$systemHasAccessTo SYSTEM INST).")
(comment NonRenewableResource "The collection of #$Individuals INST such that there is a #$FunctionalSystem SYSTEM and a #$Collection TYPE such that (#$nonRenewableResourceTypeInSystem TYPE SYSTEM), (#$isa INST TYPE), and (#$systemHasAccessTo SYSTEM INST).")
(comment OldGrowthForest-Existential "The collection of all #$Forests where some growth exists that is more than a hundred years old.  Instances contain forest growth which has been developing over a period of centuries, and for this reason are considered to be non-renewable biospheric resources within the context of a given year, or even of a given century, because no biological mechanism exists which can replace them within this time frame.  However, this doesn't preclude the possibility that logging has occurred within the forest - a case in point being the #$Amazon-Region.")
(comment OldGrowthForest-Absolute "The collection of all #$Forests where no logging has occurred for the past several hundred years.  Instances contain forest growth which has been developing over a period of centuries, and for this reason are considered to be non-renewable biospheric resources within the context of a given year, or even of a given century, because no biological mechanism exists which can replace them within this time frame.")
(disjointWith OldGrowthForest-Absolute SecondGrowthForest)
(comment SecondGrowthForest "The collection of forests wherein some logging has occurred, but where there has also been some secondary growth of trees in the affected areas.")
(comment TreeFarm-Plantation "The collection of all commercially developed #$Forests which are grown and maintained for the purpose of harvesting timber.")
(comment CriteriaPollutantType "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Instances are #$TangibleStuffCompositionTypes which the E.P.A has determined to be particularly harmful to human health and welfare.")
(disjointWith StationaryPollutionSource-Artifactual MobilePollutionSource-Artifactual)
(comment dateOfDedication "<code>(#$dateOfDedication ARTIFACT DATE)</code> means that <code>ARTIFACT</code>, an instance of #$Artifact is/was/will be officially dedicated on <code>DATE</code>, an instance of #$Date.  Where <code>CEREMONY</code> is the instance of #$DedicationCeremony for <code>ARTIFACT</code> (see #$ceremonyDedicatesArtifact), <code>DATE</code> will be the date of (see #$dateOfEvent) <code>CEREMONY</code>.")
(comment hasLeaders "<code>(#$hasLeaders GROUP LEADER)</code> means that <code>LEADER</code> is (one of) the leader(s) of <code>GROUP</code>  that to some extent directs the activities or policies of <code>GROUP</code>.  If <code>LEADER</code> is an #$Organization, it is a member organization of <code>GROUP</code> that to some extent directs the activities or policies of <code>GROUP</code>.")
(comment propertyForeclosed "<code>(#$propertyForeclosed FORECLOSING OBJ)</code> means that in the #$ForeclosingEvent <code>FORCECLOSING</code>, <code>OBJ</code> is the property forclosed.")
(comment UnicameralLegislativeOrganization "A specialization of #$LegislativeOrganization.  Each instance of #$UnicameralLegislativeOrganization is a legislature consisting of a single legislative chamber.")
(disjointWith BicameralLegislativeOrganization UnicameralLegislativeOrganization)
(comment proposalFloated "<code>(#$proposalFloated MEET PROPOSAL)</code> means that during <code>MEET</code>, the proposal <code>PROPSAL</code> was offered for consideration.")
(comment proposalAdopted "<code>(#$proposalAdopted MEET PROPOSAL)</code> means that during <code>MEET</code>, the proposal <code>PROPSAL</code> was offered for consideration and ultimately adopted by the meeting participants.")
(comment specificationCompromises "<code>(#$specificationCompromises RESULT-NORM COMPROMISED-NORM)</code> means that <code>RESULT-NORM</code> results form an attempt to compromise <code>COMPROMISED-NORM</code> with some other norm.")
(comment specificationInfluencesCWContent "<code>(#$specificationInfluencesCWContent NORM CW)</code> means that the specification <code>NORM</code> influences the content of the #$ConceptualWork <code>CW</code>.")
(comment UnitedStatesConstitutionalAmendment "The collection of amendments to the #$USConstitution.")
(comment populationBasedNumberUsedToDetermineProportionalRepresentation "<code>(#$populationBasedNumberUsedToDetermineProportionalRepresentation N AGENT ORG)</code> means that the number <code>N</code> is used as the basis for determining how many representatives <code>AGENT</code> is entitleds to have in the #$LegislativeOrganization <code>ORG</code>.")
(disjointWith Slave (CollectionDifferenceFn Person Slave))
(comment legalCodeOfGovernment "<code>(#$legalCodeOfGovernment CODE GOV)</code> means that <code>CODE</code> is part of the legal code that applies to or is enforced by <code>GOV</code>.")
(comment FederalistPapers "A group of papers published between October 1787 and August 1788, advocating the ratification of the #$USConstitution.  The papers were authored by #$AlexanderHamilton, #$JamesMadison, and #$JohnJay.")
(disjointWith PrimaryPollutant SecondaryPollutant)
(comment religionOfRule "<code>(#$religionOfRule GEO-ENT RELIGION)</code> means that #$Religion <code>RELIGON</code> is the official religion of <code>GEO-ENT</code>.")
(comment givesPreferentialTreatmentToEntityOfType "<code>(#$givesPreferentialTreatmentToEntityOfType AGENT OBJ COL)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> gives preferential treatment to <code>OBJ</code> over all other instances of the class <code>COL</code>, where <code>OBJ</code> is itself an instance of <code>COL</code>.")
(comment specificationContent "<code>(#$specificationContent SPEC CONTENT)</code> means that <code>CONTENT</code> expressess the propositional content of <code>SPEC</code>.")
(comment entitledToNConcurrentRepresentativesInLegislativeOrg "<code>(#$entitledToNConcurrentRepresentativesInLegislativeOrg AGENT N ORG)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is entitled to <code>N</code> many concurrent representatives in the #$LegislativeOrganization <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment Law "A #$Law is a miniature #$GovernmentCOC that expresses a legal requirement or restriction.  For instance, one #$Law might say, effectively, that bigamy is illegal.  A #$Law is declared to be part of a #$LegalCode by using #$subWorks.  Note that one #$Law can be part of more than one #$LegalCode.")
(comment Bill-ProposedLaw "The collection of all bills that have been filed before a legislature for consideration to become a law (see #$Law).  Different government have different procedures for enabling bills to become laws. If passed, a federal bill in the United States must either be approved (or allowed to become law without specific approval) by the chief executive or repassed (by a supermajority) over the veto of the chief executive.")
(comment LegislativeOrganization "A specialization of both #$Assembly-SocialGroup and #$GovernmentalOrganization. Each instance of #$LegislativeOrganization is a legislative (lawmaking, policy-formulating) organization that is part of some #$RegionalGovernment.")
(comment ReferralOfBillToCommittee-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  After a bill is introduced in the U.S. Congress, it is referred to an appropriate committee for deliberation.")
(comment MemberOfUSCongress "A specialization of #$ElectedOfficial and #$Legislator (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$MemberOfUSCongress is either a #$USSenator or #$USRepresentative.")
(comment Legislating-USFederal "A specialization of #$Legislating.  Each instance of this collection is a process performed by the #$USCongress and the President to determine which bills (see #$Bill-ProposedLaw) will become federal laws (see #$Law).")
(comment IntroducingABill-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$IntroducingABill-USFederalLegislating is an event in which one or more members of the #$USCongress introduces a bill for consideration as a potential law by the #$USCongress.  The person or persons who introduce the bill are the sponsors or cosponsors of the bill.")
(comment CommitteeAction-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  After a bill is introduced in the U.S. Congress, it is referred to an appropriate committee (see #$ReferralOfBillToCommittee-USFederalLegislating). Then the committee processes the bill by, for example, holding hearings or requesting information, or sending the bill to a sub-committee.  The collection #$CommitteeAction-USFederalLegislating denotes the collection of such potentially complex committee actions.")
(comment FloorAction-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$FloorAction-USFederalLegislating is an event in which a bill is placed on the calendar, debated at the scheuled time, and then voted on.  If the bill passes the vote, it is sent to the other chamber unless that chamber already has a similar measure under consideration. If either chamber does not pass the bill then it dies. If the House and Senate pass the same bill then it is sent to the President. If the House and Senate pass different bills they are sent to Conference Committee.")
(comment ConferenceCommitteeAction-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$ConferenceCommitteeAction-USFederalLegislating is an event in which a Conference Committee consisting of members from each chamber meet to work out differences in the bills that they pass.")
(comment VetoOverride-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$ConferenceCommitteeAction-USFederalLegislating is an event in which a Conference Committee consisting of members from each chamber meet to work out differences in the bills that they pass.")
(comment BillBecomesFederalLaw-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$BillBecomesFederalLaw-USFederalLegislating is an event in which a bill has completed the legislative process and thereby becomes a law.")
(comment IntroducingSomething "A specialization of #$SocialOccurrence.  Instances of this collection are events in which something is explicitly (but not necessarily formally) introduced to some agent or groump of agents. In an event of this sort, it is presumed (perhaps incorrectly) that the introduced object is not otherwise familiar to those with whom it is introduced (cf. #$acquaintedWith). A notable specializaton of this collection is #$IntroducingSomeone.")
(comment USCongressionalCommittee "A specialization of #$Committee-Organization.  Each instance of #$USCongressionalCommittee is a legislative sub-organization in the United States Congress that handles a specific duty. The U.S. Congress divides its tasks among approximately 200 committees and subcommittees.")
(comment constitutionEstablishesSystemOfGovernment "<code>(#$constitutionEstablishesSystemOfGovernment CONST GOV-TYPE)</code> means that the principles embodied in <code>CONST</code> ensure that the government type established by <code>CONST</code> is of the type <code>GOV-TYPE</code>.")
(disjointWith RepresentativeDemocracy DirectDemocracy)
(comment jurisdictionRegion "<code>(#$jurisdictionRegion ORG REG)</code> means that the #$LegalGovernmentOrganization <code>ORG</code> has jurisdiction over the #$GeographicalRegion <code>REG</code>.  It is not necessarily the case, however, that <code>ORG</code> operates within <code>REG</code>.  To represent that an organization operates within a certain region, consider the predicate #$performsInsAtLocation.")
(comment populationLevelOfTypeInEcosystem "(#$populationLevelOfTypeInEcosystem ORG-TYPE ECOSYSTEM NUMBER) means that the number of instances of ORG-TYPE currently functioning as components in ECOSYSTEM (#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole) is NUMBER.")
(disjointWith PresidentialVeto-USLegislativeProcess PresidentSigningBillIntoLaw-USLegislativeProcess)
(comment PresidentialVeto-USLegislativeProcess "A specialization of #$VetoingSomething. Each instance of #$PresidentialVeto-USLegislativeProcess is an event in which the President of the United States vetos a bill.")
(comment PresidentialReview-USFederalLegislating "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$PresidentialReview-USFederalLegislating is an event in which the US President either signs a bill into law #$PresidentSigningBillIntoLaw-USLegislativeProcess) or vetos it (see #$PresidentialVeto-USLegislativeProcess).")
(comment PresidentSigningBillIntoLaw-USLegislativeProcess "A specialization of #$ApprovingARequest. Each instance of #$PresidentSigningBillIntoLaw-USLegislativeProcess is an event in which the President of the United States signs a bill, thereby making it law.")
(comment Election "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Vote-CollectiveDecision and #$Competition.  Each instance of #$Election is an event in which members of an #$Organization cast votes to determine who, out of a group of candidates, will hold some position in that organization.  Important specializations of this collection include #$ElectionForOffice and #$PrimaryElection.")
(comment tenuresOf "<code>(#$tenuresOf PERSON INTERVAL)</code> connects a particular #$Person with one of the #$TimeInPosition-Serveds he or she has/does/will hold. For example, there are two contiguous intervals <code>INT-1</code> and <code>INT-2</code>, in which (#$isa #$BillClinton #$UnitedStatesPresident) holds, such that <code>(#$tenuresOf #$BillClinton INT-1)</code> and <code>(#$tenuresOf #$BillClinton INT-1)</code> each hold.")
(comment TimeInPosition-Served "The collection of #$StaticSituations in which a particular #$Person holds a particular #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg. For #$AppointedOffices and #$ElectedOfficials, this period of time is typically standardized. Each #$TimeInPosition-Served is associated with a particular #$TimeInPosition-Obligation; for example, #$BillClinton is associated with two #$TimeInPosition-Serveds, each with its own #$TimeInPosition-Obligation. The interval served cannot extend beyond the limits imposed by the associated obligation, but could end prematurely (e.g., in cases of #$AssassinatingSomeone or #$RetirementEvents).")
(comment obligationDuration "<code>(#$obligationPeriod OBLIGATION DURATION)</code> is used to indicate the duration of time during which a particular #$Obligation is in force. Cf. #$obligationPeriod.")
(comment termOfElectedOfficeType "<code>(#$termOfElectedOfficeType OFFICE DURATION)</code> is used to indicate the standard duration of time during which a person elected to the position <code>OFFICE</code> is obligated to serve in that office.")
(comment vicePresidentOfCountry "<code>(#$vicePresidentOfCountry  COUNTRY PERSON)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> is the vice-president of <code>COUNTRY</code>.")
(comment PocketVeto-USLegislativeProcess "A specialization of #$VetoingSomething. Each instance of #$PresidentialVeto-USLegislativeProcess is an event in which the President of the United States vetos a bill by refraining from taking action on it during the 10 days alloted for action, while during those 10 days a congressional session ends.")
(disjointWith PresidentSigningBillIntoLaw-USLegislativeProcess PresidentAllowingABillToBecomeLawWithoutSigning-USLegislativeProcess)
(comment minorityPartyOfLegislativeOrganization "<code>(#$minorityPartyOfLegislativeOrganization ORG PARTY)</code> means that aminority of persons serving in <code>ORG</code> are members of  <code>PARTY</code>.")
(comment majorityPartyOfLegislativeOrganization "<code>(#$majorityPartyOfLegislativeOrganization ORG PARTY)</code> means that the majority of persons serving in <code>ORG</code> are members of  <code>PARTY</code>.")
(comment USSenateMajorityLeader "The leader of the majority party in the U.S. Senate.")
(comment USSenateMinorityLeader "The leader of the minority party in the U.S. Senate.")
(comment USHouseMajorityLeader "The leader of the majority party in the U.S. House of Representatives.")
(comment USHouseMinorityLeader "The leader of the minority party in the U.S. House of Representatives.")
(comment organizationHead "<code>(#$organizationHead ORG HEAD)</code> means that <code>HEAD</code> is the unique leader of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment organizationOfPartyInLegislativeOrganization "<code>(#$organizationOfPartyInLegislativeOrganization LEG-ORG PARTY ORG)</code> means that <code>ORG</code> is the organization of persons serving in <code>LEG-ORG</code> who are members of <code>PARTY</code>.")
(comment USCongressionalCommittee-Standing "A specialization of #$USCongressionalCommittee (q.v.).  Each instance of #$USCongressionalCommittee-Standing is a permanent specialized committee in the U.S. Congress.")
(comment USCongressionalCommittee-Joint "A specialization of #$USCongressionalCommittee (q.v.).  Each instance of #$USCongressionalCommittee-Joint is a congressional committee made up of members from both the House and Senate.")
(disjointWith USCongressionalCommittee-Standing USCongressionalCommittee-Joint)
(disjointWith USCongressionalCommittee-Standing USCongressionalCommittee-Select)
(disjointWith USCongressionalCommittee-Joint USCongressionalCommittee-Select)
(disjointWith USCongressionalCommittee-Joint USCongressionalCommittee-Conference)
(disjointWith USCongressionalCommittee-Standing USCongressionalCommittee-Conference)
(disjointWith USCongressionalCommittee-Select USCongressionalCommittee-Conference)
(comment USCongressionalCommittee-Conference "A specialization of #$USCongressionalCommittee (q.v.).  Each instance of #$USCongressionalCommittee-Conference is a joint committee (consisting of members of both chambers) organized to negotiate a compromise bill.")
(comment USCongressionalCommittee-Select "A specialization of #$USCongressionalCommittee (q.v.).  Each instance of #$USCongressionalCommittee-Select is a temporary congressional committee organized for a special purpose, such as carrying out an investigation as part of the oversight power over the executive branch.")
(comment inReactionTo "This is the weakest and most general of all the predicates dealing with \"reaction\" or \"response\" that incorporates an intentional component.  <code>(#$inReactionTo ACT SITUATION)</code> means that some <code>AGENT</code> has a goal such that <code>AGENT</code> believes <code>SITUATION</code> changes the likelihood of the goal, and that one of the outcomes of this belief is <code>ACT</code>, which is performed by (see #$performedBy) <code>AGENT</code> (i.e., <code>ACT</code> is done deliberately).  This predicate does not cover cases of involuntary or instinctive reaction, for which a weaker sense of causation is appropriate.")
(comment PigeonholedBill-USCongress "A specialization of #$Bill-ProposedLaw.  Each instance of #$PigeonholedBill-USCongress is a bill that has been introduced and referred to a committee, but which the committee refuses to vote out.")
(comment outputCW "<code>#$outputCW EVENT CW)</code> means that during the #$CreationEvent <code>EVENT</code>, the #$ConceptualWork <code>CW</code> is created.")
(comment commanderInChief "<code>(#$commanderInChief ORG AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is the commander in chief of the #$GovernmentMilitaryOrganization, <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment CleanWaterAct "The #$CleanWaterAct emplaced regulatory and non-regulatory tools to protect all surface waters in the United States.  It sharply reduced direct pollutant discharges into waterways, financed municipal wastewater treatment facilities and regulated pollutant runoff, and supported the protection and propagation of fish, shellfish, and wildlife.")
(comment SafeDrinkingWaterAct "The #$SafeDrinkingWaterAct established a federal program to monitor and increase the safety of the drinking water supply.")
(comment OceanDumpingAct "The #$OceanDumpingAct made it unlawful for any person to dump, or transport for the purpose of dumping, sewage, sludge, or industrial waste into ocean waters.")
(comment OilSpillPreventionAndLiabilityAct "The #$OilSpillPreventionAndLiabilityAct strengthened the ability of the E.P.A. to prevent and respond to catastrophic oil spills, and established a trust fund (financed by a tax on oil production) which is available to clean up spills.")
(comment ResourceConservationAndRecoveryAct "The #$ResourceConservationAndRecoveryAct established a solid waste program that encourages states to develop comprehensive plans for management of nonhazardous solid waste (industrial and municipal), set criteria for municipal solid waste landfills and solid waste disposal facilities, and prohibited open dumping of solid waste.  It also established a hazardous waste program that established a system for control of hazardous waste from the time it is generated until its ultimate disposal.  Finally, it created an undergound storage tank (UST) program for regulating underground storage tanks containing hazardus substances and petroleum products..  ")
(comment ComprehensiveEnvironmentalResponseCompensationAndLiabilityAct "Also known as the 'superfund' act, the #$ComprehensiveEnvironmentalResponseCompensationAndLiabilityAct created a tax on the chemical and petroleum industries and provided broad Federal authority to respond directly to releases or threatened releases of hazardous substances.  It also established prohibitions and requirements concerning closed and abandoned hazardous waste sites, provided for liability of persons responsible for release of hazardous waste, and established a trust fund to provide for cleanup of hazardous waste emissions in cases where no responsible party could be identified.")
(comment ToxicSubstancesControlAct "The #$ToxicSubstanceControlAct, or TOSCA, gave the #$EnvironmentalProtectionAgency the ability to track the industrial chemicals iproduced or imported into the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  It also enables the #$EnvironmentalProtectionAgency to require reporting or testing of industrial chemicals that may pose an environmental or human health hazard, and allows the #$EnvironmentalProtectionAgency to ban the manufacture and import of chemicals that it judges to pose an unreasonable risk.")
(comment NuclearWastePolicyAct "The #$NuclearWastePolicyAct established the Federal Government's responsibility to provide a place for the permanent disposal of high-level radioactive waste, and the responsibility of the generators of such waste to bear the cost of permanent disposal.")
(comment LawOfDiminishingMarginalUtility "An instance of #$EconomicLaw that claims that, over a given period, as instances of some good are accumulated (or consumed) by an agent, the utility or desirability of those instances to that agent decrease.  For example, if an individual has a taste for apples and is hungry, he or she might be willing to purchase one or two apples at some set price, but will value additional apples less and less (and will be willing to pay less and less) as he or she consumes more.")
(comment propositionExpressedByCycLAssertion "<code>(#$propositionExpressedByCycLAssertion PROPOSITION ASSERTION)</code> means that the #$CycLAssertion <code>ASSERTION</code> is an assertion of the content of <code>PROPOSITION</code>, an instance of #$Proposition.")
(comment GovernmentalAdministrationOfficial "The collection of all members of any #$GovernmentalAdministration.  They are normally in appointed positions, whether or not their appointment has to be ratified by a legislative body.  Their positions are normally policy-making, high level policy-implementation, or advisory positions.  They are very likely to lose their position as a #$GovernmentalAdministrationOfficial upon a change in administration, especially if there is a party change.")
(comment WhiteHousePressSecretary "The primary spokesperson for the Administration of the President of the United States.")
(comment WhiteHouseChiefOfStaff "The senior member of the U.S. President's staff.")
(comment ForeignPolicy "A specialization of #$Policy.  Each instance of #$ForeignPolicy is a policy of a country for dealing with other countries.")
(comment DomesticPolicy "A specialization of #$Policy.  Each instance of #$DomesticPolicy is a policy for domestic affairs.")
(comment entitlementChecksEntitlement "<code>(#$entitlementChecksEntitlement RIGHT1 RIGHT2)</code> means that an agent's entitlement <code>RIGHT1</code> checks the power of another agent insofar as the other agent has the entitlement <code>RIGHT2</code>.")
(comment BranchOfUSGovernment "The collection of branches of #$BranchOfUSGovernment.  There are exactly three instances of this collection: #$USLegislativeBranch, #$USJudicialBranch, and #$USExecutiveBranch.")
(comment USSenateRightToConfirmPresidentialAppointees "The right of the #$USSenate to confirm certain appointments to positions made by the #$UnitedStatesPresident.")
(comment PresidentialRightToNameAppointees "The right of the U.S. President to name appointees to certain positions.")
(comment USSenateRightToApproveTreaties "The right of the #$USSenate to approve a treaty negotiated by the president.  No treaty can go into effect without approval by two-thirds of the Senate")
(comment PresidentialRightToNegotiateTreaties "The right of the U.S. President to negotiate treaties.")
(comment USCongressRightToPassLegislation "The right of the #$USCongress to pass federal laws.")
(comment PresidentialRightToVetoCongressionalLegislation "The right of the U.S. President to veto congressional legislation.")
(comment USJudicialRightToDetermineConstitutionalityOfLaw "The right of the U.S. courts to determine the constitutionality of laws.")
(comment JudicialReview "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$JudicialReview is an event in which a court reviews legislation to determine whether it may stand.")
(comment TreatyNegotiation "A specialization of #$Negotiating, Each instance of this collection is a negotiation which leads to the formation of a #$Treaty -- either between the participants or between the parties they represent in the negotiations.")
(comment Approval "The emotion of viewing positively a state of affairs or other agent's actions.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.")
(comment ApprovalOfTreaty "A subset of #$ApprovingARequest. In each instance of #$ApprovalOfTreaty, a propsed treaty is approved by an authorized agent.")
(comment courtCaseEstablishesNorm "<code>(#$courtCaseEstablishesNorm CASE NORM)</code> means that the case <code>CASE</code> established <code>NORM</code>.")
(comment goodsAndServicesProduced "<code>(#$goodsAndServicesProduced ECONOMY GOOD-OR-SERVICE)</code> means that the collection <code>GOOD-OR-SERVICE</code> is one of the types of goods and services that is produced in the economic system <code>ECONOMY</code>.")
(comment IndexicalQuerySpecification "The collection of instances of #$CycLQuerySpecification whose sentence (see #$sentenceParameterValueInSpecification) contains an indexical that needs to be resolved in order for the query to run correctly.")
(comment IndexicalQuerySpecification-IndexicalInArg1 "The collection of all instances of #$IndexicalQuerySpecification whose (unquoted) sentence (see #$sentenceParameterValueInSpecification) contains an indexical in its first argument.")
(comment QuerySpecificationTypeByFormulaArity "A collection of collections.  Each instance is a collection of instances of #$CycLQuerySpecification whose (unquoted) query sentences (see #$sentenceParameterValueInSpecification) are all such that their arg0 is of the same arity.")
(comment QuerySpecificationWithBinaryFormula "The collection of all instances of #$CycLQuerySpecification whose query sentence (see #$sentenceParameterValueInSpecification) consists of a predicate with two arguments. Any query whose formula is built from (has an arg0 of) a binary predicate is a member of this collection.")
(comment fundamentalQuestionForTheoryOrSystemType "<code>(#$fundamentalQuestionForTheoryOrSystemType QUESTION THEORY-OR-SYSTEM-TYPE)</code> means that the query specification <code>QUESTION</code> is one of the questions that any theory or system of type <code>THEORY-OR-SYSTEM-TYPE</code> must answer in order to qualify as a theory or system of that type.")
(comment decision-CourtCase "The corresponding predicate of #$CourtCaseDecisionFn.  (#$decision-CourtCase CASE DECISION) relatest the #$CourtCase CASE to the #$Proposition expressed by the decision rendered in the case.")
(comment caseTriedIn "(#$caseTriedIn CASE COURT) means that COURT is a #$Court-Judicial wherein the #$CourtCase CASE is tried.")
(comment caseTriedUnder "(#$caseTriedUnder CASE JUDGE) means that JUDGE is a #$Judge under whom the #$CourtCase CASE is tried.")
(comment MarburyVMadison-CourtCase "A landmark case heard by the U.S. Supreme Court which established the basis for the exercise of judicial review in the United States.  #$WilliamMarbury had received a judicial appointment under President #$JohnAdams which #$JohnMarshall, who was then acting as Secretary of State, failed to deliver before Adams' term expired in 1801 (Marbury's appointment, along with several others, having being made literally at the eleventh hour before Adams' term expired).  #$ThomasJefferson, when sworn in as Adams' successor, continued to withold the appointments, and Marbury petitioned the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt to compel #$JamesMadison, Jefferson's Secretary of State, to deliver them.  The court, under the leadership of the same #$JohnMarshall, eventually found that Marbury's petition was misdirected in being directly addressed to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt, inasmuch as the #$USConstitution only gave the court appelate jurisdiction, not original jurisdication, in such cases: hence, the judicial statue under which Marbury's petition was submitted was unconstitutional. This marked the first time that the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt asserted an authority, defended by Marshall in his opinion, to evaluate existing criminal and civil statutes with regard to constitutionality, i.e., the #$USJudicialRightToDetermineConstitutionalityOfLaw.")
(comment WilliamMarbury "The plaintiff in #$MarburyVMadison-CourtCase.  He had received a judicial appointment under President #$JohnAdams which #$JohnMarshall, who was then acting as Secretary of State, failed to deliver before Adams' term expired in 1801 (Marbury's appointment, along with several others, being made literally at the eleventh hour before Adams' term expired).  #$ThomasJefferson, when sworn in as Adams' successor, continued to withold the appointments, and Marbury petitioned the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt to compel #$JamesMadison, Jefferson's Secretary of State, to deliver them.  The court, under the leadership of the same #$JohnMarshall, eventually found that Marbury's petition was misdirected in being directly addressed to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt, inasmuch as the #$USConstitution only gave the court appelate jurisdiction, not original jurisdication, in such cases, so that the judicial statue under which Marbury's petition was submitted was unconstitutional.  More importantly, however, this marked the first time that the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt asserted an authority, defended by Marshall in his opinion, to evaluate existing criminal and civil statutes with regard to constitutionality, i.e., the #$USJudicialRightToDetermineConstitutionalityOfLaw.")
(comment CourtCase-Original "The class of all instances of #$CourtCase consisting of preparation and trial in #$OriginalJurisdiction.  Each is presumed to include exactly one trial plus preparations and preliminaries, and is not a case heard on appeal (see #$CourtCase-Appellate).")
(disjointWith CourtCase-Original CourtCase-Appellate)
(comment CourtCase-Appellate "The class of all instances of #$CourtCase that are heard on appeal of an original case (see #$CourtCase-Original).  Each instance is tried in exactly one #$Court-Judicial and is presumed to include exactly one trial, and follows exactly one #$CourtCase-Original within a larger #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals, (although there may be intervening appellate cases within the same #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals.")
(comment CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals "The collection of all instances of #$CourtCase that are taken through at least one or possibly more appeals to higher courts.  Each consists in exactly one #$CourtCase-Original, plus one or more instances of #$CourtCase-Appellate, all of which (the original case and the subsequent appeal(s) are #$properSubSituations of the #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals.")
(comment NthAppealOfCaseFn "Denotational function for representing the Nth appeal (including preparation, preliminaries, and trial) within a #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals.")
(comment nthAppealOfCase "The corresponding predicate of #$NthAppealOfCaseFn.")
(comment dateOfFirstHearing-CourtCase "A predicate used for identifying the hearing date for the original case (the #$CourtCase-Original) in an extended #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals.  (#$dateOfFirstHearing-CourtCase CASE DATE) means that DATE is the date on which the #$CourtCase-Original that is a #$properSubSituations of CASE was heard.")
(comment FederalCourtCase "The collection of all instances of #$CourtCase that are tried in a #$FederalCourt.")
(comment jurisdictionScopeOfCourt "This predicate captures the important concept of the scope or kind of case that a #$Court-Judicial in a given judicial system is permitted to hear.  In particular, U.S. legal tradition distinguishes between 'original jurisdiction' and 'appellate jurisdiction'.  A given #$Court-Judicial, COURT, has original jurisdiction iff (#$jurisdictionScopeOfCourt COURT #$CourtCase-Original) and appellate jurisdiction iff (#$jurisdictionScopeOfCourt COURT #$CourtCase-Appellate).")
(comment trialOfCase "In Western jurisprudence, a #$CourtCase subsumes a #$Trial as one of it's chief events.  (#$trialOfCase CASE TRIAL) means that TRIAL is a #$Trial that occurs in the course of the adjudication of CASE.")
(comment quartersOfCourt "(#$quartersOfCourt COURT QUARTERS) means that QUARTERS is the building or building-complex wherein the #$Court-Judicial COURT regularly meets.  Defeasibly, cases tried in COURT (#$caseTriedIn) occur at (#$eventOccursAt) QUARTERS.")
(comment marketQuantityDemandAtPrice "The corresponding predicate of #$MarketDemandFn.")
(comment fuelSynthesizerInSystem-FunctionalRole "A #$SystemRolePredicate.  (#$fuelSynthesizerInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that within the operating context of SYSTEM, AGENT manufactures some substance that other components within the system use as fuel.")
(comment energyStoreInSystem-FunctionalRole "A #$SystemRolePredicate.  (#$energyStoreInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that AGENT stores energy for its own and possibly others' use within the operating context of SYSTEM.")
(comment energySinkInSystem-FunctionalRole "A #$SystemRolePredicate.  (#$energySinkInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that AGENT makes an exothermic  contribution to SYSTEM.  That is, in the course of actions which contribute to the overall stability and long-term existence of SYSTEM, AGENT 'burns fuel', or more generally, releases energy.")
(comment wasteDisposerInSystem-FunctionalRole "A #$SystemRolePredicate.  (#$wasteDisposerInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that AGENT renders innocuous or useful the waste product or products of some other agent or class of agent in SYSTEM (cf. #$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole).")
(comment EcosystemOfRegionFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction, used to reify and subsequently refer to the #$Ecosystem occupying a given #$GeographicalRegion.  (#$EcosystemOfRegionFn REGION) denotes the #$Ecosystem in region, considered as a #$FunctionalSystem of interrelated and interacting biological components.")
(comment ecosystemOfRegion "The corresponding predicate of #$EcosystemOfRegionFn.")
(comment agentInEcosystem "(#$agentInEcosystem SYSTEM AGENT) means that AGENT acts constitutionally and on a regular basis in a way that directly contributes to the underlying self-regenerating process through which the overall 'operational parameters' of the #$Ecosystem SYSTEM are realized. ")
(comment producerInEcosystem "(#$producerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM AGENT) means that, as part of the biological action which contributes to the overall 'autocatalysis' of ECOSYSTEM, AGENT implements endothermic processes which chemically store energy in a form that AGENT is then able to use as fuel to supply its continued metabolism.")
(comment consumerInEcosystem "(#$consumerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM AGENT) means that, in engaging in the actions which are part of the overall 'autocatalysis' of ECOSYSTEM, AGENT expends energy without storing it or engaging in biological actions which synthsesize fuel, so that it must actively seek out and consume chemically stored energy in order to continue functioning. ")
(comment primaryConsumerInEcosystem "(#$primaryConsumerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM AGENT) means that in the course of acting in ECOSYSTEM, AGENT consumes some organisms which at the time they are consumed, are producers in ECOSYSTEM (cf. #$producerInEcosystem). ")
(comment secondaryConsumerInEcosystem "(#$secondaryConsumerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM AGENT) means that in the course of acting in ECOSYSTEM, AGENT consumes some organisms which at the time of consumption are primary consumers in ECOSYSTME (cf. #$primaryConsumerInEcosystem).")
(comment tertiaryConsumerInEcosystem "(#$tertiaryConsumerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM AGENT) means that in the course of acting in ECOSYSTEM, AGENT consumes some organisms which at the time of consumption are secodary consumers in ECOSYSTME (cf. #$secondaryConsumerInEcosystem).")
(comment n-AryConsumerInEcosystem "An important concept in representing food chains and food webs in #$Ecosystems is what might be termed 'arity of consumption' - basically, the shortest distance in the food web that separates a consumer (see #$consumerInEcosystem) from a producer (#$producerInEcosystem).  This recursively defined predicate instantiates this concept.  Thus (#$n-AryConsumerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM AGENT 1) means that there is an organism that is a producer in ECOSYSTEM (#$producerInEcosystem) which is an instance of a type which is a #$foodSourceFor AGENT, which has its habitat (#$hasHabitat) in the region of ECOSYSTEM, and (#$n-AryConsumerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM AGENT N) means that there is an organism SOURCE such that (#$n-AryConsumerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM SOURCE (#$DifferenceFn N 1)) and such it is an instance of a type which is a #$foodSourceFor AGENT which has its habitat in the region of ECOSYSTEM. ")
(comment decomposerInEcosystem "(#$decomposerInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM ORG) means that ORG is a #$Bacterium or #$Fungus that acts to decompose dead organic material in ECOSYSTEM, thereby effecting release of nitrate compounds.")
(comment DeciduousForestEcosystem "The collection of all #$Ecosystems characterized by deciduous forest ecology.  Instances feature rainfall that normally averages between 75 and 250 cm.  a year, and the soil is rich and exhibits a high organic content.")
(comment TropicalRainforestEcosystem "The collection of all #$Ecosystems characterized by tropical rainforest ecology.  Instances feature rainfall that normally averages between 200 and 400 cm. a year, and the soil is of relatively poor quality.  Characteristic vegetation includes tall trees with few lower limbs, vines, and epiphytes.")
(comment GrasslandPrairieEcosystem "The collection of all #$Ecosystems characterized by grassland prairie ecology.  Instances feature rainfall that normally averages between 10 and 60 cm. a year, and the soil is of good quality.  Sod-forming grasses predominate.")
(comment TaigaEcosystem "The collection of all #$Ecosystems characterized by taiga ecology.  Instances feature rainfall that normally averages between 20 and 60 cm. a year, with acidic soil.  Coniferous forest predominates.")
(comment TundraEcosystem "The collection of all #$Ecosystems characterized by a tundra ecology.  Instances feature rainfall that averages less than 25 cm. a year, and the soil is permafrost.  Bryophytes and lichens predominate.")
(comment ChaparralEcosystem "The collection of all #$Ecosystems characterized by chaparral ecology.  Instances feature rainfall that  averages between 50 and 75 cm. a year, primarily in the winter months, and the soil is stony and relatively infertile.  Scrub vegetation predominates.")
(comment DesertEcosystem "The collection of all #$Ecosystems characterized by high desert ecology.  Instances feature rainfall that is usually less than 25 cm. a year, with sandy soil.  Cacti and and other low-water-adapted vegetation predominate.")
(comment typicalAnnualRainfallOfClimateCycleType "(#$typicalAnnualRainfallOfClimateCycleType CLIMATE-TYPE RAINFALL-LEVEL) means that rainfall in #$GeographicalRegions characterized by the #$ClimateCycleType CLIMATE-TYPE averages about RAINFALL-LEVEL per year.")
(comment predominantVegetationTypeOfEcosystemType "(#$predominantVegetationTypeOfEcosystemType ECO-TYPE  PLANT-TYPE) means that when an #$Ecosystem instantiates ECO-TYPE, many instances of PLANT-TYPE share its region as a habitat (#$hasHabitat), and function as producers within it (#$producerInEcosystem).")
(comment Ecotone "The class of all #$GeographicalRegions that lie within the geographical boundaries of two or more #$Ecosystems of differing types, and that are characterized by the fact that many agents from both #$Ecosystems (#$agentInEcosystem) share the region in question as a habitat.")
(comment regionIsEcotoneForEcosystemTypes "(#$regionIsEcotoneForEcosystemTypes REGION ECO-TYPE1 ECO-TYPE2) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION is an #$Ecotone for an #$Ecosystem of ECO-TYPE1 and for an #$Ecosystem of ECO-TYPE2, in the sense that it lies between the boundaries of both systems, and is home to many agents in both.")
(comment Table-VisualCW "A sub-collection of #$VisualArtifact-CW.  Instances of #$Table-VisualCW are used to present information multiple dimensions.")
(comment hasNumberOfColumns "'(#$hasNumberOfColumns TABLE N)' means that the #$Table-AIS TABLE has N number of columns (see #$columnOfTable) as component parts.")
(comment Table-AIS "The collection of all instances of #$GraphicalStructure that are tables.  Every instance of #$Table-AIS has at least one #$rowOfTable and at least one #$columnOfTable and must have at least two of either #$rowOfTable or #$columnOfTable.")
(comment PriceAtQuantitySchedule "A specialization of #$Table-PCW.  Instances include any two-column tables that compare a price of some good to a quantity of that good, during some period of time.  If the quantity is interpreted as the number of units a consumer or market demand, the table is an instance of #$DemandSchedule.  If the quantity is interpreted as the number of units that a supplier or market are willing and able to supply, the table is an instance of #$SupplySchedule.")
(disjointWith DemandSchedule SupplySchedule)
(comment SupplySchedule "The collection of all instances of supply schedule, a type of #$Table-PCW used in economics to record price/quantity-of-supply pairings for some type of product in a market over time.  The pairings can be used to generate a #$SupplyCurve by plotting price points along the y-axis and quantity points along the x-axis of a #$CartesianCoordinateSystem.")
(comment DemandSchedule "The collection of all instances of demand schedule, a type of #$Table-PCW used in economics to record price/quantity-of-demand pairings for some type of product in a market over time.  The pairings can be used to generate a #$DemandCurve by plotting price points along the y-axis and quantity points along the x-axis of a #$CartesianCoordinateSystem.")
(comment writOfCase "(#$writOfCase CASE WRIT) means that WRIT is a #$Writ issued by a #$Court-Judicial in connection with the #$CourtCase CASE.")
(comment ConcludedCourtCase "The collection of all #$CourtCases that have exhausted their appeals within the context of the judicial system in which they are tried.")
(comment UnitedStatesJurisprudenceMt "A #$TheoryMicrotheory containing principles and heuristics specific to the judicial process in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment WritOfCertiori-LegalDocument "The collection of all physical #$LegalDocuments such that each instance enacts a #$WritOfCertiori-PCW.  Such a document is ordinarily created at the direction of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt when #$IssuingAWritOfCertiori, as part of the procedure by which the court agrees to hear a case that has been appealed to it.")
(comment WritOfCertiori-PCW "The collection of all propositional contents (qua #$PropositionalConceptualWorks) of instances of #$WritOfCertiori-LegalDocument.")
(comment PetitionForAWritOfCertiori-LegalDocument "The collection of all #$LegalDocuments constituting petitions to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt for writs of certiori (see #$WritOfCertiori-LegalDocument, #$WritOfCertiori-PCW).")
(comment PetitionForAWritOfCertiori-PCW "The collection of all propositional contents (qua #$PropositionalConceptualWorks) of instances of #$PetitionForAWritOfCertiori-LegalDocument.")
(comment PetitioningForAWritOfCertiori "The collection of all acts that constitute petitions to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt for an #$IssuingAWritOfCertiori by the court in a #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals.")
(comment ConferenceOfTheUnitedStatesSupremeCourt "Collection of all meetings in which the nine justices of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt come together to vote on petitions for writs of certiori (#$PetitioningForAWritOfCertiori.  The justices meet in private, even to the exclusion of their law clerks.  If four or more justices vote to grant a petition, the court issues a #$WritOfCertiori (see #$IssuingAWritOfCertiori)")
(comment DenyingAPetitionOfCertiori "The collection of all denials of instances of #$PetitioningForAWritOfCertiori by the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.")
(comment CaseHeardByTheSupremeCourt "The collection of all cases heard before the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt, upon the Court's issuing of a #$WritOfCertiori-LegalDocument mandating hearing of the case.")
(comment dateDecided-CourtCase "(<code>#$dateDecided-CourtCase CASE DATE)</code> means that <code>DATE</code> is the #$TimeInterval (date) at which a decision was/is rendered in the #$CourtCase <code>CASE</code>.")
(comment VotingRight "A specialization of #$Entitlement.  Each instance of #$VotingRight is the right of a person or group to vote.")
(comment entitlementDomainOfCourtCase "<code>(#$entitlementDomainOfCourtCase CASE RIGHTS-DOMAIN)</code> means that the #$CourtCase <code>CASE</code> involves considerations that significantly overlap with the rights that are instances of the specialization <code>RIGHTS-DOMAIN</code>.")
(comment entitlementRoles "<code>(#$entitlementRoles RIGHT ROLE)</code> means that the instance <code>RIGHT</code> of #$Entitlement is an entitlement of its #$entitledAgents to play the role <code>ROLE</code> in situations of a certain type (specifiable via #$entitlementSitType).")
(comment circuitJusticeOfCourt "Each of the chief justices of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt has jurisdiction over one or more of the instances of #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals.  This amounts essentially to administrative jurisdiction:  although the Supreme Court justice in question is technically empowered to co-preside over cases in the circuit courts within his or her sphere of authority, this seldom happens in modern times.")
(comment DistrictOfColumbiaCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving the #$DistrictOfColumbia.")
(comment FirstCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Maine-State, #$Massachusetts-State, #$NewHampshire-State, #$RhodeIsland-State, and #$PuertoRico.")
(comment SecondCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$NewYork, #$Connecticut, and #$Vermont.")
(comment ThirdCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Delaware-State, #$NewJersey-State, and #$Pennsylvania-State.")
(comment FourthCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Maryland-State, #$NorthCarolina-State, #$SouthCarolina-State, #$Virginia-State, and #$WestVirginia-State.")
(comment FifthCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Louisiana-State, #$Texas-State, and #$Mississippi-State.")
(comment SixthCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Kentucky-State, #$Michigan-State, #$Ohio-State, and #$Tennessee-State.")
(comment SeventhCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Illinois-State, #$Indiana-State, and #$Wisconsin-State.")
(comment EighthCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Arkansas-State, #$Iowa-State, #$Minnesota-State, #$Missouri-State, #$Nebraska-State, #$NorthDakota-State, and #$SouthDakota-State.")
(comment NinthCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Alaska-State, #$Arizona-State, #$California-State, #$Hawaii-State, #$Idaho-State, #$Montana-State, #$Nevada-State, #$Oregon-State and #$Washington-State.")
(comment TenthCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Colorado-State, #$Kansas-State, #$Oklahoma-State, #$Utah-State, and #$Wyoming-State.")
(comment EleventhCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals serving #$Alabama-State, #$Florida-State, and #$Georgia-State.")
(comment FederalCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The #$FederalCircuitCourtOfAppeals was created by Act of Congress in 1982.  It is the only US Federal judicial circuit with jurisdiction wholly based on subject matter rather than geographical location.  Specifically, it has appellate jurisdicton over several Federal claims courts, notably the United States Court of Federal Claims, the US Court of Appeals for Veterans Claims, the US Board of Appeals and Interferences of the United States Patent and Trademark Office, and several others.")
(comment Gerrymandering "The collection of events in which electoral boundaries are drawn in a way which gives one political party an advantage in elections.")
(comment USStateLegislature "A specialization of #$LegislativeOrganization.  Each instance of #$USStateLegislature is a legislature of a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment legislature "<code>(#$legislature GEOPOL-ENTITY LEG)</code> means that the #$LegislativeOrganization <code>LEG</code> is the #$legislature of <code>GEOPOL-ENTITY</code>.")
(comment LegislatureFn "<code>(#$LegislatureFn GEOPOL-ENTITY)</code> denotes the #$LegislativeOrganization that is the #$legislature of <code>GEOPOL-ENTITY</code>.")
(comment Redistricting "The collection of events in which electoral boundaries are redrawn.")
(comment CongressionalDistrict "The collection of all US or state congressional districts.  An election for the #$USHouseOfRepresentatives or lower house of the state legislature is open to registered residents of a congressional district, and not to those resident outside its borders.  A congressperon from a district represents all the residents of that district.")
(comment SelectionProcess-Natural "The #$Collection of all processes of all processes whereby elements of a population that reproduces with minor variance are subjected to fitness filtration by environmental conditions.")
(comment FitnessCriterionFunction "The collection of all instances of #$Function-Denotational which take #$Populations (i.e., instances of the Cyc #$Collection #$Population) as arguments and return sub-populations of those instances as determined by some set of fitness criteria.  Every #$FitnessCriterionFunction is an instance of #$ReifiableFunction, #$IndividualDenotingFunction, and #$UnaryFunction.")
(comment FitnessCriterionFunctionApplyingCriteriaFn "A #$FunctionDenotingFunction.  Where CRITERION is a ('quoted' instance of) #$CycLFormula, (#$FitnessCriterionFunctionApplyingCriteriaFn CRITERION) denotes the #$FitnessCriterionFunction which, applied to a #$Population instance, returns the subsection of that #$Population satisfying CRITERION.")
(comment processTypeImplementsFunction "(#$processTypeImplementsFunction EVENT-TYPE FUNCTION) means that there is a self-consistent interpretation which can be applied to all of the inputs and outputs of instances of EVENT-TYPE (according to some characterization of 'input' and 'output') according to which instances of EVENT-TYPE can be said to implement FUNCTION. ")
(comment processImplementsFunction "(#$processImplementsFunction PROCESS FUNCTION) means that there is an interpretation of the inputs and outputs of PROCESS (according to some rendering of 'inputs' and 'outputs') such that PROCESS can be seen as implementing a single application of FUNCTION to a particular instance of FUNCTION's domain, resulting in a particular instance of FUNCTION's range.")
(comment PresidentAllowingABillToBecomeLawWithoutSigning-USLegislativeProcess "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding. Each instance of #$PresidentAllowingABillToBecomeLawWithoutSigning-USLegislativeProcess
 is an event in which the President of the United States allows a bill to become a law without signing it.")
(comment entitlementDeniedByCourtCaseDecision "<code>(#$entitlementDeniedByCourtCaseDecision CASE RIGHTS)</code> means that the decision i the #$CourtCase <code>CASE</code> denies the #$Entitlement <code>RIGHT</code>.")
(comment PresidentialRightToVetoLineItemsInABill "The right of the U.S. President to veto line items of a bill.")
(comment PresidentialLineItemVeto-USLegislativeProcess "A specialization of #$VetoingSomething. Each instance of #$PresidentialLineItemVeto-USLegislativeProcess is an event in which the President of the United States vetos a portion of a bill.  This power was given to the U.S. president by Congress in 1996, but it was immediately struck down in the Supreme Court case Clinton v. New York City.")
(comment LineItemVeto "A specialization of #$VetoingSomething. Each instance of #$LineItemVeto is an event in which a line of a bill, as opposed to an entire bill, is vetoed.")
(comment EconomicsVisualizationGraphCW "The collection of instances of #$Graph-CW that visualize economic data or economic concepts. The printed representation of these graphs are ubiquitous in economics textbooks.")
(comment fieldTypeDerivedFromRelationArg "<code>(#$fieldTypeDerivedFromRelationArg SOURCE PRED INT)</code> means that the structured information source <code>SOURCE</code> contains information about how the relation <code>PRED</code> relate to a series of arguments, such that the value of the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> argument is explicitly represented as a field value in <code>SOURCE</code>.")
(comment meaningSentencePredicateForInfoSource "<code>(#$meaningSentencePredicateForInfoSource SOURCE PRED)</code> means that the structured information source <code>SOURCE</code> encodes the relationship <code>PRED</code> to a tuple  of arguments.  Some of these arguments are identified explicitly in <code>SOURCE</code> (see #$fieldTypeDerivedFromRelationArg); others are implicit.")
(comment sourceImplicitFieldTypeDerivedFromRelationArg "<code>(#$sourceImplicitFieldTypeDerivedFromRelationArg SOURCE PRED INT)</code> means that the structured information source <code>SOURCE</code> encodes the relation <code>PRED</code> to a series of arguments, where the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> argument of <code>PRED</code> is implicit in <code>SOURCE</code> (i.e., not the value of any field in <code>SOURCE</code>.  Implicit values may be fixed or variable; see  the spec-preds #$sourceFixesRelationArg and #$sourceVariesRelationArg.")
(comment sourceFixesRelationArg "<code>(#$sourceFixesRelationArg SOURCE PRED INT)</code> means that the structured information source <code>SOURCE</code> encodes the relation <code>PRED</code> to a series of arguments, where the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> argument of <code>PRED</code> is both implicit in <code>SOURCE</code> (i.e., not the value of any field in <code>SOURCE</code>) and has a fixed value for each proposition formed from <code>PRED</code> that <code>SOURCE</code> encodes.  To represent that the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> value varies for each such proposition, use the negation pred, #$sourceVariesRelationArg.")
(comment sourceVariesRelationArg "<code>(#$sourceVariesRelationArg SOURCE PRED INT)</code> means that the structured information source <code>SOURCE</code> encodes the relationship <code>PRED</code> among a series of arguments, where the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> argument of <code>PRED</code> is both implicit in <code>SOURCE</code> (i.e., not the value of any field in <code>SOURCE</code>) and has a potentially distinct value for each proposition formed from <code>PRED</code> that <code>SOURCE</code> encodes.  To represent that the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> value is fixed for each such proposition, use the negation pred, #$sourceFixesRelationArg.")
(comment CartesianGraphCW "The collection of instances of #$Graph-CW that visualize data using a Cartesian coordinate system structure.")
(comment 2DCartesianGraphCW "The collection of instances of #$Graph-CW that visualize data using a Cartesian coordinate system structure.")
(comment 3DCartesianGraphCW "The collection of instances of #$Graph-CW that visualize data using a three dimensional Cartesian coordinate system structure.")
(comment EconomicsVisualizationGraphTypeByEconomicConcept "The collection of sub-collections of #$EconomicsVisualizationGraphCW, each instance of which emphasizes the same economic concept.")
(comment DemandCurve "The collection of instances of #$Graph-CW that visualize the demand for a product in some real or hypothetical market.")
(comment SupplyCurve "The collection of instances of #$Graph-CW that visualize the demand for a product in some real or hypothetical market.")
(comment xAxis "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$CartesianCoordinateSystem to its x-axis.")
(comment yAxis "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$CartesianCoordinateSystem to its y-axis.")
(comment semanticsAxiomForSourceType "<code>(#$semanticsAxiomForSourceType SOURCE-TYPE ASSERTION)</code> identifies <code>ASSERTION</code> as one of the axioms that encodes how to assign a semantic interpretation to any instance of <code>SOURCE-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$StructuredInformationSource.")
(comment sourceTypeSemanticallySubsumesSourceType "A predicate that indicates a function from one class of #$StructuredInformationSource to another. <code>(#$sourceTypeSemanticallySubsumesSourceType SOURCE-TYPE-RICH SOURCE-TYPE-POOR)</code> means that there exists a mapping function from any instance of <code>SOURCE-TYPE-POOR</code> to a (real or hypothetical) instance of <code>SOURCE-TYPE-RICH</code> such that all of the propositional information encoded in <code>SOURCE-TYPE-POOR</code> is encoded in <code>SOURCE-TYPE-RICH</code>.")
(comment graphRiseDerivedFromRelationArg "A predicate used to describe the semantics of instances of #$Graph-CW.  <code>(#$graphRiseDerivedFromRelationArg GRAPH PRED INT)</code> means that the points along the #$yAxis on the graphical structure of <code>GRAPH</code> represent the values of the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> argument place for <code>PRED</code> relations encoded in <code>GRAPH</code>.")
(comment graphRunDerivedFromRelationArg "A predicate used to describe the semantics of instances of #$Graph-CW.  <code>(#$graphRunDerivedFromRelationArg GRAPH PRED INT)</code> means that the points along the #$xAxis on the graphical structure of <code>GRAPH</code> represent the values of the <code>INT</code><i>th</i> argument place for <code>PRED</code> relations encoded in <code>GRAPH</code>.")
(comment HydrologicCycle "The class of all processes wherein #$Water cycles through
multiple physical states, and possibly one or more chemical compounds,
within a #$GeographicalRegion.")
(comment TerrestrialEcoCycle "The collection of all ecological cycles occurring on #$PlanetEarth.")
(comment WaterCycle-Terrestrial "The collection of all #$HydrologicCycles occurring on #$PlanetEarth.")
(comment NitrogenCycle-Terrestrial "The collection of all terrestrial nitrogen cycles:  that is,
parallel cyclical processes (#$Cycle-Parallel) which involve #$Nitrogen
being cycled through terrestrial #$Ecosystems in various chemical forms.")
(comment PhosphorusCycle-Terrestrial "The collection of all terrestrial phosphorus cycles:  that
is, parallel cyclical processes (#$Cycle-Parallel) which involve
#$Phosphorus being cycled through terrestrial #$Ecosystems freely and
in various chemical bondings, e.g. #$Phosphates.")
(comment CarbonCycle-Terrestrial "The collection of all terrestrial carbon cycles: that is,
parallel cyclical processes (#$Cycle-Parallel) which involve #$Carbon
being cycled through terrestrial #$Ecosystems in various stereotypical
chemical forms.")
(comment SeaSurfaceAtmosphereExchange "The collection of all #$Permeation processes whereby various gasses such as gaseous
CO2 diffuse out of #$TheEarthsAtmosphere and are dissolved in the
#$EarthsOceanSea, and conversely, precipitate out of the ocean and
into the atmosphere.")
(comment PhosphateWeathering "The class of all #$Erosion processes involving #$Phosphate bearing rocks, facilitated by #$GeologicUpliftEvents.")
(comment FossilHydrocarbonCreation "The collection of processes whereby the fossil remnants of wetland regions
are buried by tectonic subduction and other geological processes, and
are slowly transformed into petrochemical #$FossilFuels in regions of
extreme temperature and pressure deep within the Earth's crust,
eventually becoming petrochemical reserves.  The process requires
millions of years for completion, which is why #$FossilFuels are
considered a #$nonRenewableResourceTypeInSystem with respect to
#$TheEarthsBiosphere on a human timescale.")
(comment PhosphateUptake-Plant "The collection of #$Ingesting processes wherein plants ingest #$Phosphates.")
(comment GeologicProcess "The collection of #$PhysicalTransformationEvents that are sufficiently wide is scope that they may be said to affect an entire #$Planet.  Examples include continental drift, #$GeologicUpliftEvents, and the (#$WaterCycleOfRegionFn #$PlanetEarth).  Many, but not all, #$GeologicProcesses take place on a scale of millions of years.")
(comment SedimentationProcess "The collection of #$GeologicProcess instances where sediments precipitate out of an atmosphere or ocean, settle, and harden into instances of #$SedimentaryRock.")
(comment GeologicUpliftEvent "The collection of all events in which tectonic stresses result in raising of a portion of the Earth's crust, usually at a tectonic plate boundary.")
(comment PhosphateLeaching "The collection of #$Leaching processes wherein soluble #$Phosphates are removed from dead organic material and enter the soil.")
(comment CivilRight "A specialization of #$Entitlement.  Each instance of #$CivilRight is a right to protection against discrimination.")
(comment ProductionPossibilitiesFrontier "An instance of #$EconomicsVisualizationGraphTypeByEconomicConcept.  Instances are 2-D Cartesian graphs that compare the number of units of some good or service that an agent or market could produce to the number of units of some alternative good or service that the agent or market could produce instead.")
(comment FirmSupplyCurve "The collection of instances of #$SupplyCurve that assume a single supplier market.")
(comment SingleSupplierMarket "The collection of instances of #$Market in which the salient good or service is supplied by a single agent.  Such markets are a convenient fiction for purposes of calculating supply and demand curves for specific agents.")
(comment MarketSupplyCurve "The collection of instances of #$SupplyCurve that consider all suppliers of a good or service in a given market.  A market supply curve can be arrived at by summing the quantity points of all the supply curves of the individual suppliers in that market (see #$FirmSupplyCurve).")
(comment relativeProductionCosts "<code>(#$relativeProductionCosts MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE-1 QUANTITY-1 PRODUCT-TYPE-2 QUANTITY-2)</code> means that the cost to <code>AGENT</code> of producing <code>QUANTITY-1</code> units of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE-1</code> is identical to the cost to <code>AGENT</code> of producing <code>QUANTITY-2</code> units of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE-2</code>.")
(comment marketIsMaximallyEfficientInProductionOfTypeWRTTypeDuringPeriod "<code>(#$marketIsMaximallyEfficientInProductionOfTypeWRTTypeDuringPeriod MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE-1 PRODUCT-TYPE-2 PERIOD)</code> means that during <code>PERIOD</code>, the instance <code>MARKET</code> of #$Market is maximally efficient/minimally inefficient in its production of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE-1</code> with respect to the alternative product type <code>PRODUCT-TYPE-2</code>.")
(comment marketProductionQuantityOverPeriod "<code>(#$marketProductionQuantityOverPeriod MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE-1 N PERIOD)</code> means that from the start to the end of the instance <code>PERIOD</code> of #$TimeInterval, the instance <code>MARKET</code> of #$Market produced <code>N</code> units of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CouplesRight "Instances of this collection are entitlements that couples have by virtue of their being a domestic unit of some sort.")
(comment USCivilRight "The entitlements which individuals--typically US citizens--have in virtue of their status within US society.")
(comment HumanRight "Instances of this collection are the entitlements that an individual has by virtue of being a human being.  Some such rights are notably described in #$BasicHumanRights-UNDeclaration, which represents those rights recognized by the #$UnitedNationsOrganization and spelled out in The Universal Declaration of Human Rights which was adopted by the UN in 1948.")
(comment ObligationTypeImposedByEntitlementTypeFn "<code>(#$ObligationTypeImposedByEntitlementTypeFn RIGHT-TYPE)</code> denotes the class of #$Obligations that are imposed on agents by virtue of some other agent having an instance of the #$Entitlement type, <code>RIGHT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment obligationTypeImposedByEntitlementType "<code>(#$obligationTypeImposedByEntitlementType RIGHT-TYPE OB-TYPE)</code> means the class of #$Obligations that are imposed on agents by virtue of some other agent having an instance of the #$Entitlement type <code>RIGHT-TYPE</code> is <code>OB-TYPE</code>.")
(comment dateHeard-CourtCase "<code>(#$dateHeard-CourtCase CASE DATE)</code> means that <code>DATE</code> is the #$TimeInterval at which <code>CASE</code> was heard.")
(comment consumerSurplusAtQuantityOfProductType "<code>(#$consumerSurplusAtQuantityOfProductType MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE SURPLUS QUANTITY)</code> identifies <code>SURPLUS</code> as the monetary value of purchasing <code>QUANTITY</code> of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code> in <code>MARKET</code>, above the actual price per instance of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code> in that market.")
(comment producerSurplusAtQuantityOfProductType "<code>(#$producerSurplusAtQuantityOfProductType MARKET PRODUCT-TYPE SURPLUS QUANTITY)</code> identifies <code>SURPLUS</code> as the monetary value of selling an isntance of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code> in <code>MARKET</code> at the #$marketClearingPrice, above what they would have been willing to sell that number of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code> had they only produced <code>QUANTITY</code> of it.")
(comment marginalUtilityOfProductTypeAtQuantity "A predicate used to relate a product type in a market at a certain demand quantity to its marginal utility in terms of some #$MonetaryValue. <code>(#$marginalUtilityOfProductTypeAtQuantity MARKET PRODUCT UTILITY QUANTITY)</code> means that the value to consumers of <code>QUANTITY</code> instances of <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code> is <code>UTILITY</code>.")
(comment totalUtilityOfProductTypeAtQuantity "A predicate used to relate a product type in a market at a certain demand quantity to its total utility in terms of some #$MonetaryValue. <code>(#$totalUtilityOfProductTypeAtQuantity MARKET PRODUCT UTILITY QUANTITY)</code> means that the sum of the marginal utility values to consumers of <code>QUANTITY</code> instances of <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code> is <code>UTILITY</code>.")
(comment netIncreasingFunctionOnArg "(A function characterizing predicate used to describe the behavior of a #$FixedArityFunction.  (#$netIncreasingFunctionOnArg FN N) is true iff the following conditional holds.  Let L-TERM be the result returned by the #$FixedArityFunction FN on a tuple of arguments where L-ARG is the Nth argument.  Let H-TERM be the result returned by FN on the same set of arguments save that the Nth argument is replaced with H-ARG, and suppose (#$greaterThan H-ARG L-ARG):  then (#$greaterThan H-TERM L-TERM).  In the vernacular, (#$netIncreasingFunctionOnAf FN N) means that the value returned by FN increases as the value of the Nth argument supplied to FN increases, the other argument values remaining constant.")
(comment netDecreasingFunctionOnArg "(A function characterizing predicate used to describe the behavior of a #$FixedArityFunction.  (#$netDecreasingFunctionOnArg FN N) is true iff the following conditional holds.  Let L-TERM be the result returned by the #$FixedArityFunction FN on a tuple of arguments where H-ARG is the Nth argument.  Let H-TERM be the result returned by FN on the same set of arguments save that the Nth argument is replaced with L-ARG, and suppose (#$greaterThan H-ARG L-ARG):  then (#$greaterThan H-TERM L-TERM).  In the vernacular, (#$netIncreasingFunctionOnAf FN N) means that the value returned by FN decreases as the value of the Nth argument supplied to FN increases, the other argument values remaining constant.")
(comment MarginalUtilityCurve "A specialization of #$Graph-CW that visualizes the relationship of the marginal utility of some product to an agent or agents in a market to its consumed quantity.")
(comment detritivoreInEcosystem "(#$detritivoreInEcosystem ECOSYSTEM ORG) means that ORG is a #$MulticellularOrganism which includes dead organic matter among its principal food sources.  Examples include earthworms and vultures.   Non-examples include bacteria and fungi whose activities actually liberate ammonium compounds and nitrates.  See also #$decomposerInEcosystem. ")
(comment majorityOpinionBy "(#$majorityOpinionBy CASE JUDGE) means that where CASE is a #$CaseHeardByTheSupremeCourt, the court's majority opinion in CASE was/is authored by JUDGE.")
(comment decisionFavors-CourtCase "A predicate for linking a court's decision (ordinarily represented using #$CourtCaseDecisionFn) with the #$LegalAgent (the #$plaintiffs or the #$defendants in the case, depending on whether the outcome favors the plaintiff or defendant.  (#$decisionFavors-CourtCase DECISION AGENT) means that the #$Court-Judicial making DECISION favors AGENT in DECISION.")
(comment majorityInCase "A predicate for documenting decision margins in the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.  Where CASE is a #$CaseHeardByTheSupremeCourt, (#$majorityInCase CASE N M) means that in CASE, N justices constituted the majority, and M justices constituted the minority.")
(comment OliverWendellHolmesJr "The son of the poet, #$OliverWendellHolmesSr, and a noted justice on the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.  Holmes is credited with being one of the first legal scholars to articulate the philosophy of legal positivism, defined roughly as the position that all laws in the human, legal sense are essentially arbitrary, deriving their authority solely from the power of the state, and not from any natural law or objective moral scheme.")
(comment EdwardDouglassWhite "A chief justice (#$chiefJusticeOfCourt) of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.  White presided over the noted case of SchenkVTheUnitedStates, in which #$OliverWendellHolmesJr, writing for the majority, first gave voice to the principle that speech constituting a 'clear and present danger' to the well-being of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica was not protected under the free speech provision of the #$FirstAmendment-USConstitution.")
(comment SchenkVTheUnitedStates-CourtCase "An important #$CaseHeardByTheSupremeCourt.  At issue was the question of whether the actions of #$CharlesSchenk, a prominent socialist who published pamphlets denouncing the draft and urging conscripts to resist enlistment, were protected by the #$FirstAmendment-USConstitution.  The court unanimously decided they were not.  #$OliverWendellHolmesJr, writing for the majority, authored an opinion stating that speech constituting a 'clear and present danger' to the welfare of the Republic was not permissable, insofar as it impugned or ran the risk of impugning, the rights of other citizens.")
(comment PollResults-CW "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$PollResults-CW is a work that reports the results of a poll (see #$Survey).")
(comment PoliticallyModeratePerson "The collection of instances of  #$Person that identify themselves a politically moderate.  The beliefs of this group generally do not constitute a coherent ideology.")
(disjointWith PoliticallyModeratePerson PoliticallyConservativePerson)
(comment PoliticallyConservativePerson "The collection of instances of  #$Person that adhere to #$Conservatism.")
(disjointWith Liberal-SocialDemocrat PoliticallyConservativePerson)
(disjointWith PoliticallyModeratePerson Liberal-SocialDemocrat)
(comment ExitPoll-CW "A specialization of #$Survey.  Each instance of GallupPoll-CW is a poll result produced by a #$Survey conduced by #$TheGallupOrganization.")
(disjointWith GallupPoll-CW ExitPoll-CW)
(comment GallupPoll-CW "A specialization of #$Survey.  Each instance of #$GallupPoll-CW is a poll result produced by a #$Survey conduced by #$TheGallupOrganization.")
(comment publicOpinions "<code>(#$publicOpinions AGENT OPINION)</code> means that the public opinion of <code>AGENT</code> is <code>OPINION</code>.")
(comment CourtCaseDecisionFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction to be used in reifying and subsequently referencing the decision rendered in a given #$CourtCase, as a propositional token.  (#$CourtCaseDecisionFn CASE COURT) refers to the decision returned by COURT in CASE.")
(comment chiefJusticeOfCourt "<code>(#$chiefJusticeOfCourt COURT JUSTICE)</code> means that <code>JUSTICE</code> is the head judge of the court, <code>COURT</code>.")
(comment hasLeadershipPosition "#$hasLeadershipPosition is used to identify the members of an organization who have been invested with the authority to lead others within the organization. <code>(#$hasLeadershipPosition ORG PERSON)</code> says that the #$Person <code>PERSON</code> is such an individual for the #$Organization <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment plottedLine "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$CartesianCoordinateSystem to the instance of #$Line-Planar that is determined by points along axes.")
(comment PointIn2DCoordinateSystemFn "An instance of #$TernaryFunction that takes a #$TwoDimensionalCoordinateSystem and two #$ScalarIntervals, and returns a #$Point.  <code>(#$PointIn2DCoordinateSystemFn SYSTEM X Y)</code> denotes the point in <code>SYSTEM</code> corresponding to the values <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code> along <code>SYSTEM</code>'s x and y axes, respectively.")
(comment pointIn2DCoordinateSystem "<code>(#$pointIn2DCoordinateSystem SYSTEM X Y POINT)</code> identifies <code>POINT</code> as the instance of #$Point with x-coordinate <code>X</code> and y-coordinate <code>Y</code> in the 2D coordinate system <code>SYSTEM</code>.")
(comment pointOnLine "A binary predicate used to relate a line to the points on the line.")
(comment QualitativeSlope "A sub-collection of #$ScalarInterval, instances are qualitative (as opposed to real numeric value) slopes.  Notable instances include #$NoSlope, #$NegativeSlope, and #$PositiveSlope.  The qualitative slope of a line can be determined from the numeric value.")
(comment lineHasSlopeAtPoint-Quantitative "<code>(#$lineHasSlopeAtPoint-Quantitative LINE POINT SLOPE)</code> means that the line <code>LINE</code> has a slope of numeric value <code>SLOPE</code> at the point </code>POINT</code>.")
(comment lineHasSlopeAtPoint "A predicate used to relate an instance of #$Line-Planar to its slope at a given point on that line.  Slopes may be specified numerically (see #$lineHasSlopeAtPoint-Quantitative) or qualitatively (see #$lineHasSlopeAtPoint-Qualitative).")
(comment lineHasSlopeAtPoint-Qualitative "A predicate used to relate an instance of #$Line-Planar to a qualitative specification of its slope at a given point on that line.")
(comment NoSlope "The instance of #$QualitativeSlope whose numeric value is 0.")
(comment PositiveSlope "The instance of #$QualitativeSlope whose numeric value is some positive number.")
(comment NegativeSlope "The instance of #$QualitativeSlope whose numeric 
value is some negative number.")
(comment USFederalSystemOfChecksAndBalances "The system of checks and balances of the federal government of the United States.  This system was instituted by the U.S. Constitution as a safeguard against any one branch of the government from becoming dominant.")
(comment marketPriceElasticityOfDemand "A predicate that relates a market to the price elasticity of demand (the responsiveness of demand to changes in price) for a product-type in that market, in terms of a real numeric value. <code>(#$marketPriceElasticityOfDemand MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE ELASTICITY)</code> means that given a change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code>, the elasticity of demand in response to that change has a numeric value of <code>ELASTICITY</code>.")
(comment marketDemandIsPriceElasticWRTChange "<code>(#$marketDemandIsPriceElasticWRTChange MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE)</code> means that given a change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code> demand will change significantly; precisely speaking, the absolute value of the elasticity of demand in response to this change is at least 1.  To represent this value, use #$marketPriceElasticityOfDemand.")
(comment marketDemandIsPriceInelasticWRTChange "<code>(#$marketDemandIsPriceInelasticWRTChange MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE)</code> means that given a change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code>, there will be little to no change in demand; precisely speaking, theabsolute value of the elasticity of demand in response to this change is between 0 and 1.  To represent this value, use #$marketPriceElasticityOfDemand.")
(comment ChiefJusticeOfTheUnitedStates "The collection of Chief Justices of the U.S. Supreme Court.")
(comment CharlesSchenk "The defendant in #$SchenkVTheUnitedStates-CourtCase.")
(comment ClearAndPresentDangerPrinciple "The legal principle first enunciated by #$OliverWendellHolmesJr, that speech acts which created dangerous situations that compromised the well-being of the U.S. Government or its citizens did not constitute protected speech under the #$FirstAmendment-USConstitution.")
(comment NorthwestOrdinance "The Northwest Ordinance established that as the United States expanded across North America it would do so by the admission of new states, rather than by the expansion of existing states.")
(comment entitlementDomainOfCodeOfConduct "<code>(#$entitlementDomainOfCodeOfConduct COC RIGHTS-DOMAIN)</code> means that the #$CodeOfConduct <code>COC</code> involves considerations that significantly overlap with the rights that are instances of the specialization of #$Entitlement, <code>RIGHTS-DOMAIN</code>.")
(comment CivilRightsActOf1964 "Landmark legislation that increased rights of minorities and increased the federal government's ability to enforce the law.")
(comment entitlementAffirmedByCourtCaseDecision "<code>(#$entitlementAffirmedByCourtCaseDecision CASE RIGHTS)</code> means that the #decision in the #$CourtCase <code>CASE</code> affirms the #$Entitlement <code>RIGHT</code>.")
(comment marketPriceElasticityOfSupply "A predicate that relates a market to the price elasticity of supply (the responsiveness of supply to changes in price) for a product-type in that market, in terms of a real numeric value. <code>(#$marketPriceElasticityOfSupply MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE ELASTICITY)</code> means that given a change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code>, the elasticity of supply in response to that change has a numeric value of <code>ELASTICITY</code>.")
(comment DemandElasticityPredicate "The collection of instances of #$StrictlyFunctionalPredicate whose functional argument (see #$strictlyFunctionalInArgs) represents the elasticity of demand for a product type in some market in response to some other market feature.")
(comment incomeElasticityOfDemand "A predicate that relates a market to the income elasticity of demand (the responsiveness of demand to changes in consumer income) for a product-type in that market, in terms of a real numeric value. <code>(#$incomeElasticityOfDemand MARKET PRODUCT OLD-INCOME-LEVEL NEW-INCOME-LEVEL ELASTICITY)</code> means that given a change in income level from <code>OLD-INCOME-LEVEL</code> to <code>NEW-INCOME-LEVEL</code> for consumers in <code>MARKET</code>, the value of the change in demand for <code>PRODUCT</code> has a numeric value of <code>ELASTICITY</code>.")
(comment marketQuantityDemandAtConsumerIncomeLevel "<code>(#$marketQuantityDemandAtConsumerIncomeLevel MARKET PRODUCT INCOME QUANTITY)</code> identifies <code>QUANTITY</code> as the quantity of demanded goods or services of type <code>PRODUCT</code> for consumers at an income level of <code>INCOME</code>, an instance of #$MonetaryValue.")
(comment consumerOfResourceTypeInSystem "(#$consumerOfResourceTypeInSystem AGENT RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM) implies that (#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) and that, where AUTOCATALYSIS is the #$autocatalyticProcessImplementsSystem of SYSTEM,  AGENT is capabale of being the #$doneBy of actions that are part of AUTOCATALYSIS in which an instance of RESOURCE-TYPE is the #$inputsDestroyed. To put it a little more roughly (#$consumerOfResourceTypeInSystem AGENT RESOURCE-TYPE SYSTEM) means that AGENT acts as a component in system, and is capable of doing things that are part of the 'life-process' of the system that involve 'consuming' instances of RESOURCE-TYPE.
")
(comment ClarenceBrandenburg "The defendant in BrandenburgVTheStateOfOhio-CourtCase.")
(comment BrandenburgVTheStateOfOhio-CourtCase "An important case concerning #$USCitizensRightToFreedomOfSpeech.  The particulars were that #$ClarenceBrandenburg, a member of the Ku Klux Klan, was taped at an Ohio Klan rally making numerous racist remarks, burning a cross, and accusing the (#$GovernmentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) of suppressing Caucasians.  He was convicted under Ohio's Criminal Syndicalism statute for advocating violence, and his appeal to state appellate court was dismissed.  The #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt struck down the law under which Brandenburg was convicted on the grounds that only speech which threatened to induce 'imminent lawless action' could be proscribed, given first amendment protections (the #$ImminentLawlessActionPrinciple).  This ruling placed considerable strictures on the #$ClearAndPresentDangerPrinciple enunciated by #$OliverWendellHolmesJr some 50 years before.")
(comment overturnsPrecedent "(#$overturnsPrecedent NORM-LATER NORM-EARLIER) means that NORM-LATER is adopted at some later date than NORM-EARLIER, and effectively overrules the convention established by NORM-EARLIER, either through specialization or outright contradiction.")
(comment ImminentLawlessActionPrinciple "The principle enunciated in #$BrandenburgVTheStateOfOhio-CourtCase.  This considerably tightened the latitude of the #$ClearAndPresentDangerPrinciple set forth by the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt six decades earlier:  specifically, the court stated that only speech which could be reasonably construed as provoking or inciting imminent violation of the law was unprotected by the #$FirstAmendment-USConstitution.")
(comment NewYorkTimesVTheUnitedStates-CourtCase "When Daniel Ellsburg leaked a top secret 2.5 million word classified report on the history of U.S. involvement in the #$VietnamWar to the #$NewYorkTimesCompany in early 1971, the paper began publishing it in installments in June of that year.  The administration of #$RichardNixon sought to have a federal district court immediately issue an injunction to cease and desist from publication, arguing that the exercise would cause irreparable harm to U.S. Defense Interests. After numerous inconclusive attempts to enlist Federal courts on one side and the other, both the administration and the paper appealed to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.  The court, in a 6-3 opinion, ruled that the administration had not shown sufficient justification for prior restraint, and that the paper was therefore free to continue publication.")
(comment marketDemandIsPriceUnitElasticWRTChange "<code>(#$marketDemandIsPriceUnitElasticWRTChange MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE)</code> means that percentage of change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code> is identical to the percentage of change in demand for that product at those prices.")
(comment marketDemandIsPerfectlyPriceInelasticWRTChange "<code>(#$marketDemandIsPerfectlyPriceInelasticWRTChange MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE)</code> means that given a change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code>, there will be no change in demand; precisely speaking, theabsolute value of the elasticity of demand in response to this change is 0.")
(comment marketDemandIsPerfectlyPriceElasticWRTChange "<code>(#$marketDemandIsPriceUnitElasticWRTChange MARKET PRODUCT OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE)</code> means that demand for <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code> is perfectly elastic (has an infinite elasticity) in response to the change in <code>MARKET</code>'s price of <code>PRODUCT</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code>.  That is, any increase in price will result in a demand of 0.")
(disjointWith LuxuryGoodOrServiceType NecessityGoodOrServiceType)
(comment MarketDependentGoodOrServiceCategoryType "An instance of #$ThirdOrderCollection. Instances are categories of products, such that inclusion  in or exclusion from a category is dependent on the properties of the market (see #$Market) under consideration.  As such, for an instance <code>CATEGORY</code> of  #$MarketDependentGoodOrServiceCategoryType and an collection <code>TYPE</code>, a sentence of the form <code>(#$isa <code>TYPE</code> <code>CATEGORY</code>)</code> will hold only in microtheories that assume a certain market as well as certain features of that market at a given time and location.")
(comment LuxuryGoodOrServiceType "An instance of #$MarketDependentGoodOrServiceCategoryType.  Instances are types of goods or services that, in the market under consideration, are luxury goods or services, i.e., types of items for which demand is highly sensitive to changes in price.")
(comment NecessityGoodOrServiceType "An instance of #$MarketDependentGoodOrServiceCategoryType.  Instances are types of goods or services that, in the market under consideration, are \"necessities,\" i.e., types of items for which demand is highly insensitive to changes in price.")
(comment NormalGoodOrServiceType "An instance of #$MarketDependentGoodOrServiceCategoryType.  Instances are types of goods or services that, in the market under consideration, are \"normal\" goods or services, i.e., types of items for which demand increases as income increases and vice versa.")
(disjointWith NormalGoodOrServiceType InferiorGoodOrServiceType)
(comment InferiorGoodOrServiceType "An instance of #$MarketDependentGoodOrServiceCategoryType.  Instances are types of goods or services that, in the market under consideration, are \"inferior\" goods or services, i.e., types of items for which demand increases as income decreases and vice versa.")
(comment crossPriceElasticityOfDemand "<code>(#$crossPriceElasticityOfDemand MARKET PRODUCT-1 OLD-PRICE NEW-PRICE PRODUCT-2 ELASTICITY)</code> identifies <code>ELASTICITY</code> as the real numeric value of the degree to which demand in <code>MARKET</code> for <code>PRODUCT-2</code> shifts in response to a change in price of <code>PRODUCT-1</code> from <code>OLD-PRICE</code> to <code>NEW-PRICE</code> in <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment dissentingOpinionBy "(#$dissentingOpinionBy CASE JUDGE) means that where CASE is a #$CaseHeardByTheSupremeCourt, a dissenting opinion in CASE was/is authored by JUDGE.")
(comment justiceOfCourt "A specialization of #$organizationKeyMembers, #$justiceOfCourt is the relation that holds between a #$Court-Judicial and the #$Judge who presides in that court.")
(comment dissentsFromDecision "(#$concursInDecision JUDGE DECISION) means that where DECISION is a #$CourtCaseDecision-PCW in a CASE on which a #$Judge JUDGE is serving, JUDGE dissents from DECISION as a matter of public record.")
(comment opinionBy "(#$opinionBy CASE JUDGE) means that JUDGE authors an opinion connected with a #$decision-CourtCase of CASE decided by the COURT of which JUDGE is justice (#$justiceOfCourt).")
(comment CourtDecision-PCW "The collection of all decisions rendered in instances of #$CourtCase, considered as #$NormativeSpecifications.")
(comment concurringOpinionBy "Where CASE is a #$CaseHeardByTheSupremeCourt, (#$concurringOpinionBy CASE JUDGE) means that JUDGE authors a concurring opinion regarding the #$CourtDecision-PCW of CASE.")
(comment concursInDecision "(#$concursInDecision JUDGE DECISION) means that where DECISION is a #$CourtDecision-PCW in a CASE on which a #$Judge JUDGE is serving, JUDGE concurs with DECISION as a matter of public record.")
(comment MarketConditionChange "The collection of events in which some property of a market (see #$Market) changes, leading to a change in its behavior.")
(comment ChangeInDemandForAGoodOrService "The collection of events in which the demand for a good or service changes (rises or falls) within an instance of #$Market.")
(comment changeTypeInDemandFromTo "<code>(#$changeTypeInDemandFromTo TYPE PRODUCT Q1 Q2)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the subcollection of #$ChangeInDemandForAGoodOrService such that every instance is a change in the demand in some market for <code>PRODUCT</code> from quantity <code>Q1</code> to quantity <code>Q2</code>.")
(comment ChangeInDemandFn "<code>(#$ChangeInDemandFn TYPE Q1 Q2)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ChangeInDemandForAGoodOrService in which the good or service is of type <code>TYPE</code> and is a change in demand from quantity <code>Q1</code> to quantity <code>Q2</code>.")
(comment ChangeInPriceForAGoodOrService "The collection of events in which the price for a good or service changes (rises or falls) within an instance of #$Market.")
(comment changeTypeInProductPriceFromTo "<code>(#$changeTypeInProductPriceFromTo TYPE PRODUCT P1 P2)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the subcollection of #$ChangeInPriceForAGoodOrService such that every instance is a change in the price in some market for <code>PRODUCT</code> from price <code>P1</code> to price <code>P2</code>.")
(comment ChangeInPriceFn "<code>(#$ChangeInPriceFn TYPE P1 P2)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ChangeInPriceForAGoodOrService in which the good or service is of type <code>TYPE</code> and is a change in price from price <code>P1</code> to price <code>P2</code>.")
(comment ChangeInSupplyOfAGoodOrService "The collection of events in which the available supply of a good or service changes (rises or falls) within an instance of #$Market.")
(comment changeTypeInProductSupplyFromTo "<code>(#$changeTypeInProductSupplyFromTo TYPE PRODUCT Q1 Q2)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the subcollection of #$ChangeInSupplyOfAGoodOrService such that every instance is a change in the supply in some market of <code>PRODUCT</code> from quantity <code>Q1</code> to quantity <code>Q2</code>.")
(comment ChangeInSupplyFn "<code>(#$ChangeInSupplyFn TYPE P1 P2)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ChangeInSupplyOfAGoodOrService in which the good or service is of type <code>TYPE</code> and is a change in price from price <code>Q1</code> to price <code>Q2</code>.")
(comment ChangeInIncome "The collection of events in which an agent or group of agents exerience a change in income.")
(comment changeTypeInIncomeFromTo "<code>(#$changeTypeInIncomeFromTo TYPE Q1 Q2)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the subcollection of #$ChangeInIncome such that every instance is a change in some market of agent income from <code>Q1</code> to <code>Q2</code>.")
(comment ChangeInIncomeFn "<code>(#$ChangeInIncomeFn Q1 Q2)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ChangeInIncome in an agent or group of agents experience a change in income level from <code>Q1</code> to <code>Q2</code>.")
(comment marketConsequenceUnderConditionType "<code>(#$marketConsequenceUnderConditionType MARKET SENTENCE CONDITION)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is true of the instance <code>MARKET</code> #$Market whenever it is subject to <code>CONDITION</code>, a type of #$MarketConditionChange.")
(comment substituteProductTypes "<code>(#$substituteProductTypes TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> means that <code>TYPE-1</code> and <code>TYPE-2</code> are substitute product types, meaning that shifts in price in <code>TYPE-1</code> and shifts in the demand for <code>TYPE-2</code> tend to move in the same direction.  This relation is highly context-sensitive; product-type complementarity holds between two product types in specific markets under specific conditions.  As such <code>(#$substituteProductTypes TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> will be true only in contexts (microtheories) where such markets are identified and where such conditions obtain.")
(comment complementaryProductTypes "<code>(#$complementaryProductTypes TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> means that <code>TYPE-1</code> and <code>TYPE-2</code> are complementary product types, meaning that shifts in price in <code>TYPE-1</code> tend to influence demand for <code>TYPE-2</code> in an opposite direction and vice versa.  This relation is highly context-sensitive; product-type complementarity holds between two product types in specific markets under specific conditions.  As such <code>(#$complementaryProductTypes TYPE-1 TYPE-2)</code> will be true only in contexts (microtheories) where such markets are identified and where such conditions obtain.")
(comment WilliamODouglas "#$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt justice from April 17, 1939 to January 19, 1980.")
(comment WilliamJBrennanJr "#$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt justice from October 16, 1856 to July 20, 1990.")
(comment PotterStewart "#$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt justice from October 14, 1958 to July 3, 1981.")
(comment ByronWhite "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from April 16, 1962 to June 28, 1993.")
(comment WilliamRehnquist "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from January 7, 1972 to September 26, 1986, and chief justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from September 26, 1986 to September 3, 2005.")
(comment ConstitutionallyProtectedRightToAbortionUnderDueProcess "The principle enunciated in RoeVWade-CourtCase, that a constitutional right to an abortion exists as a privacy entitlement under the due process clause of the #$FourteenthAmendment-USConstitution.")
(comment RoeVWade-CourtCase "A landmark #$CourtCase heard by the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt, whose decision affirmed the #$ConstitutionallyProtectedRightToAbortionUnderDueProcess.")
(comment NormaLMcCorvey "Plaintiff in #$RoeVWade-CourtCase.")
(comment delegatesPowersOfType "(#$delegatesPowersOfType NORM AGENT ACTIVITY-TYPE ROLE) means that ther #$NormativeSpecification NORM delegates to AGENT the legal authority and responsibility to play ROLE in extended instances of ACTIVITY-TYPE.")
(comment predatorTypeHasPreyTypeInEcosystem "(#$predatorTypeHasPreyTypeInEcosystem PREDATOR-TYPE PREY-TYPE SYSTEM) means that many instance of PREDATOR-TYPE consume instances of PREY-TYPE as resources in SYSTEM (#$consumerOfResourceTypeInSystem).  More specifically, this means that instances of PREDATOR-TYPE are capable of enacting (#$doneBy) subevents in the autocatalytic 'lifetime' of SYSTEM (#$autocatalyticProcessImplementsSystem) in which instances of PREY-TYPE are #$inputsDestroyed.")
(comment priceCeiling "<code>(#$priceCeiling MARKET PRODUCT PRICE)</code> means that the instance <code>PRICE</code> of #$MonetaryValue has been imposed as the maximum price at which <code>PRODUCT</code> may be sold in <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment priceFloor "<code>(#$priceFloor MARKET PRODUCT PRICE)</code> means that the instance <code>PRICE</code> of #$MonetaryValue has been imposed as the minimum price at which <code>PRODUCT</code> may be sold in <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment marketPriceCeilingIsIneffective "<code>(#$marketPriceCeilingIsIneffective MARKET PRODUCT)</code> means that the price ceiling (see #$priceCeiling) imposed on <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code> is no lower than the actual price (see #$marketClearingPrice) for <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code>, and so has no effect on <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment marketPriceCeilingIsEffective "<code>(#$marketPriceCeilingIsEffective MARKET PRODUCT)</code> means that the price ceiling (see #$priceCeiling) imposed on <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code> is lower than the actual price (see #$marketClearingPrice) for <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code>, and so has a potential effect on <code>MARKET</code>, such as encouraging the creation of a black market or queuing costs due to an artficial shortage in supply.")
(comment marketPriceFloorIsEffective "<code>(#$marketPriceFloorIsEffective MARKET PRODUCT)</code> means that the price floor (see #$priceFloor) imposed on <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code> is higher than the actual price (see #$marketClearingPrice) for <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code>, and so has a potential effect on <code>MARKET</code>, such as creating a supply surplus.")
(comment marketPriceFloorIsIneffective "<code>(#$marketPriceFloorIsIneffective MARKET PRODUCT)</code> means that the price floor (see #$priceFloor) imposed on <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code> is no higher than the actual price (see #$marketClearingPrice) for <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code>, and so has no effect on <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment marketSupplySurplus "<code>(#$marketSupplySurplus MARKET PRODUCT QUANTITY)</code> means that in <code>MARKET</code> there is a surplus of <code>QUANTITY</code> instances of <code>PRODUCT</code>.")
(comment marketSupplyShortage "<code>(#$marketSupplyShortage MARKET PRODUCT QUANTITY)</code> means that in <code>MARKET</code> there is a shortage of <code>QUANTITY</code> instances of <code>PRODUCT</code>.")
(comment queuingCost "<code>(#$queingCost MARKET PRODUCT COST)</code> identifies <code>COST</code> as the real monetary value of having to endure a shortage-induced delay in access to <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code>.  To offset <code>COST</code> individuals in the market may be tempted to enter a black market (see #$BlackMarket) to get access to <code>PRODUCT</code>.")
(comment marketSpawnedFromMarketDueToCondition "<code>(#$marketSpawnedFromMarketDueToCondition NEW-MARKET MARKET EVENT)</code> #$means that the instance <code>NEW-MARKET</code> of #$Market arose to fill a need not met by <code>MARKET</code> due primarily or substantially to <code>EVENT</code>, an instance of #$MarketConditionChange that occurred in <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment BlackMarket "The collection of instances of illegal (see #$IllegalAction) markets (see #$Market).")
(comment marketMinimumWage "<code>(#$marketMinimumWage MARKET WAGE)</code> means that <code>WAGE</code> is the minimum amount that workers in <code>MARKET</code> may be paid.")
(comment CaseAppealedToTheSupremeCourt "The collection of all instances of #$CourtCaseWithOneOrMoreAppeals that are appealed to the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.  The procedure is for the #$plaintiffs or #$defendants in the case to engage in a #$PetitioningForAWritOfCertiori, that is, a request that the court issue a #$WritOfCertiori-LegalDocument to hear the case.  The court periodically meets in private conference (#$ConferenceOfTheUnitedStatesSupremeCourt) to consider a filtered subset of these petitions (#$PetitionForAWritOfCertiori-LegalDocument.  The court votes on each petition:  if four or more justices agree that the case rises to the level of a constitutuional issue, the court proceeds with an #$IssuingAWritOfCertiori.  Otherwise, the court executes a #$DenyingAPetitionOfCertiori.  The criteria used in deciding whether or not a cert petition merits the court's attention include resolving a conflict in the interpretation of a federal law or a constitutional provision, correcting an egregious departure from accepted jurisprudence, resolving an important question of federal law, and reviewing a decision of a lower court that conflicts with a previous decision of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt.")
(comment PraxisOfFn "A denoting function used to refer to the normative cultural practices or praxis of a given organization as a #$Culture-Practice.")
(comment praxisOf "Corresponding predicate of #$PraxisOfFn.")
(comment UnitedStatesJudiciaryConventions-Specification "The customary judicial and juridical practice of the #$USJudicialBranch as established through precedent.")
(comment SeparationOfPowersPrinciple "Guiding principle of the #$USConstitution, to check the power of centralized government by assigning different powers to the appurtenances of the different branches of government (#$BranchOfUSGovernment).")
(comment ThirdParty-American "The collection of all 'third parties' in the American political system:  i.e., #$PoliticalParty instances that have their headquarters and residence in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica and are different from the #$DemocraticParty-US and #$RepublicanParty-US.")
(comment SingleIssueParty-American "The collection of all 'third' parties (#$ThirdParty-American instances) that coalesce around a single identifiable issue or principle.")
(comment Electorate "The collection of all geopolitical electorates.  Each instance is a maximal group of people empowered to vote in the territory of a given #$GeopoliticalEntity at a given time.")
(comment ElectorateOfFn "Function used to refer the maximal group of people permitted to vote in elections within the territory of a given #$GeopoliticalEntity.  (#$ElectorateOfFn GEO-AGENT) denotes the maximal group of people legally empowered to vote within the territory of GEO-AGENT (#$TerritoryFn).")
(comment hasElectorate "The corresponding predicate of #$ElectorateOfFn")
(comment PollutionSource-Artifactual "The collection of all #$Artifacts that are sources of pollution in various #$Ecosystems.")
(comment StationaryPollutionSource-Artifactual "The collection of all #$Artifacts that are sources of pollution in various #$Ecosystems, and that are incapable of autonomous motion.")
(comment MobilePollutionSource-Artifactual "The collection of all #$Artifacts that are sources of pollution in various #$Ecosystems, and that are capable of autonomous motion.")
(comment PointSourceForPollutantOfTypeFn "A function used for referring to classes of pollutant sources.  (#$PointSourceForPollutantOfTypeFn POLLUTANT-TYPE) denotes the class of all instances of #$PollutionSource-Artifactual that release point source dispersive emissions of samples of POLLUTANT-TYPE.")
(comment artifactTypeIsPointSourceForPollutantOfType "The corresponding predicate of #$PointSourceForPollutantOfTypeFn.")
(comment PrimaryPollutant "The class of all instances of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance that are directly emitted by some #$PollutionSource-Artifactual.")
(comment SecondaryPollutant "The collection of all instances of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance that come into being as the result of a #$ChemicalSynthesis involving at least one #$PrimaryPollutant.")
(comment Biome "The collection of #$Ecosystems that exist on dry land (islands or continental land masses).")
(comment AquaticLifeZone "The collection of all #$Ecosystems that exist within bodies of fresh or salt water.")
(comment MarginalUtilityFn "At any time <i>t</i> withing the time period <code>PERIOD</code>, <code>(#$MarginalUtilityFn MARKET TYPE QUANTITY)</code> denotes the marginal utility of one additional instance of <code>TYPE</code> to <code>AGENT</code> within a period of time <code>PERIOD</code>, given <code>QUANTITY</code> instances of <code>TYPE</code> already consumed in <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment deadweightLossOfTax "<code>(#$deadweightLossOfTax MARKET PRODUCT TAX LOSS)</code> identifies <code>LOSS</code> as the monetary loss from the sum of the consumer surplus (see #$consumerSurplusAtQuantityOfProductType) and the producer surplus (see #$producerSurplusAtQuantityOfProductType) caused by a tax of amount <code>TAX</code> on <code>PRODUCT</code> in <code>MARKET</code>.")
(comment SamuelAlito "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from January, 2006 to the present.")
(comment StephenBreyer "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from August, 1994 to the present.")
(comment RuthBaderGinsburg "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from August, 1993 to the present.")
(comment ClarenceThomas "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from October, 1991 to the present.")
(comment DavidSouter "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from October, 1990 to the present.")
(comment AnthonyKennedy "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from February, 1988 to the present.")
(comment AntoninScalia "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from September, 1986 to the present.")
(comment JohnPaulStevens "Associate justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from December, 1975 to the present.")
(comment JohnRoberts "Chief justice of the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt from September, 2005 to the present.")
(comment PoliticalActionCommittee "The collection of all committees formed for the exclusive purpose of rasing campaign funds, as defined and delimited by the #$1974FederalElectionCampaignAct.")
(comment 1974FederalElectionCampaignAct "Election campaign law that allows corporations, unions, and trade associations to form #$PoliticalActionCommittees as a means of raising funds.")
(comment specificationPermitsSituationType "The predicate #$specificationPermitsSituationType relates an instance of $#NormativeSpecification SPECIFICATION to a sub-collection of #$Situation. An assertion of the form (#$specificationPermitsSituationType SPECIFICATION SIT-TYPE) means that SPECIFICATION permits the realization of instances of SIT-TYPE..")
(comment Lobbying-PoliticalActivity "The collection of all #$PoliticalActions in which one agent attempts to influence an elected representative or a group of elected representatives to take some action.")
(comment KilledBill-ProposedLaw "The collection of all legislative bills that are 'defunct' in the sense that they have exhausted their options for becoming law in the system in which they have been proposed, without becoming law.")
(comment billHasStatus "(#$billHasStatus BILL BILL-TYPE) means that BILL is regarded as instantiating BILL-TYPE, where BILL-TYPE equates to one of three possibilities: #$Bill-ProposedLaw, #$KilledBill-ProposedLaw, or #$Law.")
(disjointWith KilledBill-ProposedLaw Law)
(comment onlyEventOfTypeForPatient "<code>(#$onlyEventOfTypeForPatient EVT TYPE)</code> means that <code>EVT</code> is the only event of the type <code>TYPE</code> that is recorded in the patient's record.")
(comment treatmentTypeForConditionType "<code>(#$treatmentTypeForConditionType CONDITION TREATMENT)</code> means that <code>TREATMENT</code> is the collection of medical treatment events in which an instance of <code>CONDITION</code> is treated.")
(comment AirplaneTakeOff "A specialization of #$TakeOff-Flight.  Each instance of this collection is an event in which an #$Airplane leaves the ground and becomes airborne.")
(comment HelicopterTakeOff "A specialization of #$TakeOff-Flight.  Each instance of this collection is an event in which a #$Helicopter leaves the ground and becomes airborne.")
(comment YouTube-WebSite "A video-sharing website run by #$YouTube-TheCompany, which became a subsidiary of #$GoogleInc in 2006.")
(comment YouTube-TheCompany "The company that developed the video-sharing website, #$YouTube-WebSite.  YouTube became a subsidiary of #$GoogleInc in 2006.")
(comment MedicalReport-CW "A specialization of #$WrittenReportOnSituation-CW.  Each instance is a report that specifies some body of facts about either individual patients, groups of patients, or about medical techniques, procedures, equipment, etc.")
(comment VideoGameSystem "The collection of #$Computers which are specifically designed for playing games.  This collection inlcudes handheld portables, consumer systems like Xbox and Playstation as well as stand-alone arcade machines.  For the collection of such systems designed for end user purchase see #$HomeVideoGameMachine.")
(comment HomeVideoGameMachine "The collection of #$Computers which are designed primarily for purchase by end use consumers and are specifically designed for playing games.  While possibly complete computers (in Turing's sense), virtually all programs written for these systems are games. Such systems generally do not use stored programs, but instead run games off of cartridge or CD.  They often contain specialized graphics and sound hardware and are designed to output to a television set or to a small build in screen in the case of handheld games.  Examples are the Gameboy, Super Nintendo, Xbox, and Sony Playstation2.")
(comment CommaSeparatedValueFile "The subcollection of #$ComputerFile-AIS, instances of which are encoded in the Comma Separated Value file format (.csv).")
(comment sinceStartDatePerRecord "<code>(#$sinceStartDatePerRecord DATE SYS STATUS RECORD-MT)</code> means that since <code>DATE</code>, the system <code>SYS</code> has had the status <code>STATUS</code>, per the information in the microtheory, <code>RECORD-MT</code>.")
(comment predHighlyRelevantForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$predHighlyRelevantForJustificationParaphrase PRED)</code> means that when <code>PRED</code> is the arg0 in a support for a proof, a paraphrase of that proof explicitly mention that support, and that paraphrase should print the support in a manner that emphasizes it (e.g. by printing the support in bold or italic).")
(comment missionRequiresNSubSystemsInSetForSystem "<code>(#$missionRequiresNSubSystemsInSetForSystem MISSION N SET SYSTEM)</code> means that <code>MISSION</code> requires at least <code>N</code> many of the systems in the set <code>SET</code> to be functioning, to support the functioning of the further required system, <code>SYSTEM</code>..")
(comment cardinalityOfSubSystemsWithStatus "<code>(#$cardinalityOfSubSystemsWithStatus DATE STATUS CARD SYSTEM SET)</code> means that as of <code>DATE</code>, the cardinality of the set <code>SET</code> of sub-systems of <code>SYSTEM</code> with the status <code>STATUS</code> is <code>CARD</code>.")
(comment standardPrefixForURI "This relates a URI to a prefix string considered the standard prefix for that URI.")
(comment standardTreatmentTypeForConditionType "<code>(#$standardTreatmentTypeForConditionType TREATMENT-TYPE CONDITION-TYPE)</code> means that <code>TREATMENT-TYPE</code> is used to treat the #$AilmentCondition <code>CONDITION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Meat "A specialization of #$EdibleStuff.  Each instance of #$Meat is some piece of animal flesh (usually a piece of skeletal muscle tissue, possibly combined with fat) that is edible.")
(comment Sausage "The collection of all sausages.  A specialization of #$SolidFoodArtifact.  Each instance of #$Sausage is a food product typically  from ground meat and sometimes other ingredients such as herbs, and typically shaped roughly as a cylinder. Recenlty, some vegetarian sausages have been developed (see #$VegetarianSausage).")
(comment VegetarianSausage "A specialization of #$Sausage.  Each instance of #$VegetarianSausage is a sausage which contains no meat or meat by-products.")
(comment ElectionForPositionInPolityFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for referencing particular #$Elections.  (#$ElectionForPositionInPolityFn POSITION POLITY DATE) denotes the unique #$Election held by POLITY on DATE to fill the position POSITION-TYPE.")
(comment electionForPositionInPolity "The corresponding predicate of #$ElectionForPositionInPolityFn.")
(comment electionWinners "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates an #$Election to the individual who wins it.  (#$electionWinners ELECTION WINNER) means that WINNER is the winner of ELECTION.")
(comment winnerDeclaredOnDate "(#$winnerDeclaredOnDate ELECTION DATE) means that DATE is the date at which a winner is declared in ELECTION by the appropriate authorities.")
(comment ElectionTypeByPolityType "A type-level faceting collection (#$FacetingCollectionType) that facets #$Elections by the scope of the organization (#$Country, #$State-Geopolitical, #$Municipality...) holding the election.  Important instances include #$NationalElection, where the polity holding the #$Election is a #$Country, #$StateElection, where the polity holding the #$Election is a #$State-Geopolitical, and #$LocalElection, where the polity holding the #$Election is a #$Municipality.")
(comment NationalElection "The collection of all #$Elections in which the polity holding the #$Election is a #$Country.")
(comment StateElection "The collection of all #$Elections in which the polity holding the #$Election is a #$State-Geopolitical.")
(comment LocalElection "The collection of all #$Elections in which the polity holding the #$Election is a #$Municipality.")
(comment contraindicatedDrug "(#$contraindicatedDrug AILMENT DRUG) means that DRUG is contraindicated in patients suffering from #$AilmentCondition AILMENT.")
(comment SurgicalIncision-Sternotomy-PartialConvertedToFull "A #$Sternotomy having two phases.  In the first, a #$SurgicalIncision-Sternotomy-Partial is performed, then later a #$SurgicalIncision-Sternotomy-Full is performed on the same #$Sternum.")
(comment sksiDifferent "#$sksiDifferent is a binary predicate similar to #$different, but is intended to only be solved via an external knowledge source.  <code>(#$sksiDifferent THING1 THING2)</code> is true when <code>THING1</code> and <code>THING2</code> are determined by the external source to not be equal.")
(comment sksiEquals "#$sksiEquals is a binary predicate similar to #$equals, but is intended to only be solved via an external knowledge source.  <code>(#$sksiEquals THING1 THING2)</code> is true when <code>THING1</code> and <code>THING2</code> are determined by the external source to be equal.")
(comment EarthsGravity-UnitOfAcceleration "The nominal acceleration that the earth's gravity provides at sea level, defined as exactly 9.80665 meters/sec^2, as established by the third General Conference on Weights and Measures in 1901.")
(comment primaryElectionOf "(#$primaryElectionOf PRIMARY GENERAL-ELECTION) means that PRIMARY is a #$PrimaryElection held in order to establish a slate of #$electionCandidates to run in GENERAL-ELECTION.")
(comment ElectionForCandidacyInElectionFn "A #$TernaryFunction used for reifying instances of #$PrimaryElection.  (#$ElectionForCandidacyInElectionFn POLITY POLITICAL-PARTY ELECTION) denotes the #$PrimaryElection held in the territory of POLITY and under the auspices of POLITY's government in order to select a candidate from POLITICAL-PARTY tobe an #$electionCandidates in ELECTION.")
(comment electionForCandidacyInElection "The corresponding predicate of #$ElectionForCandidacyInElectionFn.")
(comment runOffElectionOf "(#$runOffElectionOf RUNOFF ELECTION) means that RUNOFF is an election held subsequent to ELECTION in order to break a deadlock between two #$electionCandidates in ELECTION who have tied for first place.")
(comment UserOfProgramFn "(#$UserOfProgramFn PROGRAM USER) denotes USER during the time USER is using program.")
(comment userOfProgramUsingProgram "An expression of the form (#$userOfProgramUsingProgram USER-OF-PROGRAM PROGRAM USER) states that 'USER-OF-PROGRAM' denotes USER while USER is using program. This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$UserOfProgramFn.")
(comment OWLPropertyLogicalSchemaFn "This function denotes a logical schema for a given OWL property.")
(comment hasOWLPropertyLogicalSchema "This is the corresponding predicate to #$OWLPropertyLogicalSchemaFn.")
(comment ReifiedMappingForPredFn "This function denotes a CMLS for a set of terms relative to a particular knowledge store and predicate.")
(comment campaignOfElection "(#$campaignOfElection CAMPAIGN ELECTION) means that ELECTION is the #$Election that the #$PoliticalElectionCampaign CAMPAIGN is targeted for and that CAMPAIGN's directors intend to win.")
(comment garnersVotes "(#$garnersVotes AGENT ELECTION NUMBER) means that the number of votes received by AGENT in ELECTION is NUMBER.")
(comment meaningSentencePredicateForSchema "(#$meaningSentencePredicateForSchema SCHEMA PRED) means that PRED appears as the operator in a meaning sentence in SCHEMA.")
(comment metricComparisonTypes-Definite "A #$RuleMacroPredicate that supports estimation of size comparisons.  Where TYPE1 and TYPE2 are specializations of #$SpatialThing-Localized, METRIC-PRED is a #$MeasurableQuantitySlot such as #$areaOfRegion, and COMP is a #$NumericComparisonPredicate such as #$greaterThan, (#$metricComparisonTypes-Definite TYPE1 TYPE2 METRIC-PRED COMP) means that for any instance INST1 of TYPE1 and any instance INST2 of TYPE2, if (METRIC-PRED INST1 QUANT1) is true and (METRIC-PRED INST2 QUANT2) is true, then the quantity QUANT1 bears the relation COMP to the quantity QUANT2.")
(comment logicalFieldValueForSchemaMeaningSentenceInArg "<code>(#$logicalFieldValueForSchemaMeaningSentenceInArg LS LFVI ARG-POS) means that in a meaning sentence for LS the logical field value indexical LFVI is the term in ARG-POS.  This is a useful abstraction of information for logical schemas which have exactly one meaning sentence with a binary predicate in arg0.</code>")
(comment ImportingAnOWLFileIntoAKnowledgeBase "The collection of actions in which some agent imports, either by hand or via some import mechanism, an OWL file into a knowledge base.  This import results in an updating of the knowledge base either by removing existing statements, adding additional statements, or some combination of both.")
(comment termActedOnDuringOWLImport "(#$termActedOnDuringOWLImport IMPORT TERM) means that TERM either was created during IMPORT, or had its assertions updated during IMPORT (had an assertion added or deleted).")
(comment Atherectomy-PercutaneousProcedure "A type of percutaneous procedure.  Each instance of #$Atherectomy-PercutaneousProcedure  is a procedure performed via a catheter in order to remove the atheromatous plaque in the lining of an artery.   When that removal is performed via surgical incision, then the procedure is called an \"endarterectomy\".")
(comment electionsForPositionsInGoverningBody "The corresponding Predicate of #$ElectionsForPositionsInGoverningBodyFn.")
(comment candidateInGroupOfElections "(#$candidateInGroupOfElections ELECTION-GROUP CANDIDATE) means that CANDIDATE is an #$electionCandidates in some election that occurs as part of the politically delimited group of elections, ELECTION-GROUP.")
(comment seatsWonInElections "(#$seatsWonInElections ELECTIONS PARTY NUM) means that in the group of elections (e.g., to some legislative body) designated by ELECTIONS, PARTY wins/won/has won NUM seats.")
(comment ElectionsForPositionsInGoverningBodyFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used for talking about a group of elections held to elect members of a particular governing body.  Specifically, where ORG is a #$GovernmentalOrganization, (#$ElectionsForPositionsInGoverningBodyFn ORG DATE) refers to the group of elections held on DATE to elect some (possibly all) of the members of ORG.")
(comment CorrespondingRangeCollectionFn "This function denotes a (typically) 2nd order collection that is used as the arg2Isa of an OWLProperty in a given Ontology.")
(comment DoctoralDegree "The collection of all doctoral degrees, including Ph.D. degrees and medical doctoral degrees.  A specialization of #$GraduateDegree.")
(comment MedicalDegree-Physicians "Doctor of Medicine degree, abbreviated \"M.D.\".  All instances of #$Doctor-MD have one. ")
(comment PageOfPaper-IBO "The collection of all pages of paper that are bound in books, magazines pamhlets, etc. #$PageOfPaper-IBO is a type of #$SheetOfPaper and #$Paper-IBO. #$PageOfPaper-IBO is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Back-AnimalBodyPart "The collection of all backs of animals. A type of #$ExternalAnatomicalPart and #$AnimalBodyPart (qq.v.). The concept #$Back-AnimalBodyPart is an #$ExternalAnimalBodyRegionType and a #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType.  Any animal that has a back has exactly one back.  On humans, the back has significant sub-parts, such as major muscles including tha #$LatissimusDorsi and the #$Trapezius.")
(comment Candy "The collection of all candy. A type of #$SolidFoodArtifact, #$Food-ReadyToEat, and #$SweetTaste. The collection #$Candy is a #$SnackFoodType and an #$ExistingStuffType.  Each instance of #$Candy is a relatively small and very sugary confection.  Representative specializations of #$Candy include #$Jellybean, #$Lollipop and #$CandyBar.")
(comment CourseOfAMeal "The collection of all courses of meals. A type of #$Food-ReadyToEat. #$CourseOfAMeal is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Representative specializations of #$CourseOfAMeal include #$Appetizer and #$Entree.")
(comment Virginia-State "Virginia: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment IndexDivider "The collection of all index dividers. A type of #$StationeryProduct and #$FreeSheet. The collection #$IndexDivider is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$IndexDivider is a free sheet designed to be used to separate paers in a file.")
(comment HotDog "The collection of all hot dogs. A type of #$Sausage. The collection #$HotDog is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$HotDog is a small sausage of uniform texture and consistency, typically made of pork, beef, or turkey, but possiblly tofu.")
(comment PhotographicFilm "The collection of all photographic films. A type of #$Film-FreeSheet, #$ArtificialMaterial, #$DeviceWithNoMovingParts, and #$InformationStorageDevice. The collection #$PhotographicFilm is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and an #$ExistingStuffType. Each instance of #$PhotographicFilm is a sheet of plastic coated with one or more light-sensitive emulsion layers.")
(comment Nausea "The collection of all conditions in which nausea is experiences as a physiological condition. A type of #$AilmentCondition, and an instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType.")
(comment Dried "The collection of all dried food. A type of #$PreparedFood. The collection #$Dried is a #$FoodTypeByPreparationStyle and an #$EdibleStuffTypeByPreparationStyle.")
(comment OfficeSpace-Personal "The collection of all personal office space. A type of #$SpaceInAFixedHOC and #$Workplace. #$OfficeSpace-Personal is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Baseball-Ball "The collection of all baseballs. A type of #$Ball and an instance ofa #$BallTypeByGame.  Each instance of #$Baseball-Ball is a ball intended to be used in playing the game of baseball.  Typically, baseballs have cork or rubber cores covered by twine and wrapped in white leather with red stitching.")
(comment FootballTeam "The collection of all football teams. A type of #$SportsTeam. #$FootballTeam is a #$SportsTeamTypeBySport.  Each instance of #$FootballTeam is a team of persons who are associated with the intent and objective of playing at least one game of football.")
(comment LivingRoom "The collection of all living rooms. A type of room of a modern residence. #$LivingRoom is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$LivingRoom is a room in a house that is primarily used for activities such as lounging, entertaining, reading, or watching television.")
(comment Chip-Snack "The collection of all chips. A type of #$SnackFood, #$SolidFoodArtifact, and #$Flaky-CoherentPhysicalStructure. The collection #$Chip-Snack is a #$SnackFoodType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$Chip-Snack is a thin, crispy and fairly small snack food object, often prepared through baking or deep-frying.")
(comment FederalUnion "The collection of all federal unions. A type of #$GovernmentRelatedEntity and #$GeopoliticalEntity. The collection #$FederalUnion is an #$ArtifactualFeatureType and a #$FacetInstanceCollection.")
(comment Bedroom "The collection of all bedrooms. A type of #$RoomInAConstruction and #$PartOfBuilding. #$Bedroom is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$Bedroom is a room in a house that contains furniture for sleeping.")
(comment AirplaneWing "The collection of all wings of airplanes. A type of #$AirplanePart, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$MechanicalDevice. The collection #$AirplaneWing is a #$ManufacturedGoodsType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment AlcoholicBeverage "The collection of all alcoholic beverages. A type of #$Drink, #$ArtificialMaterial, #$Mixture, and #$LuxuryItem. #$AlcoholicBeverage is #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  Each instance of #$AlcoholicBeverage is a drink that contains a non-trivial amount of alcohol.  Notable specializations include #$Beer and #$Wine.")
(comment RestrictedRating "The collection of all movies that have been rated \"R\" (\"Restricted\") by the Motion Picture Association of America.  #$RestrictedRating is an instance of #$MPAAAdvisoryClassification-Film.")
(comment HumanMaleGivenName "A type of #$HumanGivenName. #$HumanMaleGivenName is a #$LinguisticObjectType. Each instance of #$HumanMaleGivenName is a name typically given to males, as opposed to females.")
(comment PalmOfHand "The collection of all palms of hands. A type of #$ExternalAnatomicalPart, #$AnimalBodyPart, #$SurfaceRegion-Finite, and #$SurfaceRegion-Tangible. The collection #$PalmOfHand is an #$ExternalAnimalBodyRegionType and a #$SymmetricAnatomicalPartType.")
(comment Dummy "The collection of all models of the human figure. A type of #$Artifact-HumanCreated.")
(comment Texas-State "Texas: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment Pea-Foodstuff "The collection of all peas. A type of #$Vegetable-Food. The collection #$Pea-Foodstuff is an #$AgriculturalCommodity, an #$ExistingStuffType, and a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.  Each instance of #$Pea-Foodstuff is a small spherical seed from the pod of a pea plant.  Peas are typically green or yellow.")
(comment ElbowJoint "The collection of all joints formed at the place where the humerus, radius, and ulna come together mear the middle of the arm. The collection #$ElbowJoint is a #$SymmetricAnatomicalPartType and an #$InternalAnimalBodyRegionType.")
(comment ParentalGuidance13Rating "The collection of all movies rated \"PG-13\" by the Motion Picture Association of America. #$ParentalGuidance13Rating is an #$MPAAAdvisoryClassification-Film.")
(comment FootballGame-American "The collection of all American football games. A type of #$BallAndGoalGame, #$PedestrianSportsEvent, #$ContactSportsEvent, #$TimeLimitedSportsEvent, and #$CooperativeTeamSportsCompetition.")
(comment ColaSoftDrink "The collection of all cola soft drinks. A type of #$SoftDrink-Flavored. The collection #$ColaSoftDrink is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType, an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory, a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType, and a #$ManufacturedGoodsType.  Well-known specializations include #$PepsiCola and #$CocaCola.")
(comment SoleOfFoot "The collection of all soles of feet. A type of #$ExternalAnatomicalPart. Each instance of #$SoleOfFoot is the bottom part of a foot.")
(comment Football-American "American football (known in the U.S. as \"football\"): a #$TeamSport, a #$SportsGame, and a #$TwoTeamGame. American football is a popular competetive contact sport.")
(comment BitterTaste "The collection of all bitter-tasting objects. An #$ObjectTypeByTaste.")
(comment Honey "The collection of all honey. A type of #$Sweetener, #$LiquidTangibleThing, and #$SweetTaste. The collection #$Honey is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  Each instance of #$Honey is a portion of fluid produced by bees as a food source.")
(comment Frozen "The collection of all frozen food. A type of #$ConvenienceFood and #$PreparedFood. The collection #$Frozen is a #$FoodTypeByPreparationStyle and an #$EdibleStuffTypeByPreparationStyle.")
(comment JuniorHighLevel "The collection of all persons who have achieved junior high level education. A type of #$SecondarySchoolLevel. The collection #$JuniorHighLevel is a #$PersonTypeByEducationLevel.")
(comment China-Dinnerware "The collection of all dinnerware made from porcelain. A type of #$FoodVessel, #$NonPoweredDevice, and #$RigidPortableObject. The collection #$China-Dinnerware is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Lamb-Meat "The collection of all lamb meat. The collection #$Lamb-Meat is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.")
(comment MilitaryThing-SpatiallyLocalized "The collection of all military objects.")
(comment ElementaryLevel "The collection of all persons who have achieved elementary-school level education. The collection #$ElementaryLevel is a #$PersonTypeByEducationLevel.")
(comment FordCar "The collection of all Ford automobiles. A type of #$AmericanAutomobile. The collection #$FordCar is an #$AutomobileTypeByBrand.")
(comment Wheat-Foodstuff "The collection of all wheat berries. A type of #$CommonFoodAllergen and #$VegetableMatter.")
(comment Vinegar "The collection of all vinegar. A type of #$SourTaste, #$LiquidTangibleThing, and #$FoodIngredientOnly. The collection #$Vinegar is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.")
(comment LibrarySpace "The collection of all libraries. A type of #$CollectionDisplaySetting and #$SpaceInAFixedHOC. #$LibrarySpace is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$LibrarySpace is a space in a human occupation construct that facilitates the storage (and display) of books or other information-storage media, such as records or CDs.")
(comment EggWhites-Food "The collection of all egg whites. A type of edible part of chicken's eggs and #$LiquidTangibleThing. The collection #$EggWhites-Food is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and an #$ExistingStuffType.  Each instance of #$EggWhite-Food is the clear liquid contained within a poultry egg, which can be separated and used for cooking.")
(comment NewYork-State "New York: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment Roasted "The collection of all roasted food. A type of #$Cooked. The collection #$Roasted is a #$FoodTypeByPreparationStyle, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$EdibleStuffTypeByPreparationStyle.")
(comment FootballBall-American "The collection of all balls designed to be used to play American football. A type of #$Ball, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$Projectile-Device. Each instance of #$FootballBall-American is a prolate spheroid ball with fairly pointed ends, made of leather, rubber or plastic, and filled with an inflatable bladder.")
(comment Yeast "The collection of all yeast. A type of #$Ascomycota-Division. The collection #$Yeast is an #$OrganismClassificationType.  Each instance of #$Yeast is a fungal micro organism.")
(comment BaseballPlayer "The collection of all persons who play baseball. A type of #$UpperMiddleClass, #$PersonWithOccupation, and #$Athlete. #$BaseballPlayer is an #$AthleteTypeBySport.")
(comment VitaminPill "The collection of all vitamin pills. A type of #$DietarySupplement, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$Pill. The collection #$VitaminPill is a #$PharmacyProductType.")
(comment HumanFemaleGivenName "The collection of all human female names. A type of #$HumanGivenName. #$HumanFemaleGivenName is a #$LinguisticObjectType.  Each instance of #$HumanFemaleGivenName is a name typically given to females, as opposed to males.")
(comment ResearchProject "The collection of all research projects. A type of #$Research and #$Project. The collection #$ResearchProject is a #$ProcessType and a #$SkilledActivityType.")
(comment WoolStuff "The collection of all wool. A type of #$SolidAnimalMatter, #$ProtectiveCovering, #$Fibrous, and #$ExtrudedBodyPart. The collection #$WoolStuff is an #$ExternalAnimalBodyRegionType and an #$ExistingStuffType.  Notable specializations of #$WoolStuff include #$SheepWool, LlamaWool and #$AngoraWool.")
(comment Ethiopia "Ethiopia: an #$AfricanCountry and a #$LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment AutomobileSteeringSystem "The collection of all steering mechanisms of automobiles. A type of #$MechanicalAutoPart. The collection #$AutomobileSteeringSystem is a #$ManufacturedGoodsType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.  By default, each instance of #$Automobile has exactly one of these mechanisms.")
(comment MustardSeed "The collection of all mustard seeds. A type of #$Spice, #$ExternalAnatomicalPart, and #$Seed. The collection #$MustardSeed is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$MustardSeed is a small, spicy seed whose primary use is to season food or to create the spicy condiment, mustardd")
(comment Windshield "The collection of all windshields. A type of #$AutomobileWindow. The collection #$Windshield is a #$ManufacturedGoodsType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.  Each instance of #$Windshield is the large front window of an #$Automobile.")
(comment ChryslerCar "The collection of all Chrysler automobiles. A type of #$AmericanAutomobile. The collection #$ChryslerCar is an #$AutomobileTypeByBrand.")
(comment Bell "The collection of all bells. A type of #$PercussionInstrument. The collection #$Bell is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$Bell is a simple instrument, formed of metal, glass or ceramic in the shape of an open-ended drum, which resonates when struck.")
(comment Whisky "The collection of all whisky. A type of #$Liquor-Drink. The collection #$Whisky is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  Each instance of #$Whisky is an alcoholic beverage made by distilling fermented grain, such as barley, rye, wheat or corn.")
(comment Golf "Golf: a #$SportsGame and a #$Game.  Golf is a sport in which a player swings clubs at a small ball with the aim of causing the ball to enter each of the holes (in a prescribed sequence) in a golf course in as few strokes as possible.")
(comment HumanActivities-Topic "A #$CycVocabularyTopLevelTopic and a #$KBDependentCollection.")
(comment Estonia "Estonia: a #$BalticState, a #$Republic, and an #$EasternEuropeanCountry.")
(comment Pennsylvania-State "Pennsylvania: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment Georgia-State "Georgia: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment VehicleBrakeSystem "The collection of all brake systems of vehicles. A type of #$VehiclePart, #$Device-UserControlled, and #$NewAutoDealerPartsMarketCategory. The collection #$VehicleBrakeSystem is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  The brake system of a vehicle is a system intended to be used to slow or stop the vehicle.")
(comment MiddleClass "The collection of all persons whose economic status is middle class. A type of #$HomoSapiens, #$MiddleClass is a #$PersonTypeBySocialClass.")
(comment Florida-State "Florida: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment Illinois-State "Illinois: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment ContactLens "The collection of all contact lenses. A type of #$SomethingToWear, #$Eyewear, and #$Lens-Artificial. Each instance of #$ContactLens is a small lens designed to be worn in direct contact with the eye.")
(comment ShockAbsorber "The collection of all shock absorbers. A type of #$MechanicalAutoPart, #$NewAutoDealerPartsMarketCategory, and #$KineticEnergyPoweredDevice. The collection #$ShockAbsorber is a #$ManufacturedGoodsType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment AirplaneCockpit "The collection of all cockpits. Each instsance of #$AirplaneCockpit is an interior of a cavity in an airplane where the pilot sits and controls the airplane. The collection #$AirplaneCockpit is a #$ManufacturedGoodsType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment Ukraine "Ukraine: a #$FinanciallyHurting and an #$EasternEuropeanCountry.")
(comment ScubaGear "The collection of all scuba gear. A type of #$SportsEquipment and #$SomethingToWear. The collection #$ScubaGear is an (#$EquipmentTypeForEventTypeFn #$ScubaDiving), a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and a #$SomethingToWearTypeByGenericCategory.  Each instance of #$ScubaGear is equipment used to perfomr scuba diving.")
(comment Colorado-State "Colorado: a #$LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity and a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment CycMetaphysics-Topic "A #$CycVocabularyTopLevelTopic and a #$KBDependentCollection.")
(comment CarBombing "The collection of all car bombings. A type of #$Bombing-RoadVehicleDelivered. The collection #$CarBombing is an #$AttackTypeByWeaponType, and a #$TerroristAttackTacticType.  Each instance of #$CarBombing is an attack in which an explosive is detonated within an automobile.")
(comment SaladDressing "The collection of all salad dressing. A type of #$Emulsion, #$Condiment, and #$Sauce. The collection #$SaladDressing is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and an #$ExistingStuffType.  Each instance of #$SaladDressing is a liquid condiment used to moisturize and enhance the flavor of a salad.")
(comment Thorn "The collection of all thorns. A type of #$PlantPart and #$ExternalAnatomicalPart. The collection #$Thorn is a #$PlantPartType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$Thorn is a small and very sharp protrusion on the stem or branch of a plant.")
(comment ParentalGuidanceRating "The collection of all movies that are rated \"PG\" by the Motion Picture Association of America. #$ParentalGuidanceRating is an #$MPAAAdvisoryClassification-Film.")
(comment Washington-State "Washington: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment NorthCarolina-State "North Carolina: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment Cracker-FoodItem "The collection of all crackers. A type of #$Biscuit, #$SolidFoodArtifact, #$SaltyTaste, #$Flaky-CoherentPhysicalStructure, and #$SnackFood. The collection #$Cracker-FoodItem is a #$SnackFoodType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$Cracker-FoodItem is a thin and crisp biscuit.")
(comment Ohio-State "Ohio: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment GazaStrip "The Gaza Strip: a #$Territory.")
(comment Throat "The collection of all throats. A type of #$InternalAnatomicalPart and #$AnimalBodyPart. The collection #$Throat is an #$InternalAnimalBodyRegionType and a #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType.  Each instance of #$Throat is an interior of a neck.")
(comment AmericanAutomobile "The collection of all American cars. A type of #$Automobile-GasolineEngine. The collection #$AmericanAutomobile is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Michigan-State "Michigan: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment Cuba "Cuba: an #$IndependentCountry and a #$NorthAmericanCountry.")
(comment SriLanka "Sri Lanka: a #$SouthAsianCountry and an #$IndependentCountry.")
(comment VegetableOil "The collection of all vegetable oil. A type of #$EdibleOil, #$InanimateObject-Natural, and #$PlantProduct. The collection #$VegetableOil is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.")
(comment Uganda "Uganda: an #$AfricanCountry and a #$LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment BakingPowder "The collection of all baking powder. A type of #$Powder and #$FoodIngredientOnly. The collection #$BakingPowder is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and an #$ExistingStuffType.  Each instance of #$BakingPowder is a portion of dry powder that produces gas under certain conditions (such as exposure to liquid or heat).  This gas-producing quality is typically exploited to caused baked goods to rise.")
(comment FurPelt "The collection of all fur pelts, which are skins of animals covered with fur. A type of #$NonPoweredDevice and #$DurableGood.")
(comment File-Tool "The collection of all files. A type of #$HandTool. The collection #$File-Tool is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$File-Tool is a jhand tool used to reduced the size of an object by wearing it away or cutting it down incrementally.")
(comment Mayonnaise "The collection of all mayonnaise. A type of #$Condiment, #$Sauce, and #$Emulsion. The collection #$Mayonnaise is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and an #$ExistingStuffType.  Each instance of #$Mayonnaise is a thick liquid condiment made of vegetable oil and egg yolks.")
(comment ScotchWhisky "The collection of all Scotch whiskey. A type of #$Whisky. The collection #$ScotchWhisky is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and an #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment AudiCar "The collection of all Audis. A type of #$GermanCar. The collection #$AudiCar is an #$AutomobileTypeByBrand and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment EggYolk-Food "The collection of all yolks of eggs. A type of edible part of chicken's eggs. The collection #$EggYolk-Food is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and an #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment IvoryCoast "The Ivory Coast: an #$AfricanCountry.")
(comment Cover-Protector "The collection of all covers designed to protect objects. A type of #$PhysicalDevice. The collection #$Cover-Protector is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment GraduationCeremony "The collection of all ceremonies performed on the occasion of the graduation of a class from an eduactional institution. A type of #$AwardsCeremony.")
(comment DemocraticRepublicOfTheCongo "Democratic Republic of the Congo: an #$AfricanCountry.")
(comment OperaHouse "The collection of all opera houses. A type of #$Theater-PhysicalStructure and #$LargeBuilding. The collection #$OperaHouse is an #$ArtifactTypeByFunction.  Each instance of #$OperaHouse is a large building used for large musical performances.")
(comment Missouri-State "Missouri: a #$LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity and a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment RockBand "The collection of all rock bands. A type of #$Band-MusicGroup and #$RockMusicPerformer.  Each instance of #$RockBand is a music group that performs primarily rock music songs.")
(comment BMWCar "The collection of all BMW automobiles. A type of #$GermanCar and #$LuxuryCar. The collection #$BMWCar is an #$AutomobileTypeByBrand and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment SodiumBicarbonate "The collection of all sodium bicarbonate. A type of #$WaterSolubleStuff, #$DrugSubstance, #$InorganicCompound, #$IonicCompound, #$StrongElectrolyte, and #$Salt-ChemicalSubstance. #$SodiumBicarbonate is an #$IonicCompoundType.  Each instance of #$SodiumBicarbonate is a portion of salt with the chemical formula NaHCO3.")
(comment Serbia "Serbia: a #$LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity, a #$CountrySubsidiary, a #$Country, and a #$BalkanCountry.")
(comment Iowa-State "Iowa: a #$LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity and a #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment Massachusetts-State "Massachusetts: a #$State-UnitedStates.")
